[{"id":"b107","title":"費馬恩海峽沉管隧道","titleEn":"Fehmarnbelt immersed tunnel","category":"underground","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"費馬恩海峽的官方工程頁列18公里沉管隧道，並記載2020年開始施工。本課以跨國道路鐵路共同走廊為背景，逐步檢查箱體量產、重量帳、海床支承、止水接頭和設備交付。未來營運效益與施工進度分開表述，不把建設中的設施描述為已完成營運。","summaryEn":"The official Fehmarnbelt project page describes an 18 km immersed tunnel and construction beginning in 2020. Using a cross-border road and rail corridor, this course examines element production, mass balance, seabed support, sealing and equipment handover. Future service benefits remain separate from construction progress; the facility is not described as already operational.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"ug-landmarks","subcategoryTitle":"世界隧道與地下巨作","subcategoryTitleEn":"World tunnels and underground landmarks","learningTrack":"underground","learningSubdiscipline":"ug-landmarks","learningTags":["underground","ug-landmarks","tunnel"],"architectureFamily":"tunnel","architectureNodes":[["路線里程與端點","Alignment chainage and endpoints"],["頂板跨中彎矩","Roof-span bending"],["剩餘浮力","Residual buoyancy"],["止水壓縮餘量","Gasket compression reserve"],["擴散特徵長度","Diffusion characteristic length"],["資產資料完整度","Asset-record completeness"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,5],[1,5]],"diagram":{"type":"tunnel","labels":["路線里程與端點","頂板跨中彎矩","剩餘浮力","止水壓縮餘量","擴散特徵長度"],"labelsEn":["Alignment chainage and endpoints","Roof-span bending","Residual buoyancy","Gasket compression reserve","Diffusion characteristic length"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"原創綜合審查：先計算「矩形沉管的框架受力」，再獨立計算「接頭壓縮與水密包絡」。原創教學假設：單位長載重=26 kN/m；跨距=3.15 m。M=qL²/8=32.2481 kN·m。僅把跨距增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為39.0202 kN·m。邊界：均載簡支單向條帶，連續框架及板效應另驗；不是本工程實測或允收值。原創教學假設：初始壓縮=20 mm；張開量=4 mm；幾何公差=2 mm。c_res=c0−opening−tolerance=14 mm。僅把張開量增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為13.6 mm。邊界：單向幾何餘量，不是接觸壓或水密合格證明；不是本工程實測或允收值。兩組結果的單位與邊界不同，不能直接相加。請列出一項缺少的現場輸入，說明它會影響哪個結論，以及哪種獨立量測可以縮小不確定度。","textEn":"Original integrated review: first calculate rectangular immersed-box frame action, then independently calculate joint compression and sealing envelope. Original teaching assumptions: line load=26 kN/m; span=3.15 m. M=qL²/8=32.2481 kN·m. Increasing only span by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 39.0202 kN·m. Boundary: Uniformly loaded simply supported strip; frame continuity and plate action need separate checks. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Original teaching assumptions: initial compression=20 mm; opening=4 mm; tolerance=2 mm. c_res=c0−opening−tolerance=14 mm. Increasing only opening by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 13.6 mm. Boundary: One-direction geometric reserve, not contact pressure or proof of watertightness. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. The outputs have different units and boundaries and cannot simply be added. Identify one missing field input, explain which conclusion it changes and select an independent measurement to reduce uncertainty.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":14,"enrichmentVersion":14,"stages":[{"id":"b107-v14-s1","title":"地層條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Ground conditions, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「服務邊界與路線代價」與「矩形沉管的框架受力」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\" and \"Rectangular immersed-box frame action\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b107-v14-01","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「路線里程與端點」如何影響費馬恩海峽沉管隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Alignment chainage and endpoints” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Fehmarnbelt immersed tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"費馬恩同時服務道路與鐵路，教學比較先固定兩端接線，分開道路車程、列車時間及施工海域範圍。隧道選線同時改變洞口、覆土與縱坡，短路線不保證低地質風險。比較方案必須使用相同起訖點，並分開主孔、引道及服務坑的工程數量；交通時間只是需求的一個指標，不能代替施工可達性或長期維修評估。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「路線里程與端點」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Because Fehmarnbelt carries road and rail, fix approach endpoints and separate road travel, rail travel and the marine construction boundary. Alignment changes portals, cover and gradient together, so a shorter tunnel need not have lower geological risk. Compare options between identical endpoints and distinguish running bores, approaches and service galleries. Travel time measures one service benefit but cannot replace assessment of construction access, maintenance closures or exposure to uncertain ground. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Alignment chainage and endpoints” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：長度=14.4 km；速度=60 km/h。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: length=14.4 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=14.4 min.","failure":"常見誤解：「最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「路線里程與端點」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Alignment chainage and endpoints”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-01-k1","title":"服務邊界與路線代價","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost","text":"費馬恩同時服務道路與鐵路，教學比較先固定兩端接線，分開道路車程、列車時間及施工海域範圍。隧道選線同時改變洞口、覆土與縱坡，短路線不保證低地質風險。","textEn":"Because Fehmarnbelt carries road and rail, fix approach endpoints and separate road travel, rail travel and the marine construction boundary. Alignment changes portals, cover and gradient together, so a shorter tunnel need not have lower geological risk.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「服務邊界與路線代價」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\" is correct?","options":["最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。","費馬恩同時服務道路與鐵路，教學比較先固定兩端接線，分開道路車程、列車時間及施工海域範圍。","矩形沉管可以直接使用圓環均勻外壓公式設計。"],"optionsEn":["The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.","Because Fehmarnbelt carries road and rail, fix approach endpoints and separate road travel, rail travel and the marine construction boundary.","A rectangular immersed tube can be designed directly with a circular-ring pressure formula."],"answer":1,"explanation":"費馬恩同時服務道路與鐵路，教學比較先固定兩端接線，分開道路車程、列車時間及施工海域範圍。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Because Fehmarnbelt carries road and rail, fix approach endpoints and separate road travel, rail travel and the marine construction boundary. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b107-v14-02","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：定量估算","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「路線里程與端點」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Alignment chainage and endpoints” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：長度=14.4 km；速度=60 km/h。t=60L/v=14.4 min。僅把長度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為15.84 min。邊界：假想交通旅程，未含加減速、排隊及實際時刻表；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: length=14.4 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=14.4 min. Increasing only length by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 15.84 min. Boundary: Hypothetical transport journey excluding acceleration, queues and the real timetable. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對兩種運輸模式各自的端點與速度假設。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check mode-specific endpoints and speed assumptions independently.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：長度=14.4 km；速度=60 km/h。t=60L/v=14.4 min。僅把長度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為15.84 min。邊界：假想交通旅程，未含加減速、排隊及實際時刻表；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: length=14.4 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=14.4 min. Increasing only length by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 15.84 min. Boundary: Hypothetical transport journey excluding acceleration, queues and the real timetable. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「服務邊界與路線代價」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\", which statement holds?","options":["剩餘浮力為正就代表浮運姿態在所有波況穩定。","接縫平均寬度合格就不必量測局部錯台及扭轉。","原創教學假設：長度=14.4 km；速度=60 km/h。"],"optionsEn":["Positive residual buoyancy establishes stability in every sea state.","An acceptable average joint width makes local offset and twist measurements unnecessary.","Original teaching assumptions: length=14.4 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=14.4 min."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：長度=14.4 km；速度=60 km/h。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: length=14.4 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=14.4 min. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b107-v14-03","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「路線里程與端點」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Alignment chainage and endpoints” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對兩種運輸模式各自的端點與速度假設。把縱斷面、地形與地質剖面疊合，以端點坐標獨立反算距離，再將主孔與支坑數量分開核對。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check mode-specific endpoints and speed assumptions independently. Overlay the longitudinal profile, terrain and geology; independently derive distances from endpoint coordinates and reconcile running-bore and gallery quantities separately. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「路線里程與端點」的交付需回答：核對兩種運輸模式各自的端點與速度假設。在方案表中凍結起訖點、計量範圍及地質假設，任何改線都要同步更新高程、數量與服務情境，不能只替換總長。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Fehmarnbelt immersed tunnel, the alignment chainage and endpoints handover must address the following evidence: Check mode-specific endpoints and speed assumptions independently. Freeze endpoints, measurement scope and ground assumptions in the option register; realignment requires coordinated updates to elevations, quantities and service scenarios rather than replacing one length.","failure":"注意干擾：把鐵路節時套到道路會混淆接線與停站條件。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Applying rail time savings to roads mixes approach and stopping conditions. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對兩種運輸模式各自的端點與速度假設。把縱斷面、地形與地質剖面疊合，以端點坐標獨立反算距離，再將主孔與支坑數量分開核對。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Check mode-specific endpoints and speed assumptions independently. Overlay the longitudinal profile, terrain and geology; independently derive distances from endpoint coordinates and reconcile running-bore and gallery quantities separately. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「路線里程與端點」的交付需回答：核對兩種運輸模式各自的端點與速度假設。在方案表中凍結起訖點、計量範圍及地質假設，任何改線都要同步更新高程、數量與服務情境，不能只替換總長。","textEn":"For Fehmarnbelt immersed tunnel, the alignment chainage and endpoints handover must address the following evidence: Check mode-specific endpoints and speed assumptions independently. Freeze endpoints, measurement scope and ground assumptions in the option register; realignment requires coordinated updates to elevations, quantities and service scenarios rather than replacing one length.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「服務邊界與路線代價」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\"?","options":["核對兩種運輸模式各自的端點與速度假設。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","擴散長度就是鋼筋開始腐蝕的位置和精確時間。"],"optionsEn":["Check mode-specific endpoints and speed assumptions independently.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Diffusion length gives the exact location and time of corrosion initiation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"核對兩種運輸模式各自的端點與速度假設。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check mode-specific endpoints and speed assumptions independently. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b107-v14-04","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：失效診斷","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「路線里程與端點」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Alignment chainage and endpoints” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把鐵路節時套到道路會混淆接線與停站條件。混用全線與單孔長度會同時扭曲工程數量、行程及逃生距離，造成方案比較失去共同基準。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Applying rail time savings to roads mixes approach and stopping conditions. Mixing whole-route and single-bore lengths distorts quantities, journey time and escape distance, destroying the common basis of an option comparison. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：比較方案必須使用相同起訖點，並分開主孔、引道及服務坑的工程數量；交通時間只是需求的一個指標，不能代替施工可達性或長期維修評估。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Travel time measures one service benefit but cannot replace assessment of construction access, maintenance closures or exposure to uncertain ground.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把鐵路節時套到道路會混淆接線與停站條件。混用全線與單孔長度會同時扭曲工程數量、行程及逃生距離，造成方案比較失去共同基準。","textEn":"Applying rail time savings to roads mixes approach and stopping conditions. Mixing whole-route and single-bore lengths distorts quantities, journey time and escape distance, destroying the common basis of an option comparison.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「服務邊界與路線代價」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","把鐵路節時套到道路會混淆接線與停站條件。","矩形沉管可以直接使用圓環均勻外壓公式設計。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Applying rail time savings to roads mixes approach and stopping conditions.","A rectangular immersed tube can be designed directly with a circular-ring pressure formula."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把鐵路節時套到道路會混淆接線與停站條件。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Applying rail time savings to roads mixes approach and stopping conditions. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b107-v14-05","title":"矩形沉管的框架受力：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Rectangular immersed-box frame action: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-04"],"objective":"說明「頂板跨中彎矩」如何影響費馬恩海峽沉管隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Roof-span bending” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Fehmarnbelt immersed tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"費馬恩沉管採矩形箱體的教學剖面，研究中牆將頂板分跨後的框架作用，明確排除圓形薄環替代。矩形沉管的頂板、側牆與中牆透過框架連續性傳遞水土壓力，不能套圓形薄環的膜應力。單向簡支條帶只能估計局部彎矩量級；施工浮運、落底、回填和使用期的邊界不同，支承沉陷、接頭剪力及裂縫寬度仍須分階段檢核。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「頂板跨中彎矩」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Use a rectangular immersed-box teaching section and examine how internal walls divide roof spans and create frame action, excluding thin-ring substitution. A rectangular immersed tube transfers water and earth pressure through roof, walls and internal partitions acting as a frame. A circular thin-ring membrane formula is inappropriate. A simply supported strip estimates one bending scale only; flotation, placement, backfill and service change the restraints, requiring staged checks of settlement, joint shear and cracking. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Roof-span bending” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：單位長載重=26 kN/m；跨距=3.15 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: line load=26 kN/m; span=3.15 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「矩形沉管可以直接使用圓環均勻外壓公式設計。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A rectangular immersed tube can be designed directly with a circular-ring pressure formula.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「頂板跨中彎矩」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Roof-span bending”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-05-k1","title":"矩形沉管的框架受力","titleEn":"Rectangular immersed-box frame action","text":"費馬恩沉管採矩形箱體的教學剖面，研究中牆將頂板分跨後的框架作用，明確排除圓形薄環替代。矩形沉管的頂板、側牆與中牆透過框架連續性傳遞水土壓力，不能套圓形薄環的膜應力。","textEn":"Use a rectangular immersed-box teaching section and examine how internal walls divide roof spans and create frame action, excluding thin-ring substitution. A rectangular immersed tube transfers water and earth pressure through roof, walls and internal partitions acting as a frame.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：矩形沉管可以直接使用圓環均勻外壓公式設計。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A rectangular immersed tube can be designed directly with a circular-ring pressure formula. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「矩形沉管的框架受力」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Rectangular immersed-box frame action\" is correct?","options":["矩形沉管可以直接使用圓環均勻外壓公式設計。","混凝土抗壓強度合格就代表厚壁構件不會產生熱裂縫。","費馬恩沉管採矩形箱體的教學剖面，研究中牆將頂板分跨後的框架作用，明確排除圓形薄環替代。"],"optionsEn":["A rectangular immersed tube can be designed directly with a circular-ring pressure formula.","Adequate compressive strength proves that thick concrete cannot develop thermal cracks.","Use a rectangular immersed-box teaching section and examine how internal walls divide roof spans and create frame action, excluding thin-ring substitution."],"answer":2,"explanation":"費馬恩沉管採矩形箱體的教學剖面，研究中牆將頂板分跨後的框架作用，明確排除圓形薄環替代。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Use a rectangular immersed-box teaching section and examine how internal walls divide roof spans and create frame action, excluding thin-ring substitution. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b107-v14-06","title":"矩形沉管的框架受力：定量估算","titleEn":"Rectangular immersed-box frame action: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「頂板跨中彎矩」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Roof-span bending” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：單位長載重=26 kN/m；跨距=3.15 m。M=qL²/8=32.2481 kN·m。僅把跨距增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為39.0202 kN·m。邊界：均載簡支單向條帶，連續框架及板效應另驗；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: line load=26 kN/m; span=3.15 m. M=qL²/8=32.2481 kN·m. Increasing only span by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 39.0202 kN·m. Boundary: Uniformly loaded simply supported strip; frame continuity and plate action need separate checks. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比對中牆剛度變更前後頂板正負彎矩分配。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare positive and negative roof moments before and after changing partition stiffness.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：單位長載重=26 kN/m；跨距=3.15 m。M=qL²/8=32.2481 kN·m。僅把跨距增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為39.0202 kN·m。邊界：均載簡支單向條帶，連續框架及板效應另驗；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: line load=26 kN/m; span=3.15 m. M=qL²/8=32.2481 kN·m. Increasing only span by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 39.0202 kN·m. Boundary: Uniformly loaded simply supported strip; frame continuity and plate action need separate checks. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「矩形沉管的框架受力」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Rectangular immersed-box frame action\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：單位長載重=26 kN/m；跨距=3.15 m。","各管節平均高程接近就能排除接頭差異變形。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: line load=26 kN/m; span=3.15 m.","Similar mean element elevations exclude differential movement at joints.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：單位長載重=26 kN/m；跨距=3.15 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: line load=26 kN/m; span=3.15 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b107-v14-07","title":"矩形沉管的框架受力：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Rectangular immersed-box frame action: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「頂板跨中彎矩」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Roof-span bending” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比對中牆剛度變更前後頂板正負彎矩分配。比對頂板及中牆應變，使用含支承剛度的框架模型核對彎矩分配，將落底前後量測分開。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare positive and negative roof moments before and after changing partition stiffness. Compare roof and partition strain with a frame model including support stiffness, keeping measurements before and after bedding separate. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「頂板跨中彎矩」的交付需回答：比對中牆剛度變更前後頂板正負彎矩分配。把單條帶、整體框架及接頭模型分開提交，標註適用施工階段和受力方向，保留裂縫及水密試驗的獨立判定。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Fehmarnbelt immersed tunnel, the roof-span bending handover must address the following evidence: Compare positive and negative roof moments before and after changing partition stiffness. Submit strip, whole-frame and joint models separately, identifying stage and load direction while retaining independent cracking and watertightness assessments.","failure":"注意干擾：漏列中牆會同時改變跨距、彎矩及接頭反力。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Omitting a partition changes span, bending and joint reactions together. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比對中牆剛度變更前後頂板正負彎矩分配。比對頂板及中牆應變，使用含支承剛度的框架模型核對彎矩分配，將落底前後量測分開。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Compare positive and negative roof moments before and after changing partition stiffness. Compare roof and partition strain with a frame model including support stiffness, keeping measurements before and after bedding separate. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「頂板跨中彎矩」的交付需回答：比對中牆剛度變更前後頂板正負彎矩分配。把單條帶、整體框架及接頭模型分開提交，標註適用施工階段和受力方向，保留裂縫及水密試驗的獨立判定。","textEn":"For Fehmarnbelt immersed tunnel, the roof-span bending handover must address the following evidence: Compare positive and negative roof moments before and after changing partition stiffness. Submit strip, whole-frame and joint models separately, identifying stage and load direction while retaining independent cracking and watertightness assessments.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「矩形沉管的框架受力」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Rectangular immersed-box frame action\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","比對中牆剛度變更前後頂板正負彎矩分配。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Compare positive and negative roof moments before and after changing partition stiffness.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time."],"answer":1,"explanation":"比對中牆剛度變更前後頂板正負彎矩分配。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare positive and negative roof moments before and after changing partition stiffness. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b107-v14-08","title":"矩形沉管的框架受力：失效診斷","titleEn":"Rectangular immersed-box frame action: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「頂板跨中彎矩」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Roof-span bending” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"漏列中牆會同時改變跨距、彎矩及接頭反力。忽略中牆支承或不均勻底床會錯估正負彎矩，局部裂縫可能是邊界變化而非材料強度不足。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Omitting a partition changes span, bending and joint reactions together. Omitting partition support or uneven bedding misallocates positive and negative moments; local cracking may reflect changed restraints rather than weak material. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：單向簡支條帶只能估計局部彎矩量級；施工浮運、落底、回填和使用期的邊界不同，支承沉陷、接頭剪力及裂縫寬度仍須分階段檢核。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A simply supported strip estimates one bending scale only; flotation, placement, backfill and service change the restraints, requiring staged checks of settlement, joint shear and cracking.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「矩形沉管可以直接使用圓環均勻外壓公式設計。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A rectangular immersed tube can be designed directly with a circular-ring pressure formula.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"漏列中牆會同時改變跨距、彎矩及接頭反力。忽略中牆支承或不均勻底床會錯估正負彎矩，局部裂縫可能是邊界變化而非材料強度不足。","textEn":"Omitting a partition changes span, bending and joint reactions together. Omitting partition support or uneven bedding misallocates positive and negative moments; local cracking may reflect changed restraints rather than weak material.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「矩形沉管的框架受力」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Rectangular immersed-box frame action\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","混凝土抗壓強度合格就代表厚壁構件不會產生熱裂縫。","漏列中牆會同時改變跨距、彎矩及接頭反力。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Adequate compressive strength proves that thick concrete cannot develop thermal cracks.","Omitting a partition changes span, bending and joint reactions together."],"answer":2,"explanation":"漏列中牆會同時改變跨距、彎矩及接頭反力。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Omitting a partition changes span, bending and joint reactions together. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b107-v14-s2","title":"機制、材料與定量設計","titleEn":"Mechanisms, materials and quantitative design","description":"本階段聚焦「溫度拘束與構件裂縫」與「浮運重量帳與姿態穩定」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Thermal restraint and component cracking\" and \"Tow-out mass balance and stability\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b107-v14-09","title":"溫度拘束與構件裂縫：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Thermal restraint and component cracking: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-08"],"objective":"說明「拘束溫度應變」如何影響費馬恩海峽沉管隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Restrained thermal strain” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Fehmarnbelt immersed tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"管節量產的混凝土溫度歷程不同於沉放後海水環境，研究早齡拘束與長期降溫的裂縫機制。厚壁構件在水化升溫後冷卻，若相鄰構件或基座限制收縮，熱應變會轉為拉應力。抗壓強度達標不等於抗裂合格，因為彈性模數成熟、徐變、溫度梯度與澆置順序都影響實際拘束；完全拘束彈性估算只能當量級上限比較。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「拘束溫度應變」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Production temperature histories differ from immersed seawater conditions; examine early restraint and later cooling as distinct cracking mechanisms. A thick element cools after hydration, and restraint from adjacent pours or its base converts contraction into tension. Compressive-strength compliance does not establish crack resistance because modulus development, creep, gradients and pour sequence influence restraint. A fully restrained elastic estimate is therefore a scale bound, not a prediction of actual cracking or residual stress. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Restrained thermal strain” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：線膨脹係數=1e-05 K⁻¹；溫差=26 K；彈性模數=25 GPa。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: expansion coefficient=1e-05 K⁻¹; temperature difference=26 K; elastic modulus=25 GPa. σ=EαΔT, GPa→MPa ×1000=6.5 MPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「混凝土抗壓強度合格就代表厚壁構件不會產生熱裂縫。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Adequate compressive strength proves that thick concrete cannot develop thermal cracks.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「拘束溫度應變」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Restrained thermal strain”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-09-k1","title":"溫度拘束與構件裂縫","titleEn":"Thermal restraint and component cracking","text":"管節量產的混凝土溫度歷程不同於沉放後海水環境，研究早齡拘束與長期降溫的裂縫機制。厚壁構件在水化升溫後冷卻，若相鄰構件或基座限制收縮，熱應變會轉為拉應力。","textEn":"Production temperature histories differ from immersed seawater conditions; examine early restraint and later cooling as distinct cracking mechanisms. A thick element cools after hydration, and restraint from adjacent pours or its base converts contraction into tension.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：混凝土抗壓強度合格就代表厚壁構件不會產生熱裂縫。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Adequate compressive strength proves that thick concrete cannot develop thermal cracks. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「溫度拘束與構件裂縫」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Thermal restraint and component cracking\" is correct?","options":["管節量產的混凝土溫度歷程不同於沉放後海水環境，研究早齡拘束與長期降溫的裂縫機制。","混凝土抗壓強度合格就代表厚壁構件不會產生熱裂縫。","剩餘浮力為正就代表浮運姿態在所有波況穩定。"],"optionsEn":["Production temperature histories differ from immersed seawater conditions; examine early restraint and later cooling as distinct cracking mechanisms.","Adequate compressive strength proves that thick concrete cannot develop thermal cracks.","Positive residual buoyancy establishes stability in every sea state."],"answer":0,"explanation":"管節量產的混凝土溫度歷程不同於沉放後海水環境，研究早齡拘束與長期降溫的裂縫機制。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Production temperature histories differ from immersed seawater conditions; examine early restraint and later cooling as distinct cracking mechanisms. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b107-v14-10","title":"溫度拘束與構件裂縫：定量估算","titleEn":"Thermal restraint and component cracking: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「拘束溫度應變」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Restrained thermal strain” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：線膨脹係數=1e-05 K⁻¹；溫差=26 K；彈性模數=25 GPa。σ=EαΔT, GPa→MPa ×1000=6.5 MPa。僅把溫差增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為7.15 MPa。邊界：完全拘束線彈性量級，未含徐變開裂和拘束鬆弛；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: expansion coefficient=1e-05 K⁻¹; temperature difference=26 K; elastic modulus=25 GPa. σ=EαΔT, GPa→MPa ×1000=6.5 MPa. Increasing only temperature difference by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 7.15 MPa. Boundary: Fully restrained linear-elastic scale without creep, cracking or restraint relaxation. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將內外溫度、養護時間與裂縫出現日期對照。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare internal and surface temperatures, curing duration and crack onset.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：線膨脹係數=1e-05 K⁻¹；溫差=26 K；彈性模數=25 GPa。σ=EαΔT, GPa→MPa ×1000=6.5 MPa。僅把溫差增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為7.15 MPa。邊界：完全拘束線彈性量級，未含徐變開裂和拘束鬆弛；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: expansion coefficient=1e-05 K⁻¹; temperature difference=26 K; elastic modulus=25 GPa. σ=EαΔT, GPa→MPa ×1000=6.5 MPa. Increasing only temperature difference by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 7.15 MPa. Boundary: Fully restrained linear-elastic scale without creep, cracking or restraint relaxation. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「溫度拘束與構件裂縫」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Thermal restraint and component cracking\", which statement holds?","options":["接縫平均寬度合格就不必量測局部錯台及扭轉。","原創教學假設：線膨脹係數=1e-05 K⁻¹；溫差=26 K；彈性模數=25 GPa。","擴散長度就是鋼筋開始腐蝕的位置和精確時間。"],"optionsEn":["An acceptable average joint width makes local offset and twist measurements unnecessary.","Original teaching assumptions: expansion coefficient=1e-05 K⁻¹; temperature difference=26 K; elastic modulus=25 GPa. σ=EαΔT, GPa→MPa ×1000=6.5 MPa.","Diffusion length gives the exact location and time of corrosion initiation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：線膨脹係數=1e-05 K⁻¹；溫差=26 K；彈性模數=25 GPa。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: expansion coefficient=1e-05 K⁻¹; temperature difference=26 K; elastic modulus=25 GPa. σ=EαΔT, GPa→MPa ×1000=6.5 MPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b107-v14-11","title":"溫度拘束與構件裂縫：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Thermal restraint and component cracking: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「拘束溫度應變」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Restrained thermal strain” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將內外溫度、養護時間與裂縫出現日期對照。記錄核心表面溫度及同條件試體成熟度，將裂縫位置與溫差、拆模及鄰段澆置時間配對，檢查熱歷程是否被遺漏。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare internal and surface temperatures, curing duration and crack onset. Record core/surface temperature and matched-cured maturity, pairing cracks with temperature differences, formwork removal and adjacent pours to identify missing thermal history. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「拘束溫度應變」的交付需回答：將內外溫度、養護時間與裂縫出現日期對照。澆置前核准溫度監測及養護方案，變更材料、拆模或澆置順序時重新檢查熱分析，將裂縫與接縫止水的責任一併交付。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Fehmarnbelt immersed tunnel, the restrained thermal strain handover must address the following evidence: Compare internal and surface temperatures, curing duration and crack onset. Approve monitoring and curing before pours, revisit thermal analysis after material or sequence changes, and hand over crack and waterstop responsibilities together.","failure":"注意干擾：只用最高溫忽略溫差及拘束，可能誤判裂縫原因。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Peak temperature alone misses gradients and restraint and can misdiagnose cracks. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將內外溫度、養護時間與裂縫出現日期對照。記錄核心表面溫度及同條件試體成熟度，將裂縫位置與溫差、拆模及鄰段澆置時間配對，檢查熱歷程是否被遺漏。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Compare internal and surface temperatures, curing duration and crack onset. Record core/surface temperature and matched-cured maturity, pairing cracks with temperature differences, formwork removal and adjacent pours to identify missing thermal history. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「拘束溫度應變」的交付需回答：將內外溫度、養護時間與裂縫出現日期對照。澆置前核准溫度監測及養護方案，變更材料、拆模或澆置順序時重新檢查熱分析，將裂縫與接縫止水的責任一併交付。","textEn":"For Fehmarnbelt immersed tunnel, the restrained thermal strain handover must address the following evidence: Compare internal and surface temperatures, curing duration and crack onset. Approve monitoring and curing before pours, revisit thermal analysis after material or sequence changes, and hand over crack and waterstop responsibilities together.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「溫度拘束與構件裂縫」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Thermal restraint and component cracking\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。","將內外溫度、養護時間與裂縫出現日期對照。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.","Compare internal and surface temperatures, curing duration and crack onset."],"answer":2,"explanation":"將內外溫度、養護時間與裂縫出現日期對照。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare internal and surface temperatures, curing duration and crack onset. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b107-v14-12","title":"溫度拘束與構件裂縫：失效診斷","titleEn":"Thermal restraint and component cracking: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「拘束溫度應變」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Restrained thermal strain” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只用最高溫忽略溫差及拘束，可能誤判裂縫原因。標準養護試體合格而現場過早冷卻，仍可能形成貫穿裂縫並影響止水；僅增加後續抗壓試驗無法重建失去的養護。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Peak temperature alone misses gradients and restraint and can misdiagnose cracks. Passing standard-cured specimens does not prevent through-cracking after rapid cooling, and more later strength tests cannot reconstruct inadequate curing. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：抗壓強度達標不等於抗裂合格，因為彈性模數成熟、徐變、溫度梯度與澆置順序都影響實際拘束；完全拘束彈性估算只能當量級上限比較。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A fully restrained elastic estimate is therefore a scale bound, not a prediction of actual cracking or residual stress.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「混凝土抗壓強度合格就代表厚壁構件不會產生熱裂縫。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Adequate compressive strength proves that thick concrete cannot develop thermal cracks.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只用最高溫忽略溫差及拘束，可能誤判裂縫原因。標準養護試體合格而現場過早冷卻，仍可能形成貫穿裂縫並影響止水；僅增加後續抗壓試驗無法重建失去的養護。","textEn":"Peak temperature alone misses gradients and restraint and can misdiagnose cracks. Passing standard-cured specimens does not prevent through-cracking after rapid cooling, and more later strength tests cannot reconstruct inadequate curing.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「溫度拘束與構件裂縫」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Thermal restraint and component cracking\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["只用最高溫忽略溫差及拘束，可能誤判裂縫原因。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","剩餘浮力為正就代表浮運姿態在所有波況穩定。"],"optionsEn":["Peak temperature alone misses gradients and restraint and can misdiagnose cracks.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Positive residual buoyancy establishes stability in every sea state."],"answer":0,"explanation":"只用最高溫忽略溫差及拘束，可能誤判裂縫原因。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Peak temperature alone misses gradients and restraint and can misdiagnose cracks. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b107-v14-13","title":"浮運重量帳與姿態穩定：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Tow-out mass balance and stability: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-12"],"objective":"說明「剩餘浮力」如何影響費馬恩海峽沉管隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Residual buoyancy” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Fehmarnbelt immersed tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"費馬恩浮運教學情境把臨時封端、壓載和設備納入重量帳，研究同總質量但不同重心的差異。浮力由排開水體重量決定，總質量還包含設備、臨時封端及艙內液體。重量帳只能判定淨垂直力，不能證明浮運穩定；壓載液自由表面、重心位置、拖纜與波浪都會改變傾斜反應，落底接觸亦需另建模型。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「剩餘浮力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Include temporary bulkheads, ballast and equipment in tow-out mass accounting and compare equal masses with different centres of gravity. Buoyancy equals displaced water weight, while total mass includes equipment, temporary bulkheads and liquid contents. A mass balance determines net vertical force but does not establish towing stability. Ballast free surfaces, centre of gravity, tow lines and waves affect heel response, and initial contact with the bed needs another model. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Residual buoyancy” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：水密度=1025 kg/m³；排水體積=11200 m³；總質量=1.11356e+07 kg。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: water density=1025 kg/m³; displacement=11200 m³; mass=1.11356e+07 kg.","failure":"常見誤解：「剩餘浮力為正就代表浮運姿態在所有波況穩定。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Positive residual buoyancy establishes stability in every sea state.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「剩餘浮力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Residual buoyancy”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-13-k1","title":"浮運重量帳與姿態穩定","titleEn":"Tow-out mass balance and stability","text":"費馬恩浮運教學情境把臨時封端、壓載和設備納入重量帳，研究同總質量但不同重心的差異。浮力由排開水體重量決定，總質量還包含設備、臨時封端及艙內液體。","textEn":"Include temporary bulkheads, ballast and equipment in tow-out mass accounting and compare equal masses with different centres of gravity. Buoyancy equals displaced water weight, while total mass includes equipment, temporary bulkheads and liquid contents.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：剩餘浮力為正就代表浮運姿態在所有波況穩定。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Positive residual buoyancy establishes stability in every sea state. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「浮運重量帳與姿態穩定」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Tow-out mass balance and stability\" is correct?","options":["剩餘浮力為正就代表浮運姿態在所有波況穩定。","費馬恩浮運教學情境把臨時封端、壓載和設備納入重量帳，研究同總質量但不同重心的差異。","各管節平均高程接近就能排除接頭差異變形。"],"optionsEn":["Positive residual buoyancy establishes stability in every sea state.","Include temporary bulkheads, ballast and equipment in tow-out mass accounting and compare equal masses with different centres of gravity.","Similar mean element elevations exclude differential movement at joints."],"answer":1,"explanation":"費馬恩浮運教學情境把臨時封端、壓載和設備納入重量帳，研究同總質量但不同重心的差異。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Include temporary bulkheads, ballast and equipment in tow-out mass accounting and compare equal masses with different centres of gravity. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b107-v14-14","title":"浮運重量帳與姿態穩定：定量估算","titleEn":"Tow-out mass balance and stability: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「剩餘浮力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Residual buoyancy” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：水密度=1025 kg/m³；排水體積=11200 m³；總質量=1.11356e+07 kg。R=(ρV−m)g/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=3378.56 kN。僅把排水體積增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為14640.4 kN。邊界：靜水剩餘浮力，不驗證傾斜穩性及自由液面；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: water density=1025 kg/m³; displacement=11200 m³; mass=1.11356e+07 kg. R=(ρV−m)g/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=3378.56 kN. Increasing only displacement by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 14640.4 kN. Boundary: Still-water buoyancy reserve, not heel stability or free-surface verification. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以吃水與艙內液位回查清冊，另查自由液面。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use draught and tank levels to reconcile the register and separately assess free surfaces.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：水密度=1025 kg/m³；排水體積=11200 m³；總質量=1.11356e+07 kg。R=(ρV−m)g/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=3378.56 kN。僅把排水體積增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為14640.4 kN。邊界：靜水剩餘浮力，不驗證傾斜穩性及自由液面；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: water density=1025 kg/m³; displacement=11200 m³; mass=1.11356e+07 kg. R=(ρV−m)g/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=3378.56 kN. Increasing only displacement by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 14640.4 kN. Boundary: Still-water buoyancy reserve, not heel stability or free-surface verification. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「浮運重量帳與姿態穩定」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Tow-out mass balance and stability\", which statement holds?","options":["兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。","原創教學假設：水密度=1025 kg/m³；排水體積=11200 m³；總質量=1.11356e+07 kg。"],"optionsEn":["Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.","Original teaching assumptions: water density=1025 kg/m³; displacement=11200 m³; mass=1.11356e+07 kg."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：水密度=1025 kg/m³；排水體積=11200 m³；總質量=1.11356e+07 kg。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: water density=1025 kg/m³; displacement=11200 m³; mass=1.11356e+07 kg. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b107-v14-15","title":"浮運重量帳與姿態穩定：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Tow-out mass balance and stability: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「剩餘浮力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Residual buoyancy” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以吃水與艙內液位回查清冊，另查自由液面。以實際重量清冊和吃水測量互核，量測液艙水位及橫傾，檢查密度與體積是否採同一狀態。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use draught and tank levels to reconcile the register and separately assess free surfaces. Reconcile an itemised mass register with draught measurements, tank levels and heel, checking that density and displaced volume describe the same state. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「剩餘浮力」的交付需回答：以吃水與艙內液位回查清冊，另查自由液面。質量清冊每次變更都重新確認重心和吃水，操作窗口依核准海事方案及量測決定，不由本課靜力式制定。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Fehmarnbelt immersed tunnel, the residual buoyancy handover must address the following evidence: Use draught and tank levels to reconcile the register and separately assess free surfaces. Update centre of gravity and draught after every mass-register change; approved marine procedures and observations determine operating windows, not this static classroom equation.","failure":"注意干擾：只增壓載而未評估偏心，可能改善重量帳卻惡化橫傾。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Added eccentric ballast can improve mass balance while worsening heel. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以吃水與艙內液位回查清冊，另查自由液面。以實際重量清冊和吃水測量互核，量測液艙水位及橫傾，檢查密度與體積是否採同一狀態。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Use draught and tank levels to reconcile the register and separately assess free surfaces. Reconcile an itemised mass register with draught measurements, tank levels and heel, checking that density and displaced volume describe the same state. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「剩餘浮力」的交付需回答：以吃水與艙內液位回查清冊，另查自由液面。質量清冊每次變更都重新確認重心和吃水，操作窗口依核准海事方案及量測決定，不由本課靜力式制定。","textEn":"For Fehmarnbelt immersed tunnel, the residual buoyancy handover must address the following evidence: Use draught and tank levels to reconcile the register and separately assess free surfaces. Update centre of gravity and draught after every mass-register change; approved marine procedures and observations determine operating windows, not this static classroom equation.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「浮運重量帳與姿態穩定」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Tow-out mass balance and stability\"?","options":["以吃水與艙內液位回查清冊，另查自由液面。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Use draught and tank levels to reconcile the register and separately assess free surfaces.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以吃水與艙內液位回查清冊，另查自由液面。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use draught and tank levels to reconcile the register and separately assess free surfaces. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b107-v14-16","title":"浮運重量帳與姿態穩定：失效診斷","titleEn":"Tow-out mass balance and stability: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「剩餘浮力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Residual buoyancy” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只增壓載而未評估偏心，可能改善重量帳卻惡化橫傾。漏列臨時設備或自由液面會使浮力帳看似足夠卻缺乏回正能力，偏載也可能先造成局部接觸。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Added eccentric ballast can improve mass balance while worsening heel. Missing temporary equipment or free-surface effects can leave an apparently adequate buoyancy balance with insufficient restoring capacity and premature local contact. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：重量帳只能判定淨垂直力，不能證明浮運穩定；壓載液自由表面、重心位置、拖纜與波浪都會改變傾斜反應，落底接觸亦需另建模型。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Ballast free surfaces, centre of gravity, tow lines and waves affect heel response, and initial contact with the bed needs another model.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「剩餘浮力為正就代表浮運姿態在所有波況穩定。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Positive residual buoyancy establishes stability in every sea state.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只增壓載而未評估偏心，可能改善重量帳卻惡化橫傾。漏列臨時設備或自由液面會使浮力帳看似足夠卻缺乏回正能力，偏載也可能先造成局部接觸。","textEn":"Added eccentric ballast can improve mass balance while worsening heel. Missing temporary equipment or free-surface effects can leave an apparently adequate buoyancy balance with insufficient restoring capacity and premature local contact.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「浮運重量帳與姿態穩定」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Tow-out mass balance and stability\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","只增壓載而未評估偏心，可能改善重量帳卻惡化橫傾。","各管節平均高程接近就能排除接頭差異變形。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Added eccentric ballast can improve mass balance while worsening heel.","Similar mean element elevations exclude differential movement at joints."],"answer":1,"explanation":"只增壓載而未評估偏心，可能改善重量帳卻惡化橫傾。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Added eccentric ballast can improve mass balance while worsening heel. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b107-v14-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「基床變形與接頭轉角」與「接頭壓縮與水密包絡」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Bedding movement and joint rotation\" and \"Joint compression and sealing envelope\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b107-v14-17","title":"基床變形與接頭轉角：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Bedding movement and joint rotation: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-16"],"objective":"說明「差異沉陷梯度」如何影響費馬恩海峽沉管隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Differential settlement gradient” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Fehmarnbelt immersed tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"海床整平和後續回填決定沉管支承，費馬恩情境須把落底瞬間與長期固結分開。沉管基床將箱體荷載傳給海床，局部沖刷、回填不均與軟弱層固結會改變接觸分布。總沉陷小不代表接頭轉角小；相鄰管節的差異位移和支承長度才控制局部變形，施工量測須保留時間與潮位基準。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「差異沉陷梯度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Seabed preparation and backfill determine support; distinguish first contact from long-term consolidation in the Fehmarnbelt setting. The bed transfers tube load into the seabed, and scour, uneven backfill or consolidation alter contact. Small total settlement does not imply small joint rotation; differential movement and support length control local distortion. Construction observations must preserve time and tidal datum because immediate placement and delayed consolidation describe different mechanisms. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Differential settlement gradient” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：差異沉陷=6 mm；基線長度=140 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: differential settlement=6 mm; baseline=140 m. β=Δs/L=0.0428571 mm/m.","failure":"常見誤解：「各管節平均高程接近就能排除接頭差異變形。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Similar mean element elevations exclude differential movement at joints.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「差異沉陷梯度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Differential settlement gradient”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-17-k1","title":"基床變形與接頭轉角","titleEn":"Bedding movement and joint rotation","text":"海床整平和後續回填決定沉管支承，費馬恩情境須把落底瞬間與長期固結分開。沉管基床將箱體荷載傳給海床，局部沖刷、回填不均與軟弱層固結會改變接觸分布。","textEn":"Seabed preparation and backfill determine support; distinguish first contact from long-term consolidation in the Fehmarnbelt setting. The bed transfers tube load into the seabed, and scour, uneven backfill or consolidation alter contact.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：各管節平均高程接近就能排除接頭差異變形。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Similar mean element elevations exclude differential movement at joints. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「基床變形與接頭轉角」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Bedding movement and joint rotation\" is correct?","options":["各管節平均高程接近就能排除接頭差異變形。","接縫平均寬度合格就不必量測局部錯台及扭轉。","海床整平和後續回填決定沉管支承，費馬恩情境須把落底瞬間與長期固結分開。"],"optionsEn":["Similar mean element elevations exclude differential movement at joints.","An acceptable average joint width makes local offset and twist measurements unnecessary.","Seabed preparation and backfill determine support; distinguish first contact from long-term consolidation in the Fehmarnbelt setting."],"answer":2,"explanation":"海床整平和後續回填決定沉管支承，費馬恩情境須把落底瞬間與長期固結分開。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Seabed preparation and backfill determine support; distinguish first contact from long-term consolidation in the Fehmarnbelt setting. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b107-v14-18","title":"基床變形與接頭轉角：定量估算","titleEn":"Bedding movement and joint rotation: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「差異沉陷梯度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Differential settlement gradient” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：差異沉陷=6 mm；基線長度=140 m。β=Δs/L=0.0428571 mm/m。僅把差異沉陷增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.0471429 mm/m。邊界：小變形角變化指標，不是完整固結解；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: differential settlement=6 mm; baseline=140 m. β=Δs/L=0.0428571 mm/m. Increasing only differential settlement by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.0471429 mm/m. Boundary: Small-deformation angular-distortion indicator, not a consolidation solution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：配對海床測深、管節高程及回填時序。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Pair bathymetry, element elevation and backfill chronology.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：差異沉陷=6 mm；基線長度=140 m。β=Δs/L=0.0428571 mm/m。僅把差異沉陷增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.0471429 mm/m。邊界：小變形角變化指標，不是完整固結解；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: differential settlement=6 mm; baseline=140 m. β=Δs/L=0.0428571 mm/m. Increasing only differential settlement by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.0471429 mm/m. Boundary: Small-deformation angular-distortion indicator, not a consolidation solution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「基床變形與接頭轉角」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Bedding movement and joint rotation\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：差異沉陷=6 mm；基線長度=140 m。","擴散長度就是鋼筋開始腐蝕的位置和精確時間。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: differential settlement=6 mm; baseline=140 m. β=Δs/L=0.0428571 mm/m.","Diffusion length gives the exact location and time of corrosion initiation.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：差異沉陷=6 mm；基線長度=140 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: differential settlement=6 mm; baseline=140 m. β=Δs/L=0.0428571 mm/m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b107-v14-19","title":"基床變形與接頭轉角：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Bedding movement and joint rotation: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「差異沉陷梯度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Differential settlement gradient” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"配對海床測深、管節高程及回填時序。用管節水準網、海床剖面及孔壓變化交叉核對，將整體下沉與相鄰節轉角分開評估。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Pair bathymetry, element elevation and backfill chronology. Cross-check tube levelling, seabed profiles and pore-pressure change, separating overall settlement from rotation between neighbouring elements. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「差異沉陷梯度」的交付需回答：配對海床測深、管節高程及回填時序。將基床施工紀錄與長期水準資料連結至管節編號，差異變形先查基準和孔壓，再由設計者判斷接觸及接頭。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Fehmarnbelt immersed tunnel, the differential settlement gradient handover must address the following evidence: Pair bathymetry, element elevation and backfill chronology. Link bedding records and long-term levelling to element identifiers; check datum and pore pressure before designers interpret contact and joint behaviour.","failure":"注意干擾：落底後高程穩定不保證軟弱層固結已結束。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Stable elevation immediately after placement does not establish completed consolidation. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"配對海床測深、管節高程及回填時序。用管節水準網、海床剖面及孔壓變化交叉核對，將整體下沉與相鄰節轉角分開評估。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Pair bathymetry, element elevation and backfill chronology. Cross-check tube levelling, seabed profiles and pore-pressure change, separating overall settlement from rotation between neighbouring elements. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「差異沉陷梯度」的交付需回答：配對海床測深、管節高程及回填時序。將基床施工紀錄與長期水準資料連結至管節編號，差異變形先查基準和孔壓，再由設計者判斷接觸及接頭。","textEn":"For Fehmarnbelt immersed tunnel, the differential settlement gradient handover must address the following evidence: Pair bathymetry, element elevation and backfill chronology. Link bedding records and long-term levelling to element identifiers; check datum and pore pressure before designers interpret contact and joint behaviour.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「基床變形與接頭轉角」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Bedding movement and joint rotation\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","配對海床測深、管節高程及回填時序。","矩形沉管可以直接使用圓環均勻外壓公式設計。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Pair bathymetry, element elevation and backfill chronology.","A rectangular immersed tube can be designed directly with a circular-ring pressure formula."],"answer":1,"explanation":"配對海床測深、管節高程及回填時序。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Pair bathymetry, element elevation and backfill chronology. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b107-v14-20","title":"基床變形與接頭轉角：失效診斷","titleEn":"Bedding movement and joint rotation: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「差異沉陷梯度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Differential settlement gradient” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"落底後高程穩定不保證軟弱層固結已結束。只追蹤平均高程可能漏掉單側失去支承，接頭剪力與止水錯台會先於明顯整體下沉增加。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Stable elevation immediately after placement does not establish completed consolidation. Mean elevation can conceal loss of support on one side, allowing joint shear and gasket offset to grow before obvious overall settlement. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：總沉陷小不代表接頭轉角小；相鄰管節的差異位移和支承長度才控制局部變形，施工量測須保留時間與潮位基準。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Construction observations must preserve time and tidal datum because immediate placement and delayed consolidation describe different mechanisms.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「各管節平均高程接近就能排除接頭差異變形。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Similar mean element elevations exclude differential movement at joints.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"落底後高程穩定不保證軟弱層固結已結束。只追蹤平均高程可能漏掉單側失去支承，接頭剪力與止水錯台會先於明顯整體下沉增加。","textEn":"Stable elevation immediately after placement does not establish completed consolidation. Mean elevation can conceal loss of support on one side, allowing joint shear and gasket offset to grow before obvious overall settlement.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「基床變形與接頭轉角」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Bedding movement and joint rotation\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","接縫平均寬度合格就不必量測局部錯台及扭轉。","落底後高程穩定不保證軟弱層固結已結束。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","An acceptable average joint width makes local offset and twist measurements unnecessary.","Stable elevation immediately after placement does not establish completed consolidation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"落底後高程穩定不保證軟弱層固結已結束。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Stable elevation immediately after placement does not establish completed consolidation. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b107-v14-21","title":"接頭壓縮與水密包絡：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Joint compression and sealing envelope: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-20"],"objective":"說明「止水壓縮餘量」如何影響費馬恩海峽沉管隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Gasket compression reserve” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Fehmarnbelt immersed tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"連續沉放多管節時，接頭累積方向偏差和局部止水壓縮不同，研究幾何誤差如何傳到最末接合。止水條依受控壓縮維持連續接觸，接縫轉角、錯台、污染與材料鬆弛都會降低最不利點的接觸能力。平均壓縮量不能掩蓋局部脫離；全尺寸試驗的結果只對測試過的幾何、水壓及荷載歷程有效，幾何餘量本身並不是接觸壓力。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「止水壓縮餘量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Across many immersed elements, accumulated alignment error and local gasket compression differ; trace geometry into the final closure. A gasket seals through controlled continuous compression; rotation, offset, contamination and relaxation reduce contact at the weakest point. Average compression cannot compensate for local separation. Full-size test results apply only to their tested geometry, head and load history, while a calculated geometric reserve is neither contact pressure nor evidence of watertightness. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Gasket compression reserve” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：初始壓縮=20 mm；張開量=4 mm；幾何公差=2 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: initial compression=20 mm; opening=4 mm; tolerance=2 mm. c_res=c0−opening−tolerance=14 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「接縫平均寬度合格就不必量測局部錯台及扭轉。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"An acceptable average joint width makes local offset and twist measurements unnecessary.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「止水壓縮餘量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Gasket compression reserve”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-21-k1","title":"接頭壓縮與水密包絡","titleEn":"Joint compression and sealing envelope","text":"連續沉放多管節時，接頭累積方向偏差和局部止水壓縮不同，研究幾何誤差如何傳到最末接合。止水條依受控壓縮維持連續接觸，接縫轉角、錯台、污染與材料鬆弛都會降低最不利點的接觸能力。","textEn":"Across many immersed elements, accumulated alignment error and local gasket compression differ; trace geometry into the final closure. A gasket seals through controlled continuous compression; rotation, offset, contamination and relaxation reduce contact at the weakest point.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：接縫平均寬度合格就不必量測局部錯台及扭轉。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: An acceptable average joint width makes local offset and twist measurements unnecessary. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「接頭壓縮與水密包絡」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Joint compression and sealing envelope\" is correct?","options":["連續沉放多管節時，接頭累積方向偏差和局部止水壓縮不同，研究幾何誤差如何傳到最末接合。","接縫平均寬度合格就不必量測局部錯台及扭轉。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Across many immersed elements, accumulated alignment error and local gasket compression differ; trace geometry into the final closure.","An acceptable average joint width makes local offset and twist measurements unnecessary.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error."],"answer":0,"explanation":"連續沉放多管節時，接頭累積方向偏差和局部止水壓縮不同，研究幾何誤差如何傳到最末接合。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Across many immersed elements, accumulated alignment error and local gasket compression differ; trace geometry into the final closure. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b107-v14-22","title":"接頭壓縮與水密包絡：定量估算","titleEn":"Joint compression and sealing envelope: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「止水壓縮餘量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Gasket compression reserve” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：初始壓縮=20 mm；張開量=4 mm；幾何公差=2 mm。c_res=c0−opening−tolerance=14 mm。僅把張開量增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為13.6 mm。邊界：單向幾何餘量，不是接觸壓或水密合格證明；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: initial compression=20 mm; opening=4 mm; tolerance=2 mm. c_res=c0−opening−tolerance=14 mm. Increasing only opening by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 13.6 mm. Boundary: One-direction geometric reserve, not contact pressure or proof of watertightness. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：分開核對全線坐標與每個接頭的錯台和壓縮。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check whole-route coordinates separately from joint offset and compression.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：初始壓縮=20 mm；張開量=4 mm；幾何公差=2 mm。c_res=c0−opening−tolerance=14 mm。僅把張開量增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為13.6 mm。邊界：單向幾何餘量，不是接觸壓或水密合格證明；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: initial compression=20 mm; opening=4 mm; tolerance=2 mm. c_res=c0−opening−tolerance=14 mm. Increasing only opening by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 13.6 mm. Boundary: One-direction geometric reserve, not contact pressure or proof of watertightness. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「接頭壓縮與水密包絡」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Joint compression and sealing envelope\", which statement holds?","options":["只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。","原創教學假設：初始壓縮=20 mm；張開量=4 mm；幾何公差=2 mm。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.","Original teaching assumptions: initial compression=20 mm; opening=4 mm; tolerance=2 mm. c_res=c0−opening−tolerance=14 mm.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：初始壓縮=20 mm；張開量=4 mm；幾何公差=2 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: initial compression=20 mm; opening=4 mm; tolerance=2 mm. c_res=c0−opening−tolerance=14 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b107-v14-23","title":"接頭壓縮與水密包絡：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Joint compression and sealing envelope: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「止水壓縮餘量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Gasket compression reserve” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"分開核對全線坐標與每個接頭的錯台和壓縮。全尺寸接頭試驗分別改變張開、錯台與外水壓，記錄漏水起點與卸載後殘餘位移，對照材料批次及溫度。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check whole-route coordinates separately from joint offset and compression. Vary opening, offset and pressure in full-size joint tests, recording leakage onset and residual movement against material batch and temperature. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「止水壓縮餘量」的交付需回答：分開核對全線坐標與每個接頭的錯台和壓縮。保存接縫幾何與試驗壓力的配對紀錄，由設計者核定允收包絡；驗收時不能把課堂的幾何餘量當產品認證數字。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Fehmarnbelt immersed tunnel, the gasket compression reserve handover must address the following evidence: Check whole-route coordinates separately from joint offset and compression. Retain paired joint geometry and test pressure, with the designer approving the acceptance envelope; classroom geometric reserves are not product certification values.","failure":"注意干擾：全線位置正確仍可能有局部扭轉造成接頭漏水。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Correct overall alignment can coexist with local twist and joint leakage. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"分開核對全線坐標與每個接頭的錯台和壓縮。全尺寸接頭試驗分別改變張開、錯台與外水壓，記錄漏水起點與卸載後殘餘位移，對照材料批次及溫度。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Check whole-route coordinates separately from joint offset and compression. Vary opening, offset and pressure in full-size joint tests, recording leakage onset and residual movement against material batch and temperature. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「止水壓縮餘量」的交付需回答：分開核對全線坐標與每個接頭的錯台和壓縮。保存接縫幾何與試驗壓力的配對紀錄，由設計者核定允收包絡；驗收時不能把課堂的幾何餘量當產品認證數字。","textEn":"For Fehmarnbelt immersed tunnel, the gasket compression reserve handover must address the following evidence: Check whole-route coordinates separately from joint offset and compression. Retain paired joint geometry and test pressure, with the designer approving the acceptance envelope; classroom geometric reserves are not product certification values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「接頭壓縮與水密包絡」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Joint compression and sealing envelope\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","混凝土抗壓強度合格就代表厚壁構件不會產生熱裂縫。","分開核對全線坐標與每個接頭的錯台和壓縮。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Adequate compressive strength proves that thick concrete cannot develop thermal cracks.","Check whole-route coordinates separately from joint offset and compression."],"answer":2,"explanation":"分開核對全線坐標與每個接頭的錯台和壓縮。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check whole-route coordinates separately from joint offset and compression. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b107-v14-24","title":"接頭壓縮與水密包絡：失效診斷","titleEn":"Joint compression and sealing envelope: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「止水壓縮餘量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Gasket compression reserve” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"全線位置正確仍可能有局部扭轉造成接頭漏水。扭曲或沾污的止水條可形成旁通通道，即使平均縫寬合格仍可能漏水；盲目灌漿也可能只轉移出水位置。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Correct overall alignment can coexist with local twist and joint leakage. A twisted or contaminated gasket creates bypass leakage despite acceptable mean width; indiscriminate grouting may merely move the outlet. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：平均壓縮量不能掩蓋局部脫離；全尺寸試驗的結果只對測試過的幾何、水壓及荷載歷程有效，幾何餘量本身並不是接觸壓力。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Full-size test results apply only to their tested geometry, head and load history, while a calculated geometric reserve is neither contact pressure nor evidence of watertightness.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「接縫平均寬度合格就不必量測局部錯台及扭轉。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"An acceptable average joint width makes local offset and twist measurements unnecessary.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"全線位置正確仍可能有局部扭轉造成接頭漏水。扭曲或沾污的止水條可形成旁通通道，即使平均縫寬合格仍可能漏水；盲目灌漿也可能只轉移出水位置。","textEn":"Correct overall alignment can coexist with local twist and joint leakage. A twisted or contaminated gasket creates bypass leakage despite acceptable mean width; indiscriminate grouting may merely move the outlet.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「接頭壓縮與水密包絡」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Joint compression and sealing envelope\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["全線位置正確仍可能有局部扭轉造成接頭漏水。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Correct overall alignment can coexist with local twist and joint leakage.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error."],"answer":0,"explanation":"全線位置正確仍可能有局部扭轉造成接頭漏水。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Correct overall alignment can coexist with local twist and joint leakage. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b107-v14-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「控制網與貫通誤差」與「氯鹽遷移與耐久判讀」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Control network and breakthrough error\" and \"Chloride transport and durability interpretation\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b107-v14-25","title":"控制網與貫通誤差：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-24"],"objective":"說明「方向角誤差」如何影響費馬恩海峽沉管隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Orientation error” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Fehmarnbelt immersed tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"海上定位、岸上控制與水下落底量測必須統一基準，教學中辨認潮位改正與姿態的耦合。長隧道的微小方向誤差會沿距離累積，地下控制網又缺少直接衛星定位，必須把地表基準可靠傳到洞內。閉合差很小不代表無系統誤差；尺度、折光、儀器定向與高程基準可能共同偏移，誤差相關性也使平方和估算失真。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「方向角誤差」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Marine positioning, shore control and underwater placement measurements need one reference; distinguish tidal correction from element attitude. Small orientation errors accumulate over long drives, while underground networks lack direct satellite positioning and depend on transferring surface control. A small closure does not exclude systematic bias: scale, refraction, orientation and vertical datum may shift together. Correlated errors also invalidate a naive root-sum-square combination of supposedly independent observations. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Orientation error” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：控制長度=3720 m；方向偏角=2.6 arcsec。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: control length=3720 m; orientation error=2.6 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0468912 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「方向角誤差」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Orientation error”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-25-k1","title":"控制網與貫通誤差","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error","text":"海上定位、岸上控制與水下落底量測必須統一基準，教學中辨認潮位改正與姿態的耦合。長隧道的微小方向誤差會沿距離累積，地下控制網又缺少直接衛星定位，必須把地表基準可靠傳到洞內。","textEn":"Marine positioning, shore control and underwater placement measurements need one reference; distinguish tidal correction from element attitude. Small orientation errors accumulate over long drives, while underground networks lack direct satellite positioning and depend on transferring surface control.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「控制網與貫通誤差」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Control network and breakthrough error\" is correct?","options":["兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。","海上定位、岸上控制與水下落底量測必須統一基準，教學中辨認潮位改正與姿態的耦合。","擴散長度就是鋼筋開始腐蝕的位置和精確時間。"],"optionsEn":["Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.","Marine positioning, shore control and underwater placement measurements need one reference; distinguish tidal correction from element attitude.","Diffusion length gives the exact location and time of corrosion initiation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"海上定位、岸上控制與水下落底量測必須統一基準，教學中辨認潮位改正與姿態的耦合。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Marine positioning, shore control and underwater placement measurements need one reference; distinguish tidal correction from element attitude. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b107-v14-26","title":"控制網與貫通誤差：定量估算","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「方向角誤差」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Orientation error” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：控制長度=3720 m；方向偏角=2.6 arcsec。e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0468912 m。僅把方向偏角增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.0515803 m。邊界：小角度方向偏差，未加入控制網相關性及折光；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: control length=3720 m; orientation error=2.6 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0468912 m. Increasing only orientation error by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.0515803 m. Boundary: Small-angle orientation error without network correlation or refraction. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用獨立岸基控制和姿態量測檢查水下位置。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check underwater position with independent shore control and attitude measurements.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：控制長度=3720 m；方向偏角=2.6 arcsec。e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0468912 m。僅把方向偏角增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.0515803 m。邊界：小角度方向偏差，未加入控制網相關性及折光；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: control length=3720 m; orientation error=2.6 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0468912 m. Increasing only orientation error by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.0515803 m. Boundary: Small-angle orientation error without network correlation or refraction. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「控制網與貫通誤差」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Control network and breakthrough error\", which statement holds?","options":["全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。","矩形沉管可以直接使用圓環均勻外壓公式設計。","原創教學假設：控制長度=3720 m；方向偏角=2.6 arcsec。"],"optionsEn":["Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.","A rectangular immersed tube can be designed directly with a circular-ring pressure formula.","Original teaching assumptions: control length=3720 m; orientation error=2.6 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0468912 m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：控制長度=3720 m；方向偏角=2.6 arcsec。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: control length=3720 m; orientation error=2.6 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0468912 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b107-v14-27","title":"控制網與貫通誤差：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「方向角誤差」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Orientation error” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用獨立岸基控制和姿態量測檢查水下位置。由獨立測量組複核地表到洞內的轉換，保留原始角距及溫度資料，用不同控制線比較方向與高程偏差。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check underwater position with independent shore control and attitude measurements. Independently check surface-to-tunnel transformations, retain raw angles, distances and temperatures, and compare orientation and elevation through separate control routes. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「方向角誤差」的交付需回答：用獨立岸基控制和姿態量測檢查水下位置。貫通前凍結座標、尺度與高程版本，獨立組直接使用原始觀測重算；不得只傳遞整理好的坐標而遺失校正資訊。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Fehmarnbelt immersed tunnel, the orientation error handover must address the following evidence: Check underwater position with independent shore control and attitude measurements. Freeze coordinate, scale and height revisions before breakthrough; independent reviewers recompute raw observations rather than receiving only adjusted coordinates without corrections.","failure":"注意干擾：潮位基準誤差可使多個管節共同偏高而相互吻合。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A tidal-datum bias can place several mutually aligned elements at the wrong elevation. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用獨立岸基控制和姿態量測檢查水下位置。由獨立測量組複核地表到洞內的轉換，保留原始角距及溫度資料，用不同控制線比較方向與高程偏差。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Check underwater position with independent shore control and attitude measurements. Independently check surface-to-tunnel transformations, retain raw angles, distances and temperatures, and compare orientation and elevation through separate control routes. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「方向角誤差」的交付需回答：用獨立岸基控制和姿態量測檢查水下位置。貫通前凍結座標、尺度與高程版本，獨立組直接使用原始觀測重算；不得只傳遞整理好的坐標而遺失校正資訊。","textEn":"For Fehmarnbelt immersed tunnel, the orientation error handover must address the following evidence: Check underwater position with independent shore control and attitude measurements. Freeze coordinate, scale and height revisions before breakthrough; independent reviewers recompute raw observations rather than receiving only adjusted coordinates without corrections.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「控制網與貫通誤差」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Control network and breakthrough error\"?","options":["用獨立岸基控制和姿態量測檢查水下位置。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","剩餘浮力為正就代表浮運姿態在所有波況穩定。"],"optionsEn":["Check underwater position with independent shore control and attitude measurements.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Positive residual buoyancy establishes stability in every sea state."],"answer":0,"explanation":"用獨立岸基控制和姿態量測檢查水下位置。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check underwater position with independent shore control and attitude measurements. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b107-v14-28","title":"控制網與貫通誤差：失效診斷","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「方向角誤差」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Orientation error” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"潮位基準誤差可使多個管節共同偏高而相互吻合。共用錯誤基準可能讓兩組測量同時看似一致，直到貫通或軌道銜接才發現系統偏差，修正成本遠高於早期複核。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A tidal-datum bias can place several mutually aligned elements at the wrong elevation. A shared wrong datum can make separate surveys appear consistent until breakthrough or track connection exposes bias that is costly to correct. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：閉合差很小不代表無系統誤差；尺度、折光、儀器定向與高程基準可能共同偏移，誤差相關性也使平方和估算失真。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Correlated errors also invalidate a naive root-sum-square combination of supposedly independent observations.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"潮位基準誤差可使多個管節共同偏高而相互吻合。共用錯誤基準可能讓兩組測量同時看似一致，直到貫通或軌道銜接才發現系統偏差，修正成本遠高於早期複核。","textEn":"A tidal-datum bias can place several mutually aligned elements at the wrong elevation. A shared wrong datum can make separate surveys appear consistent until breakthrough or track connection exposes bias that is costly to correct.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「控制網與貫通誤差」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Control network and breakthrough error\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","潮位基準誤差可使多個管節共同偏高而相互吻合。","擴散長度就是鋼筋開始腐蝕的位置和精確時間。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","A tidal-datum bias can place several mutually aligned elements at the wrong elevation.","Diffusion length gives the exact location and time of corrosion initiation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"潮位基準誤差可使多個管節共同偏高而相互吻合。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A tidal-datum bias can place several mutually aligned elements at the wrong elevation. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b107-v14-29","title":"氯鹽遷移與耐久判讀：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Chloride transport and durability interpretation: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-28"],"objective":"說明「擴散特徵長度」如何影響費馬恩海峽沉管隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Diffusion characteristic length” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Fehmarnbelt immersed tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"海水環境下的費馬恩箱體耐久課題由材料傳輸和接縫路徑分開討論，不能只以平均混凝土係數代表全體。海水或除冰鹽可提供氯離子，材料孔隙與裂縫控制其傳輸；鋼筋腐蝕還需要局部電化學條件。平方根擴散長度僅顯示時間尺度，並不是腐蝕門檻深度；表面濃度變化、乾濕循環、結合效應及施工裂縫須另行辨識。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「擴散特徵長度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Separate material transport from joint pathways in marine durability rather than representing the entire structure with one concrete coefficient. Seawater or deicing salt supplies chloride, while pores and cracks govern transport; reinforcement corrosion also depends on local electrochemical conditions. A square-root diffusion length indicates a time scale, not a corrosion-threshold depth. Surface concentration, wetting cycles, binding and construction cracks must be distinguished rather than hidden in one fitted diffusivity. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Diffusion characteristic length” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：擴散係數=3e-12 m²/s；暴露時間=17 year。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: diffusivity=3e-12 m²/s; exposure=17 year. ℓ=√(Dt); 1 year=365.25×86400 s; m→mm ×1000=40.1178 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「擴散長度就是鋼筋開始腐蝕的位置和精確時間。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Diffusion length gives the exact location and time of corrosion initiation.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「擴散特徵長度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Diffusion characteristic length”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-29-k1","title":"氯鹽遷移與耐久判讀","titleEn":"Chloride transport and durability interpretation","text":"海水環境下的費馬恩箱體耐久課題由材料傳輸和接縫路徑分開討論，不能只以平均混凝土係數代表全體。海水或除冰鹽可提供氯離子，材料孔隙與裂縫控制其傳輸；鋼筋腐蝕還需要局部電化學條件。","textEn":"Separate material transport from joint pathways in marine durability rather than representing the entire structure with one concrete coefficient. Seawater or deicing salt supplies chloride, while pores and cracks govern transport; reinforcement corrosion also depends on local electrochemical conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：擴散長度就是鋼筋開始腐蝕的位置和精確時間。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Diffusion length gives the exact location and time of corrosion initiation. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「氯鹽遷移與耐久判讀」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Chloride transport and durability interpretation\" is correct?","options":["擴散長度就是鋼筋開始腐蝕的位置和精確時間。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。","海水環境下的費馬恩箱體耐久課題由材料傳輸和接縫路徑分開討論，不能只以平均混凝土係數代表全體。"],"optionsEn":["Diffusion length gives the exact location and time of corrosion initiation.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.","Separate material transport from joint pathways in marine durability rather than representing the entire structure with one concrete coefficient."],"answer":2,"explanation":"海水環境下的費馬恩箱體耐久課題由材料傳輸和接縫路徑分開討論，不能只以平均混凝土係數代表全體。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Separate material transport from joint pathways in marine durability rather than representing the entire structure with one concrete coefficient. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b107-v14-30","title":"氯鹽遷移與耐久判讀：定量估算","titleEn":"Chloride transport and durability interpretation: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「擴散特徵長度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Diffusion characteristic length” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：擴散係數=3e-12 m²/s；暴露時間=17 year。ℓ=√(Dt); 1 year=365.25×86400 s; m→mm ×1000=40.1178 mm。僅把暴露時間增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為42.0759 mm。邊界：特徵長度，不是腐蝕起始壽命或氯鹽門檻深度；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: diffusivity=3e-12 m²/s; exposure=17 year. ℓ=√(Dt); 1 year=365.25×86400 s; m→mm ×1000=40.1178 mm. Increasing only exposure by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 42.0759 mm. Boundary: Characteristic length, not corrosion-initiation life or chloride-threshold depth. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比較未裂區與接縫鄰近區的含水和氯鹽剖面。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare moisture and chloride profiles in uncracked zones and near joints.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：擴散係數=3e-12 m²/s；暴露時間=17 year。ℓ=√(Dt); 1 year=365.25×86400 s; m→mm ×1000=40.1178 mm。僅把暴露時間增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為42.0759 mm。邊界：特徵長度，不是腐蝕起始壽命或氯鹽門檻深度；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: diffusivity=3e-12 m²/s; exposure=17 year. ℓ=√(Dt); 1 year=365.25×86400 s; m→mm ×1000=40.1178 mm. Increasing only exposure by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 42.0759 mm. Boundary: Characteristic length, not corrosion-initiation life or chloride-threshold depth. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「氯鹽遷移與耐久判讀」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Chloride transport and durability interpretation\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：擴散係數=3e-12 m²/s；暴露時間=17 year。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。","混凝土抗壓強度合格就代表厚壁構件不會產生熱裂縫。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: diffusivity=3e-12 m²/s; exposure=17 year. ℓ=√(Dt); 1 year=365.25×86400 s; m→mm ×1000=40.1178 mm.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.","Adequate compressive strength proves that thick concrete cannot develop thermal cracks."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：擴散係數=3e-12 m²/s；暴露時間=17 year。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: diffusivity=3e-12 m²/s; exposure=17 year. ℓ=√(Dt); 1 year=365.25×86400 s; m→mm ×1000=40.1178 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b107-v14-31","title":"氯鹽遷移與耐久判讀：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Chloride transport and durability interpretation: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「擴散特徵長度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Diffusion characteristic length” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比較未裂區與接縫鄰近區的含水和氯鹽剖面。以分層取樣的氯鹽剖面配合裂縫圖與電位量測，檢查擴散模型是否只適用未開裂材料。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare moisture and chloride profiles in uncracked zones and near joints. Combine depth-resolved chloride samples with crack maps and potential measurements, checking whether the diffusion model applies only to uncracked material. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「擴散特徵長度」的交付需回答：比較未裂區與接縫鄰近區的含水和氯鹽剖面。保留取樣深度、含水狀態及材料批次，用多種證據解釋劣化；維修優先序依構件功能與實際病害制定。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Fehmarnbelt immersed tunnel, the diffusion characteristic length handover must address the following evidence: Compare moisture and chloride profiles in uncracked zones and near joints. Retain sample depth, moisture and material batches and interpret deterioration using multiple evidence types; prioritise repairs by function and observed defects.","failure":"注意干擾：接縫快速入滲若併入材料平均值，會掩蓋局部維修需求。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Averaging rapid joint ingress into bulk material hides local repair needs. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比較未裂區與接縫鄰近區的含水和氯鹽剖面。以分層取樣的氯鹽剖面配合裂縫圖與電位量測，檢查擴散模型是否只適用未開裂材料。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Compare moisture and chloride profiles in uncracked zones and near joints. Combine depth-resolved chloride samples with crack maps and potential measurements, checking whether the diffusion model applies only to uncracked material. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「擴散特徵長度」的交付需回答：比較未裂區與接縫鄰近區的含水和氯鹽剖面。保留取樣深度、含水狀態及材料批次，用多種證據解釋劣化；維修優先序依構件功能與實際病害制定。","textEn":"For Fehmarnbelt immersed tunnel, the diffusion characteristic length handover must address the following evidence: Compare moisture and chloride profiles in uncracked zones and near joints. Retain sample depth, moisture and material batches and interpret deterioration using multiple evidence types; prioritise repairs by function and observed defects.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「氯鹽遷移與耐久判讀」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Chloride transport and durability interpretation\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","比較未裂區與接縫鄰近區的含水和氯鹽剖面。","各管節平均高程接近就能排除接頭差異變形。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Compare moisture and chloride profiles in uncracked zones and near joints.","Similar mean element elevations exclude differential movement at joints."],"answer":1,"explanation":"比較未裂區與接縫鄰近區的含水和氯鹽剖面。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare moisture and chloride profiles in uncracked zones and near joints. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b107-v14-32","title":"氯鹽遷移與耐久判讀：失效診斷","titleEn":"Chloride transport and durability interpretation: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「擴散特徵長度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Diffusion characteristic length” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"接縫快速入滲若併入材料平均值，會掩蓋局部維修需求。把一次電位讀值當腐蝕速率會誤判剩餘壽命，裂縫快速傳輸也可能被平均材料係數掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Averaging rapid joint ingress into bulk material hides local repair needs. Treating one potential reading as corrosion rate misjudges remaining life, while averaged material coefficients conceal rapid crack transport. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：平方根擴散長度僅顯示時間尺度，並不是腐蝕門檻深度；表面濃度變化、乾濕循環、結合效應及施工裂縫須另行辨識。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Surface concentration, wetting cycles, binding and construction cracks must be distinguished rather than hidden in one fitted diffusivity.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「擴散長度就是鋼筋開始腐蝕的位置和精確時間。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Diffusion length gives the exact location and time of corrosion initiation.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"接縫快速入滲若併入材料平均值，會掩蓋局部維修需求。把一次電位讀值當腐蝕速率會誤判剩餘壽命，裂縫快速傳輸也可能被平均材料係數掩蓋。","textEn":"Averaging rapid joint ingress into bulk material hides local repair needs. Treating one potential reading as corrosion rate misjudges remaining life, while averaged material coefficients conceal rapid crack transport.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「氯鹽遷移與耐久判讀」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Chloride transport and durability interpretation\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。","接縫快速入滲若併入材料平均值，會掩蓋局部維修需求。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.","Averaging rapid joint ingress into bulk material hides local repair needs."],"answer":2,"explanation":"接縫快速入滲若併入材料平均值，會掩蓋局部維修需求。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Averaging rapid joint ingress into bulk material hides local repair needs. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b107-v14-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「疏散時間與分區可用性」與「資產編碼與可追溯交接」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Evacuation time and zone availability\" and \"Asset identity and traceable handover\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b107-v14-33","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-32"],"objective":"說明「所需疏散時間」如何影響費馬恩海峽沉管隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Required evacuation time” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Fehmarnbelt immersed tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"道路與鐵路同走廊的應變假設不能混用，研究不同使用者、車輛和隔離狀態對通行時間的影響。疏散時間包含辨識、反應、移動及排隊，不只由出口距離決定。人員速度會受煙熱、能見度及行動能力影響，安全判斷還要比較可用安全時間；橫通道存在但門或鄰孔不可用時，圖上的最短路線不一定能作實際選擇。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「所需疏散時間」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Road and rail emergency assumptions are not interchangeable; examine how users, vehicles and isolation states change movement time. Evacuation includes detection, response, travel and queues, not merely distance to an exit. Smoke, visibility and mobility alter walking speed, while safety requires comparison with available safe time. A passage shown on a plan may be unusable because its door or receiving bore is unavailable, invalidating the nominal shortest route. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Required evacuation time” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：前置時間=92 s；行走距離=360 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=92 s; travel distance=360 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「所需疏散時間」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Required evacuation time”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-33-k1","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability","text":"道路與鐵路同走廊的應變假設不能混用，研究不同使用者、車輛和隔離狀態對通行時間的影響。疏散時間包含辨識、反應、移動及排隊，不只由出口距離決定。","textEn":"Road and rail emergency assumptions are not interchangeable; examine how users, vehicles and isolation states change movement time. Evacuation includes detection, response, travel and queues, not merely distance to an exit.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「疏散時間與分區可用性」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Evacuation time and zone availability\" is correct?","options":["道路與鐵路同走廊的應變假設不能混用，研究不同使用者、車輛和隔離狀態對通行時間的影響。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。"],"optionsEn":["Road and rail emergency assumptions are not interchangeable; examine how users, vehicles and isolation states change movement time.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted."],"answer":0,"explanation":"道路與鐵路同走廊的應變假設不能混用，研究不同使用者、車輛和隔離狀態對通行時間的影響。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Road and rail emergency assumptions are not interchangeable; examine how users, vehicles and isolation states change movement time. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b107-v14-34","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性：定量估算","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「所需疏散時間」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Required evacuation time” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：前置時間=92 s；行走距離=360 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。RSET=tpre+d/v=542 s。僅把行走距離增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為587 s。邊界：單群體固定速度，不含排隊煙熱及能力差異，不能單獨判安全；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=92 s; travel distance=360 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s. RSET=tpre+d/v=542 s. Increasing only travel distance by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 587 s. Boundary: One group at fixed speed without queues, smoke or mobility differences; not a safety conclusion. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：各模式分開演練起始通知、下車與安全區轉移。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Exercise notification, detraining and safe-area transfer separately for each mode.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：前置時間=92 s；行走距離=360 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。RSET=tpre+d/v=542 s。僅把行走距離增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為587 s。邊界：單群體固定速度，不含排隊煙熱及能力差異，不能單獨判安全；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=92 s; travel distance=360 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s. RSET=tpre+d/v=542 s. Increasing only travel distance by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 587 s. Boundary: One group at fixed speed without queues, smoke or mobility differences; not a safety conclusion. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「疏散時間與分區可用性」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Evacuation time and zone availability\", which statement holds?","options":["矩形沉管可以直接使用圓環均勻外壓公式設計。","原創教學假設：前置時間=92 s；行走距離=360 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。","剩餘浮力為正就代表浮運姿態在所有波況穩定。"],"optionsEn":["A rectangular immersed tube can be designed directly with a circular-ring pressure formula.","Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=92 s; travel distance=360 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s.","Positive residual buoyancy establishes stability in every sea state."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：前置時間=92 s；行走距離=360 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=92 s; travel distance=360 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b107-v14-35","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「所需疏散時間」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Required evacuation time” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"各模式分開演練起始通知、下車與安全區轉移。以人流模擬或受控演練分辨前置時間、行走與門口排隊，核對每個出口接收區的可用狀態及通訊紀錄。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Exercise notification, detraining and safe-area transfer separately for each mode. Separate pre-movement, travel and doorway queues through simulation or controlled drills, checking receiving-zone availability and communication records for each exit. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「所需疏散時間」的交付需回答：各模式分開演練起始通知、下車與安全區轉移。疏散模型保留人口、速度分布及出口狀態，演練改動由營運與防災責任者批准，教材算例不得當作現場指揮程序。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Fehmarnbelt immersed tunnel, the required evacuation time handover must address the following evidence: Exercise notification, detraining and safe-area transfer separately for each mode. Retain population, speed distribution and exit states; operations and fire-safety owners approve drill changes, and classroom calculations are not incident-command procedures.","failure":"注意干擾：共用一個步速會漏掉列車下車及道路人群差異。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: One walking speed omits detraining and road-user differences. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"各模式分開演練起始通知、下車與安全區轉移。以人流模擬或受控演練分辨前置時間、行走與門口排隊，核對每個出口接收區的可用狀態及通訊紀錄。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Exercise notification, detraining and safe-area transfer separately for each mode. Separate pre-movement, travel and doorway queues through simulation or controlled drills, checking receiving-zone availability and communication records for each exit. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「所需疏散時間」的交付需回答：各模式分開演練起始通知、下車與安全區轉移。疏散模型保留人口、速度分布及出口狀態，演練改動由營運與防災責任者批准，教材算例不得當作現場指揮程序。","textEn":"For Fehmarnbelt immersed tunnel, the required evacuation time handover must address the following evidence: Exercise notification, detraining and safe-area transfer separately for each mode. Retain population, speed distribution and exit states; operations and fire-safety owners approve drill changes, and classroom calculations are not incident-command procedures.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「疏散時間與分區可用性」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Evacuation time and zone availability\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","接縫平均寬度合格就不必量測局部錯台及扭轉。","各模式分開演練起始通知、下車與安全區轉移。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","An acceptable average joint width makes local offset and twist measurements unnecessary.","Exercise notification, detraining and safe-area transfer separately for each mode."],"answer":2,"explanation":"各模式分開演練起始通知、下車與安全區轉移。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Exercise notification, detraining and safe-area transfer separately for each mode. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b107-v14-36","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性：失效診斷","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「所需疏散時間」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Required evacuation time” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"共用一個步速會漏掉列車下車及道路人群差異。以最快成人速度套全部旅客會低估需求，若忽略接收孔受煙或車流影響，疏散可能移到另一個危險邊界。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"One walking speed omits detraining and road-user differences. Applying the fastest adult speed to everyone understates demand; overlooking smoke or traffic in the receiving bore can transfer evacuees into another hazard. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：人員速度會受煙熱、能見度及行動能力影響，安全判斷還要比較可用安全時間；橫通道存在但門或鄰孔不可用時，圖上的最短路線不一定能作實際選擇。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A passage shown on a plan may be unusable because its door or receiving bore is unavailable, invalidating the nominal shortest route.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"共用一個步速會漏掉列車下車及道路人群差異。以最快成人速度套全部旅客會低估需求，若忽略接收孔受煙或車流影響，疏散可能移到另一個危險邊界。","textEn":"One walking speed omits detraining and road-user differences. Applying the fastest adult speed to everyone understates demand; overlooking smoke or traffic in the receiving bore can transfer evacuees into another hazard.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「疏散時間與分區可用性」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Evacuation time and zone availability\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["共用一個步速會漏掉列車下車及道路人群差異。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。"],"optionsEn":["One walking speed omits detraining and road-user differences.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted."],"answer":0,"explanation":"共用一個步速會漏掉列車下車及道路人群差異。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"One walking speed omits detraining and road-user differences. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b107-v14-37","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-36"],"objective":"說明「資產資料完整度」如何影響費馬恩海峽沉管隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Asset-record completeness” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Fehmarnbelt immersed tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"量產管節需以編號串起工廠試驗、沉放位置與營運設備，研究修訂後材料紀錄是否仍可追溯。地下設備的竣工資料必須讓維護人員找到正確位置、材料批次和控制版本。只有上傳圖面而沒有變更歷程，無法分辨元件替換與真正劣化；告警、儀器、線路及工單使用一致識別碼，才可能把量測趨勢連回實際受力或水力系統。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「資產資料完整度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Element identifiers must link factory tests, installed position and operational equipment after revisions to production records. Handover must let maintainers find the correct location, material batch and control revision. Drawings without change history cannot distinguish replacement from deterioration. Consistent identifiers across alarms, instruments, circuits and work orders are essential for linking trends to the physical structural or hydraulic system instead of treating each record as an isolated file. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Asset-record completeness” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：設備總數=106 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: asset count=106 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=84.9057 %.","failure":"常見誤解：「全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「資產資料完整度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Asset-record completeness”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-37-k1","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover","text":"量產管節需以編號串起工廠試驗、沉放位置與營運設備，研究修訂後材料紀錄是否仍可追溯。地下設備的竣工資料必須讓維護人員找到正確位置、材料批次和控制版本。","textEn":"Element identifiers must link factory tests, installed position and operational equipment after revisions to production records. Handover must let maintainers find the correct location, material batch and control revision.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「資產編碼與可追溯交接」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Asset identity and traceable handover\" is correct?","options":["全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。","量產管節需以編號串起工廠試驗、沉放位置與營運設備，研究修訂後材料紀錄是否仍可追溯。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.","Element identifiers must link factory tests, installed position and operational equipment after revisions to production records.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":1,"explanation":"量產管節需以編號串起工廠試驗、沉放位置與營運設備，研究修訂後材料紀錄是否仍可追溯。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Element identifiers must link factory tests, installed position and operational equipment after revisions to production records. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b107-v14-38","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：定量估算","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「資產資料完整度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Asset-record completeness” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：設備總數=106 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。coverage=100(N−missing)/N=84.9057 %。僅把缺紀錄數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為83.3962 %。邊界：資料完整度，不等於安全或可靠度；擾動為連續敏感度，實際個數為整數；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: asset count=106 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=84.9057 %. Increasing only missing records by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 83.3962 %. Boundary: Record completeness, not safety or reliability; perturbation is continuous sensitivity while actual counts are integers. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：抽選管節從材料批次一路追到竣工坐標和檢修表。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Trace a sampled element from material batch to as-built position and maintenance sheet.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：設備總數=106 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。coverage=100(N−missing)/N=84.9057 %。僅把缺紀錄數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為83.3962 %。邊界：資料完整度，不等於安全或可靠度；擾動為連續敏感度，實際個數為整數；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: asset count=106 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=84.9057 %. Increasing only missing records by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 83.3962 %. Boundary: Record completeness, not safety or reliability; perturbation is continuous sensitivity while actual counts are integers. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「資產編碼與可追溯交接」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Asset identity and traceable handover\", which statement holds?","options":["混凝土抗壓強度合格就代表厚壁構件不會產生熱裂縫。","各管節平均高程接近就能排除接頭差異變形。","原創教學假設：設備總數=106 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。"],"optionsEn":["Adequate compressive strength proves that thick concrete cannot develop thermal cracks.","Similar mean element elevations exclude differential movement at joints.","Original teaching assumptions: asset count=106 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=84.9057 %."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：設備總數=106 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: asset count=106 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=84.9057 %. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b107-v14-39","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「資產資料完整度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Asset-record completeness” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"抽選管節從材料批次一路追到竣工坐標和檢修表。抽取一條告警，從控制畫面追到設備、線路、圖面和工單，核對位置、版本及校正日期並記錄無法閉合的欄位。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Trace a sampled element from material batch to as-built position and maintenance sheet. Trace a sampled alarm from screen to equipment, circuit, drawing and work order, checking location, revision and calibration dates and recording broken links. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「資產資料完整度」的交付需回答：抽選管節從材料批次一路追到竣工坐標和檢修表。交接以可完成的定位、查找與復原任務驗證，由維護責任人確認現場可用性；完整度只是資料指標，不代表結構安全或設備可靠。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Fehmarnbelt immersed tunnel, the asset-record completeness handover must address the following evidence: Trace a sampled element from material batch to as-built position and maintenance sheet. Validate handover through achievable location, retrieval and recovery tasks witnessed by maintainers; completeness measures records, not structural safety or equipment reliability.","failure":"注意干擾：現場交換管節而未更新資料會使試驗證據指向錯誤位置。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Unrecorded element substitution assigns test evidence to the wrong location. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"抽選管節從材料批次一路追到竣工坐標和檢修表。抽取一條告警，從控制畫面追到設備、線路、圖面和工單，核對位置、版本及校正日期並記錄無法閉合的欄位。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Trace a sampled element from material batch to as-built position and maintenance sheet. Trace a sampled alarm from screen to equipment, circuit, drawing and work order, checking location, revision and calibration dates and recording broken links. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「資產資料完整度」的交付需回答：抽選管節從材料批次一路追到竣工坐標和檢修表。交接以可完成的定位、查找與復原任務驗證，由維護責任人確認現場可用性；完整度只是資料指標，不代表結構安全或設備可靠。","textEn":"For Fehmarnbelt immersed tunnel, the asset-record completeness handover must address the following evidence: Trace a sampled element from material batch to as-built position and maintenance sheet. Validate handover through achievable location, retrieval and recovery tasks witnessed by maintainers; completeness measures records, not structural safety or equipment reliability.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「資產編碼與可追溯交接」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Asset identity and traceable handover\"?","options":["抽選管節從材料批次一路追到竣工坐標和檢修表。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Trace a sampled element from material batch to as-built position and maintenance sheet.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error."],"answer":0,"explanation":"抽選管節從材料批次一路追到竣工坐標和檢修表。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Trace a sampled element from material batch to as-built position and maintenance sheet. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b107-v14-40","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：失效診斷","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b107-v14-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「資產資料完整度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Asset-record completeness” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"現場交換管節而未更新資料會使試驗證據指向錯誤位置。設備改名卻未更新控制畫面會引導人員隔離錯誤回路，材料批次缺漏則使同批缺陷無法追蹤到其他位置。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Unrecorded element substitution assigns test evidence to the wrong location. Renaming an asset without updating the screen can isolate the wrong circuit; missing material batches prevent tracing related defects at other locations. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：只有上傳圖面而沒有變更歷程，無法分辨元件替換與真正劣化；告警、儀器、線路及工單使用一致識別碼，才可能把量測趨勢連回實際受力或水力系統。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Consistent identifiers across alarms, instruments, circuits and work orders are essential for linking trends to the physical structural or hydraulic system instead of treating each record as an isolated file.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b107-v14-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"現場交換管節而未更新資料會使試驗證據指向錯誤位置。設備改名卻未更新控制畫面會引導人員隔離錯誤回路，材料批次缺漏則使同批缺陷無法追蹤到其他位置。","textEn":"Unrecorded element substitution assigns test evidence to the wrong location. Renaming an asset without updating the screen can isolate the wrong circuit; missing material batches prevent tracing related defects at other locations.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b107-v14-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「資產編碼與可追溯交接」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Asset identity and traceable handover\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","現場交換管節而未更新資料會使試驗證據指向錯誤位置。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Unrecorded element substitution assigns test evidence to the wrong location.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":1,"explanation":"現場交換管節而未更新資料會使試驗證據指向錯誤位置。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Unrecorded element substitution assigns test evidence to the wrong location. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b107","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"curriculumVersion":14,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000},{"id":"b108","title":"馬爾馬拉海底隧道","titleEn":"Marmaray immersed tunnel","category":"underground","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"馬爾馬拉跨越博斯普魯斯海峽，承包商資料列沉管段1387公尺，這不是整個鐵路計畫的長度。2013年的通車背景提供都市交通與海底工程的交會案例。本課從管節浮運、基床與接頭開始，再串接鑽掘段、軌道和救援系統，強調不同結構交界的變形相容。","summaryEn":"Marmaray crosses the Bosphorus; contractor records identify a 1387 m immersed section, distinct from the overall railway programme. Its 2013 opening links urban transport and subsea engineering. The course follows flotation, bedding and joints into bored-tunnel transitions, track and rescue systems, emphasising compatible deformation between different structural forms.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"ug-landmarks","subcategoryTitle":"世界隧道與地下巨作","subcategoryTitleEn":"World tunnels and underground landmarks","learningTrack":"underground","learningSubdiscipline":"ug-landmarks","learningTags":["underground","ug-landmarks","tunnel"],"architectureFamily":"tunnel","architectureNodes":[["路線里程與端點","Alignment chainage and endpoints"],["剩餘浮力","Residual buoyancy"],["差異沉陷梯度","Differential settlement gradient"],["方向角誤差","Orientation error"],["入口壓力擾動","Portal pressure disturbance"],["資產資料完整度","Asset-record completeness"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,5],[1,5]],"diagram":{"type":"tunnel","labels":["路線里程與端點","剩餘浮力","差異沉陷梯度","方向角誤差","入口壓力擾動"],"labelsEn":["Alignment chainage and endpoints","Residual buoyancy","Differential settlement gradient","Orientation error","Portal pressure disturbance"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"原創綜合審查：先計算「浮運重量帳與姿態穩定」，再獨立計算「控制網與貫通誤差」。原創教學假設：水密度=1025 kg/m³；排水體積=11400 m³；總質量=1.13344e+07 kg。R=(ρV−m)g/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=3438.9 kN。僅把排水體積增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為14901.9 kN。邊界：靜水剩餘浮力，不驗證傾斜穩性及自由液面；不是本工程實測或允收值。原創教學假設：控制長度=3840 m；方向偏角=2.5 arcsec。e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0465421 m。僅把方向偏角增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.0511963 m。邊界：小角度方向偏差，未加入控制網相關性及折光；不是本工程實測或允收值。兩組結果的單位與邊界不同，不能直接相加。請列出一項缺少的現場輸入，說明它會影響哪個結論，以及哪種獨立量測可以縮小不確定度。","textEn":"Original integrated review: first calculate tow-out mass balance and stability, then independently calculate control network and breakthrough error. Original teaching assumptions: water density=1025 kg/m³; displacement=11400 m³; mass=1.13344e+07 kg. R=(ρV−m)g/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=3438.9 kN. Increasing only displacement by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 14901.9 kN. Boundary: Still-water buoyancy reserve, not heel stability or free-surface verification. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Original teaching assumptions: control length=3840 m; orientation error=2.5 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0465421 m. Increasing only orientation error by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.0511963 m. Boundary: Small-angle orientation error without network correlation or refraction. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. The outputs have different units and boundaries and cannot simply be added. Identify one missing field input, explain which conclusion it changes and select an independent measurement to reduce uncertainty.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":14,"enrichmentVersion":14,"stages":[{"id":"b108-v14-s1","title":"地層條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Ground conditions, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「服務邊界與路線代價」與「浮運重量帳與姿態穩定」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\" and \"Tow-out mass balance and stability\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b108-v14-01","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「路線里程與端點」如何影響馬爾馬拉海底隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Alignment chainage and endpoints” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Marmaray immersed tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"馬爾馬拉沉管長度與整體通勤鐵路範圍必須分開，學員先辨認海峽段和兩側地下接線。隧道選線同時改變洞口、覆土與縱坡，短路線不保證低地質風險。比較方案必須使用相同起訖點，並分開主孔、引道及服務坑的工程數量；交通時間只是需求的一個指標，不能代替施工可達性或長期維修評估。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「路線里程與端點」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Separate the immersed crossing from the commuter-rail programme, identifying the strait section and underground approaches on both sides. Alignment changes portals, cover and gradient together, so a shorter tunnel need not have lower geological risk. Compare options between identical endpoints and distinguish running bores, approaches and service galleries. Travel time measures one service benefit but cannot replace assessment of construction access, maintenance closures or exposure to uncertain ground. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Alignment chainage and endpoints” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：長度=14.8 km；速度=60 km/h。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: length=14.8 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=14.8 min.","failure":"常見誤解：「最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「路線里程與端點」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Alignment chainage and endpoints”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b108-v14-01-k1","title":"服務邊界與路線代價","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost","text":"馬爾馬拉沉管長度與整體通勤鐵路範圍必須分開，學員先辨認海峽段和兩側地下接線。隧道選線同時改變洞口、覆土與縱坡，短路線不保證低地質風險。","textEn":"Separate the immersed crossing from the commuter-rail programme, identifying the strait section and underground approaches on both sides. Alignment changes portals, cover and gradient together, so a shorter tunnel need not have lower geological risk.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]},{"id":"b108-v14-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「服務邊界與路線代價」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\" is correct?","options":["最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。","馬爾馬拉沉管長度與整體通勤鐵路範圍必須分開，學員先辨認海峽段和兩側地下接線。","剩餘浮力為正就代表浮運姿態在所有波況穩定。"],"optionsEn":["The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.","Separate the immersed crossing from the commuter-rail programme, identifying the strait section and underground approaches on both sides.","Positive residual buoyancy establishes stability in every sea state."],"answer":1,"explanation":"馬爾馬拉沉管長度與整體通勤鐵路範圍必須分開，學員先辨認海峽段和兩側地下接線。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Separate the immersed crossing from the commuter-rail programme, identifying the strait section and underground approaches on both sides. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b108-v14-02","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：定量估算","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b108-v14-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「路線里程與端點」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Alignment chainage and endpoints” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：長度=14.8 km；速度=60 km/h。t=60L/v=14.8 min。僅把長度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為16.28 min。邊界：假想交通旅程，未含加減速、排隊及實際時刻表；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: length=14.8 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=14.8 min. Increasing only length by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 16.28 min. Boundary: Hypothetical transport journey excluding acceleration, queues and the real timetable. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以不同顏色分列沉管、鑽掘和地面段的工程數量。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Separate quantities for immersed, bored and surface sections in the scope register.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b108-v14-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：長度=14.8 km；速度=60 km/h。t=60L/v=14.8 min。僅把長度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為16.28 min。邊界：假想交通旅程，未含加減速、排隊及實際時刻表；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: length=14.8 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=14.8 min. Increasing only length by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 16.28 min. Boundary: Hypothetical transport journey excluding acceleration, queues and the real timetable. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]},{"id":"b108-v14-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「服務邊界與路線代價」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\", which statement holds?","options":["各管節平均高程接近就能排除接頭差異變形。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。","原創教學假設：長度=14.8 km；速度=60 km/h。"],"optionsEn":["Similar mean element elevations exclude differential movement at joints.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.","Original teaching assumptions: length=14.8 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=14.8 min."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：長度=14.8 km；速度=60 km/h。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: length=14.8 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=14.8 min. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b108-v14-03","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b108-v14-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「路線里程與端點」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Alignment chainage and endpoints” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以不同顏色分列沉管、鑽掘和地面段的工程數量。把縱斷面、地形與地質剖面疊合，以端點坐標獨立反算距離，再將主孔與支坑數量分開核對。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Separate quantities for immersed, bored and surface sections in the scope register. Overlay the longitudinal profile, terrain and geology; independently derive distances from endpoint coordinates and reconcile running-bore and gallery quantities separately. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「路線里程與端點」的交付需回答：以不同顏色分列沉管、鑽掘和地面段的工程數量。在方案表中凍結起訖點、計量範圍及地質假設，任何改線都要同步更新高程、數量與服務情境，不能只替換總長。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Marmaray immersed tunnel, the alignment chainage and endpoints handover must address the following evidence: Separate quantities for immersed, bored and surface sections in the scope register. Freeze endpoints, measurement scope and ground assumptions in the option register; realignment requires coordinated updates to elevations, quantities and service scenarios rather than replacing one length.","failure":"注意干擾：以整線長度報沉管數量會讓造價與風險比較失真。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using whole-line length for immersed quantities distorts cost and risk comparisons. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b108-v14-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以不同顏色分列沉管、鑽掘和地面段的工程數量。把縱斷面、地形與地質剖面疊合，以端點坐標獨立反算距離，再將主孔與支坑數量分開核對。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Separate quantities for immersed, bored and surface sections in the scope register. Overlay the longitudinal profile, terrain and geology; independently derive distances from endpoint coordinates and reconcile running-bore and gallery quantities separately. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]},{"id":"b108-v14-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「路線里程與端點」的交付需回答：以不同顏色分列沉管、鑽掘和地面段的工程數量。在方案表中凍結起訖點、計量範圍及地質假設，任何改線都要同步更新高程、數量與服務情境，不能只替換總長。","textEn":"For Marmaray immersed tunnel, the alignment chainage and endpoints handover must address the following evidence: Separate quantities for immersed, bored and surface sections in the scope register. Freeze endpoints, measurement scope and ground assumptions in the option register; realignment requires coordinated updates to elevations, quantities and service scenarios rather than replacing one length.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「服務邊界與路線代價」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\"?","options":["以不同顏色分列沉管、鑽掘和地面段的工程數量。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","動壓公式算出的數值就是長鐵路隧道完整壓力波。"],"optionsEn":["Separate quantities for immersed, bored and surface sections in the scope register.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","A dynamic-pressure calculation is the complete pressure-wave prediction for a long rail tunnel."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以不同顏色分列沉管、鑽掘和地面段的工程數量。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Separate quantities for immersed, bored and surface sections in the scope register. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b108-v14-04","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：失效診斷","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b108-v14-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「路線里程與端點」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Alignment chainage and endpoints” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"以整線長度報沉管數量會讓造價與風險比較失真。混用全線與單孔長度會同時扭曲工程數量、行程及逃生距離，造成方案比較失去共同基準。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using whole-line length for immersed quantities distorts cost and risk comparisons. Mixing whole-route and single-bore lengths distorts quantities, journey time and escape distance, destroying the common basis of an option comparison. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：比較方案必須使用相同起訖點，並分開主孔、引道及服務坑的工程數量；交通時間只是需求的一個指標，不能代替施工可達性或長期維修評估。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Travel time measures one service benefit but cannot replace assessment of construction access, maintenance closures or exposure to uncertain ground.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b108-v14-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"以整線長度報沉管數量會讓造價與風險比較失真。混用全線與單孔長度會同時扭曲工程數量、行程及逃生距離，造成方案比較失去共同基準。","textEn":"Using whole-line length for immersed quantities distorts cost and risk comparisons. Mixing whole-route and single-bore lengths distorts quantities, journey time and escape distance, destroying the common basis of an option comparison.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]},{"id":"b108-v14-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「服務邊界與路線代價」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","以整線長度報沉管數量會讓造價與風險比較失真。","剩餘浮力為正就代表浮運姿態在所有波況穩定。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Using whole-line length for immersed quantities distorts cost and risk comparisons.","Positive residual buoyancy establishes stability in every sea state."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以整線長度報沉管數量會讓造價與風險比較失真。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using whole-line length for immersed quantities distorts cost and risk comparisons. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b108-v14-05","title":"浮運重量帳與姿態穩定：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Tow-out mass balance and stability: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b108-v14-04"],"objective":"說明「剩餘浮力」如何影響馬爾馬拉海底隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Residual buoyancy” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Marmaray immersed tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"博斯普魯斯施工情境要求把浮運重量帳和海流作用分開，靜水浮力不足以描述拖航姿態。浮力由排開水體重量決定，總質量還包含設備、臨時封端及艙內液體。重量帳只能判定淨垂直力，不能證明浮運穩定；壓載液自由表面、重心位置、拖纜與波浪都會改變傾斜反應，落底接觸亦需另建模型。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「剩餘浮力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Separate tow-out mass balance from current effects in the Bosphorus setting; still-water buoyancy cannot describe towing attitude alone. Buoyancy equals displaced water weight, while total mass includes equipment, temporary bulkheads and liquid contents. A mass balance determines net vertical force but does not establish towing stability. Ballast free surfaces, centre of gravity, tow lines and waves affect heel response, and initial contact with the bed needs another model. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Residual buoyancy” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：水密度=1025 kg/m³；排水體積=11400 m³；總質量=1.13344e+07 kg。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: water density=1025 kg/m³; displacement=11400 m³; mass=1.13344e+07 kg.","failure":"常見誤解：「剩餘浮力為正就代表浮運姿態在所有波況穩定。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Positive residual buoyancy establishes stability in every sea state.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「剩餘浮力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Residual buoyancy”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b108-v14-05-k1","title":"浮運重量帳與姿態穩定","titleEn":"Tow-out mass balance and stability","text":"博斯普魯斯施工情境要求把浮運重量帳和海流作用分開，靜水浮力不足以描述拖航姿態。浮力由排開水體重量決定，總質量還包含設備、臨時封端及艙內液體。","textEn":"Separate tow-out mass balance from current effects in the Bosphorus setting; still-water buoyancy cannot describe towing attitude alone. Buoyancy equals displaced water weight, while total mass includes equipment, temporary bulkheads and liquid contents.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]},{"id":"b108-v14-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：剩餘浮力為正就代表浮運姿態在所有波況穩定。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Positive residual buoyancy establishes stability in every sea state. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「浮運重量帳與姿態穩定」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Tow-out mass balance and stability\" is correct?","options":["剩餘浮力為正就代表浮運姿態在所有波況穩定。","矩形沉管可以直接使用圓環均勻外壓公式設計。","博斯普魯斯施工情境要求把浮運重量帳和海流作用分開，靜水浮力不足以描述拖航姿態。"],"optionsEn":["Positive residual buoyancy establishes stability in every sea state.","A rectangular immersed tube can be designed directly with a circular-ring pressure formula.","Separate tow-out mass balance from current effects in the Bosphorus setting; still-water buoyancy cannot describe towing attitude alone."],"answer":2,"explanation":"博斯普魯斯施工情境要求把浮運重量帳和海流作用分開，靜水浮力不足以描述拖航姿態。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Separate tow-out mass balance from current effects in the Bosphorus setting; still-water buoyancy cannot describe towing attitude alone. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b108-v14-06","title":"浮運重量帳與姿態穩定：定量估算","titleEn":"Tow-out mass balance and stability: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b108-v14-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「剩餘浮力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Residual buoyancy” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：水密度=1025 kg/m³；排水體積=11400 m³；總質量=1.13344e+07 kg。R=(ρV−m)g/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=3438.9 kN。僅把排水體積增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為14901.9 kN。邊界：靜水剩餘浮力，不驗證傾斜穩性及自由液面；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: water density=1025 kg/m³; displacement=11400 m³; mass=1.13344e+07 kg. R=(ρV−m)g/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=3438.9 kN. Increasing only displacement by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 14901.9 kN. Boundary: Still-water buoyancy reserve, not heel stability or free-surface verification. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將吃水觀測與海流、拖纜及液艙狀態同時記錄。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Record draught together with current, towline and tank states.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b108-v14-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：水密度=1025 kg/m³；排水體積=11400 m³；總質量=1.13344e+07 kg。R=(ρV−m)g/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=3438.9 kN。僅把排水體積增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為14901.9 kN。邊界：靜水剩餘浮力，不驗證傾斜穩性及自由液面；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: water density=1025 kg/m³; displacement=11400 m³; mass=1.13344e+07 kg. R=(ρV−m)g/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=3438.9 kN. Increasing only displacement by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 14901.9 kN. Boundary: Still-water buoyancy reserve, not heel stability or free-surface verification. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]},{"id":"b108-v14-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「浮運重量帳與姿態穩定」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Tow-out mass balance and stability\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：水密度=1025 kg/m³；排水體積=11400 m³；總質量=1.13344e+07 kg。","接縫平均寬度合格就不必量測局部錯台及扭轉。","基線隧道坡度很小，所以不必做牽引與制動分析。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: water density=1025 kg/m³; displacement=11400 m³; mass=1.13344e+07 kg.","An acceptable average joint width makes local offset and twist measurements unnecessary.","A small base-tunnel gradient eliminates the need for traction and braking analysis."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：水密度=1025 kg/m³；排水體積=11400 m³；總質量=1.13344e+07 kg。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: water density=1025 kg/m³; displacement=11400 m³; mass=1.13344e+07 kg. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b108-v14-07","title":"浮運重量帳與姿態穩定：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Tow-out mass balance and stability: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b108-v14-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「剩餘浮力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Residual buoyancy” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將吃水觀測與海流、拖纜及液艙狀態同時記錄。以實際重量清冊和吃水測量互核，量測液艙水位及橫傾，檢查密度與體積是否採同一狀態。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Record draught together with current, towline and tank states. Reconcile an itemised mass register with draught measurements, tank levels and heel, checking that density and displaced volume describe the same state. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「剩餘浮力」的交付需回答：將吃水觀測與海流、拖纜及液艙狀態同時記錄。質量清冊每次變更都重新確認重心和吃水，操作窗口依核准海事方案及量測決定，不由本課靜力式制定。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Marmaray immersed tunnel, the residual buoyancy handover must address the following evidence: Record draught together with current, towline and tank states. Update centre of gravity and draught after every mass-register change; approved marine procedures and observations determine operating windows, not this static classroom equation.","failure":"注意干擾：靜水計算正確而忽略流向變化仍可造成偏航和接近誤差。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Correct static buoyancy with changing currents omitted still permits yaw and approach error. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b108-v14-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將吃水觀測與海流、拖纜及液艙狀態同時記錄。以實際重量清冊和吃水測量互核，量測液艙水位及橫傾，檢查密度與體積是否採同一狀態。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Record draught together with current, towline and tank states. Reconcile an itemised mass register with draught measurements, tank levels and heel, checking that density and displaced volume describe the same state. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]},{"id":"b108-v14-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「剩餘浮力」的交付需回答：將吃水觀測與海流、拖纜及液艙狀態同時記錄。質量清冊每次變更都重新確認重心和吃水，操作窗口依核准海事方案及量測決定，不由本課靜力式制定。","textEn":"For Marmaray immersed tunnel, the residual buoyancy handover must address the following evidence: Record draught together with current, towline and tank states. Update centre of gravity and draught after every mass-register change; approved marine procedures and observations determine operating windows, not this static classroom equation.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「浮運重量帳與姿態穩定」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Tow-out mass balance and stability\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","將吃水觀測與海流、拖纜及液艙狀態同時記錄。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Record draught together with current, towline and tank states.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time."],"answer":1,"explanation":"將吃水觀測與海流、拖纜及液艙狀態同時記錄。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Record draught together with current, towline and tank states. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b108-v14-08","title":"浮運重量帳與姿態穩定：失效診斷","titleEn":"Tow-out mass balance and stability: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b108-v14-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「剩餘浮力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Residual buoyancy” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"靜水計算正確而忽略流向變化仍可造成偏航和接近誤差。漏列臨時設備或自由液面會使浮力帳看似足夠卻缺乏回正能力，偏載也可能先造成局部接觸。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Correct static buoyancy with changing currents omitted still permits yaw and approach error. Missing temporary equipment or free-surface effects can leave an apparently adequate buoyancy balance with insufficient restoring capacity and premature local contact. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：重量帳只能判定淨垂直力，不能證明浮運穩定；壓載液自由表面、重心位置、拖纜與波浪都會改變傾斜反應，落底接觸亦需另建模型。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Ballast free surfaces, centre of gravity, tow lines and waves affect heel response, and initial contact with the bed needs another model.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「剩餘浮力為正就代表浮運姿態在所有波況穩定。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Positive residual buoyancy establishes stability in every sea state.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b108-v14-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"靜水計算正確而忽略流向變化仍可造成偏航和接近誤差。漏列臨時設備或自由液面會使浮力帳看似足夠卻缺乏回正能力，偏載也可能先造成局部接觸。","textEn":"Correct static buoyancy with changing currents omitted still permits yaw and approach error. Missing temporary equipment or free-surface effects can leave an apparently adequate buoyancy balance with insufficient restoring capacity and premature local contact.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]},{"id":"b108-v14-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「浮運重量帳與姿態穩定」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Tow-out mass balance and stability\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","矩形沉管可以直接使用圓環均勻外壓公式設計。","靜水計算正確而忽略流向變化仍可造成偏航和接近誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","A rectangular immersed tube can be designed directly with a circular-ring pressure formula.","Correct static buoyancy with changing currents omitted still permits yaw and approach error."],"answer":2,"explanation":"靜水計算正確而忽略流向變化仍可造成偏航和接近誤差。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Correct static buoyancy with changing currents omitted still permits yaw and approach error. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b108-v14-s2","title":"機制、材料與定量設計","titleEn":"Mechanisms, materials and quantitative design","description":"本階段聚焦「矩形沉管的框架受力」與「基床變形與接頭轉角」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Rectangular immersed-box frame action\" and \"Bedding movement and joint rotation\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b108-v14-09","title":"矩形沉管的框架受力：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Rectangular immersed-box frame action: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b108-v14-08"],"objective":"說明「頂板跨中彎矩」如何影響馬爾馬拉海底隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Roof-span bending” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Marmaray immersed tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"馬爾馬拉矩形沉管頂板的分跨由內牆決定，研究鐵路淨空與結構牆位置之間的協調。矩形沉管的頂板、側牆與中牆透過框架連續性傳遞水土壓力，不能套圓形薄環的膜應力。單向簡支條帶只能估計局部彎矩量級；施工浮運、落底、回填和使用期的邊界不同，支承沉陷、接頭剪力及裂縫寬度仍須分階段檢核。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「頂板跨中彎矩」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Internal walls define roof spans in a rectangular tube; examine coordination between railway clearance and structural partition positions. A rectangular immersed tube transfers water and earth pressure through roof, walls and internal partitions acting as a frame. A circular thin-ring membrane formula is inappropriate. A simply supported strip estimates one bending scale only; flotation, placement, backfill and service change the restraints, requiring staged checks of settlement, joint shear and cracking. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Roof-span bending” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：單位長載重=27 kN/m；跨距=3.3 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: line load=27 kN/m; span=3.3 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「矩形沉管可以直接使用圓環均勻外壓公式設計。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A rectangular immersed tube can be designed directly with a circular-ring pressure formula.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「頂板跨中彎矩」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Roof-span bending”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b108-v14-09-k1","title":"矩形沉管的框架受力","titleEn":"Rectangular immersed-box frame action","text":"馬爾馬拉矩形沉管頂板的分跨由內牆決定，研究鐵路淨空與結構牆位置之間的協調。矩形沉管的頂板、側牆與中牆透過框架連續性傳遞水土壓力，不能套圓形薄環的膜應力。","textEn":"Internal walls define roof spans in a rectangular tube; examine coordination between railway clearance and structural partition positions. A rectangular immersed tube transfers water and earth pressure through roof, walls and internal partitions acting as a frame.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]},{"id":"b108-v14-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：矩形沉管可以直接使用圓環均勻外壓公式設計。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A rectangular immersed tube can be designed directly with a circular-ring pressure formula. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「矩形沉管的框架受力」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Rectangular immersed-box frame action\" is correct?","options":["馬爾馬拉矩形沉管頂板的分跨由內牆決定，研究鐵路淨空與結構牆位置之間的協調。","矩形沉管可以直接使用圓環均勻外壓公式設計。","各管節平均高程接近就能排除接頭差異變形。"],"optionsEn":["Internal walls define roof spans in a rectangular tube; examine coordination between railway clearance and structural partition positions.","A rectangular immersed tube can be designed directly with a circular-ring pressure formula.","Similar mean element elevations exclude differential movement at joints."],"answer":0,"explanation":"馬爾馬拉矩形沉管頂板的分跨由內牆決定，研究鐵路淨空與結構牆位置之間的協調。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Internal walls define roof spans in a rectangular tube; examine coordination between railway clearance and structural partition positions. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b108-v14-10","title":"矩形沉管的框架受力：定量估算","titleEn":"Rectangular immersed-box frame action: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b108-v14-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「頂板跨中彎矩」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Roof-span bending” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：單位長載重=27 kN/m；跨距=3.3 m。M=qL²/8=36.7537 kN·m。僅把跨距增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為44.472 kN·m。邊界：均載簡支單向條帶，連續框架及板效應另驗；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: line load=27 kN/m; span=3.3 m. M=qL²/8=36.7537 kN·m. Increasing only span by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 44.472 kN·m. Boundary: Uniformly loaded simply supported strip; frame continuity and plate action need separate checks. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：對照軌道限界圖和框架支承圖，檢查牆位版本。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Reconcile railway envelope and frame-support drawings, checking wall-location revisions.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b108-v14-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：單位長載重=27 kN/m；跨距=3.3 m。M=qL²/8=36.7537 kN·m。僅把跨距增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為44.472 kN·m。邊界：均載簡支單向條帶，連續框架及板效應另驗；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: line load=27 kN/m; span=3.3 m. M=qL²/8=36.7537 kN·m. Increasing only span by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 44.472 kN·m. Boundary: Uniformly loaded simply supported strip; frame continuity and plate action need separate checks. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]},{"id":"b108-v14-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「矩形沉管的框架受力」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Rectangular immersed-box frame action\", which statement holds?","options":["兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。","原創教學假設：單位長載重=27 kN/m；跨距=3.3 m。","動壓公式算出的數值就是長鐵路隧道完整壓力波。"],"optionsEn":["Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.","Original teaching assumptions: line load=27 kN/m; span=3.3 m.","A dynamic-pressure calculation is the complete pressure-wave prediction for a long rail tunnel."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：單位長載重=27 kN/m；跨距=3.3 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: line load=27 kN/m; span=3.3 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b108-v14-11","title":"矩形沉管的框架受力：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Rectangular immersed-box frame action: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b108-v14-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「頂板跨中彎矩」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Roof-span bending” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"對照軌道限界圖和框架支承圖，檢查牆位版本。比對頂板及中牆應變，使用含支承剛度的框架模型核對彎矩分配，將落底前後量測分開。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Reconcile railway envelope and frame-support drawings, checking wall-location revisions. Compare roof and partition strain with a frame model including support stiffness, keeping measurements before and after bedding separate. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「頂板跨中彎矩」的交付需回答：對照軌道限界圖和框架支承圖，檢查牆位版本。把單條帶、整體框架及接頭模型分開提交，標註適用施工階段和受力方向，保留裂縫及水密試驗的獨立判定。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Marmaray immersed tunnel, the roof-span bending handover must address the following evidence: Reconcile railway envelope and frame-support drawings, checking wall-location revisions. Submit strip, whole-frame and joint models separately, identifying stage and load direction while retaining independent cracking and watertightness assessments.","failure":"注意干擾：設備或淨空調整若刪減支承，原條帶彎矩便失去邊界。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A clearance change removing support invalidates the original strip model. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b108-v14-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"對照軌道限界圖和框架支承圖，檢查牆位版本。比對頂板及中牆應變，使用含支承剛度的框架模型核對彎矩分配，將落底前後量測分開。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Reconcile railway envelope and frame-support drawings, checking wall-location revisions. Compare roof and partition strain with a frame model including support stiffness, keeping measurements before and after bedding separate. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]},{"id":"b108-v14-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「頂板跨中彎矩」的交付需回答：對照軌道限界圖和框架支承圖，檢查牆位版本。把單條帶、整體框架及接頭模型分開提交，標註適用施工階段和受力方向，保留裂縫及水密試驗的獨立判定。","textEn":"For Marmaray immersed tunnel, the roof-span bending handover must address the following evidence: Reconcile railway envelope and frame-support drawings, checking wall-location revisions. Submit strip, whole-frame and joint models separately, identifying stage and load direction while retaining independent cracking and watertightness assessments.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「矩形沉管的框架受力」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Rectangular immersed-box frame action\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。","對照軌道限界圖和框架支承圖，檢查牆位版本。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.","Reconcile railway envelope and frame-support drawings, checking wall-location revisions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"對照軌道限界圖和框架支承圖，檢查牆位版本。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Reconcile railway envelope and frame-support drawings, checking wall-location revisions. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b108-v14-12","title":"矩形沉管的框架受力：失效診斷","titleEn":"Rectangular immersed-box frame action: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b108-v14-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「頂板跨中彎矩」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Roof-span bending” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"設備或淨空調整若刪減支承，原條帶彎矩便失去邊界。忽略中牆支承或不均勻底床會錯估正負彎矩，局部裂縫可能是邊界變化而非材料強度不足。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A clearance change removing support invalidates the original strip model. Omitting partition support or uneven bedding misallocates positive and negative moments; local cracking may reflect changed restraints rather than weak material. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：單向簡支條帶只能估計局部彎矩量級；施工浮運、落底、回填和使用期的邊界不同，支承沉陷、接頭剪力及裂縫寬度仍須分階段檢核。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A simply supported strip estimates one bending scale only; flotation, placement, backfill and service change the restraints, requiring staged checks of settlement, joint shear and cracking.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「矩形沉管可以直接使用圓環均勻外壓公式設計。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A rectangular immersed tube can be designed directly with a circular-ring pressure formula.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b108-v14-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"設備或淨空調整若刪減支承，原條帶彎矩便失去邊界。忽略中牆支承或不均勻底床會錯估正負彎矩，局部裂縫可能是邊界變化而非材料強度不足。","textEn":"A clearance change removing support invalidates the original strip model. Omitting partition support or uneven bedding misallocates positive and negative moments; local cracking may reflect changed restraints rather than weak material.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]},{"id":"b108-v14-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「矩形沉管的框架受力」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Rectangular immersed-box frame action\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["設備或淨空調整若刪減支承，原條帶彎矩便失去邊界。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","各管節平均高程接近就能排除接頭差異變形。"],"optionsEn":["A clearance change removing support invalidates the original strip model.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Similar mean element elevations exclude differential movement at joints."],"answer":0,"explanation":"設備或淨空調整若刪減支承，原條帶彎矩便失去邊界。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A clearance change removing support invalidates the original strip model. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b108-v14-13","title":"基床變形與接頭轉角：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Bedding movement and joint rotation: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b108-v14-12"],"objective":"說明「差異沉陷梯度」如何影響馬爾馬拉海底隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Differential settlement gradient” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Marmaray immersed tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"沉管到鑽掘段的剛度轉換使馬爾馬拉教學聚焦差異沉陷，不能只以海床平均高程判定接合。沉管基床將箱體荷載傳給海床，局部沖刷、回填不均與軟弱層固結會改變接觸分布。總沉陷小不代表接頭轉角小；相鄰管節的差異位移和支承長度才控制局部變形，施工量測須保留時間與潮位基準。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「差異沉陷梯度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The stiffness transition to bored tunnels focuses attention on differential settlement rather than mean seabed level alone. The bed transfers tube load into the seabed, and scour, uneven backfill or consolidation alter contact. Small total settlement does not imply small joint rotation; differential movement and support length control local distortion. Construction observations must preserve time and tidal datum because immediate placement and delayed consolidation describe different mechanisms. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Differential settlement gradient” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：差異沉陷=7 mm；基線長度=130 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: differential settlement=7 mm; baseline=130 m. β=Δs/L=0.0538462 mm/m.","failure":"常見誤解：「各管節平均高程接近就能排除接頭差異變形。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Similar mean element elevations exclude differential movement at joints.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「差異沉陷梯度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Differential settlement gradient”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b108-v14-13-k1","title":"基床變形與接頭轉角","titleEn":"Bedding movement and joint rotation","text":"沉管到鑽掘段的剛度轉換使馬爾馬拉教學聚焦差異沉陷，不能只以海床平均高程判定接合。沉管基床將箱體荷載傳給海床，局部沖刷、回填不均與軟弱層固結會改變接觸分布。","textEn":"The stiffness transition to bored tunnels focuses attention on differential settlement rather than mean seabed level alone. The bed transfers tube load into the seabed, and scour, uneven backfill or consolidation alter contact.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]},{"id":"b108-v14-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：各管節平均高程接近就能排除接頭差異變形。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Similar mean element elevations exclude differential movement at joints. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「基床變形與接頭轉角」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Bedding movement and joint rotation\" is correct?","options":["各管節平均高程接近就能排除接頭差異變形。","沉管到鑽掘段的剛度轉換使馬爾馬拉教學聚焦差異沉陷，不能只以海床平均高程判定接合。","接縫平均寬度合格就不必量測局部錯台及扭轉。"],"optionsEn":["Similar mean element elevations exclude differential movement at joints.","The stiffness transition to bored tunnels focuses attention on differential settlement rather than mean seabed level alone.","An acceptable average joint width makes local offset and twist measurements unnecessary."],"answer":1,"explanation":"沉管到鑽掘段的剛度轉換使馬爾馬拉教學聚焦差異沉陷，不能只以海床平均高程判定接合。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The stiffness transition to bored tunnels focuses attention on differential settlement rather than mean seabed level alone. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b108-v14-14","title":"基床變形與接頭轉角：定量估算","titleEn":"Bedding movement and joint rotation: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b108-v14-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「差異沉陷梯度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Differential settlement gradient” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：差異沉陷=7 mm；基線長度=130 m。β=Δs/L=0.0538462 mm/m。僅把差異沉陷增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.0592308 mm/m。邊界：小變形角變化指標，不是完整固結解；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: differential settlement=7 mm; baseline=130 m. β=Δs/L=0.0538462 mm/m. Increasing only differential settlement by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.0592308 mm/m. Boundary: Small-deformation angular-distortion indicator, not a consolidation solution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在轉換兩側設成對高程與接頭位移基線。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Establish paired elevation and joint-movement baselines across the transition.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b108-v14-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：差異沉陷=7 mm；基線長度=130 m。β=Δs/L=0.0538462 mm/m。僅把差異沉陷增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.0592308 mm/m。邊界：小變形角變化指標，不是完整固結解；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: differential settlement=7 mm; baseline=130 m. β=Δs/L=0.0538462 mm/m. Increasing only differential settlement by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.0592308 mm/m. Boundary: Small-deformation angular-distortion indicator, not a consolidation solution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]},{"id":"b108-v14-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「基床變形與接頭轉角」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Bedding movement and joint rotation\", which statement holds?","options":["基線隧道坡度很小，所以不必做牽引與制動分析。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。","原創教學假設：差異沉陷=7 mm；基線長度=130 m。"],"optionsEn":["A small base-tunnel gradient eliminates the need for traction and braking analysis.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.","Original teaching assumptions: differential settlement=7 mm; baseline=130 m. β=Δs/L=0.0538462 mm/m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：差異沉陷=7 mm；基線長度=130 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: differential settlement=7 mm; baseline=130 m. β=Δs/L=0.0538462 mm/m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b108-v14-15","title":"基床變形與接頭轉角：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Bedding movement and joint rotation: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b108-v14-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「差異沉陷梯度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Differential settlement gradient” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在轉換兩側設成對高程與接頭位移基線。用管節水準網、海床剖面及孔壓變化交叉核對，將整體下沉與相鄰節轉角分開評估。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Establish paired elevation and joint-movement baselines across the transition. Cross-check tube levelling, seabed profiles and pore-pressure change, separating overall settlement from rotation between neighbouring elements. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「差異沉陷梯度」的交付需回答：在轉換兩側設成對高程與接頭位移基線。將基床施工紀錄與長期水準資料連結至管節編號，差異變形先查基準和孔壓，再由設計者判斷接觸及接頭。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Marmaray immersed tunnel, the differential settlement gradient handover must address the following evidence: Establish paired elevation and joint-movement baselines across the transition. Link bedding records and long-term levelling to element identifiers; check datum and pore pressure before designers interpret contact and joint behaviour.","failure":"注意干擾：兩端剛度不同會把小沉陷差集中成局部轉角。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Different end stiffness can concentrate small settlement differences into local rotation. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b108-v14-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在轉換兩側設成對高程與接頭位移基線。用管節水準網、海床剖面及孔壓變化交叉核對，將整體下沉與相鄰節轉角分開評估。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Establish paired elevation and joint-movement baselines across the transition. Cross-check tube levelling, seabed profiles and pore-pressure change, separating overall settlement from rotation between neighbouring elements. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]},{"id":"b108-v14-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「差異沉陷梯度」的交付需回答：在轉換兩側設成對高程與接頭位移基線。將基床施工紀錄與長期水準資料連結至管節編號，差異變形先查基準和孔壓，再由設計者判斷接觸及接頭。","textEn":"For Marmaray immersed tunnel, the differential settlement gradient handover must address the following evidence: Establish paired elevation and joint-movement baselines across the transition. Link bedding records and long-term levelling to element identifiers; check datum and pore pressure before designers interpret contact and joint behaviour.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「基床變形與接頭轉角」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Bedding movement and joint rotation\"?","options":["在轉換兩側設成對高程與接頭位移基線。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Establish paired elevation and joint-movement baselines across the transition.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":0,"explanation":"在轉換兩側設成對高程與接頭位移基線。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Establish paired elevation and joint-movement baselines across the transition. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b108-v14-16","title":"基床變形與接頭轉角：失效診斷","titleEn":"Bedding movement and joint rotation: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b108-v14-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「差異沉陷梯度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Differential settlement gradient” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"兩端剛度不同會把小沉陷差集中成局部轉角。只追蹤平均高程可能漏掉單側失去支承，接頭剪力與止水錯台會先於明顯整體下沉增加。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Different end stiffness can concentrate small settlement differences into local rotation. Mean elevation can conceal loss of support on one side, allowing joint shear and gasket offset to grow before obvious overall settlement. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：總沉陷小不代表接頭轉角小；相鄰管節的差異位移和支承長度才控制局部變形，施工量測須保留時間與潮位基準。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Construction observations must preserve time and tidal datum because immediate placement and delayed consolidation describe different mechanisms.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「各管節平均高程接近就能排除接頭差異變形。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Similar mean element elevations exclude differential movement at joints.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b108-v14-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"兩端剛度不同會把小沉陷差集中成局部轉角。只追蹤平均高程可能漏掉單側失去支承，接頭剪力與止水錯台會先於明顯整體下沉增加。","textEn":"Different end stiffness can concentrate small settlement differences into local rotation. Mean elevation can conceal loss of support on one side, allowing joint shear and gasket offset to grow before obvious overall settlement.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]},{"id":"b108-v14-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「基床變形與接頭轉角」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Bedding movement and joint rotation\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","兩端剛度不同會把小沉陷差集中成局部轉角。","接縫平均寬度合格就不必量測局部錯台及扭轉。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Different end stiffness can concentrate small settlement differences into local rotation.","An acceptable average joint width makes local offset and twist measurements unnecessary."],"answer":1,"explanation":"兩端剛度不同會把小沉陷差集中成局部轉角。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Different end stiffness can concentrate small settlement differences into local rotation. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b108-v14-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「接頭壓縮與水密包絡」與「控制網與貫通誤差」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Joint compression and sealing envelope\" and \"Control network and breakthrough error\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b108-v14-17","title":"接頭壓縮與水密包絡：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Joint compression and sealing envelope: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b108-v14-16"],"objective":"說明「止水壓縮餘量」如何影響馬爾馬拉海底隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Gasket compression reserve” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Marmaray immersed tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"跨海接頭要容納施工偏差和假想地震相對位移，研究張開、剪移及止水壓縮不可互相替代。止水條依受控壓縮維持連續接觸，接縫轉角、錯台、污染與材料鬆弛都會降低最不利點的接觸能力。平均壓縮量不能掩蓋局部脫離；全尺寸試驗的結果只對測試過的幾何、水壓及荷載歷程有效，幾何餘量本身並不是接觸壓力。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「止水壓縮餘量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Crossing joints accommodate construction tolerances and hypothetical seismic relative motion; opening, shear and compression are distinct quantities. A gasket seals through controlled continuous compression; rotation, offset, contamination and relaxation reduce contact at the weakest point. Average compression cannot compensate for local separation. Full-size test results apply only to their tested geometry, head and load history, while a calculated geometric reserve is neither contact pressure nor evidence of watertightness. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Gasket compression reserve” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：初始壓縮=21 mm；張開量=3.8 mm；幾何公差=2 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: initial compression=21 mm; opening=3.8 mm; tolerance=2 mm. c_res=c0−opening−tolerance=15.2 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「接縫平均寬度合格就不必量測局部錯台及扭轉。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"An acceptable average joint width makes local offset and twist measurements unnecessary.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「止水壓縮餘量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Gasket compression reserve”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b108-v14-17-k1","title":"接頭壓縮與水密包絡","titleEn":"Joint compression and sealing envelope","text":"跨海接頭要容納施工偏差和假想地震相對位移，研究張開、剪移及止水壓縮不可互相替代。止水條依受控壓縮維持連續接觸，接縫轉角、錯台、污染與材料鬆弛都會降低最不利點的接觸能力。","textEn":"Crossing joints accommodate construction tolerances and hypothetical seismic relative motion; opening, shear and compression are distinct quantities. A gasket seals through controlled continuous compression; rotation, offset, contamination and relaxation reduce contact at the weakest point.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]},{"id":"b108-v14-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：接縫平均寬度合格就不必量測局部錯台及扭轉。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: An acceptable average joint width makes local offset and twist measurements unnecessary. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「接頭壓縮與水密包絡」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Joint compression and sealing envelope\" is correct?","options":["接縫平均寬度合格就不必量測局部錯台及扭轉。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。","跨海接頭要容納施工偏差和假想地震相對位移，研究張開、剪移及止水壓縮不可互相替代。"],"optionsEn":["An acceptable average joint width makes local offset and twist measurements unnecessary.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.","Crossing joints accommodate construction tolerances and hypothetical seismic relative motion; opening, shear and compression are distinct quantities."],"answer":2,"explanation":"跨海接頭要容納施工偏差和假想地震相對位移，研究張開、剪移及止水壓縮不可互相替代。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Crossing joints accommodate construction tolerances and hypothetical seismic relative motion; opening, shear and compression are distinct quantities. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b108-v14-18","title":"接頭壓縮與水密包絡：定量估算","titleEn":"Joint compression and sealing envelope: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b108-v14-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「止水壓縮餘量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Gasket compression reserve” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：初始壓縮=21 mm；張開量=3.8 mm；幾何公差=2 mm。c_res=c0−opening−tolerance=15.2 mm。僅把張開量增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為14.82 mm。邊界：單向幾何餘量，不是接觸壓或水密合格證明；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: initial compression=21 mm; opening=3.8 mm; tolerance=2 mm. c_res=c0−opening−tolerance=15.2 mm. Increasing only opening by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 14.82 mm. Boundary: One-direction geometric reserve, not contact pressure or proof of watertightness. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用組合位移試驗核對止水包絡而非單向壓縮。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check the seal envelope with combined displacement rather than compression alone.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b108-v14-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：初始壓縮=21 mm；張開量=3.8 mm；幾何公差=2 mm。c_res=c0−opening−tolerance=15.2 mm。僅把張開量增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為14.82 mm。邊界：單向幾何餘量，不是接觸壓或水密合格證明；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: initial compression=21 mm; opening=3.8 mm; tolerance=2 mm. c_res=c0−opening−tolerance=15.2 mm. Increasing only opening by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 14.82 mm. Boundary: One-direction geometric reserve, not contact pressure or proof of watertightness. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]},{"id":"b108-v14-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「接頭壓縮與水密包絡」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Joint compression and sealing envelope\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：初始壓縮=21 mm；張開量=3.8 mm；幾何公差=2 mm。","動壓公式算出的數值就是長鐵路隧道完整壓力波。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: initial compression=21 mm; opening=3.8 mm; tolerance=2 mm. c_res=c0−opening−tolerance=15.2 mm.","A dynamic-pressure calculation is the complete pressure-wave prediction for a long rail tunnel.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：初始壓縮=21 mm；張開量=3.8 mm；幾何公差=2 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: initial compression=21 mm; opening=3.8 mm; tolerance=2 mm. c_res=c0−opening−tolerance=15.2 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b108-v14-19","title":"接頭壓縮與水密包絡：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Joint compression and sealing envelope: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b108-v14-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「止水壓縮餘量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Gasket compression reserve” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用組合位移試驗核對止水包絡而非單向壓縮。全尺寸接頭試驗分別改變張開、錯台與外水壓，記錄漏水起點與卸載後殘餘位移，對照材料批次及溫度。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check the seal envelope with combined displacement rather than compression alone. Vary opening, offset and pressure in full-size joint tests, recording leakage onset and residual movement against material batch and temperature. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「止水壓縮餘量」的交付需回答：用組合位移試驗核對止水包絡而非單向壓縮。保存接縫幾何與試驗壓力的配對紀錄，由設計者核定允收包絡；驗收時不能把課堂的幾何餘量當產品認證數字。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Marmaray immersed tunnel, the gasket compression reserve handover must address the following evidence: Check the seal envelope with combined displacement rather than compression alone. Retain paired joint geometry and test pressure, with the designer approving the acceptance envelope; classroom geometric reserves are not product certification values.","failure":"注意干擾：只驗張開而未驗剪移可能漏掉止水翻轉或局部脫離。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Testing opening without shear can miss gasket roll or local separation. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b108-v14-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用組合位移試驗核對止水包絡而非單向壓縮。全尺寸接頭試驗分別改變張開、錯台與外水壓，記錄漏水起點與卸載後殘餘位移，對照材料批次及溫度。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Check the seal envelope with combined displacement rather than compression alone. Vary opening, offset and pressure in full-size joint tests, recording leakage onset and residual movement against material batch and temperature. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]},{"id":"b108-v14-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「止水壓縮餘量」的交付需回答：用組合位移試驗核對止水包絡而非單向壓縮。保存接縫幾何與試驗壓力的配對紀錄，由設計者核定允收包絡；驗收時不能把課堂的幾何餘量當產品認證數字。","textEn":"For Marmaray immersed tunnel, the gasket compression reserve handover must address the following evidence: Check the seal envelope with combined displacement rather than compression alone. Retain paired joint geometry and test pressure, with the designer approving the acceptance envelope; classroom geometric reserves are not product certification values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「接頭壓縮與水密包絡」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Joint compression and sealing envelope\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","用組合位移試驗核對止水包絡而非單向壓縮。","剩餘浮力為正就代表浮運姿態在所有波況穩定。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Check the seal envelope with combined displacement rather than compression alone.","Positive residual buoyancy establishes stability in every sea state."],"answer":1,"explanation":"用組合位移試驗核對止水包絡而非單向壓縮。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check the seal envelope with combined displacement rather than compression alone. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b108-v14-20","title":"接頭壓縮與水密包絡：失效診斷","titleEn":"Joint compression and sealing envelope: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b108-v14-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「止水壓縮餘量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Gasket compression reserve” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只驗張開而未驗剪移可能漏掉止水翻轉或局部脫離。扭曲或沾污的止水條可形成旁通通道，即使平均縫寬合格仍可能漏水；盲目灌漿也可能只轉移出水位置。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Testing opening without shear can miss gasket roll or local separation. A twisted or contaminated gasket creates bypass leakage despite acceptable mean width; indiscriminate grouting may merely move the outlet. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：平均壓縮量不能掩蓋局部脫離；全尺寸試驗的結果只對測試過的幾何、水壓及荷載歷程有效，幾何餘量本身並不是接觸壓力。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Full-size test results apply only to their tested geometry, head and load history, while a calculated geometric reserve is neither contact pressure nor evidence of watertightness.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「接縫平均寬度合格就不必量測局部錯台及扭轉。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"An acceptable average joint width makes local offset and twist measurements unnecessary.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b108-v14-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只驗張開而未驗剪移可能漏掉止水翻轉或局部脫離。扭曲或沾污的止水條可形成旁通通道，即使平均縫寬合格仍可能漏水；盲目灌漿也可能只轉移出水位置。","textEn":"Testing opening without shear can miss gasket roll or local separation. A twisted or contaminated gasket creates bypass leakage despite acceptable mean width; indiscriminate grouting may merely move the outlet.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]},{"id":"b108-v14-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「接頭壓縮與水密包絡」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Joint compression and sealing envelope\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。","只驗張開而未驗剪移可能漏掉止水翻轉或局部脫離。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.","Testing opening without shear can miss gasket roll or local separation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"只驗張開而未驗剪移可能漏掉止水翻轉或局部脫離。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Testing opening without shear can miss gasket roll or local separation. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b108-v14-21","title":"控制網與貫通誤差：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b108-v14-20"],"objective":"說明「方向角誤差」如何影響馬爾馬拉海底隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Orientation error” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Marmaray immersed tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"水下管節與兩側鑽掘孔的控制網需要共同轉換，分析不同施工隊各自閉合但接合仍偏差的情境。長隧道的微小方向誤差會沿距離累積，地下控制網又缺少直接衛星定位，必須把地表基準可靠傳到洞內。閉合差很小不代表無系統誤差；尺度、折光、儀器定向與高程基準可能共同偏移，誤差相關性也使平方和估算失真。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「方向角誤差」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Underwater elements and bored approaches require common transformations even when each construction team reports a closed survey network. Small orientation errors accumulate over long drives, while underground networks lack direct satellite positioning and depend on transferring surface control. A small closure does not exclude systematic bias: scale, refraction, orientation and vertical datum may shift together. Correlated errors also invalidate a naive root-sum-square combination of supposedly independent observations. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Orientation error” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：控制長度=3840 m；方向偏角=2.5 arcsec。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: control length=3840 m; orientation error=2.5 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0465421 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「方向角誤差」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Orientation error”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b108-v14-21-k1","title":"控制網與貫通誤差","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error","text":"水下管節與兩側鑽掘孔的控制網需要共同轉換，分析不同施工隊各自閉合但接合仍偏差的情境。長隧道的微小方向誤差會沿距離累積，地下控制網又缺少直接衛星定位，必須把地表基準可靠傳到洞內。","textEn":"Underwater elements and bored approaches require common transformations even when each construction team reports a closed survey network. Small orientation errors accumulate over long drives, while underground networks lack direct satellite positioning and depend on transferring surface control.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]},{"id":"b108-v14-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「控制網與貫通誤差」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Control network and breakthrough error\" is correct?","options":["水下管節與兩側鑽掘孔的控制網需要共同轉換，分析不同施工隊各自閉合但接合仍偏差的情境。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。","基線隧道坡度很小，所以不必做牽引與制動分析。"],"optionsEn":["Underwater elements and bored approaches require common transformations even when each construction team reports a closed survey network.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.","A small base-tunnel gradient eliminates the need for traction and braking analysis."],"answer":0,"explanation":"水下管節與兩側鑽掘孔的控制網需要共同轉換，分析不同施工隊各自閉合但接合仍偏差的情境。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Underwater elements and bored approaches require common transformations even when each construction team reports a closed survey network. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b108-v14-22","title":"控制網與貫通誤差：定量估算","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b108-v14-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「方向角誤差」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Orientation error” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：控制長度=3840 m；方向偏角=2.5 arcsec。e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0465421 m。僅把方向偏角增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.0511963 m。邊界：小角度方向偏差，未加入控制網相關性及折光；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: control length=3840 m; orientation error=2.5 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0465421 m. Increasing only orientation error by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.0511963 m. Boundary: Small-angle orientation error without network correlation or refraction. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：由第三條獨立控制線核對交界方向與高程。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use a third independent control route to check interface direction and elevation.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b108-v14-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：控制長度=3840 m；方向偏角=2.5 arcsec。e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0465421 m。僅把方向偏角增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.0511963 m。邊界：小角度方向偏差，未加入控制網相關性及折光；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: control length=3840 m; orientation error=2.5 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0465421 m. Increasing only orientation error by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.0511963 m. Boundary: Small-angle orientation error without network correlation or refraction. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]},{"id":"b108-v14-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「控制網與貫通誤差」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Control network and breakthrough error\", which statement holds?","options":["只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。","原創教學假設：控制長度=3840 m；方向偏角=2.5 arcsec。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.","Original teaching assumptions: control length=3840 m; orientation error=2.5 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0465421 m.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：控制長度=3840 m；方向偏角=2.5 arcsec。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: control length=3840 m; orientation error=2.5 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0465421 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b108-v14-23","title":"控制網與貫通誤差：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b108-v14-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「方向角誤差」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Orientation error” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"由第三條獨立控制線核對交界方向與高程。由獨立測量組複核地表到洞內的轉換，保留原始角距及溫度資料，用不同控制線比較方向與高程偏差。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use a third independent control route to check interface direction and elevation. Independently check surface-to-tunnel transformations, retain raw angles, distances and temperatures, and compare orientation and elevation through separate control routes. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「方向角誤差」的交付需回答：由第三條獨立控制線核對交界方向與高程。貫通前凍結座標、尺度與高程版本，獨立組直接使用原始觀測重算；不得只傳遞整理好的坐標而遺失校正資訊。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Marmaray immersed tunnel, the orientation error handover must address the following evidence: Use a third independent control route to check interface direction and elevation. Freeze coordinate, scale and height revisions before breakthrough; independent reviewers recompute raw observations rather than receiving only adjusted coordinates without corrections.","failure":"注意干擾：共用錯誤岸基點會使三段各自看似正確卻整體偏移。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A wrong shore benchmark can make separately consistent sections collectively misplaced. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b108-v14-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"由第三條獨立控制線核對交界方向與高程。由獨立測量組複核地表到洞內的轉換，保留原始角距及溫度資料，用不同控制線比較方向與高程偏差。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Use a third independent control route to check interface direction and elevation. Independently check surface-to-tunnel transformations, retain raw angles, distances and temperatures, and compare orientation and elevation through separate control routes. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]},{"id":"b108-v14-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「方向角誤差」的交付需回答：由第三條獨立控制線核對交界方向與高程。貫通前凍結座標、尺度與高程版本，獨立組直接使用原始觀測重算；不得只傳遞整理好的坐標而遺失校正資訊。","textEn":"For Marmaray immersed tunnel, the orientation error handover must address the following evidence: Use a third independent control route to check interface direction and elevation. Freeze coordinate, scale and height revisions before breakthrough; independent reviewers recompute raw observations rather than receiving only adjusted coordinates without corrections.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「控制網與貫通誤差」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Control network and breakthrough error\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","矩形沉管可以直接使用圓環均勻外壓公式設計。","由第三條獨立控制線核對交界方向與高程。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","A rectangular immersed tube can be designed directly with a circular-ring pressure formula.","Use a third independent control route to check interface direction and elevation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"由第三條獨立控制線核對交界方向與高程。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use a third independent control route to check interface direction and elevation. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b108-v14-24","title":"控制網與貫通誤差：失效診斷","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b108-v14-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「方向角誤差」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Orientation error” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"共用錯誤岸基點會使三段各自看似正確卻整體偏移。共用錯誤基準可能讓兩組測量同時看似一致，直到貫通或軌道銜接才發現系統偏差，修正成本遠高於早期複核。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A wrong shore benchmark can make separately consistent sections collectively misplaced. A shared wrong datum can make separate surveys appear consistent until breakthrough or track connection exposes bias that is costly to correct. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：閉合差很小不代表無系統誤差；尺度、折光、儀器定向與高程基準可能共同偏移，誤差相關性也使平方和估算失真。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Correlated errors also invalidate a naive root-sum-square combination of supposedly independent observations.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b108-v14-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"共用錯誤岸基點會使三段各自看似正確卻整體偏移。共用錯誤基準可能讓兩組測量同時看似一致，直到貫通或軌道銜接才發現系統偏差，修正成本遠高於早期複核。","textEn":"A wrong shore benchmark can make separately consistent sections collectively misplaced. A shared wrong datum can make separate surveys appear consistent until breakthrough or track connection exposes bias that is costly to correct.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]},{"id":"b108-v14-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「控制網與貫通誤差」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Control network and breakthrough error\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["共用錯誤岸基點會使三段各自看似正確卻整體偏移。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","基線隧道坡度很小，所以不必做牽引與制動分析。"],"optionsEn":["A wrong shore benchmark can make separately consistent sections collectively misplaced.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","A small base-tunnel gradient eliminates the need for traction and braking analysis."],"answer":0,"explanation":"共用錯誤岸基點會使三段各自看似正確卻整體偏移。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A wrong shore benchmark can make separately consistent sections collectively misplaced. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b108-v14-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「基線縱坡與牽引需求」與「列車壓力波與動壓量級」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Base-alignment grade and traction demand\" and \"Train pressure waves and dynamic-pressure scale\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b108-v14-25","title":"基線縱坡與牽引需求：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Base-alignment grade and traction demand: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b108-v14-24"],"objective":"說明「坡度阻力功率」如何影響馬爾馬拉海底隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Grade-resistance power” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Marmaray immersed tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"馬爾馬拉鐵路的坡度功率教材與車站加速分開，研究水下低點兩側坡段的符號和能量方向。基線鐵路用較小縱坡降低重載列車的重力阻力，但仍有滾動、空氣阻力及加速需求。土建線形和供電容量必須使用同一列車與速度情境，短距陡坡也不能被平均坡度掩蓋；制動方向的能量處理則是另一個需要獨立檢核的工況。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「坡度阻力功率」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Separate grade power from station acceleration and examine slope sign and energy direction on either side of the low point. A base alignment reduces heavy-train gravity resistance through gentler gradients, but rolling resistance, aerodynamic drag and acceleration remain. Civil geometry and power capacity must use consistent train and speed cases. Short steep sections cannot be hidden in an average gradient, while braking energy in the opposite direction requires its own operating and electrical assessment. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Grade-resistance power” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：列車質量=1.34e+06 kg；縱坡=0.0062 無因次；速度=20 m/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: train mass=1.34e+06 kg; grade=0.0062 dimensionless; speed=20 m/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「基線隧道坡度很小，所以不必做牽引與制動分析。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A small base-tunnel gradient eliminates the need for traction and braking analysis.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「坡度阻力功率」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Grade-resistance power”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b108-v14-25-k1","title":"基線縱坡與牽引需求","titleEn":"Base-alignment grade and traction demand","text":"馬爾馬拉鐵路的坡度功率教材與車站加速分開，研究水下低點兩側坡段的符號和能量方向。基線鐵路用較小縱坡降低重載列車的重力阻力，但仍有滾動、空氣阻力及加速需求。","textEn":"Separate grade power from station acceleration and examine slope sign and energy direction on either side of the low point. A base alignment reduces heavy-train gravity resistance through gentler gradients, but rolling resistance, aerodynamic drag and acceleration remain.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]},{"id":"b108-v14-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：基線隧道坡度很小，所以不必做牽引與制動分析。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A small base-tunnel gradient eliminates the need for traction and braking analysis. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「基線縱坡與牽引需求」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Base-alignment grade and traction demand\" is correct?","options":["基線隧道坡度很小，所以不必做牽引與制動分析。","馬爾馬拉鐵路的坡度功率教材與車站加速分開，研究水下低點兩側坡段的符號和能量方向。","動壓公式算出的數值就是長鐵路隧道完整壓力波。"],"optionsEn":["A small base-tunnel gradient eliminates the need for traction and braking analysis.","Separate grade power from station acceleration and examine slope sign and energy direction on either side of the low point.","A dynamic-pressure calculation is the complete pressure-wave prediction for a long rail tunnel."],"answer":1,"explanation":"馬爾馬拉鐵路的坡度功率教材與車站加速分開，研究水下低點兩側坡段的符號和能量方向。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Separate grade power from station acceleration and examine slope sign and energy direction on either side of the low point. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b108-v14-26","title":"基線縱坡與牽引需求：定量估算","titleEn":"Base-alignment grade and traction demand: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b108-v14-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「坡度阻力功率」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Grade-resistance power” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：列車質量=1.34e+06 kg；縱坡=0.0062 無因次；速度=20 m/s。P=mgiv/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=1630.03 kW。僅把縱坡增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為1793.03 kW。邊界：僅坡度阻力，不含滾動、氣動、加速及效率；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: train mass=1.34e+06 kg; grade=0.0062 dimensionless; speed=20 m/s. P=mgiv/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=1630.03 kW. Increasing only grade by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 1793.03 kW. Boundary: Grade resistance only, excluding rolling, aerodynamic, acceleration and efficiency losses. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：按行車方向重算上坡與下坡分量並核對質量。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Recompute uphill and downhill terms by travel direction and check mass.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b108-v14-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：列車質量=1.34e+06 kg；縱坡=0.0062 無因次；速度=20 m/s。P=mgiv/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=1630.03 kW。僅把縱坡增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為1793.03 kW。邊界：僅坡度阻力，不含滾動、氣動、加速及效率；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: train mass=1.34e+06 kg; grade=0.0062 dimensionless; speed=20 m/s. P=mgiv/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=1630.03 kW. Increasing only grade by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 1793.03 kW. Boundary: Grade resistance only, excluding rolling, aerodynamic, acceleration and efficiency losses. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]},{"id":"b108-v14-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「基線縱坡與牽引需求」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Base-alignment grade and traction demand\", which statement holds?","options":["全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。","剩餘浮力為正就代表浮運姿態在所有波況穩定。","原創教學假設：列車質量=1.34e+06 kg；縱坡=0.0062 無因次；速度=20 m/s。"],"optionsEn":["Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.","Positive residual buoyancy establishes stability in every sea state.","Original teaching assumptions: train mass=1.34e+06 kg; grade=0.0062 dimensionless; speed=20 m/s."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：列車質量=1.34e+06 kg；縱坡=0.0062 無因次；速度=20 m/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: train mass=1.34e+06 kg; grade=0.0062 dimensionless; speed=20 m/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b108-v14-27","title":"基線縱坡與牽引需求：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Base-alignment grade and traction demand: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b108-v14-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「坡度阻力功率」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Grade-resistance power” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"按行車方向重算上坡與下坡分量並核對質量。以里程高程表逐段計算坡度，對照列車性能曲線和供電模型，另檢核低速牽引及下坡制動，不只比較平均功率。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Recompute uphill and downhill terms by travel direction and check mass. Calculate local grades from chainage and elevation, compare with train-performance and power models, and separately check low-speed traction and downhill braking. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「坡度阻力功率」的交付需回答：按行車方向重算上坡與下坡分量並核對質量。軌頂高程交付前，由土建、軌道、供電和營運共同確認同版線形及列車包絡，變更坡度時同步更新性能與容量計算。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Marmaray immersed tunnel, the grade-resistance power handover must address the following evidence: Recompute uphill and downhill terms by travel direction and check mass. Civil, track, power and operations teams approve one alignment and train envelope before handover; grade changes update both performance and capacity calculations.","failure":"注意干擾：忘記坡度方向會把制動需求錯記成牽引需求。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Ignoring slope sign misclassifies braking demand as traction demand. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b108-v14-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"按行車方向重算上坡與下坡分量並核對質量。以里程高程表逐段計算坡度，對照列車性能曲線和供電模型，另檢核低速牽引及下坡制動，不只比較平均功率。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Recompute uphill and downhill terms by travel direction and check mass. Calculate local grades from chainage and elevation, compare with train-performance and power models, and separately check low-speed traction and downhill braking. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]},{"id":"b108-v14-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「坡度阻力功率」的交付需回答：按行車方向重算上坡與下坡分量並核對質量。軌頂高程交付前，由土建、軌道、供電和營運共同確認同版線形及列車包絡，變更坡度時同步更新性能與容量計算。","textEn":"For Marmaray immersed tunnel, the grade-resistance power handover must address the following evidence: Recompute uphill and downhill terms by travel direction and check mass. Civil, track, power and operations teams approve one alignment and train envelope before handover; grade changes update both performance and capacity calculations.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「基線縱坡與牽引需求」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Base-alignment grade and traction demand\"?","options":["按行車方向重算上坡與下坡分量並核對質量。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","各管節平均高程接近就能排除接頭差異變形。"],"optionsEn":["Recompute uphill and downhill terms by travel direction and check mass.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Similar mean element elevations exclude differential movement at joints."],"answer":0,"explanation":"按行車方向重算上坡與下坡分量並核對質量。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Recompute uphill and downhill terms by travel direction and check mass. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b108-v14-28","title":"基線縱坡與牽引需求：失效診斷","titleEn":"Base-alignment grade and traction demand: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b108-v14-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「坡度阻力功率」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Grade-resistance power” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"忘記坡度方向會把制動需求錯記成牽引需求。平均坡度低卻存在短陡坡時，峰值功率可能超過預估，速度下降又會增加區段占用時間，牽連營運容量。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Ignoring slope sign misclassifies braking demand as traction demand. A short steep grade can exceed power estimates despite a low average, reducing speed and extending block occupation with capacity consequences. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：土建線形和供電容量必須使用同一列車與速度情境，短距陡坡也不能被平均坡度掩蓋；制動方向的能量處理則是另一個需要獨立檢核的工況。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Short steep sections cannot be hidden in an average gradient, while braking energy in the opposite direction requires its own operating and electrical assessment.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「基線隧道坡度很小，所以不必做牽引與制動分析。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A small base-tunnel gradient eliminates the need for traction and braking analysis.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b108-v14-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"忘記坡度方向會把制動需求錯記成牽引需求。平均坡度低卻存在短陡坡時，峰值功率可能超過預估，速度下降又會增加區段占用時間，牽連營運容量。","textEn":"Ignoring slope sign misclassifies braking demand as traction demand. A short steep grade can exceed power estimates despite a low average, reducing speed and extending block occupation with capacity consequences.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]},{"id":"b108-v14-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「基線縱坡與牽引需求」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Base-alignment grade and traction demand\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","忘記坡度方向會把制動需求錯記成牽引需求。","動壓公式算出的數值就是長鐵路隧道完整壓力波。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Ignoring slope sign misclassifies braking demand as traction demand.","A dynamic-pressure calculation is the complete pressure-wave prediction for a long rail tunnel."],"answer":1,"explanation":"忘記坡度方向會把制動需求錯記成牽引需求。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Ignoring slope sign misclassifies braking demand as traction demand. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b108-v14-29","title":"列車壓力波與動壓量級：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Train pressure waves and dynamic-pressure scale: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b108-v14-28"],"objective":"說明「入口壓力擾動」如何影響馬爾馬拉海底隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Portal pressure disturbance” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Marmaray immersed tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"沉管與鑽掘斷面改變可反射列車壓力波，馬爾馬拉教學將動壓尺度和交界波形分開。列車進洞壓縮前方空氣，波動在洞口、橫通道和斷面變化處傳播與反射。速度和阻塞比影響壓力量級，但不可壓動壓只是比較尺度，不能替代可壓縮瞬變計算；兩車交會、門位與列車外形都可能改變乘客及設備的壓力歷程。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「入口壓力擾動」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Changes between immersed and bored sections can reflect train pressure waves; separate dynamic-pressure scaling from interface wave shape. A train entering a tunnel compresses the air ahead, producing waves reflected at portals, passages and section changes. Speed and blockage influence magnitude, but incompressible dynamic pressure is only a comparison scale, not a compressible transient solution. Train encounters, door states and vehicle shape change the pressure histories experienced by passengers and equipment. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Portal pressure disturbance” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；列車速度=47 m/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: air density=1.2 kg/m³; train speed=47 m/s. q=ρv²/2=1325.4 Pa.","failure":"常見誤解：「動壓公式算出的數值就是長鐵路隧道完整壓力波。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A dynamic-pressure calculation is the complete pressure-wave prediction for a long rail tunnel.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「入口壓力擾動」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Portal pressure disturbance”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b108-v14-29-k1","title":"列車壓力波與動壓量級","titleEn":"Train pressure waves and dynamic-pressure scale","text":"沉管與鑽掘斷面改變可反射列車壓力波，馬爾馬拉教學將動壓尺度和交界波形分開。列車進洞壓縮前方空氣，波動在洞口、橫通道和斷面變化處傳播與反射。","textEn":"Changes between immersed and bored sections can reflect train pressure waves; separate dynamic-pressure scaling from interface wave shape. A train entering a tunnel compresses the air ahead, producing waves reflected at portals, passages and section changes.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]},{"id":"b108-v14-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：動壓公式算出的數值就是長鐵路隧道完整壓力波。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A dynamic-pressure calculation is the complete pressure-wave prediction for a long rail tunnel. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「列車壓力波與動壓量級」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Train pressure waves and dynamic-pressure scale\" is correct?","options":["動壓公式算出的數值就是長鐵路隧道完整壓力波。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。","沉管與鑽掘斷面改變可反射列車壓力波，馬爾馬拉教學將動壓尺度和交界波形分開。"],"optionsEn":["A dynamic-pressure calculation is the complete pressure-wave prediction for a long rail tunnel.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.","Changes between immersed and bored sections can reflect train pressure waves; separate dynamic-pressure scaling from interface wave shape."],"answer":2,"explanation":"沉管與鑽掘斷面改變可反射列車壓力波，馬爾馬拉教學將動壓尺度和交界波形分開。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Changes between immersed and bored sections can reflect train pressure waves; separate dynamic-pressure scaling from interface wave shape. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b108-v14-30","title":"列車壓力波與動壓量級：定量估算","titleEn":"Train pressure waves and dynamic-pressure scale: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b108-v14-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「入口壓力擾動」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Portal pressure disturbance” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；列車速度=47 m/s。q=ρv²/2=1325.4 Pa。僅把列車速度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為1603.73 Pa。邊界：不可壓動壓尺度，不是可壓縮列車壓力波解；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: air density=1.2 kg/m³; train speed=47 m/s. q=ρv²/2=1325.4 Pa. Increasing only train speed by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 1603.73 Pa. Boundary: Incompressible dynamic-pressure scale, not a compressible train pressure-wave solution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比較交界前後時間對齊的壓力訊號與車速。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare time-aligned pressure signals and train speed across the transition.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b108-v14-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；列車速度=47 m/s。q=ρv²/2=1325.4 Pa。僅把列車速度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為1603.73 Pa。邊界：不可壓動壓尺度，不是可壓縮列車壓力波解；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: air density=1.2 kg/m³; train speed=47 m/s. q=ρv²/2=1325.4 Pa. Increasing only train speed by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 1603.73 Pa. Boundary: Incompressible dynamic-pressure scale, not a compressible train pressure-wave solution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]},{"id":"b108-v14-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「列車壓力波與動壓量級」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Train pressure waves and dynamic-pressure scale\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；列車速度=47 m/s。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。","矩形沉管可以直接使用圓環均勻外壓公式設計。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: air density=1.2 kg/m³; train speed=47 m/s. q=ρv²/2=1325.4 Pa.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.","A rectangular immersed tube can be designed directly with a circular-ring pressure formula."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；列車速度=47 m/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: air density=1.2 kg/m³; train speed=47 m/s. q=ρv²/2=1325.4 Pa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b108-v14-31","title":"列車壓力波與動壓量級：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Train pressure waves and dynamic-pressure scale: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b108-v14-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「入口壓力擾動」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Portal pressure disturbance” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比較交界前後時間對齊的壓力訊號與車速。以相同列車編組、速度和門位量測多點壓力歷程，檢查峰值、上升時間及反射抵達時刻，而不只比較一個最大值。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare time-aligned pressure signals and train speed across the transition. Measure pressure histories at several points with matching train formation, speed and door states, comparing rise time and reflection arrival as well as peaks. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「入口壓力擾動」的交付需回答：比較交界前後時間對齊的壓力訊號與車速。試車報告記錄編組、速度、溫度及門位版本，土建斷面變更與設備耐壓驗證共用同一氣動模型，不能各自選有利情境。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Marmaray immersed tunnel, the portal pressure disturbance handover must address the following evidence: Compare time-aligned pressure signals and train speed across the transition. Trial reports retain formation, speed, temperature and door revisions; civil changes and equipment-pressure checks share one aerodynamic model rather than selectively favourable cases.","failure":"注意干擾：將交界反射峰當作車速增加會誤判氣動因果。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Mistaking a reflection peak for a speed increase misidentifies the aerodynamic cause. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b108-v14-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比較交界前後時間對齊的壓力訊號與車速。以相同列車編組、速度和門位量測多點壓力歷程，檢查峰值、上升時間及反射抵達時刻，而不只比較一個最大值。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Compare time-aligned pressure signals and train speed across the transition. Measure pressure histories at several points with matching train formation, speed and door states, comparing rise time and reflection arrival as well as peaks. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]},{"id":"b108-v14-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「入口壓力擾動」的交付需回答：比較交界前後時間對齊的壓力訊號與車速。試車報告記錄編組、速度、溫度及門位版本，土建斷面變更與設備耐壓驗證共用同一氣動模型，不能各自選有利情境。","textEn":"For Marmaray immersed tunnel, the portal pressure disturbance handover must address the following evidence: Compare time-aligned pressure signals and train speed across the transition. Trial reports retain formation, speed, temperature and door revisions; civil changes and equipment-pressure checks share one aerodynamic model rather than selectively favourable cases.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「列車壓力波與動壓量級」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Train pressure waves and dynamic-pressure scale\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","比較交界前後時間對齊的壓力訊號與車速。","接縫平均寬度合格就不必量測局部錯台及扭轉。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Compare time-aligned pressure signals and train speed across the transition.","An acceptable average joint width makes local offset and twist measurements unnecessary."],"answer":1,"explanation":"比較交界前後時間對齊的壓力訊號與車速。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare time-aligned pressure signals and train speed across the transition. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b108-v14-32","title":"列車壓力波與動壓量級：失效診斷","titleEn":"Train pressure waves and dynamic-pressure scale: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b108-v14-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「入口壓力擾動」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Portal pressure disturbance” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"將交界反射峰當作車速增加會誤判氣動因果。以單一動壓數字當允收值會漏掉壓力梯度與反射疊加，可能使門扇、密封或乘客舒適度需求被低估。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Mistaking a reflection peak for a speed increase misidentifies the aerodynamic cause. Using one dynamic-pressure value for acceptance misses gradients and superposed reflections, understating demands on doors, seals or passenger comfort. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：速度和阻塞比影響壓力量級，但不可壓動壓只是比較尺度，不能替代可壓縮瞬變計算；兩車交會、門位與列車外形都可能改變乘客及設備的壓力歷程。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Train encounters, door states and vehicle shape change the pressure histories experienced by passengers and equipment.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「動壓公式算出的數值就是長鐵路隧道完整壓力波。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A dynamic-pressure calculation is the complete pressure-wave prediction for a long rail tunnel.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b108-v14-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"將交界反射峰當作車速增加會誤判氣動因果。以單一動壓數字當允收值會漏掉壓力梯度與反射疊加，可能使門扇、密封或乘客舒適度需求被低估。","textEn":"Mistaking a reflection peak for a speed increase misidentifies the aerodynamic cause. Using one dynamic-pressure value for acceptance misses gradients and superposed reflections, understating demands on doors, seals or passenger comfort.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]},{"id":"b108-v14-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「列車壓力波與動壓量級」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Train pressure waves and dynamic-pressure scale\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。","將交界反射峰當作車速增加會誤判氣動因果。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.","Mistaking a reflection peak for a speed increase misidentifies the aerodynamic cause."],"answer":2,"explanation":"將交界反射峰當作車速增加會誤判氣動因果。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Mistaking a reflection peak for a speed increase misidentifies the aerodynamic cause. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b108-v14-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「疏散時間與分區可用性」與「資產編碼與可追溯交接」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Evacuation time and zone availability\" and \"Asset identity and traceable handover\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b108-v14-33","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b108-v14-32"],"objective":"說明「所需疏散時間」如何影響馬爾馬拉海底隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Required evacuation time” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Marmaray immersed tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"都市鐵路使用者密度和下車位置改變通道壅塞，馬爾馬拉案例需分別檢查列車與車站介面。疏散時間包含辨識、反應、移動及排隊，不只由出口距離決定。人員速度會受煙熱、能見度及行動能力影響，安全判斷還要比較可用安全時間；橫通道存在但門或鄰孔不可用時，圖上的最短路線不一定能作實際選擇。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「所需疏散時間」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Urban passenger density and detraining position change passage congestion, requiring separate train and station-interface checks. Evacuation includes detection, response, travel and queues, not merely distance to an exit. Smoke, visibility and mobility alter walking speed, while safety requires comparison with available safe time. A passage shown on a plan may be unusable because its door or receiving bore is unavailable, invalidating the nominal shortest route. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Required evacuation time” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：前置時間=94 s；行走距離=360 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=94 s; travel distance=360 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「所需疏散時間」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Required evacuation time”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b108-v14-33-k1","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability","text":"都市鐵路使用者密度和下車位置改變通道壅塞，馬爾馬拉案例需分別檢查列車與車站介面。疏散時間包含辨識、反應、移動及排隊，不只由出口距離決定。","textEn":"Urban passenger density and detraining position change passage congestion, requiring separate train and station-interface checks. Evacuation includes detection, response, travel and queues, not merely distance to an exit.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]},{"id":"b108-v14-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「疏散時間與分區可用性」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Evacuation time and zone availability\" is correct?","options":["都市鐵路使用者密度和下車位置改變通道壅塞，馬爾馬拉案例需分別檢查列車與車站介面。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。"],"optionsEn":["Urban passenger density and detraining position change passage congestion, requiring separate train and station-interface checks.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted."],"answer":0,"explanation":"都市鐵路使用者密度和下車位置改變通道壅塞，馬爾馬拉案例需分別檢查列車與車站介面。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Urban passenger density and detraining position change passage congestion, requiring separate train and station-interface checks. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b108-v14-34","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性：定量估算","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b108-v14-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「所需疏散時間」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Required evacuation time” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：前置時間=94 s；行走距離=360 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。RSET=tpre+d/v=544 s。僅把行走距離增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為589 s。邊界：單群體固定速度，不含排隊煙熱及能力差異，不能單獨判安全；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=94 s; travel distance=360 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s. RSET=tpre+d/v=544 s. Increasing only travel distance by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 589 s. Boundary: One group at fixed speed without queues, smoke or mobility differences; not a safety conclusion. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：把下車流率與通道行走時間分開量測。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure detraining flow rate separately from passage walking time.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b108-v14-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：前置時間=94 s；行走距離=360 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。RSET=tpre+d/v=544 s。僅把行走距離增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為589 s。邊界：單群體固定速度，不含排隊煙熱及能力差異，不能單獨判安全；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=94 s; travel distance=360 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s. RSET=tpre+d/v=544 s. Increasing only travel distance by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 589 s. Boundary: One group at fixed speed without queues, smoke or mobility differences; not a safety conclusion. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]},{"id":"b108-v14-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「疏散時間與分區可用性」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Evacuation time and zone availability\", which statement holds?","options":["剩餘浮力為正就代表浮運姿態在所有波況穩定。","原創教學假設：前置時間=94 s；行走距離=360 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。","各管節平均高程接近就能排除接頭差異變形。"],"optionsEn":["Positive residual buoyancy establishes stability in every sea state.","Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=94 s; travel distance=360 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s.","Similar mean element elevations exclude differential movement at joints."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：前置時間=94 s；行走距離=360 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=94 s; travel distance=360 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b108-v14-35","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b108-v14-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「所需疏散時間」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Required evacuation time” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"把下車流率與通道行走時間分開量測。以人流模擬或受控演練分辨前置時間、行走與門口排隊，核對每個出口接收區的可用狀態及通訊紀錄。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure detraining flow rate separately from passage walking time. Separate pre-movement, travel and doorway queues through simulation or controlled drills, checking receiving-zone availability and communication records for each exit. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「所需疏散時間」的交付需回答：把下車流率與通道行走時間分開量測。疏散模型保留人口、速度分布及出口狀態，演練改動由營運與防災責任者批准，教材算例不得當作現場指揮程序。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Marmaray immersed tunnel, the required evacuation time handover must address the following evidence: Measure detraining flow rate separately from passage walking time. Retain population, speed distribution and exit states; operations and fire-safety owners approve drill changes, and classroom calculations are not incident-command procedures.","failure":"注意干擾：以空通道步速代表滿載列車撤離會漏掉排隊。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using empty-passage speed for a full train omits queuing. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b108-v14-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"把下車流率與通道行走時間分開量測。以人流模擬或受控演練分辨前置時間、行走與門口排隊，核對每個出口接收區的可用狀態及通訊紀錄。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Measure detraining flow rate separately from passage walking time. Separate pre-movement, travel and doorway queues through simulation or controlled drills, checking receiving-zone availability and communication records for each exit. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]},{"id":"b108-v14-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「所需疏散時間」的交付需回答：把下車流率與通道行走時間分開量測。疏散模型保留人口、速度分布及出口狀態，演練改動由營運與防災責任者批准，教材算例不得當作現場指揮程序。","textEn":"For Marmaray immersed tunnel, the required evacuation time handover must address the following evidence: Measure detraining flow rate separately from passage walking time. Retain population, speed distribution and exit states; operations and fire-safety owners approve drill changes, and classroom calculations are not incident-command procedures.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「疏散時間與分區可用性」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Evacuation time and zone availability\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。","把下車流率與通道行走時間分開量測。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.","Measure detraining flow rate separately from passage walking time."],"answer":2,"explanation":"把下車流率與通道行走時間分開量測。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure detraining flow rate separately from passage walking time. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b108-v14-36","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性：失效診斷","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b108-v14-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「所需疏散時間」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Required evacuation time” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"以空通道步速代表滿載列車撤離會漏掉排隊。以最快成人速度套全部旅客會低估需求，若忽略接收孔受煙或車流影響，疏散可能移到另一個危險邊界。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using empty-passage speed for a full train omits queuing. Applying the fastest adult speed to everyone understates demand; overlooking smoke or traffic in the receiving bore can transfer evacuees into another hazard. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：人員速度會受煙熱、能見度及行動能力影響，安全判斷還要比較可用安全時間；橫通道存在但門或鄰孔不可用時，圖上的最短路線不一定能作實際選擇。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A passage shown on a plan may be unusable because its door or receiving bore is unavailable, invalidating the nominal shortest route.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b108-v14-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"以空通道步速代表滿載列車撤離會漏掉排隊。以最快成人速度套全部旅客會低估需求，若忽略接收孔受煙或車流影響，疏散可能移到另一個危險邊界。","textEn":"Using empty-passage speed for a full train omits queuing. Applying the fastest adult speed to everyone understates demand; overlooking smoke or traffic in the receiving bore can transfer evacuees into another hazard.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]},{"id":"b108-v14-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「疏散時間與分區可用性」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Evacuation time and zone availability\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["以空通道步速代表滿載列車撤離會漏掉排隊。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。"],"optionsEn":["Using empty-passage speed for a full train omits queuing.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以空通道步速代表滿載列車撤離會漏掉排隊。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using empty-passage speed for a full train omits queuing. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b108-v14-37","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b108-v14-36"],"objective":"說明「資產資料完整度」如何影響馬爾馬拉海底隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Asset-record completeness” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Marmaray immersed tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"跨國承包介面使馬爾馬拉資料交付需要統一里程、設備名稱與語言版本，研究維護查詢的可追溯性。地下設備的竣工資料必須讓維護人員找到正確位置、材料批次和控制版本。只有上傳圖面而沒有變更歷程，無法分辨元件替換與真正劣化；告警、儀器、線路及工單使用一致識別碼，才可能把量測趨勢連回實際受力或水力系統。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「資產資料完整度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Cross-border contracting makes consistent chainage, naming and language revisions important for traceable maintenance queries. Handover must let maintainers find the correct location, material batch and control revision. Drawings without change history cannot distinguish replacement from deterioration. Consistent identifiers across alarms, instruments, circuits and work orders are essential for linking trends to the physical structural or hydraulic system instead of treating each record as an isolated file. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Asset-record completeness” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：設備總數=107 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: asset count=107 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=85.0467 %.","failure":"常見誤解：「全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「資產資料完整度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Asset-record completeness”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b108-v14-37-k1","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover","text":"跨國承包介面使馬爾馬拉資料交付需要統一里程、設備名稱與語言版本，研究維護查詢的可追溯性。地下設備的竣工資料必須讓維護人員找到正確位置、材料批次和控制版本。","textEn":"Cross-border contracting makes consistent chainage, naming and language revisions important for traceable maintenance queries. Handover must let maintainers find the correct location, material batch and control revision.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]},{"id":"b108-v14-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「資產編碼與可追溯交接」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Asset identity and traceable handover\" is correct?","options":["全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。","跨國承包介面使馬爾馬拉資料交付需要統一里程、設備名稱與語言版本，研究維護查詢的可追溯性。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.","Cross-border contracting makes consistent chainage, naming and language revisions important for traceable maintenance queries.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":1,"explanation":"跨國承包介面使馬爾馬拉資料交付需要統一里程、設備名稱與語言版本，研究維護查詢的可追溯性。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Cross-border contracting makes consistent chainage, naming and language revisions important for traceable maintenance queries. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b108-v14-38","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：定量估算","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b108-v14-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「資產資料完整度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Asset-record completeness” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：設備總數=107 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。coverage=100(N−missing)/N=85.0467 %。僅把缺紀錄數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為83.5514 %。邊界：資料完整度，不等於安全或可靠度；擾動為連續敏感度，實際個數為整數；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: asset count=107 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=85.0467 %. Increasing only missing records by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 83.5514 %. Boundary: Record completeness, not safety or reliability; perturbation is continuous sensitivity while actual counts are integers. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：抽查同一設備的現場標籤、翻譯圖紙與控制顯示。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Sample consistency among field labels, translated drawings and control displays.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b108-v14-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：設備總數=107 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。coverage=100(N−missing)/N=85.0467 %。僅把缺紀錄數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為83.5514 %。邊界：資料完整度，不等於安全或可靠度；擾動為連續敏感度，實際個數為整數；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: asset count=107 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=85.0467 %. Increasing only missing records by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 83.5514 %. Boundary: Record completeness, not safety or reliability; perturbation is continuous sensitivity while actual counts are integers. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]},{"id":"b108-v14-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「資產編碼與可追溯交接」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Asset identity and traceable handover\", which statement holds?","options":["矩形沉管可以直接使用圓環均勻外壓公式設計。","接縫平均寬度合格就不必量測局部錯台及扭轉。","原創教學假設：設備總數=107 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。"],"optionsEn":["A rectangular immersed tube can be designed directly with a circular-ring pressure formula.","An acceptable average joint width makes local offset and twist measurements unnecessary.","Original teaching assumptions: asset count=107 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=85.0467 %."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：設備總數=107 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: asset count=107 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=85.0467 %. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b108-v14-39","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b108-v14-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「資產資料完整度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Asset-record completeness” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"抽查同一設備的現場標籤、翻譯圖紙與控制顯示。抽取一條告警，從控制畫面追到設備、線路、圖面和工單，核對位置、版本及校正日期並記錄無法閉合的欄位。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Sample consistency among field labels, translated drawings and control displays. Trace a sampled alarm from screen to equipment, circuit, drawing and work order, checking location, revision and calibration dates and recording broken links. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「資產資料完整度」的交付需回答：抽查同一設備的現場標籤、翻譯圖紙與控制顯示。交接以可完成的定位、查找與復原任務驗證，由維護責任人確認現場可用性；完整度只是資料指標，不代表結構安全或設備可靠。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Marmaray immersed tunnel, the asset-record completeness handover must address the following evidence: Sample consistency among field labels, translated drawings and control displays. Validate handover through achievable location, retrieval and recovery tasks witnessed by maintainers; completeness measures records, not structural safety or equipment reliability.","failure":"注意干擾：翻譯名稱相似而識別碼不同會把檢修紀錄連到錯誤裝置。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Similar translated names with different identifiers can mislink maintenance records. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b108-v14-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"抽查同一設備的現場標籤、翻譯圖紙與控制顯示。抽取一條告警，從控制畫面追到設備、線路、圖面和工單，核對位置、版本及校正日期並記錄無法閉合的欄位。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Sample consistency among field labels, translated drawings and control displays. Trace a sampled alarm from screen to equipment, circuit, drawing and work order, checking location, revision and calibration dates and recording broken links. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]},{"id":"b108-v14-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「資產資料完整度」的交付需回答：抽查同一設備的現場標籤、翻譯圖紙與控制顯示。交接以可完成的定位、查找與復原任務驗證，由維護責任人確認現場可用性；完整度只是資料指標，不代表結構安全或設備可靠。","textEn":"For Marmaray immersed tunnel, the asset-record completeness handover must address the following evidence: Sample consistency among field labels, translated drawings and control displays. Validate handover through achievable location, retrieval and recovery tasks witnessed by maintainers; completeness measures records, not structural safety or equipment reliability.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「資產編碼與可追溯交接」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Asset identity and traceable handover\"?","options":["抽查同一設備的現場標籤、翻譯圖紙與控制顯示。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","基線隧道坡度很小，所以不必做牽引與制動分析。"],"optionsEn":["Sample consistency among field labels, translated drawings and control displays.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","A small base-tunnel gradient eliminates the need for traction and braking analysis."],"answer":0,"explanation":"抽查同一設備的現場標籤、翻譯圖紙與控制顯示。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Sample consistency among field labels, translated drawings and control displays. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b108-v14-40","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：失效診斷","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b108-v14-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「資產資料完整度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Asset-record completeness” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"翻譯名稱相似而識別碼不同會把檢修紀錄連到錯誤裝置。設備改名卻未更新控制畫面會引導人員隔離錯誤回路，材料批次缺漏則使同批缺陷無法追蹤到其他位置。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Similar translated names with different identifiers can mislink maintenance records. Renaming an asset without updating the screen can isolate the wrong circuit; missing material batches prevent tracing related defects at other locations. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：只有上傳圖面而沒有變更歷程，無法分辨元件替換與真正劣化；告警、儀器、線路及工單使用一致識別碼，才可能把量測趨勢連回實際受力或水力系統。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Consistent identifiers across alarms, instruments, circuits and work orders are essential for linking trends to the physical structural or hydraulic system instead of treating each record as an isolated file.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b108-v14-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"翻譯名稱相似而識別碼不同會把檢修紀錄連到錯誤裝置。設備改名卻未更新控制畫面會引導人員隔離錯誤回路，材料批次缺漏則使同批缺陷無法追蹤到其他位置。","textEn":"Similar translated names with different identifiers can mislink maintenance records. Renaming an asset without updating the screen can isolate the wrong circuit; missing material batches prevent tracing related defects at other locations.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]},{"id":"b108-v14-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「資產編碼與可追溯交接」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Asset identity and traceable handover\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","翻譯名稱相似而識別碼不同會把檢修紀錄連到錯誤裝置。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Similar translated names with different identifiers can mislink maintenance records.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":1,"explanation":"翻譯名稱相似而識別碼不同會把檢修紀錄連到錯誤裝置。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Similar translated names with different identifiers can mislink maintenance records. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b108","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b108-event-0"],"curriculumVersion":14,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000},{"id":"b109","title":"歐亞海底公路隧道","titleEn":"Eurasia Tunnel","category":"underground","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"歐亞隧道官方將計畫分為14.6公里走廊及其中5.4公里隧道與連接段，2016年開始服務。本課集中雙層道路圓形隧道：先檢查外水壓與襯砌，再分開樓板受力、通風、行車視覺及撤離；所有斷面尺寸及荷載算例均屬教學假設，不能當成實際設計值。","summaryEn":"The operator distinguishes a 14.6 km corridor from its 5.4 km tunnel-and-connection section and records service beginning in 2016. This course focuses on a circular tunnel with a double-deck roadway, linking external pressure and lining to deck loads, ventilation, driver vision and evacuation. All numerical section dimensions and loads are teaching assumptions.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"ug-landmarks","subcategoryTitle":"世界隧道與地下巨作","subcategoryTitleEn":"World tunnels and underground landmarks","learningTrack":"underground","learningSubdiscipline":"ug-landmarks","learningTags":["underground","ug-landmarks","tunnel"],"architectureFamily":"tunnel","architectureNodes":[["路線里程與端點","Alignment chainage and endpoints"],["測壓水頭","Piezometric head"],["襯砌環向壓縮","Lining hoop compression"],["止水壓縮餘量","Gasket compression reserve"],["漫反射亮度","Diffuse luminance"],["資產資料完整度","Asset-record completeness"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,5],[1,5]],"diagram":{"type":"tunnel","labels":["路線里程與端點","測壓水頭","襯砌環向壓縮","止水壓縮餘量","漫反射亮度"],"labelsEn":["Alignment chainage and endpoints","Piezometric head","Lining hoop compression","Gasket compression reserve","Diffuse luminance"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"原創綜合審查：先計算「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」，再獨立計算「接頭壓縮與水密包絡」。原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=63 m。p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=618.03 kPa。僅把水頭增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為679.833 kPa。邊界：靜水表壓，不是土體總壓或原位量測；不是本工程實測或允收值。原創教學假設：初始壓縮=18 mm；張開量=4 mm；幾何公差=2 mm。c_res=c0−opening−tolerance=12 mm。僅把張開量增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為11.6 mm。邊界：單向幾何餘量，不是接觸壓或水密合格證明；不是本工程實測或允收值。兩組結果的單位與邊界不同，不能直接相加。請列出一項缺少的現場輸入，說明它會影響哪個結論，以及哪種獨立量測可以縮小不確定度。","textEn":"Original integrated review: first calculate piezometric head and lining pressure, then independently calculate joint compression and sealing envelope. Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=63 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=618.03 kPa. Increasing only head by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 679.833 kPa. Boundary: Hydrostatic gauge pressure, not total earth pressure or an in-situ measurement. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Original teaching assumptions: initial compression=18 mm; opening=4 mm; tolerance=2 mm. c_res=c0−opening−tolerance=12 mm. Increasing only opening by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 11.6 mm. Boundary: One-direction geometric reserve, not contact pressure or proof of watertightness. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. The outputs have different units and boundaries and cannot simply be added. Identify one missing field input, explain which conclusion it changes and select an independent measurement to reduce uncertainty.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":14,"enrichmentVersion":14,"stages":[{"id":"b109-v14-s1","title":"地層條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Ground conditions, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「服務邊界與路線代價」與「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\" and \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b109-v14-01","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「路線里程與端點」如何影響歐亞海底公路隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Alignment chainage and endpoints” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Eurasia Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"歐亞道路走廊與隧道連接段有不同長度範圍，先固定起訖點再比較壅塞與自由行車時間。隧道選線同時改變洞口、覆土與縱坡，短路線不保證低地質風險。比較方案必須使用相同起訖點，並分開主孔、引道及服務坑的工程數量；交通時間只是需求的一個指標，不能代替施工可達性或長期維修評估。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「路線里程與端點」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The road corridor and tunnel connection have different scope lengths; fix endpoints before comparing congested and free-flow travel. Alignment changes portals, cover and gradient together, so a shorter tunnel need not have lower geological risk. Compare options between identical endpoints and distinguish running bores, approaches and service galleries. Travel time measures one service benefit but cannot replace assessment of construction access, maintenance closures or exposure to uncertain ground. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Alignment chainage and endpoints” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：長度=15.2 km；速度=60 km/h。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: length=15.2 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=15.2 min.","failure":"常見誤解：「最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「路線里程與端點」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Alignment chainage and endpoints”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b109-v14-01-k1","title":"服務邊界與路線代價","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost","text":"歐亞道路走廊與隧道連接段有不同長度範圍，先固定起訖點再比較壅塞與自由行車時間。隧道選線同時改變洞口、覆土與縱坡，短路線不保證低地質風險。","textEn":"The road corridor and tunnel connection have different scope lengths; fix endpoints before comparing congested and free-flow travel. Alignment changes portals, cover and gradient together, so a shorter tunnel need not have lower geological risk.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]},{"id":"b109-v14-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「服務邊界與路線代價」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\" is correct?","options":["最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。","歐亞道路走廊與隧道連接段有不同長度範圍，先固定起訖點再比較壅塞與自由行車時間。","目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。"],"optionsEn":["The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.","The road corridor and tunnel connection have different scope lengths; fix endpoints before comparing congested and free-flow travel.","No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design."],"answer":1,"explanation":"歐亞道路走廊與隧道連接段有不同長度範圍，先固定起訖點再比較壅塞與自由行車時間。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The road corridor and tunnel connection have different scope lengths; fix endpoints before comparing congested and free-flow travel. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b109-v14-02","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：定量估算","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b109-v14-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「路線里程與端點」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Alignment chainage and endpoints” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：長度=15.2 km；速度=60 km/h。t=60L/v=15.2 min。僅把長度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為16.72 min。邊界：假想交通旅程，未含加減速、排隊及實際時刻表；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: length=15.2 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=15.2 min. Increasing only length by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 16.72 min. Boundary: Hypothetical transport journey excluding acceleration, queues and the real timetable. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對時間資料是否包括市區引道及入口排隊。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check whether time data include urban approaches and entrance queues.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b109-v14-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：長度=15.2 km；速度=60 km/h。t=60L/v=15.2 min。僅把長度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為16.72 min。邊界：假想交通旅程，未含加減速、排隊及實際時刻表；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: length=15.2 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=15.2 min. Increasing only length by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 16.72 min. Boundary: Hypothetical transport journey excluding acceleration, queues and the real timetable. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]},{"id":"b109-v14-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「服務邊界與路線代價」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\", which statement holds?","options":["混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。","接縫平均寬度合格就不必量測局部錯台及扭轉。","原創教學假設：長度=15.2 km；速度=60 km/h。"],"optionsEn":["Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure.","An acceptable average joint width makes local offset and twist measurements unnecessary.","Original teaching assumptions: length=15.2 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=15.2 min."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：長度=15.2 km；速度=60 km/h。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: length=15.2 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=15.2 min. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b109-v14-03","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b109-v14-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「路線里程與端點」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Alignment chainage and endpoints” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對時間資料是否包括市區引道及入口排隊。把縱斷面、地形與地質剖面疊合，以端點坐標獨立反算距離，再將主孔與支坑數量分開核對。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check whether time data include urban approaches and entrance queues. Overlay the longitudinal profile, terrain and geology; independently derive distances from endpoint coordinates and reconcile running-bore and gallery quantities separately. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「路線里程與端點」的交付需回答：核對時間資料是否包括市區引道及入口排隊。在方案表中凍結起訖點、計量範圍及地質假設，任何改線都要同步更新高程、數量與服務情境，不能只替換總長。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Eurasia Tunnel, the alignment chainage and endpoints handover must address the following evidence: Check whether time data include urban approaches and entrance queues. Freeze endpoints, measurement scope and ground assumptions in the option register; realignment requires coordinated updates to elevations, quantities and service scenarios rather than replacing one length.","failure":"注意干擾：把隧道內時間宣稱為全走廊旅行時間會誇大效益。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Presenting in-tunnel time as whole-corridor time overstates the benefit. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b109-v14-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對時間資料是否包括市區引道及入口排隊。把縱斷面、地形與地質剖面疊合，以端點坐標獨立反算距離，再將主孔與支坑數量分開核對。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Check whether time data include urban approaches and entrance queues. Overlay the longitudinal profile, terrain and geology; independently derive distances from endpoint coordinates and reconcile running-bore and gallery quantities separately. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]},{"id":"b109-v14-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「路線里程與端點」的交付需回答：核對時間資料是否包括市區引道及入口排隊。在方案表中凍結起訖點、計量範圍及地質假設，任何改線都要同步更新高程、數量與服務情境，不能只替換總長。","textEn":"For Eurasia Tunnel, the alignment chainage and endpoints handover must address the following evidence: Check whether time data include urban approaches and entrance queues. Freeze endpoints, measurement scope and ground assumptions in the option register; realignment requires coordinated updates to elevations, quantities and service scenarios rather than replacing one length.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「服務邊界與路線代價」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\"?","options":["核對時間資料是否包括市區引道及入口排隊。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","照度越高就必然使隧道內所有物體更容易辨識。"],"optionsEn":["Check whether time data include urban approaches and entrance queues.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Higher illuminance necessarily makes every tunnel object easier to detect."],"answer":0,"explanation":"核對時間資料是否包括市區引道及入口排隊。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check whether time data include urban approaches and entrance queues. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b109-v14-04","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：失效診斷","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b109-v14-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「路線里程與端點」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Alignment chainage and endpoints” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把隧道內時間宣稱為全走廊旅行時間會誇大效益。混用全線與單孔長度會同時扭曲工程數量、行程及逃生距離，造成方案比較失去共同基準。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Presenting in-tunnel time as whole-corridor time overstates the benefit. Mixing whole-route and single-bore lengths distorts quantities, journey time and escape distance, destroying the common basis of an option comparison. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：比較方案必須使用相同起訖點，並分開主孔、引道及服務坑的工程數量；交通時間只是需求的一個指標，不能代替施工可達性或長期維修評估。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Travel time measures one service benefit but cannot replace assessment of construction access, maintenance closures or exposure to uncertain ground.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b109-v14-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把隧道內時間宣稱為全走廊旅行時間會誇大效益。混用全線與單孔長度會同時扭曲工程數量、行程及逃生距離，造成方案比較失去共同基準。","textEn":"Presenting in-tunnel time as whole-corridor time overstates the benefit. Mixing whole-route and single-bore lengths distorts quantities, journey time and escape distance, destroying the common basis of an option comparison.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]},{"id":"b109-v14-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「服務邊界與路線代價」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","把隧道內時間宣稱為全走廊旅行時間會誇大效益。","目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Presenting in-tunnel time as whole-corridor time overstates the benefit.","No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把隧道內時間宣稱為全走廊旅行時間會誇大效益。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Presenting in-tunnel time as whole-corridor time overstates the benefit. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b109-v14-05","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b109-v14-04"],"objective":"說明「測壓水頭」如何影響歐亞海底公路隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Piezometric head” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Eurasia Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"海底盾構段的外壓教材採測壓水頭，研究海面、地層和施工降水條件不一致的情境。水壓取決於連通含水層的測壓水頭，不必等於地表或海面至洞頂的幾何深度。排水降低水壓卻可能增加有效應力與沉陷；停泵或排水堵塞後水頭又會回升，因此防水、排水及環境保水是互相制約的設計選擇。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「測壓水頭」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Use piezometric head for the subsea bored section and examine differences among sea level, strata and construction drainage conditions. Water pressure follows piezometric head in the connected aquifer, not automatically the geometric depth below ground or sea level. Drainage reduces pressure but can increase effective stress and settlement. Head may recover after a pump outage or blockage, coupling waterproofing, drainage capacity and preservation of surrounding groundwater in the permanent design. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Piezometric head” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=63 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=63 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=618.03 kPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「測壓水頭」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Piezometric head”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b109-v14-05-k1","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure","text":"海底盾構段的外壓教材採測壓水頭，研究海面、地層和施工降水條件不一致的情境。水壓取決於連通含水層的測壓水頭，不必等於地表或海面至洞頂的幾何深度。","textEn":"Use piezometric head for the subsea bored section and examine differences among sea level, strata and construction drainage conditions. Water pressure follows piezometric head in the connected aquifer, not automatically the geometric depth below ground or sea level.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]},{"id":"b109-v14-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\" is correct?","options":["目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。","刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。","海底盾構段的外壓教材採測壓水頭，研究海面、地層和施工降水條件不一致的情境。"],"optionsEn":["No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.","A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance.","Use piezometric head for the subsea bored section and examine differences among sea level, strata and construction drainage conditions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"海底盾構段的外壓教材採測壓水頭，研究海面、地層和施工降水條件不一致的情境。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Use piezometric head for the subsea bored section and examine differences among sea level, strata and construction drainage conditions. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b109-v14-06","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓：定量估算","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b109-v14-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「測壓水頭」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Piezometric head” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=63 m。p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=618.03 kPa。僅把水頭增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為679.833 kPa。邊界：靜水表壓，不是土體總壓或原位量測；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=63 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=618.03 kPa. Increasing only head by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 679.833 kPa. Boundary: Hydrostatic gauge pressure, not total earth pressure or an in-situ measurement. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將孔壓與海潮序列比較，分辨延遲及隔離層。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare pore pressure with tidal histories to identify lag and isolated layers.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b109-v14-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=63 m。p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=618.03 kPa。僅把水頭增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為679.833 kPa。邊界：靜水表壓，不是土體總壓或原位量測；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=63 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=618.03 kPa. Increasing only head by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 679.833 kPa. Boundary: Hydrostatic gauge pressure, not total earth pressure or an in-situ measurement. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]},{"id":"b109-v14-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=63 m。","只要空間分成兩層就可以採用相同的樓板荷載。","風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=63 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=618.03 kPa.","Any space divided into two levels can use the same deck loading.","Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=63 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=63 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=618.03 kPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b109-v14-07","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b109-v14-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「測壓水頭」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Piezometric head” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將孔壓與海潮序列比較，分辨延遲及隔離層。使用分層測壓管及流量計，配合降雨或潮位序列分辨補注與設備影響，將讀值統一換算至同一高程基準。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare pore pressure with tidal histories to identify lag and isolated layers. Use nested piezometers and flowmeters with rainfall or tide histories to distinguish recharge from equipment effects, converting observations to a common elevation datum. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「測壓水頭」的交付需回答：將孔壓與海潮序列比較，分辨延遲及隔離層。設計檢核應分列正常排水、堵塞與停電水位，將環境受體的容許變化和監測責任一起交付，不把抽水量當唯一指標。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Eurasia Tunnel, the piezometric head handover must address the following evidence: Compare pore pressure with tidal histories to identify lag and isolated layers. Separate normal drainage, blocked-drain and power-outage heads and hand over receptor limits and monitoring responsibility together rather than using pump flow as the sole indicator.","failure":"注意干擾：直接以海面深度代替所有水頭會忽略地層連通差異。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Replacing all heads with sea depth ignores differences in connectivity. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b109-v14-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將孔壓與海潮序列比較，分辨延遲及隔離層。使用分層測壓管及流量計，配合降雨或潮位序列分辨補注與設備影響，將讀值統一換算至同一高程基準。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Compare pore pressure with tidal histories to identify lag and isolated layers. Use nested piezometers and flowmeters with rainfall or tide histories to distinguish recharge from equipment effects, converting observations to a common elevation datum. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]},{"id":"b109-v14-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「測壓水頭」的交付需回答：將孔壓與海潮序列比較，分辨延遲及隔離層。設計檢核應分列正常排水、堵塞與停電水位，將環境受體的容許變化和監測責任一起交付，不把抽水量當唯一指標。","textEn":"For Eurasia Tunnel, the piezometric head handover must address the following evidence: Compare pore pressure with tidal histories to identify lag and isolated layers. Separate normal drainage, blocked-drain and power-outage heads and hand over receptor limits and monitoring responsibility together rather than using pump flow as the sole indicator.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","將孔壓與海潮序列比較，分辨延遲及隔離層。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Compare pore pressure with tidal histories to identify lag and isolated layers.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time."],"answer":1,"explanation":"將孔壓與海潮序列比較，分辨延遲及隔離層。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare pore pressure with tidal histories to identify lag and isolated layers. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b109-v14-08","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓：失效診斷","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b109-v14-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「測壓水頭」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Piezometric head” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"直接以海面深度代替所有水頭會忽略地層連通差異。將暫時降水後的低水頭當成永久狀態，會漏掉停泵後外壓回升；過度排水也可能引起周邊地層壓密。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Replacing all heads with sea depth ignores differences in connectivity. Treating temporarily lowered head as permanent misses pressure recovery after outage; excessive drainage can also consolidate surrounding ground. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：排水降低水壓卻可能增加有效應力與沉陷；停泵或排水堵塞後水頭又會回升，因此防水、排水及環境保水是互相制約的設計選擇。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Head may recover after a pump outage or blockage, coupling waterproofing, drainage capacity and preservation of surrounding groundwater in the permanent design.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b109-v14-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"直接以海面深度代替所有水頭會忽略地層連通差異。將暫時降水後的低水頭當成永久狀態，會漏掉停泵後外壓回升；過度排水也可能引起周邊地層壓密。","textEn":"Replacing all heads with sea depth ignores differences in connectivity. Treating temporarily lowered head as permanent misses pressure recovery after outage; excessive drainage can also consolidate surrounding ground.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]},{"id":"b109-v14-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。","直接以海面深度代替所有水頭會忽略地層連通差異。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance.","Replacing all heads with sea depth ignores differences in connectivity."],"answer":2,"explanation":"直接以海面深度代替所有水頭會忽略地層連通差異。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Replacing all heads with sea depth ignores differences in connectivity. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b109-v14-s2","title":"機制、材料與定量設計","titleEn":"Mechanisms, materials and quantitative design","description":"本階段聚焦「掘進利用率與設備停時」與「環向受力與接縫柔度」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime\" and \"Ring force and joint flexibility\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b109-v14-09","title":"掘進利用率與設備停時：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b109-v14-08"],"objective":"說明「有效掘進利用率」如何影響歐亞海底公路隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Effective boring utilisation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Eurasia Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"歐亞海底掘進背景用來分離切削、環片拼裝與維修停時，探討高瞬時效率未必提高日產量。TBM瞬時貫入率只描述刀盤切削的一段時間，拼裝、換刀、出渣與維修決定每天真正進尺。岩石強度與磨蝕性對刀具的影響不同，混合掌子面又產生不對稱作用；比較機器績效須按地質分區和停時原因分類，不能只排序最高進尺。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「有效掘進利用率」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Separate cutting, segment erection and maintenance in subsea boring, testing why high instantaneous performance need not raise daily advance. Instantaneous penetration describes only active cutting; erection, cutter changes, muck handling and repairs determine daily advance. Strength and abrasivity affect cutters differently, while mixed faces impose asymmetric loading. Compare performance by ground domain and downtime cause, because the highest short-duration penetration rate can coexist with poor daily production and increased maintenance demand. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Effective boring utilisation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：切削速率=1.74 m/h；有效利用率=0.28 無因次。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: active penetration=1.74 m/h; utilisation=0.28 dimensionless.","failure":"常見誤解：「刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「有效掘進利用率」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Effective boring utilisation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b109-v14-09-k1","title":"掘進利用率與設備停時","titleEn":"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime","text":"歐亞海底掘進背景用來分離切削、環片拼裝與維修停時，探討高瞬時效率未必提高日產量。TBM瞬時貫入率只描述刀盤切削的一段時間，拼裝、換刀、出渣與維修決定每天真正進尺。","textEn":"Separate cutting, segment erection and maintenance in subsea boring, testing why high instantaneous performance need not raise daily advance. Instantaneous penetration describes only active cutting; erection, cutter changes, muck handling and repairs determine daily advance.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]},{"id":"b109-v14-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「掘進利用率與設備停時」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime\" is correct?","options":["歐亞海底掘進背景用來分離切削、環片拼裝與維修停時，探討高瞬時效率未必提高日產量。","刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。","混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。"],"optionsEn":["Separate cutting, segment erection and maintenance in subsea boring, testing why high instantaneous performance need not raise daily advance.","A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance.","Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure."],"answer":0,"explanation":"歐亞海底掘進背景用來分離切削、環片拼裝與維修停時，探討高瞬時效率未必提高日產量。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Separate cutting, segment erection and maintenance in subsea boring, testing why high instantaneous performance need not raise daily advance. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b109-v14-10","title":"掘進利用率與設備停時：定量估算","titleEn":"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b109-v14-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「有效掘進利用率」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Effective boring utilisation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：切削速率=1.74 m/h；有效利用率=0.28 無因次。D=24vu=11.6928 m/day。僅把有效利用率增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為12.8621 m/day。邊界：平均循環模型，未表示地質轉換及停機分布；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: active penetration=1.74 m/h; utilisation=0.28 dimensionless. D=24vu=11.6928 m/day. Increasing only utilisation by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 12.8621 m/day. Boundary: Mean-cycle model without ground transitions or downtime distribution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：把扭矩推力與停機原因對齊同一里程。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Align torque, thrust and downtime causes at common chainage.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b109-v14-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：切削速率=1.74 m/h；有效利用率=0.28 無因次。D=24vu=11.6928 m/day。僅把有效利用率增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為12.8621 m/day。邊界：平均循環模型，未表示地質轉換及停機分布；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: active penetration=1.74 m/h; utilisation=0.28 dimensionless. D=24vu=11.6928 m/day. Increasing only utilisation by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 12.8621 m/day. Boundary: Mean-cycle model without ground transitions or downtime distribution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]},{"id":"b109-v14-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「掘進利用率與設備停時」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime\", which statement holds?","options":["接縫平均寬度合格就不必量測局部錯台及扭轉。","原創教學假設：切削速率=1.74 m/h；有效利用率=0.28 無因次。","照度越高就必然使隧道內所有物體更容易辨識。"],"optionsEn":["An acceptable average joint width makes local offset and twist measurements unnecessary.","Original teaching assumptions: active penetration=1.74 m/h; utilisation=0.28 dimensionless.","Higher illuminance necessarily makes every tunnel object easier to detect."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：切削速率=1.74 m/h；有效利用率=0.28 無因次。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: active penetration=1.74 m/h; utilisation=0.28 dimensionless. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b109-v14-11","title":"掘進利用率與設備停時：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b109-v14-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「有效掘進利用率」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Effective boring utilisation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"把扭矩推力與停機原因對齊同一里程。由時間戳分離切削、拼裝與故障，將刀具位置、磨耗量及推力扭矩對齊里程，檢查停時是否集中在特定地層。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Align torque, thrust and downtime causes at common chainage. Separate cutting, erection and faults by timestamp; align cutter position, wear, thrust and torque with chainage and test clustering by ground type. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「有效掘進利用率」的交付需回答：把扭矩推力與停機原因對齊同一里程。停機紀錄使用可追溯原因碼，把地質變化與設備故障分開統計，參數調整只能在設備和施工團隊核准程序內進行。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Eurasia Tunnel, the effective boring utilisation handover must address the following evidence: Align torque, thrust and downtime causes at common chainage. Use traceable downtime codes, separating geological change from equipment faults; parameter changes stay within procedures approved by equipment and construction teams.","failure":"注意干擾：拼裝等待被歸為刀具問題會導致錯誤設備調整。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Erection queues labelled as cutter problems prompt incorrect machine changes. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b109-v14-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"把扭矩推力與停機原因對齊同一里程。由時間戳分離切削、拼裝與故障，將刀具位置、磨耗量及推力扭矩對齊里程，檢查停時是否集中在特定地層。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Align torque, thrust and downtime causes at common chainage. Separate cutting, erection and faults by timestamp; align cutter position, wear, thrust and torque with chainage and test clustering by ground type. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]},{"id":"b109-v14-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「有效掘進利用率」的交付需回答：把扭矩推力與停機原因對齊同一里程。停機紀錄使用可追溯原因碼，把地質變化與設備故障分開統計，參數調整只能在設備和施工團隊核准程序內進行。","textEn":"For Eurasia Tunnel, the effective boring utilisation handover must address the following evidence: Align torque, thrust and downtime causes at common chainage. Use traceable downtime codes, separating geological change from equipment faults; parameter changes stay within procedures approved by equipment and construction teams.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「掘進利用率與設備停時」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。","把扭矩推力與停機原因對齊同一里程。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.","Align torque, thrust and downtime causes at common chainage."],"answer":2,"explanation":"把扭矩推力與停機原因對齊同一里程。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Align torque, thrust and downtime causes at common chainage. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b109-v14-12","title":"掘進利用率與設備停時：失效診斷","titleEn":"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b109-v14-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「有效掘進利用率」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Effective boring utilisation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"拼裝等待被歸為刀具問題會導致錯誤設備調整。只提高瞬時進尺可能使出渣或刀具超出有效工況，短暫改善後增加停機，平均進尺和零件壽命反而下降。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Erection queues labelled as cutter problems prompt incorrect machine changes. Higher instantaneous advance can overload cutters or muck transport and create longer stoppages that reduce average progress and component life. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：岩石強度與磨蝕性對刀具的影響不同，混合掌子面又產生不對稱作用；比較機器績效須按地質分區和停時原因分類，不能只排序最高進尺。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Compare performance by ground domain and downtime cause, because the highest short-duration penetration rate can coexist with poor daily production and increased maintenance demand.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b109-v14-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"拼裝等待被歸為刀具問題會導致錯誤設備調整。只提高瞬時進尺可能使出渣或刀具超出有效工況，短暫改善後增加停機，平均進尺和零件壽命反而下降。","textEn":"Erection queues labelled as cutter problems prompt incorrect machine changes. Higher instantaneous advance can overload cutters or muck transport and create longer stoppages that reduce average progress and component life.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]},{"id":"b109-v14-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「掘進利用率與設備停時」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["拼裝等待被歸為刀具問題會導致錯誤設備調整。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。"],"optionsEn":["Erection queues labelled as cutter problems prompt incorrect machine changes.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure."],"answer":0,"explanation":"拼裝等待被歸為刀具問題會導致錯誤設備調整。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Erection queues labelled as cutter problems prompt incorrect machine changes. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b109-v14-13","title":"環向受力與接縫柔度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Ring force and joint flexibility: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b109-v14-12"],"objective":"說明「襯砌環向壓縮」如何影響歐亞海底公路隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Lining hoop compression” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Eurasia Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"圓形襯砌承受海底外壓，同時受雙層樓板支承反力，教學薄環結果需與局部接觸分開。圓形襯砌對均勻外壓可主要以環向壓縮抵抗，但接頭轉動、偏壓與背填空隙會引起彎矩。薄環膜應力只說明其中一條受力路徑；脫模、運輸、頂推及永久狀態的荷載不同，環片局部接觸與止水條件必須另外檢核。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「襯砌環向壓縮」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The circular lining carries external pressure and internal deck reactions, requiring membrane estimates to be separated from local contact effects. A circular lining resists uniform external pressure largely through hoop compression, but joint rotation, uneven load and backfill voids generate bending. Thin-ring membrane stress describes only one load path. Demoulding, transport, jacking and permanent states impose different actions, requiring separate checks of local segment contact and sealing rather than one permanent-load calculation. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Lining hoop compression” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：均勻外壓=0.46 MPa；半徑=3.3 m；厚度=0.35 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: uniform external pressure=0.46 MPa; radius=3.3 m; thickness=0.35 m. σθ=pr/t=4.33714 MPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「襯砌環向壓縮」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Lining hoop compression”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b109-v14-13-k1","title":"環向受力與接縫柔度","titleEn":"Ring force and joint flexibility","text":"圓形襯砌承受海底外壓，同時受雙層樓板支承反力，教學薄環結果需與局部接觸分開。圓形襯砌對均勻外壓可主要以環向壓縮抵抗，但接頭轉動、偏壓與背填空隙會引起彎矩。","textEn":"The circular lining carries external pressure and internal deck reactions, requiring membrane estimates to be separated from local contact effects. A circular lining resists uniform external pressure largely through hoop compression, but joint rotation, uneven load and backfill voids generate bending.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]},{"id":"b109-v14-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「環向受力與接縫柔度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Ring force and joint flexibility\" is correct?","options":["混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。","圓形襯砌承受海底外壓，同時受雙層樓板支承反力，教學薄環結果需與局部接觸分開。","只要空間分成兩層就可以採用相同的樓板荷載。"],"optionsEn":["Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure.","The circular lining carries external pressure and internal deck reactions, requiring membrane estimates to be separated from local contact effects.","Any space divided into two levels can use the same deck loading."],"answer":1,"explanation":"圓形襯砌承受海底外壓，同時受雙層樓板支承反力，教學薄環結果需與局部接觸分開。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The circular lining carries external pressure and internal deck reactions, requiring membrane estimates to be separated from local contact effects. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b109-v14-14","title":"環向受力與接縫柔度：定量估算","titleEn":"Ring force and joint flexibility: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b109-v14-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「襯砌環向壓縮」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Lining hoop compression” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：均勻外壓=0.46 MPa；半徑=3.3 m；厚度=0.35 m。σθ=pr/t=4.33714 MPa。僅把均勻外壓增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為4.77086 MPa。邊界：薄圓環膜應力，不是接縫、偏壓或矩形框架解；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: uniform external pressure=0.46 MPa; radius=3.3 m; thickness=0.35 m. σθ=pr/t=4.33714 MPa. Increasing only uniform external pressure by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 4.77086 MPa. Boundary: Thin circular-ring membrane stress, not a joint, uneven-load or rectangular-frame solution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比較遠離與鄰近樓板支承處的應變和接縫變形。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare strain and joint movement near and away from deck supports.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b109-v14-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：均勻外壓=0.46 MPa；半徑=3.3 m；厚度=0.35 m。σθ=pr/t=4.33714 MPa。僅把均勻外壓增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為4.77086 MPa。邊界：薄圓環膜應力，不是接縫、偏壓或矩形框架解；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: uniform external pressure=0.46 MPa; radius=3.3 m; thickness=0.35 m. σθ=pr/t=4.33714 MPa. Increasing only uniform external pressure by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 4.77086 MPa. Boundary: Thin circular-ring membrane stress, not a joint, uneven-load or rectangular-frame solution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]},{"id":"b109-v14-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「環向受力與接縫柔度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Ring force and joint flexibility\", which statement holds?","options":["風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。","原創教學假設：均勻外壓=0.46 MPa；半徑=3.3 m；厚度=0.35 m。"],"optionsEn":["Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.","Original teaching assumptions: uniform external pressure=0.46 MPa; radius=3.3 m; thickness=0.35 m. σθ=pr/t=4.33714 MPa."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：均勻外壓=0.46 MPa；半徑=3.3 m；厚度=0.35 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: uniform external pressure=0.46 MPa; radius=3.3 m; thickness=0.35 m. σθ=pr/t=4.33714 MPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b109-v14-15","title":"環向受力與接縫柔度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Ring force and joint flexibility: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b109-v14-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「襯砌環向壓縮」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Lining hoop compression” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比較遠離與鄰近樓板支承處的應變和接縫變形。將環形變形、接縫張開與應變和含接頭彈簧的模型比較，分開安裝後、背填後及水頭回升後的基準。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare strain and joint movement near and away from deck supports. Compare ring distortion, joint opening and strain with a joint-spring model, separating baselines after installation, grouting and head recovery. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「襯砌環向壓縮」的交付需回答：比較遠離與鄰近樓板支承處的應變和接縫變形。設計圖應分開標註各施工階段、接頭剛度及背填條件，構件驗收同時核對幾何、材料批次與止水試驗適用包絡。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Eurasia Tunnel, the lining hoop compression handover must address the following evidence: Compare strain and joint movement near and away from deck supports. Drawings distinguish stages, joint stiffness and backfill conditions; component acceptance reconciles geometry, material batches and the applicable sealing-test envelope.","failure":"注意干擾：均勻壓力模型可能漏掉支承處局部彎矩及裂縫。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A uniform-pressure model misses local bending and cracking at supports. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b109-v14-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比較遠離與鄰近樓板支承處的應變和接縫變形。將環形變形、接縫張開與應變和含接頭彈簧的模型比較，分開安裝後、背填後及水頭回升後的基準。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Compare strain and joint movement near and away from deck supports. Compare ring distortion, joint opening and strain with a joint-spring model, separating baselines after installation, grouting and head recovery. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]},{"id":"b109-v14-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「襯砌環向壓縮」的交付需回答：比較遠離與鄰近樓板支承處的應變和接縫變形。設計圖應分開標註各施工階段、接頭剛度及背填條件，構件驗收同時核對幾何、材料批次與止水試驗適用包絡。","textEn":"For Eurasia Tunnel, the lining hoop compression handover must address the following evidence: Compare strain and joint movement near and away from deck supports. Drawings distinguish stages, joint stiffness and backfill conditions; component acceptance reconciles geometry, material batches and the applicable sealing-test envelope.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「環向受力與接縫柔度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Ring force and joint flexibility\"?","options":["比較遠離與鄰近樓板支承處的應變和接縫變形。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Compare strain and joint movement near and away from deck supports.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":0,"explanation":"比較遠離與鄰近樓板支承處的應變和接縫變形。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare strain and joint movement near and away from deck supports. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b109-v14-16","title":"環向受力與接縫柔度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Ring force and joint flexibility: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b109-v14-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「襯砌環向壓縮」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Lining hoop compression” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"均勻壓力模型可能漏掉支承處局部彎矩及裂縫。局部脫空增加環片彎曲，裂縫未必代表混凝土平均強度不足；忽略接縫接觸會把補強方向導向錯誤位置。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A uniform-pressure model misses local bending and cracking at supports. Local voids increase bending, so cracks need not indicate inadequate mean concrete strength; neglecting joint contact can misdirect strengthening. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：薄環膜應力只說明其中一條受力路徑；脫模、運輸、頂推及永久狀態的荷載不同，環片局部接觸與止水條件必須另外檢核。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Demoulding, transport, jacking and permanent states impose different actions, requiring separate checks of local segment contact and sealing rather than one permanent-load calculation.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b109-v14-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"均勻壓力模型可能漏掉支承處局部彎矩及裂縫。局部脫空增加環片彎曲，裂縫未必代表混凝土平均強度不足；忽略接縫接觸會把補強方向導向錯誤位置。","textEn":"A uniform-pressure model misses local bending and cracking at supports. Local voids increase bending, so cracks need not indicate inadequate mean concrete strength; neglecting joint contact can misdirect strengthening.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]},{"id":"b109-v14-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「環向受力與接縫柔度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Ring force and joint flexibility\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","均勻壓力模型可能漏掉支承處局部彎矩及裂縫。","只要空間分成兩層就可以採用相同的樓板荷載。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","A uniform-pressure model misses local bending and cracking at supports.","Any space divided into two levels can use the same deck loading."],"answer":1,"explanation":"均勻壓力模型可能漏掉支承處局部彎矩及裂縫。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A uniform-pressure model misses local bending and cracking at supports. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b109-v14-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「內部樓板與荷載路徑」與「接頭壓縮與水密包絡」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Internal decks and load paths\" and \"Joint compression and sealing envelope\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b109-v14-17","title":"內部樓板與荷載路徑：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Internal decks and load paths: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b109-v14-16"],"objective":"說明「樓板條帶受彎」如何影響歐亞海底公路隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Deck-strip bending” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Eurasia Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"歐亞雙層道路中間樓板是實際行車荷載路徑，教材條帶只示範均載彎矩，另列集中輪載需求。雙層公路的樓板、或隧道內設備隔板，都把局部荷載傳給支承，但兩者功能與設計作用並不相同。簡支條帶可估計均載彎矩，集中輪載、剪力、疲勞與火災降強度必須另驗；幾何空間分層不能取代結構邊界的確認。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「樓板條帶受彎」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The intermediate roadway deck is a traffic-load path; the teaching strip illustrates distributed bending while concentrated wheel loads remain separate. A double-deck road slab and an equipment partition both transfer local loads to supports but serve different functions and design actions. A simply supported strip estimates uniform-load bending. Concentrated wheel loads, shear, fatigue and fire-reduced strength require separate checks; dividing space geometrically does not establish the actual structural restraints. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Deck-strip bending” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：單位長載重=28 kN/m；跨距=3.6 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: line load=28 kN/m; span=3.6 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要空間分成兩層就可以採用相同的樓板荷載。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Any space divided into two levels can use the same deck loading.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「樓板條帶受彎」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Deck-strip bending”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b109-v14-17-k1","title":"內部樓板與荷載路徑","titleEn":"Internal decks and load paths","text":"歐亞雙層道路中間樓板是實際行車荷載路徑，教材條帶只示範均載彎矩，另列集中輪載需求。雙層公路的樓板、或隧道內設備隔板，都把局部荷載傳給支承，但兩者功能與設計作用並不相同。","textEn":"The intermediate roadway deck is a traffic-load path; the teaching strip illustrates distributed bending while concentrated wheel loads remain separate. A double-deck road slab and an equipment partition both transfer local loads to supports but serve different functions and design actions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]},{"id":"b109-v14-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要空間分成兩層就可以採用相同的樓板荷載。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Any space divided into two levels can use the same deck loading. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「內部樓板與荷載路徑」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Internal decks and load paths\" is correct?","options":["只要空間分成兩層就可以採用相同的樓板荷載。","接縫平均寬度合格就不必量測局部錯台及扭轉。","歐亞雙層道路中間樓板是實際行車荷載路徑，教材條帶只示範均載彎矩，另列集中輪載需求。"],"optionsEn":["Any space divided into two levels can use the same deck loading.","An acceptable average joint width makes local offset and twist measurements unnecessary.","The intermediate roadway deck is a traffic-load path; the teaching strip illustrates distributed bending while concentrated wheel loads remain separate."],"answer":2,"explanation":"歐亞雙層道路中間樓板是實際行車荷載路徑，教材條帶只示範均載彎矩，另列集中輪載需求。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The intermediate roadway deck is a traffic-load path; the teaching strip illustrates distributed bending while concentrated wheel loads remain separate. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b109-v14-18","title":"內部樓板與荷載路徑：定量估算","titleEn":"Internal decks and load paths: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b109-v14-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「樓板條帶受彎」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Deck-strip bending” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：單位長載重=28 kN/m；跨距=3.6 m。M=qL²/8=45.36 kN·m。僅把跨距增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為54.8856 kN·m。邊界：均載簡支單向條帶，連續框架及板效應另驗；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: line load=28 kN/m; span=3.6 m. M=qL²/8=45.36 kN·m. Increasing only span by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 54.8856 kN·m. Boundary: Uniformly loaded simply supported strip; frame continuity and plate action need separate checks. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對行車面、支承和施工階段，不與設備隔板混用。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check roadway surface, supports and stages without substituting equipment-partition assumptions.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b109-v14-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：單位長載重=28 kN/m；跨距=3.6 m。M=qL²/8=45.36 kN·m。僅把跨距增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為54.8856 kN·m。邊界：均載簡支單向條帶，連續框架及板效應另驗；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: line load=28 kN/m; span=3.6 m. M=qL²/8=45.36 kN·m. Increasing only span by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 54.8856 kN·m. Boundary: Uniformly loaded simply supported strip; frame continuity and plate action need separate checks. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]},{"id":"b109-v14-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「內部樓板與荷載路徑」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Internal decks and load paths\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：單位長載重=28 kN/m；跨距=3.6 m。","照度越高就必然使隧道內所有物體更容易辨識。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: line load=28 kN/m; span=3.6 m.","Higher illuminance necessarily makes every tunnel object easier to detect.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：單位長載重=28 kN/m；跨距=3.6 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: line load=28 kN/m; span=3.6 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b109-v14-19","title":"內部樓板與荷載路徑：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Internal decks and load paths: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b109-v14-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「樓板條帶受彎」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Deck-strip bending” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對行車面、支承和施工階段，不與設備隔板混用。核對支承位置、施工接縫及荷載分布，將實測撓度與分階段模型比較，分辨整體變形與支承滑移。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check roadway surface, supports and stages without substituting equipment-partition assumptions. Check support positions, construction joints and load distribution; compare measured deflection with staged models to distinguish member bending from support slip. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「樓板條帶受彎」的交付需回答：核對行車面、支承和施工階段，不與設備隔板混用。交付時明示樓板用途、支承及各施工階段，讓建築淨空、設備配置及結構假設在同一版本中核對。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Eurasia Tunnel, the deck-strip bending handover must address the following evidence: Check roadway surface, supports and stages without substituting equipment-partition assumptions. State deck function, supports and construction stages at handover so clearance, equipment layout and structural assumptions can be reconciled in one revision.","failure":"注意干擾：把樓板當非承重分隔會漏掉交通彎剪和疲勞作用。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Treating the deck as nonstructural separation omits traffic bending, shear and fatigue. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b109-v14-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對行車面、支承和施工階段，不與設備隔板混用。核對支承位置、施工接縫及荷載分布，將實測撓度與分階段模型比較，分辨整體變形與支承滑移。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Check roadway surface, supports and stages without substituting equipment-partition assumptions. Check support positions, construction joints and load distribution; compare measured deflection with staged models to distinguish member bending from support slip. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]},{"id":"b109-v14-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「樓板條帶受彎」的交付需回答：核對行車面、支承和施工階段，不與設備隔板混用。交付時明示樓板用途、支承及各施工階段，讓建築淨空、設備配置及結構假設在同一版本中核對。","textEn":"For Eurasia Tunnel, the deck-strip bending handover must address the following evidence: Check roadway surface, supports and stages without substituting equipment-partition assumptions. State deck function, supports and construction stages at handover so clearance, equipment layout and structural assumptions can be reconciled in one revision.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「內部樓板與荷載路徑」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Internal decks and load paths\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","核對行車面、支承和施工階段，不與設備隔板混用。","目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Check roadway surface, supports and stages without substituting equipment-partition assumptions.","No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design."],"answer":1,"explanation":"核對行車面、支承和施工階段，不與設備隔板混用。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check roadway surface, supports and stages without substituting equipment-partition assumptions. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b109-v14-20","title":"內部樓板與荷載路徑：失效診斷","titleEn":"Internal decks and load paths: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b109-v14-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「樓板條帶受彎」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Deck-strip bending” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把樓板當非承重分隔會漏掉交通彎剪和疲勞作用。把隔板誤當行車樓板會使用錯誤荷載，反之漏掉交通集中荷載則低估局部彎剪與疲勞。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Treating the deck as nonstructural separation omits traffic bending, shear and fatigue. Mistaking a partition for a roadway deck applies the wrong actions, while omitting concentrated traffic load underestimates local bending, shear and fatigue. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：簡支條帶可估計均載彎矩，集中輪載、剪力、疲勞與火災降強度必須另驗；幾何空間分層不能取代結構邊界的確認。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Concentrated wheel loads, shear, fatigue and fire-reduced strength require separate checks; dividing space geometrically does not establish the actual structural restraints.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要空間分成兩層就可以採用相同的樓板荷載。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Any space divided into two levels can use the same deck loading.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b109-v14-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把樓板當非承重分隔會漏掉交通彎剪和疲勞作用。把隔板誤當行車樓板會使用錯誤荷載，反之漏掉交通集中荷載則低估局部彎剪與疲勞。","textEn":"Treating the deck as nonstructural separation omits traffic bending, shear and fatigue. Mistaking a partition for a roadway deck applies the wrong actions, while omitting concentrated traffic load underestimates local bending, shear and fatigue.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]},{"id":"b109-v14-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「內部樓板與荷載路徑」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Internal decks and load paths\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","接縫平均寬度合格就不必量測局部錯台及扭轉。","把樓板當非承重分隔會漏掉交通彎剪和疲勞作用。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","An acceptable average joint width makes local offset and twist measurements unnecessary.","Treating the deck as nonstructural separation omits traffic bending, shear and fatigue."],"answer":2,"explanation":"把樓板當非承重分隔會漏掉交通彎剪和疲勞作用。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Treating the deck as nonstructural separation omits traffic bending, shear and fatigue. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b109-v14-21","title":"接頭壓縮與水密包絡：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Joint compression and sealing envelope: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b109-v14-20"],"objective":"說明「止水壓縮餘量」如何影響歐亞海底公路隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Gasket compression reserve” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Eurasia Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"圓孔接頭與變形介面的止水能力需對應不同位移形式，研究平均壓縮合格但局部錯台的情境。止水條依受控壓縮維持連續接觸，接縫轉角、錯台、污染與材料鬆弛都會降低最不利點的接觸能力。平均壓縮量不能掩蓋局部脫離；全尺寸試驗的結果只對測試過的幾何、水壓及荷載歷程有效，幾何餘量本身並不是接觸壓力。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「止水壓縮餘量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Match sealing performance to different displacement modes at ring joints and movement interfaces, including local offsets despite acceptable average compression. A gasket seals through controlled continuous compression; rotation, offset, contamination and relaxation reduce contact at the weakest point. Average compression cannot compensate for local separation. Full-size test results apply only to their tested geometry, head and load history, while a calculated geometric reserve is neither contact pressure nor evidence of watertightness. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Gasket compression reserve” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：初始壓縮=18 mm；張開量=4 mm；幾何公差=2 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: initial compression=18 mm; opening=4 mm; tolerance=2 mm. c_res=c0−opening−tolerance=12 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「接縫平均寬度合格就不必量測局部錯台及扭轉。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"An acceptable average joint width makes local offset and twist measurements unnecessary.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「止水壓縮餘量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Gasket compression reserve”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b109-v14-21-k1","title":"接頭壓縮與水密包絡","titleEn":"Joint compression and sealing envelope","text":"圓孔接頭與變形介面的止水能力需對應不同位移形式，研究平均壓縮合格但局部錯台的情境。止水條依受控壓縮維持連續接觸，接縫轉角、錯台、污染與材料鬆弛都會降低最不利點的接觸能力。","textEn":"Match sealing performance to different displacement modes at ring joints and movement interfaces, including local offsets despite acceptable average compression. A gasket seals through controlled continuous compression; rotation, offset, contamination and relaxation reduce contact at the weakest point.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]},{"id":"b109-v14-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：接縫平均寬度合格就不必量測局部錯台及扭轉。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: An acceptable average joint width makes local offset and twist measurements unnecessary. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「接頭壓縮與水密包絡」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Joint compression and sealing envelope\" is correct?","options":["圓孔接頭與變形介面的止水能力需對應不同位移形式，研究平均壓縮合格但局部錯台的情境。","接縫平均寬度合格就不必量測局部錯台及扭轉。","風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。"],"optionsEn":["Match sealing performance to different displacement modes at ring joints and movement interfaces, including local offsets despite acceptable average compression.","An acceptable average joint width makes local offset and twist measurements unnecessary.","Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel."],"answer":0,"explanation":"圓孔接頭與變形介面的止水能力需對應不同位移形式，研究平均壓縮合格但局部錯台的情境。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Match sealing performance to different displacement modes at ring joints and movement interfaces, including local offsets despite acceptable average compression. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b109-v14-22","title":"接頭壓縮與水密包絡：定量估算","titleEn":"Joint compression and sealing envelope: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b109-v14-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「止水壓縮餘量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Gasket compression reserve” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：初始壓縮=18 mm；張開量=4 mm；幾何公差=2 mm。c_res=c0−opening−tolerance=12 mm。僅把張開量增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為11.6 mm。邊界：單向幾何餘量，不是接觸壓或水密合格證明；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: initial compression=18 mm; opening=4 mm; tolerance=2 mm. c_res=c0−opening−tolerance=12 mm. Increasing only opening by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 11.6 mm. Boundary: One-direction geometric reserve, not contact pressure or proof of watertightness. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將最不利角點的壓縮和剪移一起送入接頭試驗。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use compression and shear at the adverse corner in joint tests.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b109-v14-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：初始壓縮=18 mm；張開量=4 mm；幾何公差=2 mm。c_res=c0−opening−tolerance=12 mm。僅把張開量增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為11.6 mm。邊界：單向幾何餘量，不是接觸壓或水密合格證明；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: initial compression=18 mm; opening=4 mm; tolerance=2 mm. c_res=c0−opening−tolerance=12 mm. Increasing only opening by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 11.6 mm. Boundary: One-direction geometric reserve, not contact pressure or proof of watertightness. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]},{"id":"b109-v14-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「接頭壓縮與水密包絡」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Joint compression and sealing envelope\", which statement holds?","options":["只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。","原創教學假設：初始壓縮=18 mm；張開量=4 mm；幾何公差=2 mm。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.","Original teaching assumptions: initial compression=18 mm; opening=4 mm; tolerance=2 mm. c_res=c0−opening−tolerance=12 mm.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：初始壓縮=18 mm；張開量=4 mm；幾何公差=2 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: initial compression=18 mm; opening=4 mm; tolerance=2 mm. c_res=c0−opening−tolerance=12 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b109-v14-23","title":"接頭壓縮與水密包絡：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Joint compression and sealing envelope: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b109-v14-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「止水壓縮餘量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Gasket compression reserve” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將最不利角點的壓縮和剪移一起送入接頭試驗。全尺寸接頭試驗分別改變張開、錯台與外水壓，記錄漏水起點與卸載後殘餘位移，對照材料批次及溫度。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use compression and shear at the adverse corner in joint tests. Vary opening, offset and pressure in full-size joint tests, recording leakage onset and residual movement against material batch and temperature. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「止水壓縮餘量」的交付需回答：將最不利角點的壓縮和剪移一起送入接頭試驗。保存接縫幾何與試驗壓力的配對紀錄，由設計者核定允收包絡；驗收時不能把課堂的幾何餘量當產品認證數字。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Eurasia Tunnel, the gasket compression reserve handover must address the following evidence: Use compression and shear at the adverse corner in joint tests. Retain paired joint geometry and test pressure, with the designer approving the acceptance envelope; classroom geometric reserves are not product certification values.","failure":"注意干擾：只取平均縫寬會掩蓋局部止水脫離。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Mean joint width can conceal local gasket separation. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b109-v14-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將最不利角點的壓縮和剪移一起送入接頭試驗。全尺寸接頭試驗分別改變張開、錯台與外水壓，記錄漏水起點與卸載後殘餘位移，對照材料批次及溫度。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Use compression and shear at the adverse corner in joint tests. Vary opening, offset and pressure in full-size joint tests, recording leakage onset and residual movement against material batch and temperature. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]},{"id":"b109-v14-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「止水壓縮餘量」的交付需回答：將最不利角點的壓縮和剪移一起送入接頭試驗。保存接縫幾何與試驗壓力的配對紀錄，由設計者核定允收包絡；驗收時不能把課堂的幾何餘量當產品認證數字。","textEn":"For Eurasia Tunnel, the gasket compression reserve handover must address the following evidence: Use compression and shear at the adverse corner in joint tests. Retain paired joint geometry and test pressure, with the designer approving the acceptance envelope; classroom geometric reserves are not product certification values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「接頭壓縮與水密包絡」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Joint compression and sealing envelope\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。","將最不利角點的壓縮和剪移一起送入接頭試驗。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance.","Use compression and shear at the adverse corner in joint tests."],"answer":2,"explanation":"將最不利角點的壓縮和剪移一起送入接頭試驗。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use compression and shear at the adverse corner in joint tests. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b109-v14-24","title":"接頭壓縮與水密包絡：失效診斷","titleEn":"Joint compression and sealing envelope: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b109-v14-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「止水壓縮餘量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Gasket compression reserve” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只取平均縫寬會掩蓋局部止水脫離。扭曲或沾污的止水條可形成旁通通道，即使平均縫寬合格仍可能漏水；盲目灌漿也可能只轉移出水位置。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Mean joint width can conceal local gasket separation. A twisted or contaminated gasket creates bypass leakage despite acceptable mean width; indiscriminate grouting may merely move the outlet. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：平均壓縮量不能掩蓋局部脫離；全尺寸試驗的結果只對測試過的幾何、水壓及荷載歷程有效，幾何餘量本身並不是接觸壓力。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Full-size test results apply only to their tested geometry, head and load history, while a calculated geometric reserve is neither contact pressure nor evidence of watertightness.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「接縫平均寬度合格就不必量測局部錯台及扭轉。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"An acceptable average joint width makes local offset and twist measurements unnecessary.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b109-v14-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只取平均縫寬會掩蓋局部止水脫離。扭曲或沾污的止水條可形成旁通通道，即使平均縫寬合格仍可能漏水；盲目灌漿也可能只轉移出水位置。","textEn":"Mean joint width can conceal local gasket separation. A twisted or contaminated gasket creates bypass leakage despite acceptable mean width; indiscriminate grouting may merely move the outlet.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]},{"id":"b109-v14-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「接頭壓縮與水密包絡」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Joint compression and sealing envelope\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["只取平均縫寬會掩蓋局部止水脫離。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。"],"optionsEn":["Mean joint width can conceal local gasket separation.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel."],"answer":0,"explanation":"只取平均縫寬會掩蓋局部止水脫離。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Mean joint width can conceal local gasket separation. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b109-v14-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「通風網路與壓力損失」與「視覺適應與路面亮度」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Ventilation network and pressure loss\" and \"Visual adaptation and pavement luminance\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b109-v14-25","title":"通風網路與壓力損失：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Ventilation network and pressure loss: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b109-v14-24"],"objective":"說明「風道摩擦壓損」如何影響歐亞海底公路隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Duct friction loss” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Eurasia Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"雙層道路的通風支路與樓板隔離相互作用，研究一層門位變化是否改變另一層的風量。風機提供壓差，實際風量由風道摩阻、局部損失、外風與其他風機共同決定。支路開關會重新分配整個網路，不能把額定風量直接加總；正常污染稀釋與火災控煙也有不同目標，需要分別建立受控邊界和故障情境。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「風道摩擦壓損」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Ventilation branches interact with deck separation; test whether changing doors on one level redistributes air on the other. Fans supply pressure, but actual flow follows friction, local losses, external wind and interactions with other fans. Switching a branch redistributes the network rather than simply adding rated flows. Routine dilution and fire smoke control have different objectives, so each needs explicit boundaries, operating states and failure cases rather than one universal flow target. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Duct friction loss” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：達西因子=0.025 無因次；風道長度=820 m；水力直徑=4 m；空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；平均風速=3.6 m/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.025 dimensionless; duct length=820 m; hydraulic diameter=4 m; air density=1.2 kg/m³; mean velocity=3.6 m/s. Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=39.852 Pa.","failure":"常見誤解：「風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「風道摩擦壓損」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Duct friction loss”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b109-v14-25-k1","title":"通風網路與壓力損失","titleEn":"Ventilation network and pressure loss","text":"雙層道路的通風支路與樓板隔離相互作用，研究一層門位變化是否改變另一層的風量。風機提供壓差，實際風量由風道摩阻、局部損失、外風與其他風機共同決定。","textEn":"Ventilation branches interact with deck separation; test whether changing doors on one level redistributes air on the other. Fans supply pressure, but actual flow follows friction, local losses, external wind and interactions with other fans.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]},{"id":"b109-v14-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「通風網路與壓力損失」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Ventilation network and pressure loss\" is correct?","options":["風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。","雙層道路的通風支路與樓板隔離相互作用，研究一層門位變化是否改變另一層的風量。","照度越高就必然使隧道內所有物體更容易辨識。"],"optionsEn":["Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.","Ventilation branches interact with deck separation; test whether changing doors on one level redistributes air on the other.","Higher illuminance necessarily makes every tunnel object easier to detect."],"answer":1,"explanation":"雙層道路的通風支路與樓板隔離相互作用，研究一層門位變化是否改變另一層的風量。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Ventilation branches interact with deck separation; test whether changing doors on one level redistributes air on the other. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b109-v14-26","title":"通風網路與壓力損失：定量估算","titleEn":"Ventilation network and pressure loss: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b109-v14-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「風道摩擦壓損」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Duct friction loss” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：達西因子=0.025 無因次；風道長度=820 m；水力直徑=4 m；空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；平均風速=3.6 m/s。Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=39.852 Pa。僅把平均風速增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為48.2209 Pa。邊界：定密度直管摩阻，局部損失及外風另計；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.025 dimensionless; duct length=820 m; hydraulic diameter=4 m; air density=1.2 kg/m³; mean velocity=3.6 m/s. Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=39.852 Pa. Increasing only mean velocity by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 48.2209 Pa. Boundary: Constant-density straight-duct friction; local loss and external wind are separate. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同步量測兩層壓差與風量，保留車流狀態。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure pressure and flow on both levels simultaneously and record traffic state.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b109-v14-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：達西因子=0.025 無因次；風道長度=820 m；水力直徑=4 m；空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；平均風速=3.6 m/s。Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=39.852 Pa。僅把平均風速增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為48.2209 Pa。邊界：定密度直管摩阻，局部損失及外風另計；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.025 dimensionless; duct length=820 m; hydraulic diameter=4 m; air density=1.2 kg/m³; mean velocity=3.6 m/s. Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=39.852 Pa. Increasing only mean velocity by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 48.2209 Pa. Boundary: Constant-density straight-duct friction; local loss and external wind are separate. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]},{"id":"b109-v14-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「通風網路與壓力損失」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Ventilation network and pressure loss\", which statement holds?","options":["全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。","目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。","原創教學假設：達西因子=0.025 無因次；風道長度=820 m；水力直徑=4 m；空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；平均風速=3.6 m/s。"],"optionsEn":["Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.","No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.","Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.025 dimensionless."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：達西因子=0.025 無因次；風道長度=820 m；水力直徑=4 m；空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；平均風速=3.6 m/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.025 dimensionless; duct length=820 m; hydraulic diameter=4 m; air density=1.2 kg/m³; mean velocity=3.6 m/s. Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=39.852 Pa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b109-v14-27","title":"通風網路與壓力損失：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Ventilation network and pressure loss: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b109-v14-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「風道摩擦壓損」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Duct friction loss” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同步量測兩層壓差與風量，保留車流狀態。沿線同步量測靜壓與風速，記錄風門及其他風機狀態，再把實測工作點和風機曲線、網路壓損比較。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure pressure and flow on both levels simultaneously and record traffic state. Measure pressure and velocity synchronously, record dampers and other fans, and compare the measured duty point with fan curves and network resistance. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「風道摩擦壓損」的交付需回答：同步量測兩層壓差與風量，保留車流狀態。驗收採明確風門和車流邊界，維修改線後重新核對網路工作點，火災模式由防災責任工程師簽認而非沿用正常模式。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Eurasia Tunnel, the duct friction loss handover must address the following evidence: Measure pressure and flow on both levels simultaneously and record traffic state. Commission with specified damper and traffic boundaries, recheck duty points after rerouting, and have the fire-safety engineer approve emergency modes independently.","failure":"注意干擾：兩層風機額定量相加不能代表各層實際有效換氣。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Summed fan ratings do not establish effective airflow on each level. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b109-v14-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同步量測兩層壓差與風量，保留車流狀態。沿線同步量測靜壓與風速，記錄風門及其他風機狀態，再把實測工作點和風機曲線、網路壓損比較。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Measure pressure and flow on both levels simultaneously and record traffic state. Measure pressure and velocity synchronously, record dampers and other fans, and compare the measured duty point with fan curves and network resistance. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]},{"id":"b109-v14-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「風道摩擦壓損」的交付需回答：同步量測兩層壓差與風量，保留車流狀態。驗收採明確風門和車流邊界，維修改線後重新核對網路工作點，火災模式由防災責任工程師簽認而非沿用正常模式。","textEn":"For Eurasia Tunnel, the duct friction loss handover must address the following evidence: Measure pressure and flow on both levels simultaneously and record traffic state. Commission with specified damper and traffic boundaries, recheck duty points after rerouting, and have the fire-safety engineer approve emergency modes independently.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「通風網路與壓力損失」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Ventilation network and pressure loss\"?","options":["同步量測兩層壓差與風量，保留車流狀態。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。"],"optionsEn":["Measure pressure and flow on both levels simultaneously and record traffic state.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure."],"answer":0,"explanation":"同步量測兩層壓差與風量，保留車流狀態。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure pressure and flow on both levels simultaneously and record traffic state. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b109-v14-28","title":"通風網路與壓力損失：失效診斷","titleEn":"Ventilation network and pressure loss: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b109-v14-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「風道摩擦壓損」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Duct friction loss” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"兩層風機額定量相加不能代表各層實際有效換氣。只看風機轉速會漏掉風門誤位或短路漏風，可能在總耗電增加時，真正需要的區段反而風量不足。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Summed fan ratings do not establish effective airflow on each level. Fan speed alone misses a misplaced damper or leakage shortcut; total power may rise while the critical section receives less air. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：支路開關會重新分配整個網路，不能把額定風量直接加總；正常污染稀釋與火災控煙也有不同目標，需要分別建立受控邊界和故障情境。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Routine dilution and fire smoke control have different objectives, so each needs explicit boundaries, operating states and failure cases rather than one universal flow target.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b109-v14-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"兩層風機額定量相加不能代表各層實際有效換氣。只看風機轉速會漏掉風門誤位或短路漏風，可能在總耗電增加時，真正需要的區段反而風量不足。","textEn":"Summed fan ratings do not establish effective airflow on each level. Fan speed alone misses a misplaced damper or leakage shortcut; total power may rise while the critical section receives less air.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]},{"id":"b109-v14-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「通風網路與壓力損失」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Ventilation network and pressure loss\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","兩層風機額定量相加不能代表各層實際有效換氣。","照度越高就必然使隧道內所有物體更容易辨識。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Summed fan ratings do not establish effective airflow on each level.","Higher illuminance necessarily makes every tunnel object easier to detect."],"answer":1,"explanation":"兩層風機額定量相加不能代表各層實際有效換氣。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Summed fan ratings do not establish effective airflow on each level. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b109-v14-29","title":"視覺適應與路面亮度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Visual adaptation and pavement luminance: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b109-v14-28"],"objective":"說明「漫反射亮度」如何影響歐亞海底公路隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Diffuse luminance” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Eurasia Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"雙層道路入口與轉接段的視角不同，歐亞教材區分照度、路面反射及駕駛看到的亮度。駕駛從洞外進入洞內時視覺適應需要時間，照度並不等同從駕駛視角看到的亮度。路面反射、濕度、燈具配光及背景對比共同影響辨識；朗伯模型只示範理想漫反射，不能直接制定入口段燈具間距或真實道路安全值。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「漫反射亮度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Different viewing geometries at entrances and transitions require illuminance, pavement reflection and driver-view luminance to be distinguished. Driver adaptation takes time when entering a tunnel, and illuminance is not the luminance seen from the driving position. Pavement reflection, wetness, luminaire distribution and background contrast affect detection. A Lambertian model illustrates ideal diffuse reflection only; it cannot establish entrance-zone spacing or actual road-safety limits without photometric and operational assessment. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Diffuse luminance” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：照度=96 lx；反射率=0.27 無因次。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: illuminance=96 lx; reflectance=0.27 dimensionless.","failure":"常見誤解：「照度越高就必然使隧道內所有物體更容易辨識。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Higher illuminance necessarily makes every tunnel object easier to detect.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「漫反射亮度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Diffuse luminance”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b109-v14-29-k1","title":"視覺適應與路面亮度","titleEn":"Visual adaptation and pavement luminance","text":"雙層道路入口與轉接段的視角不同，歐亞教材區分照度、路面反射及駕駛看到的亮度。駕駛從洞外進入洞內時視覺適應需要時間，照度並不等同從駕駛視角看到的亮度。","textEn":"Different viewing geometries at entrances and transitions require illuminance, pavement reflection and driver-view luminance to be distinguished. Driver adaptation takes time when entering a tunnel, and illuminance is not the luminance seen from the driving position.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]},{"id":"b109-v14-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：照度越高就必然使隧道內所有物體更容易辨識。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Higher illuminance necessarily makes every tunnel object easier to detect. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「視覺適應與路面亮度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Visual adaptation and pavement luminance\" is correct?","options":["照度越高就必然使隧道內所有物體更容易辨識。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。","雙層道路入口與轉接段的視角不同，歐亞教材區分照度、路面反射及駕駛看到的亮度。"],"optionsEn":["Higher illuminance necessarily makes every tunnel object easier to detect.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.","Different viewing geometries at entrances and transitions require illuminance, pavement reflection and driver-view luminance to be distinguished."],"answer":2,"explanation":"雙層道路入口與轉接段的視角不同，歐亞教材區分照度、路面反射及駕駛看到的亮度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Different viewing geometries at entrances and transitions require illuminance, pavement reflection and driver-view luminance to be distinguished. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b109-v14-30","title":"視覺適應與路面亮度：定量估算","titleEn":"Visual adaptation and pavement luminance: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b109-v14-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「漫反射亮度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Diffuse luminance” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：照度=96 lx；反射率=0.27 無因次。L=ρE/π=8.25059 cd/m²。僅把照度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為9.07565 cd/m²。邊界：理想朗伯漫反射，不是真實濕路面亮度；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: illuminance=96 lx; reflectance=0.27 dimensionless. L=ρE/π=8.25059 cd/m². Increasing only illuminance by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 9.07565 cd/m². Boundary: Ideal Lambertian reflection, not actual wet-road luminance. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：從各層駕駛視高核對亮度而非只量地面照度。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure luminance from each driving eye height rather than ground illuminance alone.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b109-v14-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：照度=96 lx；反射率=0.27 無因次。L=ρE/π=8.25059 cd/m²。僅把照度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為9.07565 cd/m²。邊界：理想朗伯漫反射，不是真實濕路面亮度；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: illuminance=96 lx; reflectance=0.27 dimensionless. L=ρE/π=8.25059 cd/m². Increasing only illuminance by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 9.07565 cd/m². Boundary: Ideal Lambertian reflection, not actual wet-road luminance. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]},{"id":"b109-v14-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「視覺適應與路面亮度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Visual adaptation and pavement luminance\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：照度=96 lx；反射率=0.27 無因次。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。","刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: illuminance=96 lx; reflectance=0.27 dimensionless.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.","A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：照度=96 lx；反射率=0.27 無因次。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: illuminance=96 lx; reflectance=0.27 dimensionless. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b109-v14-31","title":"視覺適應與路面亮度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Visual adaptation and pavement luminance: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b109-v14-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「漫反射亮度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Diffuse luminance” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"從各層駕駛視高核對亮度而非只量地面照度。以駕駛視角的亮度量測配合照度網格，分別檢查乾濕路面與燈具衰減，保留外部天空條件。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure luminance from each driving eye height rather than ground illuminance alone. Combine driver-view luminance with illuminance grids, checking dry and wet pavement and lamp depreciation while preserving exterior sky conditions. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「漫反射亮度」的交付需回答：從各層駕駛視高核對亮度而非只量地面照度。將視角、路面狀態和光度校正連同量測交付，照明調整需按核准場景測試，不把理想反射公式當驗收標準。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Eurasia Tunnel, the diffuse luminance handover must address the following evidence: Measure luminance from each driving eye height rather than ground illuminance alone. Hand over viewing geometry, pavement state and photometric calibration; test changes against approved scenarios rather than treating ideal reflection as an acceptance criterion.","failure":"注意干擾：兩層照度相同不保證障礙物對比相同。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Equal illuminance on two levels does not ensure equal obstacle contrast. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b109-v14-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"從各層駕駛視高核對亮度而非只量地面照度。以駕駛視角的亮度量測配合照度網格，分別檢查乾濕路面與燈具衰減，保留外部天空條件。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Measure luminance from each driving eye height rather than ground illuminance alone. Combine driver-view luminance with illuminance grids, checking dry and wet pavement and lamp depreciation while preserving exterior sky conditions. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]},{"id":"b109-v14-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「漫反射亮度」的交付需回答：從各層駕駛視高核對亮度而非只量地面照度。將視角、路面狀態和光度校正連同量測交付，照明調整需按核准場景測試，不把理想反射公式當驗收標準。","textEn":"For Eurasia Tunnel, the diffuse luminance handover must address the following evidence: Measure luminance from each driving eye height rather than ground illuminance alone. Hand over viewing geometry, pavement state and photometric calibration; test changes against approved scenarios rather than treating ideal reflection as an acceptance criterion.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「視覺適應與路面亮度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Visual adaptation and pavement luminance\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","從各層駕駛視高核對亮度而非只量地面照度。","只要空間分成兩層就可以採用相同的樓板荷載。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Measure luminance from each driving eye height rather than ground illuminance alone.","Any space divided into two levels can use the same deck loading."],"answer":1,"explanation":"從各層駕駛視高核對亮度而非只量地面照度。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure luminance from each driving eye height rather than ground illuminance alone. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b109-v14-32","title":"視覺適應與路面亮度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Visual adaptation and pavement luminance: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b109-v14-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「漫反射亮度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Diffuse luminance” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"兩層照度相同不保證障礙物對比相同。照度平均值合格仍可能存在低亮度障礙區或眩光，感測器沾污也會使調光系統低估外界亮度。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Equal illuminance on two levels does not ensure equal obstacle contrast. Acceptable average illuminance can coexist with dark obstacles or glare, while sensor contamination may bias adaptive lighting controls. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：路面反射、濕度、燈具配光及背景對比共同影響辨識；朗伯模型只示範理想漫反射，不能直接制定入口段燈具間距或真實道路安全值。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A Lambertian model illustrates ideal diffuse reflection only; it cannot establish entrance-zone spacing or actual road-safety limits without photometric and operational assessment.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「照度越高就必然使隧道內所有物體更容易辨識。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Higher illuminance necessarily makes every tunnel object easier to detect.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b109-v14-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"兩層照度相同不保證障礙物對比相同。照度平均值合格仍可能存在低亮度障礙區或眩光，感測器沾污也會使調光系統低估外界亮度。","textEn":"Equal illuminance on two levels does not ensure equal obstacle contrast. Acceptable average illuminance can coexist with dark obstacles or glare, while sensor contamination may bias adaptive lighting controls.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]},{"id":"b109-v14-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「視覺適應與路面亮度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Visual adaptation and pavement luminance\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。","兩層照度相同不保證障礙物對比相同。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.","Equal illuminance on two levels does not ensure equal obstacle contrast."],"answer":2,"explanation":"兩層照度相同不保證障礙物對比相同。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Equal illuminance on two levels does not ensure equal obstacle contrast. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b109-v14-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「疏散時間與分區可用性」與「資產編碼與可追溯交接」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Evacuation time and zone availability\" and \"Asset identity and traceable handover\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b109-v14-33","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b109-v14-32"],"objective":"說明「所需疏散時間」如何影響歐亞海底公路隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Required evacuation time” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Eurasia Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"從雙層道路轉入安全通道時存在垂直及水平移動，教學時間帳要保留找門與下車延遲。疏散時間包含辨識、反應、移動及排隊，不只由出口距離決定。人員速度會受煙熱、能見度及行動能力影響，安全判斷還要比較可用安全時間；橫通道存在但門或鄰孔不可用時，圖上的最短路線不一定能作實際選擇。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「所需疏散時間」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Moving from a double-deck roadway to safety combines vertical and horizontal travel with door-finding and vehicle-exit delay. Evacuation includes detection, response, travel and queues, not merely distance to an exit. Smoke, visibility and mobility alter walking speed, while safety requires comparison with available safe time. A passage shown on a plan may be unusable because its door or receiving bore is unavailable, invalidating the nominal shortest route. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Required evacuation time” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：前置時間=96 s；行走距離=360 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=96 s; travel distance=360 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「所需疏散時間」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Required evacuation time”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b109-v14-33-k1","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability","text":"從雙層道路轉入安全通道時存在垂直及水平移動，教學時間帳要保留找門與下車延遲。疏散時間包含辨識、反應、移動及排隊，不只由出口距離決定。","textEn":"Moving from a double-deck roadway to safety combines vertical and horizontal travel with door-finding and vehicle-exit delay. Evacuation includes detection, response, travel and queues, not merely distance to an exit.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]},{"id":"b109-v14-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「疏散時間與分區可用性」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Evacuation time and zone availability\" is correct?","options":["從雙層道路轉入安全通道時存在垂直及水平移動，教學時間帳要保留找門與下車延遲。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。"],"optionsEn":["Moving from a double-deck roadway to safety combines vertical and horizontal travel with door-finding and vehicle-exit delay.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted."],"answer":0,"explanation":"從雙層道路轉入安全通道時存在垂直及水平移動，教學時間帳要保留找門與下車延遲。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Moving from a double-deck roadway to safety combines vertical and horizontal travel with door-finding and vehicle-exit delay. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b109-v14-34","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性：定量估算","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b109-v14-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「所需疏散時間」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Required evacuation time” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：前置時間=96 s；行走距離=360 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。RSET=tpre+d/v=546 s。僅把行走距離增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為591 s。邊界：單群體固定速度，不含排隊煙熱及能力差異，不能單獨判安全；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=96 s; travel distance=360 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s. RSET=tpre+d/v=546 s. Increasing only travel distance by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 591 s. Boundary: One group at fixed speed without queues, smoke or mobility differences; not a safety conclusion. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：分階段記錄從車內到安全通道的實際路徑。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Record the staged route from vehicle interior to the safe passage.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b109-v14-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：前置時間=96 s；行走距離=360 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。RSET=tpre+d/v=546 s。僅把行走距離增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為591 s。邊界：單群體固定速度，不含排隊煙熱及能力差異，不能單獨判安全；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=96 s; travel distance=360 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s. RSET=tpre+d/v=546 s. Increasing only travel distance by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 591 s. Boundary: One group at fixed speed without queues, smoke or mobility differences; not a safety conclusion. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]},{"id":"b109-v14-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「疏散時間與分區可用性」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Evacuation time and zone availability\", which statement holds?","options":["目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。","原創教學假設：前置時間=96 s；行走距離=360 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。","混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。"],"optionsEn":["No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.","Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=96 s; travel distance=360 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s.","Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：前置時間=96 s；行走距離=360 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=96 s; travel distance=360 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b109-v14-35","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b109-v14-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「所需疏散時間」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Required evacuation time” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"分階段記錄從車內到安全通道的實際路徑。以人流模擬或受控演練分辨前置時間、行走與門口排隊，核對每個出口接收區的可用狀態及通訊紀錄。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Record the staged route from vehicle interior to the safe passage. Separate pre-movement, travel and doorway queues through simulation or controlled drills, checking receiving-zone availability and communication records for each exit. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「所需疏散時間」的交付需回答：分階段記錄從車內到安全通道的實際路徑。疏散模型保留人口、速度分布及出口狀態，演練改動由營運與防災責任者批准，教材算例不得當作現場指揮程序。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Eurasia Tunnel, the required evacuation time handover must address the following evidence: Record the staged route from vehicle interior to the safe passage. Retain population, speed distribution and exit states; operations and fire-safety owners approve drill changes, and classroom calculations are not incident-command procedures.","failure":"注意干擾：只量平面最短線會漏掉樓層轉換和排隊。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A plan-view shortest line omits level changes and queues. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b109-v14-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"分階段記錄從車內到安全通道的實際路徑。以人流模擬或受控演練分辨前置時間、行走與門口排隊，核對每個出口接收區的可用狀態及通訊紀錄。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Record the staged route from vehicle interior to the safe passage. Separate pre-movement, travel and doorway queues through simulation or controlled drills, checking receiving-zone availability and communication records for each exit. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]},{"id":"b109-v14-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「所需疏散時間」的交付需回答：分階段記錄從車內到安全通道的實際路徑。疏散模型保留人口、速度分布及出口狀態，演練改動由營運與防災責任者批准，教材算例不得當作現場指揮程序。","textEn":"For Eurasia Tunnel, the required evacuation time handover must address the following evidence: Record the staged route from vehicle interior to the safe passage. Retain population, speed distribution and exit states; operations and fire-safety owners approve drill changes, and classroom calculations are not incident-command procedures.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「疏散時間與分區可用性」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Evacuation time and zone availability\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","接縫平均寬度合格就不必量測局部錯台及扭轉。","分階段記錄從車內到安全通道的實際路徑。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","An acceptable average joint width makes local offset and twist measurements unnecessary.","Record the staged route from vehicle interior to the safe passage."],"answer":2,"explanation":"分階段記錄從車內到安全通道的實際路徑。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Record the staged route from vehicle interior to the safe passage. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b109-v14-36","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性：失效診斷","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b109-v14-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「所需疏散時間」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Required evacuation time” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只量平面最短線會漏掉樓層轉換和排隊。以最快成人速度套全部旅客會低估需求，若忽略接收孔受煙或車流影響，疏散可能移到另一個危險邊界。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A plan-view shortest line omits level changes and queues. Applying the fastest adult speed to everyone understates demand; overlooking smoke or traffic in the receiving bore can transfer evacuees into another hazard. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：人員速度會受煙熱、能見度及行動能力影響，安全判斷還要比較可用安全時間；橫通道存在但門或鄰孔不可用時，圖上的最短路線不一定能作實際選擇。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A passage shown on a plan may be unusable because its door or receiving bore is unavailable, invalidating the nominal shortest route.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b109-v14-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只量平面最短線會漏掉樓層轉換和排隊。以最快成人速度套全部旅客會低估需求，若忽略接收孔受煙或車流影響，疏散可能移到另一個危險邊界。","textEn":"A plan-view shortest line omits level changes and queues. Applying the fastest adult speed to everyone understates demand; overlooking smoke or traffic in the receiving bore can transfer evacuees into another hazard.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]},{"id":"b109-v14-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「疏散時間與分區可用性」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Evacuation time and zone availability\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["只量平面最短線會漏掉樓層轉換和排隊。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。"],"optionsEn":["A plan-view shortest line omits level changes and queues.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted."],"answer":0,"explanation":"只量平面最短線會漏掉樓層轉換和排隊。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A plan-view shortest line omits level changes and queues. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b109-v14-37","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b109-v14-36"],"objective":"說明「資產資料完整度」如何影響歐亞海底公路隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Asset-record completeness” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Eurasia Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"道路系統資料需保留樓層與方向，研究相同里程上下層設備被錯配時如何影響維修和告警定位。地下設備的竣工資料必須讓維護人員找到正確位置、材料批次和控制版本。只有上傳圖面而沒有變更歷程，無法分辨元件替換與真正劣化；告警、儀器、線路及工單使用一致識別碼，才可能把量測趨勢連回實際受力或水力系統。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「資產資料完整度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Asset records must retain level and direction to prevent upper- and lower-deck equipment at one chainage being confused. Handover must let maintainers find the correct location, material batch and control revision. Drawings without change history cannot distinguish replacement from deterioration. Consistent identifiers across alarms, instruments, circuits and work orders are essential for linking trends to the physical structural or hydraulic system instead of treating each record as an isolated file. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Asset-record completeness” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：設備總數=108 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: asset count=108 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=85.1852 %.","failure":"常見誤解：「全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「資產資料完整度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Asset-record completeness”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b109-v14-37-k1","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover","text":"道路系統資料需保留樓層與方向，研究相同里程上下層設備被錯配時如何影響維修和告警定位。地下設備的竣工資料必須讓維護人員找到正確位置、材料批次和控制版本。","textEn":"Asset records must retain level and direction to prevent upper- and lower-deck equipment at one chainage being confused. Handover must let maintainers find the correct location, material batch and control revision.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]},{"id":"b109-v14-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「資產編碼與可追溯交接」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Asset identity and traceable handover\" is correct?","options":["全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。","道路系統資料需保留樓層與方向，研究相同里程上下層設備被錯配時如何影響維修和告警定位。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.","Asset records must retain level and direction to prevent upper- and lower-deck equipment at one chainage being confused.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":1,"explanation":"道路系統資料需保留樓層與方向，研究相同里程上下層設備被錯配時如何影響維修和告警定位。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Asset records must retain level and direction to prevent upper- and lower-deck equipment at one chainage being confused. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b109-v14-38","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：定量估算","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b109-v14-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「資產資料完整度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Asset-record completeness” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：設備總數=108 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。coverage=100(N−missing)/N=85.1852 %。僅把缺紀錄數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為83.7037 %。邊界：資料完整度，不等於安全或可靠度；擾動為連續敏感度，實際個數為整數；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: asset count=108 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=85.1852 %. Increasing only missing records by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 83.7037 %. Boundary: Record completeness, not safety or reliability; perturbation is continuous sensitivity while actual counts are integers. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：抽查告警座標能否唯一定位到樓層、方向和裝置。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Test whether alarm coordinates uniquely identify level, direction and asset.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b109-v14-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：設備總數=108 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。coverage=100(N−missing)/N=85.1852 %。僅把缺紀錄數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為83.7037 %。邊界：資料完整度，不等於安全或可靠度；擾動為連續敏感度，實際個數為整數；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: asset count=108 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=85.1852 %. Increasing only missing records by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 83.7037 %. Boundary: Record completeness, not safety or reliability; perturbation is continuous sensitivity while actual counts are integers. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]},{"id":"b109-v14-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「資產編碼與可追溯交接」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Asset identity and traceable handover\", which statement holds?","options":["刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。","只要空間分成兩層就可以採用相同的樓板荷載。","原創教學假設：設備總數=108 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。"],"optionsEn":["A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance.","Any space divided into two levels can use the same deck loading.","Original teaching assumptions: asset count=108 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=85.1852 %."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：設備總數=108 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: asset count=108 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=85.1852 %. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b109-v14-39","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b109-v14-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「資產資料完整度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Asset-record completeness” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"抽查告警座標能否唯一定位到樓層、方向和裝置。抽取一條告警，從控制畫面追到設備、線路、圖面和工單，核對位置、版本及校正日期並記錄無法閉合的欄位。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Test whether alarm coordinates uniquely identify level, direction and asset. Trace a sampled alarm from screen to equipment, circuit, drawing and work order, checking location, revision and calibration dates and recording broken links. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「資產資料完整度」的交付需回答：抽查告警座標能否唯一定位到樓層、方向和裝置。交接以可完成的定位、查找與復原任務驗證，由維護責任人確認現場可用性；完整度只是資料指標，不代表結構安全或設備可靠。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Eurasia Tunnel, the asset-record completeness handover must address the following evidence: Test whether alarm coordinates uniquely identify level, direction and asset. Validate handover through achievable location, retrieval and recovery tasks witnessed by maintainers; completeness measures records, not structural safety or equipment reliability.","failure":"注意干擾：缺樓層欄位會把修繕隊送到同里程的錯誤位置。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Missing level data sends maintainers to the wrong location at the correct chainage. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b109-v14-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"抽查告警座標能否唯一定位到樓層、方向和裝置。抽取一條告警，從控制畫面追到設備、線路、圖面和工單，核對位置、版本及校正日期並記錄無法閉合的欄位。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Test whether alarm coordinates uniquely identify level, direction and asset. Trace a sampled alarm from screen to equipment, circuit, drawing and work order, checking location, revision and calibration dates and recording broken links. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]},{"id":"b109-v14-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「資產資料完整度」的交付需回答：抽查告警座標能否唯一定位到樓層、方向和裝置。交接以可完成的定位、查找與復原任務驗證，由維護責任人確認現場可用性；完整度只是資料指標，不代表結構安全或設備可靠。","textEn":"For Eurasia Tunnel, the asset-record completeness handover must address the following evidence: Test whether alarm coordinates uniquely identify level, direction and asset. Validate handover through achievable location, retrieval and recovery tasks witnessed by maintainers; completeness measures records, not structural safety or equipment reliability.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「資產編碼與可追溯交接」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Asset identity and traceable handover\"?","options":["抽查告警座標能否唯一定位到樓層、方向和裝置。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。"],"optionsEn":["Test whether alarm coordinates uniquely identify level, direction and asset.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel."],"answer":0,"explanation":"抽查告警座標能否唯一定位到樓層、方向和裝置。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Test whether alarm coordinates uniquely identify level, direction and asset. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b109-v14-40","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：失效診斷","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"],"prerequisiteIds":["b109-v14-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「資產資料完整度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Asset-record completeness” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"缺樓層欄位會把修繕隊送到同里程的錯誤位置。設備改名卻未更新控制畫面會引導人員隔離錯誤回路，材料批次缺漏則使同批缺陷無法追蹤到其他位置。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Missing level data sends maintainers to the wrong location at the correct chainage. Renaming an asset without updating the screen can isolate the wrong circuit; missing material batches prevent tracing related defects at other locations. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：只有上傳圖面而沒有變更歷程，無法分辨元件替換與真正劣化；告警、儀器、線路及工單使用一致識別碼，才可能把量測趨勢連回實際受力或水力系統。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Consistent identifiers across alarms, instruments, circuits and work orders are essential for linking trends to the physical structural or hydraulic system instead of treating each record as an isolated file.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b109-v14-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"缺樓層欄位會把修繕隊送到同里程的錯誤位置。設備改名卻未更新控制畫面會引導人員隔離錯誤回路，材料批次缺漏則使同批缺陷無法追蹤到其他位置。","textEn":"Missing level data sends maintainers to the wrong location at the correct chainage. Renaming an asset without updating the screen can isolate the wrong circuit; missing material batches prevent tracing related defects at other locations.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]},{"id":"b109-v14-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「資產編碼與可追溯交接」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Asset identity and traceable handover\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","缺樓層欄位會把修繕隊送到同里程的錯誤位置。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Missing level data sends maintainers to the wrong location at the correct chainage.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":1,"explanation":"缺樓層欄位會把修繕隊送到同里程的錯誤位置。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Missing level data sends maintainers to the wrong location at the correct chainage. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b109","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b109-event-0"],"curriculumVersion":14,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000},{"id":"b110","title":"東京灣跨海公路隧道","titleEn":"Tokyo Bay Aqua-Line tunnel","category":"underground","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"東京灣跨海公路結合海底隧道、人工島與橋梁，大林組工程史列整體道路15.1公里及1997年施工標竣工。本課把整體走廊與承包商施工範圍分開，聚焦人工島支承、地下接合、環片與止水、通風和鹽害；不把某一標段紀錄泛化為整個工程所有部位的參數。","summaryEn":"The Tokyo Bay Aqua-Line combines a subsea tunnel, artificial islands and a bridge. Obayashi records a 15.1 km road corridor and completion of its contract in 1997. The course separates corridor and contract scope, focusing on island support, underground connections, segments, sealing, ventilation and marine deterioration without generalising one contract to every structure.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"ug-landmarks","subcategoryTitle":"世界隧道與地下巨作","subcategoryTitleEn":"World tunnels and underground landmarks","learningTrack":"underground","learningSubdiscipline":"ug-landmarks","learningTags":["underground","ug-landmarks","tunnel"],"architectureFamily":"tunnel","architectureNodes":[["路線里程與端點","Alignment chainage and endpoints"],["測壓水頭","Piezometric head"],["襯砌背後幾何空隙","Geometric lining annulus"],["止水壓縮餘量","Gasket compression reserve"],["差異沉陷梯度","Differential settlement gradient"],["擴散特徵長度","Diffusion characteristic length"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,5],[1,5]],"diagram":{"type":"tunnel","labels":["路線里程與端點","測壓水頭","襯砌背後幾何空隙","止水壓縮餘量","差異沉陷梯度"],"labelsEn":["Alignment chainage and endpoints","Piezometric head","Geometric lining annulus","Gasket compression reserve","Differential settlement gradient"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"原創綜合審查：先計算「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」，再獨立計算「接頭壓縮與水密包絡」。原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=67 m。p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=657.27 kPa。僅把水頭增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為722.997 kPa。邊界：靜水表壓，不是土體總壓或原位量測；不是本工程實測或允收值。原創教學假設：初始壓縮=19 mm；張開量=4 mm；幾何公差=2 mm。c_res=c0−opening−tolerance=13 mm。僅把張開量增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為12.6 mm。邊界：單向幾何餘量，不是接觸壓或水密合格證明；不是本工程實測或允收值。兩組結果的單位與邊界不同，不能直接相加。請列出一項缺少的現場輸入，說明它會影響哪個結論，以及哪種獨立量測可以縮小不確定度。","textEn":"Original integrated review: first calculate piezometric head and lining pressure, then independently calculate joint compression and sealing envelope. Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=67 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=657.27 kPa. Increasing only head by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 722.997 kPa. Boundary: Hydrostatic gauge pressure, not total earth pressure or an in-situ measurement. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Original teaching assumptions: initial compression=19 mm; opening=4 mm; tolerance=2 mm. c_res=c0−opening−tolerance=13 mm. Increasing only opening by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 12.6 mm. Boundary: One-direction geometric reserve, not contact pressure or proof of watertightness. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. The outputs have different units and boundaries and cannot simply be added. Identify one missing field input, explain which conclusion it changes and select an independent measurement to reduce uncertainty.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":14,"enrichmentVersion":14,"stages":[{"id":"b110-v14-s1","title":"地層條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Ground conditions, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「服務邊界與路線代價」與「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\" and \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b110-v14-01","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「路線里程與端點」如何影響東京灣跨海公路隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Alignment chainage and endpoints” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Tokyo Bay Aqua-Line tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"東京灣跨海公路的橋、島和隧道服務不同功能，教學路線比較保留人工島轉接與整條道路端點。隧道選線同時改變洞口、覆土與縱坡，短路線不保證低地質風險。比較方案必須使用相同起訖點，並分開主孔、引道及服務坑的工程數量；交通時間只是需求的一個指標，不能代替施工可達性或長期維修評估。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「路線里程與端點」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Bridge, island and tunnel serve different functions; retain island transitions and whole-road endpoints when comparing the crossing. Alignment changes portals, cover and gradient together, so a shorter tunnel need not have lower geological risk. Compare options between identical endpoints and distinguish running bores, approaches and service galleries. Travel time measures one service benefit but cannot replace assessment of construction access, maintenance closures or exposure to uncertain ground. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Alignment chainage and endpoints” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：長度=15.6 km；速度=60 km/h。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: length=15.6 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=15.6 min.","failure":"常見誤解：「最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「路線里程與端點」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Alignment chainage and endpoints”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b110-v14-01-k1","title":"服務邊界與路線代價","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost","text":"東京灣跨海公路的橋、島和隧道服務不同功能，教學路線比較保留人工島轉接與整條道路端點。隧道選線同時改變洞口、覆土與縱坡，短路線不保證低地質風險。","textEn":"Bridge, island and tunnel serve different functions; retain island transitions and whole-road endpoints when comparing the crossing. Alignment changes portals, cover and gradient together, so a shorter tunnel need not have lower geological risk.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b110-v14-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「服務邊界與路線代價」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\" is correct?","options":["最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。","東京灣跨海公路的橋、島和隧道服務不同功能，教學路線比較保留人工島轉接與整條道路端點。","目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。"],"optionsEn":["The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.","Bridge, island and tunnel serve different functions; retain island transitions and whole-road endpoints when comparing the crossing.","No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design."],"answer":1,"explanation":"東京灣跨海公路的橋、島和隧道服務不同功能，教學路線比較保留人工島轉接與整條道路端點。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Bridge, island and tunnel serve different functions; retain island transitions and whole-road endpoints when comparing the crossing. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b110-v14-02","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：定量估算","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b110-v14-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「路線里程與端點」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Alignment chainage and endpoints” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：長度=15.6 km；速度=60 km/h。t=60L/v=15.6 min。僅把長度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為17.16 min。邊界：假想交通旅程，未含加減速、排隊及實際時刻表；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: length=15.6 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=15.6 min. Increasing only length by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 17.16 min. Boundary: Hypothetical transport journey excluding acceleration, queues and the real timetable. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將橋長、隧道長與道路連接範圍分欄核對。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Reconcile bridge, tunnel and connecting-road scope in separate columns.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b110-v14-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：長度=15.6 km；速度=60 km/h。t=60L/v=15.6 min。僅把長度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為17.16 min。邊界：假想交通旅程，未含加減速、排隊及實際時刻表；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: length=15.6 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=15.6 min. Increasing only length by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 17.16 min. Boundary: Hypothetical transport journey excluding acceleration, queues and the real timetable. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b110-v14-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「服務邊界與路線代價」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\", which statement holds?","options":["灌入體積等於理論空隙就能證明襯砌背後全部填滿。","接縫平均寬度合格就不必量測局部錯台及扭轉。","原創教學假設：長度=15.6 km；速度=60 km/h。"],"optionsEn":["Injected volume equal to the theoretical annulus proves complete filling behind the lining.","An acceptable average joint width makes local offset and twist measurements unnecessary.","Original teaching assumptions: length=15.6 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=15.6 min."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：長度=15.6 km；速度=60 km/h。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: length=15.6 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=15.6 min. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b110-v14-03","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b110-v14-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「路線里程與端點」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Alignment chainage and endpoints” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將橋長、隧道長與道路連接範圍分欄核對。把縱斷面、地形與地質剖面疊合，以端點坐標獨立反算距離，再將主孔與支坑數量分開核對。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Reconcile bridge, tunnel and connecting-road scope in separate columns. Overlay the longitudinal profile, terrain and geology; independently derive distances from endpoint coordinates and reconcile running-bore and gallery quantities separately. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「路線里程與端點」的交付需回答：將橋長、隧道長與道路連接範圍分欄核對。在方案表中凍結起訖點、計量範圍及地質假設，任何改線都要同步更新高程、數量與服務情境，不能只替換總長。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Tokyo Bay Aqua-Line tunnel, the alignment chainage and endpoints handover must address the following evidence: Reconcile bridge, tunnel and connecting-road scope in separate columns. Freeze endpoints, measurement scope and ground assumptions in the option register; realignment requires coordinated updates to elevations, quantities and service scenarios rather than replacing one length.","failure":"注意干擾：把整條道路長度當盾構掘進長度會誤估設備需求。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Treating road length as shield-drive length misstates equipment requirements. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b110-v14-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將橋長、隧道長與道路連接範圍分欄核對。把縱斷面、地形與地質剖面疊合，以端點坐標獨立反算距離，再將主孔與支坑數量分開核對。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Reconcile bridge, tunnel and connecting-road scope in separate columns. Overlay the longitudinal profile, terrain and geology; independently derive distances from endpoint coordinates and reconcile running-bore and gallery quantities separately. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b110-v14-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「路線里程與端點」的交付需回答：將橋長、隧道長與道路連接範圍分欄核對。在方案表中凍結起訖點、計量範圍及地質假設，任何改線都要同步更新高程、數量與服務情境，不能只替換總長。","textEn":"For Tokyo Bay Aqua-Line tunnel, the alignment chainage and endpoints handover must address the following evidence: Reconcile bridge, tunnel and connecting-road scope in separate columns. Freeze endpoints, measurement scope and ground assumptions in the option register; realignment requires coordinated updates to elevations, quantities and service scenarios rather than replacing one length.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「服務邊界與路線代價」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\"?","options":["將橋長、隧道長與道路連接範圍分欄核對。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","各管節平均高程接近就能排除接頭差異變形。"],"optionsEn":["Reconcile bridge, tunnel and connecting-road scope in separate columns.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Similar mean element elevations exclude differential movement at joints."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將橋長、隧道長與道路連接範圍分欄核對。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Reconcile bridge, tunnel and connecting-road scope in separate columns. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b110-v14-04","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：失效診斷","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b110-v14-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「路線里程與端點」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Alignment chainage and endpoints” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把整條道路長度當盾構掘進長度會誤估設備需求。混用全線與單孔長度會同時扭曲工程數量、行程及逃生距離，造成方案比較失去共同基準。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Treating road length as shield-drive length misstates equipment requirements. Mixing whole-route and single-bore lengths distorts quantities, journey time and escape distance, destroying the common basis of an option comparison. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：比較方案必須使用相同起訖點，並分開主孔、引道及服務坑的工程數量；交通時間只是需求的一個指標，不能代替施工可達性或長期維修評估。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Travel time measures one service benefit but cannot replace assessment of construction access, maintenance closures or exposure to uncertain ground.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b110-v14-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把整條道路長度當盾構掘進長度會誤估設備需求。混用全線與單孔長度會同時扭曲工程數量、行程及逃生距離，造成方案比較失去共同基準。","textEn":"Treating road length as shield-drive length misstates equipment requirements. Mixing whole-route and single-bore lengths distorts quantities, journey time and escape distance, destroying the common basis of an option comparison.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b110-v14-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「服務邊界與路線代價」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","把整條道路長度當盾構掘進長度會誤估設備需求。","目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Treating road length as shield-drive length misstates equipment requirements.","No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把整條道路長度當盾構掘進長度會誤估設備需求。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Treating road length as shield-drive length misstates equipment requirements. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b110-v14-05","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b110-v14-04"],"objective":"說明「測壓水頭」如何影響東京灣跨海公路隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Piezometric head” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Tokyo Bay Aqua-Line tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"人工島與海底孔的水頭邊界不同，研究島內降水和海床補注如何影響接合區壓力。水壓取決於連通含水層的測壓水頭，不必等於地表或海面至洞頂的幾何深度。排水降低水壓卻可能增加有效應力與沉陷；停泵或排水堵塞後水頭又會回升，因此防水、排水及環境保水是互相制約的設計選擇。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「測壓水頭」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Artificial-island and subsea heads differ; examine how island drainage and seabed recharge affect connection-zone pressure. Water pressure follows piezometric head in the connected aquifer, not automatically the geometric depth below ground or sea level. Drainage reduces pressure but can increase effective stress and settlement. Head may recover after a pump outage or blockage, coupling waterproofing, drainage capacity and preservation of surrounding groundwater in the permanent design. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Piezometric head” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=67 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=67 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=657.27 kPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「測壓水頭」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Piezometric head”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b110-v14-05-k1","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure","text":"人工島與海底孔的水頭邊界不同，研究島內降水和海床補注如何影響接合區壓力。水壓取決於連通含水層的測壓水頭，不必等於地表或海面至洞頂的幾何深度。","textEn":"Artificial-island and subsea heads differ; examine how island drainage and seabed recharge affect connection-zone pressure. Water pressure follows piezometric head in the connected aquifer, not automatically the geometric depth below ground or sea level.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b110-v14-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\" is correct?","options":["目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。","刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。","人工島與海底孔的水頭邊界不同，研究島內降水和海床補注如何影響接合區壓力。"],"optionsEn":["No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.","A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance.","Artificial-island and subsea heads differ; examine how island drainage and seabed recharge affect connection-zone pressure."],"answer":2,"explanation":"人工島與海底孔的水頭邊界不同，研究島內降水和海床補注如何影響接合區壓力。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Artificial-island and subsea heads differ; examine how island drainage and seabed recharge affect connection-zone pressure. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b110-v14-06","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓：定量估算","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b110-v14-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「測壓水頭」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Piezometric head” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=67 m。p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=657.27 kPa。僅把水頭增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為722.997 kPa。邊界：靜水表壓，不是土體總壓或原位量測；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=67 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=657.27 kPa. Increasing only head by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 722.997 kPa. Boundary: Hydrostatic gauge pressure, not total earth pressure or an in-situ measurement. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比較島內外測壓管與潮位反應的幅度和延遲。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare amplitudes and lags of piezometer and tide responses inside and outside the island.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b110-v14-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=67 m。p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=657.27 kPa。僅把水頭增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為722.997 kPa。邊界：靜水表壓，不是土體總壓或原位量測；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=67 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=657.27 kPa. Increasing only head by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 722.997 kPa. Boundary: Hydrostatic gauge pressure, not total earth pressure or an in-situ measurement. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b110-v14-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=67 m。","混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=67 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=657.27 kPa.","Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=67 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=67 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=657.27 kPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b110-v14-07","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b110-v14-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「測壓水頭」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Piezometric head” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比較島內外測壓管與潮位反應的幅度和延遲。使用分層測壓管及流量計，配合降雨或潮位序列分辨補注與設備影響，將讀值統一換算至同一高程基準。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare amplitudes and lags of piezometer and tide responses inside and outside the island. Use nested piezometers and flowmeters with rainfall or tide histories to distinguish recharge from equipment effects, converting observations to a common elevation datum. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「測壓水頭」的交付需回答：比較島內外測壓管與潮位反應的幅度和延遲。設計檢核應分列正常排水、堵塞與停電水位，將環境受體的容許變化和監測責任一起交付，不把抽水量當唯一指標。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Tokyo Bay Aqua-Line tunnel, the piezometric head handover must address the following evidence: Compare amplitudes and lags of piezometer and tide responses inside and outside the island. Separate normal drainage, blocked-drain and power-outage heads and hand over receptor limits and monitoring responsibility together rather than using pump flow as the sole indicator.","failure":"注意干擾：島內低水頭不代表接合外圍海床同樣卸壓。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Low island head does not establish relief in the surrounding seabed. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b110-v14-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比較島內外測壓管與潮位反應的幅度和延遲。使用分層測壓管及流量計，配合降雨或潮位序列分辨補注與設備影響，將讀值統一換算至同一高程基準。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Compare amplitudes and lags of piezometer and tide responses inside and outside the island. Use nested piezometers and flowmeters with rainfall or tide histories to distinguish recharge from equipment effects, converting observations to a common elevation datum. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b110-v14-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「測壓水頭」的交付需回答：比較島內外測壓管與潮位反應的幅度和延遲。設計檢核應分列正常排水、堵塞與停電水位，將環境受體的容許變化和監測責任一起交付，不把抽水量當唯一指標。","textEn":"For Tokyo Bay Aqua-Line tunnel, the piezometric head handover must address the following evidence: Compare amplitudes and lags of piezometer and tide responses inside and outside the island. Separate normal drainage, blocked-drain and power-outage heads and hand over receptor limits and monitoring responsibility together rather than using pump flow as the sole indicator.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","比較島內外測壓管與潮位反應的幅度和延遲。","風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Compare amplitudes and lags of piezometer and tide responses inside and outside the island.","Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel."],"answer":1,"explanation":"比較島內外測壓管與潮位反應的幅度和延遲。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare amplitudes and lags of piezometer and tide responses inside and outside the island. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b110-v14-08","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓：失效診斷","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b110-v14-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「測壓水頭」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Piezometric head” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"島內低水頭不代表接合外圍海床同樣卸壓。將暫時降水後的低水頭當成永久狀態，會漏掉停泵後外壓回升；過度排水也可能引起周邊地層壓密。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Low island head does not establish relief in the surrounding seabed. Treating temporarily lowered head as permanent misses pressure recovery after outage; excessive drainage can also consolidate surrounding ground. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：排水降低水壓卻可能增加有效應力與沉陷；停泵或排水堵塞後水頭又會回升，因此防水、排水及環境保水是互相制約的設計選擇。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Head may recover after a pump outage or blockage, coupling waterproofing, drainage capacity and preservation of surrounding groundwater in the permanent design.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b110-v14-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"島內低水頭不代表接合外圍海床同樣卸壓。將暫時降水後的低水頭當成永久狀態，會漏掉停泵後外壓回升；過度排水也可能引起周邊地層壓密。","textEn":"Low island head does not establish relief in the surrounding seabed. Treating temporarily lowered head as permanent misses pressure recovery after outage; excessive drainage can also consolidate surrounding ground.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b110-v14-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。","島內低水頭不代表接合外圍海床同樣卸壓。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance.","Low island head does not establish relief in the surrounding seabed."],"answer":2,"explanation":"島內低水頭不代表接合外圍海床同樣卸壓。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Low island head does not establish relief in the surrounding seabed. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b110-v14-s2","title":"機制、材料與定量設計","titleEn":"Mechanisms, materials and quantitative design","description":"本階段聚焦「掘進利用率與設備停時」與「背填連續性與體積帳」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime\" and \"Backfill continuity and volume balance\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b110-v14-09","title":"掘進利用率與設備停時：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b110-v14-08"],"objective":"說明「有效掘進利用率」如何影響東京灣跨海公路隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Effective boring utilisation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Tokyo Bay Aqua-Line tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"大直徑海底盾構的切削與環片物流互相制約，教材以Aqua-Line背景區分單次高進尺與整班利用率。TBM瞬時貫入率只描述刀盤切削的一段時間，拼裝、換刀、出渣與維修決定每天真正進尺。岩石強度與磨蝕性對刀具的影響不同，混合掌子面又產生不對稱作用；比較機器績效須按地質分區和停時原因分類，不能只排序最高進尺。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「有效掘進利用率」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Large-diameter cutting and segment logistics interact; distinguish high short-duration advance from whole-shift utilisation in the Aqua-Line setting. Instantaneous penetration describes only active cutting; erection, cutter changes, muck handling and repairs determine daily advance. Strength and abrasivity affect cutters differently, while mixed faces impose asymmetric loading. Compare performance by ground domain and downtime cause, because the highest short-duration penetration rate can coexist with poor daily production and increased maintenance demand. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Effective boring utilisation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：切削速率=1.77 m/h；有效利用率=0.28 無因次。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: active penetration=1.77 m/h; utilisation=0.28 dimensionless.","failure":"常見誤解：「刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「有效掘進利用率」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Effective boring utilisation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b110-v14-09-k1","title":"掘進利用率與設備停時","titleEn":"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime","text":"大直徑海底盾構的切削與環片物流互相制約，教材以Aqua-Line背景區分單次高進尺與整班利用率。TBM瞬時貫入率只描述刀盤切削的一段時間，拼裝、換刀、出渣與維修決定每天真正進尺。","textEn":"Large-diameter cutting and segment logistics interact; distinguish high short-duration advance from whole-shift utilisation in the Aqua-Line setting. Instantaneous penetration describes only active cutting; erection, cutter changes, muck handling and repairs determine daily advance.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b110-v14-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「掘進利用率與設備停時」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime\" is correct?","options":["大直徑海底盾構的切削與環片物流互相制約，教材以Aqua-Line背景區分單次高進尺與整班利用率。","刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。","灌入體積等於理論空隙就能證明襯砌背後全部填滿。"],"optionsEn":["Large-diameter cutting and segment logistics interact; distinguish high short-duration advance from whole-shift utilisation in the Aqua-Line setting.","A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance.","Injected volume equal to the theoretical annulus proves complete filling behind the lining."],"answer":0,"explanation":"大直徑海底盾構的切削與環片物流互相制約，教材以Aqua-Line背景區分單次高進尺與整班利用率。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Large-diameter cutting and segment logistics interact; distinguish high short-duration advance from whole-shift utilisation in the Aqua-Line setting. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b110-v14-10","title":"掘進利用率與設備停時：定量估算","titleEn":"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b110-v14-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「有效掘進利用率」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Effective boring utilisation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：切削速率=1.77 m/h；有效利用率=0.28 無因次。D=24vu=11.8944 m/day。僅把有效利用率增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為13.0838 m/day。邊界：平均循環模型，未表示地質轉換及停機分布；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: active penetration=1.77 m/h; utilisation=0.28 dimensionless. D=24vu=11.8944 m/day. Increasing only utilisation by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 13.0838 m/day. Boundary: Mean-cycle model without ground transitions or downtime distribution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：把環片到場、拼裝和切削時間對齊，找真正瓶頸。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Align segment delivery, erection and cutting times to identify the bottleneck.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b110-v14-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：切削速率=1.77 m/h；有效利用率=0.28 無因次。D=24vu=11.8944 m/day。僅把有效利用率增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為13.0838 m/day。邊界：平均循環模型，未表示地質轉換及停機分布；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: active penetration=1.77 m/h; utilisation=0.28 dimensionless. D=24vu=11.8944 m/day. Increasing only utilisation by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 13.0838 m/day. Boundary: Mean-cycle model without ground transitions or downtime distribution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b110-v14-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「掘進利用率與設備停時」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime\", which statement holds?","options":["接縫平均寬度合格就不必量測局部錯台及扭轉。","原創教學假設：切削速率=1.77 m/h；有效利用率=0.28 無因次。","各管節平均高程接近就能排除接頭差異變形。"],"optionsEn":["An acceptable average joint width makes local offset and twist measurements unnecessary.","Original teaching assumptions: active penetration=1.77 m/h; utilisation=0.28 dimensionless.","Similar mean element elevations exclude differential movement at joints."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：切削速率=1.77 m/h；有效利用率=0.28 無因次。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: active penetration=1.77 m/h; utilisation=0.28 dimensionless. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b110-v14-11","title":"掘進利用率與設備停時：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b110-v14-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「有效掘進利用率」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Effective boring utilisation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"把環片到場、拼裝和切削時間對齊，找真正瓶頸。由時間戳分離切削、拼裝與故障，將刀具位置、磨耗量及推力扭矩對齊里程，檢查停時是否集中在特定地層。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Align segment delivery, erection and cutting times to identify the bottleneck. Separate cutting, erection and faults by timestamp; align cutter position, wear, thrust and torque with chainage and test clustering by ground type. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「有效掘進利用率」的交付需回答：把環片到場、拼裝和切削時間對齊，找真正瓶頸。停機紀錄使用可追溯原因碼，把地質變化與設備故障分開統計，參數調整只能在設備和施工團隊核准程序內進行。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Tokyo Bay Aqua-Line tunnel, the effective boring utilisation handover must address the following evidence: Align segment delivery, erection and cutting times to identify the bottleneck. Use traceable downtime codes, separating geological change from equipment faults; parameter changes stay within procedures approved by equipment and construction teams.","failure":"注意干擾：提高切削速度但環片供應不足只會增加等待。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Faster cutting with inadequate segment supply merely increases waiting. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b110-v14-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"把環片到場、拼裝和切削時間對齊，找真正瓶頸。由時間戳分離切削、拼裝與故障，將刀具位置、磨耗量及推力扭矩對齊里程，檢查停時是否集中在特定地層。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Align segment delivery, erection and cutting times to identify the bottleneck. Separate cutting, erection and faults by timestamp; align cutter position, wear, thrust and torque with chainage and test clustering by ground type. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b110-v14-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「有效掘進利用率」的交付需回答：把環片到場、拼裝和切削時間對齊，找真正瓶頸。停機紀錄使用可追溯原因碼，把地質變化與設備故障分開統計，參數調整只能在設備和施工團隊核准程序內進行。","textEn":"For Tokyo Bay Aqua-Line tunnel, the effective boring utilisation handover must address the following evidence: Align segment delivery, erection and cutting times to identify the bottleneck. Use traceable downtime codes, separating geological change from equipment faults; parameter changes stay within procedures approved by equipment and construction teams.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「掘進利用率與設備停時」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","擴散長度就是鋼筋開始腐蝕的位置和精確時間。","把環片到場、拼裝和切削時間對齊，找真正瓶頸。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Diffusion length gives the exact location and time of corrosion initiation.","Align segment delivery, erection and cutting times to identify the bottleneck."],"answer":2,"explanation":"把環片到場、拼裝和切削時間對齊，找真正瓶頸。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Align segment delivery, erection and cutting times to identify the bottleneck. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b110-v14-12","title":"掘進利用率與設備停時：失效診斷","titleEn":"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b110-v14-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「有效掘進利用率」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Effective boring utilisation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"提高切削速度但環片供應不足只會增加等待。只提高瞬時進尺可能使出渣或刀具超出有效工況，短暫改善後增加停機，平均進尺和零件壽命反而下降。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Faster cutting with inadequate segment supply merely increases waiting. Higher instantaneous advance can overload cutters or muck transport and create longer stoppages that reduce average progress and component life. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：岩石強度與磨蝕性對刀具的影響不同，混合掌子面又產生不對稱作用；比較機器績效須按地質分區和停時原因分類，不能只排序最高進尺。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Compare performance by ground domain and downtime cause, because the highest short-duration penetration rate can coexist with poor daily production and increased maintenance demand.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b110-v14-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"提高切削速度但環片供應不足只會增加等待。只提高瞬時進尺可能使出渣或刀具超出有效工況，短暫改善後增加停機，平均進尺和零件壽命反而下降。","textEn":"Faster cutting with inadequate segment supply merely increases waiting. Higher instantaneous advance can overload cutters or muck transport and create longer stoppages that reduce average progress and component life.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b110-v14-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「掘進利用率與設備停時」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["提高切削速度但環片供應不足只會增加等待。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","灌入體積等於理論空隙就能證明襯砌背後全部填滿。"],"optionsEn":["Faster cutting with inadequate segment supply merely increases waiting.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Injected volume equal to the theoretical annulus proves complete filling behind the lining."],"answer":0,"explanation":"提高切削速度但環片供應不足只會增加等待。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Faster cutting with inadequate segment supply merely increases waiting. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b110-v14-13","title":"背填連續性與體積帳：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Backfill continuity and volume balance: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b110-v14-12"],"objective":"說明「襯砌背後幾何空隙」如何影響東京灣跨海公路隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Geometric lining annulus” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Tokyo Bay Aqua-Line tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"海底環片背填需填補幾何空隙，教學體積不能當實際灌漿完成量，因為地層吸收和超挖仍未知。盾尾空隙須由背填恢復襯砌與地層的接觸，但幾何空隙不是必然注入量。超挖、地層吸收、回流和材料體積變化都會改變收支；注入量達到目標仍不代表每個位置填滿，需要把壓力、時間與後續變形一起判讀。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「襯砌背後幾何空隙」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Backfill fills geometric voids, but teaching volume cannot prove completion because ground take and overbreak remain uncertain. Backfill restores contact across the shield-tail gap, but geometric void is not the required injected volume. Overbreak, absorption, return and material volume change alter the balance. Meeting a volume target does not prove complete spatial filling; pressure, timing and later deformation must be interpreted together rather than using a single total. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Geometric lining annulus” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：開挖外徑=8.36 m；襯砌外徑=8.06 m；環長=1.5 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: excavated diameter=8.36 m; lining diameter=8.06 m; ring length=1.5 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「灌入體積等於理論空隙就能證明襯砌背後全部填滿。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Injected volume equal to the theoretical annulus proves complete filling behind the lining.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「襯砌背後幾何空隙」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Geometric lining annulus”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b110-v14-13-k1","title":"背填連續性與體積帳","titleEn":"Backfill continuity and volume balance","text":"海底環片背填需填補幾何空隙，教學體積不能當實際灌漿完成量，因為地層吸收和超挖仍未知。盾尾空隙須由背填恢復襯砌與地層的接觸，但幾何空隙不是必然注入量。","textEn":"Backfill fills geometric voids, but teaching volume cannot prove completion because ground take and overbreak remain uncertain. Backfill restores contact across the shield-tail gap, but geometric void is not the required injected volume.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b110-v14-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：灌入體積等於理論空隙就能證明襯砌背後全部填滿。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Injected volume equal to the theoretical annulus proves complete filling behind the lining. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「背填連續性與體積帳」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Backfill continuity and volume balance\" is correct?","options":["灌入體積等於理論空隙就能證明襯砌背後全部填滿。","海底環片背填需填補幾何空隙，教學體積不能當實際灌漿完成量，因為地層吸收和超挖仍未知。","混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。"],"optionsEn":["Injected volume equal to the theoretical annulus proves complete filling behind the lining.","Backfill fills geometric voids, but teaching volume cannot prove completion because ground take and overbreak remain uncertain.","Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure."],"answer":1,"explanation":"海底環片背填需填補幾何空隙，教學體積不能當實際灌漿完成量，因為地層吸收和超挖仍未知。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Backfill fills geometric voids, but teaching volume cannot prove completion because ground take and overbreak remain uncertain. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b110-v14-14","title":"背填連續性與體積帳：定量估算","titleEn":"Backfill continuity and volume balance: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b110-v14-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「襯砌背後幾何空隙」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Geometric lining annulus” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：開挖外徑=8.36 m；襯砌外徑=8.06 m；環長=1.5 m。V=π(De²−Dl²)L/4=5.80331 m³。僅把環長增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為6.38364 m³。邊界：同心幾何空隙，不等於實際灌漿需求或完成證明；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: excavated diameter=8.36 m; lining diameter=8.06 m; ring length=1.5 m. V=π(De²−Dl²)L/4=5.80331 m³. Increasing only ring length by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 6.38364 m³. Boundary: Concentric geometric void, not actual grout demand or proof of completion. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將注入量、壓力和環片位移同步檢查。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check injected volume, pressure and segment movement together.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b110-v14-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：開挖外徑=8.36 m；襯砌外徑=8.06 m；環長=1.5 m。V=π(De²−Dl²)L/4=5.80331 m³。僅把環長增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為6.38364 m³。邊界：同心幾何空隙，不等於實際灌漿需求或完成證明；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: excavated diameter=8.36 m; lining diameter=8.06 m; ring length=1.5 m. V=π(De²−Dl²)L/4=5.80331 m³. Increasing only ring length by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 6.38364 m³. Boundary: Concentric geometric void, not actual grout demand or proof of completion. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b110-v14-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「背填連續性與體積帳」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Backfill continuity and volume balance\", which statement holds?","options":["兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。","風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。","原創教學假設：開挖外徑=8.36 m；襯砌外徑=8.06 m；環長=1.5 m。"],"optionsEn":["Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.","Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.","Original teaching assumptions: excavated diameter=8.36 m; lining diameter=8.06 m; ring length=1.5 m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：開挖外徑=8.36 m；襯砌外徑=8.06 m；環長=1.5 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: excavated diameter=8.36 m; lining diameter=8.06 m; ring length=1.5 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b110-v14-15","title":"背填連續性與體積帳：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Backfill continuity and volume balance: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b110-v14-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「襯砌背後幾何空隙」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Geometric lining annulus” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將注入量、壓力和環片位移同步檢查。用環片及開挖尺寸計算幾何空隙，核對注入回流質量與時間戳，再以適當無損檢測及變形資料查局部缺填。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check injected volume, pressure and segment movement together. Calculate the annulus from lining and excavation dimensions, reconcile injected/returned mass and timing, then use suitable nondestructive and deformation evidence for local gaps. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「襯砌背後幾何空隙」的交付需回答：將注入量、壓力和環片位移同步檢查。將每環幾何、材料批次及注入回流紀錄綁定，缺填診斷由土建及地工共同確認，後續處置不只追求增加總注量。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Tokyo Bay Aqua-Line tunnel, the geometric lining annulus handover must address the following evidence: Check injected volume, pressure and segment movement together. Link each ring to geometry, material batch and injection/return records; structural and ground teams diagnose gaps together rather than merely increasing volume.","failure":"注意干擾：注入量大於理論空隙可能表示流失而不是更好填充。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Injection above theoretical void volume may indicate loss rather than better filling. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b110-v14-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將注入量、壓力和環片位移同步檢查。用環片及開挖尺寸計算幾何空隙，核對注入回流質量與時間戳，再以適當無損檢測及變形資料查局部缺填。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Check injected volume, pressure and segment movement together. Calculate the annulus from lining and excavation dimensions, reconcile injected/returned mass and timing, then use suitable nondestructive and deformation evidence for local gaps. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b110-v14-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「襯砌背後幾何空隙」的交付需回答：將注入量、壓力和環片位移同步檢查。將每環幾何、材料批次及注入回流紀錄綁定，缺填診斷由土建及地工共同確認，後續處置不只追求增加總注量。","textEn":"For Tokyo Bay Aqua-Line tunnel, the geometric lining annulus handover must address the following evidence: Check injected volume, pressure and segment movement together. Link each ring to geometry, material batch and injection/return records; structural and ground teams diagnose gaps together rather than merely increasing volume.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「背填連續性與體積帳」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Backfill continuity and volume balance\"?","options":["將注入量、壓力和環片位移同步檢查。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Check injected volume, pressure and segment movement together.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將注入量、壓力和環片位移同步檢查。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check injected volume, pressure and segment movement together. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b110-v14-16","title":"背填連續性與體積帳：失效診斷","titleEn":"Backfill continuity and volume balance: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b110-v14-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「襯砌背後幾何空隙」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Geometric lining annulus” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"注入量大於理論空隙可能表示流失而不是更好填充。局部通道讓材料回流時，總注量可能正常但背後仍有空洞，環片變形與接頭滲漏可能延後出現。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Injection above theoretical void volume may indicate loss rather than better filling. Preferential return paths can give normal total injection while leaving voids, with delayed segment distortion and leakage. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：超挖、地層吸收、回流和材料體積變化都會改變收支；注入量達到目標仍不代表每個位置填滿，需要把壓力、時間與後續變形一起判讀。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Meeting a volume target does not prove complete spatial filling; pressure, timing and later deformation must be interpreted together rather than using a single total.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「灌入體積等於理論空隙就能證明襯砌背後全部填滿。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Injected volume equal to the theoretical annulus proves complete filling behind the lining.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b110-v14-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"注入量大於理論空隙可能表示流失而不是更好填充。局部通道讓材料回流時，總注量可能正常但背後仍有空洞，環片變形與接頭滲漏可能延後出現。","textEn":"Injection above theoretical void volume may indicate loss rather than better filling. Preferential return paths can give normal total injection while leaving voids, with delayed segment distortion and leakage.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b110-v14-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「背填連續性與體積帳」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Backfill continuity and volume balance\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","注入量大於理論空隙可能表示流失而不是更好填充。","混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Injection above theoretical void volume may indicate loss rather than better filling.","Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure."],"answer":1,"explanation":"注入量大於理論空隙可能表示流失而不是更好填充。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Injection above theoretical void volume may indicate loss rather than better filling. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b110-v14-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「環向受力與接縫柔度」與「接頭壓縮與水密包絡」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Ring force and joint flexibility\" and \"Joint compression and sealing envelope\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b110-v14-17","title":"環向受力與接縫柔度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Ring force and joint flexibility: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b110-v14-16"],"objective":"說明「襯砌環向壓縮」如何影響東京灣跨海公路隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Lining hoop compression” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Tokyo Bay Aqua-Line tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"人工島接合和海底均勻段具有不同拘束，Aqua-Line環片教材比較均勻環向力與接合局部反力。圓形襯砌對均勻外壓可主要以環向壓縮抵抗，但接頭轉動、偏壓與背填空隙會引起彎矩。薄環膜應力只說明其中一條受力路徑；脫模、運輸、頂推及永久狀態的荷載不同，環片局部接觸與止水條件必須另外檢核。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「襯砌環向壓縮」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Island connections and uniform subsea reaches have different restraints; compare hoop force with local interface reactions. A circular lining resists uniform external pressure largely through hoop compression, but joint rotation, uneven load and backfill voids generate bending. Thin-ring membrane stress describes only one load path. Demoulding, transport, jacking and permanent states impose different actions, requiring separate checks of local segment contact and sealing rather than one permanent-load calculation. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Lining hoop compression” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：均勻外壓=0.48 MPa；半徑=3.4 m；厚度=0.35 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: uniform external pressure=0.48 MPa; radius=3.4 m; thickness=0.35 m. σθ=pr/t=4.66286 MPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「襯砌環向壓縮」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Lining hoop compression”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b110-v14-17-k1","title":"環向受力與接縫柔度","titleEn":"Ring force and joint flexibility","text":"人工島接合和海底均勻段具有不同拘束，Aqua-Line環片教材比較均勻環向力與接合局部反力。圓形襯砌對均勻外壓可主要以環向壓縮抵抗，但接頭轉動、偏壓與背填空隙會引起彎矩。","textEn":"Island connections and uniform subsea reaches have different restraints; compare hoop force with local interface reactions. A circular lining resists uniform external pressure largely through hoop compression, but joint rotation, uneven load and backfill voids generate bending.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b110-v14-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「環向受力與接縫柔度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Ring force and joint flexibility\" is correct?","options":["混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。","接縫平均寬度合格就不必量測局部錯台及扭轉。","人工島接合和海底均勻段具有不同拘束，Aqua-Line環片教材比較均勻環向力與接合局部反力。"],"optionsEn":["Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure.","An acceptable average joint width makes local offset and twist measurements unnecessary.","Island connections and uniform subsea reaches have different restraints; compare hoop force with local interface reactions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"人工島接合和海底均勻段具有不同拘束，Aqua-Line環片教材比較均勻環向力與接合局部反力。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Island connections and uniform subsea reaches have different restraints; compare hoop force with local interface reactions. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b110-v14-18","title":"環向受力與接縫柔度：定量估算","titleEn":"Ring force and joint flexibility: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b110-v14-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「襯砌環向壓縮」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Lining hoop compression” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：均勻外壓=0.48 MPa；半徑=3.4 m；厚度=0.35 m。σθ=pr/t=4.66286 MPa。僅把均勻外壓增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為5.12914 MPa。邊界：薄圓環膜應力，不是接縫、偏壓或矩形框架解；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: uniform external pressure=0.48 MPa; radius=3.4 m; thickness=0.35 m. σθ=pr/t=4.66286 MPa. Increasing only uniform external pressure by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 5.12914 MPa. Boundary: Thin circular-ring membrane stress, not a joint, uneven-load or rectangular-frame solution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：沿接合區與一般區量測環形變形，核對支承模型。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure distortion at interfaces and ordinary reaches to check support assumptions.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b110-v14-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：均勻外壓=0.48 MPa；半徑=3.4 m；厚度=0.35 m。σθ=pr/t=4.66286 MPa。僅把均勻外壓增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為5.12914 MPa。邊界：薄圓環膜應力，不是接縫、偏壓或矩形框架解；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: uniform external pressure=0.48 MPa; radius=3.4 m; thickness=0.35 m. σθ=pr/t=4.66286 MPa. Increasing only uniform external pressure by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 5.12914 MPa. Boundary: Thin circular-ring membrane stress, not a joint, uneven-load or rectangular-frame solution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b110-v14-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「環向受力與接縫柔度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Ring force and joint flexibility\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：均勻外壓=0.48 MPa；半徑=3.4 m；厚度=0.35 m。","各管節平均高程接近就能排除接頭差異變形。","擴散長度就是鋼筋開始腐蝕的位置和精確時間。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: uniform external pressure=0.48 MPa; radius=3.4 m; thickness=0.35 m. σθ=pr/t=4.66286 MPa.","Similar mean element elevations exclude differential movement at joints.","Diffusion length gives the exact location and time of corrosion initiation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：均勻外壓=0.48 MPa；半徑=3.4 m；厚度=0.35 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: uniform external pressure=0.48 MPa; radius=3.4 m; thickness=0.35 m. σθ=pr/t=4.66286 MPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b110-v14-19","title":"環向受力與接縫柔度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Ring force and joint flexibility: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b110-v14-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「襯砌環向壓縮」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Lining hoop compression” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"沿接合區與一般區量測環形變形，核對支承模型。將環形變形、接縫張開與應變和含接頭彈簧的模型比較，分開安裝後、背填後及水頭回升後的基準。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure distortion at interfaces and ordinary reaches to check support assumptions. Compare ring distortion, joint opening and strain with a joint-spring model, separating baselines after installation, grouting and head recovery. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「襯砌環向壓縮」的交付需回答：沿接合區與一般區量測環形變形，核對支承模型。設計圖應分開標註各施工階段、接頭剛度及背填條件，構件驗收同時核對幾何、材料批次與止水試驗適用包絡。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Tokyo Bay Aqua-Line tunnel, the lining hoop compression handover must address the following evidence: Measure distortion at interfaces and ordinary reaches to check support assumptions. Drawings distinguish stages, joint stiffness and backfill conditions; component acceptance reconciles geometry, material batches and the applicable sealing-test envelope.","failure":"注意干擾：套用一般環段模型會漏掉島體沉陷造成的局部作用。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A standard ring model misses local actions from island settlement. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b110-v14-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"沿接合區與一般區量測環形變形，核對支承模型。將環形變形、接縫張開與應變和含接頭彈簧的模型比較，分開安裝後、背填後及水頭回升後的基準。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Measure distortion at interfaces and ordinary reaches to check support assumptions. Compare ring distortion, joint opening and strain with a joint-spring model, separating baselines after installation, grouting and head recovery. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b110-v14-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「襯砌環向壓縮」的交付需回答：沿接合區與一般區量測環形變形，核對支承模型。設計圖應分開標註各施工階段、接頭剛度及背填條件，構件驗收同時核對幾何、材料批次與止水試驗適用包絡。","textEn":"For Tokyo Bay Aqua-Line tunnel, the lining hoop compression handover must address the following evidence: Measure distortion at interfaces and ordinary reaches to check support assumptions. Drawings distinguish stages, joint stiffness and backfill conditions; component acceptance reconciles geometry, material batches and the applicable sealing-test envelope.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「環向受力與接縫柔度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Ring force and joint flexibility\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","沿接合區與一般區量測環形變形，核對支承模型。","目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Measure distortion at interfaces and ordinary reaches to check support assumptions.","No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design."],"answer":1,"explanation":"沿接合區與一般區量測環形變形，核對支承模型。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure distortion at interfaces and ordinary reaches to check support assumptions. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b110-v14-20","title":"環向受力與接縫柔度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Ring force and joint flexibility: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b110-v14-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「襯砌環向壓縮」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Lining hoop compression” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"套用一般環段模型會漏掉島體沉陷造成的局部作用。局部脫空增加環片彎曲，裂縫未必代表混凝土平均強度不足；忽略接縫接觸會把補強方向導向錯誤位置。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A standard ring model misses local actions from island settlement. Local voids increase bending, so cracks need not indicate inadequate mean concrete strength; neglecting joint contact can misdirect strengthening. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：薄環膜應力只說明其中一條受力路徑；脫模、運輸、頂推及永久狀態的荷載不同，環片局部接觸與止水條件必須另外檢核。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Demoulding, transport, jacking and permanent states impose different actions, requiring separate checks of local segment contact and sealing rather than one permanent-load calculation.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b110-v14-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"套用一般環段模型會漏掉島體沉陷造成的局部作用。局部脫空增加環片彎曲，裂縫未必代表混凝土平均強度不足；忽略接縫接觸會把補強方向導向錯誤位置。","textEn":"A standard ring model misses local actions from island settlement. Local voids increase bending, so cracks need not indicate inadequate mean concrete strength; neglecting joint contact can misdirect strengthening.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b110-v14-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「環向受力與接縫柔度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Ring force and joint flexibility\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","接縫平均寬度合格就不必量測局部錯台及扭轉。","套用一般環段模型會漏掉島體沉陷造成的局部作用。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","An acceptable average joint width makes local offset and twist measurements unnecessary.","A standard ring model misses local actions from island settlement."],"answer":2,"explanation":"套用一般環段模型會漏掉島體沉陷造成的局部作用。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A standard ring model misses local actions from island settlement. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b110-v14-21","title":"接頭壓縮與水密包絡：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Joint compression and sealing envelope: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b110-v14-20"],"objective":"說明「止水壓縮餘量」如何影響東京灣跨海公路隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Gasket compression reserve” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Tokyo Bay Aqua-Line tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"大林組記載接合與防水措施，本課以假想接縫研究幾何容許與實際水密試驗的差別。止水條依受控壓縮維持連續接觸，接縫轉角、錯台、污染與材料鬆弛都會降低最不利點的接觸能力。平均壓縮量不能掩蓋局部脫離；全尺寸試驗的結果只對測試過的幾何、水壓及荷載歷程有效，幾何餘量本身並不是接觸壓力。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「止水壓縮餘量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Using documented connection and waterproofing context, a hypothetical joint distinguishes geometric allowance from actual pressure-test performance. A gasket seals through controlled continuous compression; rotation, offset, contamination and relaxation reduce contact at the weakest point. Average compression cannot compensate for local separation. Full-size test results apply only to their tested geometry, head and load history, while a calculated geometric reserve is neither contact pressure nor evidence of watertightness. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Gasket compression reserve” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：初始壓縮=19 mm；張開量=4 mm；幾何公差=2 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: initial compression=19 mm; opening=4 mm; tolerance=2 mm. c_res=c0−opening−tolerance=13 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「接縫平均寬度合格就不必量測局部錯台及扭轉。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"An acceptable average joint width makes local offset and twist measurements unnecessary.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「止水壓縮餘量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Gasket compression reserve”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b110-v14-21-k1","title":"接頭壓縮與水密包絡","titleEn":"Joint compression and sealing envelope","text":"大林組記載接合與防水措施，本課以假想接縫研究幾何容許與實際水密試驗的差別。止水條依受控壓縮維持連續接觸，接縫轉角、錯台、污染與材料鬆弛都會降低最不利點的接觸能力。","textEn":"Using documented connection and waterproofing context, a hypothetical joint distinguishes geometric allowance from actual pressure-test performance. A gasket seals through controlled continuous compression; rotation, offset, contamination and relaxation reduce contact at the weakest point.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b110-v14-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：接縫平均寬度合格就不必量測局部錯台及扭轉。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: An acceptable average joint width makes local offset and twist measurements unnecessary. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「接頭壓縮與水密包絡」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Joint compression and sealing envelope\" is correct?","options":["大林組記載接合與防水措施，本課以假想接縫研究幾何容許與實際水密試驗的差別。","接縫平均寬度合格就不必量測局部錯台及扭轉。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Using documented connection and waterproofing context, a hypothetical joint distinguishes geometric allowance from actual pressure-test performance.","An acceptable average joint width makes local offset and twist measurements unnecessary.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error."],"answer":0,"explanation":"大林組記載接合與防水措施，本課以假想接縫研究幾何容許與實際水密試驗的差別。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Using documented connection and waterproofing context, a hypothetical joint distinguishes geometric allowance from actual pressure-test performance. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b110-v14-22","title":"接頭壓縮與水密包絡：定量估算","titleEn":"Joint compression and sealing envelope: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b110-v14-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「止水壓縮餘量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Gasket compression reserve” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：初始壓縮=19 mm；張開量=4 mm；幾何公差=2 mm。c_res=c0−opening−tolerance=13 mm。僅把張開量增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為12.6 mm。邊界：單向幾何餘量，不是接觸壓或水密合格證明；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: initial compression=19 mm; opening=4 mm; tolerance=2 mm. c_res=c0−opening−tolerance=13 mm. Increasing only opening by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 12.6 mm. Boundary: One-direction geometric reserve, not contact pressure or proof of watertightness. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將錯台、張開和水壓組合試驗與現場幾何配對。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Match combined offset, opening and pressure tests with field geometry.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b110-v14-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：初始壓縮=19 mm；張開量=4 mm；幾何公差=2 mm。c_res=c0−opening−tolerance=13 mm。僅把張開量增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為12.6 mm。邊界：單向幾何餘量，不是接觸壓或水密合格證明；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: initial compression=19 mm; opening=4 mm; tolerance=2 mm. c_res=c0−opening−tolerance=13 mm. Increasing only opening by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 12.6 mm. Boundary: One-direction geometric reserve, not contact pressure or proof of watertightness. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b110-v14-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「接頭壓縮與水密包絡」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Joint compression and sealing envelope\", which statement holds?","options":["風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。","原創教學假設：初始壓縮=19 mm；張開量=4 mm；幾何公差=2 mm。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.","Original teaching assumptions: initial compression=19 mm; opening=4 mm; tolerance=2 mm. c_res=c0−opening−tolerance=13 mm.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：初始壓縮=19 mm；張開量=4 mm；幾何公差=2 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: initial compression=19 mm; opening=4 mm; tolerance=2 mm. c_res=c0−opening−tolerance=13 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b110-v14-23","title":"接頭壓縮與水密包絡：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Joint compression and sealing envelope: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b110-v14-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「止水壓縮餘量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Gasket compression reserve” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將錯台、張開和水壓組合試驗與現場幾何配對。全尺寸接頭試驗分別改變張開、錯台與外水壓，記錄漏水起點與卸載後殘餘位移，對照材料批次及溫度。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Match combined offset, opening and pressure tests with field geometry. Vary opening, offset and pressure in full-size joint tests, recording leakage onset and residual movement against material batch and temperature. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「止水壓縮餘量」的交付需回答：將錯台、張開和水壓組合試驗與現場幾何配對。保存接縫幾何與試驗壓力的配對紀錄，由設計者核定允收包絡；驗收時不能把課堂的幾何餘量當產品認證數字。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Tokyo Bay Aqua-Line tunnel, the gasket compression reserve handover must address the following evidence: Match combined offset, opening and pressure tests with field geometry. Retain paired joint geometry and test pressure, with the designer approving the acceptance envelope; classroom geometric reserves are not product certification values.","failure":"注意干擾：只查止水材料證明未必涵蓋現場接合位移組合。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Material certification alone may not cover the installed displacement combination. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b110-v14-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將錯台、張開和水壓組合試驗與現場幾何配對。全尺寸接頭試驗分別改變張開、錯台與外水壓，記錄漏水起點與卸載後殘餘位移，對照材料批次及溫度。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Match combined offset, opening and pressure tests with field geometry. Vary opening, offset and pressure in full-size joint tests, recording leakage onset and residual movement against material batch and temperature. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b110-v14-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「止水壓縮餘量」的交付需回答：將錯台、張開和水壓組合試驗與現場幾何配對。保存接縫幾何與試驗壓力的配對紀錄，由設計者核定允收包絡；驗收時不能把課堂的幾何餘量當產品認證數字。","textEn":"For Tokyo Bay Aqua-Line tunnel, the gasket compression reserve handover must address the following evidence: Match combined offset, opening and pressure tests with field geometry. Retain paired joint geometry and test pressure, with the designer approving the acceptance envelope; classroom geometric reserves are not product certification values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「接頭壓縮與水密包絡」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Joint compression and sealing envelope\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。","將錯台、張開和水壓組合試驗與現場幾何配對。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance.","Match combined offset, opening and pressure tests with field geometry."],"answer":2,"explanation":"將錯台、張開和水壓組合試驗與現場幾何配對。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Match combined offset, opening and pressure tests with field geometry. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b110-v14-24","title":"接頭壓縮與水密包絡：失效診斷","titleEn":"Joint compression and sealing envelope: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b110-v14-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「止水壓縮餘量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Gasket compression reserve” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只查止水材料證明未必涵蓋現場接合位移組合。扭曲或沾污的止水條可形成旁通通道，即使平均縫寬合格仍可能漏水；盲目灌漿也可能只轉移出水位置。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Material certification alone may not cover the installed displacement combination. A twisted or contaminated gasket creates bypass leakage despite acceptable mean width; indiscriminate grouting may merely move the outlet. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：平均壓縮量不能掩蓋局部脫離；全尺寸試驗的結果只對測試過的幾何、水壓及荷載歷程有效，幾何餘量本身並不是接觸壓力。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Full-size test results apply only to their tested geometry, head and load history, while a calculated geometric reserve is neither contact pressure nor evidence of watertightness.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「接縫平均寬度合格就不必量測局部錯台及扭轉。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"An acceptable average joint width makes local offset and twist measurements unnecessary.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b110-v14-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只查止水材料證明未必涵蓋現場接合位移組合。扭曲或沾污的止水條可形成旁通通道，即使平均縫寬合格仍可能漏水；盲目灌漿也可能只轉移出水位置。","textEn":"Material certification alone may not cover the installed displacement combination. A twisted or contaminated gasket creates bypass leakage despite acceptable mean width; indiscriminate grouting may merely move the outlet.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b110-v14-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「接頭壓縮與水密包絡」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Joint compression and sealing envelope\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["只查止水材料證明未必涵蓋現場接合位移組合。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Material certification alone may not cover the installed displacement combination.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error."],"answer":0,"explanation":"只查止水材料證明未必涵蓋現場接合位移組合。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Material certification alone may not cover the installed displacement combination. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b110-v14-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「控制網與貫通誤差」與「基床變形與接頭轉角」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Control network and breakthrough error\" and \"Bedding movement and joint rotation\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b110-v14-25","title":"控制網與貫通誤差：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b110-v14-24"],"objective":"說明「方向角誤差」如何影響東京灣跨海公路隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Orientation error” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Tokyo Bay Aqua-Line tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"從不同人工島相向掘進的控制網需獨立覆核，研究水下接合前方向和高程不確定性。長隧道的微小方向誤差會沿距離累積，地下控制網又缺少直接衛星定位，必須把地表基準可靠傳到洞內。閉合差很小不代表無系統誤差；尺度、折光、儀器定向與高程基準可能共同偏移，誤差相關性也使平方和估算失真。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「方向角誤差」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Opposing drives from separate islands need independent control checks before underwater connection, including direction and height uncertainty. Small orientation errors accumulate over long drives, while underground networks lack direct satellite positioning and depend on transferring surface control. A small closure does not exclude systematic bias: scale, refraction, orientation and vertical datum may shift together. Correlated errors also invalidate a naive root-sum-square combination of supposedly independent observations. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Orientation error” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：控制長度=4080 m；方向偏角=2.6 arcsec。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: control length=4080 m; orientation error=2.6 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.051429 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「方向角誤差」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Orientation error”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b110-v14-25-k1","title":"控制網與貫通誤差","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error","text":"從不同人工島相向掘進的控制網需獨立覆核，研究水下接合前方向和高程不確定性。長隧道的微小方向誤差會沿距離累積，地下控制網又缺少直接衛星定位，必須把地表基準可靠傳到洞內。","textEn":"Opposing drives from separate islands need independent control checks before underwater connection, including direction and height uncertainty. Small orientation errors accumulate over long drives, while underground networks lack direct satellite positioning and depend on transferring surface control.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b110-v14-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「控制網與貫通誤差」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Control network and breakthrough error\" is correct?","options":["兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。","從不同人工島相向掘進的控制網需獨立覆核，研究水下接合前方向和高程不確定性。","各管節平均高程接近就能排除接頭差異變形。"],"optionsEn":["Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.","Opposing drives from separate islands need independent control checks before underwater connection, including direction and height uncertainty.","Similar mean element elevations exclude differential movement at joints."],"answer":1,"explanation":"從不同人工島相向掘進的控制網需獨立覆核，研究水下接合前方向和高程不確定性。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Opposing drives from separate islands need independent control checks before underwater connection, including direction and height uncertainty. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b110-v14-26","title":"控制網與貫通誤差：定量估算","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b110-v14-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「方向角誤差」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Orientation error” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：控制長度=4080 m；方向偏角=2.6 arcsec。e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.051429 m。僅把方向偏角增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.0565719 m。邊界：小角度方向偏差，未加入控制網相關性及折光；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: control length=4080 m; orientation error=2.6 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.051429 m. Increasing only orientation error by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.0565719 m. Boundary: Small-angle orientation error without network correlation or refraction. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以原始角距重算兩端網絡，交叉核對獨立接合探測。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Recompute both networks from raw observations and cross-check independent connection surveys.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b110-v14-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：控制長度=4080 m；方向偏角=2.6 arcsec。e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.051429 m。僅把方向偏角增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.0565719 m。邊界：小角度方向偏差，未加入控制網相關性及折光；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: control length=4080 m; orientation error=2.6 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.051429 m. Increasing only orientation error by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.0565719 m. Boundary: Small-angle orientation error without network correlation or refraction. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b110-v14-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「控制網與貫通誤差」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Control network and breakthrough error\", which statement holds?","options":["擴散長度就是鋼筋開始腐蝕的位置和精確時間。","目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。","原創教學假設：控制長度=4080 m；方向偏角=2.6 arcsec。"],"optionsEn":["Diffusion length gives the exact location and time of corrosion initiation.","No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.","Original teaching assumptions: control length=4080 m; orientation error=2.6 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.051429 m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：控制長度=4080 m；方向偏角=2.6 arcsec。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: control length=4080 m; orientation error=2.6 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.051429 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b110-v14-27","title":"控制網與貫通誤差：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b110-v14-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「方向角誤差」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Orientation error” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以原始角距重算兩端網絡，交叉核對獨立接合探測。由獨立測量組複核地表到洞內的轉換，保留原始角距及溫度資料，用不同控制線比較方向與高程偏差。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Recompute both networks from raw observations and cross-check independent connection surveys. Independently check surface-to-tunnel transformations, retain raw angles, distances and temperatures, and compare orientation and elevation through separate control routes. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「方向角誤差」的交付需回答：以原始角距重算兩端網絡，交叉核對獨立接合探測。貫通前凍結座標、尺度與高程版本，獨立組直接使用原始觀測重算；不得只傳遞整理好的坐標而遺失校正資訊。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Tokyo Bay Aqua-Line tunnel, the orientation error handover must address the following evidence: Recompute both networks from raw observations and cross-check independent connection surveys. Freeze coordinate, scale and height revisions before breakthrough; independent reviewers recompute raw observations rather than receiving only adjusted coordinates without corrections.","failure":"注意干擾：兩端共用尺度錯誤可能在長距離累積而未被局部閉合發現。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Shared scale error accumulates over long drives without appearing in local closure. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b110-v14-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以原始角距重算兩端網絡，交叉核對獨立接合探測。由獨立測量組複核地表到洞內的轉換，保留原始角距及溫度資料，用不同控制線比較方向與高程偏差。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Recompute both networks from raw observations and cross-check independent connection surveys. Independently check surface-to-tunnel transformations, retain raw angles, distances and temperatures, and compare orientation and elevation through separate control routes. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b110-v14-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「方向角誤差」的交付需回答：以原始角距重算兩端網絡，交叉核對獨立接合探測。貫通前凍結座標、尺度與高程版本，獨立組直接使用原始觀測重算；不得只傳遞整理好的坐標而遺失校正資訊。","textEn":"For Tokyo Bay Aqua-Line tunnel, the orientation error handover must address the following evidence: Recompute both networks from raw observations and cross-check independent connection surveys. Freeze coordinate, scale and height revisions before breakthrough; independent reviewers recompute raw observations rather than receiving only adjusted coordinates without corrections.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「控制網與貫通誤差」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Control network and breakthrough error\"?","options":["以原始角距重算兩端網絡，交叉核對獨立接合探測。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","灌入體積等於理論空隙就能證明襯砌背後全部填滿。"],"optionsEn":["Recompute both networks from raw observations and cross-check independent connection surveys.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Injected volume equal to the theoretical annulus proves complete filling behind the lining."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以原始角距重算兩端網絡，交叉核對獨立接合探測。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Recompute both networks from raw observations and cross-check independent connection surveys. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b110-v14-28","title":"控制網與貫通誤差：失效診斷","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b110-v14-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「方向角誤差」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Orientation error” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"兩端共用尺度錯誤可能在長距離累積而未被局部閉合發現。共用錯誤基準可能讓兩組測量同時看似一致，直到貫通或軌道銜接才發現系統偏差，修正成本遠高於早期複核。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Shared scale error accumulates over long drives without appearing in local closure. A shared wrong datum can make separate surveys appear consistent until breakthrough or track connection exposes bias that is costly to correct. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：閉合差很小不代表無系統誤差；尺度、折光、儀器定向與高程基準可能共同偏移，誤差相關性也使平方和估算失真。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Correlated errors also invalidate a naive root-sum-square combination of supposedly independent observations.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b110-v14-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"兩端共用尺度錯誤可能在長距離累積而未被局部閉合發現。共用錯誤基準可能讓兩組測量同時看似一致，直到貫通或軌道銜接才發現系統偏差，修正成本遠高於早期複核。","textEn":"Shared scale error accumulates over long drives without appearing in local closure. A shared wrong datum can make separate surveys appear consistent until breakthrough or track connection exposes bias that is costly to correct.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b110-v14-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「控制網與貫通誤差」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Control network and breakthrough error\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","兩端共用尺度錯誤可能在長距離累積而未被局部閉合發現。","各管節平均高程接近就能排除接頭差異變形。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Shared scale error accumulates over long drives without appearing in local closure.","Similar mean element elevations exclude differential movement at joints."],"answer":1,"explanation":"兩端共用尺度錯誤可能在長距離累積而未被局部閉合發現。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Shared scale error accumulates over long drives without appearing in local closure. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b110-v14-29","title":"基床變形與接頭轉角：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Bedding movement and joint rotation: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b110-v14-28"],"objective":"說明「差異沉陷梯度」如何影響東京灣跨海公路隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Differential settlement gradient” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Tokyo Bay Aqua-Line tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"人工島填築地盤與海底孔連接形成差異沉陷課題，研究工後固結如何傳到柔性接合。沉管基床將箱體荷載傳給海床，局部沖刷、回填不均與軟弱層固結會改變接觸分布。總沉陷小不代表接頭轉角小；相鄰管節的差異位移和支承長度才控制局部變形，施工量測須保留時間與潮位基準。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「差異沉陷梯度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Reclaimed island ground creates differential settlement at the tunnel connection; examine how postconstruction consolidation reaches flexible interfaces. The bed transfers tube load into the seabed, and scour, uneven backfill or consolidation alter contact. Small total settlement does not imply small joint rotation; differential movement and support length control local distortion. Construction observations must preserve time and tidal datum because immediate placement and delayed consolidation describe different mechanisms. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Differential settlement gradient” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：差異沉陷=5 mm；基線長度=170 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: differential settlement=5 mm; baseline=170 m. β=Δs/L=0.0294118 mm/m.","failure":"常見誤解：「各管節平均高程接近就能排除接頭差異變形。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Similar mean element elevations exclude differential movement at joints.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「差異沉陷梯度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Differential settlement gradient”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b110-v14-29-k1","title":"基床變形與接頭轉角","titleEn":"Bedding movement and joint rotation","text":"人工島填築地盤與海底孔連接形成差異沉陷課題，研究工後固結如何傳到柔性接合。沉管基床將箱體荷載傳給海床，局部沖刷、回填不均與軟弱層固結會改變接觸分布。","textEn":"Reclaimed island ground creates differential settlement at the tunnel connection; examine how postconstruction consolidation reaches flexible interfaces. The bed transfers tube load into the seabed, and scour, uneven backfill or consolidation alter contact.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b110-v14-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：各管節平均高程接近就能排除接頭差異變形。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Similar mean element elevations exclude differential movement at joints. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「基床變形與接頭轉角」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Bedding movement and joint rotation\" is correct?","options":["各管節平均高程接近就能排除接頭差異變形。","風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。","人工島填築地盤與海底孔連接形成差異沉陷課題，研究工後固結如何傳到柔性接合。"],"optionsEn":["Similar mean element elevations exclude differential movement at joints.","Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.","Reclaimed island ground creates differential settlement at the tunnel connection; examine how postconstruction consolidation reaches flexible interfaces."],"answer":2,"explanation":"人工島填築地盤與海底孔連接形成差異沉陷課題，研究工後固結如何傳到柔性接合。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Reclaimed island ground creates differential settlement at the tunnel connection; examine how postconstruction consolidation reaches flexible interfaces. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b110-v14-30","title":"基床變形與接頭轉角：定量估算","titleEn":"Bedding movement and joint rotation: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b110-v14-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「差異沉陷梯度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Differential settlement gradient” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：差異沉陷=5 mm；基線長度=170 m。β=Δs/L=0.0294118 mm/m。僅把差異沉陷增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.0323529 mm/m。邊界：小變形角變化指標，不是完整固結解；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: differential settlement=5 mm; baseline=170 m. β=Δs/L=0.0294118 mm/m. Increasing only differential settlement by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.0323529 mm/m. Boundary: Small-deformation angular-distortion indicator, not a consolidation solution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將島體沉陷、孔壓及接頭轉角按同一時序比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare island settlement, pore pressure and joint rotation on one timeline.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b110-v14-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：差異沉陷=5 mm；基線長度=170 m。β=Δs/L=0.0294118 mm/m。僅把差異沉陷增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.0323529 mm/m。邊界：小變形角變化指標，不是完整固結解；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: differential settlement=5 mm; baseline=170 m. β=Δs/L=0.0294118 mm/m. Increasing only differential settlement by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.0323529 mm/m. Boundary: Small-deformation angular-distortion indicator, not a consolidation solution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b110-v14-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「基床變形與接頭轉角」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Bedding movement and joint rotation\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：差異沉陷=5 mm；基線長度=170 m。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。","刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: differential settlement=5 mm; baseline=170 m. β=Δs/L=0.0294118 mm/m.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.","A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：差異沉陷=5 mm；基線長度=170 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: differential settlement=5 mm; baseline=170 m. β=Δs/L=0.0294118 mm/m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b110-v14-31","title":"基床變形與接頭轉角：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Bedding movement and joint rotation: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b110-v14-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「差異沉陷梯度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Differential settlement gradient” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將島體沉陷、孔壓及接頭轉角按同一時序比較。用管節水準網、海床剖面及孔壓變化交叉核對，將整體下沉與相鄰節轉角分開評估。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare island settlement, pore pressure and joint rotation on one timeline. Cross-check tube levelling, seabed profiles and pore-pressure change, separating overall settlement from rotation between neighbouring elements. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「差異沉陷梯度」的交付需回答：將島體沉陷、孔壓及接頭轉角按同一時序比較。將基床施工紀錄與長期水準資料連結至管節編號，差異變形先查基準和孔壓，再由設計者判斷接觸及接頭。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Tokyo Bay Aqua-Line tunnel, the differential settlement gradient handover must address the following evidence: Compare island settlement, pore pressure and joint rotation on one timeline. Link bedding records and long-term levelling to element identifiers; check datum and pore pressure before designers interpret contact and joint behaviour.","failure":"注意干擾：只追蹤隧道中心高程會漏掉島體一側持續下沉。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Tunnel-centre elevation alone misses continuing settlement on the island side. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b110-v14-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將島體沉陷、孔壓及接頭轉角按同一時序比較。用管節水準網、海床剖面及孔壓變化交叉核對，將整體下沉與相鄰節轉角分開評估。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Compare island settlement, pore pressure and joint rotation on one timeline. Cross-check tube levelling, seabed profiles and pore-pressure change, separating overall settlement from rotation between neighbouring elements. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b110-v14-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「差異沉陷梯度」的交付需回答：將島體沉陷、孔壓及接頭轉角按同一時序比較。將基床施工紀錄與長期水準資料連結至管節編號，差異變形先查基準和孔壓，再由設計者判斷接觸及接頭。","textEn":"For Tokyo Bay Aqua-Line tunnel, the differential settlement gradient handover must address the following evidence: Compare island settlement, pore pressure and joint rotation on one timeline. Link bedding records and long-term levelling to element identifiers; check datum and pore pressure before designers interpret contact and joint behaviour.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「基床變形與接頭轉角」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Bedding movement and joint rotation\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","將島體沉陷、孔壓及接頭轉角按同一時序比較。","混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Compare island settlement, pore pressure and joint rotation on one timeline.","Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure."],"answer":1,"explanation":"將島體沉陷、孔壓及接頭轉角按同一時序比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare island settlement, pore pressure and joint rotation on one timeline. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b110-v14-32","title":"基床變形與接頭轉角：失效診斷","titleEn":"Bedding movement and joint rotation: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b110-v14-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「差異沉陷梯度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Differential settlement gradient” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只追蹤隧道中心高程會漏掉島體一側持續下沉。只追蹤平均高程可能漏掉單側失去支承，接頭剪力與止水錯台會先於明顯整體下沉增加。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Tunnel-centre elevation alone misses continuing settlement on the island side. Mean elevation can conceal loss of support on one side, allowing joint shear and gasket offset to grow before obvious overall settlement. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：總沉陷小不代表接頭轉角小；相鄰管節的差異位移和支承長度才控制局部變形，施工量測須保留時間與潮位基準。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Construction observations must preserve time and tidal datum because immediate placement and delayed consolidation describe different mechanisms.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「各管節平均高程接近就能排除接頭差異變形。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Similar mean element elevations exclude differential movement at joints.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b110-v14-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只追蹤隧道中心高程會漏掉島體一側持續下沉。只追蹤平均高程可能漏掉單側失去支承，接頭剪力與止水錯台會先於明顯整體下沉增加。","textEn":"Tunnel-centre elevation alone misses continuing settlement on the island side. Mean elevation can conceal loss of support on one side, allowing joint shear and gasket offset to grow before obvious overall settlement.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b110-v14-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「基床變形與接頭轉角」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Bedding movement and joint rotation\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。","只追蹤隧道中心高程會漏掉島體一側持續下沉。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.","Tunnel-centre elevation alone misses continuing settlement on the island side."],"answer":2,"explanation":"只追蹤隧道中心高程會漏掉島體一側持續下沉。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Tunnel-centre elevation alone misses continuing settlement on the island side. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b110-v14-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「通風網路與壓力損失」與「氯鹽遷移與耐久判讀」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Ventilation network and pressure loss\" and \"Chloride transport and durability interpretation\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b110-v14-33","title":"通風網路與壓力損失：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Ventilation network and pressure loss: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b110-v14-32"],"objective":"說明「風道摩擦壓損」如何影響東京灣跨海公路隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Duct friction loss” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Tokyo Bay Aqua-Line tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"海上通風設施與隧道內阻力構成共同網路，研究外風改變時風機工況點的移動。風機提供壓差，實際風量由風道摩阻、局部損失、外風與其他風機共同決定。支路開關會重新分配整個網路，不能把額定風量直接加總；正常污染稀釋與火災控煙也有不同目標，需要分別建立受控邊界和故障情境。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「風道摩擦壓損」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Offshore ventilation structures and tunnel resistance form one network; examine operating-point changes under external wind. Fans supply pressure, but actual flow follows friction, local losses, external wind and interactions with other fans. Switching a branch redistributes the network rather than simply adding rated flows. Routine dilution and fire smoke control have different objectives, so each needs explicit boundaries, operating states and failure cases rather than one universal flow target. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Duct friction loss” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：達西因子=0.025 無因次；風道長度=860 m；水力直徑=4 m；空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；平均風速=3.8 m/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.025 dimensionless; duct length=860 m; hydraulic diameter=4 m; air density=1.2 kg/m³; mean velocity=3.8 m/s. Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=46.569 Pa.","failure":"常見誤解：「風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「風道摩擦壓損」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Duct friction loss”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b110-v14-33-k1","title":"通風網路與壓力損失","titleEn":"Ventilation network and pressure loss","text":"海上通風設施與隧道內阻力構成共同網路，研究外風改變時風機工況點的移動。風機提供壓差，實際風量由風道摩阻、局部損失、外風與其他風機共同決定。","textEn":"Offshore ventilation structures and tunnel resistance form one network; examine operating-point changes under external wind. Fans supply pressure, but actual flow follows friction, local losses, external wind and interactions with other fans.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b110-v14-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「通風網路與壓力損失」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Ventilation network and pressure loss\" is correct?","options":["海上通風設施與隧道內阻力構成共同網路，研究外風改變時風機工況點的移動。","風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。","擴散長度就是鋼筋開始腐蝕的位置和精確時間。"],"optionsEn":["Offshore ventilation structures and tunnel resistance form one network; examine operating-point changes under external wind.","Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.","Diffusion length gives the exact location and time of corrosion initiation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"海上通風設施與隧道內阻力構成共同網路，研究外風改變時風機工況點的移動。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Offshore ventilation structures and tunnel resistance form one network; examine operating-point changes under external wind. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b110-v14-34","title":"通風網路與壓力損失：定量估算","titleEn":"Ventilation network and pressure loss: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b110-v14-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「風道摩擦壓損」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Duct friction loss” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：達西因子=0.025 無因次；風道長度=860 m；水力直徑=4 m；空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；平均風速=3.8 m/s。Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=46.569 Pa。僅把平均風速增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為56.3485 Pa。邊界：定密度直管摩阻，局部損失及外風另計；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.025 dimensionless; duct length=860 m; hydraulic diameter=4 m; air density=1.2 kg/m³; mean velocity=3.8 m/s. Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=46.569 Pa. Increasing only mean velocity by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 56.3485 Pa. Boundary: Constant-density straight-duct friction; local loss and external wind are separate. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同步記錄外風、風機狀態與孔內壓差。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Synchronise external wind, fan state and tunnel pressure difference.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b110-v14-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：達西因子=0.025 無因次；風道長度=860 m；水力直徑=4 m；空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；平均風速=3.8 m/s。Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=46.569 Pa。僅把平均風速增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為56.3485 Pa。邊界：定密度直管摩阻，局部損失及外風另計；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.025 dimensionless; duct length=860 m; hydraulic diameter=4 m; air density=1.2 kg/m³; mean velocity=3.8 m/s. Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=46.569 Pa. Increasing only mean velocity by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 56.3485 Pa. Boundary: Constant-density straight-duct friction; local loss and external wind are separate. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b110-v14-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「通風網路與壓力損失」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Ventilation network and pressure loss\", which statement holds?","options":["目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。","原創教學假設：達西因子=0.025 無因次；風道長度=860 m；水力直徑=4 m；空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；平均風速=3.8 m/s。","灌入體積等於理論空隙就能證明襯砌背後全部填滿。"],"optionsEn":["No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.","Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.025 dimensionless.","Injected volume equal to the theoretical annulus proves complete filling behind the lining."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：達西因子=0.025 無因次；風道長度=860 m；水力直徑=4 m；空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；平均風速=3.8 m/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.025 dimensionless; duct length=860 m; hydraulic diameter=4 m; air density=1.2 kg/m³; mean velocity=3.8 m/s. Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=46.569 Pa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b110-v14-35","title":"通風網路與壓力損失：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Ventilation network and pressure loss: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b110-v14-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「風道摩擦壓損」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Duct friction loss” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同步記錄外風、風機狀態與孔內壓差。沿線同步量測靜壓與風速，記錄風門及其他風機狀態，再把實測工作點和風機曲線、網路壓損比較。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Synchronise external wind, fan state and tunnel pressure difference. Measure pressure and velocity synchronously, record dampers and other fans, and compare the measured duty point with fan curves and network resistance. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「風道摩擦壓損」的交付需回答：同步記錄外風、風機狀態與孔內壓差。驗收採明確風門和車流邊界，維修改線後重新核對網路工作點，火災模式由防災責任工程師簽認而非沿用正常模式。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Tokyo Bay Aqua-Line tunnel, the duct friction loss handover must address the following evidence: Synchronise external wind, fan state and tunnel pressure difference. Commission with specified damper and traffic boundaries, recheck duty points after rerouting, and have the fire-safety engineer approve emergency modes independently.","failure":"注意干擾：風量下降若只歸於風機老化會漏掉外風邊界改變。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Attributing reduced flow only to ageing fans misses changed external-wind boundaries. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b110-v14-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同步記錄外風、風機狀態與孔內壓差。沿線同步量測靜壓與風速，記錄風門及其他風機狀態，再把實測工作點和風機曲線、網路壓損比較。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Synchronise external wind, fan state and tunnel pressure difference. Measure pressure and velocity synchronously, record dampers and other fans, and compare the measured duty point with fan curves and network resistance. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b110-v14-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「風道摩擦壓損」的交付需回答：同步記錄外風、風機狀態與孔內壓差。驗收採明確風門和車流邊界，維修改線後重新核對網路工作點，火災模式由防災責任工程師簽認而非沿用正常模式。","textEn":"For Tokyo Bay Aqua-Line tunnel, the duct friction loss handover must address the following evidence: Synchronise external wind, fan state and tunnel pressure difference. Commission with specified damper and traffic boundaries, recheck duty points after rerouting, and have the fire-safety engineer approve emergency modes independently.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「通風網路與壓力損失」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Ventilation network and pressure loss\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","接縫平均寬度合格就不必量測局部錯台及扭轉。","同步記錄外風、風機狀態與孔內壓差。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","An acceptable average joint width makes local offset and twist measurements unnecessary.","Synchronise external wind, fan state and tunnel pressure difference."],"answer":2,"explanation":"同步記錄外風、風機狀態與孔內壓差。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Synchronise external wind, fan state and tunnel pressure difference. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b110-v14-36","title":"通風網路與壓力損失：失效診斷","titleEn":"Ventilation network and pressure loss: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b110-v14-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「風道摩擦壓損」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Duct friction loss” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"風量下降若只歸於風機老化會漏掉外風邊界改變。只看風機轉速會漏掉風門誤位或短路漏風，可能在總耗電增加時，真正需要的區段反而風量不足。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Attributing reduced flow only to ageing fans misses changed external-wind boundaries. Fan speed alone misses a misplaced damper or leakage shortcut; total power may rise while the critical section receives less air. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：支路開關會重新分配整個網路，不能把額定風量直接加總；正常污染稀釋與火災控煙也有不同目標，需要分別建立受控邊界和故障情境。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Routine dilution and fire smoke control have different objectives, so each needs explicit boundaries, operating states and failure cases rather than one universal flow target.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b110-v14-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"風量下降若只歸於風機老化會漏掉外風邊界改變。只看風機轉速會漏掉風門誤位或短路漏風，可能在總耗電增加時，真正需要的區段反而風量不足。","textEn":"Attributing reduced flow only to ageing fans misses changed external-wind boundaries. Fan speed alone misses a misplaced damper or leakage shortcut; total power may rise while the critical section receives less air.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b110-v14-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「通風網路與壓力損失」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Ventilation network and pressure loss\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["風量下降若只歸於風機老化會漏掉外風邊界改變。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","擴散長度就是鋼筋開始腐蝕的位置和精確時間。"],"optionsEn":["Attributing reduced flow only to ageing fans misses changed external-wind boundaries.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Diffusion length gives the exact location and time of corrosion initiation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"風量下降若只歸於風機老化會漏掉外風邊界改變。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Attributing reduced flow only to ageing fans misses changed external-wind boundaries. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b110-v14-37","title":"氯鹽遷移與耐久判讀：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Chloride transport and durability interpretation: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b110-v14-36"],"objective":"說明「擴散特徵長度」如何影響東京灣跨海公路隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Diffusion characteristic length” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Tokyo Bay Aqua-Line tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"海上人工島與孔內環片暴露環境不同，Aqua-Line耐久教學分開鹽霧、海水與乾燥設備區。海水或除冰鹽可提供氯離子，材料孔隙與裂縫控制其傳輸；鋼筋腐蝕還需要局部電化學條件。平方根擴散長度僅顯示時間尺度，並不是腐蝕門檻深度；表面濃度變化、乾濕循環、結合效應及施工裂縫須另行辨識。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「擴散特徵長度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Separate salt spray, seawater and dry equipment zones because artificial islands and tunnel segments have different exposure environments. Seawater or deicing salt supplies chloride, while pores and cracks govern transport; reinforcement corrosion also depends on local electrochemical conditions. A square-root diffusion length indicates a time scale, not a corrosion-threshold depth. Surface concentration, wetting cycles, binding and construction cracks must be distinguished rather than hidden in one fitted diffusivity. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Diffusion characteristic length” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：擴散係數=2e-12 m²/s；暴露時間=19 year。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: diffusivity=2e-12 m²/s; exposure=19 year. ℓ=√(Dt); 1 year=365.25×86400 s; m→mm ×1000=34.6293 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「擴散長度就是鋼筋開始腐蝕的位置和精確時間。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Diffusion length gives the exact location and time of corrosion initiation.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「擴散特徵長度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Diffusion characteristic length”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b110-v14-37-k1","title":"氯鹽遷移與耐久判讀","titleEn":"Chloride transport and durability interpretation","text":"海上人工島與孔內環片暴露環境不同，Aqua-Line耐久教學分開鹽霧、海水與乾燥設備區。海水或除冰鹽可提供氯離子，材料孔隙與裂縫控制其傳輸；鋼筋腐蝕還需要局部電化學條件。","textEn":"Separate salt spray, seawater and dry equipment zones because artificial islands and tunnel segments have different exposure environments. Seawater or deicing salt supplies chloride, while pores and cracks govern transport; reinforcement corrosion also depends on local electrochemical conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b110-v14-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：擴散長度就是鋼筋開始腐蝕的位置和精確時間。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Diffusion length gives the exact location and time of corrosion initiation. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「氯鹽遷移與耐久判讀」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Chloride transport and durability interpretation\" is correct?","options":["擴散長度就是鋼筋開始腐蝕的位置和精確時間。","海上人工島與孔內環片暴露環境不同，Aqua-Line耐久教學分開鹽霧、海水與乾燥設備區。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Diffusion length gives the exact location and time of corrosion initiation.","Separate salt spray, seawater and dry equipment zones because artificial islands and tunnel segments have different exposure environments.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":1,"explanation":"海上人工島與孔內環片暴露環境不同，Aqua-Line耐久教學分開鹽霧、海水與乾燥設備區。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Separate salt spray, seawater and dry equipment zones because artificial islands and tunnel segments have different exposure environments. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b110-v14-38","title":"氯鹽遷移與耐久判讀：定量估算","titleEn":"Chloride transport and durability interpretation: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b110-v14-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「擴散特徵長度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Diffusion characteristic length” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：擴散係數=2e-12 m²/s；暴露時間=19 year。ℓ=√(Dt); 1 year=365.25×86400 s; m→mm ×1000=34.6293 mm。僅把暴露時間增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為36.3195 mm。邊界：特徵長度，不是腐蝕起始壽命或氯鹽門檻深度；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: diffusivity=2e-12 m²/s; exposure=19 year. ℓ=√(Dt); 1 year=365.25×86400 s; m→mm ×1000=34.6293 mm. Increasing only exposure by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 36.3195 mm. Boundary: Characteristic length, not corrosion-initiation life or chloride-threshold depth. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：按暴露區取樣，核對材料、裂縫及保護層深度。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Sample by exposure zone and check material, cracking and cover depth.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b110-v14-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：擴散係數=2e-12 m²/s；暴露時間=19 year。ℓ=√(Dt); 1 year=365.25×86400 s; m→mm ×1000=34.6293 mm。僅把暴露時間增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為36.3195 mm。邊界：特徵長度，不是腐蝕起始壽命或氯鹽門檻深度；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: diffusivity=2e-12 m²/s; exposure=19 year. ℓ=√(Dt); 1 year=365.25×86400 s; m→mm ×1000=34.6293 mm. Increasing only exposure by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 36.3195 mm. Boundary: Characteristic length, not corrosion-initiation life or chloride-threshold depth. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b110-v14-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「氯鹽遷移與耐久判讀」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Chloride transport and durability interpretation\", which statement holds?","options":["刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。","混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。","原創教學假設：擴散係數=2e-12 m²/s；暴露時間=19 year。"],"optionsEn":["A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance.","Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure.","Original teaching assumptions: diffusivity=2e-12 m²/s; exposure=19 year. ℓ=√(Dt); 1 year=365.25×86400 s; m→mm ×1000=34.6293 mm."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：擴散係數=2e-12 m²/s；暴露時間=19 year。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: diffusivity=2e-12 m²/s; exposure=19 year. ℓ=√(Dt); 1 year=365.25×86400 s; m→mm ×1000=34.6293 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b110-v14-39","title":"氯鹽遷移與耐久判讀：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Chloride transport and durability interpretation: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b110-v14-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「擴散特徵長度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Diffusion characteristic length” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"按暴露區取樣，核對材料、裂縫及保護層深度。以分層取樣的氯鹽剖面配合裂縫圖與電位量測，檢查擴散模型是否只適用未開裂材料。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Sample by exposure zone and check material, cracking and cover depth. Combine depth-resolved chloride samples with crack maps and potential measurements, checking whether the diffusion model applies only to uncracked material. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「擴散特徵長度」的交付需回答：按暴露區取樣，核對材料、裂縫及保護層深度。保留取樣深度、含水狀態及材料批次，用多種證據解釋劣化；維修優先序依構件功能與實際病害制定。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Tokyo Bay Aqua-Line tunnel, the diffusion characteristic length handover must address the following evidence: Sample by exposure zone and check material, cracking and cover depth. Retain sample depth, moisture and material batches and interpret deterioration using multiple evidence types; prioritise repairs by function and observed defects.","failure":"注意干擾：混合取樣平均值會掩蓋高鹽濕區的局部劣化。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A mixed-sample average conceals local deterioration in wet saline zones. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b110-v14-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"按暴露區取樣，核對材料、裂縫及保護層深度。以分層取樣的氯鹽剖面配合裂縫圖與電位量測，檢查擴散模型是否只適用未開裂材料。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Sample by exposure zone and check material, cracking and cover depth. Combine depth-resolved chloride samples with crack maps and potential measurements, checking whether the diffusion model applies only to uncracked material. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b110-v14-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「擴散特徵長度」的交付需回答：按暴露區取樣，核對材料、裂縫及保護層深度。保留取樣深度、含水狀態及材料批次，用多種證據解釋劣化；維修優先序依構件功能與實際病害制定。","textEn":"For Tokyo Bay Aqua-Line tunnel, the diffusion characteristic length handover must address the following evidence: Sample by exposure zone and check material, cracking and cover depth. Retain sample depth, moisture and material batches and interpret deterioration using multiple evidence types; prioritise repairs by function and observed defects.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「氯鹽遷移與耐久判讀」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Chloride transport and durability interpretation\"?","options":["按暴露區取樣，核對材料、裂縫及保護層深度。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Sample by exposure zone and check material, cracking and cover depth.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error."],"answer":0,"explanation":"按暴露區取樣，核對材料、裂縫及保護層深度。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Sample by exposure zone and check material, cracking and cover depth. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b110-v14-40","title":"氯鹽遷移與耐久判讀：失效診斷","titleEn":"Chloride transport and durability interpretation: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b110-v14-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「擴散特徵長度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Diffusion characteristic length” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"混合取樣平均值會掩蓋高鹽濕區的局部劣化。把一次電位讀值當腐蝕速率會誤判剩餘壽命，裂縫快速傳輸也可能被平均材料係數掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A mixed-sample average conceals local deterioration in wet saline zones. Treating one potential reading as corrosion rate misjudges remaining life, while averaged material coefficients conceal rapid crack transport. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：平方根擴散長度僅顯示時間尺度，並不是腐蝕門檻深度；表面濃度變化、乾濕循環、結合效應及施工裂縫須另行辨識。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Surface concentration, wetting cycles, binding and construction cracks must be distinguished rather than hidden in one fitted diffusivity.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「擴散長度就是鋼筋開始腐蝕的位置和精確時間。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Diffusion length gives the exact location and time of corrosion initiation.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b110-v14-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"混合取樣平均值會掩蓋高鹽濕區的局部劣化。把一次電位讀值當腐蝕速率會誤判剩餘壽命，裂縫快速傳輸也可能被平均材料係數掩蓋。","textEn":"A mixed-sample average conceals local deterioration in wet saline zones. Treating one potential reading as corrosion rate misjudges remaining life, while averaged material coefficients conceal rapid crack transport.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b110-v14-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「氯鹽遷移與耐久判讀」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Chloride transport and durability interpretation\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","混合取樣平均值會掩蓋高鹽濕區的局部劣化。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","A mixed-sample average conceals local deterioration in wet saline zones.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":1,"explanation":"混合取樣平均值會掩蓋高鹽濕區的局部劣化。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A mixed-sample average conceals local deterioration in wet saline zones. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b110","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"curriculumVersion":14,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000},{"id":"b111","title":"拉爾達隧道","titleEn":"Laerdal Tunnel","category":"underground","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"拉爾達隧道官方列長24.5公里，於2000年11月開通；同一官方頁也說明後續更新工程。本課將原始營運與更新情境分開，從長距離行車視覺、岩體應力、通風及水量出發，追蹤夜間工程窗口和恢復營運的證據需求，避免以景觀照明取代完整系統評估。","summaryEn":"The road authority reports Laerdal as 24.5 km long and opened in November 2000, while also describing later upgrades. This course separates original service from renewal scenarios, following driver vision, rock stress, ventilation and water into night-work windows and evidence for restoring service. Decorative lighting is not treated as a substitute for system assessment.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"ug-landmarks","subcategoryTitle":"世界隧道與地下巨作","subcategoryTitleEn":"World tunnels and underground landmarks","learningTrack":"underground","learningSubdiscipline":"ug-landmarks","learningTags":["underground","ug-landmarks","tunnel"],"architectureFamily":"tunnel","architectureNodes":[["路線里程與端點","Alignment chainage and endpoints"],["洞壁切向應力","Tangential wall stress"],["漫反射亮度","Diffuse luminance"],["測壓水頭","Piezometric head"],["所需疏散時間","Required evacuation time"],["資產資料完整度","Asset-record completeness"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,5],[1,5]],"diagram":{"type":"tunnel","labels":["路線里程與端點","洞壁切向應力","漫反射亮度","測壓水頭","所需疏散時間"],"labelsEn":["Alignment chainage and endpoints","Tangential wall stress","Diffuse luminance","Piezometric head","Required evacuation time"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"原創綜合審查：先計算「覆土應力與洞壁重分配」，再獨立計算「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」。原創教學假設：覆土深度=800 m；岩體單位重=26 kN/m³。σθ,max=3γH/1000=62.4 MPa。僅把覆土深度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為68.64 MPa。邊界：無支承彈性圓孔，僅垂直遠場壓縮且水平遠場應力為零時，側壁最大環向壓應力；不是任意位置應力或完整三維原位解；不是本工程實測或允收值。原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=75 m。p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=735.75 kPa。僅把水頭增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為809.325 kPa。邊界：靜水表壓，不是土體總壓或原位量測；不是本工程實測或允收值。兩組結果的單位與邊界不同，不能直接相加。請列出一項缺少的現場輸入，說明它會影響哪個結論，以及哪種獨立量測可以縮小不確定度。","textEn":"Original integrated review: first calculate cover stress and wall redistribution, then independently calculate piezometric head and lining pressure. Original teaching assumptions: cover=800 m; rock unit weight=26 kN/m³. σθ,max=3γH/1000=62.4 MPa. Increasing only cover by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 68.64 MPa. Boundary: Maximum tangential compression at the sidewalls of an unsupported elastic circular hole under vertical uniaxial remote loading with zero horizontal remote stress; not stress at any point or the complete three-dimensional in-situ state. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=75 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=735.75 kPa. Increasing only head by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 809.325 kPa. Boundary: Hydrostatic gauge pressure, not total earth pressure or an in-situ measurement. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. The outputs have different units and boundaries and cannot simply be added. Identify one missing field input, explain which conclusion it changes and select an independent measurement to reduce uncertainty.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":14,"enrichmentVersion":14,"stages":[{"id":"b111-v14-s1","title":"地層條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Ground conditions, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「服務邊界與路線代價」與「覆土應力與洞壁重分配」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\" and \"Cover stress and wall redistribution\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b111-v14-01","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「路線里程與端點」如何影響拉爾達隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Alignment chainage and endpoints” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Laerdal Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"拉爾達長距離道路的需求包含冬季連通與維修繞行，不能只以自由車流穿越時間代表整體服務。隧道選線同時改變洞口、覆土與縱坡，短路線不保證低地質風險。比較方案必須使用相同起訖點，並分開主孔、引道及服務坑的工程數量；交通時間只是需求的一個指標，不能代替施工可達性或長期維修評估。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「路線里程與端點」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A long road crossing serves continuity and maintenance diversion as well as free-flow travel; journey time alone does not capture the service. Alignment changes portals, cover and gradient together, so a shorter tunnel need not have lower geological risk. Compare options between identical endpoints and distinguish running bores, approaches and service galleries. Travel time measures one service benefit but cannot replace assessment of construction access, maintenance closures or exposure to uncertain ground. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Alignment chainage and endpoints” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：長度=16 km；速度=60 km/h。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: length=16 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=16 min.","failure":"常見誤解：「最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「路線里程與端點」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Alignment chainage and endpoints”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b111-v14-01-k1","title":"服務邊界與路線代價","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost","text":"拉爾達長距離道路的需求包含冬季連通與維修繞行，不能只以自由車流穿越時間代表整體服務。隧道選線同時改變洞口、覆土與縱坡，短路線不保證低地質風險。","textEn":"A long road crossing serves continuity and maintenance diversion as well as free-flow travel; journey time alone does not capture the service. Alignment changes portals, cover and gradient together, so a shorter tunnel need not have lower geological risk.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b111-v14-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「服務邊界與路線代價」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\" is correct?","options":["最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。","拉爾達長距離道路的需求包含冬季連通與維修繞行，不能只以自由車流穿越時間代表整體服務。","知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。"],"optionsEn":["The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.","A long road crossing serves continuity and maintenance diversion as well as free-flow travel; journey time alone does not capture the service.","Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction."],"answer":1,"explanation":"拉爾達長距離道路的需求包含冬季連通與維修繞行，不能只以自由車流穿越時間代表整體服務。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A long road crossing serves continuity and maintenance diversion as well as free-flow travel; journey time alone does not capture the service. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b111-v14-02","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：定量估算","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b111-v14-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「路線里程與端點」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Alignment chainage and endpoints” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：長度=16 km；速度=60 km/h。t=60L/v=16 min。僅把長度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為17.6 min。邊界：假想交通旅程，未含加減速、排隊及實際時刻表；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: length=16 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=16 min. Increasing only length by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 17.6 min. Boundary: Hypothetical transport journey excluding acceleration, queues and the real timetable. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比較相同端點的正常、封閉及替代路線假設。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare normal, closed and diversion cases between identical endpoints.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b111-v14-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：長度=16 km；速度=60 km/h。t=60L/v=16 min。僅把長度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為17.6 min。邊界：假想交通旅程，未含加減速、排隊及實際時刻表；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: length=16 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=16 min. Increasing only length by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 17.6 min. Boundary: Hypothetical transport journey excluding acceleration, queues and the real timetable. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b111-v14-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「服務邊界與路線代價」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\", which statement holds?","options":["照度越高就必然使隧道內所有物體更容易辨識。","目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。","原創教學假設：長度=16 km；速度=60 km/h。"],"optionsEn":["Higher illuminance necessarily makes every tunnel object easier to detect.","No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.","Original teaching assumptions: length=16 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=16 min."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：長度=16 km；速度=60 km/h。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: length=16 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=16 min. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b111-v14-03","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b111-v14-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「路線里程與端點」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Alignment chainage and endpoints” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比較相同端點的正常、封閉及替代路線假設。把縱斷面、地形與地質剖面疊合，以端點坐標獨立反算距離，再將主孔與支坑數量分開核對。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare normal, closed and diversion cases between identical endpoints. Overlay the longitudinal profile, terrain and geology; independently derive distances from endpoint coordinates and reconcile running-bore and gallery quantities separately. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「路線里程與端點」的交付需回答：比較相同端點的正常、封閉及替代路線假設。在方案表中凍結起訖點、計量範圍及地質假設，任何改線都要同步更新高程、數量與服務情境，不能只替換總長。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Laerdal Tunnel, the alignment chainage and endpoints handover must address the following evidence: Compare normal, closed and diversion cases between identical endpoints. Freeze endpoints, measurement scope and ground assumptions in the option register; realignment requires coordinated updates to elevations, quantities and service scenarios rather than replacing one length.","failure":"注意干擾：忽略封閉時替代路線會低估更新工程對使用者的影響。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Omitting the diversion understates the user impact of renewal closures. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b111-v14-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比較相同端點的正常、封閉及替代路線假設。把縱斷面、地形與地質剖面疊合，以端點坐標獨立反算距離，再將主孔與支坑數量分開核對。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Compare normal, closed and diversion cases between identical endpoints. Overlay the longitudinal profile, terrain and geology; independently derive distances from endpoint coordinates and reconcile running-bore and gallery quantities separately. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b111-v14-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「路線里程與端點」的交付需回答：比較相同端點的正常、封閉及替代路線假設。在方案表中凍結起訖點、計量範圍及地質假設，任何改線都要同步更新高程、數量與服務情境，不能只替換總長。","textEn":"For Laerdal Tunnel, the alignment chainage and endpoints handover must address the following evidence: Compare normal, closed and diversion cases between identical endpoints. Freeze endpoints, measurement scope and ground assumptions in the option register; realignment requires coordinated updates to elevations, quantities and service scenarios rather than replacing one length.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「服務邊界與路線代價」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\"?","options":["比較相同端點的正常、封閉及替代路線假設。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。"],"optionsEn":["Compare normal, closed and diversion cases between identical endpoints.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time."],"answer":0,"explanation":"比較相同端點的正常、封閉及替代路線假設。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare normal, closed and diversion cases between identical endpoints. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b111-v14-04","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：失效診斷","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b111-v14-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「路線里程與端點」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Alignment chainage and endpoints” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"忽略封閉時替代路線會低估更新工程對使用者的影響。混用全線與單孔長度會同時扭曲工程數量、行程及逃生距離，造成方案比較失去共同基準。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Omitting the diversion understates the user impact of renewal closures. Mixing whole-route and single-bore lengths distorts quantities, journey time and escape distance, destroying the common basis of an option comparison. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：比較方案必須使用相同起訖點，並分開主孔、引道及服務坑的工程數量；交通時間只是需求的一個指標，不能代替施工可達性或長期維修評估。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Travel time measures one service benefit but cannot replace assessment of construction access, maintenance closures or exposure to uncertain ground.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b111-v14-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"忽略封閉時替代路線會低估更新工程對使用者的影響。混用全線與單孔長度會同時扭曲工程數量、行程及逃生距離，造成方案比較失去共同基準。","textEn":"Omitting the diversion understates the user impact of renewal closures. Mixing whole-route and single-bore lengths distorts quantities, journey time and escape distance, destroying the common basis of an option comparison.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b111-v14-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「服務邊界與路線代價」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","忽略封閉時替代路線會低估更新工程對使用者的影響。","知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Omitting the diversion understates the user impact of renewal closures.","Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction."],"answer":1,"explanation":"忽略封閉時替代路線會低估更新工程對使用者的影響。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Omitting the diversion understates the user impact of renewal closures. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b111-v14-05","title":"覆土應力與洞壁重分配：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Cover stress and wall redistribution: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b111-v14-04"],"objective":"說明「洞壁切向應力」如何影響拉爾達隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Tangential wall stress” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Laerdal Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"官方更新頁指出岩體高應力使施工具挑戰，本課研究既有洞壁再擾動與新開挖的應力差異。開挖使岩體洞壁失去徑向拘束，遠場荷載轉移到周圍岩體，局部切向應力可能升高。圓孔彈性解可辨識量級，但節理、非圓斷面、塑性區與原位應力比會改變峰值位置，不能只用覆土重量推定全部三維應力。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「洞壁切向應力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The authority identifies high rock stress as a renewal challenge; examine differences between disturbing an existing wall and making a new opening. Excavation removes radial confinement at the wall and transfers load through the surrounding rock, potentially raising local tangential stress. An elastic circular-hole solution identifies scale, but joints, noncircular geometry, yielding and the in-situ stress ratio alter the peak location. Cover weight alone cannot establish the complete three-dimensional stress state or support demand. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Tangential wall stress” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：覆土深度=800 m；岩體單位重=26 kN/m³。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: cover=800 m; rock unit weight=26 kN/m³. σθ,max=3γH/1000=62.4 MPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「洞壁切向應力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Tangential wall stress”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b111-v14-05-k1","title":"覆土應力與洞壁重分配","titleEn":"Cover stress and wall redistribution","text":"官方更新頁指出岩體高應力使施工具挑戰，本課研究既有洞壁再擾動與新開挖的應力差異。開挖使岩體洞壁失去徑向拘束，遠場荷載轉移到周圍岩體，局部切向應力可能升高。","textEn":"The authority identifies high rock stress as a renewal challenge; examine differences between disturbing an existing wall and making a new opening. Excavation removes radial confinement at the wall and transfers load through the surrounding rock, potentially raising local tangential stress.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b111-v14-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「覆土應力與洞壁重分配」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Cover stress and wall redistribution\" is correct?","options":["知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。","支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。","官方更新頁指出岩體高應力使施工具挑戰，本課研究既有洞壁再擾動與新開挖的應力差異。"],"optionsEn":["Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction.","Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem.","The authority identifies high rock stress as a renewal challenge; examine differences between disturbing an existing wall and making a new opening."],"answer":2,"explanation":"官方更新頁指出岩體高應力使施工具挑戰，本課研究既有洞壁再擾動與新開挖的應力差異。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The authority identifies high rock stress as a renewal challenge; examine differences between disturbing an existing wall and making a new opening. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b111-v14-06","title":"覆土應力與洞壁重分配：定量估算","titleEn":"Cover stress and wall redistribution: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b111-v14-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「洞壁切向應力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Tangential wall stress” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：覆土深度=800 m；岩體單位重=26 kN/m³。σθ,max=3γH/1000=62.4 MPa。僅把覆土深度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為68.64 MPa。邊界：無支承彈性圓孔，僅垂直遠場壓縮且水平遠場應力為零時，側壁最大環向壓應力；不是任意位置應力或完整三維原位解；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: cover=800 m; rock unit weight=26 kN/m³. σθ,max=3γH/1000=62.4 MPa. Increasing only cover by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 68.64 MPa. Boundary: Maximum tangential compression at the sidewalls of an unsupported elastic circular hole under vertical uniaxial remote loading with zero horizontal remote stress; not stress at any point or the complete three-dimensional in-situ state. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將舊剝落圖與新施工位移對齊，辨識局部擾動範圍。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Align old spalling maps and new movement to identify local disturbance.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b111-v14-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：覆土深度=800 m；岩體單位重=26 kN/m³。σθ,max=3γH/1000=62.4 MPa。僅把覆土深度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為68.64 MPa。邊界：無支承彈性圓孔，僅垂直遠場壓縮且水平遠場應力為零時，側壁最大環向壓應力；不是任意位置應力或完整三維原位解；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: cover=800 m; rock unit weight=26 kN/m³. σθ,max=3γH/1000=62.4 MPa. Increasing only cover by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 68.64 MPa. Boundary: Maximum tangential compression at the sidewalls of an unsupported elastic circular hole under vertical uniaxial remote loading with zero horizontal remote stress; not stress at any point or the complete three-dimensional in-situ state. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b111-v14-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「覆土應力與洞壁重分配」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Cover stress and wall redistribution\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：覆土深度=800 m；岩體單位重=26 kN/m³。","風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。","增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: cover=800 m; rock unit weight=26 kN/m³. σθ,max=3γH/1000=62.4 MPa.","Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.","Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：覆土深度=800 m；岩體單位重=26 kN/m³。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: cover=800 m; rock unit weight=26 kN/m³. σθ,max=3γH/1000=62.4 MPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b111-v14-07","title":"覆土應力與洞壁重分配：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Cover stress and wall redistribution: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b111-v14-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「洞壁切向應力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Tangential wall stress” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將舊剝落圖與新施工位移對齊，辨識局部擾動範圍。將原位應力量測、岩石試驗及洞壁破壞方位相互比較，再用多點伸長計檢查變形是否與所假設應力方向一致。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Align old spalling maps and new movement to identify local disturbance. Compare in-situ stress measurements, rock tests and wall-damage orientation, then use multipoint extensometers to test consistency with the assumed stress directions. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「洞壁切向應力」的交付需回答：將舊剝落圖與新施工位移對齊，辨識局部擾動範圍。保留應力模型的座標、邊界和材料假設，量測與預測不符時先核對代表性，再由岩力設計者選擇非線性或節理模型。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Laerdal Tunnel, the tangential wall stress handover must address the following evidence: Align old spalling maps and new movement to identify local disturbance. Record stress-model coordinates, boundaries and material assumptions; when observations disagree, check representativeness before the rock designer selects nonlinear or jointed models.","failure":"注意干擾：舊洞已存在多年不代表局部再開挖不會重分配應力。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Long-standing excavation does not prevent stress redistribution from local new work. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b111-v14-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將舊剝落圖與新施工位移對齊，辨識局部擾動範圍。將原位應力量測、岩石試驗及洞壁破壞方位相互比較，再用多點伸長計檢查變形是否與所假設應力方向一致。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Align old spalling maps and new movement to identify local disturbance. Compare in-situ stress measurements, rock tests and wall-damage orientation, then use multipoint extensometers to test consistency with the assumed stress directions. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b111-v14-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「洞壁切向應力」的交付需回答：將舊剝落圖與新施工位移對齊，辨識局部擾動範圍。保留應力模型的座標、邊界和材料假設，量測與預測不符時先核對代表性，再由岩力設計者選擇非線性或節理模型。","textEn":"For Laerdal Tunnel, the tangential wall stress handover must address the following evidence: Align old spalling maps and new movement to identify local disturbance. Record stress-model coordinates, boundaries and material assumptions; when observations disagree, check representativeness before the rock designer selects nonlinear or jointed models.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「覆土應力與洞壁重分配」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Cover stress and wall redistribution\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","將舊剝落圖與新施工位移對齊，辨識局部擾動範圍。","設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Align old spalling maps and new movement to identify local disturbance.","Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety."],"answer":1,"explanation":"將舊剝落圖與新施工位移對齊，辨識局部擾動範圍。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Align old spalling maps and new movement to identify local disturbance. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b111-v14-08","title":"覆土應力與洞壁重分配：失效診斷","titleEn":"Cover stress and wall redistribution: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b111-v14-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「洞壁切向應力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Tangential wall stress” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"舊洞已存在多年不代表局部再開挖不會重分配應力。把彈性峰值直接當岩體強度可能誤判支護需求；相反地忽略剝落或擠壓也會讓局部破壞逐步侵入淨空。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Long-standing excavation does not prevent stress redistribution from local new work. Equating an elastic peak with rock-mass strength misjudges support demand; overlooking spalling or squeezing lets damage progressively consume clearance. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：圓孔彈性解可辨識量級，但節理、非圓斷面、塑性區與原位應力比會改變峰值位置，不能只用覆土重量推定全部三維應力。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Cover weight alone cannot establish the complete three-dimensional stress state or support demand.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b111-v14-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"舊洞已存在多年不代表局部再開挖不會重分配應力。把彈性峰值直接當岩體強度可能誤判支護需求；相反地忽略剝落或擠壓也會讓局部破壞逐步侵入淨空。","textEn":"Long-standing excavation does not prevent stress redistribution from local new work. Equating an elastic peak with rock-mass strength misjudges support demand; overlooking spalling or squeezing lets damage progressively consume clearance.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b111-v14-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「覆土應力與洞壁重分配」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Cover stress and wall redistribution\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。","舊洞已存在多年不代表局部再開挖不會重分配應力。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem.","Long-standing excavation does not prevent stress redistribution from local new work."],"answer":2,"explanation":"舊洞已存在多年不代表局部再開挖不會重分配應力。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Long-standing excavation does not prevent stress redistribution from local new work. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b111-v14-s2","title":"機制、材料與定量設計","titleEn":"Mechanisms, materials and quantitative design","description":"本階段聚焦「支護啟動與變形容量」與「視覺適應與路面亮度」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Support activation and deformation capacity\" and \"Visual adaptation and pavement luminance\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b111-v14-09","title":"支護啟動與變形容量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Support activation and deformation capacity: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b111-v14-08"],"objective":"說明「支護安裝時點」如何影響拉爾達隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Support activation time” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Laerdal Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"在營運多年後更新支護的教學情境中，分開原支護劣化、新錨固啟動和施工卸載。支護荷載由開挖釋放量和支護啟動時間共同決定，越早安裝不一定讓構件受力越小。地盤反力與支護曲線必須連同掌子面距離及封閉順序理解；擠壓性地層還需保留變形容量，不能只追求高剛度與高材料強度。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「支護安裝時點」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Separate deterioration of old support, activation of new anchors and construction unloading during hypothetical renewal. Support load depends on stress release and activation time, so earlier installation does not necessarily reduce member forces. Interpret ground-reaction and support curves together with distance from the face and closure sequence. Squeezing ground also needs deformation capacity; high stiffness and material strength alone do not guarantee a compatible support response. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Support activation time” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：局部剛度=40 kN/mm；位移=7 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: local stiffness=40 kN/mm; movement=7 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「支護安裝時點」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Support activation time”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b111-v14-09-k1","title":"支護啟動與變形容量","titleEn":"Support activation and deformation capacity","text":"在營運多年後更新支護的教學情境中，分開原支護劣化、新錨固啟動和施工卸載。支護荷載由開挖釋放量和支護啟動時間共同決定，越早安裝不一定讓構件受力越小。","textEn":"Separate deterioration of old support, activation of new anchors and construction unloading during hypothetical renewal. Support load depends on stress release and activation time, so earlier installation does not necessarily reduce member forces.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b111-v14-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「支護啟動與變形容量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Support activation and deformation capacity\" is correct?","options":["在營運多年後更新支護的教學情境中，分開原支護劣化、新錨固啟動和施工卸載。","支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。","照度越高就必然使隧道內所有物體更容易辨識。"],"optionsEn":["Separate deterioration of old support, activation of new anchors and construction unloading during hypothetical renewal.","Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem.","Higher illuminance necessarily makes every tunnel object easier to detect."],"answer":0,"explanation":"在營運多年後更新支護的教學情境中，分開原支護劣化、新錨固啟動和施工卸載。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Separate deterioration of old support, activation of new anchors and construction unloading during hypothetical renewal. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b111-v14-10","title":"支護啟動與變形容量：定量估算","titleEn":"Support activation and deformation capacity: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b111-v14-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「支護安裝時點」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Support activation time” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：局部剛度=40 kN/mm；位移=7 mm。F=ku=280 kN。僅把位移增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為308 kN。邊界：線性局部彈簧，不含屈服或時間效應；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: local stiffness=40 kN/mm; movement=7 mm. F=ku=280 kN. Increasing only movement by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 308 kN. Boundary: Local linear spring without yielding or time effects. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：量測基線先於拆換建立，並記錄每一支護改動。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Establish the baseline before replacement and record every support change.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b111-v14-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：局部剛度=40 kN/mm；位移=7 mm。F=ku=280 kN。僅把位移增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為308 kN。邊界：線性局部彈簧，不含屈服或時間效應；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: local stiffness=40 kN/mm; movement=7 mm. F=ku=280 kN. Increasing only movement by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 308 kN. Boundary: Local linear spring without yielding or time effects. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b111-v14-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「支護啟動與變形容量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Support activation and deformation capacity\", which statement holds?","options":["目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。","原創教學假設：局部剛度=40 kN/mm；位移=7 mm。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。"],"optionsEn":["No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.","Original teaching assumptions: local stiffness=40 kN/mm; movement=7 mm.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：局部剛度=40 kN/mm；位移=7 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: local stiffness=40 kN/mm; movement=7 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b111-v14-11","title":"支護啟動與變形容量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Support activation and deformation capacity: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b111-v14-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「支護安裝時點」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Support activation time” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"量測基線先於拆換建立，並記錄每一支護改動。同步記錄收斂、支護荷重與安裝里程，比較同一地質分區內的速率及荷載，不將不同開挖齡期讀值直接混合。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Establish the baseline before replacement and record every support change. Synchronise convergence, support loads and installation chainage; compare rates and loads within one ground domain without mixing readings at different excavation ages. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「支護安裝時點」的交付需回答：量測基線先於拆換建立，並記錄每一支護改動。把安裝時間和量測資料一起交付支護設計者，任何級別變更都需地質及位移證據，不能憑單一瞬間讀值自行改支護。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Laerdal Tunnel, the support activation time handover must address the following evidence: Establish the baseline before replacement and record every support change. Submit installation times with measurements to the support designer; class changes need both ground and movement evidence, not an isolated instantaneous reading.","failure":"注意干擾：拆換造成的位移若誤歸自然岩體變形會影響後續選型。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Misattributing replacement movement to natural ground response misdirects later support selection. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b111-v14-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"量測基線先於拆換建立，並記錄每一支護改動。同步記錄收斂、支護荷重與安裝里程，比較同一地質分區內的速率及荷載，不將不同開挖齡期讀值直接混合。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Establish the baseline before replacement and record every support change. Synchronise convergence, support loads and installation chainage; compare rates and loads within one ground domain without mixing readings at different excavation ages. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b111-v14-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「支護安裝時點」的交付需回答：量測基線先於拆換建立，並記錄每一支護改動。把安裝時間和量測資料一起交付支護設計者，任何級別變更都需地質及位移證據，不能憑單一瞬間讀值自行改支護。","textEn":"For Laerdal Tunnel, the support activation time handover must address the following evidence: Establish the baseline before replacement and record every support change. Submit installation times with measurements to the support designer; class changes need both ground and movement evidence, not an isolated instantaneous reading.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「支護啟動與變形容量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Support activation and deformation capacity\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。","量測基線先於拆換建立，並記錄每一支護改動。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.","Establish the baseline before replacement and record every support change."],"answer":2,"explanation":"量測基線先於拆換建立，並記錄每一支護改動。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Establish the baseline before replacement and record every support change. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b111-v14-12","title":"支護啟動與變形容量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Support activation and deformation capacity: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b111-v14-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「支護安裝時點」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Support activation time” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"拆換造成的位移若誤歸自然岩體變形會影響後續選型。過晚封閉會讓不可回復變形增加，過硬且行程不足的支護也可能脆裂，兩者都可能表現為裂縫而需不同處理。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Misattributing replacement movement to natural ground response misdirects later support selection. Late closure increases irreversible movement, while excessively stiff support with little travel can fail brittly; both produce cracks but require different diagnoses. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：地盤反力與支護曲線必須連同掌子面距離及封閉順序理解；擠壓性地層還需保留變形容量，不能只追求高剛度與高材料強度。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Squeezing ground also needs deformation capacity; high stiffness and material strength alone do not guarantee a compatible support response.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b111-v14-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"拆換造成的位移若誤歸自然岩體變形會影響後續選型。過晚封閉會讓不可回復變形增加，過硬且行程不足的支護也可能脆裂，兩者都可能表現為裂縫而需不同處理。","textEn":"Misattributing replacement movement to natural ground response misdirects later support selection. Late closure increases irreversible movement, while excessively stiff support with little travel can fail brittly; both produce cracks but require different diagnoses.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b111-v14-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「支護啟動與變形容量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Support activation and deformation capacity\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["拆換造成的位移若誤歸自然岩體變形會影響後續選型。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","照度越高就必然使隧道內所有物體更容易辨識。"],"optionsEn":["Misattributing replacement movement to natural ground response misdirects later support selection.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Higher illuminance necessarily makes every tunnel object easier to detect."],"answer":0,"explanation":"拆換造成的位移若誤歸自然岩體變形會影響後續選型。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Misattributing replacement movement to natural ground response misdirects later support selection. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b111-v14-13","title":"視覺適應與路面亮度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Visual adaptation and pavement luminance: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b111-v14-12"],"objective":"說明「漫反射亮度」如何影響拉爾達隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Diffuse luminance” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Laerdal Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"長隧道的視覺節奏與障礙辨識是不同任務，拉爾達教材檢查照明變化是否改變路面對比。駕駛從洞外進入洞內時視覺適應需要時間，照度並不等同從駕駛視角看到的亮度。路面反射、濕度、燈具配光及背景對比共同影響辨識；朗伯模型只示範理想漫反射，不能直接制定入口段燈具間距或真實道路安全值。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「漫反射亮度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Visual rhythm and obstacle detection are distinct tasks; examine how lighting transitions affect pavement contrast over a long drive. Driver adaptation takes time when entering a tunnel, and illuminance is not the luminance seen from the driving position. Pavement reflection, wetness, luminaire distribution and background contrast affect detection. A Lambertian model illustrates ideal diffuse reflection only; it cannot establish entrance-zone spacing or actual road-safety limits without photometric and operational assessment. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Diffuse luminance” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：照度=100 lx；反射率=0.23 無因次。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: illuminance=100 lx; reflectance=0.23 dimensionless.","failure":"常見誤解：「照度越高就必然使隧道內所有物體更容易辨識。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Higher illuminance necessarily makes every tunnel object easier to detect.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「漫反射亮度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Diffuse luminance”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b111-v14-13-k1","title":"視覺適應與路面亮度","titleEn":"Visual adaptation and pavement luminance","text":"長隧道的視覺節奏與障礙辨識是不同任務，拉爾達教材檢查照明變化是否改變路面對比。駕駛從洞外進入洞內時視覺適應需要時間，照度並不等同從駕駛視角看到的亮度。","textEn":"Visual rhythm and obstacle detection are distinct tasks; examine how lighting transitions affect pavement contrast over a long drive. Driver adaptation takes time when entering a tunnel, and illuminance is not the luminance seen from the driving position.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b111-v14-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：照度越高就必然使隧道內所有物體更容易辨識。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Higher illuminance necessarily makes every tunnel object easier to detect. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「視覺適應與路面亮度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Visual adaptation and pavement luminance\" is correct?","options":["照度越高就必然使隧道內所有物體更容易辨識。","長隧道的視覺節奏與障礙辨識是不同任務，拉爾達教材檢查照明變化是否改變路面對比。","風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。"],"optionsEn":["Higher illuminance necessarily makes every tunnel object easier to detect.","Visual rhythm and obstacle detection are distinct tasks; examine how lighting transitions affect pavement contrast over a long drive.","Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel."],"answer":1,"explanation":"長隧道的視覺節奏與障礙辨識是不同任務，拉爾達教材檢查照明變化是否改變路面對比。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Visual rhythm and obstacle detection are distinct tasks; examine how lighting transitions affect pavement contrast over a long drive. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b111-v14-14","title":"視覺適應與路面亮度：定量估算","titleEn":"Visual adaptation and pavement luminance: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b111-v14-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「漫反射亮度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Diffuse luminance” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：照度=100 lx；反射率=0.23 無因次。L=ρE/π=7.32113 cd/m²。僅把照度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為8.05324 cd/m²。邊界：理想朗伯漫反射，不是真實濕路面亮度；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: illuminance=100 lx; reflectance=0.23 dimensionless. L=ρE/π=7.32113 cd/m². Increasing only illuminance by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 8.05324 cd/m². Boundary: Ideal Lambertian reflection, not actual wet-road luminance. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：從駕駛視角比較過渡區、一般區與濕路面。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare transition zones, ordinary reaches and wet surfaces from the driver viewpoint.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b111-v14-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：照度=100 lx；反射率=0.23 無因次。L=ρE/π=7.32113 cd/m²。僅把照度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為8.05324 cd/m²。邊界：理想朗伯漫反射，不是真實濕路面亮度；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: illuminance=100 lx; reflectance=0.23 dimensionless. L=ρE/π=7.32113 cd/m². Increasing only illuminance by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 8.05324 cd/m². Boundary: Ideal Lambertian reflection, not actual wet-road luminance. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b111-v14-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「視覺適應與路面亮度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Visual adaptation and pavement luminance\", which statement holds?","options":["增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。","設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。","原創教學假設：照度=100 lx；反射率=0.23 無因次。"],"optionsEn":["Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.","Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety.","Original teaching assumptions: illuminance=100 lx; reflectance=0.23 dimensionless."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：照度=100 lx；反射率=0.23 無因次。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: illuminance=100 lx; reflectance=0.23 dimensionless. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b111-v14-15","title":"視覺適應與路面亮度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Visual adaptation and pavement luminance: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b111-v14-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「漫反射亮度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Diffuse luminance” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"從駕駛視角比較過渡區、一般區與濕路面。以駕駛視角的亮度量測配合照度網格，分別檢查乾濕路面與燈具衰減，保留外部天空條件。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare transition zones, ordinary reaches and wet surfaces from the driver viewpoint. Combine driver-view luminance with illuminance grids, checking dry and wet pavement and lamp depreciation while preserving exterior sky conditions. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「漫反射亮度」的交付需回答：從駕駛視角比較過渡區、一般區與濕路面。將視角、路面狀態和光度校正連同量測交付，照明調整需按核准場景測試，不把理想反射公式當驗收標準。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Laerdal Tunnel, the diffuse luminance handover must address the following evidence: Compare transition zones, ordinary reaches and wet surfaces from the driver viewpoint. Hand over viewing geometry, pavement state and photometric calibration; test changes against approved scenarios rather than treating ideal reflection as an acceptance criterion.","failure":"注意干擾：覺得明亮舒適不能證明所有障礙在不利背景可辨識。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Perceived brightness and comfort do not prove detection against adverse backgrounds. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b111-v14-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"從駕駛視角比較過渡區、一般區與濕路面。以駕駛視角的亮度量測配合照度網格，分別檢查乾濕路面與燈具衰減，保留外部天空條件。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Compare transition zones, ordinary reaches and wet surfaces from the driver viewpoint. Combine driver-view luminance with illuminance grids, checking dry and wet pavement and lamp depreciation while preserving exterior sky conditions. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b111-v14-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「漫反射亮度」的交付需回答：從駕駛視角比較過渡區、一般區與濕路面。將視角、路面狀態和光度校正連同量測交付，照明調整需按核准場景測試，不把理想反射公式當驗收標準。","textEn":"For Laerdal Tunnel, the diffuse luminance handover must address the following evidence: Compare transition zones, ordinary reaches and wet surfaces from the driver viewpoint. Hand over viewing geometry, pavement state and photometric calibration; test changes against approved scenarios rather than treating ideal reflection as an acceptance criterion.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「視覺適應與路面亮度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Visual adaptation and pavement luminance\"?","options":["從駕駛視角比較過渡區、一般區與濕路面。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Compare transition zones, ordinary reaches and wet surfaces from the driver viewpoint.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":0,"explanation":"從駕駛視角比較過渡區、一般區與濕路面。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare transition zones, ordinary reaches and wet surfaces from the driver viewpoint. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b111-v14-16","title":"視覺適應與路面亮度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Visual adaptation and pavement luminance: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b111-v14-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「漫反射亮度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Diffuse luminance” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"覺得明亮舒適不能證明所有障礙在不利背景可辨識。照度平均值合格仍可能存在低亮度障礙區或眩光，感測器沾污也會使調光系統低估外界亮度。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Perceived brightness and comfort do not prove detection against adverse backgrounds. Acceptable average illuminance can coexist with dark obstacles or glare, while sensor contamination may bias adaptive lighting controls. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：路面反射、濕度、燈具配光及背景對比共同影響辨識；朗伯模型只示範理想漫反射，不能直接制定入口段燈具間距或真實道路安全值。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A Lambertian model illustrates ideal diffuse reflection only; it cannot establish entrance-zone spacing or actual road-safety limits without photometric and operational assessment.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「照度越高就必然使隧道內所有物體更容易辨識。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Higher illuminance necessarily makes every tunnel object easier to detect.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b111-v14-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"覺得明亮舒適不能證明所有障礙在不利背景可辨識。照度平均值合格仍可能存在低亮度障礙區或眩光，感測器沾污也會使調光系統低估外界亮度。","textEn":"Perceived brightness and comfort do not prove detection against adverse backgrounds. Acceptable average illuminance can coexist with dark obstacles or glare, while sensor contamination may bias adaptive lighting controls.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b111-v14-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「視覺適應與路面亮度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Visual adaptation and pavement luminance\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","覺得明亮舒適不能證明所有障礙在不利背景可辨識。","風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Perceived brightness and comfort do not prove detection against adverse backgrounds.","Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel."],"answer":1,"explanation":"覺得明亮舒適不能證明所有障礙在不利背景可辨識。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Perceived brightness and comfort do not prove detection against adverse backgrounds. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b111-v14-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「通風網路與壓力損失」與「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Ventilation network and pressure loss\" and \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b111-v14-17","title":"通風網路與壓力損失：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Ventilation network and pressure loss: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b111-v14-16"],"objective":"說明「風道摩擦壓損」如何影響拉爾達隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Duct friction loss” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Laerdal Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"長道路通風需保留車流活塞效應與外風，研究夜間低車流時原有風量假設是否仍適用。風機提供壓差，實際風量由風道摩阻、局部損失、外風與其他風機共同決定。支路開關會重新分配整個網路，不能把額定風量直接加總；正常污染稀釋與火災控煙也有不同目標，需要分別建立受控邊界和故障情境。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「風道摩擦壓損」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Retain traffic piston effects and external wind, testing whether assumptions remain valid during low-traffic night work. Fans supply pressure, but actual flow follows friction, local losses, external wind and interactions with other fans. Switching a branch redistributes the network rather than simply adding rated flows. Routine dilution and fire smoke control have different objectives, so each needs explicit boundaries, operating states and failure cases rather than one universal flow target. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Duct friction loss” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：達西因子=0.025 無因次；風道長度=900 m；水力直徑=4 m；空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；平均風速=3.4 m/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.025 dimensionless; duct length=900 m; hydraulic diameter=4 m; air density=1.2 kg/m³; mean velocity=3.4 m/s. Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=39.015 Pa.","failure":"常見誤解：「風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「風道摩擦壓損」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Duct friction loss”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b111-v14-17-k1","title":"通風網路與壓力損失","titleEn":"Ventilation network and pressure loss","text":"長道路通風需保留車流活塞效應與外風，研究夜間低車流時原有風量假設是否仍適用。風機提供壓差，實際風量由風道摩阻、局部損失、外風與其他風機共同決定。","textEn":"Retain traffic piston effects and external wind, testing whether assumptions remain valid during low-traffic night work. Fans supply pressure, but actual flow follows friction, local losses, external wind and interactions with other fans.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b111-v14-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「通風網路與壓力損失」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Ventilation network and pressure loss\" is correct?","options":["風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。","目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。","長道路通風需保留車流活塞效應與外風，研究夜間低車流時原有風量假設是否仍適用。"],"optionsEn":["Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.","No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.","Retain traffic piston effects and external wind, testing whether assumptions remain valid during low-traffic night work."],"answer":2,"explanation":"長道路通風需保留車流活塞效應與外風，研究夜間低車流時原有風量假設是否仍適用。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Retain traffic piston effects and external wind, testing whether assumptions remain valid during low-traffic night work. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b111-v14-18","title":"通風網路與壓力損失：定量估算","titleEn":"Ventilation network and pressure loss: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b111-v14-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「風道摩擦壓損」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Duct friction loss” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：達西因子=0.025 無因次；風道長度=900 m；水力直徑=4 m；空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；平均風速=3.4 m/s。Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=39.015 Pa。僅把平均風速增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為47.2082 Pa。邊界：定密度直管摩阻，局部損失及外風另計；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.025 dimensionless; duct length=900 m; hydraulic diameter=4 m; air density=1.2 kg/m³; mean velocity=3.4 m/s. Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=39.015 Pa. Increasing only mean velocity by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 47.2082 Pa. Boundary: Constant-density straight-duct friction; local loss and external wind are separate. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比較車流高低時段同風機設定下的風速與壓差。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare flow and pressure at the same fan setting under high and low traffic.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b111-v14-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：達西因子=0.025 無因次；風道長度=900 m；水力直徑=4 m；空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；平均風速=3.4 m/s。Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=39.015 Pa。僅把平均風速增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為47.2082 Pa。邊界：定密度直管摩阻，局部損失及外風另計；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.025 dimensionless; duct length=900 m; hydraulic diameter=4 m; air density=1.2 kg/m³; mean velocity=3.4 m/s. Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=39.015 Pa. Increasing only mean velocity by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 47.2082 Pa. Boundary: Constant-density straight-duct friction; local loss and external wind are separate. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b111-v14-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「通風網路與壓力損失」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Ventilation network and pressure loss\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：達西因子=0.025 無因次；風道長度=900 m；水力直徑=4 m；空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；平均風速=3.4 m/s。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.025 dimensionless.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：達西因子=0.025 無因次；風道長度=900 m；水力直徑=4 m；空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；平均風速=3.4 m/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.025 dimensionless; duct length=900 m; hydraulic diameter=4 m; air density=1.2 kg/m³; mean velocity=3.4 m/s. Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=39.015 Pa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b111-v14-19","title":"通風網路與壓力損失：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Ventilation network and pressure loss: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b111-v14-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「風道摩擦壓損」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Duct friction loss” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比較車流高低時段同風機設定下的風速與壓差。沿線同步量測靜壓與風速，記錄風門及其他風機狀態，再把實測工作點和風機曲線、網路壓損比較。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare flow and pressure at the same fan setting under high and low traffic. Measure pressure and velocity synchronously, record dampers and other fans, and compare the measured duty point with fan curves and network resistance. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「風道摩擦壓損」的交付需回答：比較車流高低時段同風機設定下的風速與壓差。驗收採明確風門和車流邊界，維修改線後重新核對網路工作點，火災模式由防災責任工程師簽認而非沿用正常模式。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Laerdal Tunnel, the duct friction loss handover must address the following evidence: Compare flow and pressure at the same fan setting under high and low traffic. Commission with specified damper and traffic boundaries, recheck duty points after rerouting, and have the fire-safety engineer approve emergency modes independently.","failure":"注意干擾：將白天交通助流套到夜間會高估施工區換氣。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Transferring daytime traffic-assisted flow to night work overstates ventilation. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b111-v14-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比較車流高低時段同風機設定下的風速與壓差。沿線同步量測靜壓與風速，記錄風門及其他風機狀態，再把實測工作點和風機曲線、網路壓損比較。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Compare flow and pressure at the same fan setting under high and low traffic. Measure pressure and velocity synchronously, record dampers and other fans, and compare the measured duty point with fan curves and network resistance. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b111-v14-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「風道摩擦壓損」的交付需回答：比較車流高低時段同風機設定下的風速與壓差。驗收採明確風門和車流邊界，維修改線後重新核對網路工作點，火災模式由防災責任工程師簽認而非沿用正常模式。","textEn":"For Laerdal Tunnel, the duct friction loss handover must address the following evidence: Compare flow and pressure at the same fan setting under high and low traffic. Commission with specified damper and traffic boundaries, recheck duty points after rerouting, and have the fire-safety engineer approve emergency modes independently.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「通風網路與壓力損失」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Ventilation network and pressure loss\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","比較車流高低時段同風機設定下的風速與壓差。","知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Compare flow and pressure at the same fan setting under high and low traffic.","Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction."],"answer":1,"explanation":"比較車流高低時段同風機設定下的風速與壓差。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare flow and pressure at the same fan setting under high and low traffic. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b111-v14-20","title":"通風網路與壓力損失：失效診斷","titleEn":"Ventilation network and pressure loss: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b111-v14-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「風道摩擦壓損」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Duct friction loss” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"將白天交通助流套到夜間會高估施工區換氣。只看風機轉速會漏掉風門誤位或短路漏風，可能在總耗電增加時，真正需要的區段反而風量不足。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Transferring daytime traffic-assisted flow to night work overstates ventilation. Fan speed alone misses a misplaced damper or leakage shortcut; total power may rise while the critical section receives less air. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：支路開關會重新分配整個網路，不能把額定風量直接加總；正常污染稀釋與火災控煙也有不同目標，需要分別建立受控邊界和故障情境。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Routine dilution and fire smoke control have different objectives, so each needs explicit boundaries, operating states and failure cases rather than one universal flow target.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b111-v14-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"將白天交通助流套到夜間會高估施工區換氣。只看風機轉速會漏掉風門誤位或短路漏風，可能在總耗電增加時，真正需要的區段反而風量不足。","textEn":"Transferring daytime traffic-assisted flow to night work overstates ventilation. Fan speed alone misses a misplaced damper or leakage shortcut; total power may rise while the critical section receives less air.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b111-v14-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「通風網路與壓力損失」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Ventilation network and pressure loss\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。","將白天交通助流套到夜間會高估施工區換氣。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.","Transferring daytime traffic-assisted flow to night work overstates ventilation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"將白天交通助流套到夜間會高估施工區換氣。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Transferring daytime traffic-assisted flow to night work overstates ventilation. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b111-v14-21","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b111-v14-20"],"objective":"說明「測壓水頭」如何影響拉爾達隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Piezometric head” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Laerdal Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"拉爾達山區裂隙補注與道路排水在教學模型中分開，研究季節水量變化對設備更新安排的影響。水壓取決於連通含水層的測壓水頭，不必等於地表或海面至洞頂的幾何深度。排水降低水壓卻可能增加有效應力與沉陷；停泵或排水堵塞後水頭又會回升，因此防水、排水及環境保水是互相制約的設計選擇。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「測壓水頭」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Separate fracture recharge from road drainage and examine seasonal water effects on renewal planning. Water pressure follows piezometric head in the connected aquifer, not automatically the geometric depth below ground or sea level. Drainage reduces pressure but can increase effective stress and settlement. Head may recover after a pump outage or blockage, coupling waterproofing, drainage capacity and preservation of surrounding groundwater in the permanent design. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Piezometric head” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=75 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=75 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=735.75 kPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「測壓水頭」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Piezometric head”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b111-v14-21-k1","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure","text":"拉爾達山區裂隙補注與道路排水在教學模型中分開，研究季節水量變化對設備更新安排的影響。水壓取決於連通含水層的測壓水頭，不必等於地表或海面至洞頂的幾何深度。","textEn":"Separate fracture recharge from road drainage and examine seasonal water effects on renewal planning. Water pressure follows piezometric head in the connected aquifer, not automatically the geometric depth below ground or sea level.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b111-v14-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\" is correct?","options":["拉爾達山區裂隙補注與道路排水在教學模型中分開，研究季節水量變化對設備更新安排的影響。","目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。","增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。"],"optionsEn":["Separate fracture recharge from road drainage and examine seasonal water effects on renewal planning.","No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.","Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly."],"answer":0,"explanation":"拉爾達山區裂隙補注與道路排水在教學模型中分開，研究季節水量變化對設備更新安排的影響。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Separate fracture recharge from road drainage and examine seasonal water effects on renewal planning. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b111-v14-22","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓：定量估算","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b111-v14-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「測壓水頭」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Piezometric head” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=75 m。p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=735.75 kPa。僅把水頭增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為809.325 kPa。邊界：靜水表壓，不是土體總壓或原位量測；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=75 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=735.75 kPa. Increasing only head by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 809.325 kPa. Boundary: Hydrostatic gauge pressure, not total earth pressure or an in-situ measurement. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：按降雨與季節對照排水、水頭及堵塞紀錄。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare drainage, head and blockage records against rainfall and season.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b111-v14-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=75 m。p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=735.75 kPa。僅把水頭增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為809.325 kPa。邊界：靜水表壓，不是土體總壓或原位量測；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=75 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=735.75 kPa. Increasing only head by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 809.325 kPa. Boundary: Hydrostatic gauge pressure, not total earth pressure or an in-situ measurement. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b111-v14-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\", which statement holds?","options":["設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。","原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=75 m。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety.","Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=75 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=735.75 kPa.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=75 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=75 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=735.75 kPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b111-v14-23","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b111-v14-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「測壓水頭」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Piezometric head” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"按降雨與季節對照排水、水頭及堵塞紀錄。使用分層測壓管及流量計，配合降雨或潮位序列分辨補注與設備影響，將讀值統一換算至同一高程基準。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare drainage, head and blockage records against rainfall and season. Use nested piezometers and flowmeters with rainfall or tide histories to distinguish recharge from equipment effects, converting observations to a common elevation datum. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「測壓水頭」的交付需回答：按降雨與季節對照排水、水頭及堵塞紀錄。設計檢核應分列正常排水、堵塞與停電水位，將環境受體的容許變化和監測責任一起交付，不把抽水量當唯一指標。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Laerdal Tunnel, the piezometric head handover must address the following evidence: Compare drainage, head and blockage records against rainfall and season. Separate normal drainage, blocked-drain and power-outage heads and hand over receptor limits and monitoring responsibility together rather than using pump flow as the sole indicator.","failure":"注意干擾：融雪期增流若當設備故障，可能無效更換正常泵組。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Treating snowmelt inflow as equipment failure can prompt needless pump replacement. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b111-v14-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"按降雨與季節對照排水、水頭及堵塞紀錄。使用分層測壓管及流量計，配合降雨或潮位序列分辨補注與設備影響，將讀值統一換算至同一高程基準。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Compare drainage, head and blockage records against rainfall and season. Use nested piezometers and flowmeters with rainfall or tide histories to distinguish recharge from equipment effects, converting observations to a common elevation datum. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b111-v14-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「測壓水頭」的交付需回答：按降雨與季節對照排水、水頭及堵塞紀錄。設計檢核應分列正常排水、堵塞與停電水位，將環境受體的容許變化和監測責任一起交付，不把抽水量當唯一指標。","textEn":"For Laerdal Tunnel, the piezometric head handover must address the following evidence: Compare drainage, head and blockage records against rainfall and season. Separate normal drainage, blocked-drain and power-outage heads and hand over receptor limits and monitoring responsibility together rather than using pump flow as the sole indicator.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。","按降雨與季節對照排水、水頭及堵塞紀錄。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem.","Compare drainage, head and blockage records against rainfall and season."],"answer":2,"explanation":"按降雨與季節對照排水、水頭及堵塞紀錄。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare drainage, head and blockage records against rainfall and season. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b111-v14-24","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓：失效診斷","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b111-v14-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「測壓水頭」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Piezometric head” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"融雪期增流若當設備故障，可能無效更換正常泵組。將暫時降水後的低水頭當成永久狀態，會漏掉停泵後外壓回升；過度排水也可能引起周邊地層壓密。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Treating snowmelt inflow as equipment failure can prompt needless pump replacement. Treating temporarily lowered head as permanent misses pressure recovery after outage; excessive drainage can also consolidate surrounding ground. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：排水降低水壓卻可能增加有效應力與沉陷；停泵或排水堵塞後水頭又會回升，因此防水、排水及環境保水是互相制約的設計選擇。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Head may recover after a pump outage or blockage, coupling waterproofing, drainage capacity and preservation of surrounding groundwater in the permanent design.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b111-v14-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"融雪期增流若當設備故障，可能無效更換正常泵組。將暫時降水後的低水頭當成永久狀態，會漏掉停泵後外壓回升；過度排水也可能引起周邊地層壓密。","textEn":"Treating snowmelt inflow as equipment failure can prompt needless pump replacement. Treating temporarily lowered head as permanent misses pressure recovery after outage; excessive drainage can also consolidate surrounding ground.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b111-v14-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["融雪期增流若當設備故障，可能無效更換正常泵組。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。"],"optionsEn":["Treating snowmelt inflow as equipment failure can prompt needless pump replacement.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly."],"answer":0,"explanation":"融雪期增流若當設備故障，可能無效更換正常泵組。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Treating snowmelt inflow as equipment failure can prompt needless pump replacement. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b111-v14-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」與「疏散時間與分區可用性」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Shared access and transport bottlenecks\" and \"Evacuation time and zone availability\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b111-v14-25","title":"共享通道與運輸瓶頸：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Shared access and transport bottlenecks: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b111-v14-24"],"objective":"說明「出渣運輸節拍」如何影響拉爾達隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Muck-transport cycle” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Laerdal Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"官方描述夜間更新與通行安排，本課將施工準備、出渣及恢復檢查從可用窗口逐項扣除。多工作面只有在供電、通風、出渣與材料供應同步充足時才增加總產量。共用豎井或軌道形成串聯瓶頸，排隊和維修窗口會降低名目容量；緩衝區太大又可能侵占通行與救援空間，因此不能單純把各面產能相加。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「出渣運輸節拍」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"For night renewal, deduct preparation, spoil handling and restoration checks from the available access window. Multiple headings increase output only when power, air, muck transport and materials support them together. Shared shafts or railways become serial bottlenecks, while queues and maintenance reduce nominal capacity. Large buffers may obstruct personnel and rescue access, so face capacities cannot simply be added without a network-level transport and storage check. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Muck-transport cycle” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=30 t；往返週期=36 min。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=30 t; cycle=36 min.","failure":"常見誤解：「增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「出渣運輸節拍」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Muck-transport cycle”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b111-v14-25-k1","title":"共享通道與運輸瓶頸","titleEn":"Shared access and transport bottlenecks","text":"官方描述夜間更新與通行安排，本課將施工準備、出渣及恢復檢查從可用窗口逐項扣除。多工作面只有在供電、通風、出渣與材料供應同步充足時才增加總產量。","textEn":"For night renewal, deduct preparation, spoil handling and restoration checks from the available access window. Multiple headings increase output only when power, air, muck transport and materials support them together.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b111-v14-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Shared access and transport bottlenecks\" is correct?","options":["增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。","官方描述夜間更新與通行安排，本課將施工準備、出渣及恢復檢查從可用窗口逐項扣除。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。"],"optionsEn":["Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.","For night renewal, deduct preparation, spoil handling and restoration checks from the available access window.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time."],"answer":1,"explanation":"官方描述夜間更新與通行安排，本課將施工準備、出渣及恢復檢查從可用窗口逐項扣除。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"For night renewal, deduct preparation, spoil handling and restoration checks from the available access window. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b111-v14-26","title":"共享通道與運輸瓶頸：定量估算","titleEn":"Shared access and transport bottlenecks: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b111-v14-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「出渣運輸節拍」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Muck-transport cycle” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=30 t；往返週期=36 min。C=N payload 60/T=200 t/h。僅把往返週期增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為181.818 t/h。邊界：無排隊理想循環，並非共享路段實際產能；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=30 t; cycle=36 min. C=N payload 60/T=200 t/h. Increasing only cycle by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 181.818 t/h. Boundary: Ideal cycle without queues, not actual shared-route production. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：記錄首個工作面開始與最後恢復確認的時間戳。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Record first productive work and final restoration sign-off timestamps.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b111-v14-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=30 t；往返週期=36 min。C=N payload 60/T=200 t/h。僅把往返週期增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為181.818 t/h。邊界：無排隊理想循環，並非共享路段實際產能；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=30 t; cycle=36 min. C=N payload 60/T=200 t/h. Increasing only cycle by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 181.818 t/h. Boundary: Ideal cycle without queues, not actual shared-route production. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b111-v14-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Shared access and transport bottlenecks\", which statement holds?","options":["全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。","知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。","原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=30 t；往返週期=36 min。"],"optionsEn":["Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.","Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction.","Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=30 t; cycle=36 min."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=30 t；往返週期=36 min。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=30 t; cycle=36 min. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b111-v14-27","title":"共享通道與運輸瓶頸：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Shared access and transport bottlenecks: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b111-v14-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「出渣運輸節拍」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Muck-transport cycle” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"記錄首個工作面開始與最後恢復確認的時間戳。以裝載質量、往返時間及排隊時間重建物流曲線，再核對緩衝占用、共用通道優先權與維修時段。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Record first productive work and final restoration sign-off timestamps. Reconstruct flow from payload, round-trip and queue times, then check buffer occupancy, shared-route priorities and maintenance periods. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「出渣運輸節拍」的交付需回答：記錄首個工作面開始與最後恢復確認的時間戳。每日排程同時標示人員、材料和維修的占用時段，任何物流改線先檢查通風與應變通道，不能只看運量提升。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Laerdal Tunnel, the muck-transport cycle handover must address the following evidence: Record first productive work and final restoration sign-off timestamps. Schedules show personnel, materials and maintenance occupancy together; rerouting first checks ventilation and emergency access rather than only throughput gains.","failure":"注意干擾：以封閉總時長當有效施工時間會持續低估工期。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Treating full closure duration as productive time repeatedly understates programme length. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b111-v14-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"記錄首個工作面開始與最後恢復確認的時間戳。以裝載質量、往返時間及排隊時間重建物流曲線，再核對緩衝占用、共用通道優先權與維修時段。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Record first productive work and final restoration sign-off timestamps. Reconstruct flow from payload, round-trip and queue times, then check buffer occupancy, shared-route priorities and maintenance periods. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b111-v14-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「出渣運輸節拍」的交付需回答：記錄首個工作面開始與最後恢復確認的時間戳。每日排程同時標示人員、材料和維修的占用時段，任何物流改線先檢查通風與應變通道，不能只看運量提升。","textEn":"For Laerdal Tunnel, the muck-transport cycle handover must address the following evidence: Record first productive work and final restoration sign-off timestamps. Schedules show personnel, materials and maintenance occupancy together; rerouting first checks ventilation and emergency access rather than only throughput gains.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Shared access and transport bottlenecks\"?","options":["記錄首個工作面開始與最後恢復確認的時間戳。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","照度越高就必然使隧道內所有物體更容易辨識。"],"optionsEn":["Record first productive work and final restoration sign-off timestamps.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Higher illuminance necessarily makes every tunnel object easier to detect."],"answer":0,"explanation":"記錄首個工作面開始與最後恢復確認的時間戳。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Record first productive work and final restoration sign-off timestamps. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b111-v14-28","title":"共享通道與運輸瓶頸：失效診斷","titleEn":"Shared access and transport bottlenecks: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b111-v14-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「出渣運輸節拍」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Muck-transport cycle” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"以封閉總時長當有效施工時間會持續低估工期。把理想往返時間當全天常數會忽略交會等待與卸料堵塞，導致工作面停工或把材料堆入必要通道。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Treating full closure duration as productive time repeatedly understates programme length. Treating an ideal cycle as constant all day misses passing delays and unloading blockages, stopping headings or pushing material into essential access space. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：共用豎井或軌道形成串聯瓶頸，排隊和維修窗口會降低名目容量；緩衝區太大又可能侵占通行與救援空間，因此不能單純把各面產能相加。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Large buffers may obstruct personnel and rescue access, so face capacities cannot simply be added without a network-level transport and storage check.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b111-v14-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"以封閉總時長當有效施工時間會持續低估工期。把理想往返時間當全天常數會忽略交會等待與卸料堵塞，導致工作面停工或把材料堆入必要通道。","textEn":"Treating full closure duration as productive time repeatedly understates programme length. Treating an ideal cycle as constant all day misses passing delays and unloading blockages, stopping headings or pushing material into essential access space.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b111-v14-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Shared access and transport bottlenecks\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","以封閉總時長當有效施工時間會持續低估工期。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Treating full closure duration as productive time repeatedly understates programme length.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以封閉總時長當有效施工時間會持續低估工期。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Treating full closure duration as productive time repeatedly understates programme length. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b111-v14-29","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b111-v14-28"],"objective":"說明「所需疏散時間」如何影響拉爾達隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Required evacuation time” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Laerdal Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"長距離公路事故需要辨認行車者反應延遲與路線可用性，更新區域還會改變原有標示。疏散時間包含辨識、反應、移動及排隊，不只由出口距離決定。人員速度會受煙熱、能見度及行動能力影響，安全判斷還要比較可用安全時間；橫通道存在但門或鄰孔不可用時，圖上的最短路線不一定能作實際選擇。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「所需疏散時間」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Incident travel includes user response delay and route availability, while renewal zones can alter familiar signs. Evacuation includes detection, response, travel and queues, not merely distance to an exit. Smoke, visibility and mobility alter walking speed, while safety requires comparison with available safe time. A passage shown on a plan may be unusable because its door or receiving bore is unavailable, invalidating the nominal shortest route. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Required evacuation time” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：前置時間=100 s；行走距離=340 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=100 s; travel distance=340 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「所需疏散時間」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Required evacuation time”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b111-v14-29-k1","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability","text":"長距離公路事故需要辨認行車者反應延遲與路線可用性，更新區域還會改變原有標示。疏散時間包含辨識、反應、移動及排隊，不只由出口距離決定。","textEn":"Incident travel includes user response delay and route availability, while renewal zones can alter familiar signs. Evacuation includes detection, response, travel and queues, not merely distance to an exit.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b111-v14-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「疏散時間與分區可用性」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Evacuation time and zone availability\" is correct?","options":["只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。","設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。","長距離公路事故需要辨認行車者反應延遲與路線可用性，更新區域還會改變原有標示。"],"optionsEn":["Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.","Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety.","Incident travel includes user response delay and route availability, while renewal zones can alter familiar signs."],"answer":2,"explanation":"長距離公路事故需要辨認行車者反應延遲與路線可用性，更新區域還會改變原有標示。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Incident travel includes user response delay and route availability, while renewal zones can alter familiar signs. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b111-v14-30","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性：定量估算","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b111-v14-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「所需疏散時間」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Required evacuation time” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：前置時間=100 s；行走距離=340 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。RSET=tpre+d/v=525 s。僅把行走距離增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為567.5 s。邊界：單群體固定速度，不含排隊煙熱及能力差異，不能單獨判安全；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=100 s; travel distance=340 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s. RSET=tpre+d/v=525 s. Increasing only travel distance by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 567.5 s. Boundary: One group at fixed speed without queues, smoke or mobility differences; not a safety conclusion. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：沿現行施工階段路徑走查，分列辨識和移動時間。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Walk the current stage route and separate recognition from movement time.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b111-v14-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：前置時間=100 s；行走距離=340 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。RSET=tpre+d/v=525 s。僅把行走距離增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為567.5 s。邊界：單群體固定速度，不含排隊煙熱及能力差異，不能單獨判安全；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=100 s; travel distance=340 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s. RSET=tpre+d/v=525 s. Increasing only travel distance by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 567.5 s. Boundary: One group at fixed speed without queues, smoke or mobility differences; not a safety conclusion. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b111-v14-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「疏散時間與分區可用性」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Evacuation time and zone availability\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：前置時間=100 s；行走距離=340 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。","支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=100 s; travel distance=340 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.","Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：前置時間=100 s；行走距離=340 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=100 s; travel distance=340 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b111-v14-31","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b111-v14-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「所需疏散時間」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Required evacuation time” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"沿現行施工階段路徑走查，分列辨識和移動時間。以人流模擬或受控演練分辨前置時間、行走與門口排隊，核對每個出口接收區的可用狀態及通訊紀錄。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Walk the current stage route and separate recognition from movement time. Separate pre-movement, travel and doorway queues through simulation or controlled drills, checking receiving-zone availability and communication records for each exit. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「所需疏散時間」的交付需回答：沿現行施工階段路徑走查，分列辨識和移動時間。疏散模型保留人口、速度分布及出口狀態，演練改動由營運與防災責任者批准，教材算例不得當作現場指揮程序。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Laerdal Tunnel, the required evacuation time handover must address the following evidence: Walk the current stage route and separate recognition from movement time. Retain population, speed distribution and exit states; operations and fire-safety owners approve drill changes, and classroom calculations are not incident-command procedures.","failure":"注意干擾：只使用完工後地圖可能把人引入尚未恢復的區段。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A final-layout map can direct users into an unrestored section. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b111-v14-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"沿現行施工階段路徑走查，分列辨識和移動時間。以人流模擬或受控演練分辨前置時間、行走與門口排隊，核對每個出口接收區的可用狀態及通訊紀錄。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Walk the current stage route and separate recognition from movement time. Separate pre-movement, travel and doorway queues through simulation or controlled drills, checking receiving-zone availability and communication records for each exit. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b111-v14-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「所需疏散時間」的交付需回答：沿現行施工階段路徑走查，分列辨識和移動時間。疏散模型保留人口、速度分布及出口狀態，演練改動由營運與防災責任者批准，教材算例不得當作現場指揮程序。","textEn":"For Laerdal Tunnel, the required evacuation time handover must address the following evidence: Walk the current stage route and separate recognition from movement time. Retain population, speed distribution and exit states; operations and fire-safety owners approve drill changes, and classroom calculations are not incident-command procedures.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「疏散時間與分區可用性」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Evacuation time and zone availability\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","沿現行施工階段路徑走查，分列辨識和移動時間。","風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Walk the current stage route and separate recognition from movement time.","Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel."],"answer":1,"explanation":"沿現行施工階段路徑走查，分列辨識和移動時間。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Walk the current stage route and separate recognition from movement time. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b111-v14-32","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性：失效診斷","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b111-v14-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「所需疏散時間」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Required evacuation time” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只使用完工後地圖可能把人引入尚未恢復的區段。以最快成人速度套全部旅客會低估需求，若忽略接收孔受煙或車流影響，疏散可能移到另一個危險邊界。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A final-layout map can direct users into an unrestored section. Applying the fastest adult speed to everyone understates demand; overlooking smoke or traffic in the receiving bore can transfer evacuees into another hazard. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：人員速度會受煙熱、能見度及行動能力影響，安全判斷還要比較可用安全時間；橫通道存在但門或鄰孔不可用時，圖上的最短路線不一定能作實際選擇。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A passage shown on a plan may be unusable because its door or receiving bore is unavailable, invalidating the nominal shortest route.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b111-v14-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只使用完工後地圖可能把人引入尚未恢復的區段。以最快成人速度套全部旅客會低估需求，若忽略接收孔受煙或車流影響，疏散可能移到另一個危險邊界。","textEn":"A final-layout map can direct users into an unrestored section. Applying the fastest adult speed to everyone understates demand; overlooking smoke or traffic in the receiving bore can transfer evacuees into another hazard.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b111-v14-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「疏散時間與分區可用性」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Evacuation time and zone availability\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。","只使用完工後地圖可能把人引入尚未恢復的區段。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety.","A final-layout map can direct users into an unrestored section."],"answer":2,"explanation":"只使用完工後地圖可能把人引入尚未恢復的區段。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A final-layout map can direct users into an unrestored section. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b111-v14-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「設備備援與共同失效」與「資產編碼與可追溯交接」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Equipment redundancy and common failure\" and \"Asset identity and traceable handover\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b111-v14-33","title":"設備備援與共同失效：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Equipment redundancy and common failure: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b111-v14-32"],"objective":"說明「系統不可用率」如何影響拉爾達隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “System unavailability” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Laerdal Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"更新期間臨時電源與永久控制可能共用上游供電，研究切換成功與真正冗餘的差別。兩套設備只有在故障近似獨立且切換可靠時，並聯才顯著降低不可用率。共用配電、控制軟體、冷卻或受淹位置會把獨立假設破壞；維修停用也改變當下配置，因此可靠度模型必須明列共有資源和設備狀態，不能只數備用台數。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「系統不可用率」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Temporary power and permanent controls may share an upstream source; distinguish successful transfer from genuine redundancy. Parallel equipment sharply reduces unavailability only when failures are approximately independent and transfer works. Shared power, software, cooling or flood exposure breaks that assumption. Planned maintenance also changes the available configuration, so reliability models must identify shared resources and states rather than count spare units or multiply unsupported independent probabilities. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “System unavailability” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：單機不可用率=0.02 無因次。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: single-unit unavailability=0.02 dimensionless.","failure":"常見誤解：「設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「系統不可用率」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “System unavailability”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b111-v14-33-k1","title":"設備備援與共同失效","titleEn":"Equipment redundancy and common failure","text":"更新期間臨時電源與永久控制可能共用上游供電，研究切換成功與真正冗餘的差別。兩套設備只有在故障近似獨立且切換可靠時，並聯才顯著降低不可用率。","textEn":"Temporary power and permanent controls may share an upstream source; distinguish successful transfer from genuine redundancy. Parallel equipment sharply reduces unavailability only when failures are approximately independent and transfer works.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b111-v14-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「設備備援與共同失效」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Equipment redundancy and common failure\" is correct?","options":["更新期間臨時電源與永久控制可能共用上游供電，研究切換成功與真正冗餘的差別。","設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。"],"optionsEn":["Temporary power and permanent controls may share an upstream source; distinguish successful transfer from genuine redundancy.","Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted."],"answer":0,"explanation":"更新期間臨時電源與永久控制可能共用上游供電，研究切換成功與真正冗餘的差別。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Temporary power and permanent controls may share an upstream source; distinguish successful transfer from genuine redundancy. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b111-v14-34","title":"設備備援與共同失效：定量估算","titleEn":"Equipment redundancy and common failure: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b111-v14-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「系統不可用率」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “System unavailability” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：單機不可用率=0.02 無因次。Uparallel=U²=0.0004 probability。僅把單機不可用率增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.000484 probability。邊界：完全獨立並聯與完美切換，不含共同失效；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: single-unit unavailability=0.02 dimensionless. Uparallel=U²=0.0004 probability. Increasing only single-unit unavailability by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.000484 probability. Boundary: Independent parallel units with perfect transfer, excluding common failures. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：追查每條電源到上游共同點並核對失電測試。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Trace feeds to shared upstream points and check outage tests.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b111-v14-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：單機不可用率=0.02 無因次。Uparallel=U²=0.0004 probability。僅把單機不可用率增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.000484 probability。邊界：完全獨立並聯與完美切換，不含共同失效；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: single-unit unavailability=0.02 dimensionless. Uparallel=U²=0.0004 probability. Increasing only single-unit unavailability by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.000484 probability. Boundary: Independent parallel units with perfect transfer, excluding common failures. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b111-v14-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「設備備援與共同失效」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Equipment redundancy and common failure\", which statement holds?","options":["知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。","原創教學假設：單機不可用率=0.02 無因次。","照度越高就必然使隧道內所有物體更容易辨識。"],"optionsEn":["Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction.","Original teaching assumptions: single-unit unavailability=0.02 dimensionless.","Higher illuminance necessarily makes every tunnel object easier to detect."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：單機不可用率=0.02 無因次。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: single-unit unavailability=0.02 dimensionless. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b111-v14-35","title":"設備備援與共同失效：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Equipment redundancy and common failure: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b111-v14-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「系統不可用率」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “System unavailability” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"追查每條電源到上游共同點並核對失電測試。由設備清單畫出故障樹，將電源、控制及實體位置追到共同節點，並用事件及維修紀錄檢查獨立假設。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Trace feeds to shared upstream points and check outage tests. Build a fault tree from the asset list, trace power, control and location to shared nodes, and test independence against incident and maintenance records. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「系統不可用率」的交付需回答：追查每條電源到上游共同點並核對失電測試。維修計畫附當日可用配置與剩餘備援，任何共同資源更動同步更新故障樹，切換試驗由設備及營運團隊共同見證。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Laerdal Tunnel, the system unavailability handover must address the following evidence: Trace feeds to shared upstream points and check outage tests. Attach the actual configuration and remaining redundancy to maintenance plans, update fault trees after shared-resource changes, and witness transfer tests jointly.","failure":"注意干擾：兩條電纜共用同一配電盤不能假設失效獨立。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Two cables on one board do not justify independent-failure assumptions. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b111-v14-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"追查每條電源到上游共同點並核對失電測試。由設備清單畫出故障樹，將電源、控制及實體位置追到共同節點，並用事件及維修紀錄檢查獨立假設。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Trace feeds to shared upstream points and check outage tests. Build a fault tree from the asset list, trace power, control and location to shared nodes, and test independence against incident and maintenance records. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b111-v14-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「系統不可用率」的交付需回答：追查每條電源到上游共同點並核對失電測試。維修計畫附當日可用配置與剩餘備援，任何共同資源更動同步更新故障樹，切換試驗由設備及營運團隊共同見證。","textEn":"For Laerdal Tunnel, the system unavailability handover must address the following evidence: Trace feeds to shared upstream points and check outage tests. Attach the actual configuration and remaining redundancy to maintenance plans, update fault trees after shared-resource changes, and witness transfer tests jointly.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「設備備援與共同失效」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Equipment redundancy and common failure\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。","追查每條電源到上游共同點並核對失電測試。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.","Trace feeds to shared upstream points and check outage tests."],"answer":2,"explanation":"追查每條電源到上游共同點並核對失電測試。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Trace feeds to shared upstream points and check outage tests. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b111-v14-36","title":"設備備援與共同失效：失效診斷","titleEn":"Equipment redundancy and common failure: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b111-v14-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「系統不可用率」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “System unavailability” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"兩條電纜共用同一配電盤不能假設失效獨立。重複安裝卻共用單一供電可能在一次故障中全部停機，帳面可靠度很高但實際不可用時間沒有降低。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Two cables on one board do not justify independent-failure assumptions. Duplicated equipment on one supply can fail together in a single event, leaving actual downtime unchanged despite optimistic calculated reliability. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：共用配電、控制軟體、冷卻或受淹位置會把獨立假設破壞；維修停用也改變當下配置，因此可靠度模型必須明列共有資源和設備狀態，不能只數備用台數。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Planned maintenance also changes the available configuration, so reliability models must identify shared resources and states rather than count spare units or multiply unsupported independent probabilities.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b111-v14-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"兩條電纜共用同一配電盤不能假設失效獨立。重複安裝卻共用單一供電可能在一次故障中全部停機，帳面可靠度很高但實際不可用時間沒有降低。","textEn":"Two cables on one board do not justify independent-failure assumptions. Duplicated equipment on one supply can fail together in a single event, leaving actual downtime unchanged despite optimistic calculated reliability.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b111-v14-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「設備備援與共同失效」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Equipment redundancy and common failure\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["兩條電纜共用同一配電盤不能假設失效獨立。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。"],"optionsEn":["Two cables on one board do not justify independent-failure assumptions.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted."],"answer":0,"explanation":"兩條電纜共用同一配電盤不能假設失效獨立。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Two cables on one board do not justify independent-failure assumptions. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b111-v14-37","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b111-v14-36"],"objective":"說明「資產資料完整度」如何影響拉爾達隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Asset-record completeness” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Laerdal Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"拉爾達更新資料需保留舊新設備並存期間的狀態，避免竣工資料提前覆蓋仍在服務的舊系統。地下設備的竣工資料必須讓維護人員找到正確位置、材料批次和控制版本。只有上傳圖面而沒有變更歷程，無法分辨元件替換與真正劣化；告警、儀器、線路及工單使用一致識別碼，才可能把量測趨勢連回實際受力或水力系統。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「資產資料完整度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Maintain coexistence states during renewal so new as-built records do not overwrite still-operating legacy systems prematurely. Handover must let maintainers find the correct location, material batch and control revision. Drawings without change history cannot distinguish replacement from deterioration. Consistent identifiers across alarms, instruments, circuits and work orders are essential for linking trends to the physical structural or hydraulic system instead of treating each record as an isolated file. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Asset-record completeness” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：設備總數=110 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: asset count=110 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=85.4545 %.","failure":"常見誤解：「全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「資產資料完整度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Asset-record completeness”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b111-v14-37-k1","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover","text":"拉爾達更新資料需保留舊新設備並存期間的狀態，避免竣工資料提前覆蓋仍在服務的舊系統。地下設備的竣工資料必須讓維護人員找到正確位置、材料批次和控制版本。","textEn":"Maintain coexistence states during renewal so new as-built records do not overwrite still-operating legacy systems prematurely. Handover must let maintainers find the correct location, material batch and control revision.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b111-v14-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「資產編碼與可追溯交接」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Asset identity and traceable handover\" is correct?","options":["全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。","拉爾達更新資料需保留舊新設備並存期間的狀態，避免竣工資料提前覆蓋仍在服務的舊系統。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.","Maintain coexistence states during renewal so new as-built records do not overwrite still-operating legacy systems prematurely.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":1,"explanation":"拉爾達更新資料需保留舊新設備並存期間的狀態，避免竣工資料提前覆蓋仍在服務的舊系統。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Maintain coexistence states during renewal so new as-built records do not overwrite still-operating legacy systems prematurely. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b111-v14-38","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：定量估算","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b111-v14-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「資產資料完整度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Asset-record completeness” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：設備總數=110 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。coverage=100(N−missing)/N=85.4545 %。僅把缺紀錄數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為84 %。邊界：資料完整度，不等於安全或可靠度；擾動為連續敏感度，實際個數為整數；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: asset count=110 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=85.4545 %. Increasing only missing records by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 84 %. Boundary: Record completeness, not safety or reliability; perturbation is continuous sensitivity while actual counts are integers. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：抽查切換日期前後的設備狀態與控制位址。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check asset state and control address before and after transfer dates.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b111-v14-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：設備總數=110 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。coverage=100(N−missing)/N=85.4545 %。僅把缺紀錄數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為84 %。邊界：資料完整度，不等於安全或可靠度；擾動為連續敏感度，實際個數為整數；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: asset count=110 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=85.4545 %. Increasing only missing records by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 84 %. Boundary: Record completeness, not safety or reliability; perturbation is continuous sensitivity while actual counts are integers. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b111-v14-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「資產編碼與可追溯交接」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Asset identity and traceable handover\", which statement holds?","options":["支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。","風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。","原創教學假設：設備總數=110 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。"],"optionsEn":["Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem.","Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.","Original teaching assumptions: asset count=110 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=85.4545 %."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：設備總數=110 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: asset count=110 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=85.4545 %. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b111-v14-39","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b111-v14-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「資產資料完整度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Asset-record completeness” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"抽查切換日期前後的設備狀態與控制位址。抽取一條告警，從控制畫面追到設備、線路、圖面和工單，核對位置、版本及校正日期並記錄無法閉合的欄位。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check asset state and control address before and after transfer dates. Trace a sampled alarm from screen to equipment, circuit, drawing and work order, checking location, revision and calibration dates and recording broken links. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「資產資料完整度」的交付需回答：抽查切換日期前後的設備狀態與控制位址。交接以可完成的定位、查找與復原任務驗證，由維護責任人確認現場可用性；完整度只是資料指標，不代表結構安全或設備可靠。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Laerdal Tunnel, the asset-record completeness handover must address the following evidence: Check asset state and control address before and after transfer dates. Validate handover through achievable location, retrieval and recovery tasks witnessed by maintainers; completeness measures records, not structural safety or equipment reliability.","failure":"注意干擾：提前標記已更新會讓維修人員找不到實際在線設備。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Premature completion status leaves maintainers unable to identify the online asset. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b111-v14-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"抽查切換日期前後的設備狀態與控制位址。抽取一條告警，從控制畫面追到設備、線路、圖面和工單，核對位置、版本及校正日期並記錄無法閉合的欄位。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Check asset state and control address before and after transfer dates. Trace a sampled alarm from screen to equipment, circuit, drawing and work order, checking location, revision and calibration dates and recording broken links. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b111-v14-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「資產資料完整度」的交付需回答：抽查切換日期前後的設備狀態與控制位址。交接以可完成的定位、查找與復原任務驗證，由維護責任人確認現場可用性；完整度只是資料指標，不代表結構安全或設備可靠。","textEn":"For Laerdal Tunnel, the asset-record completeness handover must address the following evidence: Check asset state and control address before and after transfer dates. Validate handover through achievable location, retrieval and recovery tasks witnessed by maintainers; completeness measures records, not structural safety or equipment reliability.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「資產編碼與可追溯交接」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Asset identity and traceable handover\"?","options":["抽查切換日期前後的設備狀態與控制位址。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。"],"optionsEn":["Check asset state and control address before and after transfer dates.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly."],"answer":0,"explanation":"抽查切換日期前後的設備狀態與控制位址。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check asset state and control address before and after transfer dates. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b111-v14-40","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：失效診斷","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b111-v14-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「資產資料完整度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Asset-record completeness” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"提前標記已更新會讓維修人員找不到實際在線設備。設備改名卻未更新控制畫面會引導人員隔離錯誤回路，材料批次缺漏則使同批缺陷無法追蹤到其他位置。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Premature completion status leaves maintainers unable to identify the online asset. Renaming an asset without updating the screen can isolate the wrong circuit; missing material batches prevent tracing related defects at other locations. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：只有上傳圖面而沒有變更歷程，無法分辨元件替換與真正劣化；告警、儀器、線路及工單使用一致識別碼，才可能把量測趨勢連回實際受力或水力系統。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Consistent identifiers across alarms, instruments, circuits and work orders are essential for linking trends to the physical structural or hydraulic system instead of treating each record as an isolated file.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b111-v14-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"提前標記已更新會讓維修人員找不到實際在線設備。設備改名卻未更新控制畫面會引導人員隔離錯誤回路，材料批次缺漏則使同批缺陷無法追蹤到其他位置。","textEn":"Premature completion status leaves maintainers unable to identify the online asset. Renaming an asset without updating the screen can isolate the wrong circuit; missing material batches prevent tracing related defects at other locations.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b111-v14-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「資產編碼與可追溯交接」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Asset identity and traceable handover\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","提前標記已更新會讓維修人員找不到實際在線設備。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Premature completion status leaves maintainers unable to identify the online asset.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":1,"explanation":"提前標記已更新會讓維修人員找不到實際在線設備。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Premature completion status leaves maintainers unable to identify the online asset. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b111","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"curriculumVersion":14,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000},{"id":"b112","title":"聖哥達公路隧道","titleEn":"Gotthard Road Tunnel","category":"underground","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"聖哥達公路隧道自1980年營運，瑞士公路主管機關說明第二孔16.9公里路線用於支持原孔整修，並強調計畫不增加交通容量。本課由這個限制出發，分析雙孔隔離、共用服務坑、岩體擾動和分期切換，將新增土建空間與營運容量清楚區分。","summaryEn":"Gotthard Road Tunnel has operated since 1980. FEDRO describes a 16.9 km second-tube alignment supporting refurbishment of the first tube without increasing traffic capacity. Starting from that constraint, this course examines bore isolation, shared service infrastructure, rock disturbance and staged transfer, distinguishing new civil space from operational capacity.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"ug-landmarks","subcategoryTitle":"世界隧道與地下巨作","subcategoryTitleEn":"World tunnels and underground landmarks","learningTrack":"underground","learningSubdiscipline":"ug-landmarks","learningTags":["underground","ug-landmarks","tunnel"],"architectureFamily":"tunnel","architectureNodes":[["路線里程與端點","Alignment chainage and endpoints"],["破碎帶連通性","Fault-zone connectivity"],["支護安裝時點","Support activation time"],["出渣運輸節拍","Muck-transport cycle"],["風道摩擦壓損","Duct friction loss"],["資產資料完整度","Asset-record completeness"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,5],[1,5]],"diagram":{"type":"tunnel","labels":["路線里程與端點","破碎帶連通性","支護安裝時點","出渣運輸節拍","風道摩擦壓損"],"labelsEn":["Alignment chainage and endpoints","Fault-zone connectivity","Support activation time","Muck-transport cycle","Duct friction loss"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"原創綜合審查：先計算「破碎帶連通與預報更新」，再獨立計算「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」。原創教學假設：滲透係數=2e-06 m/s；水力坡降=2.1 無因次；通水面積=310 m²。Q=k i A=0.001302 m³/s。僅把滲透係數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.0014322 m³/s。邊界：均質飽和達西流，不代表裂隙集中流；不是本工程實測或允收值。原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=31 t；往返週期=35 min。C=N payload 60/T=212.571 t/h。僅把往返週期增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為193.247 t/h。邊界：無排隊理想循環，並非共享路段實際產能；不是本工程實測或允收值。兩組結果的單位與邊界不同，不能直接相加。請列出一項缺少的現場輸入，說明它會影響哪個結論，以及哪種獨立量測可以縮小不確定度。","textEn":"Original integrated review: first calculate fault connectivity and forecast updating, then independently calculate shared access and transport bottlenecks. Original teaching assumptions: conductivity=2e-06 m/s; hydraulic gradient=2.1 dimensionless; flow area=310 m². Q=k i A=0.001302 m³/s. Increasing only conductivity by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.0014322 m³/s. Boundary: Homogeneous saturated Darcy flow, not concentrated fracture flow. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=31 t; cycle=35 min. C=N payload 60/T=212.571 t/h. Increasing only cycle by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 193.247 t/h. Boundary: Ideal cycle without queues, not actual shared-route production. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. The outputs have different units and boundaries and cannot simply be added. Identify one missing field input, explain which conclusion it changes and select an independent measurement to reduce uncertainty.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":14,"enrichmentVersion":14,"stages":[{"id":"b112-v14-s1","title":"地層條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Ground conditions, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「服務邊界與路線代價」與「破碎帶連通與預報更新」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\" and \"Fault connectivity and forecast updating\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b112-v14-01","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「路線里程與端點」如何影響聖哥達公路隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Alignment chainage and endpoints” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Gotthard Road Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"聖哥達第二孔提供整修替代路徑，教學先把物理車道與核准營運容量分開，不以洞孔數推估交通量。隧道選線同時改變洞口、覆土與縱坡，短路線不保證低地質風險。比較方案必須使用相同起訖點，並分開主孔、引道及服務坑的工程數量；交通時間只是需求的一個指標，不能代替施工可達性或長期維修評估。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「路線里程與端點」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The second tube enables refurbishment; distinguish physical lanes from approved operating capacity rather than inferring flow from bore count. Alignment changes portals, cover and gradient together, so a shorter tunnel need not have lower geological risk. Compare options between identical endpoints and distinguish running bores, approaches and service galleries. Travel time measures one service benefit but cannot replace assessment of construction access, maintenance closures or exposure to uncertain ground. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Alignment chainage and endpoints” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：長度=16.4 km；速度=60 km/h。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: length=16.4 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=16.4 min.","failure":"常見誤解：「最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「路線里程與端點」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Alignment chainage and endpoints”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b112-v14-01-k1","title":"服務邊界與路線代價","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost","text":"聖哥達第二孔提供整修替代路徑，教學先把物理車道與核准營運容量分開，不以洞孔數推估交通量。隧道選線同時改變洞口、覆土與縱坡，短路線不保證低地質風險。","textEn":"The second tube enables refurbishment; distinguish physical lanes from approved operating capacity rather than inferring flow from bore count. Alignment changes portals, cover and gradient together, so a shorter tunnel need not have lower geological risk.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b112-v14-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「服務邊界與路線代價」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\" is correct?","options":["最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。","聖哥達第二孔提供整修替代路徑，教學先把物理車道與核准營運容量分開，不以洞孔數推估交通量。","岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。"],"optionsEn":["The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.","The second tube enables refurbishment; distinguish physical lanes from approved operating capacity rather than inferring flow from bore count.","Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow."],"answer":1,"explanation":"聖哥達第二孔提供整修替代路徑，教學先把物理車道與核准營運容量分開，不以洞孔數推估交通量。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The second tube enables refurbishment; distinguish physical lanes from approved operating capacity rather than inferring flow from bore count. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b112-v14-02","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：定量估算","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b112-v14-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「路線里程與端點」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Alignment chainage and endpoints” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：長度=16.4 km；速度=60 km/h。t=60L/v=16.4 min。僅把長度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為18.04 min。邊界：假想交通旅程，未含加減速、排隊及實際時刻表；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: length=16.4 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=16.4 min. Increasing only length by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 18.04 min. Boundary: Hypothetical transport journey excluding acceleration, queues and the real timetable. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將各階段可開放車道和工程封閉狀態列成表。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Tabulate usable lanes and work closures by stage.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b112-v14-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：長度=16.4 km；速度=60 km/h。t=60L/v=16.4 min。僅把長度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為18.04 min。邊界：假想交通旅程，未含加減速、排隊及實際時刻表；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: length=16.4 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=16.4 min. Increasing only length by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 18.04 min. Boundary: Hypothetical transport journey excluding acceleration, queues and the real timetable. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b112-v14-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「服務邊界與路線代價」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\", which statement holds?","options":["支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。","增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。","原創教學假設：長度=16.4 km；速度=60 km/h。"],"optionsEn":["Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem.","Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.","Original teaching assumptions: length=16.4 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=16.4 min."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：長度=16.4 km；速度=60 km/h。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: length=16.4 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=16.4 min. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b112-v14-03","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b112-v14-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「路線里程與端點」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Alignment chainage and endpoints” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將各階段可開放車道和工程封閉狀態列成表。把縱斷面、地形與地質剖面疊合，以端點坐標獨立反算距離，再將主孔與支坑數量分開核對。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Tabulate usable lanes and work closures by stage. Overlay the longitudinal profile, terrain and geology; independently derive distances from endpoint coordinates and reconcile running-bore and gallery quantities separately. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「路線里程與端點」的交付需回答：將各階段可開放車道和工程封閉狀態列成表。在方案表中凍結起訖點、計量範圍及地質假設，任何改線都要同步更新高程、數量與服務情境，不能只替換總長。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Gotthard Road Tunnel, the alignment chainage and endpoints handover must address the following evidence: Tabulate usable lanes and work closures by stage. Freeze endpoints, measurement scope and ground assumptions in the option register; realignment requires coordinated updates to elevations, quantities and service scenarios rather than replacing one length.","failure":"注意干擾：兩孔存在不等於可同時開放全部車道。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Two physical bores do not imply every lane can operate simultaneously. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b112-v14-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將各階段可開放車道和工程封閉狀態列成表。把縱斷面、地形與地質剖面疊合，以端點坐標獨立反算距離，再將主孔與支坑數量分開核對。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Tabulate usable lanes and work closures by stage. Overlay the longitudinal profile, terrain and geology; independently derive distances from endpoint coordinates and reconcile running-bore and gallery quantities separately. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b112-v14-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「路線里程與端點」的交付需回答：將各階段可開放車道和工程封閉狀態列成表。在方案表中凍結起訖點、計量範圍及地質假設，任何改線都要同步更新高程、數量與服務情境，不能只替換總長。","textEn":"For Gotthard Road Tunnel, the alignment chainage and endpoints handover must address the following evidence: Tabulate usable lanes and work closures by stage. Freeze endpoints, measurement scope and ground assumptions in the option register; realignment requires coordinated updates to elevations, quantities and service scenarios rather than replacing one length.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「服務邊界與路線代價」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\"?","options":["將各階段可開放車道和工程封閉狀態列成表。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。"],"optionsEn":["Tabulate usable lanes and work closures by stage.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將各階段可開放車道和工程封閉狀態列成表。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Tabulate usable lanes and work closures by stage. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b112-v14-04","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：失效診斷","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b112-v14-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「路線里程與端點」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Alignment chainage and endpoints” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"兩孔存在不等於可同時開放全部車道。混用全線與單孔長度會同時扭曲工程數量、行程及逃生距離，造成方案比較失去共同基準。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Two physical bores do not imply every lane can operate simultaneously. Mixing whole-route and single-bore lengths distorts quantities, journey time and escape distance, destroying the common basis of an option comparison. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：比較方案必須使用相同起訖點，並分開主孔、引道及服務坑的工程數量；交通時間只是需求的一個指標，不能代替施工可達性或長期維修評估。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Travel time measures one service benefit but cannot replace assessment of construction access, maintenance closures or exposure to uncertain ground.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b112-v14-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"兩孔存在不等於可同時開放全部車道。混用全線與單孔長度會同時扭曲工程數量、行程及逃生距離，造成方案比較失去共同基準。","textEn":"Two physical bores do not imply every lane can operate simultaneously. Mixing whole-route and single-bore lengths distorts quantities, journey time and escape distance, destroying the common basis of an option comparison.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b112-v14-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「服務邊界與路線代價」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","兩孔存在不等於可同時開放全部車道。","岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Two physical bores do not imply every lane can operate simultaneously.","Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow."],"answer":1,"explanation":"兩孔存在不等於可同時開放全部車道。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Two physical bores do not imply every lane can operate simultaneously. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b112-v14-05","title":"破碎帶連通與預報更新：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Fault connectivity and forecast updating: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b112-v14-04"],"objective":"說明「破碎帶連通性」如何影響聖哥達公路隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Fault-zone connectivity” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Gotthard Road Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"新孔與舊孔平行仍可能遇不同節理，聖哥達教材檢查以既有孔資料外推到側向距離的限制。斷層帶可以含很硬的岩塊，但整體變形與湧水常由填充節理和連通裂隙控制。單一岩芯強度不能代表整個掌子面；超前鑽孔、出水變化與揭露地質須回饋同一里程模型，預報則應保留不同情境及其證據權重。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「破碎帶連通性」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Parallel new and old bores may intercept different joints; examine limits on laterally extrapolating existing-bore records. A fault zone may contain strong intact blocks while filled joints and connected fractures govern its bulk deformation and inflow. One core strength does not represent the entire face. Probe records, water response and exposed geology must update a common chainage model, preserving competing interpretations and their evidential weight rather than treating a forecast as certainty. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Fault-zone connectivity” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：滲透係數=2e-06 m/s；水力坡降=2.1 無因次；通水面積=310 m²。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: conductivity=2e-06 m/s; hydraulic gradient=2.1 dimensionless; flow area=310 m².","failure":"常見誤解：「岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「破碎帶連通性」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Fault-zone connectivity”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b112-v14-05-k1","title":"破碎帶連通與預報更新","titleEn":"Fault connectivity and forecast updating","text":"新孔與舊孔平行仍可能遇不同節理，聖哥達教材檢查以既有孔資料外推到側向距離的限制。斷層帶可以含很硬的岩塊，但整體變形與湧水常由填充節理和連通裂隙控制。","textEn":"Parallel new and old bores may intercept different joints; examine limits on laterally extrapolating existing-bore records. A fault zone may contain strong intact blocks while filled joints and connected fractures govern its bulk deformation and inflow.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b112-v14-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「破碎帶連通與預報更新」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Fault connectivity and forecast updating\" is correct?","options":["岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。","知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。","新孔與舊孔平行仍可能遇不同節理，聖哥達教材檢查以既有孔資料外推到側向距離的限制。"],"optionsEn":["Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow.","Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction.","Parallel new and old bores may intercept different joints; examine limits on laterally extrapolating existing-bore records."],"answer":2,"explanation":"新孔與舊孔平行仍可能遇不同節理，聖哥達教材檢查以既有孔資料外推到側向距離的限制。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Parallel new and old bores may intercept different joints; examine limits on laterally extrapolating existing-bore records. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b112-v14-06","title":"破碎帶連通與預報更新：定量估算","titleEn":"Fault connectivity and forecast updating: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b112-v14-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「破碎帶連通性」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Fault-zone connectivity” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：滲透係數=2e-06 m/s；水力坡降=2.1 無因次；通水面積=310 m²。Q=k i A=0.001302 m³/s。僅把滲透係數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.0014322 m³/s。邊界：均質飽和達西流，不代表裂隙集中流；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: conductivity=2e-06 m/s; hydraulic gradient=2.1 dimensionless; flow area=310 m². Q=k i A=0.001302 m³/s. Increasing only conductivity by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.0014322 m³/s. Boundary: Homogeneous saturated Darcy flow, not concentrated fracture flow. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：對照舊孔地質與新探孔差異，保留未證實延伸。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare old exposures with new probes and retain uncertain persistence.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b112-v14-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：滲透係數=2e-06 m/s；水力坡降=2.1 無因次；通水面積=310 m²。Q=k i A=0.001302 m³/s。僅把滲透係數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.0014322 m³/s。邊界：均質飽和達西流，不代表裂隙集中流；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: conductivity=2e-06 m/s; hydraulic gradient=2.1 dimensionless; flow area=310 m². Q=k i A=0.001302 m³/s. Increasing only conductivity by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.0014322 m³/s. Boundary: Homogeneous saturated Darcy flow, not concentrated fracture flow. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b112-v14-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「破碎帶連通與預報更新」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Fault connectivity and forecast updating\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：滲透係數=2e-06 m/s；水力坡降=2.1 無因次；通水面積=310 m²。","目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: conductivity=2e-06 m/s; hydraulic gradient=2.1 dimensionless; flow area=310 m².","No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：滲透係數=2e-06 m/s；水力坡降=2.1 無因次；通水面積=310 m²。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: conductivity=2e-06 m/s; hydraulic gradient=2.1 dimensionless; flow area=310 m². Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b112-v14-07","title":"破碎帶連通與預報更新：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Fault connectivity and forecast updating: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b112-v14-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「破碎帶連通性」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Fault-zone connectivity” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"對照舊孔地質與新探孔差異，保留未證實延伸。將岩心回收、裂隙方位與出水曲線按里程對齊，用未參與建模的孔段作交叉檢驗，檢查是否只擬合已知資料。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare old exposures with new probes and retain uncertain persistence. Align recovery, fracture orientation and inflow by chainage; test the interpretation against a withheld borehole interval to detect fitting only the known observations. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「破碎帶連通性」的交付需回答：對照舊孔地質與新探孔差異，保留未證實延伸。每次地質模型更新保留舊版與新增證據，差異由地質及支護設計者共同判讀，施工條件改變需重新確認核准範圍。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Gotthard Road Tunnel, the fault-zone connectivity handover must address the following evidence: Compare old exposures with new probes and retain uncertain persistence. Retain previous interpretations and new evidence at every update; geology and support designers jointly interpret differences and reconfirm approved bounds when ground conditions change.","failure":"注意干擾：把舊孔地質直接平移可能漏掉斜交破碎帶。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Direct lateral copying can miss oblique fault zones. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b112-v14-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"對照舊孔地質與新探孔差異，保留未證實延伸。將岩心回收、裂隙方位與出水曲線按里程對齊，用未參與建模的孔段作交叉檢驗，檢查是否只擬合已知資料。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Compare old exposures with new probes and retain uncertain persistence. Align recovery, fracture orientation and inflow by chainage; test the interpretation against a withheld borehole interval to detect fitting only the known observations. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b112-v14-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「破碎帶連通性」的交付需回答：對照舊孔地質與新探孔差異，保留未證實延伸。每次地質模型更新保留舊版與新增證據，差異由地質及支護設計者共同判讀，施工條件改變需重新確認核准範圍。","textEn":"For Gotthard Road Tunnel, the fault-zone connectivity handover must address the following evidence: Compare old exposures with new probes and retain uncertain persistence. Retain previous interpretations and new evidence at every update; geology and support designers jointly interpret differences and reconfirm approved bounds when ground conditions change.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「破碎帶連通與預報更新」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Fault connectivity and forecast updating\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","對照舊孔地質與新探孔差異，保留未證實延伸。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Compare old exposures with new probes and retain uncertain persistence.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time."],"answer":1,"explanation":"對照舊孔地質與新探孔差異，保留未證實延伸。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare old exposures with new probes and retain uncertain persistence. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b112-v14-08","title":"破碎帶連通與預報更新：失效診斷","titleEn":"Fault connectivity and forecast updating: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b112-v14-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「破碎帶連通性」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Fault-zone connectivity” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把舊孔地質直接平移可能漏掉斜交破碎帶。只用完整岩石強度會漏掉軟弱填充物，可能在看似堅硬的地層中出現收斂加快、支護過載或水量突增。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Direct lateral copying can miss oblique fault zones. Intact strength alone misses weak infill, allowing accelerating convergence, support overload or sudden inflow in ground that superficially appears strong. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：單一岩芯強度不能代表整個掌子面；超前鑽孔、出水變化與揭露地質須回饋同一里程模型，預報則應保留不同情境及其證據權重。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Probe records, water response and exposed geology must update a common chainage model, preserving competing interpretations and their evidential weight rather than treating a forecast as certainty.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b112-v14-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把舊孔地質直接平移可能漏掉斜交破碎帶。只用完整岩石強度會漏掉軟弱填充物，可能在看似堅硬的地層中出現收斂加快、支護過載或水量突增。","textEn":"Direct lateral copying can miss oblique fault zones. Intact strength alone misses weak infill, allowing accelerating convergence, support overload or sudden inflow in ground that superficially appears strong.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b112-v14-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「破碎帶連通與預報更新」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Fault connectivity and forecast updating\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。","把舊孔地質直接平移可能漏掉斜交破碎帶。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction.","Direct lateral copying can miss oblique fault zones."],"answer":2,"explanation":"把舊孔地質直接平移可能漏掉斜交破碎帶。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Direct lateral copying can miss oblique fault zones. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b112-v14-s2","title":"機制、材料與定量設計","titleEn":"Mechanisms, materials and quantitative design","description":"本階段聚焦「覆土應力與洞壁重分配」與「支護啟動與變形容量」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Cover stress and wall redistribution\" and \"Support activation and deformation capacity\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b112-v14-09","title":"覆土應力與洞壁重分配：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Cover stress and wall redistribution: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b112-v14-08"],"objective":"說明「洞壁切向應力」如何影響聖哥達公路隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Tangential wall stress” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Gotthard Road Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"新開挖改變舊孔周圍應力，研究兩孔與服務坑相互作用而非把每孔當無限岩體中的孤立圓孔。開挖使岩體洞壁失去徑向拘束，遠場荷載轉移到周圍岩體，局部切向應力可能升高。圓孔彈性解可辨識量級，但節理、非圓斷面、塑性區與原位應力比會改變峰值位置，不能只用覆土重量推定全部三維應力。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「洞壁切向應力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"New excavation changes stress around the existing bore; examine interaction with the service gallery rather than isolated holes in infinite rock. Excavation removes radial confinement at the wall and transfers load through the surrounding rock, potentially raising local tangential stress. An elastic circular-hole solution identifies scale, but joints, noncircular geometry, yielding and the in-situ stress ratio alter the peak location. Cover weight alone cannot establish the complete three-dimensional stress state or support demand. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Tangential wall stress” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：覆土深度=830 m；岩體單位重=26 kN/m³。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: cover=830 m; rock unit weight=26 kN/m³. σθ,max=3γH/1000=64.74 MPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「洞壁切向應力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Tangential wall stress”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b112-v14-09-k1","title":"覆土應力與洞壁重分配","titleEn":"Cover stress and wall redistribution","text":"新開挖改變舊孔周圍應力，研究兩孔與服務坑相互作用而非把每孔當無限岩體中的孤立圓孔。開挖使岩體洞壁失去徑向拘束，遠場荷載轉移到周圍岩體，局部切向應力可能升高。","textEn":"New excavation changes stress around the existing bore; examine interaction with the service gallery rather than isolated holes in infinite rock. Excavation removes radial confinement at the wall and transfers load through the surrounding rock, potentially raising local tangential stress.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b112-v14-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「覆土應力與洞壁重分配」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Cover stress and wall redistribution\" is correct?","options":["新開挖改變舊孔周圍應力，研究兩孔與服務坑相互作用而非把每孔當無限岩體中的孤立圓孔。","知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。","支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。"],"optionsEn":["New excavation changes stress around the existing bore; examine interaction with the service gallery rather than isolated holes in infinite rock.","Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction.","Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem."],"answer":0,"explanation":"新開挖改變舊孔周圍應力，研究兩孔與服務坑相互作用而非把每孔當無限岩體中的孤立圓孔。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"New excavation changes stress around the existing bore; examine interaction with the service gallery rather than isolated holes in infinite rock. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b112-v14-10","title":"覆土應力與洞壁重分配：定量估算","titleEn":"Cover stress and wall redistribution: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b112-v14-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「洞壁切向應力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Tangential wall stress” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：覆土深度=830 m；岩體單位重=26 kN/m³。σθ,max=3γH/1000=64.74 MPa。僅把覆土深度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為71.214 MPa。邊界：無支承彈性圓孔，僅垂直遠場壓縮且水平遠場應力為零時，側壁最大環向壓應力；不是任意位置應力或完整三維原位解；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: cover=830 m; rock unit weight=26 kN/m³. σθ,max=3γH/1000=64.74 MPa. Increasing only cover by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 71.214 MPa. Boundary: Maximum tangential compression at the sidewalls of an unsupported elastic circular hole under vertical uniaxial remote loading with zero horizontal remote stress; not stress at any point or the complete three-dimensional in-situ state. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：跨孔布置位移與應力證據，按掌子面距離排序。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare inter-bore displacement and stress evidence by face distance.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b112-v14-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：覆土深度=830 m；岩體單位重=26 kN/m³。σθ,max=3γH/1000=64.74 MPa。僅把覆土深度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為71.214 MPa。邊界：無支承彈性圓孔，僅垂直遠場壓縮且水平遠場應力為零時，側壁最大環向壓應力；不是任意位置應力或完整三維原位解；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: cover=830 m; rock unit weight=26 kN/m³. σθ,max=3γH/1000=64.74 MPa. Increasing only cover by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 71.214 MPa. Boundary: Maximum tangential compression at the sidewalls of an unsupported elastic circular hole under vertical uniaxial remote loading with zero horizontal remote stress; not stress at any point or the complete three-dimensional in-situ state. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b112-v14-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「覆土應力與洞壁重分配」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Cover stress and wall redistribution\", which statement holds?","options":["增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。","原創教學假設：覆土深度=830 m；岩體單位重=26 kN/m³。","風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。"],"optionsEn":["Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.","Original teaching assumptions: cover=830 m; rock unit weight=26 kN/m³. σθ,max=3γH/1000=64.74 MPa.","Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：覆土深度=830 m；岩體單位重=26 kN/m³。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: cover=830 m; rock unit weight=26 kN/m³. σθ,max=3γH/1000=64.74 MPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b112-v14-11","title":"覆土應力與洞壁重分配：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Cover stress and wall redistribution: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b112-v14-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「洞壁切向應力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Tangential wall stress” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"跨孔布置位移與應力證據，按掌子面距離排序。將原位應力量測、岩石試驗及洞壁破壞方位相互比較，再用多點伸長計檢查變形是否與所假設應力方向一致。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare inter-bore displacement and stress evidence by face distance. Compare in-situ stress measurements, rock tests and wall-damage orientation, then use multipoint extensometers to test consistency with the assumed stress directions. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「洞壁切向應力」的交付需回答：跨孔布置位移與應力證據，按掌子面距離排序。保留應力模型的座標、邊界和材料假設，量測與預測不符時先核對代表性，再由岩力設計者選擇非線性或節理模型。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Gotthard Road Tunnel, the tangential wall stress handover must address the following evidence: Compare inter-bore displacement and stress evidence by face distance. Record stress-model coordinates, boundaries and material assumptions; when observations disagree, check representativeness before the rock designer selects nonlinear or jointed models.","failure":"注意干擾：孤立圓孔解會漏掉岩柱重分配與方向性。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: An isolated-hole solution omits pillar redistribution and directional effects. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b112-v14-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"跨孔布置位移與應力證據，按掌子面距離排序。將原位應力量測、岩石試驗及洞壁破壞方位相互比較，再用多點伸長計檢查變形是否與所假設應力方向一致。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Compare inter-bore displacement and stress evidence by face distance. Compare in-situ stress measurements, rock tests and wall-damage orientation, then use multipoint extensometers to test consistency with the assumed stress directions. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b112-v14-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「洞壁切向應力」的交付需回答：跨孔布置位移與應力證據，按掌子面距離排序。保留應力模型的座標、邊界和材料假設，量測與預測不符時先核對代表性，再由岩力設計者選擇非線性或節理模型。","textEn":"For Gotthard Road Tunnel, the tangential wall stress handover must address the following evidence: Compare inter-bore displacement and stress evidence by face distance. Record stress-model coordinates, boundaries and material assumptions; when observations disagree, check representativeness before the rock designer selects nonlinear or jointed models.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「覆土應力與洞壁重分配」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Cover stress and wall redistribution\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。","跨孔布置位移與應力證據，按掌子面距離排序。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.","Compare inter-bore displacement and stress evidence by face distance."],"answer":2,"explanation":"跨孔布置位移與應力證據，按掌子面距離排序。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare inter-bore displacement and stress evidence by face distance. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b112-v14-12","title":"覆土應力與洞壁重分配：失效診斷","titleEn":"Cover stress and wall redistribution: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b112-v14-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「洞壁切向應力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Tangential wall stress” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"孤立圓孔解會漏掉岩柱重分配與方向性。把彈性峰值直接當岩體強度可能誤判支護需求；相反地忽略剝落或擠壓也會讓局部破壞逐步侵入淨空。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"An isolated-hole solution omits pillar redistribution and directional effects. Equating an elastic peak with rock-mass strength misjudges support demand; overlooking spalling or squeezing lets damage progressively consume clearance. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：圓孔彈性解可辨識量級，但節理、非圓斷面、塑性區與原位應力比會改變峰值位置，不能只用覆土重量推定全部三維應力。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Cover weight alone cannot establish the complete three-dimensional stress state or support demand.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b112-v14-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"孤立圓孔解會漏掉岩柱重分配與方向性。把彈性峰值直接當岩體強度可能誤判支護需求；相反地忽略剝落或擠壓也會讓局部破壞逐步侵入淨空。","textEn":"An isolated-hole solution omits pillar redistribution and directional effects. Equating an elastic peak with rock-mass strength misjudges support demand; overlooking spalling or squeezing lets damage progressively consume clearance.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b112-v14-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「覆土應力與洞壁重分配」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Cover stress and wall redistribution\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["孤立圓孔解會漏掉岩柱重分配與方向性。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。"],"optionsEn":["An isolated-hole solution omits pillar redistribution and directional effects.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem."],"answer":0,"explanation":"孤立圓孔解會漏掉岩柱重分配與方向性。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"An isolated-hole solution omits pillar redistribution and directional effects. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b112-v14-13","title":"支護啟動與變形容量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Support activation and deformation capacity: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b112-v14-12"],"objective":"說明「支護安裝時點」如何影響聖哥達公路隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Support activation time” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Gotthard Road Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"舊孔整修時拆換構件會改變暫時支承路徑，教材把拆除、補強和重新啟用分開建模。支護荷載由開挖釋放量和支護啟動時間共同決定，越早安裝不一定讓構件受力越小。地盤反力與支護曲線必須連同掌子面距離及封閉順序理解；擠壓性地層還需保留變形容量，不能只追求高剛度與高材料強度。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「支護安裝時點」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Replacement during first-bore refurbishment changes temporary support paths; model removal, strengthening and reactivation separately. Support load depends on stress release and activation time, so earlier installation does not necessarily reduce member forces. Interpret ground-reaction and support curves together with distance from the face and closure sequence. Squeezing ground also needs deformation capacity; high stiffness and material strength alone do not guarantee a compatible support response. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Support activation time” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：局部剛度=41 kN/mm；位移=8 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: local stiffness=41 kN/mm; movement=8 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「支護安裝時點」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Support activation time”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b112-v14-13-k1","title":"支護啟動與變形容量","titleEn":"Support activation and deformation capacity","text":"舊孔整修時拆換構件會改變暫時支承路徑，教材把拆除、補強和重新啟用分開建模。支護荷載由開挖釋放量和支護啟動時間共同決定，越早安裝不一定讓構件受力越小。","textEn":"Replacement during first-bore refurbishment changes temporary support paths; model removal, strengthening and reactivation separately. Support load depends on stress release and activation time, so earlier installation does not necessarily reduce member forces.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b112-v14-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「支護啟動與變形容量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Support activation and deformation capacity\" is correct?","options":["支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。","舊孔整修時拆換構件會改變暫時支承路徑，教材把拆除、補強和重新啟用分開建模。","目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。"],"optionsEn":["Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem.","Replacement during first-bore refurbishment changes temporary support paths; model removal, strengthening and reactivation separately.","No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design."],"answer":1,"explanation":"舊孔整修時拆換構件會改變暫時支承路徑，教材把拆除、補強和重新啟用分開建模。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Replacement during first-bore refurbishment changes temporary support paths; model removal, strengthening and reactivation separately. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b112-v14-14","title":"支護啟動與變形容量：定量估算","titleEn":"Support activation and deformation capacity: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b112-v14-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「支護安裝時點」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Support activation time” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：局部剛度=41 kN/mm；位移=8 mm。F=ku=328 kN。僅把位移增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為360.8 kN。邊界：線性局部彈簧，不含屈服或時間效應；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: local stiffness=41 kN/mm; movement=8 mm. F=ku=328 kN. Increasing only movement by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 360.8 kN. Boundary: Local linear spring without yielding or time effects. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：每階段核對封閉環、安裝齡期和收斂基線。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check ring closure, installation age and convergence baseline at each stage.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b112-v14-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：局部剛度=41 kN/mm；位移=8 mm。F=ku=328 kN。僅把位移增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為360.8 kN。邊界：線性局部彈簧，不含屈服或時間效應；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: local stiffness=41 kN/mm; movement=8 mm. F=ku=328 kN. Increasing only movement by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 360.8 kN. Boundary: Local linear spring without yielding or time effects. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b112-v14-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「支護啟動與變形容量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Support activation and deformation capacity\", which statement holds?","options":["兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。","原創教學假設：局部剛度=41 kN/mm；位移=8 mm。"],"optionsEn":["Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.","Original teaching assumptions: local stiffness=41 kN/mm; movement=8 mm."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：局部剛度=41 kN/mm；位移=8 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: local stiffness=41 kN/mm; movement=8 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b112-v14-15","title":"支護啟動與變形容量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Support activation and deformation capacity: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b112-v14-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「支護安裝時點」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Support activation time” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"每階段核對封閉環、安裝齡期和收斂基線。同步記錄收斂、支護荷重與安裝里程，比較同一地質分區內的速率及荷載，不將不同開挖齡期讀值直接混合。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check ring closure, installation age and convergence baseline at each stage. Synchronise convergence, support loads and installation chainage; compare rates and loads within one ground domain without mixing readings at different excavation ages. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「支護安裝時點」的交付需回答：每階段核對封閉環、安裝齡期和收斂基線。把安裝時間和量測資料一起交付支護設計者，任何級別變更都需地質及位移證據，不能憑單一瞬間讀值自行改支護。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Gotthard Road Tunnel, the support activation time handover must address the following evidence: Check ring closure, installation age and convergence baseline at each stage. Submit installation times with measurements to the support designer; class changes need both ground and movement evidence, not an isolated instantaneous reading.","failure":"注意干擾：最終補強合格不能證明拆除中間階段仍有連續受力路徑。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Adequate final strengthening does not establish a continuous load path during removal. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b112-v14-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"每階段核對封閉環、安裝齡期和收斂基線。同步記錄收斂、支護荷重與安裝里程，比較同一地質分區內的速率及荷載，不將不同開挖齡期讀值直接混合。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Check ring closure, installation age and convergence baseline at each stage. Synchronise convergence, support loads and installation chainage; compare rates and loads within one ground domain without mixing readings at different excavation ages. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b112-v14-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「支護安裝時點」的交付需回答：每階段核對封閉環、安裝齡期和收斂基線。把安裝時間和量測資料一起交付支護設計者，任何級別變更都需地質及位移證據，不能憑單一瞬間讀值自行改支護。","textEn":"For Gotthard Road Tunnel, the support activation time handover must address the following evidence: Check ring closure, installation age and convergence baseline at each stage. Submit installation times with measurements to the support designer; class changes need both ground and movement evidence, not an isolated instantaneous reading.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「支護啟動與變形容量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Support activation and deformation capacity\"?","options":["每階段核對封閉環、安裝齡期和收斂基線。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Check ring closure, installation age and convergence baseline at each stage.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":0,"explanation":"每階段核對封閉環、安裝齡期和收斂基線。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check ring closure, installation age and convergence baseline at each stage. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b112-v14-16","title":"支護啟動與變形容量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Support activation and deformation capacity: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b112-v14-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「支護安裝時點」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Support activation time” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"最終補強合格不能證明拆除中間階段仍有連續受力路徑。過晚封閉會讓不可回復變形增加，過硬且行程不足的支護也可能脆裂，兩者都可能表現為裂縫而需不同處理。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Adequate final strengthening does not establish a continuous load path during removal. Late closure increases irreversible movement, while excessively stiff support with little travel can fail brittly; both produce cracks but require different diagnoses. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：地盤反力與支護曲線必須連同掌子面距離及封閉順序理解；擠壓性地層還需保留變形容量，不能只追求高剛度與高材料強度。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Squeezing ground also needs deformation capacity; high stiffness and material strength alone do not guarantee a compatible support response.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b112-v14-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"最終補強合格不能證明拆除中間階段仍有連續受力路徑。過晚封閉會讓不可回復變形增加，過硬且行程不足的支護也可能脆裂，兩者都可能表現為裂縫而需不同處理。","textEn":"Adequate final strengthening does not establish a continuous load path during removal. Late closure increases irreversible movement, while excessively stiff support with little travel can fail brittly; both produce cracks but require different diagnoses.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b112-v14-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「支護啟動與變形容量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Support activation and deformation capacity\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","最終補強合格不能證明拆除中間階段仍有連續受力路徑。","目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Adequate final strengthening does not establish a continuous load path during removal.","No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design."],"answer":1,"explanation":"最終補強合格不能證明拆除中間階段仍有連續受力路徑。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Adequate final strengthening does not establish a continuous load path during removal. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b112-v14-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」與「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\" and \"Shared access and transport bottlenecks\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b112-v14-17","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b112-v14-16"],"objective":"說明「測壓水頭」如何影響聖哥達公路隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Piezometric head” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Gotthard Road Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"第二孔排水可能改變舊孔外水頭，研究施工期卸壓與整修後封閉排水的不同永久狀態。水壓取決於連通含水層的測壓水頭，不必等於地表或海面至洞頂的幾何深度。排水降低水壓卻可能增加有效應力與沉陷；停泵或排水堵塞後水頭又會回升，因此防水、排水及環境保水是互相制約的設計選擇。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「測壓水頭」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Second-bore drainage may change first-bore head; distinguish temporary relief from later sealed or altered drainage states. Water pressure follows piezometric head in the connected aquifer, not automatically the geometric depth below ground or sea level. Drainage reduces pressure but can increase effective stress and settlement. Head may recover after a pump outage or blockage, coupling waterproofing, drainage capacity and preservation of surrounding groundwater in the permanent design. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Piezometric head” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=78 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=78 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=765.18 kPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「測壓水頭」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Piezometric head”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b112-v14-17-k1","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure","text":"第二孔排水可能改變舊孔外水頭，研究施工期卸壓與整修後封閉排水的不同永久狀態。水壓取決於連通含水層的測壓水頭，不必等於地表或海面至洞頂的幾何深度。","textEn":"Second-bore drainage may change first-bore head; distinguish temporary relief from later sealed or altered drainage states. Water pressure follows piezometric head in the connected aquifer, not automatically the geometric depth below ground or sea level.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b112-v14-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\" is correct?","options":["目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。","增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。","第二孔排水可能改變舊孔外水頭，研究施工期卸壓與整修後封閉排水的不同永久狀態。"],"optionsEn":["No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.","Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.","Second-bore drainage may change first-bore head; distinguish temporary relief from later sealed or altered drainage states."],"answer":2,"explanation":"第二孔排水可能改變舊孔外水頭，研究施工期卸壓與整修後封閉排水的不同永久狀態。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Second-bore drainage may change first-bore head; distinguish temporary relief from later sealed or altered drainage states. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b112-v14-18","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓：定量估算","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b112-v14-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「測壓水頭」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Piezometric head” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=78 m。p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=765.18 kPa。僅把水頭增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為841.698 kPa。邊界：靜水表壓，不是土體總壓或原位量測；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=78 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=765.18 kPa. Increasing only head by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 841.698 kPa. Boundary: Hydrostatic gauge pressure, not total earth pressure or an in-situ measurement. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在排水變更前後同步比較兩孔壓力與出流。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare pressure and flow in both bores before and after drainage changes.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b112-v14-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=78 m。p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=765.18 kPa。僅把水頭增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為841.698 kPa。邊界：靜水表壓，不是土體總壓或原位量測；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=78 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=765.18 kPa. Increasing only head by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 841.698 kPa. Boundary: Hydrostatic gauge pressure, not total earth pressure or an in-situ measurement. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b112-v14-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=78 m。","風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=78 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=765.18 kPa.","Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=78 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=78 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=765.18 kPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b112-v14-19","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b112-v14-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「測壓水頭」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Piezometric head” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在排水變更前後同步比較兩孔壓力與出流。使用分層測壓管及流量計，配合降雨或潮位序列分辨補注與設備影響，將讀值統一換算至同一高程基準。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare pressure and flow in both bores before and after drainage changes. Use nested piezometers and flowmeters with rainfall or tide histories to distinguish recharge from equipment effects, converting observations to a common elevation datum. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「測壓水頭」的交付需回答：在排水變更前後同步比較兩孔壓力與出流。設計檢核應分列正常排水、堵塞與停電水位，將環境受體的容許變化和監測責任一起交付，不把抽水量當唯一指標。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Gotthard Road Tunnel, the piezometric head handover must address the following evidence: Compare pressure and flow in both bores before and after drainage changes. Separate normal drainage, blocked-drain and power-outage heads and hand over receptor limits and monitoring responsibility together rather than using pump flow as the sole indicator.","failure":"注意干擾：暫時低水頭若永久化假設，停泵回升將被漏算。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Treating temporary low head as permanent misses recovery after pumping stops. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b112-v14-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在排水變更前後同步比較兩孔壓力與出流。使用分層測壓管及流量計，配合降雨或潮位序列分辨補注與設備影響，將讀值統一換算至同一高程基準。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Compare pressure and flow in both bores before and after drainage changes. Use nested piezometers and flowmeters with rainfall or tide histories to distinguish recharge from equipment effects, converting observations to a common elevation datum. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b112-v14-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「測壓水頭」的交付需回答：在排水變更前後同步比較兩孔壓力與出流。設計檢核應分列正常排水、堵塞與停電水位，將環境受體的容許變化和監測責任一起交付，不把抽水量當唯一指標。","textEn":"For Gotthard Road Tunnel, the piezometric head handover must address the following evidence: Compare pressure and flow in both bores before and after drainage changes. Separate normal drainage, blocked-drain and power-outage heads and hand over receptor limits and monitoring responsibility together rather than using pump flow as the sole indicator.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","在排水變更前後同步比較兩孔壓力與出流。","岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Compare pressure and flow in both bores before and after drainage changes.","Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow."],"answer":1,"explanation":"在排水變更前後同步比較兩孔壓力與出流。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare pressure and flow in both bores before and after drainage changes. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b112-v14-20","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓：失效診斷","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b112-v14-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「測壓水頭」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Piezometric head” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"暫時低水頭若永久化假設，停泵回升將被漏算。將暫時降水後的低水頭當成永久狀態，會漏掉停泵後外壓回升；過度排水也可能引起周邊地層壓密。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Treating temporary low head as permanent misses recovery after pumping stops. Treating temporarily lowered head as permanent misses pressure recovery after outage; excessive drainage can also consolidate surrounding ground. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：排水降低水壓卻可能增加有效應力與沉陷；停泵或排水堵塞後水頭又會回升，因此防水、排水及環境保水是互相制約的設計選擇。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Head may recover after a pump outage or blockage, coupling waterproofing, drainage capacity and preservation of surrounding groundwater in the permanent design.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b112-v14-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"暫時低水頭若永久化假設，停泵回升將被漏算。將暫時降水後的低水頭當成永久狀態，會漏掉停泵後外壓回升；過度排水也可能引起周邊地層壓密。","textEn":"Treating temporary low head as permanent misses recovery after pumping stops. Treating temporarily lowered head as permanent misses pressure recovery after outage; excessive drainage can also consolidate surrounding ground.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b112-v14-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。","暫時低水頭若永久化假設，停泵回升將被漏算。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.","Treating temporary low head as permanent misses recovery after pumping stops."],"answer":2,"explanation":"暫時低水頭若永久化假設，停泵回升將被漏算。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Treating temporary low head as permanent misses recovery after pumping stops. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b112-v14-21","title":"共享通道與運輸瓶頸：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Shared access and transport bottlenecks: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b112-v14-20"],"objective":"說明「出渣運輸節拍」如何影響聖哥達公路隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Muck-transport cycle” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Gotthard Road Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"營運孔、施工孔與服務坑共享接口時，材料與應變進出必須排定優先權，不只最大化出渣量。多工作面只有在供電、通風、出渣與材料供應同步充足時才增加總產量。共用豎井或軌道形成串聯瓶頸，排隊和維修窗口會降低名目容量；緩衝區太大又可能侵占通行與救援空間，因此不能單純把各面產能相加。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「出渣運輸節拍」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Where operating, construction and service routes meet, prioritise emergency and material access rather than maximising spoil flow alone. Multiple headings increase output only when power, air, muck transport and materials support them together. Shared shafts or railways become serial bottlenecks, while queues and maintenance reduce nominal capacity. Large buffers may obstruct personnel and rescue access, so face capacities cannot simply be added without a network-level transport and storage check. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Muck-transport cycle” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=31 t；往返週期=35 min。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=31 t; cycle=35 min.","failure":"常見誤解：「增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「出渣運輸節拍」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Muck-transport cycle”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b112-v14-21-k1","title":"共享通道與運輸瓶頸","titleEn":"Shared access and transport bottlenecks","text":"營運孔、施工孔與服務坑共享接口時，材料與應變進出必須排定優先權，不只最大化出渣量。多工作面只有在供電、通風、出渣與材料供應同步充足時才增加總產量。","textEn":"Where operating, construction and service routes meet, prioritise emergency and material access rather than maximising spoil flow alone. Multiple headings increase output only when power, air, muck transport and materials support them together.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b112-v14-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Shared access and transport bottlenecks\" is correct?","options":["營運孔、施工孔與服務坑共享接口時，材料與應變進出必須排定優先權，不只最大化出渣量。","增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Where operating, construction and service routes meet, prioritise emergency and material access rather than maximising spoil flow alone.","Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error."],"answer":0,"explanation":"營運孔、施工孔與服務坑共享接口時，材料與應變進出必須排定優先權，不只最大化出渣量。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Where operating, construction and service routes meet, prioritise emergency and material access rather than maximising spoil flow alone. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b112-v14-22","title":"共享通道與運輸瓶頸：定量估算","titleEn":"Shared access and transport bottlenecks: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b112-v14-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「出渣運輸節拍」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Muck-transport cycle” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=31 t；往返週期=35 min。C=N payload 60/T=212.571 t/h。僅把往返週期增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為193.247 t/h。邊界：無排隊理想循環，並非共享路段實際產能；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=31 t; cycle=35 min. C=N payload 60/T=212.571 t/h. Increasing only cycle by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 193.247 t/h. Boundary: Ideal cycle without queues, not actual shared-route production. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：檢查交會點在設備故障及維修時的排隊長度。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check interface queues during equipment failure and maintenance.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b112-v14-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=31 t；往返週期=35 min。C=N payload 60/T=212.571 t/h。僅把往返週期增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為193.247 t/h。邊界：無排隊理想循環，並非共享路段實際產能；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=31 t; cycle=35 min. C=N payload 60/T=212.571 t/h. Increasing only cycle by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 193.247 t/h. Boundary: Ideal cycle without queues, not actual shared-route production. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b112-v14-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Shared access and transport bottlenecks\", which statement holds?","options":["只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。","原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=31 t；往返週期=35 min。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.","Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=31 t; cycle=35 min.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=31 t；往返週期=35 min。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=31 t; cycle=35 min. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b112-v14-23","title":"共享通道與運輸瓶頸：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Shared access and transport bottlenecks: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b112-v14-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「出渣運輸節拍」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Muck-transport cycle” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"檢查交會點在設備故障及維修時的排隊長度。以裝載質量、往返時間及排隊時間重建物流曲線，再核對緩衝占用、共用通道優先權與維修時段。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check interface queues during equipment failure and maintenance. Reconstruct flow from payload, round-trip and queue times, then check buffer occupancy, shared-route priorities and maintenance periods. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「出渣運輸節拍」的交付需回答：檢查交會點在設備故障及維修時的排隊長度。每日排程同時標示人員、材料和維修的占用時段，任何物流改線先檢查通風與應變通道，不能只看運量提升。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Gotthard Road Tunnel, the muck-transport cycle handover must address the following evidence: Check interface queues during equipment failure and maintenance. Schedules show personnel, materials and maintenance occupancy together; rerouting first checks ventilation and emergency access rather than only throughput gains.","failure":"注意干擾：出渣車占滿共享接口可能阻斷整修隊撤離。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Spoil vehicles occupying a shared interface can obstruct work-team withdrawal. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b112-v14-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"檢查交會點在設備故障及維修時的排隊長度。以裝載質量、往返時間及排隊時間重建物流曲線，再核對緩衝占用、共用通道優先權與維修時段。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Check interface queues during equipment failure and maintenance. Reconstruct flow from payload, round-trip and queue times, then check buffer occupancy, shared-route priorities and maintenance periods. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b112-v14-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「出渣運輸節拍」的交付需回答：檢查交會點在設備故障及維修時的排隊長度。每日排程同時標示人員、材料和維修的占用時段，任何物流改線先檢查通風與應變通道，不能只看運量提升。","textEn":"For Gotthard Road Tunnel, the muck-transport cycle handover must address the following evidence: Check interface queues during equipment failure and maintenance. Schedules show personnel, materials and maintenance occupancy together; rerouting first checks ventilation and emergency access rather than only throughput gains.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Shared access and transport bottlenecks\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。","檢查交會點在設備故障及維修時的排隊長度。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction.","Check interface queues during equipment failure and maintenance."],"answer":2,"explanation":"檢查交會點在設備故障及維修時的排隊長度。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check interface queues during equipment failure and maintenance. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b112-v14-24","title":"共享通道與運輸瓶頸：失效診斷","titleEn":"Shared access and transport bottlenecks: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b112-v14-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「出渣運輸節拍」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Muck-transport cycle” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"出渣車占滿共享接口可能阻斷整修隊撤離。把理想往返時間當全天常數會忽略交會等待與卸料堵塞，導致工作面停工或把材料堆入必要通道。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Spoil vehicles occupying a shared interface can obstruct work-team withdrawal. Treating an ideal cycle as constant all day misses passing delays and unloading blockages, stopping headings or pushing material into essential access space. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：共用豎井或軌道形成串聯瓶頸，排隊和維修窗口會降低名目容量；緩衝區太大又可能侵占通行與救援空間，因此不能單純把各面產能相加。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Large buffers may obstruct personnel and rescue access, so face capacities cannot simply be added without a network-level transport and storage check.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b112-v14-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"出渣車占滿共享接口可能阻斷整修隊撤離。把理想往返時間當全天常數會忽略交會等待與卸料堵塞，導致工作面停工或把材料堆入必要通道。","textEn":"Spoil vehicles occupying a shared interface can obstruct work-team withdrawal. Treating an ideal cycle as constant all day misses passing delays and unloading blockages, stopping headings or pushing material into essential access space.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b112-v14-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Shared access and transport bottlenecks\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["出渣車占滿共享接口可能阻斷整修隊撤離。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Spoil vehicles occupying a shared interface can obstruct work-team withdrawal.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error."],"answer":0,"explanation":"出渣車占滿共享接口可能阻斷整修隊撤離。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Spoil vehicles occupying a shared interface can obstruct work-team withdrawal. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b112-v14-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「控制網與貫通誤差」與「通風網路與壓力損失」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Control network and breakthrough error\" and \"Ventilation network and pressure loss\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b112-v14-25","title":"控制網與貫通誤差：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b112-v14-24"],"objective":"說明「方向角誤差」如何影響聖哥達公路隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Orientation error” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Gotthard Road Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"新舊孔控制網需要共同坐標但也需要獨立覆核，研究舊基準長期位移對新施工定位的影響。長隧道的微小方向誤差會沿距離累積，地下控制網又缺少直接衛星定位，必須把地表基準可靠傳到洞內。閉合差很小不代表無系統誤差；尺度、折光、儀器定向與高程基準可能共同偏移，誤差相關性也使平方和估算失真。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「方向角誤差」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"New and old networks need common coordinates and independent checks; assess long-term movement of legacy reference points. Small orientation errors accumulate over long drives, while underground networks lack direct satellite positioning and depend on transferring surface control. A small closure does not exclude systematic bias: scale, refraction, orientation and vertical datum may shift together. Correlated errors also invalidate a naive root-sum-square combination of supposedly independent observations. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Orientation error” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：控制長度=4320 m；方向偏角=2.6 arcsec。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: control length=4320 m; orientation error=2.6 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0544543 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「方向角誤差」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Orientation error”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b112-v14-25-k1","title":"控制網與貫通誤差","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error","text":"新舊孔控制網需要共同坐標但也需要獨立覆核，研究舊基準長期位移對新施工定位的影響。長隧道的微小方向誤差會沿距離累積，地下控制網又缺少直接衛星定位，必須把地表基準可靠傳到洞內。","textEn":"New and old networks need common coordinates and independent checks; assess long-term movement of legacy reference points. Small orientation errors accumulate over long drives, while underground networks lack direct satellite positioning and depend on transferring surface control.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b112-v14-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「控制網與貫通誤差」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Control network and breakthrough error\" is correct?","options":["兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。","新舊孔控制網需要共同坐標但也需要獨立覆核，研究舊基準長期位移對新施工定位的影響。","風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。"],"optionsEn":["Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.","New and old networks need common coordinates and independent checks; assess long-term movement of legacy reference points.","Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel."],"answer":1,"explanation":"新舊孔控制網需要共同坐標但也需要獨立覆核，研究舊基準長期位移對新施工定位的影響。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"New and old networks need common coordinates and independent checks; assess long-term movement of legacy reference points. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b112-v14-26","title":"控制網與貫通誤差：定量估算","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b112-v14-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「方向角誤差」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Orientation error” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：控制長度=4320 m；方向偏角=2.6 arcsec。e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0544543 m。僅把方向偏角增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.0598997 m。邊界：小角度方向偏差，未加入控制網相關性及折光；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: control length=4320 m; orientation error=2.6 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0544543 m. Increasing only orientation error by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.0598997 m. Boundary: Small-angle orientation error without network correlation or refraction. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以洞外穩定控制重新核對舊點而非假定不動。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Recheck legacy points from stable external control rather than assuming immobility.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b112-v14-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：控制長度=4320 m；方向偏角=2.6 arcsec。e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0544543 m。僅把方向偏角增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.0598997 m。邊界：小角度方向偏差，未加入控制網相關性及折光；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: control length=4320 m; orientation error=2.6 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0544543 m. Increasing only orientation error by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.0598997 m. Boundary: Small-angle orientation error without network correlation or refraction. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b112-v14-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「控制網與貫通誤差」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Control network and breakthrough error\", which statement holds?","options":["全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。","岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。","原創教學假設：控制長度=4320 m；方向偏角=2.6 arcsec。"],"optionsEn":["Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.","Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow.","Original teaching assumptions: control length=4320 m; orientation error=2.6 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0544543 m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：控制長度=4320 m；方向偏角=2.6 arcsec。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: control length=4320 m; orientation error=2.6 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0544543 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b112-v14-27","title":"控制網與貫通誤差：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b112-v14-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「方向角誤差」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Orientation error” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以洞外穩定控制重新核對舊點而非假定不動。由獨立測量組複核地表到洞內的轉換，保留原始角距及溫度資料，用不同控制線比較方向與高程偏差。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Recheck legacy points from stable external control rather than assuming immobility. Independently check surface-to-tunnel transformations, retain raw angles, distances and temperatures, and compare orientation and elevation through separate control routes. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「方向角誤差」的交付需回答：以洞外穩定控制重新核對舊點而非假定不動。貫通前凍結座標、尺度與高程版本，獨立組直接使用原始觀測重算；不得只傳遞整理好的坐標而遺失校正資訊。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Gotthard Road Tunnel, the orientation error handover must address the following evidence: Recheck legacy points from stable external control rather than assuming immobility. Freeze coordinate, scale and height revisions before breakthrough; independent reviewers recompute raw observations rather than receiving only adjusted coordinates without corrections.","failure":"注意干擾：移動基準會讓新孔看似偏移，導致錯誤幾何修正。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A moving reference makes the new bore appear displaced and prompts wrong corrections. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b112-v14-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以洞外穩定控制重新核對舊點而非假定不動。由獨立測量組複核地表到洞內的轉換，保留原始角距及溫度資料，用不同控制線比較方向與高程偏差。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Recheck legacy points from stable external control rather than assuming immobility. Independently check surface-to-tunnel transformations, retain raw angles, distances and temperatures, and compare orientation and elevation through separate control routes. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b112-v14-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「方向角誤差」的交付需回答：以洞外穩定控制重新核對舊點而非假定不動。貫通前凍結座標、尺度與高程版本，獨立組直接使用原始觀測重算；不得只傳遞整理好的坐標而遺失校正資訊。","textEn":"For Gotthard Road Tunnel, the orientation error handover must address the following evidence: Recheck legacy points from stable external control rather than assuming immobility. Freeze coordinate, scale and height revisions before breakthrough; independent reviewers recompute raw observations rather than receiving only adjusted coordinates without corrections.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「控制網與貫通誤差」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Control network and breakthrough error\"?","options":["以洞外穩定控制重新核對舊點而非假定不動。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。"],"optionsEn":["Recheck legacy points from stable external control rather than assuming immobility.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以洞外穩定控制重新核對舊點而非假定不動。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Recheck legacy points from stable external control rather than assuming immobility. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b112-v14-28","title":"控制網與貫通誤差：失效診斷","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b112-v14-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「方向角誤差」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Orientation error” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"移動基準會讓新孔看似偏移，導致錯誤幾何修正。共用錯誤基準可能讓兩組測量同時看似一致，直到貫通或軌道銜接才發現系統偏差，修正成本遠高於早期複核。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A moving reference makes the new bore appear displaced and prompts wrong corrections. A shared wrong datum can make separate surveys appear consistent until breakthrough or track connection exposes bias that is costly to correct. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：閉合差很小不代表無系統誤差；尺度、折光、儀器定向與高程基準可能共同偏移，誤差相關性也使平方和估算失真。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Correlated errors also invalidate a naive root-sum-square combination of supposedly independent observations.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b112-v14-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"移動基準會讓新孔看似偏移，導致錯誤幾何修正。共用錯誤基準可能讓兩組測量同時看似一致，直到貫通或軌道銜接才發現系統偏差，修正成本遠高於早期複核。","textEn":"A moving reference makes the new bore appear displaced and prompts wrong corrections. A shared wrong datum can make separate surveys appear consistent until breakthrough or track connection exposes bias that is costly to correct.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b112-v14-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「控制網與貫通誤差」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Control network and breakthrough error\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","移動基準會讓新孔看似偏移，導致錯誤幾何修正。","風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","A moving reference makes the new bore appear displaced and prompts wrong corrections.","Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel."],"answer":1,"explanation":"移動基準會讓新孔看似偏移，導致錯誤幾何修正。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A moving reference makes the new bore appear displaced and prompts wrong corrections. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b112-v14-29","title":"通風網路與壓力損失：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Ventilation network and pressure loss: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b112-v14-28"],"objective":"說明「風道摩擦壓損」如何影響聖哥達公路隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Duct friction loss” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Gotthard Road Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"整修時營運與施工風路必須按階段隔離，研究共用服務坑門位如何改變壓力網。風機提供壓差，實際風量由風道摩阻、局部損失、外風與其他風機共同決定。支路開關會重新分配整個網路，不能把額定風量直接加總；正常污染稀釋與火災控煙也有不同目標，需要分別建立受控邊界和故障情境。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「風道摩擦壓損」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Stage-specific isolation is required between operational and construction airflow; test service-gallery door effects on pressure distribution. Fans supply pressure, but actual flow follows friction, local losses, external wind and interactions with other fans. Switching a branch redistributes the network rather than simply adding rated flows. Routine dilution and fire smoke control have different objectives, so each needs explicit boundaries, operating states and failure cases rather than one universal flow target. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Duct friction loss” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：達西因子=0.025 無因次；風道長度=940 m；水力直徑=4 m；空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；平均風速=3.7 m/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.025 dimensionless; duct length=940 m; hydraulic diameter=4 m; air density=1.2 kg/m³; mean velocity=3.7 m/s. Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=48.2573 Pa.","failure":"常見誤解：「風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「風道摩擦壓損」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Duct friction loss”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b112-v14-29-k1","title":"通風網路與壓力損失","titleEn":"Ventilation network and pressure loss","text":"整修時營運與施工風路必須按階段隔離，研究共用服務坑門位如何改變壓力網。風機提供壓差，實際風量由風道摩阻、局部損失、外風與其他風機共同決定。","textEn":"Stage-specific isolation is required between operational and construction airflow; test service-gallery door effects on pressure distribution. Fans supply pressure, but actual flow follows friction, local losses, external wind and interactions with other fans.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b112-v14-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「通風網路與壓力損失」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Ventilation network and pressure loss\" is correct?","options":["風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。","整修時營運與施工風路必須按階段隔離，研究共用服務坑門位如何改變壓力網。"],"optionsEn":["Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.","Stage-specific isolation is required between operational and construction airflow; test service-gallery door effects on pressure distribution."],"answer":2,"explanation":"整修時營運與施工風路必須按階段隔離，研究共用服務坑門位如何改變壓力網。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Stage-specific isolation is required between operational and construction airflow; test service-gallery door effects on pressure distribution. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b112-v14-30","title":"通風網路與壓力損失：定量估算","titleEn":"Ventilation network and pressure loss: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b112-v14-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「風道摩擦壓損」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Duct friction loss” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：達西因子=0.025 無因次；風道長度=940 m；水力直徑=4 m；空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；平均風速=3.7 m/s。Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=48.2573 Pa。僅把平均風速增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為58.3913 Pa。邊界：定密度直管摩阻，局部損失及外風另計；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.025 dimensionless; duct length=940 m; hydraulic diameter=4 m; air density=1.2 kg/m³; mean velocity=3.7 m/s. Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=48.2573 Pa. Increasing only mean velocity by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 58.3913 Pa. Boundary: Constant-density straight-duct friction; local loss and external wind are separate. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：對照隔離圖、現場門位和兩側壓差。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Reconcile isolation drawings, actual door states and pressure on both sides.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b112-v14-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：達西因子=0.025 無因次；風道長度=940 m；水力直徑=4 m；空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；平均風速=3.7 m/s。Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=48.2573 Pa。僅把平均風速增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為58.3913 Pa。邊界：定密度直管摩阻，局部損失及外風另計；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.025 dimensionless; duct length=940 m; hydraulic diameter=4 m; air density=1.2 kg/m³; mean velocity=3.7 m/s. Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=48.2573 Pa. Increasing only mean velocity by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 58.3913 Pa. Boundary: Constant-density straight-duct friction; local loss and external wind are separate. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b112-v14-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「通風網路與壓力損失」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Ventilation network and pressure loss\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：達西因子=0.025 無因次；風道長度=940 m；水力直徑=4 m；空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；平均風速=3.7 m/s。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。","知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.025 dimensionless.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.","Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：達西因子=0.025 無因次；風道長度=940 m；水力直徑=4 m；空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；平均風速=3.7 m/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.025 dimensionless; duct length=940 m; hydraulic diameter=4 m; air density=1.2 kg/m³; mean velocity=3.7 m/s. Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=48.2573 Pa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b112-v14-31","title":"通風網路與壓力損失：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Ventilation network and pressure loss: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b112-v14-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「風道摩擦壓損」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Duct friction loss” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"對照隔離圖、現場門位和兩側壓差。沿線同步量測靜壓與風速，記錄風門及其他風機狀態，再把實測工作點和風機曲線、網路壓損比較。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Reconcile isolation drawings, actual door states and pressure on both sides. Measure pressure and velocity synchronously, record dampers and other fans, and compare the measured duty point with fan curves and network resistance. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「風道摩擦壓損」的交付需回答：對照隔離圖、現場門位和兩側壓差。驗收採明確風門和車流邊界，維修改線後重新核對網路工作點，火災模式由防災責任工程師簽認而非沿用正常模式。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Gotthard Road Tunnel, the duct friction loss handover must address the following evidence: Reconcile isolation drawings, actual door states and pressure on both sides. Commission with specified damper and traffic boundaries, recheck duty points after rerouting, and have the fire-safety engineer approve emergency modes independently.","failure":"注意干擾：服務門常開會使模型中的封閉支路變成漏風通道。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: An open service door turns a modelled closed branch into a leakage path. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b112-v14-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"對照隔離圖、現場門位和兩側壓差。沿線同步量測靜壓與風速，記錄風門及其他風機狀態，再把實測工作點和風機曲線、網路壓損比較。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Reconcile isolation drawings, actual door states and pressure on both sides. Measure pressure and velocity synchronously, record dampers and other fans, and compare the measured duty point with fan curves and network resistance. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b112-v14-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「風道摩擦壓損」的交付需回答：對照隔離圖、現場門位和兩側壓差。驗收採明確風門和車流邊界，維修改線後重新核對網路工作點，火災模式由防災責任工程師簽認而非沿用正常模式。","textEn":"For Gotthard Road Tunnel, the duct friction loss handover must address the following evidence: Reconcile isolation drawings, actual door states and pressure on both sides. Commission with specified damper and traffic boundaries, recheck duty points after rerouting, and have the fire-safety engineer approve emergency modes independently.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「通風網路與壓力損失」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Ventilation network and pressure loss\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","對照隔離圖、現場門位和兩側壓差。","目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Reconcile isolation drawings, actual door states and pressure on both sides.","No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design."],"answer":1,"explanation":"對照隔離圖、現場門位和兩側壓差。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Reconcile isolation drawings, actual door states and pressure on both sides. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b112-v14-32","title":"通風網路與壓力損失：失效診斷","titleEn":"Ventilation network and pressure loss: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b112-v14-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「風道摩擦壓損」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Duct friction loss” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"服務門常開會使模型中的封閉支路變成漏風通道。只看風機轉速會漏掉風門誤位或短路漏風，可能在總耗電增加時，真正需要的區段反而風量不足。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"An open service door turns a modelled closed branch into a leakage path. Fan speed alone misses a misplaced damper or leakage shortcut; total power may rise while the critical section receives less air. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：支路開關會重新分配整個網路，不能把額定風量直接加總；正常污染稀釋與火災控煙也有不同目標，需要分別建立受控邊界和故障情境。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Routine dilution and fire smoke control have different objectives, so each needs explicit boundaries, operating states and failure cases rather than one universal flow target.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b112-v14-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"服務門常開會使模型中的封閉支路變成漏風通道。只看風機轉速會漏掉風門誤位或短路漏風，可能在總耗電增加時，真正需要的區段反而風量不足。","textEn":"An open service door turns a modelled closed branch into a leakage path. Fan speed alone misses a misplaced damper or leakage shortcut; total power may rise while the critical section receives less air.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b112-v14-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「通風網路與壓力損失」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Ventilation network and pressure loss\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。","服務門常開會使模型中的封閉支路變成漏風通道。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.","An open service door turns a modelled closed branch into a leakage path."],"answer":2,"explanation":"服務門常開會使模型中的封閉支路變成漏風通道。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"An open service door turns a modelled closed branch into a leakage path. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b112-v14-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「疏散時間與分區可用性」與「資產編碼與可追溯交接」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Evacuation time and zone availability\" and \"Asset identity and traceable handover\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b112-v14-33","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b112-v14-32"],"objective":"說明「所需疏散時間」如何影響聖哥達公路隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Required evacuation time” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Gotthard Road Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"分期切換改變人員可使用的孔別，聖哥達教材要求依實際階段重建安全區轉移路徑。疏散時間包含辨識、反應、移動及排隊，不只由出口距離決定。人員速度會受煙熱、能見度及行動能力影響，安全判斷還要比較可用安全時間；橫通道存在但門或鄰孔不可用時，圖上的最短路線不一定能作實際選擇。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「所需疏散時間」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Staged transfer changes the usable bore, so rebuild safe-area routes for the actual configuration. Evacuation includes detection, response, travel and queues, not merely distance to an exit. Smoke, visibility and mobility alter walking speed, while safety requires comparison with available safe time. A passage shown on a plan may be unusable because its door or receiving bore is unavailable, invalidating the nominal shortest route. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Required evacuation time” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：前置時間=102 s；行走距離=360 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=102 s; travel distance=360 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「所需疏散時間」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Required evacuation time”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b112-v14-33-k1","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability","text":"分期切換改變人員可使用的孔別，聖哥達教材要求依實際階段重建安全區轉移路徑。疏散時間包含辨識、反應、移動及排隊，不只由出口距離決定。","textEn":"Staged transfer changes the usable bore, so rebuild safe-area routes for the actual configuration. Evacuation includes detection, response, travel and queues, not merely distance to an exit.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b112-v14-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「疏散時間與分區可用性」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Evacuation time and zone availability\" is correct?","options":["分期切換改變人員可使用的孔別，聖哥達教材要求依實際階段重建安全區轉移路徑。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。"],"optionsEn":["Staged transfer changes the usable bore, so rebuild safe-area routes for the actual configuration.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted."],"answer":0,"explanation":"分期切換改變人員可使用的孔別，聖哥達教材要求依實際階段重建安全區轉移路徑。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Staged transfer changes the usable bore, so rebuild safe-area routes for the actual configuration. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b112-v14-34","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性：定量估算","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b112-v14-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「所需疏散時間」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Required evacuation time” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：前置時間=102 s；行走距離=360 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。RSET=tpre+d/v=552 s。僅把行走距離增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為597 s。邊界：單群體固定速度，不含排隊煙熱及能力差異，不能單獨判安全；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=102 s; travel distance=360 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s. RSET=tpre+d/v=552 s. Increasing only travel distance by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 597 s. Boundary: One group at fixed speed without queues, smoke or mobility differences; not a safety conclusion. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在每次切換後核對方向標示和橫通道狀態。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check direction signs and passage states after every transfer.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b112-v14-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：前置時間=102 s；行走距離=360 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。RSET=tpre+d/v=552 s。僅把行走距離增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為597 s。邊界：單群體固定速度，不含排隊煙熱及能力差異，不能單獨判安全；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=102 s; travel distance=360 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s. RSET=tpre+d/v=552 s. Increasing only travel distance by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 597 s. Boundary: One group at fixed speed without queues, smoke or mobility differences; not a safety conclusion. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b112-v14-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「疏散時間與分區可用性」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Evacuation time and zone availability\", which statement holds?","options":["岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。","原創教學假設：前置時間=102 s；行走距離=360 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。","支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。"],"optionsEn":["Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow.","Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=102 s; travel distance=360 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s.","Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：前置時間=102 s；行走距離=360 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=102 s; travel distance=360 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b112-v14-35","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b112-v14-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「所需疏散時間」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Required evacuation time” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在每次切換後核對方向標示和橫通道狀態。以人流模擬或受控演練分辨前置時間、行走與門口排隊，核對每個出口接收區的可用狀態及通訊紀錄。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check direction signs and passage states after every transfer. Separate pre-movement, travel and doorway queues through simulation or controlled drills, checking receiving-zone availability and communication records for each exit. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「所需疏散時間」的交付需回答：在每次切換後核對方向標示和橫通道狀態。疏散模型保留人口、速度分布及出口狀態，演練改動由營運與防災責任者批准，教材算例不得當作現場指揮程序。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Gotthard Road Tunnel, the required evacuation time handover must address the following evidence: Check direction signs and passage states after every transfer. Retain population, speed distribution and exit states; operations and fire-safety owners approve drill changes, and classroom calculations are not incident-command procedures.","failure":"注意干擾：沿用上一階段圖可能把使用者帶到施工孔。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: An earlier-stage map can direct users into the construction bore. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b112-v14-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在每次切換後核對方向標示和橫通道狀態。以人流模擬或受控演練分辨前置時間、行走與門口排隊，核對每個出口接收區的可用狀態及通訊紀錄。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Check direction signs and passage states after every transfer. Separate pre-movement, travel and doorway queues through simulation or controlled drills, checking receiving-zone availability and communication records for each exit. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b112-v14-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「所需疏散時間」的交付需回答：在每次切換後核對方向標示和橫通道狀態。疏散模型保留人口、速度分布及出口狀態，演練改動由營運與防災責任者批准，教材算例不得當作現場指揮程序。","textEn":"For Gotthard Road Tunnel, the required evacuation time handover must address the following evidence: Check direction signs and passage states after every transfer. Retain population, speed distribution and exit states; operations and fire-safety owners approve drill changes, and classroom calculations are not incident-command procedures.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「疏散時間與分區可用性」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Evacuation time and zone availability\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。","在每次切換後核對方向標示和橫通道狀態。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.","Check direction signs and passage states after every transfer."],"answer":2,"explanation":"在每次切換後核對方向標示和橫通道狀態。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check direction signs and passage states after every transfer. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b112-v14-36","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性：失效診斷","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b112-v14-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「所需疏散時間」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Required evacuation time” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"沿用上一階段圖可能把使用者帶到施工孔。以最快成人速度套全部旅客會低估需求，若忽略接收孔受煙或車流影響，疏散可能移到另一個危險邊界。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"An earlier-stage map can direct users into the construction bore. Applying the fastest adult speed to everyone understates demand; overlooking smoke or traffic in the receiving bore can transfer evacuees into another hazard. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：人員速度會受煙熱、能見度及行動能力影響，安全判斷還要比較可用安全時間；橫通道存在但門或鄰孔不可用時，圖上的最短路線不一定能作實際選擇。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A passage shown on a plan may be unusable because its door or receiving bore is unavailable, invalidating the nominal shortest route.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b112-v14-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"沿用上一階段圖可能把使用者帶到施工孔。以最快成人速度套全部旅客會低估需求，若忽略接收孔受煙或車流影響，疏散可能移到另一個危險邊界。","textEn":"An earlier-stage map can direct users into the construction bore. Applying the fastest adult speed to everyone understates demand; overlooking smoke or traffic in the receiving bore can transfer evacuees into another hazard.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b112-v14-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「疏散時間與分區可用性」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Evacuation time and zone availability\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["沿用上一階段圖可能把使用者帶到施工孔。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。"],"optionsEn":["An earlier-stage map can direct users into the construction bore.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted."],"answer":0,"explanation":"沿用上一階段圖可能把使用者帶到施工孔。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"An earlier-stage map can direct users into the construction bore. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b112-v14-37","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b112-v14-36"],"objective":"說明「資產資料完整度」如何影響聖哥達公路隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Asset-record completeness” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Gotthard Road Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"新舊控制系統切換需保留版本和回復條件，研究警報位址跨孔重用的風險。地下設備的竣工資料必須讓維護人員找到正確位置、材料批次和控制版本。只有上傳圖面而沒有變更歷程，無法分辨元件替換與真正劣化；告警、儀器、線路及工單使用一致識別碼，才可能把量測趨勢連回實際受力或水力系統。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「資產資料完整度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Control-system transfer needs revisions and rollback conditions, including risks from reusing alarm addresses across bores. Handover must let maintainers find the correct location, material batch and control revision. Drawings without change history cannot distinguish replacement from deterioration. Consistent identifiers across alarms, instruments, circuits and work orders are essential for linking trends to the physical structural or hydraulic system instead of treating each record as an isolated file. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Asset-record completeness” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：設備總數=111 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: asset count=111 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=85.5856 %.","failure":"常見誤解：「全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「資產資料完整度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Asset-record completeness”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b112-v14-37-k1","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover","text":"新舊控制系統切換需保留版本和回復條件，研究警報位址跨孔重用的風險。地下設備的竣工資料必須讓維護人員找到正確位置、材料批次和控制版本。","textEn":"Control-system transfer needs revisions and rollback conditions, including risks from reusing alarm addresses across bores. Handover must let maintainers find the correct location, material batch and control revision.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b112-v14-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「資產編碼與可追溯交接」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Asset identity and traceable handover\" is correct?","options":["全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。","新舊控制系統切換需保留版本和回復條件，研究警報位址跨孔重用的風險。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.","Control-system transfer needs revisions and rollback conditions, including risks from reusing alarm addresses across bores.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":1,"explanation":"新舊控制系統切換需保留版本和回復條件，研究警報位址跨孔重用的風險。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Control-system transfer needs revisions and rollback conditions, including risks from reusing alarm addresses across bores. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b112-v14-38","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：定量估算","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b112-v14-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「資產資料完整度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Asset-record completeness” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：設備總數=111 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。coverage=100(N−missing)/N=85.5856 %。僅把缺紀錄數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為84.1441 %。邊界：資料完整度，不等於安全或可靠度；擾動為連續敏感度，實際個數為整數；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: asset count=111 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=85.5856 %. Increasing only missing records by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 84.1441 %. Boundary: Record completeness, not safety or reliability; perturbation is continuous sensitivity while actual counts are integers. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：抽查切換清單與現場實際在線設備一一對應。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Match the transfer register one-to-one with field assets actually online.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b112-v14-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：設備總數=111 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。coverage=100(N−missing)/N=85.5856 %。僅把缺紀錄數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為84.1441 %。邊界：資料完整度，不等於安全或可靠度；擾動為連續敏感度，實際個數為整數；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: asset count=111 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=85.5856 %. Increasing only missing records by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 84.1441 %. Boundary: Record completeness, not safety or reliability; perturbation is continuous sensitivity while actual counts are integers. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b112-v14-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「資產編碼與可追溯交接」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Asset identity and traceable handover\", which statement holds?","options":["知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。","目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。","原創教學假設：設備總數=111 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。"],"optionsEn":["Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction.","No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.","Original teaching assumptions: asset count=111 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=85.5856 %."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：設備總數=111 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: asset count=111 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=85.5856 %. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b112-v14-39","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b112-v14-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「資產資料完整度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Asset-record completeness” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"抽查切換清單與現場實際在線設備一一對應。抽取一條告警，從控制畫面追到設備、線路、圖面和工單，核對位置、版本及校正日期並記錄無法閉合的欄位。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Match the transfer register one-to-one with field assets actually online. Trace a sampled alarm from screen to equipment, circuit, drawing and work order, checking location, revision and calibration dates and recording broken links. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「資產資料完整度」的交付需回答：抽查切換清單與現場實際在線設備一一對應。交接以可完成的定位、查找與復原任務驗證，由維護責任人確認現場可用性；完整度只是資料指標，不代表結構安全或設備可靠。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Gotthard Road Tunnel, the asset-record completeness handover must address the following evidence: Match the transfer register one-to-one with field assets actually online. Validate handover through achievable location, retrieval and recovery tasks witnessed by maintainers; completeness measures records, not structural safety or equipment reliability.","failure":"注意干擾：複製舊位址而未更新位置會造成告警定位錯孔。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Copied addresses with unchanged location data identify the wrong bore. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b112-v14-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"抽查切換清單與現場實際在線設備一一對應。抽取一條告警，從控制畫面追到設備、線路、圖面和工單，核對位置、版本及校正日期並記錄無法閉合的欄位。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Match the transfer register one-to-one with field assets actually online. Trace a sampled alarm from screen to equipment, circuit, drawing and work order, checking location, revision and calibration dates and recording broken links. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b112-v14-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「資產資料完整度」的交付需回答：抽查切換清單與現場實際在線設備一一對應。交接以可完成的定位、查找與復原任務驗證，由維護責任人確認現場可用性；完整度只是資料指標，不代表結構安全或設備可靠。","textEn":"For Gotthard Road Tunnel, the asset-record completeness handover must address the following evidence: Match the transfer register one-to-one with field assets actually online. Validate handover through achievable location, retrieval and recovery tasks witnessed by maintainers; completeness measures records, not structural safety or equipment reliability.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「資產編碼與可追溯交接」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Asset identity and traceable handover\"?","options":["抽查切換清單與現場實際在線設備一一對應。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Match the transfer register one-to-one with field assets actually online.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error."],"answer":0,"explanation":"抽查切換清單與現場實際在線設備一一對應。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Match the transfer register one-to-one with field assets actually online. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b112-v14-40","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：失效診斷","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b112-v14-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「資產資料完整度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Asset-record completeness” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"複製舊位址而未更新位置會造成告警定位錯孔。設備改名卻未更新控制畫面會引導人員隔離錯誤回路，材料批次缺漏則使同批缺陷無法追蹤到其他位置。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Copied addresses with unchanged location data identify the wrong bore. Renaming an asset without updating the screen can isolate the wrong circuit; missing material batches prevent tracing related defects at other locations. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：只有上傳圖面而沒有變更歷程，無法分辨元件替換與真正劣化；告警、儀器、線路及工單使用一致識別碼，才可能把量測趨勢連回實際受力或水力系統。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Consistent identifiers across alarms, instruments, circuits and work orders are essential for linking trends to the physical structural or hydraulic system instead of treating each record as an isolated file.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b112-v14-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"複製舊位址而未更新位置會造成告警定位錯孔。設備改名卻未更新控制畫面會引導人員隔離錯誤回路，材料批次缺漏則使同批缺陷無法追蹤到其他位置。","textEn":"Copied addresses with unchanged location data identify the wrong bore. Renaming an asset without updating the screen can isolate the wrong circuit; missing material batches prevent tracing related defects at other locations.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b112-v14-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「資產編碼與可追溯交接」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Asset identity and traceable handover\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","複製舊位址而未更新位置會造成告警定位錯孔。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Copied addresses with unchanged location data identify the wrong bore.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":1,"explanation":"複製舊位址而未更新位置會造成告警定位錯孔。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Copied addresses with unchanged location data identify the wrong bore. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b112","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"curriculumVersion":14,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000},{"id":"b113","title":"聖伯納山隧道","titleEn":"Great St Bernard Tunnel","category":"underground","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"聖伯納山隧道營運者列長5798公尺，並說明兩端高山入口與全天有人值守的控制室。1964年開通的背景使其適合學習既有公路隧道長期更新。本課將洞口氣候、雙向車流、通風、耐久及跨境資訊交接串成完整工程問題，避免把洞內性能與引道服務切割。","summaryEn":"The operator describes a 5798 m tunnel with high-altitude portals and continuously staffed control rooms at both ends. Its 1964 opening provides a setting for long-term renewal of an existing road tunnel. The course connects portal climate, bidirectional traffic, ventilation, durability and cross-border information handover rather than isolating tunnel performance from approach service.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"ug-landmarks","subcategoryTitle":"世界隧道與地下巨作","subcategoryTitleEn":"World tunnels and underground landmarks","learningTrack":"underground","learningSubdiscipline":"ug-landmarks","learningTags":["underground","ug-landmarks","tunnel"],"architectureFamily":"tunnel","architectureNodes":[["路線里程與端點","Alignment chainage and endpoints"],["風道摩擦壓損","Duct friction loss"],["拘束溫度應變","Restrained thermal strain"],["擴散特徵長度","Diffusion characteristic length"],["所需疏散時間","Required evacuation time"],["資產資料完整度","Asset-record completeness"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,5],[1,5]],"diagram":{"type":"tunnel","labels":["路線里程與端點","風道摩擦壓損","拘束溫度應變","擴散特徵長度","所需疏散時間"],"labelsEn":["Alignment chainage and endpoints","Duct friction loss","Restrained thermal strain","Diffusion characteristic length","Required evacuation time"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"原創綜合審查：先計算「通風網路與壓力損失」，再獨立計算「氯鹽遷移與耐久判讀」。原創教學假設：達西因子=0.025 無因次；風道長度=980 m；水力直徑=4 m；空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；平均風速=3.1 m/s。Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=35.3168 Pa。僅把平均風速增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為42.7333 Pa。邊界：定密度直管摩阻，局部損失及外風另計；不是本工程實測或允收值。原創教學假設：擴散係數=1e-12 m²/s；暴露時間=15 year。ℓ=√(Dt); 1 year=365.25×86400 s; m→mm ×1000=21.7569 mm。僅把暴露時間增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為22.8189 mm。邊界：特徵長度，不是腐蝕起始壽命或氯鹽門檻深度；不是本工程實測或允收值。兩組結果的單位與邊界不同，不能直接相加。請列出一項缺少的現場輸入，說明它會影響哪個結論，以及哪種獨立量測可以縮小不確定度。","textEn":"Original integrated review: first calculate ventilation network and pressure loss, then independently calculate chloride transport and durability interpretation. Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.025 dimensionless; duct length=980 m; hydraulic diameter=4 m; air density=1.2 kg/m³; mean velocity=3.1 m/s. Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=35.3168 Pa. Increasing only mean velocity by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 42.7333 Pa. Boundary: Constant-density straight-duct friction; local loss and external wind are separate. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Original teaching assumptions: diffusivity=1e-12 m²/s; exposure=15 year. ℓ=√(Dt); 1 year=365.25×86400 s; m→mm ×1000=21.7569 mm. Increasing only exposure by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 22.8189 mm. Boundary: Characteristic length, not corrosion-initiation life or chloride-threshold depth. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. The outputs have different units and boundaries and cannot simply be added. Identify one missing field input, explain which conclusion it changes and select an independent measurement to reduce uncertainty.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":14,"enrichmentVersion":14,"stages":[{"id":"b113-v14-s1","title":"地層條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Ground conditions, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「服務邊界與路線代價」與「通風網路與壓力損失」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\" and \"Ventilation network and pressure loss\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b113-v14-01","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「路線里程與端點」如何影響聖伯納山隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Alignment chainage and endpoints” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Great St Bernard Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"聖伯納山洞口和覆蓋引道共同提供高山通行，教材將隧道長度與雪季接近路段分開比較。隧道選線同時改變洞口、覆土與縱坡，短路線不保證低地質風險。比較方案必須使用相同起訖點，並分開主孔、引道及服務坑的工程數量；交通時間只是需求的一個指標，不能代替施工可達性或長期維修評估。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「路線里程與端點」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Portals and covered approaches jointly provide alpine access; distinguish tunnel length from winter approach sections. Alignment changes portals, cover and gradient together, so a shorter tunnel need not have lower geological risk. Compare options between identical endpoints and distinguish running bores, approaches and service galleries. Travel time measures one service benefit but cannot replace assessment of construction access, maintenance closures or exposure to uncertain ground. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Alignment chainage and endpoints” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：長度=16.8 km；速度=60 km/h。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: length=16.8 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=16.8 min.","failure":"常見誤解：「最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「路線里程與端點」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Alignment chainage and endpoints”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b113-v14-01-k1","title":"服務邊界與路線代價","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost","text":"聖伯納山洞口和覆蓋引道共同提供高山通行，教材將隧道長度與雪季接近路段分開比較。隧道選線同時改變洞口、覆土與縱坡，短路線不保證低地質風險。","textEn":"Portals and covered approaches jointly provide alpine access; distinguish tunnel length from winter approach sections. Alignment changes portals, cover and gradient together, so a shorter tunnel need not have lower geological risk.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]},{"id":"b113-v14-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「服務邊界與路線代價」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\" is correct?","options":["最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。","聖伯納山洞口和覆蓋引道共同提供高山通行，教材將隧道長度與雪季接近路段分開比較。","風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。"],"optionsEn":["The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.","Portals and covered approaches jointly provide alpine access; distinguish tunnel length from winter approach sections.","Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel."],"answer":1,"explanation":"聖伯納山洞口和覆蓋引道共同提供高山通行，教材將隧道長度與雪季接近路段分開比較。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Portals and covered approaches jointly provide alpine access; distinguish tunnel length from winter approach sections. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b113-v14-02","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：定量估算","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b113-v14-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「路線里程與端點」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Alignment chainage and endpoints” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：長度=16.8 km；速度=60 km/h。t=60L/v=16.8 min。僅把長度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為18.48 min。邊界：假想交通旅程，未含加減速、排隊及實際時刻表；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: length=16.8 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=16.8 min. Increasing only length by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 18.48 min. Boundary: Hypothetical transport journey excluding acceleration, queues and the real timetable. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對相同端點下的洞內、引道和等待時間。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check tunnel, approach and waiting time between equal endpoints.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b113-v14-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：長度=16.8 km；速度=60 km/h。t=60L/v=16.8 min。僅把長度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為18.48 min。邊界：假想交通旅程，未含加減速、排隊及實際時刻表；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: length=16.8 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=16.8 min. Increasing only length by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 18.48 min. Boundary: Hypothetical transport journey excluding acceleration, queues and the real timetable. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]},{"id":"b113-v14-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「服務邊界與路線代價」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\", which statement holds?","options":["混凝土抗壓強度合格就代表厚壁構件不會產生熱裂縫。","擴散長度就是鋼筋開始腐蝕的位置和精確時間。","原創教學假設：長度=16.8 km；速度=60 km/h。"],"optionsEn":["Adequate compressive strength proves that thick concrete cannot develop thermal cracks.","Diffusion length gives the exact location and time of corrosion initiation.","Original teaching assumptions: length=16.8 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=16.8 min."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：長度=16.8 km；速度=60 km/h。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: length=16.8 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=16.8 min. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b113-v14-03","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b113-v14-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「路線里程與端點」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Alignment chainage and endpoints” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對相同端點下的洞內、引道和等待時間。把縱斷面、地形與地質剖面疊合，以端點坐標獨立反算距離，再將主孔與支坑數量分開核對。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check tunnel, approach and waiting time between equal endpoints. Overlay the longitudinal profile, terrain and geology; independently derive distances from endpoint coordinates and reconcile running-bore and gallery quantities separately. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「路線里程與端點」的交付需回答：核對相同端點下的洞內、引道和等待時間。在方案表中凍結起訖點、計量範圍及地質假設，任何改線都要同步更新高程、數量與服務情境，不能只替換總長。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Great St Bernard Tunnel, the alignment chainage and endpoints handover must address the following evidence: Check tunnel, approach and waiting time between equal endpoints. Freeze endpoints, measurement scope and ground assumptions in the option register; realignment requires coordinated updates to elevations, quantities and service scenarios rather than replacing one length.","failure":"注意干擾：只評洞內時間會漏掉入口管制或引道封閉的服務中斷。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: In-tunnel time omits service interruption at approach closures or entrance controls. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b113-v14-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對相同端點下的洞內、引道和等待時間。把縱斷面、地形與地質剖面疊合，以端點坐標獨立反算距離，再將主孔與支坑數量分開核對。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Check tunnel, approach and waiting time between equal endpoints. Overlay the longitudinal profile, terrain and geology; independently derive distances from endpoint coordinates and reconcile running-bore and gallery quantities separately. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]},{"id":"b113-v14-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「路線里程與端點」的交付需回答：核對相同端點下的洞內、引道和等待時間。在方案表中凍結起訖點、計量範圍及地質假設，任何改線都要同步更新高程、數量與服務情境，不能只替換總長。","textEn":"For Great St Bernard Tunnel, the alignment chainage and endpoints handover must address the following evidence: Check tunnel, approach and waiting time between equal endpoints. Freeze endpoints, measurement scope and ground assumptions in the option register; realignment requires coordinated updates to elevations, quantities and service scenarios rather than replacing one length.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「服務邊界與路線代價」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\"?","options":["核對相同端點下的洞內、引道和等待時間。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。"],"optionsEn":["Check tunnel, approach and waiting time between equal endpoints.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time."],"answer":0,"explanation":"核對相同端點下的洞內、引道和等待時間。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check tunnel, approach and waiting time between equal endpoints. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b113-v14-04","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：失效診斷","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b113-v14-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「路線里程與端點」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Alignment chainage and endpoints” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只評洞內時間會漏掉入口管制或引道封閉的服務中斷。混用全線與單孔長度會同時扭曲工程數量、行程及逃生距離，造成方案比較失去共同基準。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"In-tunnel time omits service interruption at approach closures or entrance controls. Mixing whole-route and single-bore lengths distorts quantities, journey time and escape distance, destroying the common basis of an option comparison. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：比較方案必須使用相同起訖點，並分開主孔、引道及服務坑的工程數量；交通時間只是需求的一個指標，不能代替施工可達性或長期維修評估。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Travel time measures one service benefit but cannot replace assessment of construction access, maintenance closures or exposure to uncertain ground.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b113-v14-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只評洞內時間會漏掉入口管制或引道封閉的服務中斷。混用全線與單孔長度會同時扭曲工程數量、行程及逃生距離，造成方案比較失去共同基準。","textEn":"In-tunnel time omits service interruption at approach closures or entrance controls. Mixing whole-route and single-bore lengths distorts quantities, journey time and escape distance, destroying the common basis of an option comparison.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]},{"id":"b113-v14-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「服務邊界與路線代價」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","只評洞內時間會漏掉入口管制或引道封閉的服務中斷。","風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","In-tunnel time omits service interruption at approach closures or entrance controls.","Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel."],"answer":1,"explanation":"只評洞內時間會漏掉入口管制或引道封閉的服務中斷。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"In-tunnel time omits service interruption at approach closures or entrance controls. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b113-v14-05","title":"通風網路與壓力損失：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Ventilation network and pressure loss: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b113-v14-04"],"objective":"說明「風道摩擦壓損」如何影響聖伯納山隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Duct friction loss” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Great St Bernard Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"兩端高程與氣象不同使自然壓差影響雙向隧道風流，研究相同風機設定下季節變化。風機提供壓差，實際風量由風道摩阻、局部損失、外風與其他風機共同決定。支路開關會重新分配整個網路，不能把額定風量直接加總；正常污染稀釋與火災控煙也有不同目標，需要分別建立受控邊界和故障情境。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「風道摩擦壓損」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Different portal elevations and weather create natural pressure differences in bidirectional operation, even with unchanged fan settings. Fans supply pressure, but actual flow follows friction, local losses, external wind and interactions with other fans. Switching a branch redistributes the network rather than simply adding rated flows. Routine dilution and fire smoke control have different objectives, so each needs explicit boundaries, operating states and failure cases rather than one universal flow target. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Duct friction loss” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：達西因子=0.025 無因次；風道長度=980 m；水力直徑=4 m；空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；平均風速=3.1 m/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.025 dimensionless; duct length=980 m; hydraulic diameter=4 m; air density=1.2 kg/m³; mean velocity=3.1 m/s. Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=35.3168 Pa.","failure":"常見誤解：「風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「風道摩擦壓損」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Duct friction loss”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b113-v14-05-k1","title":"通風網路與壓力損失","titleEn":"Ventilation network and pressure loss","text":"兩端高程與氣象不同使自然壓差影響雙向隧道風流，研究相同風機設定下季節變化。風機提供壓差，實際風量由風道摩阻、局部損失、外風與其他風機共同決定。","textEn":"Different portal elevations and weather create natural pressure differences in bidirectional operation, even with unchanged fan settings. Fans supply pressure, but actual flow follows friction, local losses, external wind and interactions with other fans.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]},{"id":"b113-v14-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「通風網路與壓力損失」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Ventilation network and pressure loss\" is correct?","options":["風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。","照度越高就必然使隧道內所有物體更容易辨識。","兩端高程與氣象不同使自然壓差影響雙向隧道風流，研究相同風機設定下季節變化。"],"optionsEn":["Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.","Higher illuminance necessarily makes every tunnel object easier to detect.","Different portal elevations and weather create natural pressure differences in bidirectional operation, even with unchanged fan settings."],"answer":2,"explanation":"兩端高程與氣象不同使自然壓差影響雙向隧道風流，研究相同風機設定下季節變化。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Different portal elevations and weather create natural pressure differences in bidirectional operation, even with unchanged fan settings. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b113-v14-06","title":"通風網路與壓力損失：定量估算","titleEn":"Ventilation network and pressure loss: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b113-v14-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「風道摩擦壓損」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Duct friction loss” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：達西因子=0.025 無因次；風道長度=980 m；水力直徑=4 m；空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；平均風速=3.1 m/s。Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=35.3168 Pa。僅把平均風速增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為42.7333 Pa。邊界：定密度直管摩阻，局部損失及外風另計；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.025 dimensionless; duct length=980 m; hydraulic diameter=4 m; air density=1.2 kg/m³; mean velocity=3.1 m/s. Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=35.3168 Pa. Increasing only mean velocity by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 42.7333 Pa. Boundary: Constant-density straight-duct friction; local loss and external wind are separate. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同步量測兩端氣壓溫度與洞內風向。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Synchronise portal pressure and temperature with internal airflow direction.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b113-v14-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：達西因子=0.025 無因次；風道長度=980 m；水力直徑=4 m；空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；平均風速=3.1 m/s。Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=35.3168 Pa。僅把平均風速增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為42.7333 Pa。邊界：定密度直管摩阻，局部損失及外風另計；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.025 dimensionless; duct length=980 m; hydraulic diameter=4 m; air density=1.2 kg/m³; mean velocity=3.1 m/s. Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=35.3168 Pa. Increasing only mean velocity by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 42.7333 Pa. Boundary: Constant-density straight-duct friction; local loss and external wind are separate. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]},{"id":"b113-v14-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「通風網路與壓力損失」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Ventilation network and pressure loss\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：達西因子=0.025 無因次；風道長度=980 m；水力直徑=4 m；空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；平均風速=3.1 m/s。","目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。","混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.025 dimensionless.","No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.","Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：達西因子=0.025 無因次；風道長度=980 m；水力直徑=4 m；空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；平均風速=3.1 m/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.025 dimensionless; duct length=980 m; hydraulic diameter=4 m; air density=1.2 kg/m³; mean velocity=3.1 m/s. Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=35.3168 Pa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b113-v14-07","title":"通風網路與壓力損失：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Ventilation network and pressure loss: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b113-v14-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「風道摩擦壓損」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Duct friction loss” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同步量測兩端氣壓溫度與洞內風向。沿線同步量測靜壓與風速，記錄風門及其他風機狀態，再把實測工作點和風機曲線、網路壓損比較。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Synchronise portal pressure and temperature with internal airflow direction. Measure pressure and velocity synchronously, record dampers and other fans, and compare the measured duty point with fan curves and network resistance. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「風道摩擦壓損」的交付需回答：同步量測兩端氣壓溫度與洞內風向。驗收採明確風門和車流邊界，維修改線後重新核對網路工作點，火災模式由防災責任工程師簽認而非沿用正常模式。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Great St Bernard Tunnel, the duct friction loss handover must address the following evidence: Synchronise portal pressure and temperature with internal airflow direction. Commission with specified damper and traffic boundaries, recheck duty points after rerouting, and have the fire-safety engineer approve emergency modes independently.","failure":"注意干擾：季節反向風若當感測器故障，會漏掉真實邊界變化。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Seasonally reversed flow mistaken for sensor failure hides real boundary change. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b113-v14-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同步量測兩端氣壓溫度與洞內風向。沿線同步量測靜壓與風速，記錄風門及其他風機狀態，再把實測工作點和風機曲線、網路壓損比較。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Synchronise portal pressure and temperature with internal airflow direction. Measure pressure and velocity synchronously, record dampers and other fans, and compare the measured duty point with fan curves and network resistance. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]},{"id":"b113-v14-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「風道摩擦壓損」的交付需回答：同步量測兩端氣壓溫度與洞內風向。驗收採明確風門和車流邊界，維修改線後重新核對網路工作點，火災模式由防災責任工程師簽認而非沿用正常模式。","textEn":"For Great St Bernard Tunnel, the duct friction loss handover must address the following evidence: Synchronise portal pressure and temperature with internal airflow direction. Commission with specified damper and traffic boundaries, recheck duty points after rerouting, and have the fire-safety engineer approve emergency modes independently.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「通風網路與壓力損失」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Ventilation network and pressure loss\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","同步量測兩端氣壓溫度與洞內風向。","設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Synchronise portal pressure and temperature with internal airflow direction.","Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety."],"answer":1,"explanation":"同步量測兩端氣壓溫度與洞內風向。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Synchronise portal pressure and temperature with internal airflow direction. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b113-v14-08","title":"通風網路與壓力損失：失效診斷","titleEn":"Ventilation network and pressure loss: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b113-v14-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「風道摩擦壓損」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Duct friction loss” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"季節反向風若當感測器故障，會漏掉真實邊界變化。只看風機轉速會漏掉風門誤位或短路漏風，可能在總耗電增加時，真正需要的區段反而風量不足。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Seasonally reversed flow mistaken for sensor failure hides real boundary change. Fan speed alone misses a misplaced damper or leakage shortcut; total power may rise while the critical section receives less air. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：支路開關會重新分配整個網路，不能把額定風量直接加總；正常污染稀釋與火災控煙也有不同目標，需要分別建立受控邊界和故障情境。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Routine dilution and fire smoke control have different objectives, so each needs explicit boundaries, operating states and failure cases rather than one universal flow target.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b113-v14-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"季節反向風若當感測器故障，會漏掉真實邊界變化。只看風機轉速會漏掉風門誤位或短路漏風，可能在總耗電增加時，真正需要的區段反而風量不足。","textEn":"Seasonally reversed flow mistaken for sensor failure hides real boundary change. Fan speed alone misses a misplaced damper or leakage shortcut; total power may rise while the critical section receives less air.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]},{"id":"b113-v14-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「通風網路與壓力損失」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Ventilation network and pressure loss\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","照度越高就必然使隧道內所有物體更容易辨識。","季節反向風若當感測器故障，會漏掉真實邊界變化。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Higher illuminance necessarily makes every tunnel object easier to detect.","Seasonally reversed flow mistaken for sensor failure hides real boundary change."],"answer":2,"explanation":"季節反向風若當感測器故障，會漏掉真實邊界變化。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Seasonally reversed flow mistaken for sensor failure hides real boundary change. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b113-v14-s2","title":"機制、材料與定量設計","titleEn":"Mechanisms, materials and quantitative design","description":"本階段聚焦「視覺適應與路面亮度」與「溫度拘束與構件裂縫」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Visual adaptation and pavement luminance\" and \"Thermal restraint and component cracking\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b113-v14-09","title":"視覺適應與路面亮度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Visual adaptation and pavement luminance: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b113-v14-08"],"objective":"說明「漫反射亮度」如何影響聖伯納山隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Diffuse luminance” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Great St Bernard Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"高山洞口明暗背景可快速改變，聖伯納山教學檢查積雪反射與路面亮度的不同角色。駕駛從洞外進入洞內時視覺適應需要時間，照度並不等同從駕駛視角看到的亮度。路面反射、濕度、燈具配光及背景對比共同影響辨識；朗伯模型只示範理想漫反射，不能直接制定入口段燈具間距或真實道路安全值。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「漫反射亮度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Bright alpine portal backgrounds can change quickly; distinguish snow reflection from pavement luminance. Driver adaptation takes time when entering a tunnel, and illuminance is not the luminance seen from the driving position. Pavement reflection, wetness, luminaire distribution and background contrast affect detection. A Lambertian model illustrates ideal diffuse reflection only; it cannot establish entrance-zone spacing or actual road-safety limits without photometric and operational assessment. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Diffuse luminance” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：照度=104 lx；反射率=0.22 無因次。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: illuminance=104 lx; reflectance=0.22 dimensionless.","failure":"常見誤解：「照度越高就必然使隧道內所有物體更容易辨識。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Higher illuminance necessarily makes every tunnel object easier to detect.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「漫反射亮度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Diffuse luminance”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b113-v14-09-k1","title":"視覺適應與路面亮度","titleEn":"Visual adaptation and pavement luminance","text":"高山洞口明暗背景可快速改變，聖伯納山教學檢查積雪反射與路面亮度的不同角色。駕駛從洞外進入洞內時視覺適應需要時間，照度並不等同從駕駛視角看到的亮度。","textEn":"Bright alpine portal backgrounds can change quickly; distinguish snow reflection from pavement luminance. Driver adaptation takes time when entering a tunnel, and illuminance is not the luminance seen from the driving position.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]},{"id":"b113-v14-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：照度越高就必然使隧道內所有物體更容易辨識。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Higher illuminance necessarily makes every tunnel object easier to detect. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「視覺適應與路面亮度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Visual adaptation and pavement luminance\" is correct?","options":["高山洞口明暗背景可快速改變，聖伯納山教學檢查積雪反射與路面亮度的不同角色。","照度越高就必然使隧道內所有物體更容易辨識。","混凝土抗壓強度合格就代表厚壁構件不會產生熱裂縫。"],"optionsEn":["Bright alpine portal backgrounds can change quickly; distinguish snow reflection from pavement luminance.","Higher illuminance necessarily makes every tunnel object easier to detect.","Adequate compressive strength proves that thick concrete cannot develop thermal cracks."],"answer":0,"explanation":"高山洞口明暗背景可快速改變，聖伯納山教學檢查積雪反射與路面亮度的不同角色。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Bright alpine portal backgrounds can change quickly; distinguish snow reflection from pavement luminance. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b113-v14-10","title":"視覺適應與路面亮度：定量估算","titleEn":"Visual adaptation and pavement luminance: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b113-v14-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「漫反射亮度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Diffuse luminance” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：照度=104 lx；反射率=0.22 無因次。L=ρE/π=7.28293 cd/m²。僅把照度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為8.01122 cd/m²。邊界：理想朗伯漫反射，不是真實濕路面亮度；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: illuminance=104 lx; reflectance=0.22 dimensionless. L=ρE/π=7.28293 cd/m². Increasing only illuminance by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 8.01122 cd/m². Boundary: Ideal Lambertian reflection, not actual wet-road luminance. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在不同天空與積雪背景下量測入口視角亮度。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure entrance-view luminance under different sky and snow backgrounds.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b113-v14-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：照度=104 lx；反射率=0.22 無因次。L=ρE/π=7.28293 cd/m²。僅把照度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為8.01122 cd/m²。邊界：理想朗伯漫反射，不是真實濕路面亮度；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: illuminance=104 lx; reflectance=0.22 dimensionless. L=ρE/π=7.28293 cd/m². Increasing only illuminance by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 8.01122 cd/m². Boundary: Ideal Lambertian reflection, not actual wet-road luminance. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]},{"id":"b113-v14-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「視覺適應與路面亮度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Visual adaptation and pavement luminance\", which statement holds?","options":["擴散長度就是鋼筋開始腐蝕的位置和精確時間。","原創教學假設：照度=104 lx；反射率=0.22 無因次。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。"],"optionsEn":["Diffusion length gives the exact location and time of corrosion initiation.","Original teaching assumptions: illuminance=104 lx; reflectance=0.22 dimensionless.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：照度=104 lx；反射率=0.22 無因次。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: illuminance=104 lx; reflectance=0.22 dimensionless. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b113-v14-11","title":"視覺適應與路面亮度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Visual adaptation and pavement luminance: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b113-v14-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「漫反射亮度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Diffuse luminance” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在不同天空與積雪背景下量測入口視角亮度。以駕駛視角的亮度量測配合照度網格，分別檢查乾濕路面與燈具衰減，保留外部天空條件。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure entrance-view luminance under different sky and snow backgrounds. Combine driver-view luminance with illuminance grids, checking dry and wet pavement and lamp depreciation while preserving exterior sky conditions. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「漫反射亮度」的交付需回答：在不同天空與積雪背景下量測入口視角亮度。將視角、路面狀態和光度校正連同量測交付，照明調整需按核准場景測試，不把理想反射公式當驗收標準。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Great St Bernard Tunnel, the diffuse luminance handover must address the following evidence: Measure entrance-view luminance under different sky and snow backgrounds. Hand over viewing geometry, pavement state and photometric calibration; test changes against approved scenarios rather than treating ideal reflection as an acceptance criterion.","failure":"注意干擾：僅按洞內照度設定可能漏掉洞外高亮背景的適應需求。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Interior illuminance alone misses adaptation to a bright external background. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b113-v14-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在不同天空與積雪背景下量測入口視角亮度。以駕駛視角的亮度量測配合照度網格，分別檢查乾濕路面與燈具衰減，保留外部天空條件。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Measure entrance-view luminance under different sky and snow backgrounds. Combine driver-view luminance with illuminance grids, checking dry and wet pavement and lamp depreciation while preserving exterior sky conditions. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]},{"id":"b113-v14-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「漫反射亮度」的交付需回答：在不同天空與積雪背景下量測入口視角亮度。將視角、路面狀態和光度校正連同量測交付，照明調整需按核准場景測試，不把理想反射公式當驗收標準。","textEn":"For Great St Bernard Tunnel, the diffuse luminance handover must address the following evidence: Measure entrance-view luminance under different sky and snow backgrounds. Hand over viewing geometry, pavement state and photometric calibration; test changes against approved scenarios rather than treating ideal reflection as an acceptance criterion.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「視覺適應與路面亮度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Visual adaptation and pavement luminance\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。","在不同天空與積雪背景下量測入口視角亮度。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.","Measure entrance-view luminance under different sky and snow backgrounds."],"answer":2,"explanation":"在不同天空與積雪背景下量測入口視角亮度。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure entrance-view luminance under different sky and snow backgrounds. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b113-v14-12","title":"視覺適應與路面亮度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Visual adaptation and pavement luminance: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b113-v14-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「漫反射亮度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Diffuse luminance” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"僅按洞內照度設定可能漏掉洞外高亮背景的適應需求。照度平均值合格仍可能存在低亮度障礙區或眩光，感測器沾污也會使調光系統低估外界亮度。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Interior illuminance alone misses adaptation to a bright external background. Acceptable average illuminance can coexist with dark obstacles or glare, while sensor contamination may bias adaptive lighting controls. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：路面反射、濕度、燈具配光及背景對比共同影響辨識；朗伯模型只示範理想漫反射，不能直接制定入口段燈具間距或真實道路安全值。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A Lambertian model illustrates ideal diffuse reflection only; it cannot establish entrance-zone spacing or actual road-safety limits without photometric and operational assessment.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「照度越高就必然使隧道內所有物體更容易辨識。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Higher illuminance necessarily makes every tunnel object easier to detect.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b113-v14-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"僅按洞內照度設定可能漏掉洞外高亮背景的適應需求。照度平均值合格仍可能存在低亮度障礙區或眩光，感測器沾污也會使調光系統低估外界亮度。","textEn":"Interior illuminance alone misses adaptation to a bright external background. Acceptable average illuminance can coexist with dark obstacles or glare, while sensor contamination may bias adaptive lighting controls.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]},{"id":"b113-v14-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「視覺適應與路面亮度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Visual adaptation and pavement luminance\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["僅按洞內照度設定可能漏掉洞外高亮背景的適應需求。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","混凝土抗壓強度合格就代表厚壁構件不會產生熱裂縫。"],"optionsEn":["Interior illuminance alone misses adaptation to a bright external background.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Adequate compressive strength proves that thick concrete cannot develop thermal cracks."],"answer":0,"explanation":"僅按洞內照度設定可能漏掉洞外高亮背景的適應需求。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Interior illuminance alone misses adaptation to a bright external background. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b113-v14-13","title":"溫度拘束與構件裂縫：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Thermal restraint and component cracking: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b113-v14-12"],"objective":"說明「拘束溫度應變」如何影響聖伯納山隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Restrained thermal strain” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Great St Bernard Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"高山入口溫度循環影響混凝土與接縫，教材分開線膨脹拘束和凍融含水條件。厚壁構件在水化升溫後冷卻，若相鄰構件或基座限制收縮，熱應變會轉為拉應力。抗壓強度達標不等於抗裂合格，因為彈性模數成熟、徐變、溫度梯度與澆置順序都影響實際拘束；完全拘束彈性估算只能當量級上限比較。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「拘束溫度應變」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Portal temperature cycles affect concrete and joints; separate restrained expansion from moisture-dependent freeze-thaw behaviour. A thick element cools after hydration, and restraint from adjacent pours or its base converts contraction into tension. Compressive-strength compliance does not establish crack resistance because modulus development, creep, gradients and pour sequence influence restraint. A fully restrained elastic estimate is therefore a scale bound, not a prediction of actual cracking or residual stress. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Restrained thermal strain” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：線膨脹係數=1e-05 K⁻¹；溫差=22 K；彈性模數=25 GPa。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: expansion coefficient=1e-05 K⁻¹; temperature difference=22 K; elastic modulus=25 GPa. σ=EαΔT, GPa→MPa ×1000=5.5 MPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「混凝土抗壓強度合格就代表厚壁構件不會產生熱裂縫。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Adequate compressive strength proves that thick concrete cannot develop thermal cracks.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「拘束溫度應變」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Restrained thermal strain”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b113-v14-13-k1","title":"溫度拘束與構件裂縫","titleEn":"Thermal restraint and component cracking","text":"高山入口溫度循環影響混凝土與接縫，教材分開線膨脹拘束和凍融含水條件。厚壁構件在水化升溫後冷卻，若相鄰構件或基座限制收縮，熱應變會轉為拉應力。","textEn":"Portal temperature cycles affect concrete and joints; separate restrained expansion from moisture-dependent freeze-thaw behaviour. A thick element cools after hydration, and restraint from adjacent pours or its base converts contraction into tension.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]},{"id":"b113-v14-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：混凝土抗壓強度合格就代表厚壁構件不會產生熱裂縫。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Adequate compressive strength proves that thick concrete cannot develop thermal cracks. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「溫度拘束與構件裂縫」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Thermal restraint and component cracking\" is correct?","options":["混凝土抗壓強度合格就代表厚壁構件不會產生熱裂縫。","高山入口溫度循環影響混凝土與接縫，教材分開線膨脹拘束和凍融含水條件。","目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。"],"optionsEn":["Adequate compressive strength proves that thick concrete cannot develop thermal cracks.","Portal temperature cycles affect concrete and joints; separate restrained expansion from moisture-dependent freeze-thaw behaviour.","No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design."],"answer":1,"explanation":"高山入口溫度循環影響混凝土與接縫，教材分開線膨脹拘束和凍融含水條件。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Portal temperature cycles affect concrete and joints; separate restrained expansion from moisture-dependent freeze-thaw behaviour. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b113-v14-14","title":"溫度拘束與構件裂縫：定量估算","titleEn":"Thermal restraint and component cracking: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b113-v14-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「拘束溫度應變」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Restrained thermal strain” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：線膨脹係數=1e-05 K⁻¹；溫差=22 K；彈性模數=25 GPa。σ=EαΔT, GPa→MPa ×1000=5.5 MPa。僅把溫差增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為6.05 MPa。邊界：完全拘束線彈性量級，未含徐變開裂和拘束鬆弛；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: expansion coefficient=1e-05 K⁻¹; temperature difference=22 K; elastic modulus=25 GPa. σ=EαΔT, GPa→MPa ×1000=5.5 MPa. Increasing only temperature difference by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 6.05 MPa. Boundary: Fully restrained linear-elastic scale without creep, cracking or restraint relaxation. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將表面與內部溫度配對裂縫及滲水紀錄。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Pair surface and internal temperatures with cracking and leakage records.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b113-v14-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：線膨脹係數=1e-05 K⁻¹；溫差=22 K；彈性模數=25 GPa。σ=EαΔT, GPa→MPa ×1000=5.5 MPa。僅把溫差增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為6.05 MPa。邊界：完全拘束線彈性量級，未含徐變開裂和拘束鬆弛；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: expansion coefficient=1e-05 K⁻¹; temperature difference=22 K; elastic modulus=25 GPa. σ=EαΔT, GPa→MPa ×1000=5.5 MPa. Increasing only temperature difference by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 6.05 MPa. Boundary: Fully restrained linear-elastic scale without creep, cracking or restraint relaxation. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]},{"id":"b113-v14-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「溫度拘束與構件裂縫」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Thermal restraint and component cracking\", which statement holds?","options":["混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。","設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。","原創教學假設：線膨脹係數=1e-05 K⁻¹；溫差=22 K；彈性模數=25 GPa。"],"optionsEn":["Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure.","Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety.","Original teaching assumptions: expansion coefficient=1e-05 K⁻¹; temperature difference=22 K; elastic modulus=25 GPa. σ=EαΔT, GPa→MPa ×1000=5.5 MPa."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：線膨脹係數=1e-05 K⁻¹；溫差=22 K；彈性模數=25 GPa。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: expansion coefficient=1e-05 K⁻¹; temperature difference=22 K; elastic modulus=25 GPa. σ=EαΔT, GPa→MPa ×1000=5.5 MPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b113-v14-15","title":"溫度拘束與構件裂縫：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Thermal restraint and component cracking: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b113-v14-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「拘束溫度應變」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Restrained thermal strain” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將表面與內部溫度配對裂縫及滲水紀錄。記錄核心表面溫度及同條件試體成熟度，將裂縫位置與溫差、拆模及鄰段澆置時間配對，檢查熱歷程是否被遺漏。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Pair surface and internal temperatures with cracking and leakage records. Record core/surface temperature and matched-cured maturity, pairing cracks with temperature differences, formwork removal and adjacent pours to identify missing thermal history. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「拘束溫度應變」的交付需回答：將表面與內部溫度配對裂縫及滲水紀錄。澆置前核准溫度監測及養護方案，變更材料、拆模或澆置順序時重新檢查熱分析，將裂縫與接縫止水的責任一併交付。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Great St Bernard Tunnel, the restrained thermal strain handover must address the following evidence: Pair surface and internal temperatures with cracking and leakage records. Approve monitoring and curing before pours, revisit thermal analysis after material or sequence changes, and hand over crack and waterstop responsibilities together.","failure":"注意干擾：熱應力式不能單獨預測凍融剝落，兩機制不可混用。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Thermal-stress equations alone cannot predict freeze-thaw scaling. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b113-v14-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將表面與內部溫度配對裂縫及滲水紀錄。記錄核心表面溫度及同條件試體成熟度，將裂縫位置與溫差、拆模及鄰段澆置時間配對，檢查熱歷程是否被遺漏。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Pair surface and internal temperatures with cracking and leakage records. Record core/surface temperature and matched-cured maturity, pairing cracks with temperature differences, formwork removal and adjacent pours to identify missing thermal history. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]},{"id":"b113-v14-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「拘束溫度應變」的交付需回答：將表面與內部溫度配對裂縫及滲水紀錄。澆置前核准溫度監測及養護方案，變更材料、拆模或澆置順序時重新檢查熱分析，將裂縫與接縫止水的責任一併交付。","textEn":"For Great St Bernard Tunnel, the restrained thermal strain handover must address the following evidence: Pair surface and internal temperatures with cracking and leakage records. Approve monitoring and curing before pours, revisit thermal analysis after material or sequence changes, and hand over crack and waterstop responsibilities together.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「溫度拘束與構件裂縫」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Thermal restraint and component cracking\"?","options":["將表面與內部溫度配對裂縫及滲水紀錄。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Pair surface and internal temperatures with cracking and leakage records.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將表面與內部溫度配對裂縫及滲水紀錄。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Pair surface and internal temperatures with cracking and leakage records. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b113-v14-16","title":"溫度拘束與構件裂縫：失效診斷","titleEn":"Thermal restraint and component cracking: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b113-v14-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「拘束溫度應變」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Restrained thermal strain” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"熱應力式不能單獨預測凍融剝落，兩機制不可混用。標準養護試體合格而現場過早冷卻，仍可能形成貫穿裂縫並影響止水；僅增加後續抗壓試驗無法重建失去的養護。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Thermal-stress equations alone cannot predict freeze-thaw scaling. Passing standard-cured specimens does not prevent through-cracking after rapid cooling, and more later strength tests cannot reconstruct inadequate curing. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：抗壓強度達標不等於抗裂合格，因為彈性模數成熟、徐變、溫度梯度與澆置順序都影響實際拘束；完全拘束彈性估算只能當量級上限比較。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A fully restrained elastic estimate is therefore a scale bound, not a prediction of actual cracking or residual stress.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「混凝土抗壓強度合格就代表厚壁構件不會產生熱裂縫。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Adequate compressive strength proves that thick concrete cannot develop thermal cracks.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b113-v14-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"熱應力式不能單獨預測凍融剝落，兩機制不可混用。標準養護試體合格而現場過早冷卻，仍可能形成貫穿裂縫並影響止水；僅增加後續抗壓試驗無法重建失去的養護。","textEn":"Thermal-stress equations alone cannot predict freeze-thaw scaling. Passing standard-cured specimens does not prevent through-cracking after rapid cooling, and more later strength tests cannot reconstruct inadequate curing.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]},{"id":"b113-v14-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「溫度拘束與構件裂縫」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Thermal restraint and component cracking\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","熱應力式不能單獨預測凍融剝落，兩機制不可混用。","目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Thermal-stress equations alone cannot predict freeze-thaw scaling.","No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design."],"answer":1,"explanation":"熱應力式不能單獨預測凍融剝落，兩機制不可混用。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Thermal-stress equations alone cannot predict freeze-thaw scaling. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b113-v14-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」與「氯鹽遷移與耐久判讀」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\" and \"Chloride transport and durability interpretation\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b113-v14-17","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b113-v14-16"],"objective":"說明「測壓水頭」如何影響聖伯納山隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Piezometric head” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Great St Bernard Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"高山融雪補注和道路帶入水需分流判讀，研究聖伯納山背景下排水增量是否跟隨季節或車流。水壓取決於連通含水層的測壓水頭，不必等於地表或海面至洞頂的幾何深度。排水降低水壓卻可能增加有效應力與沉陷；停泵或排水堵塞後水頭又會回升，因此防水、排水及環境保水是互相制約的設計選擇。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「測壓水頭」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Separate snowmelt recharge and road-carried water, checking whether drainage changes follow season or traffic. Water pressure follows piezometric head in the connected aquifer, not automatically the geometric depth below ground or sea level. Drainage reduces pressure but can increase effective stress and settlement. Head may recover after a pump outage or blockage, coupling waterproofing, drainage capacity and preservation of surrounding groundwater in the permanent design. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Piezometric head” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=82 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=82 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=804.42 kPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「測壓水頭」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Piezometric head”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b113-v14-17-k1","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure","text":"高山融雪補注和道路帶入水需分流判讀，研究聖伯納山背景下排水增量是否跟隨季節或車流。水壓取決於連通含水層的測壓水頭，不必等於地表或海面至洞頂的幾何深度。","textEn":"Separate snowmelt recharge and road-carried water, checking whether drainage changes follow season or traffic. Water pressure follows piezometric head in the connected aquifer, not automatically the geometric depth below ground or sea level.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]},{"id":"b113-v14-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\" is correct?","options":["目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。","擴散長度就是鋼筋開始腐蝕的位置和精確時間。","高山融雪補注和道路帶入水需分流判讀，研究聖伯納山背景下排水增量是否跟隨季節或車流。"],"optionsEn":["No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.","Diffusion length gives the exact location and time of corrosion initiation.","Separate snowmelt recharge and road-carried water, checking whether drainage changes follow season or traffic."],"answer":2,"explanation":"高山融雪補注和道路帶入水需分流判讀，研究聖伯納山背景下排水增量是否跟隨季節或車流。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Separate snowmelt recharge and road-carried water, checking whether drainage changes follow season or traffic. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b113-v14-18","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓：定量估算","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b113-v14-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「測壓水頭」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Piezometric head” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=82 m。p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=804.42 kPa。僅把水頭增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為884.862 kPa。邊界：靜水表壓，不是土體總壓或原位量測；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=82 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=804.42 kPa. Increasing only head by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 884.862 kPa. Boundary: Hydrostatic gauge pressure, not total earth pressure or an in-situ measurement. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：對照融雪期、降雨和車流時序的水量。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare flow with snowmelt, rainfall and traffic histories.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b113-v14-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=82 m。p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=804.42 kPa。僅把水頭增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為884.862 kPa。邊界：靜水表壓，不是土體總壓或原位量測；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=82 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=804.42 kPa. Increasing only head by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 884.862 kPa. Boundary: Hydrostatic gauge pressure, not total earth pressure or an in-situ measurement. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]},{"id":"b113-v14-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=82 m。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=82 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=804.42 kPa.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=82 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=82 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=804.42 kPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b113-v14-19","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b113-v14-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「測壓水頭」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Piezometric head” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"對照融雪期、降雨和車流時序的水量。使用分層測壓管及流量計，配合降雨或潮位序列分辨補注與設備影響，將讀值統一換算至同一高程基準。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare flow with snowmelt, rainfall and traffic histories. Use nested piezometers and flowmeters with rainfall or tide histories to distinguish recharge from equipment effects, converting observations to a common elevation datum. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「測壓水頭」的交付需回答：對照融雪期、降雨和車流時序的水量。設計檢核應分列正常排水、堵塞與停電水位，將環境受體的容許變化和監測責任一起交付，不把抽水量當唯一指標。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Great St Bernard Tunnel, the piezometric head handover must address the following evidence: Compare flow with snowmelt, rainfall and traffic histories. Separate normal drainage, blocked-drain and power-outage heads and hand over receptor limits and monitoring responsibility together rather than using pump flow as the sole indicator.","failure":"注意干擾：車輛帶入水若當地下水增壓會誤導襯砌判讀。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Road-carried water misclassified as rising groundwater misleads lining assessment. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b113-v14-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"對照融雪期、降雨和車流時序的水量。使用分層測壓管及流量計，配合降雨或潮位序列分辨補注與設備影響，將讀值統一換算至同一高程基準。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Compare flow with snowmelt, rainfall and traffic histories. Use nested piezometers and flowmeters with rainfall or tide histories to distinguish recharge from equipment effects, converting observations to a common elevation datum. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]},{"id":"b113-v14-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「測壓水頭」的交付需回答：對照融雪期、降雨和車流時序的水量。設計檢核應分列正常排水、堵塞與停電水位，將環境受體的容許變化和監測責任一起交付，不把抽水量當唯一指標。","textEn":"For Great St Bernard Tunnel, the piezometric head handover must address the following evidence: Compare flow with snowmelt, rainfall and traffic histories. Separate normal drainage, blocked-drain and power-outage heads and hand over receptor limits and monitoring responsibility together rather than using pump flow as the sole indicator.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","對照融雪期、降雨和車流時序的水量。","風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Compare flow with snowmelt, rainfall and traffic histories.","Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel."],"answer":1,"explanation":"對照融雪期、降雨和車流時序的水量。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare flow with snowmelt, rainfall and traffic histories. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b113-v14-20","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓：失效診斷","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b113-v14-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「測壓水頭」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Piezometric head” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"車輛帶入水若當地下水增壓會誤導襯砌判讀。將暫時降水後的低水頭當成永久狀態，會漏掉停泵後外壓回升；過度排水也可能引起周邊地層壓密。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Road-carried water misclassified as rising groundwater misleads lining assessment. Treating temporarily lowered head as permanent misses pressure recovery after outage; excessive drainage can also consolidate surrounding ground. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：排水降低水壓卻可能增加有效應力與沉陷；停泵或排水堵塞後水頭又會回升，因此防水、排水及環境保水是互相制約的設計選擇。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Head may recover after a pump outage or blockage, coupling waterproofing, drainage capacity and preservation of surrounding groundwater in the permanent design.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b113-v14-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"車輛帶入水若當地下水增壓會誤導襯砌判讀。將暫時降水後的低水頭當成永久狀態，會漏掉停泵後外壓回升；過度排水也可能引起周邊地層壓密。","textEn":"Road-carried water misclassified as rising groundwater misleads lining assessment. Treating temporarily lowered head as permanent misses pressure recovery after outage; excessive drainage can also consolidate surrounding ground.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]},{"id":"b113-v14-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","擴散長度就是鋼筋開始腐蝕的位置和精確時間。","車輛帶入水若當地下水增壓會誤導襯砌判讀。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Diffusion length gives the exact location and time of corrosion initiation.","Road-carried water misclassified as rising groundwater misleads lining assessment."],"answer":2,"explanation":"車輛帶入水若當地下水增壓會誤導襯砌判讀。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Road-carried water misclassified as rising groundwater misleads lining assessment. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b113-v14-21","title":"氯鹽遷移與耐久判讀：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Chloride transport and durability interpretation: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b113-v14-20"],"objective":"說明「擴散特徵長度」如何影響聖伯納山隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Diffusion characteristic length” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Great St Bernard Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"除冰鹽帶入的暴露可能集中於路側低區，不能以高處乾燥取樣代表整個斷面。海水或除冰鹽可提供氯離子，材料孔隙與裂縫控制其傳輸；鋼筋腐蝕還需要局部電化學條件。平方根擴散長度僅顯示時間尺度，並不是腐蝕門檻深度；表面濃度變化、乾濕循環、結合效應及施工裂縫須另行辨識。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「擴散特徵長度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Deicing-salt exposure can concentrate near low roadside zones, so dry high-level samples do not represent the section. Seawater or deicing salt supplies chloride, while pores and cracks govern transport; reinforcement corrosion also depends on local electrochemical conditions. A square-root diffusion length indicates a time scale, not a corrosion-threshold depth. Surface concentration, wetting cycles, binding and construction cracks must be distinguished rather than hidden in one fitted diffusivity. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Diffusion characteristic length” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：擴散係數=1e-12 m²/s；暴露時間=15 year。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: diffusivity=1e-12 m²/s; exposure=15 year. ℓ=√(Dt); 1 year=365.25×86400 s; m→mm ×1000=21.7569 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「擴散長度就是鋼筋開始腐蝕的位置和精確時間。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Diffusion length gives the exact location and time of corrosion initiation.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「擴散特徵長度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Diffusion characteristic length”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b113-v14-21-k1","title":"氯鹽遷移與耐久判讀","titleEn":"Chloride transport and durability interpretation","text":"除冰鹽帶入的暴露可能集中於路側低區，不能以高處乾燥取樣代表整個斷面。海水或除冰鹽可提供氯離子，材料孔隙與裂縫控制其傳輸；鋼筋腐蝕還需要局部電化學條件。","textEn":"Deicing-salt exposure can concentrate near low roadside zones, so dry high-level samples do not represent the section. Seawater or deicing salt supplies chloride, while pores and cracks govern transport; reinforcement corrosion also depends on local electrochemical conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]},{"id":"b113-v14-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：擴散長度就是鋼筋開始腐蝕的位置和精確時間。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Diffusion length gives the exact location and time of corrosion initiation. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「氯鹽遷移與耐久判讀」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Chloride transport and durability interpretation\" is correct?","options":["除冰鹽帶入的暴露可能集中於路側低區，不能以高處乾燥取樣代表整個斷面。","擴散長度就是鋼筋開始腐蝕的位置和精確時間。","混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。"],"optionsEn":["Deicing-salt exposure can concentrate near low roadside zones, so dry high-level samples do not represent the section.","Diffusion length gives the exact location and time of corrosion initiation.","Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure."],"answer":0,"explanation":"除冰鹽帶入的暴露可能集中於路側低區，不能以高處乾燥取樣代表整個斷面。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Deicing-salt exposure can concentrate near low roadside zones, so dry high-level samples do not represent the section. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b113-v14-22","title":"氯鹽遷移與耐久判讀：定量估算","titleEn":"Chloride transport and durability interpretation: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b113-v14-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「擴散特徵長度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Diffusion characteristic length” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：擴散係數=1e-12 m²/s；暴露時間=15 year。ℓ=√(Dt); 1 year=365.25×86400 s; m→mm ×1000=21.7569 mm。僅把暴露時間增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為22.8189 mm。邊界：特徵長度，不是腐蝕起始壽命或氯鹽門檻深度；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: diffusivity=1e-12 m²/s; exposure=15 year. ℓ=√(Dt); 1 year=365.25×86400 s; m→mm ×1000=21.7569 mm. Increasing only exposure by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 22.8189 mm. Boundary: Characteristic length, not corrosion-initiation life or chloride-threshold depth. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：按高度與距車道位置比較氯鹽、含水及裂縫。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare chloride, moisture and cracks by height and distance from traffic.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b113-v14-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：擴散係數=1e-12 m²/s；暴露時間=15 year。ℓ=√(Dt); 1 year=365.25×86400 s; m→mm ×1000=21.7569 mm。僅把暴露時間增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為22.8189 mm。邊界：特徵長度，不是腐蝕起始壽命或氯鹽門檻深度；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: diffusivity=1e-12 m²/s; exposure=15 year. ℓ=√(Dt); 1 year=365.25×86400 s; m→mm ×1000=21.7569 mm. Increasing only exposure by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 22.8189 mm. Boundary: Characteristic length, not corrosion-initiation life or chloride-threshold depth. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]},{"id":"b113-v14-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「氯鹽遷移與耐久判讀」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Chloride transport and durability interpretation\", which statement holds?","options":["設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。","原創教學假設：擴散係數=1e-12 m²/s；暴露時間=15 year。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety.","Original teaching assumptions: diffusivity=1e-12 m²/s; exposure=15 year. ℓ=√(Dt); 1 year=365.25×86400 s; m→mm ×1000=21.7569 mm.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：擴散係數=1e-12 m²/s；暴露時間=15 year。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: diffusivity=1e-12 m²/s; exposure=15 year. ℓ=√(Dt); 1 year=365.25×86400 s; m→mm ×1000=21.7569 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b113-v14-23","title":"氯鹽遷移與耐久判讀：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Chloride transport and durability interpretation: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b113-v14-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「擴散特徵長度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Diffusion characteristic length” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"按高度與距車道位置比較氯鹽、含水及裂縫。以分層取樣的氯鹽剖面配合裂縫圖與電位量測，檢查擴散模型是否只適用未開裂材料。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare chloride, moisture and cracks by height and distance from traffic. Combine depth-resolved chloride samples with crack maps and potential measurements, checking whether the diffusion model applies only to uncracked material. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「擴散特徵長度」的交付需回答：按高度與距車道位置比較氯鹽、含水及裂縫。保留取樣深度、含水狀態及材料批次，用多種證據解釋劣化；維修優先序依構件功能與實際病害制定。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Great St Bernard Tunnel, the diffusion characteristic length handover must address the following evidence: Compare chloride, moisture and cracks by height and distance from traffic. Retain sample depth, moisture and material batches and interpret deterioration using multiple evidence types; prioritise repairs by function and observed defects.","failure":"注意干擾：採樣位置偏乾會系統性低估易濕區劣化。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Sampling dry locations systematically understates deterioration in wet zones. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b113-v14-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"按高度與距車道位置比較氯鹽、含水及裂縫。以分層取樣的氯鹽剖面配合裂縫圖與電位量測，檢查擴散模型是否只適用未開裂材料。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Compare chloride, moisture and cracks by height and distance from traffic. Combine depth-resolved chloride samples with crack maps and potential measurements, checking whether the diffusion model applies only to uncracked material. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]},{"id":"b113-v14-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「擴散特徵長度」的交付需回答：按高度與距車道位置比較氯鹽、含水及裂縫。保留取樣深度、含水狀態及材料批次，用多種證據解釋劣化；維修優先序依構件功能與實際病害制定。","textEn":"For Great St Bernard Tunnel, the diffusion characteristic length handover must address the following evidence: Compare chloride, moisture and cracks by height and distance from traffic. Retain sample depth, moisture and material batches and interpret deterioration using multiple evidence types; prioritise repairs by function and observed defects.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「氯鹽遷移與耐久判讀」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Chloride transport and durability interpretation\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","照度越高就必然使隧道內所有物體更容易辨識。","按高度與距車道位置比較氯鹽、含水及裂縫。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Higher illuminance necessarily makes every tunnel object easier to detect.","Compare chloride, moisture and cracks by height and distance from traffic."],"answer":2,"explanation":"按高度與距車道位置比較氯鹽、含水及裂縫。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare chloride, moisture and cracks by height and distance from traffic. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b113-v14-24","title":"氯鹽遷移與耐久判讀：失效診斷","titleEn":"Chloride transport and durability interpretation: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b113-v14-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「擴散特徵長度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Diffusion characteristic length” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"採樣位置偏乾會系統性低估易濕區劣化。把一次電位讀值當腐蝕速率會誤判剩餘壽命，裂縫快速傳輸也可能被平均材料係數掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Sampling dry locations systematically understates deterioration in wet zones. Treating one potential reading as corrosion rate misjudges remaining life, while averaged material coefficients conceal rapid crack transport. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：平方根擴散長度僅顯示時間尺度，並不是腐蝕門檻深度；表面濃度變化、乾濕循環、結合效應及施工裂縫須另行辨識。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Surface concentration, wetting cycles, binding and construction cracks must be distinguished rather than hidden in one fitted diffusivity.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「擴散長度就是鋼筋開始腐蝕的位置和精確時間。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Diffusion length gives the exact location and time of corrosion initiation.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b113-v14-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"採樣位置偏乾會系統性低估易濕區劣化。把一次電位讀值當腐蝕速率會誤判剩餘壽命，裂縫快速傳輸也可能被平均材料係數掩蓋。","textEn":"Sampling dry locations systematically understates deterioration in wet zones. Treating one potential reading as corrosion rate misjudges remaining life, while averaged material coefficients conceal rapid crack transport.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]},{"id":"b113-v14-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「氯鹽遷移與耐久判讀」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Chloride transport and durability interpretation\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["採樣位置偏乾會系統性低估易濕區劣化。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。"],"optionsEn":["Sampling dry locations systematically understates deterioration in wet zones.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure."],"answer":0,"explanation":"採樣位置偏乾會系統性低估易濕區劣化。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Sampling dry locations systematically understates deterioration in wet zones. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b113-v14-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「環向受力與接縫柔度」與「疏散時間與分區可用性」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Ring force and joint flexibility\" and \"Evacuation time and zone availability\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b113-v14-25","title":"環向受力與接縫柔度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Ring force and joint flexibility: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b113-v14-24"],"objective":"說明「襯砌環向壓縮」如何影響聖伯納山隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Lining hoop compression” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Great St Bernard Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"既有襯砌修補前先辨認地層荷載、漏水與材料劣化，聖伯納山教材不把所有裂縫歸為強度不足。圓形襯砌對均勻外壓可主要以環向壓縮抵抗，但接頭轉動、偏壓與背填空隙會引起彎矩。薄環膜應力只說明其中一條受力路徑；脫模、運輸、頂推及永久狀態的荷載不同，環片局部接觸與止水條件必須另外檢核。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「襯砌環向壓縮」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Before lining repair, distinguish ground loading, leakage and material deterioration instead of treating all cracks as inadequate strength. A circular lining resists uniform external pressure largely through hoop compression, but joint rotation, uneven load and backfill voids generate bending. Thin-ring membrane stress describes only one load path. Demoulding, transport, jacking and permanent states impose different actions, requiring separate checks of local segment contact and sealing rather than one permanent-load calculation. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Lining hoop compression” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：均勻外壓=0.54 MPa；半徑=3.6 m；厚度=0.35 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: uniform external pressure=0.54 MPa; radius=3.6 m; thickness=0.35 m. σθ=pr/t=5.55429 MPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「襯砌環向壓縮」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Lining hoop compression”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b113-v14-25-k1","title":"環向受力與接縫柔度","titleEn":"Ring force and joint flexibility","text":"既有襯砌修補前先辨認地層荷載、漏水與材料劣化，聖伯納山教材不把所有裂縫歸為強度不足。圓形襯砌對均勻外壓可主要以環向壓縮抵抗，但接頭轉動、偏壓與背填空隙會引起彎矩。","textEn":"Before lining repair, distinguish ground loading, leakage and material deterioration instead of treating all cracks as inadequate strength. A circular lining resists uniform external pressure largely through hoop compression, but joint rotation, uneven load and backfill voids generate bending.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]},{"id":"b113-v14-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「環向受力與接縫柔度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Ring force and joint flexibility\" is correct?","options":["混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。","既有襯砌修補前先辨認地層荷載、漏水與材料劣化，聖伯納山教材不把所有裂縫歸為強度不足。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。"],"optionsEn":["Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure.","Before lining repair, distinguish ground loading, leakage and material deterioration instead of treating all cracks as inadequate strength.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time."],"answer":1,"explanation":"既有襯砌修補前先辨認地層荷載、漏水與材料劣化，聖伯納山教材不把所有裂縫歸為強度不足。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Before lining repair, distinguish ground loading, leakage and material deterioration instead of treating all cracks as inadequate strength. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b113-v14-26","title":"環向受力與接縫柔度：定量估算","titleEn":"Ring force and joint flexibility: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b113-v14-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「襯砌環向壓縮」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Lining hoop compression” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：均勻外壓=0.54 MPa；半徑=3.6 m；厚度=0.35 m。σθ=pr/t=5.55429 MPa。僅把均勻外壓增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為6.10971 MPa。邊界：薄圓環膜應力，不是接縫、偏壓或矩形框架解；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: uniform external pressure=0.54 MPa; radius=3.6 m; thickness=0.35 m. σθ=pr/t=5.55429 MPa. Increasing only uniform external pressure by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 6.10971 MPa. Boundary: Thin circular-ring membrane stress, not a joint, uneven-load or rectangular-frame solution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比較裂縫方向、季節開合與外水頭變化。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare crack orientation and seasonal opening against external head changes.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b113-v14-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：均勻外壓=0.54 MPa；半徑=3.6 m；厚度=0.35 m。σθ=pr/t=5.55429 MPa。僅把均勻外壓增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為6.10971 MPa。邊界：薄圓環膜應力，不是接縫、偏壓或矩形框架解；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: uniform external pressure=0.54 MPa; radius=3.6 m; thickness=0.35 m. σθ=pr/t=5.55429 MPa. Increasing only uniform external pressure by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 6.10971 MPa. Boundary: Thin circular-ring membrane stress, not a joint, uneven-load or rectangular-frame solution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]},{"id":"b113-v14-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「環向受力與接縫柔度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Ring force and joint flexibility\", which statement holds?","options":["全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。","風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。","原創教學假設：均勻外壓=0.54 MPa；半徑=3.6 m；厚度=0.35 m。"],"optionsEn":["Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.","Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.","Original teaching assumptions: uniform external pressure=0.54 MPa; radius=3.6 m; thickness=0.35 m. σθ=pr/t=5.55429 MPa."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：均勻外壓=0.54 MPa；半徑=3.6 m；厚度=0.35 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: uniform external pressure=0.54 MPa; radius=3.6 m; thickness=0.35 m. σθ=pr/t=5.55429 MPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b113-v14-27","title":"環向受力與接縫柔度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Ring force and joint flexibility: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b113-v14-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「襯砌環向壓縮」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Lining hoop compression” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比較裂縫方向、季節開合與外水頭變化。將環形變形、接縫張開與應變和含接頭彈簧的模型比較，分開安裝後、背填後及水頭回升後的基準。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare crack orientation and seasonal opening against external head changes. Compare ring distortion, joint opening and strain with a joint-spring model, separating baselines after installation, grouting and head recovery. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「襯砌環向壓縮」的交付需回答：比較裂縫方向、季節開合與外水頭變化。設計圖應分開標註各施工階段、接頭剛度及背填條件，構件驗收同時核對幾何、材料批次與止水試驗適用包絡。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Great St Bernard Tunnel, the lining hoop compression handover must address the following evidence: Compare crack orientation and seasonal opening against external head changes. Drawings distinguish stages, joint stiffness and backfill conditions; component acceptance reconciles geometry, material batches and the applicable sealing-test envelope.","failure":"注意干擾：表面補縫而未辨認持續變形會反覆出現同類病害。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Surface sealing without identifying continuing movement leads to recurrent defects. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b113-v14-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比較裂縫方向、季節開合與外水頭變化。將環形變形、接縫張開與應變和含接頭彈簧的模型比較，分開安裝後、背填後及水頭回升後的基準。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Compare crack orientation and seasonal opening against external head changes. Compare ring distortion, joint opening and strain with a joint-spring model, separating baselines after installation, grouting and head recovery. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]},{"id":"b113-v14-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「襯砌環向壓縮」的交付需回答：比較裂縫方向、季節開合與外水頭變化。設計圖應分開標註各施工階段、接頭剛度及背填條件，構件驗收同時核對幾何、材料批次與止水試驗適用包絡。","textEn":"For Great St Bernard Tunnel, the lining hoop compression handover must address the following evidence: Compare crack orientation and seasonal opening against external head changes. Drawings distinguish stages, joint stiffness and backfill conditions; component acceptance reconciles geometry, material batches and the applicable sealing-test envelope.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「環向受力與接縫柔度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Ring force and joint flexibility\"?","options":["比較裂縫方向、季節開合與外水頭變化。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","混凝土抗壓強度合格就代表厚壁構件不會產生熱裂縫。"],"optionsEn":["Compare crack orientation and seasonal opening against external head changes.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Adequate compressive strength proves that thick concrete cannot develop thermal cracks."],"answer":0,"explanation":"比較裂縫方向、季節開合與外水頭變化。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare crack orientation and seasonal opening against external head changes. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b113-v14-28","title":"環向受力與接縫柔度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Ring force and joint flexibility: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b113-v14-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「襯砌環向壓縮」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Lining hoop compression” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"表面補縫而未辨認持續變形會反覆出現同類病害。局部脫空增加環片彎曲，裂縫未必代表混凝土平均強度不足；忽略接縫接觸會把補強方向導向錯誤位置。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Surface sealing without identifying continuing movement leads to recurrent defects. Local voids increase bending, so cracks need not indicate inadequate mean concrete strength; neglecting joint contact can misdirect strengthening. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：薄環膜應力只說明其中一條受力路徑；脫模、運輸、頂推及永久狀態的荷載不同，環片局部接觸與止水條件必須另外檢核。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Demoulding, transport, jacking and permanent states impose different actions, requiring separate checks of local segment contact and sealing rather than one permanent-load calculation.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b113-v14-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"表面補縫而未辨認持續變形會反覆出現同類病害。局部脫空增加環片彎曲，裂縫未必代表混凝土平均強度不足；忽略接縫接觸會把補強方向導向錯誤位置。","textEn":"Surface sealing without identifying continuing movement leads to recurrent defects. Local voids increase bending, so cracks need not indicate inadequate mean concrete strength; neglecting joint contact can misdirect strengthening.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]},{"id":"b113-v14-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「環向受力與接縫柔度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Ring force and joint flexibility\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","表面補縫而未辨認持續變形會反覆出現同類病害。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Surface sealing without identifying continuing movement leads to recurrent defects.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time."],"answer":1,"explanation":"表面補縫而未辨認持續變形會反覆出現同類病害。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Surface sealing without identifying continuing movement leads to recurrent defects. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b113-v14-29","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b113-v14-28"],"objective":"說明「所需疏散時間」如何影響聖伯納山隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Required evacuation time” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Great St Bernard Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"雙向交通中事故兩側使用者位置不同，教學路徑分別處理回頭、停車與前方阻隔情境。疏散時間包含辨識、反應、移動及排隊，不只由出口距離決定。人員速度會受煙熱、能見度及行動能力影響，安全判斷還要比較可用安全時間；橫通道存在但門或鄰孔不可用時，圖上的最短路線不一定能作實際選擇。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「所需疏散時間」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Users lie on different sides of an incident in bidirectional traffic; distinguish turnaround, stopped queues and blocked-forward-path cases. Evacuation includes detection, response, travel and queues, not merely distance to an exit. Smoke, visibility and mobility alter walking speed, while safety requires comparison with available safe time. A passage shown on a plan may be unusable because its door or receiving bore is unavailable, invalidating the nominal shortest route. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Required evacuation time” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：前置時間=104 s；行走距離=340 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=104 s; travel distance=340 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「所需疏散時間」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Required evacuation time”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b113-v14-29-k1","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability","text":"雙向交通中事故兩側使用者位置不同，教學路徑分別處理回頭、停車與前方阻隔情境。疏散時間包含辨識、反應、移動及排隊，不只由出口距離決定。","textEn":"Users lie on different sides of an incident in bidirectional traffic; distinguish turnaround, stopped queues and blocked-forward-path cases. Evacuation includes detection, response, travel and queues, not merely distance to an exit.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]},{"id":"b113-v14-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「疏散時間與分區可用性」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Evacuation time and zone availability\" is correct?","options":["只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。","設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。","雙向交通中事故兩側使用者位置不同，教學路徑分別處理回頭、停車與前方阻隔情境。"],"optionsEn":["Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.","Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety.","Users lie on different sides of an incident in bidirectional traffic; distinguish turnaround, stopped queues and blocked-forward-path cases."],"answer":2,"explanation":"雙向交通中事故兩側使用者位置不同，教學路徑分別處理回頭、停車與前方阻隔情境。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Users lie on different sides of an incident in bidirectional traffic; distinguish turnaround, stopped queues and blocked-forward-path cases. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b113-v14-30","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性：定量估算","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b113-v14-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「所需疏散時間」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Required evacuation time” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：前置時間=104 s；行走距離=340 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。RSET=tpre+d/v=529 s。僅把行走距離增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為571.5 s。邊界：單群體固定速度，不含排隊煙熱及能力差異，不能單獨判安全；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=104 s; travel distance=340 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s. RSET=tpre+d/v=529 s. Increasing only travel distance by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 571.5 s. Boundary: One group at fixed speed without queues, smoke or mobility differences; not a safety conclusion. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用不同起始位置測試通道及訊息可見性。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Test passage availability and message visibility from different starting positions.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b113-v14-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：前置時間=104 s；行走距離=340 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。RSET=tpre+d/v=529 s。僅把行走距離增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為571.5 s。邊界：單群體固定速度，不含排隊煙熱及能力差異，不能單獨判安全；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=104 s; travel distance=340 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s. RSET=tpre+d/v=529 s. Increasing only travel distance by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 571.5 s. Boundary: One group at fixed speed without queues, smoke or mobility differences; not a safety conclusion. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]},{"id":"b113-v14-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「疏散時間與分區可用性」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Evacuation time and zone availability\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：前置時間=104 s；行走距離=340 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。","照度越高就必然使隧道內所有物體更容易辨識。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=104 s; travel distance=340 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.","Higher illuminance necessarily makes every tunnel object easier to detect."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：前置時間=104 s；行走距離=340 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=104 s; travel distance=340 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b113-v14-31","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b113-v14-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「所需疏散時間」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Required evacuation time” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用不同起始位置測試通道及訊息可見性。以人流模擬或受控演練分辨前置時間、行走與門口排隊，核對每個出口接收區的可用狀態及通訊紀錄。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Test passage availability and message visibility from different starting positions. Separate pre-movement, travel and doorway queues through simulation or controlled drills, checking receiving-zone availability and communication records for each exit. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「所需疏散時間」的交付需回答：用不同起始位置測試通道及訊息可見性。疏散模型保留人口、速度分布及出口狀態，演練改動由營運與防災責任者批准，教材算例不得當作現場指揮程序。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Great St Bernard Tunnel, the required evacuation time handover must address the following evidence: Test passage availability and message visibility from different starting positions. Retain population, speed distribution and exit states; operations and fire-safety owners approve drill changes, and classroom calculations are not incident-command procedures.","failure":"注意干擾：假設所有人都朝同一出口會漏掉事故位置造成的阻隔。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Assuming everyone uses one exit ignores obstruction by incident location. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b113-v14-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用不同起始位置測試通道及訊息可見性。以人流模擬或受控演練分辨前置時間、行走與門口排隊，核對每個出口接收區的可用狀態及通訊紀錄。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Test passage availability and message visibility from different starting positions. Separate pre-movement, travel and doorway queues through simulation or controlled drills, checking receiving-zone availability and communication records for each exit. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]},{"id":"b113-v14-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「所需疏散時間」的交付需回答：用不同起始位置測試通道及訊息可見性。疏散模型保留人口、速度分布及出口狀態，演練改動由營運與防災責任者批准，教材算例不得當作現場指揮程序。","textEn":"For Great St Bernard Tunnel, the required evacuation time handover must address the following evidence: Test passage availability and message visibility from different starting positions. Retain population, speed distribution and exit states; operations and fire-safety owners approve drill changes, and classroom calculations are not incident-command procedures.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「疏散時間與分區可用性」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Evacuation time and zone availability\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","用不同起始位置測試通道及訊息可見性。","目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Test passage availability and message visibility from different starting positions.","No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design."],"answer":1,"explanation":"用不同起始位置測試通道及訊息可見性。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Test passage availability and message visibility from different starting positions. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b113-v14-32","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性：失效診斷","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b113-v14-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「所需疏散時間」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Required evacuation time” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"假設所有人都朝同一出口會漏掉事故位置造成的阻隔。以最快成人速度套全部旅客會低估需求，若忽略接收孔受煙或車流影響，疏散可能移到另一個危險邊界。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Assuming everyone uses one exit ignores obstruction by incident location. Applying the fastest adult speed to everyone understates demand; overlooking smoke or traffic in the receiving bore can transfer evacuees into another hazard. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：人員速度會受煙熱、能見度及行動能力影響，安全判斷還要比較可用安全時間；橫通道存在但門或鄰孔不可用時，圖上的最短路線不一定能作實際選擇。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A passage shown on a plan may be unusable because its door or receiving bore is unavailable, invalidating the nominal shortest route.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b113-v14-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"假設所有人都朝同一出口會漏掉事故位置造成的阻隔。以最快成人速度套全部旅客會低估需求，若忽略接收孔受煙或車流影響，疏散可能移到另一個危險邊界。","textEn":"Assuming everyone uses one exit ignores obstruction by incident location. Applying the fastest adult speed to everyone understates demand; overlooking smoke or traffic in the receiving bore can transfer evacuees into another hazard.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]},{"id":"b113-v14-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「疏散時間與分區可用性」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Evacuation time and zone availability\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。","假設所有人都朝同一出口會漏掉事故位置造成的阻隔。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety.","Assuming everyone uses one exit ignores obstruction by incident location."],"answer":2,"explanation":"假設所有人都朝同一出口會漏掉事故位置造成的阻隔。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Assuming everyone uses one exit ignores obstruction by incident location. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b113-v14-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「設備備援與共同失效」與「資產編碼與可追溯交接」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Equipment redundancy and common failure\" and \"Asset identity and traceable handover\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b113-v14-33","title":"設備備援與共同失效：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Equipment redundancy and common failure: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b113-v14-32"],"objective":"說明「系統不可用率」如何影響聖伯納山隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “System unavailability” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Great St Bernard Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"兩端控制室可提高監督能力，但共用通訊或電源仍會造成共同故障，研究控制權交接證據。兩套設備只有在故障近似獨立且切換可靠時，並聯才顯著降低不可用率。共用配電、控制軟體、冷卻或受淹位置會把獨立假設破壞；維修停用也改變當下配置，因此可靠度模型必須明列共有資源和設備狀態，不能只數備用台數。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「系統不可用率」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Two control rooms improve supervision but shared communication or power can still fail; examine evidence for authority transfer. Parallel equipment sharply reduces unavailability only when failures are approximately independent and transfer works. Shared power, software, cooling or flood exposure breaks that assumption. Planned maintenance also changes the available configuration, so reliability models must identify shared resources and states rather than count spare units or multiply unsupported independent probabilities. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “System unavailability” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：單機不可用率=0.022 無因次。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: single-unit unavailability=0.022 dimensionless.","failure":"常見誤解：「設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「系統不可用率」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “System unavailability”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b113-v14-33-k1","title":"設備備援與共同失效","titleEn":"Equipment redundancy and common failure","text":"兩端控制室可提高監督能力，但共用通訊或電源仍會造成共同故障，研究控制權交接證據。兩套設備只有在故障近似獨立且切換可靠時，並聯才顯著降低不可用率。","textEn":"Two control rooms improve supervision but shared communication or power can still fail; examine evidence for authority transfer. Parallel equipment sharply reduces unavailability only when failures are approximately independent and transfer works.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]},{"id":"b113-v14-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「設備備援與共同失效」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Equipment redundancy and common failure\" is correct?","options":["兩端控制室可提高監督能力，但共用通訊或電源仍會造成共同故障，研究控制權交接證據。","設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。"],"optionsEn":["Two control rooms improve supervision but shared communication or power can still fail; examine evidence for authority transfer.","Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted."],"answer":0,"explanation":"兩端控制室可提高監督能力，但共用通訊或電源仍會造成共同故障，研究控制權交接證據。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Two control rooms improve supervision but shared communication or power can still fail; examine evidence for authority transfer. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b113-v14-34","title":"設備備援與共同失效：定量估算","titleEn":"Equipment redundancy and common failure: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b113-v14-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「系統不可用率」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “System unavailability” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：單機不可用率=0.022 無因次。Uparallel=U²=0.000484 probability。僅把單機不可用率增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.00058564 probability。邊界：完全獨立並聯與完美切換，不含共同失效；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: single-unit unavailability=0.022 dimensionless. Uparallel=U²=0.000484 probability. Increasing only single-unit unavailability by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.00058564 probability. Boundary: Independent parallel units with perfect transfer, excluding common failures. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：測試主從切換並追查共用鏈路與時間同步。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Test authority transfer and trace shared links and time synchronisation.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b113-v14-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：單機不可用率=0.022 無因次。Uparallel=U²=0.000484 probability。僅把單機不可用率增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.00058564 probability。邊界：完全獨立並聯與完美切換，不含共同失效；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: single-unit unavailability=0.022 dimensionless. Uparallel=U²=0.000484 probability. Increasing only single-unit unavailability by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.00058564 probability. Boundary: Independent parallel units with perfect transfer, excluding common failures. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]},{"id":"b113-v14-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「設備備援與共同失效」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Equipment redundancy and common failure\", which statement holds?","options":["風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。","原創教學假設：單機不可用率=0.022 無因次。","混凝土抗壓強度合格就代表厚壁構件不會產生熱裂縫。"],"optionsEn":["Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.","Original teaching assumptions: single-unit unavailability=0.022 dimensionless.","Adequate compressive strength proves that thick concrete cannot develop thermal cracks."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：單機不可用率=0.022 無因次。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: single-unit unavailability=0.022 dimensionless. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b113-v14-35","title":"設備備援與共同失效：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Equipment redundancy and common failure: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b113-v14-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「系統不可用率」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “System unavailability” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"測試主從切換並追查共用鏈路與時間同步。由設備清單畫出故障樹，將電源、控制及實體位置追到共同節點，並用事件及維修紀錄檢查獨立假設。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Test authority transfer and trace shared links and time synchronisation. Build a fault tree from the asset list, trace power, control and location to shared nodes, and test independence against incident and maintenance records. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「系統不可用率」的交付需回答：測試主從切換並追查共用鏈路與時間同步。維修計畫附當日可用配置與剩餘備援，任何共同資源更動同步更新故障樹，切換試驗由設備及營運團隊共同見證。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Great St Bernard Tunnel, the system unavailability handover must address the following evidence: Test authority transfer and trace shared links and time synchronisation. Attach the actual configuration and remaining redundancy to maintenance plans, update fault trees after shared-resource changes, and witness transfer tests jointly.","failure":"注意干擾：兩室畫面一致不證明資料鏈路或電源相互獨立。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Matching displays do not prove independent data links or power. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b113-v14-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"測試主從切換並追查共用鏈路與時間同步。由設備清單畫出故障樹，將電源、控制及實體位置追到共同節點，並用事件及維修紀錄檢查獨立假設。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Test authority transfer and trace shared links and time synchronisation. Build a fault tree from the asset list, trace power, control and location to shared nodes, and test independence against incident and maintenance records. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]},{"id":"b113-v14-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「系統不可用率」的交付需回答：測試主從切換並追查共用鏈路與時間同步。維修計畫附當日可用配置與剩餘備援，任何共同資源更動同步更新故障樹，切換試驗由設備及營運團隊共同見證。","textEn":"For Great St Bernard Tunnel, the system unavailability handover must address the following evidence: Test authority transfer and trace shared links and time synchronisation. Attach the actual configuration and remaining redundancy to maintenance plans, update fault trees after shared-resource changes, and witness transfer tests jointly.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「設備備援與共同失效」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Equipment redundancy and common failure\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","擴散長度就是鋼筋開始腐蝕的位置和精確時間。","測試主從切換並追查共用鏈路與時間同步。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Diffusion length gives the exact location and time of corrosion initiation.","Test authority transfer and trace shared links and time synchronisation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"測試主從切換並追查共用鏈路與時間同步。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Test authority transfer and trace shared links and time synchronisation. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b113-v14-36","title":"設備備援與共同失效：失效診斷","titleEn":"Equipment redundancy and common failure: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b113-v14-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「系統不可用率」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “System unavailability” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"兩室畫面一致不證明資料鏈路或電源相互獨立。重複安裝卻共用單一供電可能在一次故障中全部停機，帳面可靠度很高但實際不可用時間沒有降低。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Matching displays do not prove independent data links or power. Duplicated equipment on one supply can fail together in a single event, leaving actual downtime unchanged despite optimistic calculated reliability. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：共用配電、控制軟體、冷卻或受淹位置會把獨立假設破壞；維修停用也改變當下配置，因此可靠度模型必須明列共有資源和設備狀態，不能只數備用台數。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Planned maintenance also changes the available configuration, so reliability models must identify shared resources and states rather than count spare units or multiply unsupported independent probabilities.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b113-v14-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"兩室畫面一致不證明資料鏈路或電源相互獨立。重複安裝卻共用單一供電可能在一次故障中全部停機，帳面可靠度很高但實際不可用時間沒有降低。","textEn":"Matching displays do not prove independent data links or power. Duplicated equipment on one supply can fail together in a single event, leaving actual downtime unchanged despite optimistic calculated reliability.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]},{"id":"b113-v14-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「設備備援與共同失效」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Equipment redundancy and common failure\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["兩室畫面一致不證明資料鏈路或電源相互獨立。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。"],"optionsEn":["Matching displays do not prove independent data links or power.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted."],"answer":0,"explanation":"兩室畫面一致不證明資料鏈路或電源相互獨立。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Matching displays do not prove independent data links or power. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b113-v14-37","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b113-v14-36"],"objective":"說明「資產資料完整度」如何影響聖伯納山隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Asset-record completeness” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Great St Bernard Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"跨境維修需讓兩種語言的設備清單對應同一位置和工單，研究名詞翻譯與唯一識別碼分離。地下設備的竣工資料必須讓維護人員找到正確位置、材料批次和控制版本。只有上傳圖面而沒有變更歷程，無法分辨元件替換與真正劣化；告警、儀器、線路及工單使用一致識別碼，才可能把量測趨勢連回實際受力或水力系統。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「資產資料完整度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Cross-border maintenance needs multilingual inventories linked to one location and work order, separating translated names from unique identifiers. Handover must let maintainers find the correct location, material batch and control revision. Drawings without change history cannot distinguish replacement from deterioration. Consistent identifiers across alarms, instruments, circuits and work orders are essential for linking trends to the physical structural or hydraulic system instead of treating each record as an isolated file. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Asset-record completeness” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：設備總數=112 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: asset count=112 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=85.7143 %.","failure":"常見誤解：「全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「資產資料完整度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Asset-record completeness”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b113-v14-37-k1","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover","text":"跨境維修需讓兩種語言的設備清單對應同一位置和工單，研究名詞翻譯與唯一識別碼分離。地下設備的竣工資料必須讓維護人員找到正確位置、材料批次和控制版本。","textEn":"Cross-border maintenance needs multilingual inventories linked to one location and work order, separating translated names from unique identifiers. Handover must let maintainers find the correct location, material batch and control revision.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]},{"id":"b113-v14-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「資產編碼與可追溯交接」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Asset identity and traceable handover\" is correct?","options":["全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。","跨境維修需讓兩種語言的設備清單對應同一位置和工單，研究名詞翻譯與唯一識別碼分離。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.","Cross-border maintenance needs multilingual inventories linked to one location and work order, separating translated names from unique identifiers.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":1,"explanation":"跨境維修需讓兩種語言的設備清單對應同一位置和工單，研究名詞翻譯與唯一識別碼分離。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Cross-border maintenance needs multilingual inventories linked to one location and work order, separating translated names from unique identifiers. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b113-v14-38","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：定量估算","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b113-v14-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「資產資料完整度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Asset-record completeness” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：設備總數=112 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。coverage=100(N−missing)/N=85.7143 %。僅把缺紀錄數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為84.2857 %。邊界：資料完整度，不等於安全或可靠度；擾動為連續敏感度，實際個數為整數；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: asset count=112 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=85.7143 %. Increasing only missing records by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 84.2857 %. Boundary: Record completeness, not safety or reliability; perturbation is continuous sensitivity while actual counts are integers. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：抽查兩控制室對同一告警的定位及維修責任。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check both rooms locate one alarm identically and assign the same maintenance responsibility.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b113-v14-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：設備總數=112 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。coverage=100(N−missing)/N=85.7143 %。僅把缺紀錄數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為84.2857 %。邊界：資料完整度，不等於安全或可靠度；擾動為連續敏感度，實際個數為整數；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: asset count=112 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=85.7143 %. Increasing only missing records by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 84.2857 %. Boundary: Record completeness, not safety or reliability; perturbation is continuous sensitivity while actual counts are integers. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]},{"id":"b113-v14-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「資產編碼與可追溯交接」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Asset identity and traceable handover\", which statement holds?","options":["照度越高就必然使隧道內所有物體更容易辨識。","目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。","原創教學假設：設備總數=112 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。"],"optionsEn":["Higher illuminance necessarily makes every tunnel object easier to detect.","No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.","Original teaching assumptions: asset count=112 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=85.7143 %."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：設備總數=112 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: asset count=112 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=85.7143 %. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b113-v14-39","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b113-v14-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「資產資料完整度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Asset-record completeness” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"抽查兩控制室對同一告警的定位及維修責任。抽取一條告警，從控制畫面追到設備、線路、圖面和工單，核對位置、版本及校正日期並記錄無法閉合的欄位。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check both rooms locate one alarm identically and assign the same maintenance responsibility. Trace a sampled alarm from screen to equipment, circuit, drawing and work order, checking location, revision and calibration dates and recording broken links. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「資產資料完整度」的交付需回答：抽查兩控制室對同一告警的定位及維修責任。交接以可完成的定位、查找與復原任務驗證，由維護責任人確認現場可用性；完整度只是資料指標，不代表結構安全或設備可靠。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Great St Bernard Tunnel, the asset-record completeness handover must address the following evidence: Check both rooms locate one alarm identically and assign the same maintenance responsibility. Validate handover through achievable location, retrieval and recovery tasks witnessed by maintainers; completeness measures records, not structural safety or equipment reliability.","failure":"注意干擾：同名設備位於不同洞端時，文字翻譯不能取代位置編碼。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Translation cannot replace location codes when similarly named assets occupy opposite portals. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b113-v14-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"抽查兩控制室對同一告警的定位及維修責任。抽取一條告警，從控制畫面追到設備、線路、圖面和工單，核對位置、版本及校正日期並記錄無法閉合的欄位。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Check both rooms locate one alarm identically and assign the same maintenance responsibility. Trace a sampled alarm from screen to equipment, circuit, drawing and work order, checking location, revision and calibration dates and recording broken links. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]},{"id":"b113-v14-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「資產資料完整度」的交付需回答：抽查兩控制室對同一告警的定位及維修責任。交接以可完成的定位、查找與復原任務驗證，由維護責任人確認現場可用性；完整度只是資料指標，不代表結構安全或設備可靠。","textEn":"For Great St Bernard Tunnel, the asset-record completeness handover must address the following evidence: Check both rooms locate one alarm identically and assign the same maintenance responsibility. Validate handover through achievable location, retrieval and recovery tasks witnessed by maintainers; completeness measures records, not structural safety or equipment reliability.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「資產編碼與可追溯交接」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Asset identity and traceable handover\"?","options":["抽查兩控制室對同一告警的定位及維修責任。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。"],"optionsEn":["Check both rooms locate one alarm identically and assign the same maintenance responsibility.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure."],"answer":0,"explanation":"抽查兩控制室對同一告警的定位及維修責任。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check both rooms locate one alarm identically and assign the same maintenance responsibility. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b113-v14-40","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：失效診斷","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b113-v14-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「資產資料完整度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Asset-record completeness” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"同名設備位於不同洞端時，文字翻譯不能取代位置編碼。設備改名卻未更新控制畫面會引導人員隔離錯誤回路，材料批次缺漏則使同批缺陷無法追蹤到其他位置。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Translation cannot replace location codes when similarly named assets occupy opposite portals. Renaming an asset without updating the screen can isolate the wrong circuit; missing material batches prevent tracing related defects at other locations. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：只有上傳圖面而沒有變更歷程，無法分辨元件替換與真正劣化；告警、儀器、線路及工單使用一致識別碼，才可能把量測趨勢連回實際受力或水力系統。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Consistent identifiers across alarms, instruments, circuits and work orders are essential for linking trends to the physical structural or hydraulic system instead of treating each record as an isolated file.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b113-v14-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"同名設備位於不同洞端時，文字翻譯不能取代位置編碼。設備改名卻未更新控制畫面會引導人員隔離錯誤回路，材料批次缺漏則使同批缺陷無法追蹤到其他位置。","textEn":"Translation cannot replace location codes when similarly named assets occupy opposite portals. Renaming an asset without updating the screen can isolate the wrong circuit; missing material batches prevent tracing related defects at other locations.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]},{"id":"b113-v14-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「資產編碼與可追溯交接」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Asset identity and traceable handover\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","同名設備位於不同洞端時，文字翻譯不能取代位置編碼。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Translation cannot replace location codes when similarly named assets occupy opposite portals.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":1,"explanation":"同名設備位於不同洞端時，文字翻譯不能取代位置編碼。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Translation cannot replace location codes when similarly named assets occupy opposite portals. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b113","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b113-history"],"curriculumVersion":14,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000},{"id":"b114","title":"蒙布朗隧道","titleEn":"Mont Blanc Tunnel","category":"underground","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"蒙布朗隧道連接法國與義大利，營運機構列長11.6公里並記錄1965年開通。本課以長公路的系統思考為主軸，分別研究通風網路、受熱材料、事故偵知、人的反應、設備冗餘及整修交付。歷史事件只用核對過的年代，假想事故條件不被包裝為原事故重建。","summaryEn":"Mont Blanc Tunnel connects France and Italy; its operator reports 11.6 km and opening in 1965. This course uses a systems perspective on ventilation networks, heated materials, detection, human response, redundancy and refurbishment handover. Historical dates follow checked records, while hypothetical incident conditions are not presented as reconstruction of an actual accident.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"ug-landmarks","subcategoryTitle":"世界隧道與地下巨作","subcategoryTitleEn":"World tunnels and underground landmarks","learningTrack":"underground","learningSubdiscipline":"ug-landmarks","learningTags":["underground","ug-landmarks","tunnel"],"architectureFamily":"tunnel","architectureNodes":[["路線里程與端點","Alignment chainage and endpoints"],["風道摩擦壓損","Duct friction loss"],["襯砌環向壓縮","Lining hoop compression"],["所需疏散時間","Required evacuation time"],["剩餘集水容積","Remaining sump volume"],["資產資料完整度","Asset-record completeness"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,5],[1,5]],"diagram":{"type":"tunnel","labels":["路線里程與端點","風道摩擦壓損","襯砌環向壓縮","所需疏散時間","剩餘集水容積"],"labelsEn":["Alignment chainage and endpoints","Duct friction loss","Lining hoop compression","Required evacuation time","Remaining sump volume"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"原創綜合審查：先計算「通風網路與壓力損失」，再獨立計算「疏散時間與分區可用性」。原創教學假設：達西因子=0.025 無因次；風道長度=1020 m；水力直徑=4 m；空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；平均風速=3.1 m/s。Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=36.7583 Pa。僅把平均風速增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為44.4775 Pa。邊界：定密度直管摩阻，局部損失及外風另計；不是本工程實測或允收值。原創教學假設：前置時間=106 s；行走距離=300 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。RSET=tpre+d/v=481 s。僅把行走距離增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為518.5 s。邊界：單群體固定速度，不含排隊煙熱及能力差異，不能單獨判安全；不是本工程實測或允收值。兩組結果的單位與邊界不同，不能直接相加。請列出一項缺少的現場輸入，說明它會影響哪個結論，以及哪種獨立量測可以縮小不確定度。","textEn":"Original integrated review: first calculate ventilation network and pressure loss, then independently calculate evacuation time and zone availability. Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.025 dimensionless; duct length=1020 m; hydraulic diameter=4 m; air density=1.2 kg/m³; mean velocity=3.1 m/s. Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=36.7583 Pa. Increasing only mean velocity by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 44.4775 Pa. Boundary: Constant-density straight-duct friction; local loss and external wind are separate. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=106 s; travel distance=300 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s. RSET=tpre+d/v=481 s. Increasing only travel distance by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 518.5 s. Boundary: One group at fixed speed without queues, smoke or mobility differences; not a safety conclusion. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. The outputs have different units and boundaries and cannot simply be added. Identify one missing field input, explain which conclusion it changes and select an independent measurement to reduce uncertainty.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":14,"enrichmentVersion":14,"stages":[{"id":"b114-v14-s1","title":"地層條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Ground conditions, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「服務邊界與路線代價」與「通風網路與壓力損失」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\" and \"Ventilation network and pressure loss\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b114-v14-01","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「路線里程與端點」如何影響蒙布朗隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Alignment chainage and endpoints” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Mont Blanc Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"蒙布朗跨境服務涉及兩端引道和管制，教材比較相同端點的洞內時間及整體等待而非單一最短車程。隧道選線同時改變洞口、覆土與縱坡，短路線不保證低地質風險。比較方案必須使用相同起訖點，並分開主孔、引道及服務坑的工程數量；交通時間只是需求的一個指標，不能代替施工可達性或長期維修評估。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「路線里程與端點」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Cross-border service includes approaches and controls; compare in-tunnel time and total waiting between common endpoints rather than one shortest journey. Alignment changes portals, cover and gradient together, so a shorter tunnel need not have lower geological risk. Compare options between identical endpoints and distinguish running bores, approaches and service galleries. Travel time measures one service benefit but cannot replace assessment of construction access, maintenance closures or exposure to uncertain ground. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Alignment chainage and endpoints” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：長度=17.2 km；速度=60 km/h。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: length=17.2 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=17.2 min.","failure":"常見誤解：「最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「路線里程與端點」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Alignment chainage and endpoints”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b114-v14-01-k1","title":"服務邊界與路線代價","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost","text":"蒙布朗跨境服務涉及兩端引道和管制，教材比較相同端點的洞內時間及整體等待而非單一最短車程。隧道選線同時改變洞口、覆土與縱坡，短路線不保證低地質風險。","textEn":"Cross-border service includes approaches and controls; compare in-tunnel time and total waiting between common endpoints rather than one shortest journey. Alignment changes portals, cover and gradient together, so a shorter tunnel need not have lower geological risk.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]},{"id":"b114-v14-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「服務邊界與路線代價」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\" is correct?","options":["最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。","蒙布朗跨境服務涉及兩端引道和管制，教材比較相同端點的洞內時間及整體等待而非單一最短車程。","風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。"],"optionsEn":["The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.","Cross-border service includes approaches and controls; compare in-tunnel time and total waiting between common endpoints rather than one shortest journey.","Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel."],"answer":1,"explanation":"蒙布朗跨境服務涉及兩端引道和管制，教材比較相同端點的洞內時間及整體等待而非單一最短車程。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Cross-border service includes approaches and controls; compare in-tunnel time and total waiting between common endpoints rather than one shortest journey. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b114-v14-02","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：定量估算","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b114-v14-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「路線里程與端點」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Alignment chainage and endpoints” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：長度=17.2 km；速度=60 km/h。t=60L/v=17.2 min。僅把長度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為18.92 min。邊界：假想交通旅程，未含加減速、排隊及實際時刻表；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: length=17.2 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=17.2 min. Increasing only length by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 18.92 min. Boundary: Hypothetical transport journey excluding acceleration, queues and the real timetable. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將正常行車和入口排隊時間分開紀錄。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Record ordinary travel and entrance queue time separately.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b114-v14-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：長度=17.2 km；速度=60 km/h。t=60L/v=17.2 min。僅把長度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為18.92 min。邊界：假想交通旅程，未含加減速、排隊及實際時刻表；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: length=17.2 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=17.2 min. Increasing only length by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 18.92 min. Boundary: Hypothetical transport journey excluding acceleration, queues and the real timetable. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]},{"id":"b114-v14-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「服務邊界與路線代價」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\", which statement holds?","options":["混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。","原創教學假設：長度=17.2 km；速度=60 km/h。"],"optionsEn":["Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.","Original teaching assumptions: length=17.2 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=17.2 min."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：長度=17.2 km；速度=60 km/h。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: length=17.2 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=17.2 min. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b114-v14-03","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b114-v14-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「路線里程與端點」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Alignment chainage and endpoints” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將正常行車和入口排隊時間分開紀錄。把縱斷面、地形與地質剖面疊合，以端點坐標獨立反算距離，再將主孔與支坑數量分開核對。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Record ordinary travel and entrance queue time separately. Overlay the longitudinal profile, terrain and geology; independently derive distances from endpoint coordinates and reconcile running-bore and gallery quantities separately. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「路線里程與端點」的交付需回答：將正常行車和入口排隊時間分開紀錄。在方案表中凍結起訖點、計量範圍及地質假設，任何改線都要同步更新高程、數量與服務情境，不能只替換總長。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Mont Blanc Tunnel, the alignment chainage and endpoints handover must address the following evidence: Record ordinary travel and entrance queue time separately. Freeze endpoints, measurement scope and ground assumptions in the option register; realignment requires coordinated updates to elevations, quantities and service scenarios rather than replacing one length.","failure":"注意干擾：隧道內暢通不代表兩端交通系統沒有瓶頸。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Free flow inside does not establish unconstrained approaches. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b114-v14-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將正常行車和入口排隊時間分開紀錄。把縱斷面、地形與地質剖面疊合，以端點坐標獨立反算距離，再將主孔與支坑數量分開核對。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Record ordinary travel and entrance queue time separately. Overlay the longitudinal profile, terrain and geology; independently derive distances from endpoint coordinates and reconcile running-bore and gallery quantities separately. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]},{"id":"b114-v14-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「路線里程與端點」的交付需回答：將正常行車和入口排隊時間分開紀錄。在方案表中凍結起訖點、計量範圍及地質假設，任何改線都要同步更新高程、數量與服務情境，不能只替換總長。","textEn":"For Mont Blanc Tunnel, the alignment chainage and endpoints handover must address the following evidence: Record ordinary travel and entrance queue time separately. Freeze endpoints, measurement scope and ground assumptions in the option register; realignment requires coordinated updates to elevations, quantities and service scenarios rather than replacing one length.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「服務邊界與路線代價」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\"?","options":["將正常行車和入口排隊時間分開紀錄。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","集水坑總容積除以平均入流就是保證可用的反應時間。"],"optionsEn":["Record ordinary travel and entrance queue time separately.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Gross sump volume divided by average inflow is a guaranteed response time."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將正常行車和入口排隊時間分開紀錄。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Record ordinary travel and entrance queue time separately. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b114-v14-04","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：失效診斷","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b114-v14-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「路線里程與端點」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Alignment chainage and endpoints” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"隧道內暢通不代表兩端交通系統沒有瓶頸。混用全線與單孔長度會同時扭曲工程數量、行程及逃生距離，造成方案比較失去共同基準。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Free flow inside does not establish unconstrained approaches. Mixing whole-route and single-bore lengths distorts quantities, journey time and escape distance, destroying the common basis of an option comparison. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：比較方案必須使用相同起訖點，並分開主孔、引道及服務坑的工程數量；交通時間只是需求的一個指標，不能代替施工可達性或長期維修評估。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Travel time measures one service benefit but cannot replace assessment of construction access, maintenance closures or exposure to uncertain ground.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b114-v14-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"隧道內暢通不代表兩端交通系統沒有瓶頸。混用全線與單孔長度會同時扭曲工程數量、行程及逃生距離，造成方案比較失去共同基準。","textEn":"Free flow inside does not establish unconstrained approaches. Mixing whole-route and single-bore lengths distorts quantities, journey time and escape distance, destroying the common basis of an option comparison.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]},{"id":"b114-v14-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「服務邊界與路線代價」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","隧道內暢通不代表兩端交通系統沒有瓶頸。","風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Free flow inside does not establish unconstrained approaches.","Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel."],"answer":1,"explanation":"隧道內暢通不代表兩端交通系統沒有瓶頸。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Free flow inside does not establish unconstrained approaches. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b114-v14-05","title":"通風網路與壓力損失：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Ventilation network and pressure loss: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b114-v14-04"],"objective":"說明「風道摩擦壓損」如何影響蒙布朗隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Duct friction loss” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Mont Blanc Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"蒙布朗案例用來研究正常污染稀釋與假想火災控煙的不同目標，不能只提高風量就宣稱情境改善。風機提供壓差，實際風量由風道摩阻、局部損失、外風與其他風機共同決定。支路開關會重新分配整個網路，不能把額定風量直接加總；正常污染稀釋與火災控煙也有不同目標，需要分別建立受控邊界和故障情境。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「風道摩擦壓損」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Distinguish normal pollutant dilution from hypothetical fire smoke-control objectives; more airflow alone does not prove an improved scenario. Fans supply pressure, but actual flow follows friction, local losses, external wind and interactions with other fans. Switching a branch redistributes the network rather than simply adding rated flows. Routine dilution and fire smoke control have different objectives, so each needs explicit boundaries, operating states and failure cases rather than one universal flow target. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Duct friction loss” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：達西因子=0.025 無因次；風道長度=1020 m；水力直徑=4 m；空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；平均風速=3.1 m/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.025 dimensionless; duct length=1020 m; hydraulic diameter=4 m; air density=1.2 kg/m³; mean velocity=3.1 m/s. Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=36.7583 Pa.","failure":"常見誤解：「風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「風道摩擦壓損」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Duct friction loss”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b114-v14-05-k1","title":"通風網路與壓力損失","titleEn":"Ventilation network and pressure loss","text":"蒙布朗案例用來研究正常污染稀釋與假想火災控煙的不同目標，不能只提高風量就宣稱情境改善。風機提供壓差，實際風量由風道摩阻、局部損失、外風與其他風機共同決定。","textEn":"Distinguish normal pollutant dilution from hypothetical fire smoke-control objectives; more airflow alone does not prove an improved scenario. Fans supply pressure, but actual flow follows friction, local losses, external wind and interactions with other fans.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]},{"id":"b114-v14-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「通風網路與壓力損失」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Ventilation network and pressure loss\" is correct?","options":["風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。","混凝土抗壓強度合格就代表厚壁構件不會產生熱裂縫。","蒙布朗案例用來研究正常污染稀釋與假想火災控煙的不同目標，不能只提高風量就宣稱情境改善。"],"optionsEn":["Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.","Adequate compressive strength proves that thick concrete cannot develop thermal cracks.","Distinguish normal pollutant dilution from hypothetical fire smoke-control objectives; more airflow alone does not prove an improved scenario."],"answer":2,"explanation":"蒙布朗案例用來研究正常污染稀釋與假想火災控煙的不同目標，不能只提高風量就宣稱情境改善。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Distinguish normal pollutant dilution from hypothetical fire smoke-control objectives; more airflow alone does not prove an improved scenario. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b114-v14-06","title":"通風網路與壓力損失：定量估算","titleEn":"Ventilation network and pressure loss: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b114-v14-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「風道摩擦壓損」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Duct friction loss” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：達西因子=0.025 無因次；風道長度=1020 m；水力直徑=4 m；空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；平均風速=3.1 m/s。Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=36.7583 Pa。僅把平均風速增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為44.4775 Pa。邊界：定密度直管摩阻，局部損失及外風另計；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.025 dimensionless; duct length=1020 m; hydraulic diameter=4 m; air density=1.2 kg/m³; mean velocity=3.1 m/s. Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=36.7583 Pa. Increasing only mean velocity by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 44.4775 Pa. Boundary: Constant-density straight-duct friction; local loss and external wind are separate. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在不同受控邊界下比較風向、門位及抽排分布。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare airflow direction, door states and extraction distribution under distinct controlled boundaries.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b114-v14-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：達西因子=0.025 無因次；風道長度=1020 m；水力直徑=4 m；空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；平均風速=3.1 m/s。Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=36.7583 Pa。僅把平均風速增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為44.4775 Pa。邊界：定密度直管摩阻，局部損失及外風另計；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.025 dimensionless; duct length=1020 m; hydraulic diameter=4 m; air density=1.2 kg/m³; mean velocity=3.1 m/s. Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=36.7583 Pa. Increasing only mean velocity by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 44.4775 Pa. Boundary: Constant-density straight-duct friction; local loss and external wind are separate. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]},{"id":"b114-v14-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「通風網路與壓力損失」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Ventilation network and pressure loss\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：達西因子=0.025 無因次；風道長度=1020 m；水力直徑=4 m；空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；平均風速=3.1 m/s。","照度越高就必然使隧道內所有物體更容易辨識。","設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.025 dimensionless.","Higher illuminance necessarily makes every tunnel object easier to detect.","Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：達西因子=0.025 無因次；風道長度=1020 m；水力直徑=4 m；空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；平均風速=3.1 m/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.025 dimensionless; duct length=1020 m; hydraulic diameter=4 m; air density=1.2 kg/m³; mean velocity=3.1 m/s. Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=36.7583 Pa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b114-v14-07","title":"通風網路與壓力損失：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Ventilation network and pressure loss: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b114-v14-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「風道摩擦壓損」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Duct friction loss” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在不同受控邊界下比較風向、門位及抽排分布。沿線同步量測靜壓與風速，記錄風門及其他風機狀態，再把實測工作點和風機曲線、網路壓損比較。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare airflow direction, door states and extraction distribution under distinct controlled boundaries. Measure pressure and velocity synchronously, record dampers and other fans, and compare the measured duty point with fan curves and network resistance. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「風道摩擦壓損」的交付需回答：在不同受控邊界下比較風向、門位及抽排分布。驗收採明確風門和車流邊界，維修改線後重新核對網路工作點，火災模式由防災責任工程師簽認而非沿用正常模式。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Mont Blanc Tunnel, the duct friction loss handover must address the following evidence: Compare airflow direction, door states and extraction distribution under distinct controlled boundaries. Commission with specified damper and traffic boundaries, recheck duty points after rerouting, and have the fire-safety engineer approve emergency modes independently.","failure":"注意干擾：錯誤風向可能把煙帶向人員區，即使總風量增加。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Wrong airflow direction can carry smoke toward users despite increased total flow. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b114-v14-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在不同受控邊界下比較風向、門位及抽排分布。沿線同步量測靜壓與風速，記錄風門及其他風機狀態，再把實測工作點和風機曲線、網路壓損比較。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Compare airflow direction, door states and extraction distribution under distinct controlled boundaries. Measure pressure and velocity synchronously, record dampers and other fans, and compare the measured duty point with fan curves and network resistance. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]},{"id":"b114-v14-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「風道摩擦壓損」的交付需回答：在不同受控邊界下比較風向、門位及抽排分布。驗收採明確風門和車流邊界，維修改線後重新核對網路工作點，火災模式由防災責任工程師簽認而非沿用正常模式。","textEn":"For Mont Blanc Tunnel, the duct friction loss handover must address the following evidence: Compare airflow direction, door states and extraction distribution under distinct controlled boundaries. Commission with specified damper and traffic boundaries, recheck duty points after rerouting, and have the fire-safety engineer approve emergency modes independently.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「通風網路與壓力損失」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Ventilation network and pressure loss\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","在不同受控邊界下比較風向、門位及抽排分布。","增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Compare airflow direction, door states and extraction distribution under distinct controlled boundaries.","Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly."],"answer":1,"explanation":"在不同受控邊界下比較風向、門位及抽排分布。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare airflow direction, door states and extraction distribution under distinct controlled boundaries. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b114-v14-08","title":"通風網路與壓力損失：失效診斷","titleEn":"Ventilation network and pressure loss: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b114-v14-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「風道摩擦壓損」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Duct friction loss” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"錯誤風向可能把煙帶向人員區，即使總風量增加。只看風機轉速會漏掉風門誤位或短路漏風，可能在總耗電增加時，真正需要的區段反而風量不足。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Wrong airflow direction can carry smoke toward users despite increased total flow. Fan speed alone misses a misplaced damper or leakage shortcut; total power may rise while the critical section receives less air. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：支路開關會重新分配整個網路，不能把額定風量直接加總；正常污染稀釋與火災控煙也有不同目標，需要分別建立受控邊界和故障情境。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Routine dilution and fire smoke control have different objectives, so each needs explicit boundaries, operating states and failure cases rather than one universal flow target.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b114-v14-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"錯誤風向可能把煙帶向人員區，即使總風量增加。只看風機轉速會漏掉風門誤位或短路漏風，可能在總耗電增加時，真正需要的區段反而風量不足。","textEn":"Wrong airflow direction can carry smoke toward users despite increased total flow. Fan speed alone misses a misplaced damper or leakage shortcut; total power may rise while the critical section receives less air.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]},{"id":"b114-v14-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「通風網路與壓力損失」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Ventilation network and pressure loss\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","混凝土抗壓強度合格就代表厚壁構件不會產生熱裂縫。","錯誤風向可能把煙帶向人員區，即使總風量增加。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Adequate compressive strength proves that thick concrete cannot develop thermal cracks.","Wrong airflow direction can carry smoke toward users despite increased total flow."],"answer":2,"explanation":"錯誤風向可能把煙帶向人員區，即使總風量增加。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Wrong airflow direction can carry smoke toward users despite increased total flow. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b114-v14-s2","title":"機制、材料與定量設計","titleEn":"Mechanisms, materials and quantitative design","description":"本階段聚焦「溫度拘束與構件裂縫」與「環向受力與接縫柔度」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Thermal restraint and component cracking\" and \"Ring force and joint flexibility\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b114-v14-09","title":"溫度拘束與構件裂縫：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Thermal restraint and component cracking: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b114-v14-08"],"objective":"說明「拘束溫度應變」如何影響蒙布朗隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Restrained thermal strain” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Mont Blanc Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"假想受熱襯砌的熱膨脹拘束與混凝土剝落屬不同機制，蒙布朗教材只以線彈性式建立量級。厚壁構件在水化升溫後冷卻，若相鄰構件或基座限制收縮，熱應變會轉為拉應力。抗壓強度達標不等於抗裂合格，因為彈性模數成熟、徐變、溫度梯度與澆置順序都影響實際拘束；完全拘束彈性估算只能當量級上限比較。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「拘束溫度應變」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Restrained expansion and concrete spalling are different mechanisms; a linear-elastic exercise establishes scale without predicting actual fire damage. A thick element cools after hydration, and restraint from adjacent pours or its base converts contraction into tension. Compressive-strength compliance does not establish crack resistance because modulus development, creep, gradients and pour sequence influence restraint. A fully restrained elastic estimate is therefore a scale bound, not a prediction of actual cracking or residual stress. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Restrained thermal strain” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：線膨脹係數=1e-05 K⁻¹；溫差=23 K；彈性模數=25 GPa。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: expansion coefficient=1e-05 K⁻¹; temperature difference=23 K; elastic modulus=25 GPa. σ=EαΔT, GPa→MPa ×1000=5.75 MPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「混凝土抗壓強度合格就代表厚壁構件不會產生熱裂縫。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Adequate compressive strength proves that thick concrete cannot develop thermal cracks.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「拘束溫度應變」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Restrained thermal strain”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b114-v14-09-k1","title":"溫度拘束與構件裂縫","titleEn":"Thermal restraint and component cracking","text":"假想受熱襯砌的熱膨脹拘束與混凝土剝落屬不同機制，蒙布朗教材只以線彈性式建立量級。厚壁構件在水化升溫後冷卻，若相鄰構件或基座限制收縮，熱應變會轉為拉應力。","textEn":"Restrained expansion and concrete spalling are different mechanisms; a linear-elastic exercise establishes scale without predicting actual fire damage. A thick element cools after hydration, and restraint from adjacent pours or its base converts contraction into tension.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]},{"id":"b114-v14-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：混凝土抗壓強度合格就代表厚壁構件不會產生熱裂縫。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Adequate compressive strength proves that thick concrete cannot develop thermal cracks. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「溫度拘束與構件裂縫」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Thermal restraint and component cracking\" is correct?","options":["假想受熱襯砌的熱膨脹拘束與混凝土剝落屬不同機制，蒙布朗教材只以線彈性式建立量級。","混凝土抗壓強度合格就代表厚壁構件不會產生熱裂縫。","混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。"],"optionsEn":["Restrained expansion and concrete spalling are different mechanisms; a linear-elastic exercise establishes scale without predicting actual fire damage.","Adequate compressive strength proves that thick concrete cannot develop thermal cracks.","Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure."],"answer":0,"explanation":"假想受熱襯砌的熱膨脹拘束與混凝土剝落屬不同機制，蒙布朗教材只以線彈性式建立量級。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Restrained expansion and concrete spalling are different mechanisms; a linear-elastic exercise establishes scale without predicting actual fire damage. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b114-v14-10","title":"溫度拘束與構件裂縫：定量估算","titleEn":"Thermal restraint and component cracking: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b114-v14-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「拘束溫度應變」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Restrained thermal strain” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：線膨脹係數=1e-05 K⁻¹；溫差=23 K；彈性模數=25 GPa。σ=EαΔT, GPa→MPa ×1000=5.75 MPa。僅把溫差增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為6.325 MPa。邊界：完全拘束線彈性量級，未含徐變開裂和拘束鬆弛；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: expansion coefficient=1e-05 K⁻¹; temperature difference=23 K; elastic modulus=25 GPa. σ=EαΔT, GPa→MPa ×1000=5.75 MPa. Increasing only temperature difference by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 6.325 MPa. Boundary: Fully restrained linear-elastic scale without creep, cracking or restraint relaxation. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將溫度深度分布、含水和裂縫方向一起檢查。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check temperature through depth, moisture and crack orientation together.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b114-v14-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：線膨脹係數=1e-05 K⁻¹；溫差=23 K；彈性模數=25 GPa。σ=EαΔT, GPa→MPa ×1000=5.75 MPa。僅把溫差增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為6.325 MPa。邊界：完全拘束線彈性量級，未含徐變開裂和拘束鬆弛；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: expansion coefficient=1e-05 K⁻¹; temperature difference=23 K; elastic modulus=25 GPa. σ=EαΔT, GPa→MPa ×1000=5.75 MPa. Increasing only temperature difference by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 6.325 MPa. Boundary: Fully restrained linear-elastic scale without creep, cracking or restraint relaxation. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]},{"id":"b114-v14-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「溫度拘束與構件裂縫」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Thermal restraint and component cracking\", which statement holds?","options":["只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。","原創教學假設：線膨脹係數=1e-05 K⁻¹；溫差=23 K；彈性模數=25 GPa。","集水坑總容積除以平均入流就是保證可用的反應時間。"],"optionsEn":["Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.","Original teaching assumptions: expansion coefficient=1e-05 K⁻¹; temperature difference=23 K; elastic modulus=25 GPa. σ=EαΔT, GPa→MPa ×1000=5.75 MPa.","Gross sump volume divided by average inflow is a guaranteed response time."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：線膨脹係數=1e-05 K⁻¹；溫差=23 K；彈性模數=25 GPa。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: expansion coefficient=1e-05 K⁻¹; temperature difference=23 K; elastic modulus=25 GPa. σ=EαΔT, GPa→MPa ×1000=5.75 MPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b114-v14-11","title":"溫度拘束與構件裂縫：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Thermal restraint and component cracking: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b114-v14-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「拘束溫度應變」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Restrained thermal strain” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將溫度深度分布、含水和裂縫方向一起檢查。記錄核心表面溫度及同條件試體成熟度，將裂縫位置與溫差、拆模及鄰段澆置時間配對，檢查熱歷程是否被遺漏。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check temperature through depth, moisture and crack orientation together. Record core/surface temperature and matched-cured maturity, pairing cracks with temperature differences, formwork removal and adjacent pours to identify missing thermal history. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「拘束溫度應變」的交付需回答：將溫度深度分布、含水和裂縫方向一起檢查。澆置前核准溫度監測及養護方案，變更材料、拆模或澆置順序時重新檢查熱分析，將裂縫與接縫止水的責任一併交付。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Mont Blanc Tunnel, the restrained thermal strain handover must address the following evidence: Check temperature through depth, moisture and crack orientation together. Approve monitoring and curing before pours, revisit thermal analysis after material or sequence changes, and hand over crack and waterstop responsibilities together.","failure":"注意干擾：均溫模型不能代表表層急熱梯度及剝落。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Uniform temperature cannot represent rapid surface gradients or spalling. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b114-v14-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將溫度深度分布、含水和裂縫方向一起檢查。記錄核心表面溫度及同條件試體成熟度，將裂縫位置與溫差、拆模及鄰段澆置時間配對，檢查熱歷程是否被遺漏。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Check temperature through depth, moisture and crack orientation together. Record core/surface temperature and matched-cured maturity, pairing cracks with temperature differences, formwork removal and adjacent pours to identify missing thermal history. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]},{"id":"b114-v14-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「拘束溫度應變」的交付需回答：將溫度深度分布、含水和裂縫方向一起檢查。澆置前核准溫度監測及養護方案，變更材料、拆模或澆置順序時重新檢查熱分析，將裂縫與接縫止水的責任一併交付。","textEn":"For Mont Blanc Tunnel, the restrained thermal strain handover must address the following evidence: Check temperature through depth, moisture and crack orientation together. Approve monitoring and curing before pours, revisit thermal analysis after material or sequence changes, and hand over crack and waterstop responsibilities together.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「溫度拘束與構件裂縫」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Thermal restraint and component cracking\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。","將溫度深度分布、含水和裂縫方向一起檢查。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.","Check temperature through depth, moisture and crack orientation together."],"answer":2,"explanation":"將溫度深度分布、含水和裂縫方向一起檢查。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check temperature through depth, moisture and crack orientation together. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b114-v14-12","title":"溫度拘束與構件裂縫：失效診斷","titleEn":"Thermal restraint and component cracking: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b114-v14-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「拘束溫度應變」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Restrained thermal strain” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"均溫模型不能代表表層急熱梯度及剝落。標準養護試體合格而現場過早冷卻，仍可能形成貫穿裂縫並影響止水；僅增加後續抗壓試驗無法重建失去的養護。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Uniform temperature cannot represent rapid surface gradients or spalling. Passing standard-cured specimens does not prevent through-cracking after rapid cooling, and more later strength tests cannot reconstruct inadequate curing. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：抗壓強度達標不等於抗裂合格，因為彈性模數成熟、徐變、溫度梯度與澆置順序都影響實際拘束；完全拘束彈性估算只能當量級上限比較。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A fully restrained elastic estimate is therefore a scale bound, not a prediction of actual cracking or residual stress.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「混凝土抗壓強度合格就代表厚壁構件不會產生熱裂縫。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Adequate compressive strength proves that thick concrete cannot develop thermal cracks.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b114-v14-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"均溫模型不能代表表層急熱梯度及剝落。標準養護試體合格而現場過早冷卻，仍可能形成貫穿裂縫並影響止水；僅增加後續抗壓試驗無法重建失去的養護。","textEn":"Uniform temperature cannot represent rapid surface gradients or spalling. Passing standard-cured specimens does not prevent through-cracking after rapid cooling, and more later strength tests cannot reconstruct inadequate curing.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]},{"id":"b114-v14-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「溫度拘束與構件裂縫」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Thermal restraint and component cracking\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["均溫模型不能代表表層急熱梯度及剝落。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。"],"optionsEn":["Uniform temperature cannot represent rapid surface gradients or spalling.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure."],"answer":0,"explanation":"均溫模型不能代表表層急熱梯度及剝落。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Uniform temperature cannot represent rapid surface gradients or spalling. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b114-v14-13","title":"環向受力與接縫柔度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Ring force and joint flexibility: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b114-v14-12"],"objective":"說明「襯砌環向壓縮」如何影響蒙布朗隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Lining hoop compression” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Mont Blanc Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"長期整修需區分原有缺陷與新病害，蒙布朗襯砌教學以幾何、材料和支承證據重建荷載路徑。圓形襯砌對均勻外壓可主要以環向壓縮抵抗，但接頭轉動、偏壓與背填空隙會引起彎矩。薄環膜應力只說明其中一條受力路徑；脫模、運輸、頂推及永久狀態的荷載不同，環片局部接觸與止水條件必須另外檢核。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「襯砌環向壓縮」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Refurbishment separates legacy defects from new deterioration using geometry, material and support evidence to reconstruct load paths. A circular lining resists uniform external pressure largely through hoop compression, but joint rotation, uneven load and backfill voids generate bending. Thin-ring membrane stress describes only one load path. Demoulding, transport, jacking and permanent states impose different actions, requiring separate checks of local segment contact and sealing rather than one permanent-load calculation. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Lining hoop compression” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：均勻外壓=0.56 MPa；半徑=3.3 m；厚度=0.35 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: uniform external pressure=0.56 MPa; radius=3.3 m; thickness=0.35 m. σθ=pr/t=5.28 MPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「襯砌環向壓縮」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Lining hoop compression”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b114-v14-13-k1","title":"環向受力與接縫柔度","titleEn":"Ring force and joint flexibility","text":"長期整修需區分原有缺陷與新病害，蒙布朗襯砌教學以幾何、材料和支承證據重建荷載路徑。圓形襯砌對均勻外壓可主要以環向壓縮抵抗，但接頭轉動、偏壓與背填空隙會引起彎矩。","textEn":"Refurbishment separates legacy defects from new deterioration using geometry, material and support evidence to reconstruct load paths. A circular lining resists uniform external pressure largely through hoop compression, but joint rotation, uneven load and backfill voids generate bending.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]},{"id":"b114-v14-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「環向受力與接縫柔度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Ring force and joint flexibility\" is correct?","options":["混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。","長期整修需區分原有缺陷與新病害，蒙布朗襯砌教學以幾何、材料和支承證據重建荷載路徑。","照度越高就必然使隧道內所有物體更容易辨識。"],"optionsEn":["Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure.","Refurbishment separates legacy defects from new deterioration using geometry, material and support evidence to reconstruct load paths.","Higher illuminance necessarily makes every tunnel object easier to detect."],"answer":1,"explanation":"長期整修需區分原有缺陷與新病害，蒙布朗襯砌教學以幾何、材料和支承證據重建荷載路徑。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Refurbishment separates legacy defects from new deterioration using geometry, material and support evidence to reconstruct load paths. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b114-v14-14","title":"環向受力與接縫柔度：定量估算","titleEn":"Ring force and joint flexibility: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b114-v14-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「襯砌環向壓縮」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Lining hoop compression” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：均勻外壓=0.56 MPa；半徑=3.3 m；厚度=0.35 m。σθ=pr/t=5.28 MPa。僅把均勻外壓增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為5.808 MPa。邊界：薄圓環膜應力，不是接縫、偏壓或矩形框架解；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: uniform external pressure=0.56 MPa; radius=3.3 m; thickness=0.35 m. σθ=pr/t=5.28 MPa. Increasing only uniform external pressure by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 5.808 MPa. Boundary: Thin circular-ring membrane stress, not a joint, uneven-load or rectangular-frame solution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：對照歷年裂縫圖、掃描斷面及滲水位置。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare historical crack maps, scanned sections and leak locations.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b114-v14-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：均勻外壓=0.56 MPa；半徑=3.3 m；厚度=0.35 m。σθ=pr/t=5.28 MPa。僅把均勻外壓增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為5.808 MPa。邊界：薄圓環膜應力，不是接縫、偏壓或矩形框架解；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: uniform external pressure=0.56 MPa; radius=3.3 m; thickness=0.35 m. σθ=pr/t=5.28 MPa. Increasing only uniform external pressure by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 5.808 MPa. Boundary: Thin circular-ring membrane stress, not a joint, uneven-load or rectangular-frame solution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]},{"id":"b114-v14-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「環向受力與接縫柔度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Ring force and joint flexibility\", which statement holds?","options":["設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。","增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。","原創教學假設：均勻外壓=0.56 MPa；半徑=3.3 m；厚度=0.35 m。"],"optionsEn":["Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety.","Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.","Original teaching assumptions: uniform external pressure=0.56 MPa; radius=3.3 m; thickness=0.35 m. σθ=pr/t=5.28 MPa."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：均勻外壓=0.56 MPa；半徑=3.3 m；厚度=0.35 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: uniform external pressure=0.56 MPa; radius=3.3 m; thickness=0.35 m. σθ=pr/t=5.28 MPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b114-v14-15","title":"環向受力與接縫柔度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Ring force and joint flexibility: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b114-v14-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「襯砌環向壓縮」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Lining hoop compression” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"對照歷年裂縫圖、掃描斷面及滲水位置。將環形變形、接縫張開與應變和含接頭彈簧的模型比較，分開安裝後、背填後及水頭回升後的基準。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare historical crack maps, scanned sections and leak locations. Compare ring distortion, joint opening and strain with a joint-spring model, separating baselines after installation, grouting and head recovery. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「襯砌環向壓縮」的交付需回答：對照歷年裂縫圖、掃描斷面及滲水位置。設計圖應分開標註各施工階段、接頭剛度及背填條件，構件驗收同時核對幾何、材料批次與止水試驗適用包絡。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Mont Blanc Tunnel, the lining hoop compression handover must address the following evidence: Compare historical crack maps, scanned sections and leak locations. Drawings distinguish stages, joint stiffness and backfill conditions; component acceptance reconciles geometry, material batches and the applicable sealing-test envelope.","failure":"注意干擾：把所有新看見的裂縫當新產生會錯估劣化速率。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Treating newly observed cracks as newly formed overstates deterioration rate. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b114-v14-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"對照歷年裂縫圖、掃描斷面及滲水位置。將環形變形、接縫張開與應變和含接頭彈簧的模型比較，分開安裝後、背填後及水頭回升後的基準。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Compare historical crack maps, scanned sections and leak locations. Compare ring distortion, joint opening and strain with a joint-spring model, separating baselines after installation, grouting and head recovery. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]},{"id":"b114-v14-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「襯砌環向壓縮」的交付需回答：對照歷年裂縫圖、掃描斷面及滲水位置。設計圖應分開標註各施工階段、接頭剛度及背填條件，構件驗收同時核對幾何、材料批次與止水試驗適用包絡。","textEn":"For Mont Blanc Tunnel, the lining hoop compression handover must address the following evidence: Compare historical crack maps, scanned sections and leak locations. Drawings distinguish stages, joint stiffness and backfill conditions; component acceptance reconciles geometry, material batches and the applicable sealing-test envelope.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「環向受力與接縫柔度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Ring force and joint flexibility\"?","options":["對照歷年裂縫圖、掃描斷面及滲水位置。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Compare historical crack maps, scanned sections and leak locations.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":0,"explanation":"對照歷年裂縫圖、掃描斷面及滲水位置。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare historical crack maps, scanned sections and leak locations. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b114-v14-16","title":"環向受力與接縫柔度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Ring force and joint flexibility: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b114-v14-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「襯砌環向壓縮」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Lining hoop compression” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把所有新看見的裂縫當新產生會錯估劣化速率。局部脫空增加環片彎曲，裂縫未必代表混凝土平均強度不足；忽略接縫接觸會把補強方向導向錯誤位置。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Treating newly observed cracks as newly formed overstates deterioration rate. Local voids increase bending, so cracks need not indicate inadequate mean concrete strength; neglecting joint contact can misdirect strengthening. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：薄環膜應力只說明其中一條受力路徑；脫模、運輸、頂推及永久狀態的荷載不同，環片局部接觸與止水條件必須另外檢核。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Demoulding, transport, jacking and permanent states impose different actions, requiring separate checks of local segment contact and sealing rather than one permanent-load calculation.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b114-v14-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把所有新看見的裂縫當新產生會錯估劣化速率。局部脫空增加環片彎曲，裂縫未必代表混凝土平均強度不足；忽略接縫接觸會把補強方向導向錯誤位置。","textEn":"Treating newly observed cracks as newly formed overstates deterioration rate. Local voids increase bending, so cracks need not indicate inadequate mean concrete strength; neglecting joint contact can misdirect strengthening.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]},{"id":"b114-v14-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「環向受力與接縫柔度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Ring force and joint flexibility\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","把所有新看見的裂縫當新產生會錯估劣化速率。","照度越高就必然使隧道內所有物體更容易辨識。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Treating newly observed cracks as newly formed overstates deterioration rate.","Higher illuminance necessarily makes every tunnel object easier to detect."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把所有新看見的裂縫當新產生會錯估劣化速率。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Treating newly observed cracks as newly formed overstates deterioration rate. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b114-v14-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「視覺適應與路面亮度」與「疏散時間與分區可用性」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Visual adaptation and pavement luminance\" and \"Evacuation time and zone availability\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b114-v14-17","title":"視覺適應與路面亮度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Visual adaptation and pavement luminance: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b114-v14-16"],"objective":"說明「漫反射亮度」如何影響蒙布朗隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Diffuse luminance” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Mont Blanc Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"事故和正常行車需要不同的視覺資訊，教材把路面照明與方向標示的可見性分開。駕駛從洞外進入洞內時視覺適應需要時間，照度並不等同從駕駛視角看到的亮度。路面反射、濕度、燈具配光及背景對比共同影響辨識；朗伯模型只示範理想漫反射，不能直接制定入口段燈具間距或真實道路安全值。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「漫反射亮度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Normal driving and incident response need different visual information; distinguish road lighting from visibility of directional signs. Driver adaptation takes time when entering a tunnel, and illuminance is not the luminance seen from the driving position. Pavement reflection, wetness, luminaire distribution and background contrast affect detection. A Lambertian model illustrates ideal diffuse reflection only; it cannot establish entrance-zone spacing or actual road-safety limits without photometric and operational assessment. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Diffuse luminance” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：照度=106 lx；反射率=0.24 無因次。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: illuminance=106 lx; reflectance=0.24 dimensionless.","failure":"常見誤解：「照度越高就必然使隧道內所有物體更容易辨識。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Higher illuminance necessarily makes every tunnel object easier to detect.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「漫反射亮度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Diffuse luminance”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b114-v14-17-k1","title":"視覺適應與路面亮度","titleEn":"Visual adaptation and pavement luminance","text":"事故和正常行車需要不同的視覺資訊，教材把路面照明與方向標示的可見性分開。駕駛從洞外進入洞內時視覺適應需要時間，照度並不等同從駕駛視角看到的亮度。","textEn":"Normal driving and incident response need different visual information; distinguish road lighting from visibility of directional signs. Driver adaptation takes time when entering a tunnel, and illuminance is not the luminance seen from the driving position.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]},{"id":"b114-v14-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：照度越高就必然使隧道內所有物體更容易辨識。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Higher illuminance necessarily makes every tunnel object easier to detect. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「視覺適應與路面亮度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Visual adaptation and pavement luminance\" is correct?","options":["照度越高就必然使隧道內所有物體更容易辨識。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。","事故和正常行車需要不同的視覺資訊，教材把路面照明與方向標示的可見性分開。"],"optionsEn":["Higher illuminance necessarily makes every tunnel object easier to detect.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.","Normal driving and incident response need different visual information; distinguish road lighting from visibility of directional signs."],"answer":2,"explanation":"事故和正常行車需要不同的視覺資訊，教材把路面照明與方向標示的可見性分開。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Normal driving and incident response need different visual information; distinguish road lighting from visibility of directional signs. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b114-v14-18","title":"視覺適應與路面亮度：定量估算","titleEn":"Visual adaptation and pavement luminance: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b114-v14-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「漫反射亮度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Diffuse luminance” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：照度=106 lx；反射率=0.24 無因次。L=ρE/π=8.0978 cd/m²。僅把照度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為8.90758 cd/m²。邊界：理想朗伯漫反射，不是真實濕路面亮度；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: illuminance=106 lx; reflectance=0.24 dimensionless. L=ρE/π=8.0978 cd/m². Increasing only illuminance by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 8.90758 cd/m². Boundary: Ideal Lambertian reflection, not actual wet-road luminance. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：從停車人員和駕駛兩種視角核對標示及亮度。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check signs and luminance from stopped-user and driving viewpoints.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b114-v14-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：照度=106 lx；反射率=0.24 無因次。L=ρE/π=8.0978 cd/m²。僅把照度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為8.90758 cd/m²。邊界：理想朗伯漫反射，不是真實濕路面亮度；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: illuminance=106 lx; reflectance=0.24 dimensionless. L=ρE/π=8.0978 cd/m². Increasing only illuminance by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 8.90758 cd/m². Boundary: Ideal Lambertian reflection, not actual wet-road luminance. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]},{"id":"b114-v14-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「視覺適應與路面亮度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Visual adaptation and pavement luminance\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：照度=106 lx；反射率=0.24 無因次。","集水坑總容積除以平均入流就是保證可用的反應時間。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: illuminance=106 lx; reflectance=0.24 dimensionless.","Gross sump volume divided by average inflow is a guaranteed response time.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：照度=106 lx；反射率=0.24 無因次。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: illuminance=106 lx; reflectance=0.24 dimensionless. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b114-v14-19","title":"視覺適應與路面亮度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Visual adaptation and pavement luminance: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b114-v14-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「漫反射亮度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Diffuse luminance” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"從停車人員和駕駛兩種視角核對標示及亮度。以駕駛視角的亮度量測配合照度網格，分別檢查乾濕路面與燈具衰減，保留外部天空條件。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check signs and luminance from stopped-user and driving viewpoints. Combine driver-view luminance with illuminance grids, checking dry and wet pavement and lamp depreciation while preserving exterior sky conditions. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「漫反射亮度」的交付需回答：從停車人員和駕駛兩種視角核對標示及亮度。將視角、路面狀態和光度校正連同量測交付，照明調整需按核准場景測試，不把理想反射公式當驗收標準。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Mont Blanc Tunnel, the diffuse luminance handover must address the following evidence: Check signs and luminance from stopped-user and driving viewpoints. Hand over viewing geometry, pavement state and photometric calibration; test changes against approved scenarios rather than treating ideal reflection as an acceptance criterion.","failure":"注意干擾：行車視角合格不保證下車後能辨識安全路徑。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Adequate driving visibility does not prove that a user on foot can identify the safe route. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b114-v14-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"從停車人員和駕駛兩種視角核對標示及亮度。以駕駛視角的亮度量測配合照度網格，分別檢查乾濕路面與燈具衰減，保留外部天空條件。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Check signs and luminance from stopped-user and driving viewpoints. Combine driver-view luminance with illuminance grids, checking dry and wet pavement and lamp depreciation while preserving exterior sky conditions. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]},{"id":"b114-v14-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「漫反射亮度」的交付需回答：從停車人員和駕駛兩種視角核對標示及亮度。將視角、路面狀態和光度校正連同量測交付，照明調整需按核准場景測試，不把理想反射公式當驗收標準。","textEn":"For Mont Blanc Tunnel, the diffuse luminance handover must address the following evidence: Check signs and luminance from stopped-user and driving viewpoints. Hand over viewing geometry, pavement state and photometric calibration; test changes against approved scenarios rather than treating ideal reflection as an acceptance criterion.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「視覺適應與路面亮度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Visual adaptation and pavement luminance\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","從停車人員和駕駛兩種視角核對標示及亮度。","風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Check signs and luminance from stopped-user and driving viewpoints.","Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel."],"answer":1,"explanation":"從停車人員和駕駛兩種視角核對標示及亮度。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check signs and luminance from stopped-user and driving viewpoints. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b114-v14-20","title":"視覺適應與路面亮度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Visual adaptation and pavement luminance: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b114-v14-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「漫反射亮度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Diffuse luminance” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"行車視角合格不保證下車後能辨識安全路徑。照度平均值合格仍可能存在低亮度障礙區或眩光，感測器沾污也會使調光系統低估外界亮度。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Adequate driving visibility does not prove that a user on foot can identify the safe route. Acceptable average illuminance can coexist with dark obstacles or glare, while sensor contamination may bias adaptive lighting controls. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：路面反射、濕度、燈具配光及背景對比共同影響辨識；朗伯模型只示範理想漫反射，不能直接制定入口段燈具間距或真實道路安全值。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A Lambertian model illustrates ideal diffuse reflection only; it cannot establish entrance-zone spacing or actual road-safety limits without photometric and operational assessment.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「照度越高就必然使隧道內所有物體更容易辨識。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Higher illuminance necessarily makes every tunnel object easier to detect.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b114-v14-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"行車視角合格不保證下車後能辨識安全路徑。照度平均值合格仍可能存在低亮度障礙區或眩光，感測器沾污也會使調光系統低估外界亮度。","textEn":"Adequate driving visibility does not prove that a user on foot can identify the safe route. Acceptable average illuminance can coexist with dark obstacles or glare, while sensor contamination may bias adaptive lighting controls.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]},{"id":"b114-v14-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「視覺適應與路面亮度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Visual adaptation and pavement luminance\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。","行車視角合格不保證下車後能辨識安全路徑。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.","Adequate driving visibility does not prove that a user on foot can identify the safe route."],"answer":2,"explanation":"行車視角合格不保證下車後能辨識安全路徑。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Adequate driving visibility does not prove that a user on foot can identify the safe route. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b114-v14-21","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b114-v14-20"],"objective":"說明「所需疏散時間」如何影響蒙布朗隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Required evacuation time” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Mont Blanc Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"蒙布朗假想情境將偵知、決策、下車和步行分段，避免只以出口距離估算完整撤離。疏散時間包含辨識、反應、移動及排隊，不只由出口距離決定。人員速度會受煙熱、能見度及行動能力影響，安全判斷還要比較可用安全時間；橫通道存在但門或鄰孔不可用時，圖上的最短路線不一定能作實際選擇。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「所需疏散時間」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Separate detection, decision, vehicle exit and walking in a hypothetical Mont Blanc scenario rather than estimating total evacuation from distance alone. Evacuation includes detection, response, travel and queues, not merely distance to an exit. Smoke, visibility and mobility alter walking speed, while safety requires comparison with available safe time. A passage shown on a plan may be unusable because its door or receiving bore is unavailable, invalidating the nominal shortest route. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Required evacuation time” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：前置時間=106 s；行走距離=300 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=106 s; travel distance=300 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「所需疏散時間」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Required evacuation time”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b114-v14-21-k1","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability","text":"蒙布朗假想情境將偵知、決策、下車和步行分段，避免只以出口距離估算完整撤離。疏散時間包含辨識、反應、移動及排隊，不只由出口距離決定。","textEn":"Separate detection, decision, vehicle exit and walking in a hypothetical Mont Blanc scenario rather than estimating total evacuation from distance alone. Evacuation includes detection, response, travel and queues, not merely distance to an exit.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]},{"id":"b114-v14-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「疏散時間與分區可用性」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Evacuation time and zone availability\" is correct?","options":["蒙布朗假想情境將偵知、決策、下車和步行分段，避免只以出口距離估算完整撤離。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。","設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。"],"optionsEn":["Separate detection, decision, vehicle exit and walking in a hypothetical Mont Blanc scenario rather than estimating total evacuation from distance alone.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.","Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety."],"answer":0,"explanation":"蒙布朗假想情境將偵知、決策、下車和步行分段，避免只以出口距離估算完整撤離。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Separate detection, decision, vehicle exit and walking in a hypothetical Mont Blanc scenario rather than estimating total evacuation from distance alone. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b114-v14-22","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性：定量估算","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b114-v14-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「所需疏散時間」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Required evacuation time” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：前置時間=106 s；行走距離=300 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。RSET=tpre+d/v=481 s。僅把行走距離增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為518.5 s。邊界：單群體固定速度，不含排隊煙熱及能力差異，不能單獨判安全；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=106 s; travel distance=300 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s. RSET=tpre+d/v=481 s. Increasing only travel distance by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 518.5 s. Boundary: One group at fixed speed without queues, smoke or mobility differences; not a safety conclusion. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：演練按時間戳辨認各階段，保留不同起始位置。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Timestamp each exercise stage and retain varied starting positions.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b114-v14-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：前置時間=106 s；行走距離=300 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。RSET=tpre+d/v=481 s。僅把行走距離增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為518.5 s。邊界：單群體固定速度，不含排隊煙熱及能力差異，不能單獨判安全；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=106 s; travel distance=300 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s. RSET=tpre+d/v=481 s. Increasing only travel distance by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 518.5 s. Boundary: One group at fixed speed without queues, smoke or mobility differences; not a safety conclusion. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]},{"id":"b114-v14-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「疏散時間與分區可用性」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Evacuation time and zone availability\", which statement holds?","options":["增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。","原創教學假設：前置時間=106 s；行走距離=300 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.","Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=106 s; travel distance=300 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：前置時間=106 s；行走距離=300 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=106 s; travel distance=300 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b114-v14-23","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b114-v14-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「所需疏散時間」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Required evacuation time” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"演練按時間戳辨認各階段，保留不同起始位置。以人流模擬或受控演練分辨前置時間、行走與門口排隊，核對每個出口接收區的可用狀態及通訊紀錄。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Timestamp each exercise stage and retain varied starting positions. Separate pre-movement, travel and doorway queues through simulation or controlled drills, checking receiving-zone availability and communication records for each exit. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「所需疏散時間」的交付需回答：演練按時間戳辨認各階段，保留不同起始位置。疏散模型保留人口、速度分布及出口狀態，演練改動由營運與防災責任者批准，教材算例不得當作現場指揮程序。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Mont Blanc Tunnel, the required evacuation time handover must address the following evidence: Timestamp each exercise stage and retain varied starting positions. Retain population, speed distribution and exit states; operations and fire-safety owners approve drill changes, and classroom calculations are not incident-command procedures.","failure":"注意干擾：反應延遲被省略時，精確步速仍會產生偏低總時間。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Omitted response delay produces a low total despite precise walking speed. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b114-v14-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"演練按時間戳辨認各階段，保留不同起始位置。以人流模擬或受控演練分辨前置時間、行走與門口排隊，核對每個出口接收區的可用狀態及通訊紀錄。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Timestamp each exercise stage and retain varied starting positions. Separate pre-movement, travel and doorway queues through simulation or controlled drills, checking receiving-zone availability and communication records for each exit. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]},{"id":"b114-v14-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「所需疏散時間」的交付需回答：演練按時間戳辨認各階段，保留不同起始位置。疏散模型保留人口、速度分布及出口狀態，演練改動由營運與防災責任者批准，教材算例不得當作現場指揮程序。","textEn":"For Mont Blanc Tunnel, the required evacuation time handover must address the following evidence: Timestamp each exercise stage and retain varied starting positions. Retain population, speed distribution and exit states; operations and fire-safety owners approve drill changes, and classroom calculations are not incident-command procedures.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「疏散時間與分區可用性」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Evacuation time and zone availability\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","混凝土抗壓強度合格就代表厚壁構件不會產生熱裂縫。","演練按時間戳辨認各階段，保留不同起始位置。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Adequate compressive strength proves that thick concrete cannot develop thermal cracks.","Timestamp each exercise stage and retain varied starting positions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"演練按時間戳辨認各階段，保留不同起始位置。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Timestamp each exercise stage and retain varied starting positions. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b114-v14-24","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性：失效診斷","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b114-v14-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「所需疏散時間」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Required evacuation time” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"反應延遲被省略時，精確步速仍會產生偏低總時間。以最快成人速度套全部旅客會低估需求，若忽略接收孔受煙或車流影響，疏散可能移到另一個危險邊界。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Omitted response delay produces a low total despite precise walking speed. Applying the fastest adult speed to everyone understates demand; overlooking smoke or traffic in the receiving bore can transfer evacuees into another hazard. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：人員速度會受煙熱、能見度及行動能力影響，安全判斷還要比較可用安全時間；橫通道存在但門或鄰孔不可用時，圖上的最短路線不一定能作實際選擇。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A passage shown on a plan may be unusable because its door or receiving bore is unavailable, invalidating the nominal shortest route.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b114-v14-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"反應延遲被省略時，精確步速仍會產生偏低總時間。以最快成人速度套全部旅客會低估需求，若忽略接收孔受煙或車流影響，疏散可能移到另一個危險邊界。","textEn":"Omitted response delay produces a low total despite precise walking speed. Applying the fastest adult speed to everyone understates demand; overlooking smoke or traffic in the receiving bore can transfer evacuees into another hazard.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]},{"id":"b114-v14-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「疏散時間與分區可用性」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Evacuation time and zone availability\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["反應延遲被省略時，精確步速仍會產生偏低總時間。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。"],"optionsEn":["Omitted response delay produces a low total despite precise walking speed.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety."],"answer":0,"explanation":"反應延遲被省略時，精確步速仍會產生偏低總時間。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Omitted response delay produces a low total despite precise walking speed. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b114-v14-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「設備備援與共同失效」與「停泵緩衝與有效集水容積」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Equipment redundancy and common failure\" and \"Outage buffer and effective sump volume\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b114-v14-25","title":"設備備援與共同失效：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Equipment redundancy and common failure: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b114-v14-24"],"objective":"說明「系統不可用率」如何影響蒙布朗隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “System unavailability” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Mont Blanc Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"偵知、通訊和供電構成串聯依賴，教材研究兩套感測器共用控制器時為何不能直接平方失效率。兩套設備只有在故障近似獨立且切換可靠時，並聯才顯著降低不可用率。共用配電、控制軟體、冷卻或受淹位置會把獨立假設破壞；維修停用也改變當下配置，因此可靠度模型必須明列共有資源和設備狀態，不能只數備用台數。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「系統不可用率」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Detection, communication and power form dependencies; examine why two sensors on one controller do not justify squaring failure probability. Parallel equipment sharply reduces unavailability only when failures are approximately independent and transfer works. Shared power, software, cooling or flood exposure breaks that assumption. Planned maintenance also changes the available configuration, so reliability models must identify shared resources and states rather than count spare units or multiply unsupported independent probabilities. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “System unavailability” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：單機不可用率=0.023 無因次。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: single-unit unavailability=0.023 dimensionless.","failure":"常見誤解：「設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「系統不可用率」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “System unavailability”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b114-v14-25-k1","title":"設備備援與共同失效","titleEn":"Equipment redundancy and common failure","text":"偵知、通訊和供電構成串聯依賴，教材研究兩套感測器共用控制器時為何不能直接平方失效率。兩套設備只有在故障近似獨立且切換可靠時，並聯才顯著降低不可用率。","textEn":"Detection, communication and power form dependencies; examine why two sensors on one controller do not justify squaring failure probability. Parallel equipment sharply reduces unavailability only when failures are approximately independent and transfer works.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]},{"id":"b114-v14-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「設備備援與共同失效」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Equipment redundancy and common failure\" is correct?","options":["設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。","偵知、通訊和供電構成串聯依賴，教材研究兩套感測器共用控制器時為何不能直接平方失效率。","集水坑總容積除以平均入流就是保證可用的反應時間。"],"optionsEn":["Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety.","Detection, communication and power form dependencies; examine why two sensors on one controller do not justify squaring failure probability.","Gross sump volume divided by average inflow is a guaranteed response time."],"answer":1,"explanation":"偵知、通訊和供電構成串聯依賴，教材研究兩套感測器共用控制器時為何不能直接平方失效率。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Detection, communication and power form dependencies; examine why two sensors on one controller do not justify squaring failure probability. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b114-v14-26","title":"設備備援與共同失效：定量估算","titleEn":"Equipment redundancy and common failure: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b114-v14-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「系統不可用率」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “System unavailability” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：單機不可用率=0.023 無因次。Uparallel=U²=0.000529 probability。僅把單機不可用率增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.00064009 probability。邊界：完全獨立並聯與完美切換，不含共同失效；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: single-unit unavailability=0.023 dimensionless. Uparallel=U²=0.000529 probability. Increasing only single-unit unavailability by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.00064009 probability. Boundary: Independent parallel units with perfect transfer, excluding common failures. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：沿告警鏈逐點確認共用設備和故障傳遞。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Trace shared equipment and fault propagation along the alarm chain.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b114-v14-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：單機不可用率=0.023 無因次。Uparallel=U²=0.000529 probability。僅把單機不可用率增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.00064009 probability。邊界：完全獨立並聯與完美切換，不含共同失效；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: single-unit unavailability=0.023 dimensionless. Uparallel=U²=0.000529 probability. Increasing only single-unit unavailability by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.00064009 probability. Boundary: Independent parallel units with perfect transfer, excluding common failures. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]},{"id":"b114-v14-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「設備備援與共同失效」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Equipment redundancy and common failure\", which statement holds?","options":["全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。","風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。","原創教學假設：單機不可用率=0.023 無因次。"],"optionsEn":["Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.","Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.","Original teaching assumptions: single-unit unavailability=0.023 dimensionless."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：單機不可用率=0.023 無因次。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: single-unit unavailability=0.023 dimensionless. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b114-v14-27","title":"設備備援與共同失效：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Equipment redundancy and common failure: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b114-v14-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「系統不可用率」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “System unavailability” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"沿告警鏈逐點確認共用設備和故障傳遞。由設備清單畫出故障樹，將電源、控制及實體位置追到共同節點，並用事件及維修紀錄檢查獨立假設。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Trace shared equipment and fault propagation along the alarm chain. Build a fault tree from the asset list, trace power, control and location to shared nodes, and test independence against incident and maintenance records. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「系統不可用率」的交付需回答：沿告警鏈逐點確認共用設備和故障傳遞。維修計畫附當日可用配置與剩餘備援，任何共同資源更動同步更新故障樹，切換試驗由設備及營運團隊共同見證。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Mont Blanc Tunnel, the system unavailability handover must address the following evidence: Trace shared equipment and fault propagation along the alarm chain. Attach the actual configuration and remaining redundancy to maintenance plans, update fault trees after shared-resource changes, and witness transfer tests jointly.","failure":"注意干擾：共同控制器失效會同時切斷兩個看似獨立感測通道。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A common controller failure disables two apparently independent sensing channels. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b114-v14-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"沿告警鏈逐點確認共用設備和故障傳遞。由設備清單畫出故障樹，將電源、控制及實體位置追到共同節點，並用事件及維修紀錄檢查獨立假設。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Trace shared equipment and fault propagation along the alarm chain. Build a fault tree from the asset list, trace power, control and location to shared nodes, and test independence against incident and maintenance records. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]},{"id":"b114-v14-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「系統不可用率」的交付需回答：沿告警鏈逐點確認共用設備和故障傳遞。維修計畫附當日可用配置與剩餘備援，任何共同資源更動同步更新故障樹，切換試驗由設備及營運團隊共同見證。","textEn":"For Mont Blanc Tunnel, the system unavailability handover must address the following evidence: Trace shared equipment and fault propagation along the alarm chain. Attach the actual configuration and remaining redundancy to maintenance plans, update fault trees after shared-resource changes, and witness transfer tests jointly.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「設備備援與共同失效」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Equipment redundancy and common failure\"?","options":["沿告警鏈逐點確認共用設備和故障傳遞。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。"],"optionsEn":["Trace shared equipment and fault propagation along the alarm chain.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure."],"answer":0,"explanation":"沿告警鏈逐點確認共用設備和故障傳遞。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Trace shared equipment and fault propagation along the alarm chain. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b114-v14-28","title":"設備備援與共同失效：失效診斷","titleEn":"Equipment redundancy and common failure: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b114-v14-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「系統不可用率」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “System unavailability” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"共同控制器失效會同時切斷兩個看似獨立感測通道。重複安裝卻共用單一供電可能在一次故障中全部停機，帳面可靠度很高但實際不可用時間沒有降低。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A common controller failure disables two apparently independent sensing channels. Duplicated equipment on one supply can fail together in a single event, leaving actual downtime unchanged despite optimistic calculated reliability. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：共用配電、控制軟體、冷卻或受淹位置會把獨立假設破壞；維修停用也改變當下配置，因此可靠度模型必須明列共有資源和設備狀態，不能只數備用台數。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Planned maintenance also changes the available configuration, so reliability models must identify shared resources and states rather than count spare units or multiply unsupported independent probabilities.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b114-v14-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"共同控制器失效會同時切斷兩個看似獨立感測通道。重複安裝卻共用單一供電可能在一次故障中全部停機，帳面可靠度很高但實際不可用時間沒有降低。","textEn":"A common controller failure disables two apparently independent sensing channels. Duplicated equipment on one supply can fail together in a single event, leaving actual downtime unchanged despite optimistic calculated reliability.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]},{"id":"b114-v14-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「設備備援與共同失效」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Equipment redundancy and common failure\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","共同控制器失效會同時切斷兩個看似獨立感測通道。","集水坑總容積除以平均入流就是保證可用的反應時間。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","A common controller failure disables two apparently independent sensing channels.","Gross sump volume divided by average inflow is a guaranteed response time."],"answer":1,"explanation":"共同控制器失效會同時切斷兩個看似獨立感測通道。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A common controller failure disables two apparently independent sensing channels. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b114-v14-29","title":"停泵緩衝與有效集水容積：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Outage buffer and effective sump volume: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b114-v14-28"],"objective":"說明「剩餘集水容積」如何影響蒙布朗隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Remaining sump volume” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Mont Blanc Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"道路水、清洗水和滲水在假想集水系統中有不同時間尺度，教材分析同時進流對容量的影響。集水坑在泵停止後提供有限緩衝，剩餘容積需扣除初始水量、沉積及不可用死角。緩衝時間取決於淨入流，不是名牌抽水能力；警報延遲、備援切換與水量突增會消耗餘裕，排水電力又可能與其他安全設備共用失效原因。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「剩餘集水容積」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Road water, wash water and seepage have different time scales; assess coincident inflows into a hypothetical sump. A sump offers finite buffering after pumps stop, with usable volume reduced by initial water, sediment and dead spaces. Buffer time depends on net inflow rather than pump nameplate capacity. Alarm delay, transfer time and inflow surges consume reserve, while shared electrical dependencies may disable drainage and other safety equipment together. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Remaining sump volume” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：有效剩餘容積=560 m³；淨入流=0.19 m³/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: usable reserve=560 m³; net inflow=0.19 m³/s. t=V/Q/60=49.1228 min.","failure":"常見誤解：「集水坑總容積除以平均入流就是保證可用的反應時間。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Gross sump volume divided by average inflow is a guaranteed response time.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「剩餘集水容積」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Remaining sump volume”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b114-v14-29-k1","title":"停泵緩衝與有效集水容積","titleEn":"Outage buffer and effective sump volume","text":"道路水、清洗水和滲水在假想集水系統中有不同時間尺度，教材分析同時進流對容量的影響。集水坑在泵停止後提供有限緩衝，剩餘容積需扣除初始水量、沉積及不可用死角。","textEn":"Road water, wash water and seepage have different time scales; assess coincident inflows into a hypothetical sump. A sump offers finite buffering after pumps stop, with usable volume reduced by initial water, sediment and dead spaces.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]},{"id":"b114-v14-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：集水坑總容積除以平均入流就是保證可用的反應時間。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Gross sump volume divided by average inflow is a guaranteed response time. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「停泵緩衝與有效集水容積」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Outage buffer and effective sump volume\" is correct?","options":["集水坑總容積除以平均入流就是保證可用的反應時間。","增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。","道路水、清洗水和滲水在假想集水系統中有不同時間尺度，教材分析同時進流對容量的影響。"],"optionsEn":["Gross sump volume divided by average inflow is a guaranteed response time.","Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.","Road water, wash water and seepage have different time scales; assess coincident inflows into a hypothetical sump."],"answer":2,"explanation":"道路水、清洗水和滲水在假想集水系統中有不同時間尺度，教材分析同時進流對容量的影響。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Road water, wash water and seepage have different time scales; assess coincident inflows into a hypothetical sump. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b114-v14-30","title":"停泵緩衝與有效集水容積：定量估算","titleEn":"Outage buffer and effective sump volume: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b114-v14-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「剩餘集水容積」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Remaining sump volume” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：有效剩餘容積=560 m³；淨入流=0.19 m³/s。t=V/Q/60=49.1228 min。僅把淨入流增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為44.6571 min。邊界：停泵固定入流，不含警報延遲及水量突增；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: usable reserve=560 m³; net inflow=0.19 m³/s. t=V/Q/60=49.1228 min. Increasing only net inflow by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 44.6571 min. Boundary: Constant inflow during outage, excluding alarm delay and inflow surges. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將清洗計畫與降雨和泵曲線一起閉合水量帳。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Close the balance using cleaning schedules, rainfall and pump curves.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b114-v14-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：有效剩餘容積=560 m³；淨入流=0.19 m³/s。t=V/Q/60=49.1228 min。僅把淨入流增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為44.6571 min。邊界：停泵固定入流，不含警報延遲及水量突增；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: usable reserve=560 m³; net inflow=0.19 m³/s. t=V/Q/60=49.1228 min. Increasing only net inflow by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 44.6571 min. Boundary: Constant inflow during outage, excluding alarm delay and inflow surges. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]},{"id":"b114-v14-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「停泵緩衝與有效集水容積」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Outage buffer and effective sump volume\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：有效剩餘容積=560 m³；淨入流=0.19 m³/s。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。","混凝土抗壓強度合格就代表厚壁構件不會產生熱裂縫。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: usable reserve=560 m³; net inflow=0.19 m³/s. t=V/Q/60=49.1228 min.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.","Adequate compressive strength proves that thick concrete cannot develop thermal cracks."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：有效剩餘容積=560 m³；淨入流=0.19 m³/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: usable reserve=560 m³; net inflow=0.19 m³/s. t=V/Q/60=49.1228 min. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b114-v14-31","title":"停泵緩衝與有效集水容積：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Outage buffer and effective sump volume: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b114-v14-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「剩餘集水容積」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Remaining sump volume” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將清洗計畫與降雨和泵曲線一起閉合水量帳。以水位容積曲線和流量計核對停泵水位上升率，另檢查淤積、警報時間戳及備援電力切換紀錄。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Close the balance using cleaning schedules, rainfall and pump curves. Compare outage level-rise rate with the level-volume curve and flowmeter, separately checking sediment, alarm timestamps and backup-power transfer records. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「剩餘集水容積」的交付需回答：將清洗計畫與降雨和泵曲線一起閉合水量帳。交接有效容積、初始水位及延遲預算，由排水與電氣責任人共同核對故障情境，定期清淤後保存量測證據。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Mont Blanc Tunnel, the remaining sump volume handover must address the following evidence: Close the balance using cleaning schedules, rainfall and pump curves. Handover usable volume, initial level and delay budgets; drainage and electrical owners jointly review failures and retain measurements after sediment removal.","failure":"注意干擾：只依平日滲水選泵會漏掉清洗或事件排水尖峰。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Sizing from routine seepage alone misses wash or incident-drainage peaks. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b114-v14-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將清洗計畫與降雨和泵曲線一起閉合水量帳。以水位容積曲線和流量計核對停泵水位上升率，另檢查淤積、警報時間戳及備援電力切換紀錄。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Close the balance using cleaning schedules, rainfall and pump curves. Compare outage level-rise rate with the level-volume curve and flowmeter, separately checking sediment, alarm timestamps and backup-power transfer records. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]},{"id":"b114-v14-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「剩餘集水容積」的交付需回答：將清洗計畫與降雨和泵曲線一起閉合水量帳。交接有效容積、初始水位及延遲預算，由排水與電氣責任人共同核對故障情境，定期清淤後保存量測證據。","textEn":"For Mont Blanc Tunnel, the remaining sump volume handover must address the following evidence: Close the balance using cleaning schedules, rainfall and pump curves. Handover usable volume, initial level and delay budgets; drainage and electrical owners jointly review failures and retain measurements after sediment removal.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「停泵緩衝與有效集水容積」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Outage buffer and effective sump volume\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","將清洗計畫與降雨和泵曲線一起閉合水量帳。","照度越高就必然使隧道內所有物體更容易辨識。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Close the balance using cleaning schedules, rainfall and pump curves.","Higher illuminance necessarily makes every tunnel object easier to detect."],"answer":1,"explanation":"將清洗計畫與降雨和泵曲線一起閉合水量帳。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Close the balance using cleaning schedules, rainfall and pump curves. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b114-v14-32","title":"停泵緩衝與有效集水容積：失效診斷","titleEn":"Outage buffer and effective sump volume: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b114-v14-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「剩餘集水容積」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Remaining sump volume” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只依平日滲水選泵會漏掉清洗或事件排水尖峰。未扣除沉積的總容積會高估反應時間，若警報與抽水同失電，操作者可能在緩衝已耗盡後才得知水位上升。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Sizing from routine seepage alone misses wash or incident-drainage peaks. Gross volume without sediment deduction overstates response time; shared loss of alarm and pumping power can hide rising water until the buffer is exhausted. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：緩衝時間取決於淨入流，不是名牌抽水能力；警報延遲、備援切換與水量突增會消耗餘裕，排水電力又可能與其他安全設備共用失效原因。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Alarm delay, transfer time and inflow surges consume reserve, while shared electrical dependencies may disable drainage and other safety equipment together.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「集水坑總容積除以平均入流就是保證可用的反應時間。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Gross sump volume divided by average inflow is a guaranteed response time.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b114-v14-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只依平日滲水選泵會漏掉清洗或事件排水尖峰。未扣除沉積的總容積會高估反應時間，若警報與抽水同失電，操作者可能在緩衝已耗盡後才得知水位上升。","textEn":"Sizing from routine seepage alone misses wash or incident-drainage peaks. Gross volume without sediment deduction overstates response time; shared loss of alarm and pumping power can hide rising water until the buffer is exhausted.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]},{"id":"b114-v14-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「停泵緩衝與有效集水容積」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Outage buffer and effective sump volume\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。","只依平日滲水選泵會漏掉清洗或事件排水尖峰。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.","Sizing from routine seepage alone misses wash or incident-drainage peaks."],"answer":2,"explanation":"只依平日滲水選泵會漏掉清洗或事件排水尖峰。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Sizing from routine seepage alone misses wash or incident-drainage peaks. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b114-v14-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」與「資產編碼與可追溯交接」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Shared access and transport bottlenecks\" and \"Asset identity and traceable handover\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b114-v14-33","title":"共享通道與運輸瓶頸：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Shared access and transport bottlenecks: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b114-v14-32"],"objective":"說明「出渣運輸節拍」如何影響蒙布朗隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Muck-transport cycle” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Mont Blanc Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"蒙布朗整修窗口包含隔離、施工和重新測試，短期關閉的有效工時不能以日曆時間直接估算。多工作面只有在供電、通風、出渣與材料供應同步充足時才增加總產量。共用豎井或軌道形成串聯瓶頸，排隊和維修窗口會降低名目容量；緩衝區太大又可能侵占通行與救援空間，因此不能單純把各面產能相加。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「出渣運輸節拍」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Refurbishment windows include isolation, work and retesting; productive hours differ from calendar closure duration. Multiple headings increase output only when power, air, muck transport and materials support them together. Shared shafts or railways become serial bottlenecks, while queues and maintenance reduce nominal capacity. Large buffers may obstruct personnel and rescue access, so face capacities cannot simply be added without a network-level transport and storage check. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Muck-transport cycle” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=33 t；往返週期=38 min。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=33 t; cycle=38 min.","failure":"常見誤解：「增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「出渣運輸節拍」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Muck-transport cycle”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b114-v14-33-k1","title":"共享通道與運輸瓶頸","titleEn":"Shared access and transport bottlenecks","text":"蒙布朗整修窗口包含隔離、施工和重新測試，短期關閉的有效工時不能以日曆時間直接估算。多工作面只有在供電、通風、出渣與材料供應同步充足時才增加總產量。","textEn":"Refurbishment windows include isolation, work and retesting; productive hours differ from calendar closure duration. Multiple headings increase output only when power, air, muck transport and materials support them together.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]},{"id":"b114-v14-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Shared access and transport bottlenecks\" is correct?","options":["蒙布朗整修窗口包含隔離、施工和重新測試，短期關閉的有效工時不能以日曆時間直接估算。","增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。"],"optionsEn":["Refurbishment windows include isolation, work and retesting; productive hours differ from calendar closure duration.","Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted."],"answer":0,"explanation":"蒙布朗整修窗口包含隔離、施工和重新測試，短期關閉的有效工時不能以日曆時間直接估算。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Refurbishment windows include isolation, work and retesting; productive hours differ from calendar closure duration. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b114-v14-34","title":"共享通道與運輸瓶頸：定量估算","titleEn":"Shared access and transport bottlenecks: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b114-v14-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「出渣運輸節拍」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Muck-transport cycle” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=33 t；往返週期=38 min。C=N payload 60/T=208.421 t/h。僅把往返週期增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為189.474 t/h。邊界：無排隊理想循環，並非共享路段實際產能；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=33 t; cycle=38 min. C=N payload 60/T=208.421 t/h. Increasing only cycle by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 189.474 t/h. Boundary: Ideal cycle without queues, not actual shared-route production. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用完整作業鏈核對材料搬運和恢復測試占時。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check material handling and restoration tests within the full work sequence.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b114-v14-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=33 t；往返週期=38 min。C=N payload 60/T=208.421 t/h。僅把往返週期增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為189.474 t/h。邊界：無排隊理想循環，並非共享路段實際產能；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=33 t; cycle=38 min. C=N payload 60/T=208.421 t/h. Increasing only cycle by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 189.474 t/h. Boundary: Ideal cycle without queues, not actual shared-route production. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]},{"id":"b114-v14-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Shared access and transport bottlenecks\", which statement holds?","options":["風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。","原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=33 t；往返週期=38 min。","混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。"],"optionsEn":["Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.","Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=33 t; cycle=38 min.","Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=33 t；往返週期=38 min。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=33 t; cycle=38 min. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b114-v14-35","title":"共享通道與運輸瓶頸：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Shared access and transport bottlenecks: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b114-v14-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「出渣運輸節拍」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Muck-transport cycle” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用完整作業鏈核對材料搬運和恢復測試占時。以裝載質量、往返時間及排隊時間重建物流曲線，再核對緩衝占用、共用通道優先權與維修時段。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check material handling and restoration tests within the full work sequence. Reconstruct flow from payload, round-trip and queue times, then check buffer occupancy, shared-route priorities and maintenance periods. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「出渣運輸節拍」的交付需回答：用完整作業鏈核對材料搬運和恢復測試占時。每日排程同時標示人員、材料和維修的占用時段，任何物流改線先檢查通風與應變通道，不能只看運量提升。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Mont Blanc Tunnel, the muck-transport cycle handover must address the following evidence: Check material handling and restoration tests within the full work sequence. Schedules show personnel, materials and maintenance occupancy together; rerouting first checks ventilation and emergency access rather than only throughput gains.","failure":"注意干擾：省略重測會留下設備已安裝但未證明可用的狀態。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Omitted retesting leaves installed equipment without demonstrated availability. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b114-v14-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用完整作業鏈核對材料搬運和恢復測試占時。以裝載質量、往返時間及排隊時間重建物流曲線，再核對緩衝占用、共用通道優先權與維修時段。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Check material handling and restoration tests within the full work sequence. Reconstruct flow from payload, round-trip and queue times, then check buffer occupancy, shared-route priorities and maintenance periods. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]},{"id":"b114-v14-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「出渣運輸節拍」的交付需回答：用完整作業鏈核對材料搬運和恢復測試占時。每日排程同時標示人員、材料和維修的占用時段，任何物流改線先檢查通風與應變通道，不能只看運量提升。","textEn":"For Mont Blanc Tunnel, the muck-transport cycle handover must address the following evidence: Check material handling and restoration tests within the full work sequence. Schedules show personnel, materials and maintenance occupancy together; rerouting first checks ventilation and emergency access rather than only throughput gains.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Shared access and transport bottlenecks\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。","用完整作業鏈核對材料搬運和恢復測試占時。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.","Check material handling and restoration tests within the full work sequence."],"answer":2,"explanation":"用完整作業鏈核對材料搬運和恢復測試占時。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check material handling and restoration tests within the full work sequence. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b114-v14-36","title":"共享通道與運輸瓶頸：失效診斷","titleEn":"Shared access and transport bottlenecks: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b114-v14-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「出渣運輸節拍」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Muck-transport cycle” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"省略重測會留下設備已安裝但未證明可用的狀態。把理想往返時間當全天常數會忽略交會等待與卸料堵塞，導致工作面停工或把材料堆入必要通道。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Omitted retesting leaves installed equipment without demonstrated availability. Treating an ideal cycle as constant all day misses passing delays and unloading blockages, stopping headings or pushing material into essential access space. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：共用豎井或軌道形成串聯瓶頸，排隊和維修窗口會降低名目容量；緩衝區太大又可能侵占通行與救援空間，因此不能單純把各面產能相加。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Large buffers may obstruct personnel and rescue access, so face capacities cannot simply be added without a network-level transport and storage check.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b114-v14-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"省略重測會留下設備已安裝但未證明可用的狀態。把理想往返時間當全天常數會忽略交會等待與卸料堵塞，導致工作面停工或把材料堆入必要通道。","textEn":"Omitted retesting leaves installed equipment without demonstrated availability. Treating an ideal cycle as constant all day misses passing delays and unloading blockages, stopping headings or pushing material into essential access space.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]},{"id":"b114-v14-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Shared access and transport bottlenecks\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["省略重測會留下設備已安裝但未證明可用的狀態。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。"],"optionsEn":["Omitted retesting leaves installed equipment without demonstrated availability.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted."],"answer":0,"explanation":"省略重測會留下設備已安裝但未證明可用的狀態。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Omitted retesting leaves installed equipment without demonstrated availability. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b114-v14-37","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b114-v14-36"],"objective":"說明「資產資料完整度」如何影響蒙布朗隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Asset-record completeness” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Mont Blanc Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"跨境營運資料需讓事件時間、設備狀態與工單互相對應，蒙布朗教材要求保留事件版本而非覆寫。地下設備的竣工資料必須讓維護人員找到正確位置、材料批次和控制版本。只有上傳圖面而沒有變更歷程，無法分辨元件替換與真正劣化；告警、儀器、線路及工單使用一致識別碼，才可能把量測趨勢連回實際受力或水力系統。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「資產資料完整度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Cross-border records must align event times, asset states and work orders while preserving revisions instead of overwriting history. Handover must let maintainers find the correct location, material batch and control revision. Drawings without change history cannot distinguish replacement from deterioration. Consistent identifiers across alarms, instruments, circuits and work orders are essential for linking trends to the physical structural or hydraulic system instead of treating each record as an isolated file. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Asset-record completeness” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：設備總數=113 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: asset count=113 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=85.8407 %.","failure":"常見誤解：「全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「資產資料完整度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Asset-record completeness”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b114-v14-37-k1","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover","text":"跨境營運資料需讓事件時間、設備狀態與工單互相對應，蒙布朗教材要求保留事件版本而非覆寫。地下設備的竣工資料必須讓維護人員找到正確位置、材料批次和控制版本。","textEn":"Cross-border records must align event times, asset states and work orders while preserving revisions instead of overwriting history. Handover must let maintainers find the correct location, material batch and control revision.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]},{"id":"b114-v14-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「資產編碼與可追溯交接」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Asset identity and traceable handover\" is correct?","options":["全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。","跨境營運資料需讓事件時間、設備狀態與工單互相對應，蒙布朗教材要求保留事件版本而非覆寫。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.","Cross-border records must align event times, asset states and work orders while preserving revisions instead of overwriting history.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":1,"explanation":"跨境營運資料需讓事件時間、設備狀態與工單互相對應，蒙布朗教材要求保留事件版本而非覆寫。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Cross-border records must align event times, asset states and work orders while preserving revisions instead of overwriting history. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b114-v14-38","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：定量估算","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b114-v14-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「資產資料完整度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Asset-record completeness” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：設備總數=113 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。coverage=100(N−missing)/N=85.8407 %。僅把缺紀錄數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為84.4248 %。邊界：資料完整度，不等於安全或可靠度；擾動為連續敏感度，實際個數為整數；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: asset count=113 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=85.8407 %. Increasing only missing records by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 84.4248 %. Boundary: Record completeness, not safety or reliability; perturbation is continuous sensitivity while actual counts are integers. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：抽查一個事件從偵知到維修完成的資料鏈。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Trace one event from detection through maintenance completion.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b114-v14-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：設備總數=113 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。coverage=100(N−missing)/N=85.8407 %。僅把缺紀錄數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為84.4248 %。邊界：資料完整度，不等於安全或可靠度；擾動為連續敏感度，實際個數為整數；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: asset count=113 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=85.8407 %. Increasing only missing records by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 84.4248 %. Boundary: Record completeness, not safety or reliability; perturbation is continuous sensitivity while actual counts are integers. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]},{"id":"b114-v14-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「資產編碼與可追溯交接」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Asset identity and traceable handover\", which statement holds?","options":["混凝土抗壓強度合格就代表厚壁構件不會產生熱裂縫。","照度越高就必然使隧道內所有物體更容易辨識。","原創教學假設：設備總數=113 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。"],"optionsEn":["Adequate compressive strength proves that thick concrete cannot develop thermal cracks.","Higher illuminance necessarily makes every tunnel object easier to detect.","Original teaching assumptions: asset count=113 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=85.8407 %."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：設備總數=113 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: asset count=113 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=85.8407 %. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b114-v14-39","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b114-v14-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「資產資料完整度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Asset-record completeness” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"抽查一個事件從偵知到維修完成的資料鏈。抽取一條告警，從控制畫面追到設備、線路、圖面和工單，核對位置、版本及校正日期並記錄無法閉合的欄位。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Trace one event from detection through maintenance completion. Trace a sampled alarm from screen to equipment, circuit, drawing and work order, checking location, revision and calibration dates and recording broken links. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「資產資料完整度」的交付需回答：抽查一個事件從偵知到維修完成的資料鏈。交接以可完成的定位、查找與復原任務驗證，由維護責任人確認現場可用性；完整度只是資料指標，不代表結構安全或設備可靠。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Mont Blanc Tunnel, the asset-record completeness handover must address the following evidence: Trace one event from detection through maintenance completion. Validate handover through achievable location, retrieval and recovery tasks witnessed by maintainers; completeness measures records, not structural safety or equipment reliability.","failure":"注意干擾：時鐘不同步會顛倒事件順序而誤導根因分析。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Unsynchronised clocks reverse apparent event order and mislead root-cause analysis. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b114-v14-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"抽查一個事件從偵知到維修完成的資料鏈。抽取一條告警，從控制畫面追到設備、線路、圖面和工單，核對位置、版本及校正日期並記錄無法閉合的欄位。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Trace one event from detection through maintenance completion. Trace a sampled alarm from screen to equipment, circuit, drawing and work order, checking location, revision and calibration dates and recording broken links. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]},{"id":"b114-v14-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「資產資料完整度」的交付需回答：抽查一個事件從偵知到維修完成的資料鏈。交接以可完成的定位、查找與復原任務驗證，由維護責任人確認現場可用性；完整度只是資料指標，不代表結構安全或設備可靠。","textEn":"For Mont Blanc Tunnel, the asset-record completeness handover must address the following evidence: Trace one event from detection through maintenance completion. Validate handover through achievable location, retrieval and recovery tasks witnessed by maintainers; completeness measures records, not structural safety or equipment reliability.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「資產編碼與可追溯交接」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Asset identity and traceable handover\"?","options":["抽查一個事件從偵知到維修完成的資料鏈。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。"],"optionsEn":["Trace one event from detection through maintenance completion.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety."],"answer":0,"explanation":"抽查一個事件從偵知到維修完成的資料鏈。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Trace one event from detection through maintenance completion. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b114-v14-40","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：失效診斷","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b114-v14-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「資產資料完整度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Asset-record completeness” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"時鐘不同步會顛倒事件順序而誤導根因分析。設備改名卻未更新控制畫面會引導人員隔離錯誤回路，材料批次缺漏則使同批缺陷無法追蹤到其他位置。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Unsynchronised clocks reverse apparent event order and mislead root-cause analysis. Renaming an asset without updating the screen can isolate the wrong circuit; missing material batches prevent tracing related defects at other locations. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：只有上傳圖面而沒有變更歷程，無法分辨元件替換與真正劣化；告警、儀器、線路及工單使用一致識別碼，才可能把量測趨勢連回實際受力或水力系統。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Consistent identifiers across alarms, instruments, circuits and work orders are essential for linking trends to the physical structural or hydraulic system instead of treating each record as an isolated file.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b114-v14-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"時鐘不同步會顛倒事件順序而誤導根因分析。設備改名卻未更新控制畫面會引導人員隔離錯誤回路，材料批次缺漏則使同批缺陷無法追蹤到其他位置。","textEn":"Unsynchronised clocks reverse apparent event order and mislead root-cause analysis. Renaming an asset without updating the screen can isolate the wrong circuit; missing material batches prevent tracing related defects at other locations.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]},{"id":"b114-v14-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「資產編碼與可追溯交接」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Asset identity and traceable handover\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","時鐘不同步會顛倒事件順序而誤導根因分析。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Unsynchronised clocks reverse apparent event order and mislead root-cause analysis.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":1,"explanation":"時鐘不同步會顛倒事件順序而誤導根因分析。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Unsynchronised clocks reverse apparent event order and mislead root-cause analysis. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b114","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b114-history"],"curriculumVersion":14,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000},{"id":"b115","title":"弗雷瑞斯公路隧道","titleEn":"Frejus Road Tunnel","category":"underground","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"法國交通主管機關列弗雷瑞斯原隧道12.87公里、1980年營運，並於2025年公告第二孔開通活動。本課不把原始單孔狀態當成永久現況，而以新舊孔轉換為主軸，研究重車交通、岩體、通風隔離、跨孔救援與設備版本，建立分階段可驗證的營運模型。","summaryEn":"The French transport ministry records the original Frejus tunnel as 12.87 km, in service from 1980, and announced the second-tube opening event in 2025. The course does not treat the original single-bore arrangement as permanent. It studies staged transfer, freight traffic, rock behaviour, airflow isolation, cross-bore rescue and equipment revisions.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"ug-landmarks","subcategoryTitle":"世界隧道與地下巨作","subcategoryTitleEn":"World tunnels and underground landmarks","learningTrack":"underground","learningSubdiscipline":"ug-landmarks","learningTags":["underground","ug-landmarks","tunnel"],"architectureFamily":"tunnel","architectureNodes":[["路線里程與端點","Alignment chainage and endpoints"],["破碎帶連通性","Fault-zone connectivity"],["支護安裝時點","Support activation time"],["風道摩擦壓損","Duct friction loss"],["所需疏散時間","Required evacuation time"],["資產資料完整度","Asset-record completeness"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,5],[1,5]],"diagram":{"type":"tunnel","labels":["路線里程與端點","破碎帶連通性","支護安裝時點","風道摩擦壓損","所需疏散時間"],"labelsEn":["Alignment chainage and endpoints","Fault-zone connectivity","Support activation time","Duct friction loss","Required evacuation time"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"原創綜合審查：先計算「破碎帶連通與預報更新」，再獨立計算「通風網路與壓力損失」。原創教學假設：滲透係數=5e-06 m/s；水力坡降=2.1 無因次；通水面積=340 m²。Q=k i A=0.00357 m³/s。僅把滲透係數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.003927 m³/s。邊界：均質飽和達西流，不代表裂隙集中流；不是本工程實測或允收值。原創教學假設：達西因子=0.025 無因次；風道長度=1060 m；水力直徑=4 m；空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；平均風速=3.5 m/s。Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=48.6937 Pa。僅把平均風速增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為58.9194 Pa。邊界：定密度直管摩阻，局部損失及外風另計；不是本工程實測或允收值。兩組結果的單位與邊界不同，不能直接相加。請列出一項缺少的現場輸入，說明它會影響哪個結論，以及哪種獨立量測可以縮小不確定度。","textEn":"Original integrated review: first calculate fault connectivity and forecast updating, then independently calculate ventilation network and pressure loss. Original teaching assumptions: conductivity=5e-06 m/s; hydraulic gradient=2.1 dimensionless; flow area=340 m². Q=k i A=0.00357 m³/s. Increasing only conductivity by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.003927 m³/s. Boundary: Homogeneous saturated Darcy flow, not concentrated fracture flow. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.025 dimensionless; duct length=1060 m; hydraulic diameter=4 m; air density=1.2 kg/m³; mean velocity=3.5 m/s. Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=48.6937 Pa. Increasing only mean velocity by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 58.9194 Pa. Boundary: Constant-density straight-duct friction; local loss and external wind are separate. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. The outputs have different units and boundaries and cannot simply be added. Identify one missing field input, explain which conclusion it changes and select an independent measurement to reduce uncertainty.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":14,"enrichmentVersion":14,"stages":[{"id":"b115-v14-s1","title":"地層條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Ground conditions, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「服務邊界與路線代價」與「破碎帶連通與預報更新」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\" and \"Fault connectivity and forecast updating\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b115-v14-01","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「路線里程與端點」如何影響弗雷瑞斯公路隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Alignment chainage and endpoints” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Frejus Road Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"弗雷瑞斯由原孔到第二孔的配置變化需先定義階段，教材把道路容量、救援通道和施工空間分開。隧道選線同時改變洞口、覆土與縱坡，短路線不保證低地質風險。比較方案必須使用相同起訖點，並分開主孔、引道及服務坑的工程數量；交通時間只是需求的一個指標，不能代替施工可達性或長期維修評估。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「路線里程與端點」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Define configuration stages before comparing the original and second tubes, separating road capacity, rescue access and construction space. Alignment changes portals, cover and gradient together, so a shorter tunnel need not have lower geological risk. Compare options between identical endpoints and distinguish running bores, approaches and service galleries. Travel time measures one service benefit but cannot replace assessment of construction access, maintenance closures or exposure to uncertain ground. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Alignment chainage and endpoints” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：長度=17.6 km；速度=60 km/h。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: length=17.6 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=17.6 min.","failure":"常見誤解：「最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「路線里程與端點」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Alignment chainage and endpoints”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-01-k1","title":"服務邊界與路線代價","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost","text":"弗雷瑞斯由原孔到第二孔的配置變化需先定義階段，教材把道路容量、救援通道和施工空間分開。隧道選線同時改變洞口、覆土與縱坡，短路線不保證低地質風險。","textEn":"Define configuration stages before comparing the original and second tubes, separating road capacity, rescue access and construction space. Alignment changes portals, cover and gradient together, so a shorter tunnel need not have lower geological risk.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「服務邊界與路線代價」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\" is correct?","options":["最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。","弗雷瑞斯由原孔到第二孔的配置變化需先定義階段，教材把道路容量、救援通道和施工空間分開。","岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。"],"optionsEn":["The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.","Define configuration stages before comparing the original and second tubes, separating road capacity, rescue access and construction space.","Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow."],"answer":1,"explanation":"弗雷瑞斯由原孔到第二孔的配置變化需先定義階段，教材把道路容量、救援通道和施工空間分開。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Define configuration stages before comparing the original and second tubes, separating road capacity, rescue access and construction space. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b115-v14-02","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：定量估算","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「路線里程與端點」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Alignment chainage and endpoints” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：長度=17.6 km；速度=60 km/h。t=60L/v=17.6 min。僅把長度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為19.36 min。邊界：假想交通旅程，未含加減速、排隊及實際時刻表；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: length=17.6 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=17.6 min. Increasing only length by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 19.36 min. Boundary: Hypothetical transport journey excluding acceleration, queues and the real timetable. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：每個方案附日期和孔別，不混用不同時期示意圖。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Attach dates and bore identifiers to each option and avoid mixing historical diagrams.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：長度=17.6 km；速度=60 km/h。t=60L/v=17.6 min。僅把長度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為19.36 min。邊界：假想交通旅程，未含加減速、排隊及實際時刻表；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: length=17.6 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=17.6 min. Increasing only length by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 19.36 min. Boundary: Hypothetical transport journey excluding acceleration, queues and the real timetable. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「服務邊界與路線代價」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\", which statement holds?","options":["支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。","風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。","原創教學假設：長度=17.6 km；速度=60 km/h。"],"optionsEn":["Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem.","Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.","Original teaching assumptions: length=17.6 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=17.6 min."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：長度=17.6 km；速度=60 km/h。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: length=17.6 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=17.6 min. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b115-v14-03","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「路線里程與端點」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Alignment chainage and endpoints” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"每個方案附日期和孔別，不混用不同時期示意圖。把縱斷面、地形與地質剖面疊合，以端點坐標獨立反算距離，再將主孔與支坑數量分開核對。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Attach dates and bore identifiers to each option and avoid mixing historical diagrams. Overlay the longitudinal profile, terrain and geology; independently derive distances from endpoint coordinates and reconcile running-bore and gallery quantities separately. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「路線里程與端點」的交付需回答：每個方案附日期和孔別，不混用不同時期示意圖。在方案表中凍結起訖點、計量範圍及地質假設，任何改線都要同步更新高程、數量與服務情境，不能只替換總長。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Frejus Road Tunnel, the alignment chainage and endpoints handover must address the following evidence: Attach dates and bore identifiers to each option and avoid mixing historical diagrams. Freeze endpoints, measurement scope and ground assumptions in the option register; realignment requires coordinated updates to elevations, quantities and service scenarios rather than replacing one length.","failure":"注意干擾：把舊單孔描述用於新配置會錯估對向衝突及逃生路線。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Applying an old single-bore description misstates opposing traffic and escape routes. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"每個方案附日期和孔別，不混用不同時期示意圖。把縱斷面、地形與地質剖面疊合，以端點坐標獨立反算距離，再將主孔與支坑數量分開核對。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Attach dates and bore identifiers to each option and avoid mixing historical diagrams. Overlay the longitudinal profile, terrain and geology; independently derive distances from endpoint coordinates and reconcile running-bore and gallery quantities separately. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「路線里程與端點」的交付需回答：每個方案附日期和孔別，不混用不同時期示意圖。在方案表中凍結起訖點、計量範圍及地質假設，任何改線都要同步更新高程、數量與服務情境，不能只替換總長。","textEn":"For Frejus Road Tunnel, the alignment chainage and endpoints handover must address the following evidence: Attach dates and bore identifiers to each option and avoid mixing historical diagrams. Freeze endpoints, measurement scope and ground assumptions in the option register; realignment requires coordinated updates to elevations, quantities and service scenarios rather than replacing one length.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「服務邊界與路線代價」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\"?","options":["每個方案附日期和孔別，不混用不同時期示意圖。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。"],"optionsEn":["Attach dates and bore identifiers to each option and avoid mixing historical diagrams.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time."],"answer":0,"explanation":"每個方案附日期和孔別，不混用不同時期示意圖。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Attach dates and bore identifiers to each option and avoid mixing historical diagrams. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b115-v14-04","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：失效診斷","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「路線里程與端點」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Alignment chainage and endpoints” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把舊單孔描述用於新配置會錯估對向衝突及逃生路線。混用全線與單孔長度會同時扭曲工程數量、行程及逃生距離，造成方案比較失去共同基準。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Applying an old single-bore description misstates opposing traffic and escape routes. Mixing whole-route and single-bore lengths distorts quantities, journey time and escape distance, destroying the common basis of an option comparison. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：比較方案必須使用相同起訖點，並分開主孔、引道及服務坑的工程數量；交通時間只是需求的一個指標，不能代替施工可達性或長期維修評估。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Travel time measures one service benefit but cannot replace assessment of construction access, maintenance closures or exposure to uncertain ground.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把舊單孔描述用於新配置會錯估對向衝突及逃生路線。混用全線與單孔長度會同時扭曲工程數量、行程及逃生距離，造成方案比較失去共同基準。","textEn":"Applying an old single-bore description misstates opposing traffic and escape routes. Mixing whole-route and single-bore lengths distorts quantities, journey time and escape distance, destroying the common basis of an option comparison.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「服務邊界與路線代價」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","把舊單孔描述用於新配置會錯估對向衝突及逃生路線。","岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Applying an old single-bore description misstates opposing traffic and escape routes.","Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把舊單孔描述用於新配置會錯估對向衝突及逃生路線。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Applying an old single-bore description misstates opposing traffic and escape routes. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b115-v14-05","title":"破碎帶連通與預報更新：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Fault connectivity and forecast updating: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-04"],"objective":"說明「破碎帶連通性」如何影響弗雷瑞斯公路隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Fault-zone connectivity” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Frejus Road Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"平行第二孔可利用原孔資料但不能省略新探查，弗雷瑞斯教材研究斜交節理在兩孔位置的差異。斷層帶可以含很硬的岩塊，但整體變形與湧水常由填充節理和連通裂隙控制。單一岩芯強度不能代表整個掌子面；超前鑽孔、出水變化與揭露地質須回饋同一里程模型，預報則應保留不同情境及其證據權重。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「破碎帶連通性」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The second tube can use first-bore records without replacing new investigation; examine oblique joints crossing each bore at different positions. A fault zone may contain strong intact blocks while filled joints and connected fractures govern its bulk deformation and inflow. One core strength does not represent the entire face. Probe records, water response and exposed geology must update a common chainage model, preserving competing interpretations and their evidential weight rather than treating a forecast as certainty. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Fault-zone connectivity” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：滲透係數=5e-06 m/s；水力坡降=2.1 無因次；通水面積=340 m²。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: conductivity=5e-06 m/s; hydraulic gradient=2.1 dimensionless; flow area=340 m².","failure":"常見誤解：「岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「破碎帶連通性」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Fault-zone connectivity”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-05-k1","title":"破碎帶連通與預報更新","titleEn":"Fault connectivity and forecast updating","text":"平行第二孔可利用原孔資料但不能省略新探查，弗雷瑞斯教材研究斜交節理在兩孔位置的差異。斷層帶可以含很硬的岩塊，但整體變形與湧水常由填充節理和連通裂隙控制。","textEn":"The second tube can use first-bore records without replacing new investigation; examine oblique joints crossing each bore at different positions. A fault zone may contain strong intact blocks while filled joints and connected fractures govern its bulk deformation and inflow.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「破碎帶連通與預報更新」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Fault connectivity and forecast updating\" is correct?","options":["岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。","知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。","平行第二孔可利用原孔資料但不能省略新探查，弗雷瑞斯教材研究斜交節理在兩孔位置的差異。"],"optionsEn":["Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow.","Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction.","The second tube can use first-bore records without replacing new investigation; examine oblique joints crossing each bore at different positions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"平行第二孔可利用原孔資料但不能省略新探查，弗雷瑞斯教材研究斜交節理在兩孔位置的差異。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The second tube can use first-bore records without replacing new investigation; examine oblique joints crossing each bore at different positions. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b115-v14-06","title":"破碎帶連通與預報更新：定量估算","titleEn":"Fault connectivity and forecast updating: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「破碎帶連通性」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Fault-zone connectivity” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：滲透係數=5e-06 m/s；水力坡降=2.1 無因次；通水面積=340 m²。Q=k i A=0.00357 m³/s。僅把滲透係數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.003927 m³/s。邊界：均質飽和達西流，不代表裂隙集中流；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: conductivity=5e-06 m/s; hydraulic gradient=2.1 dimensionless; flow area=340 m². Q=k i A=0.00357 m³/s. Increasing only conductivity by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.003927 m³/s. Boundary: Homogeneous saturated Darcy flow, not concentrated fracture flow. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將構造方位投影到兩孔里程，再用新揭露驗證。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Project structural orientation onto both chainages and test against new exposures.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：滲透係數=5e-06 m/s；水力坡降=2.1 無因次；通水面積=340 m²。Q=k i A=0.00357 m³/s。僅把滲透係數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.003927 m³/s。邊界：均質飽和達西流，不代表裂隙集中流；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: conductivity=5e-06 m/s; hydraulic gradient=2.1 dimensionless; flow area=340 m². Q=k i A=0.00357 m³/s. Increasing only conductivity by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.003927 m³/s. Boundary: Homogeneous saturated Darcy flow, not concentrated fracture flow. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「破碎帶連通與預報更新」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Fault connectivity and forecast updating\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：滲透係數=5e-06 m/s；水力坡降=2.1 無因次；通水面積=340 m²。","混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。","照度越高就必然使隧道內所有物體更容易辨識。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: conductivity=5e-06 m/s; hydraulic gradient=2.1 dimensionless; flow area=340 m².","Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure.","Higher illuminance necessarily makes every tunnel object easier to detect."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：滲透係數=5e-06 m/s；水力坡降=2.1 無因次；通水面積=340 m²。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: conductivity=5e-06 m/s; hydraulic gradient=2.1 dimensionless; flow area=340 m². Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b115-v14-07","title":"破碎帶連通與預報更新：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Fault connectivity and forecast updating: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「破碎帶連通性」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Fault-zone connectivity” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將構造方位投影到兩孔里程，再用新揭露驗證。將岩心回收、裂隙方位與出水曲線按里程對齊，用未參與建模的孔段作交叉檢驗，檢查是否只擬合已知資料。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Project structural orientation onto both chainages and test against new exposures. Align recovery, fracture orientation and inflow by chainage; test the interpretation against a withheld borehole interval to detect fitting only the known observations. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「破碎帶連通性」的交付需回答：將構造方位投影到兩孔里程，再用新揭露驗證。每次地質模型更新保留舊版與新增證據，差異由地質及支護設計者共同判讀，施工條件改變需重新確認核准範圍。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Frejus Road Tunnel, the fault-zone connectivity handover must address the following evidence: Project structural orientation onto both chainages and test against new exposures. Retain previous interpretations and new evidence at every update; geology and support designers jointly interpret differences and reconfirm approved bounds when ground conditions change.","failure":"注意干擾：按相同里程直接配對地質會忽略斜交造成的位置差。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Matching geology at equal chainage ignores offsets caused by oblique structures. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將構造方位投影到兩孔里程，再用新揭露驗證。將岩心回收、裂隙方位與出水曲線按里程對齊，用未參與建模的孔段作交叉檢驗，檢查是否只擬合已知資料。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Project structural orientation onto both chainages and test against new exposures. Align recovery, fracture orientation and inflow by chainage; test the interpretation against a withheld borehole interval to detect fitting only the known observations. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「破碎帶連通性」的交付需回答：將構造方位投影到兩孔里程，再用新揭露驗證。每次地質模型更新保留舊版與新增證據，差異由地質及支護設計者共同判讀，施工條件改變需重新確認核准範圍。","textEn":"For Frejus Road Tunnel, the fault-zone connectivity handover must address the following evidence: Project structural orientation onto both chainages and test against new exposures. Retain previous interpretations and new evidence at every update; geology and support designers jointly interpret differences and reconfirm approved bounds when ground conditions change.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「破碎帶連通與預報更新」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Fault connectivity and forecast updating\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","將構造方位投影到兩孔里程，再用新揭露驗證。","設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Project structural orientation onto both chainages and test against new exposures.","Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety."],"answer":1,"explanation":"將構造方位投影到兩孔里程，再用新揭露驗證。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Project structural orientation onto both chainages and test against new exposures. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b115-v14-08","title":"破碎帶連通與預報更新：失效診斷","titleEn":"Fault connectivity and forecast updating: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「破碎帶連通性」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Fault-zone connectivity” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"按相同里程直接配對地質會忽略斜交造成的位置差。只用完整岩石強度會漏掉軟弱填充物，可能在看似堅硬的地層中出現收斂加快、支護過載或水量突增。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Matching geology at equal chainage ignores offsets caused by oblique structures. Intact strength alone misses weak infill, allowing accelerating convergence, support overload or sudden inflow in ground that superficially appears strong. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：單一岩芯強度不能代表整個掌子面；超前鑽孔、出水變化與揭露地質須回饋同一里程模型，預報則應保留不同情境及其證據權重。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Probe records, water response and exposed geology must update a common chainage model, preserving competing interpretations and their evidential weight rather than treating a forecast as certainty.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"按相同里程直接配對地質會忽略斜交造成的位置差。只用完整岩石強度會漏掉軟弱填充物，可能在看似堅硬的地層中出現收斂加快、支護過載或水量突增。","textEn":"Matching geology at equal chainage ignores offsets caused by oblique structures. Intact strength alone misses weak infill, allowing accelerating convergence, support overload or sudden inflow in ground that superficially appears strong.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「破碎帶連通與預報更新」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Fault connectivity and forecast updating\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。","按相同里程直接配對地質會忽略斜交造成的位置差。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction.","Matching geology at equal chainage ignores offsets caused by oblique structures."],"answer":2,"explanation":"按相同里程直接配對地質會忽略斜交造成的位置差。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Matching geology at equal chainage ignores offsets caused by oblique structures. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b115-v14-s2","title":"機制、材料與定量設計","titleEn":"Mechanisms, materials and quantitative design","description":"本階段聚焦「覆土應力與洞壁重分配」與「支護啟動與變形容量」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Cover stress and wall redistribution\" and \"Support activation and deformation capacity\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b115-v14-09","title":"覆土應力與洞壁重分配：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Cover stress and wall redistribution: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-08"],"objective":"說明「洞壁切向應力」如何影響弗雷瑞斯公路隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Tangential wall stress” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Frejus Road Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"第二孔開挖與原孔營運並存時需檢查岩柱應力重分配，單孔覆土估算只是起點。開挖使岩體洞壁失去徑向拘束，遠場荷載轉移到周圍岩體，局部切向應力可能升高。圓孔彈性解可辨識量級，但節理、非圓斷面、塑性區與原位應力比會改變峰值位置，不能只用覆土重量推定全部三維應力。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「洞壁切向應力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"When excavation coexists with first-bore operation, examine pillar stress redistribution beyond a single-hole cover estimate. Excavation removes radial confinement at the wall and transfers load through the surrounding rock, potentially raising local tangential stress. An elastic circular-hole solution identifies scale, but joints, noncircular geometry, yielding and the in-situ stress ratio alter the peak location. Cover weight alone cannot establish the complete three-dimensional stress state or support demand. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Tangential wall stress” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：覆土深度=920 m；岩體單位重=26 kN/m³。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: cover=920 m; rock unit weight=26 kN/m³. σθ,max=3γH/1000=71.76 MPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「洞壁切向應力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Tangential wall stress”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-09-k1","title":"覆土應力與洞壁重分配","titleEn":"Cover stress and wall redistribution","text":"第二孔開挖與原孔營運並存時需檢查岩柱應力重分配，單孔覆土估算只是起點。開挖使岩體洞壁失去徑向拘束，遠場荷載轉移到周圍岩體，局部切向應力可能升高。","textEn":"When excavation coexists with first-bore operation, examine pillar stress redistribution beyond a single-hole cover estimate. Excavation removes radial confinement at the wall and transfers load through the surrounding rock, potentially raising local tangential stress.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「覆土應力與洞壁重分配」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Cover stress and wall redistribution\" is correct?","options":["第二孔開挖與原孔營運並存時需檢查岩柱應力重分配，單孔覆土估算只是起點。","知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。","支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。"],"optionsEn":["When excavation coexists with first-bore operation, examine pillar stress redistribution beyond a single-hole cover estimate.","Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction.","Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem."],"answer":0,"explanation":"第二孔開挖與原孔營運並存時需檢查岩柱應力重分配，單孔覆土估算只是起點。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"When excavation coexists with first-bore operation, examine pillar stress redistribution beyond a single-hole cover estimate. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b115-v14-10","title":"覆土應力與洞壁重分配：定量估算","titleEn":"Cover stress and wall redistribution: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「洞壁切向應力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Tangential wall stress” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：覆土深度=920 m；岩體單位重=26 kN/m³。σθ,max=3γH/1000=71.76 MPa。僅把覆土深度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為78.936 MPa。邊界：無支承彈性圓孔，僅垂直遠場壓縮且水平遠場應力為零時，側壁最大環向壓應力；不是任意位置應力或完整三維原位解；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: cover=920 m; rock unit weight=26 kN/m³. σθ,max=3γH/1000=71.76 MPa. Increasing only cover by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 78.936 MPa. Boundary: Maximum tangential compression at the sidewalls of an unsupported elastic circular hole under vertical uniaxial remote loading with zero horizontal remote stress; not stress at any point or the complete three-dimensional in-situ state. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：把原孔位移與新掌子面距離對齊，排除溫度漂移。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Align old-bore movement with new-face distance while excluding thermal drift.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：覆土深度=920 m；岩體單位重=26 kN/m³。σθ,max=3γH/1000=71.76 MPa。僅把覆土深度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為78.936 MPa。邊界：無支承彈性圓孔，僅垂直遠場壓縮且水平遠場應力為零時，側壁最大環向壓應力；不是任意位置應力或完整三維原位解；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: cover=920 m; rock unit weight=26 kN/m³. σθ,max=3γH/1000=71.76 MPa. Increasing only cover by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 78.936 MPa. Boundary: Maximum tangential compression at the sidewalls of an unsupported elastic circular hole under vertical uniaxial remote loading with zero horizontal remote stress; not stress at any point or the complete three-dimensional in-situ state. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「覆土應力與洞壁重分配」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Cover stress and wall redistribution\", which statement holds?","options":["風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。","原創教學假設：覆土深度=920 m；岩體單位重=26 kN/m³。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。"],"optionsEn":["Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.","Original teaching assumptions: cover=920 m; rock unit weight=26 kN/m³. σθ,max=3γH/1000=71.76 MPa.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：覆土深度=920 m；岩體單位重=26 kN/m³。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: cover=920 m; rock unit weight=26 kN/m³. σθ,max=3γH/1000=71.76 MPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b115-v14-11","title":"覆土應力與洞壁重分配：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Cover stress and wall redistribution: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「洞壁切向應力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Tangential wall stress” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"把原孔位移與新掌子面距離對齊，排除溫度漂移。將原位應力量測、岩石試驗及洞壁破壞方位相互比較，再用多點伸長計檢查變形是否與所假設應力方向一致。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Align old-bore movement with new-face distance while excluding thermal drift. Compare in-situ stress measurements, rock tests and wall-damage orientation, then use multipoint extensometers to test consistency with the assumed stress directions. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「洞壁切向應力」的交付需回答：把原孔位移與新掌子面距離對齊，排除溫度漂移。保留應力模型的座標、邊界和材料假設，量測與預測不符時先核對代表性，再由岩力設計者選擇非線性或節理模型。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Frejus Road Tunnel, the tangential wall stress handover must address the following evidence: Align old-bore movement with new-face distance while excluding thermal drift. Record stress-model coordinates, boundaries and material assumptions; when observations disagree, check representativeness before the rock designer selects nonlinear or jointed models.","failure":"注意干擾：未扣溫度的位移可能被誤判成新孔造成的地盤作用。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Uncorrected thermal movement can be misattributed to excavation interaction. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"把原孔位移與新掌子面距離對齊，排除溫度漂移。將原位應力量測、岩石試驗及洞壁破壞方位相互比較，再用多點伸長計檢查變形是否與所假設應力方向一致。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Align old-bore movement with new-face distance while excluding thermal drift. Compare in-situ stress measurements, rock tests and wall-damage orientation, then use multipoint extensometers to test consistency with the assumed stress directions. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「洞壁切向應力」的交付需回答：把原孔位移與新掌子面距離對齊，排除溫度漂移。保留應力模型的座標、邊界和材料假設，量測與預測不符時先核對代表性，再由岩力設計者選擇非線性或節理模型。","textEn":"For Frejus Road Tunnel, the tangential wall stress handover must address the following evidence: Align old-bore movement with new-face distance while excluding thermal drift. Record stress-model coordinates, boundaries and material assumptions; when observations disagree, check representativeness before the rock designer selects nonlinear or jointed models.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「覆土應力與洞壁重分配」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Cover stress and wall redistribution\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。","把原孔位移與新掌子面距離對齊，排除溫度漂移。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.","Align old-bore movement with new-face distance while excluding thermal drift."],"answer":2,"explanation":"把原孔位移與新掌子面距離對齊，排除溫度漂移。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Align old-bore movement with new-face distance while excluding thermal drift. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b115-v14-12","title":"覆土應力與洞壁重分配：失效診斷","titleEn":"Cover stress and wall redistribution: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「洞壁切向應力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Tangential wall stress” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"未扣溫度的位移可能被誤判成新孔造成的地盤作用。把彈性峰值直接當岩體強度可能誤判支護需求；相反地忽略剝落或擠壓也會讓局部破壞逐步侵入淨空。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Uncorrected thermal movement can be misattributed to excavation interaction. Equating an elastic peak with rock-mass strength misjudges support demand; overlooking spalling or squeezing lets damage progressively consume clearance. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：圓孔彈性解可辨識量級，但節理、非圓斷面、塑性區與原位應力比會改變峰值位置，不能只用覆土重量推定全部三維應力。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Cover weight alone cannot establish the complete three-dimensional stress state or support demand.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"未扣溫度的位移可能被誤判成新孔造成的地盤作用。把彈性峰值直接當岩體強度可能誤判支護需求；相反地忽略剝落或擠壓也會讓局部破壞逐步侵入淨空。","textEn":"Uncorrected thermal movement can be misattributed to excavation interaction. Equating an elastic peak with rock-mass strength misjudges support demand; overlooking spalling or squeezing lets damage progressively consume clearance.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「覆土應力與洞壁重分配」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Cover stress and wall redistribution\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["未扣溫度的位移可能被誤判成新孔造成的地盤作用。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。"],"optionsEn":["Uncorrected thermal movement can be misattributed to excavation interaction.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem."],"answer":0,"explanation":"未扣溫度的位移可能被誤判成新孔造成的地盤作用。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Uncorrected thermal movement can be misattributed to excavation interaction. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b115-v14-13","title":"支護啟動與變形容量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Support activation and deformation capacity: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-12"],"objective":"說明「支護安裝時點」如何影響弗雷瑞斯公路隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Support activation time” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Frejus Road Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"弗雷瑞斯新舊支護設計背景不同，教材比較荷載啟動時點及長期劣化，不只比較材料強度。支護荷載由開挖釋放量和支護啟動時間共同決定，越早安裝不一定讓構件受力越小。地盤反力與支護曲線必須連同掌子面距離及封閉順序理解；擠壓性地層還需保留變形容量，不能只追求高剛度與高材料強度。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「支護安裝時點」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"New and old support have different histories; compare activation time and ageing rather than material strength alone. Support load depends on stress release and activation time, so earlier installation does not necessarily reduce member forces. Interpret ground-reaction and support curves together with distance from the face and closure sequence. Squeezing ground also needs deformation capacity; high stiffness and material strength alone do not guarantee a compatible support response. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Support activation time” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：局部剛度=44 kN/mm；位移=8 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: local stiffness=44 kN/mm; movement=8 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「支護安裝時點」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Support activation time”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-13-k1","title":"支護啟動與變形容量","titleEn":"Support activation and deformation capacity","text":"弗雷瑞斯新舊支護設計背景不同，教材比較荷載啟動時點及長期劣化，不只比較材料強度。支護荷載由開挖釋放量和支護啟動時間共同決定，越早安裝不一定讓構件受力越小。","textEn":"New and old support have different histories; compare activation time and ageing rather than material strength alone. Support load depends on stress release and activation time, so earlier installation does not necessarily reduce member forces.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「支護啟動與變形容量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Support activation and deformation capacity\" is correct?","options":["支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。","弗雷瑞斯新舊支護設計背景不同，教材比較荷載啟動時點及長期劣化，不只比較材料強度。","混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。"],"optionsEn":["Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem.","New and old support have different histories; compare activation time and ageing rather than material strength alone.","Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure."],"answer":1,"explanation":"弗雷瑞斯新舊支護設計背景不同，教材比較荷載啟動時點及長期劣化，不只比較材料強度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"New and old support have different histories; compare activation time and ageing rather than material strength alone. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b115-v14-14","title":"支護啟動與變形容量：定量估算","titleEn":"Support activation and deformation capacity: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「支護安裝時點」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Support activation time” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：局部剛度=44 kN/mm；位移=8 mm。F=ku=352 kN。僅把位移增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為387.2 kN。邊界：線性局部彈簧，不含屈服或時間效應；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: local stiffness=44 kN/mm; movement=8 mm. F=ku=352 kN. Increasing only movement by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 387.2 kN. Boundary: Local linear spring without yielding or time effects. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：分別建立新支護荷重與舊支護檢查的時間基準。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Maintain separate time references for new support loads and legacy inspections.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：局部剛度=44 kN/mm；位移=8 mm。F=ku=352 kN。僅把位移增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為387.2 kN。邊界：線性局部彈簧，不含屈服或時間效應；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: local stiffness=44 kN/mm; movement=8 mm. F=ku=352 kN. Increasing only movement by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 387.2 kN. Boundary: Local linear spring without yielding or time effects. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「支護啟動與變形容量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Support activation and deformation capacity\", which statement holds?","options":["照度越高就必然使隧道內所有物體更容易辨識。","設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。","原創教學假設：局部剛度=44 kN/mm；位移=8 mm。"],"optionsEn":["Higher illuminance necessarily makes every tunnel object easier to detect.","Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety.","Original teaching assumptions: local stiffness=44 kN/mm; movement=8 mm."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：局部剛度=44 kN/mm；位移=8 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: local stiffness=44 kN/mm; movement=8 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b115-v14-15","title":"支護啟動與變形容量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Support activation and deformation capacity: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「支護安裝時點」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Support activation time” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"分別建立新支護荷重與舊支護檢查的時間基準。同步記錄收斂、支護荷重與安裝里程，比較同一地質分區內的速率及荷載，不將不同開挖齡期讀值直接混合。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Maintain separate time references for new support loads and legacy inspections. Synchronise convergence, support loads and installation chainage; compare rates and loads within one ground domain without mixing readings at different excavation ages. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「支護安裝時點」的交付需回答：分別建立新支護荷重與舊支護檢查的時間基準。把安裝時間和量測資料一起交付支護設計者，任何級別變更都需地質及位移證據，不能憑單一瞬間讀值自行改支護。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Frejus Road Tunnel, the support activation time handover must address the following evidence: Maintain separate time references for new support loads and legacy inspections. Submit installation times with measurements to the support designer; class changes need both ground and movement evidence, not an isolated instantaneous reading.","failure":"注意干擾：新支護較強不能證明舊孔整修可省略施工階段分析。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Stronger new support does not remove staging analysis for old-bore refurbishment. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"分別建立新支護荷重與舊支護檢查的時間基準。同步記錄收斂、支護荷重與安裝里程，比較同一地質分區內的速率及荷載，不將不同開挖齡期讀值直接混合。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Maintain separate time references for new support loads and legacy inspections. Synchronise convergence, support loads and installation chainage; compare rates and loads within one ground domain without mixing readings at different excavation ages. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「支護安裝時點」的交付需回答：分別建立新支護荷重與舊支護檢查的時間基準。把安裝時間和量測資料一起交付支護設計者，任何級別變更都需地質及位移證據，不能憑單一瞬間讀值自行改支護。","textEn":"For Frejus Road Tunnel, the support activation time handover must address the following evidence: Maintain separate time references for new support loads and legacy inspections. Submit installation times with measurements to the support designer; class changes need both ground and movement evidence, not an isolated instantaneous reading.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「支護啟動與變形容量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Support activation and deformation capacity\"?","options":["分別建立新支護荷重與舊支護檢查的時間基準。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Maintain separate time references for new support loads and legacy inspections.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":0,"explanation":"分別建立新支護荷重與舊支護檢查的時間基準。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Maintain separate time references for new support loads and legacy inspections. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b115-v14-16","title":"支護啟動與變形容量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Support activation and deformation capacity: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「支護安裝時點」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Support activation time” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"新支護較強不能證明舊孔整修可省略施工階段分析。過晚封閉會讓不可回復變形增加，過硬且行程不足的支護也可能脆裂，兩者都可能表現為裂縫而需不同處理。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Stronger new support does not remove staging analysis for old-bore refurbishment. Late closure increases irreversible movement, while excessively stiff support with little travel can fail brittly; both produce cracks but require different diagnoses. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：地盤反力與支護曲線必須連同掌子面距離及封閉順序理解；擠壓性地層還需保留變形容量，不能只追求高剛度與高材料強度。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Squeezing ground also needs deformation capacity; high stiffness and material strength alone do not guarantee a compatible support response.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"新支護較強不能證明舊孔整修可省略施工階段分析。過晚封閉會讓不可回復變形增加，過硬且行程不足的支護也可能脆裂，兩者都可能表現為裂縫而需不同處理。","textEn":"Stronger new support does not remove staging analysis for old-bore refurbishment. Late closure increases irreversible movement, while excessively stiff support with little travel can fail brittly; both produce cracks but require different diagnoses.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「支護啟動與變形容量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Support activation and deformation capacity\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","新支護較強不能證明舊孔整修可省略施工階段分析。","混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Stronger new support does not remove staging analysis for old-bore refurbishment.","Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure."],"answer":1,"explanation":"新支護較強不能證明舊孔整修可省略施工階段分析。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Stronger new support does not remove staging analysis for old-bore refurbishment. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b115-v14-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「環向受力與接縫柔度」與「通風網路與壓力損失」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Ring force and joint flexibility\" and \"Ventilation network and pressure loss\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b115-v14-17","title":"環向受力與接縫柔度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Ring force and joint flexibility: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-16"],"objective":"說明「襯砌環向壓縮」如何影響弗雷瑞斯公路隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Lining hoop compression” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Frejus Road Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"重車公路的襯砌和設備支承有不同作用，教材用均勻外壓示例後再辨識附掛設備局部荷載。圓形襯砌對均勻外壓可主要以環向壓縮抵抗，但接頭轉動、偏壓與背填空隙會引起彎矩。薄環膜應力只說明其中一條受力路徑；脫模、運輸、頂推及永久狀態的荷載不同，環片局部接觸與止水條件必須另外檢核。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「襯砌環向壓縮」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Lining and equipment supports carry different actions; follow a uniform-pressure example with identification of local suspended loads. A circular lining resists uniform external pressure largely through hoop compression, but joint rotation, uneven load and backfill voids generate bending. Thin-ring membrane stress describes only one load path. Demoulding, transport, jacking and permanent states impose different actions, requiring separate checks of local segment contact and sealing rather than one permanent-load calculation. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Lining hoop compression” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：均勻外壓=0.58 MPa；半徑=3.4 m；厚度=0.35 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: uniform external pressure=0.58 MPa; radius=3.4 m; thickness=0.35 m. σθ=pr/t=5.63429 MPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「襯砌環向壓縮」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Lining hoop compression”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-17-k1","title":"環向受力與接縫柔度","titleEn":"Ring force and joint flexibility","text":"重車公路的襯砌和設備支承有不同作用，教材用均勻外壓示例後再辨識附掛設備局部荷載。圓形襯砌對均勻外壓可主要以環向壓縮抵抗，但接頭轉動、偏壓與背填空隙會引起彎矩。","textEn":"Lining and equipment supports carry different actions; follow a uniform-pressure example with identification of local suspended loads. A circular lining resists uniform external pressure largely through hoop compression, but joint rotation, uneven load and backfill voids generate bending.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「環向受力與接縫柔度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Ring force and joint flexibility\" is correct?","options":["混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。","風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。","重車公路的襯砌和設備支承有不同作用，教材用均勻外壓示例後再辨識附掛設備局部荷載。"],"optionsEn":["Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure.","Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.","Lining and equipment supports carry different actions; follow a uniform-pressure example with identification of local suspended loads."],"answer":2,"explanation":"重車公路的襯砌和設備支承有不同作用，教材用均勻外壓示例後再辨識附掛設備局部荷載。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Lining and equipment supports carry different actions; follow a uniform-pressure example with identification of local suspended loads. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b115-v14-18","title":"環向受力與接縫柔度：定量估算","titleEn":"Ring force and joint flexibility: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「襯砌環向壓縮」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Lining hoop compression” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：均勻外壓=0.58 MPa；半徑=3.4 m；厚度=0.35 m。σθ=pr/t=5.63429 MPa。僅把均勻外壓增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為6.19771 MPa。邊界：薄圓環膜應力，不是接縫、偏壓或矩形框架解；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: uniform external pressure=0.58 MPa; radius=3.4 m; thickness=0.35 m. σθ=pr/t=5.63429 MPa. Increasing only uniform external pressure by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 6.19771 MPa. Boundary: Thin circular-ring membrane stress, not a joint, uneven-load or rectangular-frame solution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對設備錨固位置、裂縫圖及襯砌實際厚度。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check equipment anchorage, crack maps and actual lining thickness.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：均勻外壓=0.58 MPa；半徑=3.4 m；厚度=0.35 m。σθ=pr/t=5.63429 MPa。僅把均勻外壓增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為6.19771 MPa。邊界：薄圓環膜應力，不是接縫、偏壓或矩形框架解；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: uniform external pressure=0.58 MPa; radius=3.4 m; thickness=0.35 m. σθ=pr/t=5.63429 MPa. Increasing only uniform external pressure by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 6.19771 MPa. Boundary: Thin circular-ring membrane stress, not a joint, uneven-load or rectangular-frame solution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「環向受力與接縫柔度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Ring force and joint flexibility\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：均勻外壓=0.58 MPa；半徑=3.4 m；厚度=0.35 m。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: uniform external pressure=0.58 MPa; radius=3.4 m; thickness=0.35 m. σθ=pr/t=5.63429 MPa.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：均勻外壓=0.58 MPa；半徑=3.4 m；厚度=0.35 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: uniform external pressure=0.58 MPa; radius=3.4 m; thickness=0.35 m. σθ=pr/t=5.63429 MPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b115-v14-19","title":"環向受力與接縫柔度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Ring force and joint flexibility: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「襯砌環向壓縮」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Lining hoop compression” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對設備錨固位置、裂縫圖及襯砌實際厚度。將環形變形、接縫張開與應變和含接頭彈簧的模型比較，分開安裝後、背填後及水頭回升後的基準。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check equipment anchorage, crack maps and actual lining thickness. Compare ring distortion, joint opening and strain with a joint-spring model, separating baselines after installation, grouting and head recovery. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「襯砌環向壓縮」的交付需回答：核對設備錨固位置、裂縫圖及襯砌實際厚度。設計圖應分開標註各施工階段、接頭剛度及背填條件，構件驗收同時核對幾何、材料批次與止水試驗適用包絡。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Frejus Road Tunnel, the lining hoop compression handover must address the following evidence: Check equipment anchorage, crack maps and actual lining thickness. Drawings distinguish stages, joint stiffness and backfill conditions; component acceptance reconciles geometry, material batches and the applicable sealing-test envelope.","failure":"注意干擾：新增設備未回查襯砌狀態可能把局部負擔集中在弱區。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: New equipment without lining-condition checks can concentrate load in weak zones. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對設備錨固位置、裂縫圖及襯砌實際厚度。將環形變形、接縫張開與應變和含接頭彈簧的模型比較，分開安裝後、背填後及水頭回升後的基準。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Check equipment anchorage, crack maps and actual lining thickness. Compare ring distortion, joint opening and strain with a joint-spring model, separating baselines after installation, grouting and head recovery. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「襯砌環向壓縮」的交付需回答：核對設備錨固位置、裂縫圖及襯砌實際厚度。設計圖應分開標註各施工階段、接頭剛度及背填條件，構件驗收同時核對幾何、材料批次與止水試驗適用包絡。","textEn":"For Frejus Road Tunnel, the lining hoop compression handover must address the following evidence: Check equipment anchorage, crack maps and actual lining thickness. Drawings distinguish stages, joint stiffness and backfill conditions; component acceptance reconciles geometry, material batches and the applicable sealing-test envelope.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「環向受力與接縫柔度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Ring force and joint flexibility\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","核對設備錨固位置、裂縫圖及襯砌實際厚度。","岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Check equipment anchorage, crack maps and actual lining thickness.","Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow."],"answer":1,"explanation":"核對設備錨固位置、裂縫圖及襯砌實際厚度。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check equipment anchorage, crack maps and actual lining thickness. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b115-v14-20","title":"環向受力與接縫柔度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Ring force and joint flexibility: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「襯砌環向壓縮」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Lining hoop compression” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"新增設備未回查襯砌狀態可能把局部負擔集中在弱區。局部脫空增加環片彎曲，裂縫未必代表混凝土平均強度不足；忽略接縫接觸會把補強方向導向錯誤位置。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"New equipment without lining-condition checks can concentrate load in weak zones. Local voids increase bending, so cracks need not indicate inadequate mean concrete strength; neglecting joint contact can misdirect strengthening. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：薄環膜應力只說明其中一條受力路徑；脫模、運輸、頂推及永久狀態的荷載不同，環片局部接觸與止水條件必須另外檢核。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Demoulding, transport, jacking and permanent states impose different actions, requiring separate checks of local segment contact and sealing rather than one permanent-load calculation.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"新增設備未回查襯砌狀態可能把局部負擔集中在弱區。局部脫空增加環片彎曲，裂縫未必代表混凝土平均強度不足；忽略接縫接觸會把補強方向導向錯誤位置。","textEn":"New equipment without lining-condition checks can concentrate load in weak zones. Local voids increase bending, so cracks need not indicate inadequate mean concrete strength; neglecting joint contact can misdirect strengthening.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「環向受力與接縫柔度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Ring force and joint flexibility\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。","新增設備未回查襯砌狀態可能把局部負擔集中在弱區。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.","New equipment without lining-condition checks can concentrate load in weak zones."],"answer":2,"explanation":"新增設備未回查襯砌狀態可能把局部負擔集中在弱區。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"New equipment without lining-condition checks can concentrate load in weak zones. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b115-v14-21","title":"通風網路與壓力損失：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Ventilation network and pressure loss: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-20"],"objective":"說明「風道摩擦壓損」如何影響弗雷瑞斯公路隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Duct friction loss” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Frejus Road Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"分向孔與原雙向情境的車流助風不同，弗雷瑞斯教材要求換孔後重新核對通風邊界。風機提供壓差，實際風量由風道摩阻、局部損失、外風與其他風機共同決定。支路開關會重新分配整個網路，不能把額定風量直接加總；正常污染稀釋與火災控煙也有不同目標，需要分別建立受控邊界和故障情境。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「風道摩擦壓損」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Directional tubes differ from former bidirectional traffic in piston effects; recheck airflow boundaries after configuration changes. Fans supply pressure, but actual flow follows friction, local losses, external wind and interactions with other fans. Switching a branch redistributes the network rather than simply adding rated flows. Routine dilution and fire smoke control have different objectives, so each needs explicit boundaries, operating states and failure cases rather than one universal flow target. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Duct friction loss” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：達西因子=0.025 無因次；風道長度=1060 m；水力直徑=4 m；空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；平均風速=3.5 m/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.025 dimensionless; duct length=1060 m; hydraulic diameter=4 m; air density=1.2 kg/m³; mean velocity=3.5 m/s. Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=48.6937 Pa.","failure":"常見誤解：「風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「風道摩擦壓損」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Duct friction loss”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-21-k1","title":"通風網路與壓力損失","titleEn":"Ventilation network and pressure loss","text":"分向孔與原雙向情境的車流助風不同，弗雷瑞斯教材要求換孔後重新核對通風邊界。風機提供壓差，實際風量由風道摩阻、局部損失、外風與其他風機共同決定。","textEn":"Directional tubes differ from former bidirectional traffic in piston effects; recheck airflow boundaries after configuration changes. Fans supply pressure, but actual flow follows friction, local losses, external wind and interactions with other fans.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「通風網路與壓力損失」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Ventilation network and pressure loss\" is correct?","options":["分向孔與原雙向情境的車流助風不同，弗雷瑞斯教材要求換孔後重新核對通風邊界。","風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。","照度越高就必然使隧道內所有物體更容易辨識。"],"optionsEn":["Directional tubes differ from former bidirectional traffic in piston effects; recheck airflow boundaries after configuration changes.","Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.","Higher illuminance necessarily makes every tunnel object easier to detect."],"answer":0,"explanation":"分向孔與原雙向情境的車流助風不同，弗雷瑞斯教材要求換孔後重新核對通風邊界。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Directional tubes differ from former bidirectional traffic in piston effects; recheck airflow boundaries after configuration changes. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b115-v14-22","title":"通風網路與壓力損失：定量估算","titleEn":"Ventilation network and pressure loss: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「風道摩擦壓損」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Duct friction loss” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：達西因子=0.025 無因次；風道長度=1060 m；水力直徑=4 m；空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；平均風速=3.5 m/s。Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=48.6937 Pa。僅把平均風速增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為58.9194 Pa。邊界：定密度直管摩阻，局部損失及外風另計；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.025 dimensionless; duct length=1060 m; hydraulic diameter=4 m; air density=1.2 kg/m³; mean velocity=3.5 m/s. Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=48.6937 Pa. Increasing only mean velocity by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 58.9194 Pa. Boundary: Constant-density straight-duct friction; local loss and external wind are separate. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：對比切換前後同風機設定的實測壓差和流量。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare measured pressure and flow at equal fan settings before and after transfer.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：達西因子=0.025 無因次；風道長度=1060 m；水力直徑=4 m；空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；平均風速=3.5 m/s。Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=48.6937 Pa。僅把平均風速增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為58.9194 Pa。邊界：定密度直管摩阻，局部損失及外風另計；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.025 dimensionless; duct length=1060 m; hydraulic diameter=4 m; air density=1.2 kg/m³; mean velocity=3.5 m/s. Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=48.6937 Pa. Increasing only mean velocity by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 58.9194 Pa. Boundary: Constant-density straight-duct friction; local loss and external wind are separate. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「通風網路與壓力損失」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Ventilation network and pressure loss\", which statement holds?","options":["設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。","原創教學假設：達西因子=0.025 無因次；風道長度=1060 m；水力直徑=4 m；空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；平均風速=3.5 m/s。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety.","Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.025 dimensionless.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：達西因子=0.025 無因次；風道長度=1060 m；水力直徑=4 m；空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；平均風速=3.5 m/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.025 dimensionless; duct length=1060 m; hydraulic diameter=4 m; air density=1.2 kg/m³; mean velocity=3.5 m/s. Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=48.6937 Pa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b115-v14-23","title":"通風網路與壓力損失：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Ventilation network and pressure loss: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「風道摩擦壓損」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Duct friction loss” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"對比切換前後同風機設定的實測壓差和流量。沿線同步量測靜壓與風速，記錄風門及其他風機狀態，再把實測工作點和風機曲線、網路壓損比較。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare measured pressure and flow at equal fan settings before and after transfer. Measure pressure and velocity synchronously, record dampers and other fans, and compare the measured duty point with fan curves and network resistance. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「風道摩擦壓損」的交付需回答：對比切換前後同風機設定的實測壓差和流量。驗收採明確風門和車流邊界，維修改線後重新核對網路工作點，火災模式由防災責任工程師簽認而非沿用正常模式。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Frejus Road Tunnel, the duct friction loss handover must address the following evidence: Compare measured pressure and flow at equal fan settings before and after transfer. Commission with specified damper and traffic boundaries, recheck duty points after rerouting, and have the fire-safety engineer approve emergency modes independently.","failure":"注意干擾：沿用舊控制參數可能在新車流方向下產生不符預期風向。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Old controls may produce unintended airflow under the new traffic direction. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"對比切換前後同風機設定的實測壓差和流量。沿線同步量測靜壓與風速，記錄風門及其他風機狀態，再把實測工作點和風機曲線、網路壓損比較。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Compare measured pressure and flow at equal fan settings before and after transfer. Measure pressure and velocity synchronously, record dampers and other fans, and compare the measured duty point with fan curves and network resistance. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「風道摩擦壓損」的交付需回答：對比切換前後同風機設定的實測壓差和流量。驗收採明確風門和車流邊界，維修改線後重新核對網路工作點，火災模式由防災責任工程師簽認而非沿用正常模式。","textEn":"For Frejus Road Tunnel, the duct friction loss handover must address the following evidence: Compare measured pressure and flow at equal fan settings before and after transfer. Commission with specified damper and traffic boundaries, recheck duty points after rerouting, and have the fire-safety engineer approve emergency modes independently.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「通風網路與壓力損失」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Ventilation network and pressure loss\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。","對比切換前後同風機設定的實測壓差和流量。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction.","Compare measured pressure and flow at equal fan settings before and after transfer."],"answer":2,"explanation":"對比切換前後同風機設定的實測壓差和流量。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare measured pressure and flow at equal fan settings before and after transfer. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b115-v14-24","title":"通風網路與壓力損失：失效診斷","titleEn":"Ventilation network and pressure loss: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「風道摩擦壓損」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Duct friction loss” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"沿用舊控制參數可能在新車流方向下產生不符預期風向。只看風機轉速會漏掉風門誤位或短路漏風，可能在總耗電增加時，真正需要的區段反而風量不足。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Old controls may produce unintended airflow under the new traffic direction. Fan speed alone misses a misplaced damper or leakage shortcut; total power may rise while the critical section receives less air. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：支路開關會重新分配整個網路，不能把額定風量直接加總；正常污染稀釋與火災控煙也有不同目標，需要分別建立受控邊界和故障情境。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Routine dilution and fire smoke control have different objectives, so each needs explicit boundaries, operating states and failure cases rather than one universal flow target.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"沿用舊控制參數可能在新車流方向下產生不符預期風向。只看風機轉速會漏掉風門誤位或短路漏風，可能在總耗電增加時，真正需要的區段反而風量不足。","textEn":"Old controls may produce unintended airflow under the new traffic direction. Fan speed alone misses a misplaced damper or leakage shortcut; total power may rise while the critical section receives less air.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「通風網路與壓力損失」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Ventilation network and pressure loss\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["沿用舊控制參數可能在新車流方向下產生不符預期風向。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","照度越高就必然使隧道內所有物體更容易辨識。"],"optionsEn":["Old controls may produce unintended airflow under the new traffic direction.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Higher illuminance necessarily makes every tunnel object easier to detect."],"answer":0,"explanation":"沿用舊控制參數可能在新車流方向下產生不符預期風向。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Old controls may produce unintended airflow under the new traffic direction. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b115-v14-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「視覺適應與路面亮度」與「疏散時間與分區可用性」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Visual adaptation and pavement luminance\" and \"Evacuation time and zone availability\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b115-v14-25","title":"視覺適應與路面亮度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Visual adaptation and pavement luminance: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-24"],"objective":"說明「漫反射亮度」如何影響弗雷瑞斯公路隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Diffuse luminance” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Frejus Road Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"新舊孔表面與燈具狀態不同，教學比較相同照度下路面反射造成的亮度差。駕駛從洞外進入洞內時視覺適應需要時間，照度並不等同從駕駛視角看到的亮度。路面反射、濕度、燈具配光及背景對比共同影響辨識；朗伯模型只示範理想漫反射，不能直接制定入口段燈具間距或真實道路安全值。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「漫反射亮度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Different surfaces and luminaires in old and new tubes can produce different luminance at equal illuminance. Driver adaptation takes time when entering a tunnel, and illuminance is not the luminance seen from the driving position. Pavement reflection, wetness, luminaire distribution and background contrast affect detection. A Lambertian model illustrates ideal diffuse reflection only; it cannot establish entrance-zone spacing or actual road-safety limits without photometric and operational assessment. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Diffuse luminance” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：照度=108 lx；反射率=0.26 無因次。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: illuminance=108 lx; reflectance=0.26 dimensionless.","failure":"常見誤解：「照度越高就必然使隧道內所有物體更容易辨識。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Higher illuminance necessarily makes every tunnel object easier to detect.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「漫反射亮度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Diffuse luminance”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-25-k1","title":"視覺適應與路面亮度","titleEn":"Visual adaptation and pavement luminance","text":"新舊孔表面與燈具狀態不同，教學比較相同照度下路面反射造成的亮度差。駕駛從洞外進入洞內時視覺適應需要時間，照度並不等同從駕駛視角看到的亮度。","textEn":"Different surfaces and luminaires in old and new tubes can produce different luminance at equal illuminance. Driver adaptation takes time when entering a tunnel, and illuminance is not the luminance seen from the driving position.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：照度越高就必然使隧道內所有物體更容易辨識。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Higher illuminance necessarily makes every tunnel object easier to detect. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「視覺適應與路面亮度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Visual adaptation and pavement luminance\" is correct?","options":["照度越高就必然使隧道內所有物體更容易辨識。","新舊孔表面與燈具狀態不同，教學比較相同照度下路面反射造成的亮度差。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。"],"optionsEn":["Higher illuminance necessarily makes every tunnel object easier to detect.","Different surfaces and luminaires in old and new tubes can produce different luminance at equal illuminance.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time."],"answer":1,"explanation":"新舊孔表面與燈具狀態不同，教學比較相同照度下路面反射造成的亮度差。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Different surfaces and luminaires in old and new tubes can produce different luminance at equal illuminance. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b115-v14-26","title":"視覺適應與路面亮度：定量估算","titleEn":"Visual adaptation and pavement luminance: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「漫反射亮度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Diffuse luminance” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：照度=108 lx；反射率=0.26 無因次。L=ρE/π=8.93814 cd/m²。僅把照度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為9.83196 cd/m²。邊界：理想朗伯漫反射，不是真實濕路面亮度；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: illuminance=108 lx; reflectance=0.26 dimensionless. L=ρE/π=8.93814 cd/m². Increasing only illuminance by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 9.83196 cd/m². Boundary: Ideal Lambertian reflection, not actual wet-road luminance. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以同視角和乾濕條件比較兩孔的光度量測。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare photometry in both tubes under equal viewing and wetness conditions.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：照度=108 lx；反射率=0.26 無因次。L=ρE/π=8.93814 cd/m²。僅把照度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為9.83196 cd/m²。邊界：理想朗伯漫反射，不是真實濕路面亮度；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: illuminance=108 lx; reflectance=0.26 dimensionless. L=ρE/π=8.93814 cd/m². Increasing only illuminance by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 9.83196 cd/m². Boundary: Ideal Lambertian reflection, not actual wet-road luminance. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「視覺適應與路面亮度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Visual adaptation and pavement luminance\", which statement holds?","options":["全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。","岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。","原創教學假設：照度=108 lx；反射率=0.26 無因次。"],"optionsEn":["Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.","Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow.","Original teaching assumptions: illuminance=108 lx; reflectance=0.26 dimensionless."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：照度=108 lx；反射率=0.26 無因次。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: illuminance=108 lx; reflectance=0.26 dimensionless. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b115-v14-27","title":"視覺適應與路面亮度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Visual adaptation and pavement luminance: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「漫反射亮度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Diffuse luminance” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以同視角和乾濕條件比較兩孔的光度量測。以駕駛視角的亮度量測配合照度網格，分別檢查乾濕路面與燈具衰減，保留外部天空條件。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare photometry in both tubes under equal viewing and wetness conditions. Combine driver-view luminance with illuminance grids, checking dry and wet pavement and lamp depreciation while preserving exterior sky conditions. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「漫反射亮度」的交付需回答：以同視角和乾濕條件比較兩孔的光度量測。將視角、路面狀態和光度校正連同量測交付，照明調整需按核准場景測試，不把理想反射公式當驗收標準。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Frejus Road Tunnel, the diffuse luminance handover must address the following evidence: Compare photometry in both tubes under equal viewing and wetness conditions. Hand over viewing geometry, pavement state and photometric calibration; test changes against approved scenarios rather than treating ideal reflection as an acceptance criterion.","failure":"注意干擾：以新孔量測代表舊孔會低估老化表面與燈具影響。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: New-tube measurements do not represent aged surfaces and lamps in the old tube. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以同視角和乾濕條件比較兩孔的光度量測。以駕駛視角的亮度量測配合照度網格，分別檢查乾濕路面與燈具衰減，保留外部天空條件。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Compare photometry in both tubes under equal viewing and wetness conditions. Combine driver-view luminance with illuminance grids, checking dry and wet pavement and lamp depreciation while preserving exterior sky conditions. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「漫反射亮度」的交付需回答：以同視角和乾濕條件比較兩孔的光度量測。將視角、路面狀態和光度校正連同量測交付，照明調整需按核准場景測試，不把理想反射公式當驗收標準。","textEn":"For Frejus Road Tunnel, the diffuse luminance handover must address the following evidence: Compare photometry in both tubes under equal viewing and wetness conditions. Hand over viewing geometry, pavement state and photometric calibration; test changes against approved scenarios rather than treating ideal reflection as an acceptance criterion.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「視覺適應與路面亮度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Visual adaptation and pavement luminance\"?","options":["以同視角和乾濕條件比較兩孔的光度量測。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。"],"optionsEn":["Compare photometry in both tubes under equal viewing and wetness conditions.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以同視角和乾濕條件比較兩孔的光度量測。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare photometry in both tubes under equal viewing and wetness conditions. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b115-v14-28","title":"視覺適應與路面亮度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Visual adaptation and pavement luminance: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「漫反射亮度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Diffuse luminance” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"以新孔量測代表舊孔會低估老化表面與燈具影響。照度平均值合格仍可能存在低亮度障礙區或眩光，感測器沾污也會使調光系統低估外界亮度。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"New-tube measurements do not represent aged surfaces and lamps in the old tube. Acceptable average illuminance can coexist with dark obstacles or glare, while sensor contamination may bias adaptive lighting controls. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：路面反射、濕度、燈具配光及背景對比共同影響辨識；朗伯模型只示範理想漫反射，不能直接制定入口段燈具間距或真實道路安全值。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A Lambertian model illustrates ideal diffuse reflection only; it cannot establish entrance-zone spacing or actual road-safety limits without photometric and operational assessment.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「照度越高就必然使隧道內所有物體更容易辨識。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Higher illuminance necessarily makes every tunnel object easier to detect.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"以新孔量測代表舊孔會低估老化表面與燈具影響。照度平均值合格仍可能存在低亮度障礙區或眩光，感測器沾污也會使調光系統低估外界亮度。","textEn":"New-tube measurements do not represent aged surfaces and lamps in the old tube. Acceptable average illuminance can coexist with dark obstacles or glare, while sensor contamination may bias adaptive lighting controls.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「視覺適應與路面亮度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Visual adaptation and pavement luminance\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","以新孔量測代表舊孔會低估老化表面與燈具影響。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","New-tube measurements do not represent aged surfaces and lamps in the old tube.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以新孔量測代表舊孔會低估老化表面與燈具影響。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"New-tube measurements do not represent aged surfaces and lamps in the old tube. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b115-v14-29","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-28"],"objective":"說明「所需疏散時間」如何影響弗雷瑞斯公路隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Required evacuation time” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Frejus Road Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"跨孔撤離先確認鄰孔交通已處於受控狀態，教材將橫通道距離與安全孔可用性分開。疏散時間包含辨識、反應、移動及排隊，不只由出口距離決定。人員速度會受煙熱、能見度及行動能力影響，安全判斷還要比較可用安全時間；橫通道存在但門或鄰孔不可用時，圖上的最短路線不一定能作實際選擇。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「所需疏散時間」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Cross-bore evacuation first requires a controlled receiving tube; separate passage distance from receiving-bore availability. Evacuation includes detection, response, travel and queues, not merely distance to an exit. Smoke, visibility and mobility alter walking speed, while safety requires comparison with available safe time. A passage shown on a plan may be unusable because its door or receiving bore is unavailable, invalidating the nominal shortest route. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Required evacuation time” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：前置時間=108 s；行走距離=340 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=108 s; travel distance=340 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「所需疏散時間」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Required evacuation time”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-29-k1","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability","text":"跨孔撤離先確認鄰孔交通已處於受控狀態，教材將橫通道距離與安全孔可用性分開。疏散時間包含辨識、反應、移動及排隊，不只由出口距離決定。","textEn":"Cross-bore evacuation first requires a controlled receiving tube; separate passage distance from receiving-bore availability. Evacuation includes detection, response, travel and queues, not merely distance to an exit.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「疏散時間與分區可用性」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Evacuation time and zone availability\" is correct?","options":["只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。","設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。","跨孔撤離先確認鄰孔交通已處於受控狀態，教材將橫通道距離與安全孔可用性分開。"],"optionsEn":["Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.","Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety.","Cross-bore evacuation first requires a controlled receiving tube; separate passage distance from receiving-bore availability."],"answer":2,"explanation":"跨孔撤離先確認鄰孔交通已處於受控狀態，教材將橫通道距離與安全孔可用性分開。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Cross-bore evacuation first requires a controlled receiving tube; separate passage distance from receiving-bore availability. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b115-v14-30","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性：定量估算","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「所需疏散時間」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Required evacuation time” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：前置時間=108 s；行走距離=340 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。RSET=tpre+d/v=533 s。僅把行走距離增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為575.5 s。邊界：單群體固定速度，不含排隊煙熱及能力差異，不能單獨判安全；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=108 s; travel distance=340 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s. RSET=tpre+d/v=533 s. Increasing only travel distance by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 575.5 s. Boundary: One group at fixed speed without queues, smoke or mobility differences; not a safety conclusion. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：演練同步核對交通隔離、門位和人員到達時間。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Exercise traffic isolation, door state and arrival timing together.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：前置時間=108 s；行走距離=340 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。RSET=tpre+d/v=533 s。僅把行走距離增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為575.5 s。邊界：單群體固定速度，不含排隊煙熱及能力差異，不能單獨判安全；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=108 s; travel distance=340 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s. RSET=tpre+d/v=533 s. Increasing only travel distance by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 575.5 s. Boundary: One group at fixed speed without queues, smoke or mobility differences; not a safety conclusion. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「疏散時間與分區可用性」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Evacuation time and zone availability\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：前置時間=108 s；行走距離=340 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。","知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=108 s; travel distance=340 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.","Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：前置時間=108 s；行走距離=340 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=108 s; travel distance=340 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b115-v14-31","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「所需疏散時間」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Required evacuation time” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"演練同步核對交通隔離、門位和人員到達時間。以人流模擬或受控演練分辨前置時間、行走與門口排隊，核對每個出口接收區的可用狀態及通訊紀錄。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Exercise traffic isolation, door state and arrival timing together. Separate pre-movement, travel and doorway queues through simulation or controlled drills, checking receiving-zone availability and communication records for each exit. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「所需疏散時間」的交付需回答：演練同步核對交通隔離、門位和人員到達時間。疏散模型保留人口、速度分布及出口狀態，演練改動由營運與防災責任者批准，教材算例不得當作現場指揮程序。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Frejus Road Tunnel, the required evacuation time handover must address the following evidence: Exercise traffic isolation, door state and arrival timing together. Retain population, speed distribution and exit states; operations and fire-safety owners approve drill changes, and classroom calculations are not incident-command procedures.","failure":"注意干擾：橫通道到達快不代表鄰孔車流已安全停止。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Fast passage arrival does not establish stopped traffic in the receiving bore. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"演練同步核對交通隔離、門位和人員到達時間。以人流模擬或受控演練分辨前置時間、行走與門口排隊，核對每個出口接收區的可用狀態及通訊紀錄。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Exercise traffic isolation, door state and arrival timing together. Separate pre-movement, travel and doorway queues through simulation or controlled drills, checking receiving-zone availability and communication records for each exit. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「所需疏散時間」的交付需回答：演練同步核對交通隔離、門位和人員到達時間。疏散模型保留人口、速度分布及出口狀態，演練改動由營運與防災責任者批准，教材算例不得當作現場指揮程序。","textEn":"For Frejus Road Tunnel, the required evacuation time handover must address the following evidence: Exercise traffic isolation, door state and arrival timing together. Retain population, speed distribution and exit states; operations and fire-safety owners approve drill changes, and classroom calculations are not incident-command procedures.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「疏散時間與分區可用性」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Evacuation time and zone availability\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","演練同步核對交通隔離、門位和人員到達時間。","混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Exercise traffic isolation, door state and arrival timing together.","Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure."],"answer":1,"explanation":"演練同步核對交通隔離、門位和人員到達時間。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Exercise traffic isolation, door state and arrival timing together. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b115-v14-32","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性：失效診斷","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「所需疏散時間」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Required evacuation time” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"橫通道到達快不代表鄰孔車流已安全停止。以最快成人速度套全部旅客會低估需求，若忽略接收孔受煙或車流影響，疏散可能移到另一個危險邊界。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Fast passage arrival does not establish stopped traffic in the receiving bore. Applying the fastest adult speed to everyone understates demand; overlooking smoke or traffic in the receiving bore can transfer evacuees into another hazard. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：人員速度會受煙熱、能見度及行動能力影響，安全判斷還要比較可用安全時間；橫通道存在但門或鄰孔不可用時，圖上的最短路線不一定能作實際選擇。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A passage shown on a plan may be unusable because its door or receiving bore is unavailable, invalidating the nominal shortest route.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"橫通道到達快不代表鄰孔車流已安全停止。以最快成人速度套全部旅客會低估需求，若忽略接收孔受煙或車流影響，疏散可能移到另一個危險邊界。","textEn":"Fast passage arrival does not establish stopped traffic in the receiving bore. Applying the fastest adult speed to everyone understates demand; overlooking smoke or traffic in the receiving bore can transfer evacuees into another hazard.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「疏散時間與分區可用性」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Evacuation time and zone availability\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。","橫通道到達快不代表鄰孔車流已安全停止。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety.","Fast passage arrival does not establish stopped traffic in the receiving bore."],"answer":2,"explanation":"橫通道到達快不代表鄰孔車流已安全停止。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Fast passage arrival does not establish stopped traffic in the receiving bore. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b115-v14-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「設備備援與共同失效」與「資產編碼與可追溯交接」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Equipment redundancy and common failure\" and \"Asset identity and traceable handover\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b115-v14-33","title":"設備備援與共同失效：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Equipment redundancy and common failure: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-32"],"objective":"說明「系統不可用率」如何影響弗雷瑞斯公路隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “System unavailability” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Frejus Road Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"兩孔控制若共享通訊骨幹，表面設備成雙仍可能共同失效，研究切換與隔離的測試範圍。兩套設備只有在故障近似獨立且切換可靠時，並聯才顯著降低不可用率。共用配電、控制軟體、冷卻或受淹位置會把獨立假設破壞；維修停用也改變當下配置，因此可靠度模型必須明列共有資源和設備狀態，不能只數備用台數。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「系統不可用率」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Shared communications can defeat apparent twin-bore redundancy; examine the scope of transfer and isolation tests. Parallel equipment sharply reduces unavailability only when failures are approximately independent and transfer works. Shared power, software, cooling or flood exposure breaks that assumption. Planned maintenance also changes the available configuration, so reliability models must identify shared resources and states rather than count spare units or multiply unsupported independent probabilities. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “System unavailability” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：單機不可用率=0.024 無因次。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: single-unit unavailability=0.024 dimensionless.","failure":"常見誤解：「設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「系統不可用率」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “System unavailability”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-33-k1","title":"設備備援與共同失效","titleEn":"Equipment redundancy and common failure","text":"兩孔控制若共享通訊骨幹，表面設備成雙仍可能共同失效，研究切換與隔離的測試範圍。兩套設備只有在故障近似獨立且切換可靠時，並聯才顯著降低不可用率。","textEn":"Shared communications can defeat apparent twin-bore redundancy; examine the scope of transfer and isolation tests. Parallel equipment sharply reduces unavailability only when failures are approximately independent and transfer works.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「設備備援與共同失效」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Equipment redundancy and common failure\" is correct?","options":["兩孔控制若共享通訊骨幹，表面設備成雙仍可能共同失效，研究切換與隔離的測試範圍。","設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。"],"optionsEn":["Shared communications can defeat apparent twin-bore redundancy; examine the scope of transfer and isolation tests.","Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted."],"answer":0,"explanation":"兩孔控制若共享通訊骨幹，表面設備成雙仍可能共同失效，研究切換與隔離的測試範圍。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Shared communications can defeat apparent twin-bore redundancy; examine the scope of transfer and isolation tests. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b115-v14-34","title":"設備備援與共同失效：定量估算","titleEn":"Equipment redundancy and common failure: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「系統不可用率」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “System unavailability” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：單機不可用率=0.024 無因次。Uparallel=U²=0.000576 probability。僅把單機不可用率增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.00069696 probability。邊界：完全獨立並聯與完美切換，不含共同失效；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: single-unit unavailability=0.024 dimensionless. Uparallel=U²=0.000576 probability. Increasing only single-unit unavailability by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.00069696 probability. Boundary: Independent parallel units with perfect transfer, excluding common failures. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：追查兩孔感測、控制和供電的共同節點。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Trace shared sensing, control and power nodes across both bores.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：單機不可用率=0.024 無因次。Uparallel=U²=0.000576 probability。僅把單機不可用率增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.00069696 probability。邊界：完全獨立並聯與完美切換，不含共同失效；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: single-unit unavailability=0.024 dimensionless. Uparallel=U²=0.000576 probability. Increasing only single-unit unavailability by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.00069696 probability. Boundary: Independent parallel units with perfect transfer, excluding common failures. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「設備備援與共同失效」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Equipment redundancy and common failure\", which statement holds?","options":["岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。","原創教學假設：單機不可用率=0.024 無因次。","支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。"],"optionsEn":["Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow.","Original teaching assumptions: single-unit unavailability=0.024 dimensionless.","Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：單機不可用率=0.024 無因次。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: single-unit unavailability=0.024 dimensionless. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b115-v14-35","title":"設備備援與共同失效：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Equipment redundancy and common failure: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「系統不可用率」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “System unavailability” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"追查兩孔感測、控制和供電的共同節點。由設備清單畫出故障樹，將電源、控制及實體位置追到共同節點，並用事件及維修紀錄檢查獨立假設。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Trace shared sensing, control and power nodes across both bores. Build a fault tree from the asset list, trace power, control and location to shared nodes, and test independence against incident and maintenance records. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「系統不可用率」的交付需回答：追查兩孔感測、控制和供電的共同節點。維修計畫附當日可用配置與剩餘備援，任何共同資源更動同步更新故障樹，切換試驗由設備及營運團隊共同見證。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Frejus Road Tunnel, the system unavailability handover must address the following evidence: Trace shared sensing, control and power nodes across both bores. Attach the actual configuration and remaining redundancy to maintenance plans, update fault trees after shared-resource changes, and witness transfer tests jointly.","failure":"注意干擾：只測單台停機不能揭露骨幹失效造成的雙孔影響。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Single-unit outage tests miss shared-backbone failure affecting both tubes. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"追查兩孔感測、控制和供電的共同節點。由設備清單畫出故障樹，將電源、控制及實體位置追到共同節點，並用事件及維修紀錄檢查獨立假設。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Trace shared sensing, control and power nodes across both bores. Build a fault tree from the asset list, trace power, control and location to shared nodes, and test independence against incident and maintenance records. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「系統不可用率」的交付需回答：追查兩孔感測、控制和供電的共同節點。維修計畫附當日可用配置與剩餘備援，任何共同資源更動同步更新故障樹，切換試驗由設備及營運團隊共同見證。","textEn":"For Frejus Road Tunnel, the system unavailability handover must address the following evidence: Trace shared sensing, control and power nodes across both bores. Attach the actual configuration and remaining redundancy to maintenance plans, update fault trees after shared-resource changes, and witness transfer tests jointly.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「設備備援與共同失效」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Equipment redundancy and common failure\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。","追查兩孔感測、控制和供電的共同節點。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.","Trace shared sensing, control and power nodes across both bores."],"answer":2,"explanation":"追查兩孔感測、控制和供電的共同節點。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Trace shared sensing, control and power nodes across both bores. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b115-v14-36","title":"設備備援與共同失效：失效診斷","titleEn":"Equipment redundancy and common failure: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「系統不可用率」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “System unavailability” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只測單台停機不能揭露骨幹失效造成的雙孔影響。重複安裝卻共用單一供電可能在一次故障中全部停機，帳面可靠度很高但實際不可用時間沒有降低。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Single-unit outage tests miss shared-backbone failure affecting both tubes. Duplicated equipment on one supply can fail together in a single event, leaving actual downtime unchanged despite optimistic calculated reliability. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：共用配電、控制軟體、冷卻或受淹位置會把獨立假設破壞；維修停用也改變當下配置，因此可靠度模型必須明列共有資源和設備狀態，不能只數備用台數。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Planned maintenance also changes the available configuration, so reliability models must identify shared resources and states rather than count spare units or multiply unsupported independent probabilities.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只測單台停機不能揭露骨幹失效造成的雙孔影響。重複安裝卻共用單一供電可能在一次故障中全部停機，帳面可靠度很高但實際不可用時間沒有降低。","textEn":"Single-unit outage tests miss shared-backbone failure affecting both tubes. Duplicated equipment on one supply can fail together in a single event, leaving actual downtime unchanged despite optimistic calculated reliability.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「設備備援與共同失效」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Equipment redundancy and common failure\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["只測單台停機不能揭露骨幹失效造成的雙孔影響。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。"],"optionsEn":["Single-unit outage tests miss shared-backbone failure affecting both tubes.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted."],"answer":0,"explanation":"只測單台停機不能揭露骨幹失效造成的雙孔影響。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Single-unit outage tests miss shared-backbone failure affecting both tubes. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b115-v14-37","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-36"],"objective":"說明「資產資料完整度」如何影響弗雷瑞斯公路隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Asset-record completeness” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Frejus Road Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"弗雷瑞斯版本交付應保留原孔和新孔獨立設備樹，避免複製名稱後遺失安裝日期及測試狀態。地下設備的竣工資料必須讓維護人員找到正確位置、材料批次和控制版本。只有上傳圖面而沒有變更歷程，無法分辨元件替換與真正劣化；告警、儀器、線路及工單使用一致識別碼，才可能把量測趨勢連回實際受力或水力系統。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「資產資料完整度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Maintain separate asset trees for old and new tubes, preserving installation dates and test states when names are copied. Handover must let maintainers find the correct location, material batch and control revision. Drawings without change history cannot distinguish replacement from deterioration. Consistent identifiers across alarms, instruments, circuits and work orders are essential for linking trends to the physical structural or hydraulic system instead of treating each record as an isolated file. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Asset-record completeness” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：設備總數=114 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: asset count=114 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=85.9649 %.","failure":"常見誤解：「全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「資產資料完整度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Asset-record completeness”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-37-k1","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover","text":"弗雷瑞斯版本交付應保留原孔和新孔獨立設備樹，避免複製名稱後遺失安裝日期及測試狀態。地下設備的竣工資料必須讓維護人員找到正確位置、材料批次和控制版本。","textEn":"Maintain separate asset trees for old and new tubes, preserving installation dates and test states when names are copied. Handover must let maintainers find the correct location, material batch and control revision.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「資產編碼與可追溯交接」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Asset identity and traceable handover\" is correct?","options":["全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。","弗雷瑞斯版本交付應保留原孔和新孔獨立設備樹，避免複製名稱後遺失安裝日期及測試狀態。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.","Maintain separate asset trees for old and new tubes, preserving installation dates and test states when names are copied.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":1,"explanation":"弗雷瑞斯版本交付應保留原孔和新孔獨立設備樹，避免複製名稱後遺失安裝日期及測試狀態。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Maintain separate asset trees for old and new tubes, preserving installation dates and test states when names are copied. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b115-v14-38","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：定量估算","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「資產資料完整度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Asset-record completeness” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：設備總數=114 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。coverage=100(N−missing)/N=85.9649 %。僅把缺紀錄數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為84.5614 %。邊界：資料完整度，不等於安全或可靠度；擾動為連續敏感度，實際個數為整數；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: asset count=114 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=85.9649 %. Increasing only missing records by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 84.5614 %. Boundary: Record completeness, not safety or reliability; perturbation is continuous sensitivity while actual counts are integers. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：抽查同名設備是否有唯一孔別、位置和維護週期。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check similarly named assets have unique bore, location and maintenance interval.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：設備總數=114 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。coverage=100(N−missing)/N=85.9649 %。僅把缺紀錄數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為84.5614 %。邊界：資料完整度，不等於安全或可靠度；擾動為連續敏感度，實際個數為整數；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: asset count=114 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=85.9649 %. Increasing only missing records by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 84.5614 %. Boundary: Record completeness, not safety or reliability; perturbation is continuous sensitivity while actual counts are integers. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「資產編碼與可追溯交接」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Asset identity and traceable handover\", which statement holds?","options":["知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。","混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。","原創教學假設：設備總數=114 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。"],"optionsEn":["Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction.","Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure.","Original teaching assumptions: asset count=114 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=85.9649 %."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：設備總數=114 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: asset count=114 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=85.9649 %. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b115-v14-39","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「資產資料完整度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Asset-record completeness” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"抽查同名設備是否有唯一孔別、位置和維護週期。抽取一條告警，從控制畫面追到設備、線路、圖面和工單，核對位置、版本及校正日期並記錄無法閉合的欄位。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check similarly named assets have unique bore, location and maintenance interval. Trace a sampled alarm from screen to equipment, circuit, drawing and work order, checking location, revision and calibration dates and recording broken links. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「資產資料完整度」的交付需回答：抽查同名設備是否有唯一孔別、位置和維護週期。交接以可完成的定位、查找與復原任務驗證，由維護責任人確認現場可用性；完整度只是資料指標，不代表結構安全或設備可靠。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Frejus Road Tunnel, the asset-record completeness handover must address the following evidence: Check similarly named assets have unique bore, location and maintenance interval. Validate handover through achievable location, retrieval and recovery tasks witnessed by maintainers; completeness measures records, not structural safety or equipment reliability.","failure":"注意干擾：錯把新孔測試結果覆蓋舊孔會形成虛假的驗收證據。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Overwriting old-bore records with new-bore tests creates false acceptance evidence. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"抽查同名設備是否有唯一孔別、位置和維護週期。抽取一條告警，從控制畫面追到設備、線路、圖面和工單，核對位置、版本及校正日期並記錄無法閉合的欄位。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Check similarly named assets have unique bore, location and maintenance interval. Trace a sampled alarm from screen to equipment, circuit, drawing and work order, checking location, revision and calibration dates and recording broken links. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「資產資料完整度」的交付需回答：抽查同名設備是否有唯一孔別、位置和維護週期。交接以可完成的定位、查找與復原任務驗證，由維護責任人確認現場可用性；完整度只是資料指標，不代表結構安全或設備可靠。","textEn":"For Frejus Road Tunnel, the asset-record completeness handover must address the following evidence: Check similarly named assets have unique bore, location and maintenance interval. Validate handover through achievable location, retrieval and recovery tasks witnessed by maintainers; completeness measures records, not structural safety or equipment reliability.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「資產編碼與可追溯交接」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Asset identity and traceable handover\"?","options":["抽查同名設備是否有唯一孔別、位置和維護週期。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","照度越高就必然使隧道內所有物體更容易辨識。"],"optionsEn":["Check similarly named assets have unique bore, location and maintenance interval.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Higher illuminance necessarily makes every tunnel object easier to detect."],"answer":0,"explanation":"抽查同名設備是否有唯一孔別、位置和維護週期。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check similarly named assets have unique bore, location and maintenance interval. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b115-v14-40","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：失效診斷","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「資產資料完整度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Asset-record completeness” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"錯把新孔測試結果覆蓋舊孔會形成虛假的驗收證據。設備改名卻未更新控制畫面會引導人員隔離錯誤回路，材料批次缺漏則使同批缺陷無法追蹤到其他位置。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Overwriting old-bore records with new-bore tests creates false acceptance evidence. Renaming an asset without updating the screen can isolate the wrong circuit; missing material batches prevent tracing related defects at other locations. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：只有上傳圖面而沒有變更歷程，無法分辨元件替換與真正劣化；告警、儀器、線路及工單使用一致識別碼，才可能把量測趨勢連回實際受力或水力系統。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Consistent identifiers across alarms, instruments, circuits and work orders are essential for linking trends to the physical structural or hydraulic system instead of treating each record as an isolated file.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"錯把新孔測試結果覆蓋舊孔會形成虛假的驗收證據。設備改名卻未更新控制畫面會引導人員隔離錯誤回路，材料批次缺漏則使同批缺陷無法追蹤到其他位置。","textEn":"Overwriting old-bore records with new-bore tests creates false acceptance evidence. Renaming an asset without updating the screen can isolate the wrong circuit; missing material batches prevent tracing related defects at other locations.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「資產編碼與可追溯交接」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Asset identity and traceable handover\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","錯把新孔測試結果覆蓋舊孔會形成虛假的驗收證據。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Overwriting old-bore records with new-bore tests creates false acceptance evidence.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":1,"explanation":"錯把新孔測試結果覆蓋舊孔會形成虛假的驗收證據。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Overwriting old-bore records with new-bore tests creates false acceptance evidence. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"curriculumVersion":14,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000},{"id":"b116","title":"布倫納基線隧道","titleEn":"Brenner Base Tunnel","category":"underground","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"布倫納官方區分55公里基線隧道與包含既有繞行連接的64公里地下路線，並說明下方先進坑的地質調查和未來維護用途。本課由這個三孔系統出發，分析探查更新、多工作面物流、岩體水壓、控制網與軌道需求；各標段里程碑不被誤寫為全工程完工。","summaryEn":"BBT distinguishes the 55 km base tunnel from a 64 km linked underground route including the existing bypass and describes the lower exploratory gallery. This course follows that three-tunnel system through geological updates, multi-heading logistics, rock and water response, survey control and railway needs. Lot milestones are not presented as whole-project completion.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"ug-landmarks","subcategoryTitle":"世界隧道與地下巨作","subcategoryTitleEn":"World tunnels and underground landmarks","learningTrack":"underground","learningSubdiscipline":"ug-landmarks","learningTags":["underground","ug-landmarks","tunnel"],"architectureFamily":"tunnel","architectureNodes":[["路線里程與端點","Alignment chainage and endpoints"],["破碎帶連通性","Fault-zone connectivity"],["洞壁切向應力","Tangential wall stress"],["有效掘進利用率","Effective boring utilisation"],["方向角誤差","Orientation error"],["資產資料完整度","Asset-record completeness"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,5],[1,5]],"diagram":{"type":"tunnel","labels":["路線里程與端點","破碎帶連通性","洞壁切向應力","有效掘進利用率","方向角誤差"],"labelsEn":["Alignment chainage and endpoints","Fault-zone connectivity","Tangential wall stress","Effective boring utilisation","Orientation error"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"原創綜合審查：先計算「破碎帶連通與預報更新」，再獨立計算「掘進利用率與設備停時」。原創教學假設：滲透係數=1e-06 m/s；水力坡降=2.1 無因次；通水面積=350 m²。Q=k i A=0.000735 m³/s。僅把滲透係數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.0008085 m³/s。邊界：均質飽和達西流，不代表裂隙集中流；不是本工程實測或允收值。原創教學假設：切削速率=1.95 m/h；有效利用率=0.325 無因次。D=24vu=15.21 m/day。僅把有效利用率增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為16.731 m/day。邊界：平均循環模型，未表示地質轉換及停機分布；不是本工程實測或允收值。兩組結果的單位與邊界不同，不能直接相加。請列出一項缺少的現場輸入，說明它會影響哪個結論，以及哪種獨立量測可以縮小不確定度。","textEn":"Original integrated review: first calculate fault connectivity and forecast updating, then independently calculate boring utilisation and equipment downtime. Original teaching assumptions: conductivity=1e-06 m/s; hydraulic gradient=2.1 dimensionless; flow area=350 m². Q=k i A=0.000735 m³/s. Increasing only conductivity by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.0008085 m³/s. Boundary: Homogeneous saturated Darcy flow, not concentrated fracture flow. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Original teaching assumptions: active penetration=1.95 m/h; utilisation=0.325 dimensionless. D=24vu=15.21 m/day. Increasing only utilisation by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 16.731 m/day. Boundary: Mean-cycle model without ground transitions or downtime distribution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. The outputs have different units and boundaries and cannot simply be added. Identify one missing field input, explain which conclusion it changes and select an independent measurement to reduce uncertainty.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":14,"enrichmentVersion":14,"stages":[{"id":"b116-v14-s1","title":"地層條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Ground conditions, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「服務邊界與路線代價」與「破碎帶連通與預報更新」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\" and \"Fault connectivity and forecast updating\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b116-v14-01","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「路線里程與端點」如何影響布倫納基線隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Alignment chainage and endpoints” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Brenner Base Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"布倫納55公里主體與64公里連接路線有不同端點，教材先分開工程數量、列車行程與支坑總長。隧道選線同時改變洞口、覆土與縱坡，短路線不保證低地質風險。比較方案必須使用相同起訖點，並分開主孔、引道及服務坑的工程數量；交通時間只是需求的一個指標，不能代替施工可達性或長期維修評估。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「路線里程與端點」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The 55 km main works and 64 km linked route have different endpoints; separate quantities, train travel and total gallery length. Alignment changes portals, cover and gradient together, so a shorter tunnel need not have lower geological risk. Compare options between identical endpoints and distinguish running bores, approaches and service galleries. Travel time measures one service benefit but cannot replace assessment of construction access, maintenance closures or exposure to uncertain ground. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Alignment chainage and endpoints” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：長度=18 km；速度=60 km/h。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: length=18 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=18 min.","failure":"常見誤解：「最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「路線里程與端點」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Alignment chainage and endpoints”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b116-v14-01-k1","title":"服務邊界與路線代價","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost","text":"布倫納55公里主體與64公里連接路線有不同端點，教材先分開工程數量、列車行程與支坑總長。隧道選線同時改變洞口、覆土與縱坡，短路線不保證低地質風險。","textEn":"The 55 km main works and 64 km linked route have different endpoints; separate quantities, train travel and total gallery length. Alignment changes portals, cover and gradient together, so a shorter tunnel need not have lower geological risk.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]},{"id":"b116-v14-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「服務邊界與路線代價」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\" is correct?","options":["最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。","布倫納55公里主體與64公里連接路線有不同端點，教材先分開工程數量、列車行程與支坑總長。","岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。"],"optionsEn":["The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.","The 55 km main works and 64 km linked route have different endpoints; separate quantities, train travel and total gallery length.","Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow."],"answer":1,"explanation":"布倫納55公里主體與64公里連接路線有不同端點，教材先分開工程數量、列車行程與支坑總長。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The 55 km main works and 64 km linked route have different endpoints; separate quantities, train travel and total gallery length. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b116-v14-02","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：定量估算","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b116-v14-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「路線里程與端點」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Alignment chainage and endpoints” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：長度=18 km；速度=60 km/h。t=60L/v=18 min。僅把長度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為19.8 min。邊界：假想交通旅程，未含加減速、排隊及實際時刻表；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: length=18 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=18 min. Increasing only length by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 19.8 min. Boundary: Hypothetical transport journey excluding acceleration, queues and the real timetable. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對每種長度是否沿同一路徑及包含既有段。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check whether each length follows the same route and includes existing sections.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b116-v14-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：長度=18 km；速度=60 km/h。t=60L/v=18 min。僅把長度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為19.8 min。邊界：假想交通旅程，未含加減速、排隊及實際時刻表；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: length=18 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=18 min. Increasing only length by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 19.8 min. Boundary: Hypothetical transport journey excluding acceleration, queues and the real timetable. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]},{"id":"b116-v14-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「服務邊界與路線代價」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\", which statement holds?","options":["知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。","刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。","原創教學假設：長度=18 km；速度=60 km/h。"],"optionsEn":["Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction.","A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance.","Original teaching assumptions: length=18 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=18 min."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：長度=18 km；速度=60 km/h。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: length=18 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=18 min. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b116-v14-03","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b116-v14-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「路線里程與端點」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Alignment chainage and endpoints” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對每種長度是否沿同一路徑及包含既有段。把縱斷面、地形與地質剖面疊合，以端點坐標獨立反算距離，再將主孔與支坑數量分開核對。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check whether each length follows the same route and includes existing sections. Overlay the longitudinal profile, terrain and geology; independently derive distances from endpoint coordinates and reconcile running-bore and gallery quantities separately. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「路線里程與端點」的交付需回答：核對每種長度是否沿同一路徑及包含既有段。在方案表中凍結起訖點、計量範圍及地質假設，任何改線都要同步更新高程、數量與服務情境，不能只替換總長。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Brenner Base Tunnel, the alignment chainage and endpoints handover must address the following evidence: Check whether each length follows the same route and includes existing sections. Freeze endpoints, measurement scope and ground assumptions in the option register; realignment requires coordinated updates to elevations, quantities and service scenarios rather than replacing one length.","failure":"注意干擾：把64公里當新建主孔長度會重複計入既有連接。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using 64 km as new main-bore length double-counts existing connections. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b116-v14-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對每種長度是否沿同一路徑及包含既有段。把縱斷面、地形與地質剖面疊合，以端點坐標獨立反算距離，再將主孔與支坑數量分開核對。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Check whether each length follows the same route and includes existing sections. Overlay the longitudinal profile, terrain and geology; independently derive distances from endpoint coordinates and reconcile running-bore and gallery quantities separately. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]},{"id":"b116-v14-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「路線里程與端點」的交付需回答：核對每種長度是否沿同一路徑及包含既有段。在方案表中凍結起訖點、計量範圍及地質假設，任何改線都要同步更新高程、數量與服務情境，不能只替換總長。","textEn":"For Brenner Base Tunnel, the alignment chainage and endpoints handover must address the following evidence: Check whether each length follows the same route and includes existing sections. Freeze endpoints, measurement scope and ground assumptions in the option register; realignment requires coordinated updates to elevations, quantities and service scenarios rather than replacing one length.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「服務邊界與路線代價」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\"?","options":["核對每種長度是否沿同一路徑及包含既有段。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Check whether each length follows the same route and includes existing sections.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error."],"answer":0,"explanation":"核對每種長度是否沿同一路徑及包含既有段。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check whether each length follows the same route and includes existing sections. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b116-v14-04","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：失效診斷","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b116-v14-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「路線里程與端點」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Alignment chainage and endpoints” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把64公里當新建主孔長度會重複計入既有連接。混用全線與單孔長度會同時扭曲工程數量、行程及逃生距離，造成方案比較失去共同基準。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using 64 km as new main-bore length double-counts existing connections. Mixing whole-route and single-bore lengths distorts quantities, journey time and escape distance, destroying the common basis of an option comparison. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：比較方案必須使用相同起訖點，並分開主孔、引道及服務坑的工程數量；交通時間只是需求的一個指標，不能代替施工可達性或長期維修評估。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Travel time measures one service benefit but cannot replace assessment of construction access, maintenance closures or exposure to uncertain ground.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b116-v14-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把64公里當新建主孔長度會重複計入既有連接。混用全線與單孔長度會同時扭曲工程數量、行程及逃生距離，造成方案比較失去共同基準。","textEn":"Using 64 km as new main-bore length double-counts existing connections. Mixing whole-route and single-bore lengths distorts quantities, journey time and escape distance, destroying the common basis of an option comparison.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]},{"id":"b116-v14-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「服務邊界與路線代價」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","把64公里當新建主孔長度會重複計入既有連接。","岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Using 64 km as new main-bore length double-counts existing connections.","Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把64公里當新建主孔長度會重複計入既有連接。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using 64 km as new main-bore length double-counts existing connections. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b116-v14-05","title":"破碎帶連通與預報更新：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Fault connectivity and forecast updating: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b116-v14-04"],"objective":"說明「破碎帶連通性」如何影響布倫納基線隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Fault-zone connectivity” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Brenner Base Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"下方先進坑提供布倫納主孔前方資訊，但高程差使構造外推需保留不確定性。斷層帶可以含很硬的岩塊，但整體變形與湧水常由填充節理和連通裂隙控制。單一岩芯強度不能代表整個掌子面；超前鑽孔、出水變化與揭露地質須回饋同一里程模型，預報則應保留不同情境及其證據權重。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「破碎帶連通性」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The lower exploratory gallery informs main-bore forecasts, but elevation separation leaves uncertainty in projecting structures upward. A fault zone may contain strong intact blocks while filled joints and connected fractures govern its bulk deformation and inflow. One core strength does not represent the entire face. Probe records, water response and exposed geology must update a common chainage model, preserving competing interpretations and their evidential weight rather than treating a forecast as certainty. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Fault-zone connectivity” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：滲透係數=1e-06 m/s；水力坡降=2.1 無因次；通水面積=350 m²。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: conductivity=1e-06 m/s; hydraulic gradient=2.1 dimensionless; flow area=350 m².","failure":"常見誤解：「岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「破碎帶連通性」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Fault-zone connectivity”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b116-v14-05-k1","title":"破碎帶連通與預報更新","titleEn":"Fault connectivity and forecast updating","text":"下方先進坑提供布倫納主孔前方資訊，但高程差使構造外推需保留不確定性。斷層帶可以含很硬的岩塊，但整體變形與湧水常由填充節理和連通裂隙控制。","textEn":"The lower exploratory gallery informs main-bore forecasts, but elevation separation leaves uncertainty in projecting structures upward. A fault zone may contain strong intact blocks while filled joints and connected fractures govern its bulk deformation and inflow.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]},{"id":"b116-v14-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「破碎帶連通與預報更新」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Fault connectivity and forecast updating\" is correct?","options":["岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。","目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。","下方先進坑提供布倫納主孔前方資訊，但高程差使構造外推需保留不確定性。"],"optionsEn":["Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow.","No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.","The lower exploratory gallery informs main-bore forecasts, but elevation separation leaves uncertainty in projecting structures upward."],"answer":2,"explanation":"下方先進坑提供布倫納主孔前方資訊，但高程差使構造外推需保留不確定性。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The lower exploratory gallery informs main-bore forecasts, but elevation separation leaves uncertainty in projecting structures upward. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b116-v14-06","title":"破碎帶連通與預報更新：定量估算","titleEn":"Fault connectivity and forecast updating: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b116-v14-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「破碎帶連通性」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Fault-zone connectivity” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：滲透係數=1e-06 m/s；水力坡降=2.1 無因次；通水面積=350 m²。Q=k i A=0.000735 m³/s。僅把滲透係數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.0008085 m³/s。邊界：均質飽和達西流，不代表裂隙集中流；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: conductivity=1e-06 m/s; hydraulic gradient=2.1 dimensionless; flow area=350 m². Q=k i A=0.000735 m³/s. Increasing only conductivity by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.0008085 m³/s. Boundary: Homogeneous saturated Darcy flow, not concentrated fracture flow. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以裂隙方位投影到主孔，再用超前孔覆核。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Project fractures to main-bore level and check with advance probes.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b116-v14-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：滲透係數=1e-06 m/s；水力坡降=2.1 無因次；通水面積=350 m²。Q=k i A=0.000735 m³/s。僅把滲透係數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.0008085 m³/s。邊界：均質飽和達西流，不代表裂隙集中流；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: conductivity=1e-06 m/s; hydraulic gradient=2.1 dimensionless; flow area=350 m². Q=k i A=0.000735 m³/s. Increasing only conductivity by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.0008085 m³/s. Boundary: Homogeneous saturated Darcy flow, not concentrated fracture flow. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]},{"id":"b116-v14-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「破碎帶連通與預報更新」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Fault connectivity and forecast updating\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：滲透係數=1e-06 m/s；水力坡降=2.1 無因次；通水面積=350 m²。","支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。","增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: conductivity=1e-06 m/s; hydraulic gradient=2.1 dimensionless; flow area=350 m².","Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem.","Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：滲透係數=1e-06 m/s；水力坡降=2.1 無因次；通水面積=350 m²。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: conductivity=1e-06 m/s; hydraulic gradient=2.1 dimensionless; flow area=350 m². Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b116-v14-07","title":"破碎帶連通與預報更新：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Fault connectivity and forecast updating: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b116-v14-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「破碎帶連通性」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Fault-zone connectivity” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以裂隙方位投影到主孔，再用超前孔覆核。將岩心回收、裂隙方位與出水曲線按里程對齊，用未參與建模的孔段作交叉檢驗，檢查是否只擬合已知資料。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Project fractures to main-bore level and check with advance probes. Align recovery, fracture orientation and inflow by chainage; test the interpretation against a withheld borehole interval to detect fitting only the known observations. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「破碎帶連通性」的交付需回答：以裂隙方位投影到主孔，再用超前孔覆核。每次地質模型更新保留舊版與新增證據，差異由地質及支護設計者共同判讀，施工條件改變需重新確認核准範圍。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Brenner Base Tunnel, the fault-zone connectivity handover must address the following evidence: Project fractures to main-bore level and check with advance probes. Retain previous interpretations and new evidence at every update; geology and support designers jointly interpret differences and reconfirm approved bounds when ground conditions change.","failure":"注意干擾：先進坑乾燥不證明上方主孔不會遇另一連通水帶。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A dry exploratory gallery does not exclude another connected water zone above. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b116-v14-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以裂隙方位投影到主孔，再用超前孔覆核。將岩心回收、裂隙方位與出水曲線按里程對齊，用未參與建模的孔段作交叉檢驗，檢查是否只擬合已知資料。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Project fractures to main-bore level and check with advance probes. Align recovery, fracture orientation and inflow by chainage; test the interpretation against a withheld borehole interval to detect fitting only the known observations. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]},{"id":"b116-v14-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「破碎帶連通性」的交付需回答：以裂隙方位投影到主孔，再用超前孔覆核。每次地質模型更新保留舊版與新增證據，差異由地質及支護設計者共同判讀，施工條件改變需重新確認核准範圍。","textEn":"For Brenner Base Tunnel, the fault-zone connectivity handover must address the following evidence: Project fractures to main-bore level and check with advance probes. Retain previous interpretations and new evidence at every update; geology and support designers jointly interpret differences and reconfirm approved bounds when ground conditions change.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「破碎帶連通與預報更新」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Fault connectivity and forecast updating\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","以裂隙方位投影到主孔，再用超前孔覆核。","基線隧道坡度很小，所以不必做牽引與制動分析。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Project fractures to main-bore level and check with advance probes.","A small base-tunnel gradient eliminates the need for traction and braking analysis."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以裂隙方位投影到主孔，再用超前孔覆核。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Project fractures to main-bore level and check with advance probes. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b116-v14-08","title":"破碎帶連通與預報更新：失效診斷","titleEn":"Fault connectivity and forecast updating: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b116-v14-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「破碎帶連通性」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Fault-zone connectivity” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"先進坑乾燥不證明上方主孔不會遇另一連通水帶。只用完整岩石強度會漏掉軟弱填充物，可能在看似堅硬的地層中出現收斂加快、支護過載或水量突增。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A dry exploratory gallery does not exclude another connected water zone above. Intact strength alone misses weak infill, allowing accelerating convergence, support overload or sudden inflow in ground that superficially appears strong. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：單一岩芯強度不能代表整個掌子面；超前鑽孔、出水變化與揭露地質須回饋同一里程模型，預報則應保留不同情境及其證據權重。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Probe records, water response and exposed geology must update a common chainage model, preserving competing interpretations and their evidential weight rather than treating a forecast as certainty.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b116-v14-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"先進坑乾燥不證明上方主孔不會遇另一連通水帶。只用完整岩石強度會漏掉軟弱填充物，可能在看似堅硬的地層中出現收斂加快、支護過載或水量突增。","textEn":"A dry exploratory gallery does not exclude another connected water zone above. Intact strength alone misses weak infill, allowing accelerating convergence, support overload or sudden inflow in ground that superficially appears strong.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]},{"id":"b116-v14-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「破碎帶連通與預報更新」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Fault connectivity and forecast updating\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。","先進坑乾燥不證明上方主孔不會遇另一連通水帶。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.","A dry exploratory gallery does not exclude another connected water zone above."],"answer":2,"explanation":"先進坑乾燥不證明上方主孔不會遇另一連通水帶。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A dry exploratory gallery does not exclude another connected water zone above. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b116-v14-s2","title":"機制、材料與定量設計","titleEn":"Mechanisms, materials and quantitative design","description":"本階段聚焦「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」與「覆土應力與洞壁重分配」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\" and \"Cover stress and wall redistribution\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b116-v14-09","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b116-v14-08"],"objective":"說明「測壓水頭」如何影響布倫納基線隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Piezometric head” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Brenner Base Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"三孔系統的排水互相影響，布倫納教材研究先進坑降水如何改變主孔施工與永久水頭。水壓取決於連通含水層的測壓水頭，不必等於地表或海面至洞頂的幾何深度。排水降低水壓卻可能增加有效應力與沉陷；停泵或排水堵塞後水頭又會回升，因此防水、排水及環境保水是互相制約的設計選擇。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「測壓水頭」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Drainage interacts across three galleries; examine how exploratory-gallery relief changes main-bore construction and permanent heads. Water pressure follows piezometric head in the connected aquifer, not automatically the geometric depth below ground or sea level. Drainage reduces pressure but can increase effective stress and settlement. Head may recover after a pump outage or blockage, coupling waterproofing, drainage capacity and preservation of surrounding groundwater in the permanent design. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Piezometric head” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=92 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=92 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=902.52 kPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「測壓水頭」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Piezometric head”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b116-v14-09-k1","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure","text":"三孔系統的排水互相影響，布倫納教材研究先進坑降水如何改變主孔施工與永久水頭。水壓取決於連通含水層的測壓水頭，不必等於地表或海面至洞頂的幾何深度。","textEn":"Drainage interacts across three galleries; examine how exploratory-gallery relief changes main-bore construction and permanent heads. Water pressure follows piezometric head in the connected aquifer, not automatically the geometric depth below ground or sea level.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]},{"id":"b116-v14-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\" is correct?","options":["三孔系統的排水互相影響，布倫納教材研究先進坑降水如何改變主孔施工與永久水頭。","目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。","知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。"],"optionsEn":["Drainage interacts across three galleries; examine how exploratory-gallery relief changes main-bore construction and permanent heads.","No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.","Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction."],"answer":0,"explanation":"三孔系統的排水互相影響，布倫納教材研究先進坑降水如何改變主孔施工與永久水頭。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Drainage interacts across three galleries; examine how exploratory-gallery relief changes main-bore construction and permanent heads. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b116-v14-10","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓：定量估算","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b116-v14-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「測壓水頭」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Piezometric head” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=92 m。p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=902.52 kPa。僅把水頭增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為992.772 kPa。邊界：靜水表壓，不是土體總壓或原位量測；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=92 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=902.52 kPa. Increasing only head by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 992.772 kPa. Boundary: Hydrostatic gauge pressure, not total earth pressure or an in-situ measurement. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同步比較三孔壓力、流量與補注事件。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare pressure, flow and recharge events across all three galleries.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b116-v14-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=92 m。p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=902.52 kPa。僅把水頭增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為992.772 kPa。邊界：靜水表壓，不是土體總壓或原位量測；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=92 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=902.52 kPa. Increasing only head by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 992.772 kPa. Boundary: Hydrostatic gauge pressure, not total earth pressure or an in-situ measurement. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]},{"id":"b116-v14-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\", which statement holds?","options":["刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。","原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=92 m。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。"],"optionsEn":["A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance.","Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=92 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=902.52 kPa.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=92 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=92 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=902.52 kPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b116-v14-11","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b116-v14-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「測壓水頭」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Piezometric head” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同步比較三孔壓力、流量與補注事件。使用分層測壓管及流量計，配合降雨或潮位序列分辨補注與設備影響，將讀值統一換算至同一高程基準。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare pressure, flow and recharge events across all three galleries. Use nested piezometers and flowmeters with rainfall or tide histories to distinguish recharge from equipment effects, converting observations to a common elevation datum. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「測壓水頭」的交付需回答：同步比較三孔壓力、流量與補注事件。設計檢核應分列正常排水、堵塞與停電水位，將環境受體的容許變化和監測責任一起交付，不把抽水量當唯一指標。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Brenner Base Tunnel, the piezometric head handover must address the following evidence: Compare pressure, flow and recharge events across all three galleries. Separate normal drainage, blocked-drain and power-outage heads and hand over receptor limits and monitoring responsibility together rather than using pump flow as the sole indicator.","failure":"注意干擾：把三孔出流相加而未查連通可能重複估計獨立補注。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Summing flows without connectivity checks can double-count supposedly independent recharge. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b116-v14-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同步比較三孔壓力、流量與補注事件。使用分層測壓管及流量計，配合降雨或潮位序列分辨補注與設備影響，將讀值統一換算至同一高程基準。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Compare pressure, flow and recharge events across all three galleries. Use nested piezometers and flowmeters with rainfall or tide histories to distinguish recharge from equipment effects, converting observations to a common elevation datum. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]},{"id":"b116-v14-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「測壓水頭」的交付需回答：同步比較三孔壓力、流量與補注事件。設計檢核應分列正常排水、堵塞與停電水位，將環境受體的容許變化和監測責任一起交付，不把抽水量當唯一指標。","textEn":"For Brenner Base Tunnel, the piezometric head handover must address the following evidence: Compare pressure, flow and recharge events across all three galleries. Separate normal drainage, blocked-drain and power-outage heads and hand over receptor limits and monitoring responsibility together rather than using pump flow as the sole indicator.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。","同步比較三孔壓力、流量與補注事件。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.","Compare pressure, flow and recharge events across all three galleries."],"answer":2,"explanation":"同步比較三孔壓力、流量與補注事件。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare pressure, flow and recharge events across all three galleries. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b116-v14-12","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓：失效診斷","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b116-v14-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「測壓水頭」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Piezometric head” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把三孔出流相加而未查連通可能重複估計獨立補注。將暫時降水後的低水頭當成永久狀態，會漏掉停泵後外壓回升；過度排水也可能引起周邊地層壓密。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Summing flows without connectivity checks can double-count supposedly independent recharge. Treating temporarily lowered head as permanent misses pressure recovery after outage; excessive drainage can also consolidate surrounding ground. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：排水降低水壓卻可能增加有效應力與沉陷；停泵或排水堵塞後水頭又會回升，因此防水、排水及環境保水是互相制約的設計選擇。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Head may recover after a pump outage or blockage, coupling waterproofing, drainage capacity and preservation of surrounding groundwater in the permanent design.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b116-v14-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把三孔出流相加而未查連通可能重複估計獨立補注。將暫時降水後的低水頭當成永久狀態，會漏掉停泵後外壓回升；過度排水也可能引起周邊地層壓密。","textEn":"Summing flows without connectivity checks can double-count supposedly independent recharge. Treating temporarily lowered head as permanent misses pressure recovery after outage; excessive drainage can also consolidate surrounding ground.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]},{"id":"b116-v14-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["把三孔出流相加而未查連通可能重複估計獨立補注。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。"],"optionsEn":["Summing flows without connectivity checks can double-count supposedly independent recharge.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction."],"answer":0,"explanation":"把三孔出流相加而未查連通可能重複估計獨立補注。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Summing flows without connectivity checks can double-count supposedly independent recharge. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b116-v14-13","title":"覆土應力與洞壁重分配：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Cover stress and wall redistribution: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b116-v14-12"],"objective":"說明「洞壁切向應力」如何影響布倫納基線隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Tangential wall stress” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Brenner Base Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"長基線隧道穿越不同覆土和構造，教材把彈性洞壁應力與節理控制破壞分開選模。開挖使岩體洞壁失去徑向拘束，遠場荷載轉移到周圍岩體，局部切向應力可能升高。圓孔彈性解可辨識量級，但節理、非圓斷面、塑性區與原位應力比會改變峰值位置，不能只用覆土重量推定全部三維應力。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「洞壁切向應力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A long base tunnel crosses varying cover and structure; distinguish elastic wall stress from joint-controlled failure when selecting models. Excavation removes radial confinement at the wall and transfers load through the surrounding rock, potentially raising local tangential stress. An elastic circular-hole solution identifies scale, but joints, noncircular geometry, yielding and the in-situ stress ratio alter the peak location. Cover weight alone cannot establish the complete three-dimensional stress state or support demand. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Tangential wall stress” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：覆土深度=950 m；岩體單位重=26 kN/m³。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: cover=950 m; rock unit weight=26 kN/m³. σθ,max=3γH/1000=74.1 MPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「洞壁切向應力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Tangential wall stress”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b116-v14-13-k1","title":"覆土應力與洞壁重分配","titleEn":"Cover stress and wall redistribution","text":"長基線隧道穿越不同覆土和構造，教材把彈性洞壁應力與節理控制破壞分開選模。開挖使岩體洞壁失去徑向拘束，遠場荷載轉移到周圍岩體，局部切向應力可能升高。","textEn":"A long base tunnel crosses varying cover and structure; distinguish elastic wall stress from joint-controlled failure when selecting models. Excavation removes radial confinement at the wall and transfers load through the surrounding rock, potentially raising local tangential stress.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]},{"id":"b116-v14-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「覆土應力與洞壁重分配」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Cover stress and wall redistribution\" is correct?","options":["知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。","長基線隧道穿越不同覆土和構造，教材把彈性洞壁應力與節理控制破壞分開選模。","支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。"],"optionsEn":["Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction.","A long base tunnel crosses varying cover and structure; distinguish elastic wall stress from joint-controlled failure when selecting models.","Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem."],"answer":1,"explanation":"長基線隧道穿越不同覆土和構造，教材把彈性洞壁應力與節理控制破壞分開選模。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A long base tunnel crosses varying cover and structure; distinguish elastic wall stress from joint-controlled failure when selecting models. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b116-v14-14","title":"覆土應力與洞壁重分配：定量估算","titleEn":"Cover stress and wall redistribution: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b116-v14-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「洞壁切向應力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Tangential wall stress” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：覆土深度=950 m；岩體單位重=26 kN/m³。σθ,max=3γH/1000=74.1 MPa。僅把覆土深度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為81.51 MPa。邊界：無支承彈性圓孔，僅垂直遠場壓縮且水平遠場應力為零時，側壁最大環向壓應力；不是任意位置應力或完整三維原位解；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: cover=950 m; rock unit weight=26 kN/m³. σθ,max=3γH/1000=74.1 MPa. Increasing only cover by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 81.51 MPa. Boundary: Maximum tangential compression at the sidewalls of an unsupported elastic circular hole under vertical uniaxial remote loading with zero horizontal remote stress; not stress at any point or the complete three-dimensional in-situ state. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比較原位應力方向、破壞方位和分段收斂。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare in-situ stress directions, damage orientation and segment convergence.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b116-v14-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：覆土深度=950 m；岩體單位重=26 kN/m³。σθ,max=3γH/1000=74.1 MPa。僅把覆土深度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為81.51 MPa。邊界：無支承彈性圓孔，僅垂直遠場壓縮且水平遠場應力為零時，側壁最大環向壓應力；不是任意位置應力或完整三維原位解；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: cover=950 m; rock unit weight=26 kN/m³. σθ,max=3γH/1000=74.1 MPa. Increasing only cover by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 81.51 MPa. Boundary: Maximum tangential compression at the sidewalls of an unsupported elastic circular hole under vertical uniaxial remote loading with zero horizontal remote stress; not stress at any point or the complete three-dimensional in-situ state. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]},{"id":"b116-v14-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「覆土應力與洞壁重分配」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Cover stress and wall redistribution\", which statement holds?","options":["增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。","基線隧道坡度很小，所以不必做牽引與制動分析。","原創教學假設：覆土深度=950 m；岩體單位重=26 kN/m³。"],"optionsEn":["Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.","A small base-tunnel gradient eliminates the need for traction and braking analysis.","Original teaching assumptions: cover=950 m; rock unit weight=26 kN/m³. σθ,max=3γH/1000=74.1 MPa."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：覆土深度=950 m；岩體單位重=26 kN/m³。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: cover=950 m; rock unit weight=26 kN/m³. σθ,max=3γH/1000=74.1 MPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b116-v14-15","title":"覆土應力與洞壁重分配：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Cover stress and wall redistribution: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b116-v14-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「洞壁切向應力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Tangential wall stress” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比較原位應力方向、破壞方位和分段收斂。將原位應力量測、岩石試驗及洞壁破壞方位相互比較，再用多點伸長計檢查變形是否與所假設應力方向一致。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare in-situ stress directions, damage orientation and segment convergence. Compare in-situ stress measurements, rock tests and wall-damage orientation, then use multipoint extensometers to test consistency with the assumed stress directions. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「洞壁切向應力」的交付需回答：比較原位應力方向、破壞方位和分段收斂。保留應力模型的座標、邊界和材料假設，量測與預測不符時先核對代表性，再由岩力設計者選擇非線性或節理模型。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Brenner Base Tunnel, the tangential wall stress handover must address the following evidence: Compare in-situ stress directions, damage orientation and segment convergence. Record stress-model coordinates, boundaries and material assumptions; when observations disagree, check representativeness before the rock designer selects nonlinear or jointed models.","failure":"注意干擾：單用覆土排序危險程度會漏掉低覆土弱帶的變形。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Ranking hazard by cover alone misses deformation in weak shallow zones. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b116-v14-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比較原位應力方向、破壞方位和分段收斂。將原位應力量測、岩石試驗及洞壁破壞方位相互比較，再用多點伸長計檢查變形是否與所假設應力方向一致。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Compare in-situ stress directions, damage orientation and segment convergence. Compare in-situ stress measurements, rock tests and wall-damage orientation, then use multipoint extensometers to test consistency with the assumed stress directions. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]},{"id":"b116-v14-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「洞壁切向應力」的交付需回答：比較原位應力方向、破壞方位和分段收斂。保留應力模型的座標、邊界和材料假設，量測與預測不符時先核對代表性，再由岩力設計者選擇非線性或節理模型。","textEn":"For Brenner Base Tunnel, the tangential wall stress handover must address the following evidence: Compare in-situ stress directions, damage orientation and segment convergence. Record stress-model coordinates, boundaries and material assumptions; when observations disagree, check representativeness before the rock designer selects nonlinear or jointed models.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「覆土應力與洞壁重分配」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Cover stress and wall redistribution\"?","options":["比較原位應力方向、破壞方位和分段收斂。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Compare in-situ stress directions, damage orientation and segment convergence.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":0,"explanation":"比較原位應力方向、破壞方位和分段收斂。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare in-situ stress directions, damage orientation and segment convergence. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b116-v14-16","title":"覆土應力與洞壁重分配：失效診斷","titleEn":"Cover stress and wall redistribution: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b116-v14-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「洞壁切向應力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Tangential wall stress” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"單用覆土排序危險程度會漏掉低覆土弱帶的變形。把彈性峰值直接當岩體強度可能誤判支護需求；相反地忽略剝落或擠壓也會讓局部破壞逐步侵入淨空。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Ranking hazard by cover alone misses deformation in weak shallow zones. Equating an elastic peak with rock-mass strength misjudges support demand; overlooking spalling or squeezing lets damage progressively consume clearance. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：圓孔彈性解可辨識量級，但節理、非圓斷面、塑性區與原位應力比會改變峰值位置，不能只用覆土重量推定全部三維應力。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Cover weight alone cannot establish the complete three-dimensional stress state or support demand.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b116-v14-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"單用覆土排序危險程度會漏掉低覆土弱帶的變形。把彈性峰值直接當岩體強度可能誤判支護需求；相反地忽略剝落或擠壓也會讓局部破壞逐步侵入淨空。","textEn":"Ranking hazard by cover alone misses deformation in weak shallow zones. Equating an elastic peak with rock-mass strength misjudges support demand; overlooking spalling or squeezing lets damage progressively consume clearance.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]},{"id":"b116-v14-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「覆土應力與洞壁重分配」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Cover stress and wall redistribution\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","單用覆土排序危險程度會漏掉低覆土弱帶的變形。","支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Ranking hazard by cover alone misses deformation in weak shallow zones.","Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem."],"answer":1,"explanation":"單用覆土排序危險程度會漏掉低覆土弱帶的變形。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Ranking hazard by cover alone misses deformation in weak shallow zones. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b116-v14-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「支護啟動與變形容量」與「掘進利用率與設備停時」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Support activation and deformation capacity\" and \"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b116-v14-17","title":"支護啟動與變形容量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Support activation and deformation capacity: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b116-v14-16"],"objective":"說明「支護安裝時點」如何影響布倫納基線隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Support activation time” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Brenner Base Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"多標段支護設計需要一致證據格式但不必相同參數，布倫納教材研究地質分區與封閉時序。支護荷載由開挖釋放量和支護啟動時間共同決定，越早安裝不一定讓構件受力越小。地盤反力與支護曲線必須連同掌子面距離及封閉順序理解；擠壓性地層還需保留變形容量，不能只追求高剛度與高材料強度。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「支護安裝時點」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Different lots need consistent evidence formats without identical parameters; examine ground domains and closure timing. Support load depends on stress release and activation time, so earlier installation does not necessarily reduce member forces. Interpret ground-reaction and support curves together with distance from the face and closure sequence. Squeezing ground also needs deformation capacity; high stiffness and material strength alone do not guarantee a compatible support response. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Support activation time” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：局部剛度=45 kN/mm；位移=9 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: local stiffness=45 kN/mm; movement=9 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「支護安裝時點」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Support activation time”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b116-v14-17-k1","title":"支護啟動與變形容量","titleEn":"Support activation and deformation capacity","text":"多標段支護設計需要一致證據格式但不必相同參數，布倫納教材研究地質分區與封閉時序。支護荷載由開挖釋放量和支護啟動時間共同決定，越早安裝不一定讓構件受力越小。","textEn":"Different lots need consistent evidence formats without identical parameters; examine ground domains and closure timing. Support load depends on stress release and activation time, so earlier installation does not necessarily reduce member forces.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]},{"id":"b116-v14-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「支護啟動與變形容量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Support activation and deformation capacity\" is correct?","options":["支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。","刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。","多標段支護設計需要一致證據格式但不必相同參數，布倫納教材研究地質分區與封閉時序。"],"optionsEn":["Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem.","A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance.","Different lots need consistent evidence formats without identical parameters; examine ground domains and closure timing."],"answer":2,"explanation":"多標段支護設計需要一致證據格式但不必相同參數，布倫納教材研究地質分區與封閉時序。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Different lots need consistent evidence formats without identical parameters; examine ground domains and closure timing. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b116-v14-18","title":"支護啟動與變形容量：定量估算","titleEn":"Support activation and deformation capacity: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b116-v14-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「支護安裝時點」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Support activation time” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：局部剛度=45 kN/mm；位移=9 mm。F=ku=405 kN。僅把位移增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為445.5 kN。邊界：線性局部彈簧，不含屈服或時間效應；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: local stiffness=45 kN/mm; movement=9 mm. F=ku=405 kN. Increasing only movement by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 445.5 kN. Boundary: Local linear spring without yielding or time effects. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將相同開挖齡期的荷重及收斂放在同地質組比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare loads and convergence at equal excavation age within one ground domain.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b116-v14-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：局部剛度=45 kN/mm；位移=9 mm。F=ku=405 kN。僅把位移增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為445.5 kN。邊界：線性局部彈簧，不含屈服或時間效應；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: local stiffness=45 kN/mm; movement=9 mm. F=ku=405 kN. Increasing only movement by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 445.5 kN. Boundary: Local linear spring without yielding or time effects. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]},{"id":"b116-v14-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「支護啟動與變形容量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Support activation and deformation capacity\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：局部剛度=45 kN/mm；位移=9 mm。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: local stiffness=45 kN/mm; movement=9 mm.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：局部剛度=45 kN/mm；位移=9 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: local stiffness=45 kN/mm; movement=9 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b116-v14-19","title":"支護啟動與變形容量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Support activation and deformation capacity: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b116-v14-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「支護安裝時點」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Support activation time” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將相同開挖齡期的荷重及收斂放在同地質組比較。同步記錄收斂、支護荷重與安裝里程，比較同一地質分區內的速率及荷載，不將不同開挖齡期讀值直接混合。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare loads and convergence at equal excavation age within one ground domain. Synchronise convergence, support loads and installation chainage; compare rates and loads within one ground domain without mixing readings at different excavation ages. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「支護安裝時點」的交付需回答：將相同開挖齡期的荷重及收斂放在同地質組比較。把安裝時間和量測資料一起交付支護設計者，任何級別變更都需地質及位移證據，不能憑單一瞬間讀值自行改支護。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Brenner Base Tunnel, the support activation time handover must address the following evidence: Compare loads and convergence at equal excavation age within one ground domain. Submit installation times with measurements to the support designer; class changes need both ground and movement evidence, not an isolated instantaneous reading.","failure":"注意干擾：跨地質平均參數會把真正局部擠壓訊號稀釋。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Averaging across geology dilutes genuine local squeezing signals. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b116-v14-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將相同開挖齡期的荷重及收斂放在同地質組比較。同步記錄收斂、支護荷重與安裝里程，比較同一地質分區內的速率及荷載，不將不同開挖齡期讀值直接混合。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Compare loads and convergence at equal excavation age within one ground domain. Synchronise convergence, support loads and installation chainage; compare rates and loads within one ground domain without mixing readings at different excavation ages. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]},{"id":"b116-v14-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「支護安裝時點」的交付需回答：將相同開挖齡期的荷重及收斂放在同地質組比較。把安裝時間和量測資料一起交付支護設計者，任何級別變更都需地質及位移證據，不能憑單一瞬間讀值自行改支護。","textEn":"For Brenner Base Tunnel, the support activation time handover must address the following evidence: Compare loads and convergence at equal excavation age within one ground domain. Submit installation times with measurements to the support designer; class changes need both ground and movement evidence, not an isolated instantaneous reading.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「支護啟動與變形容量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Support activation and deformation capacity\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","將相同開挖齡期的荷重及收斂放在同地質組比較。","岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Compare loads and convergence at equal excavation age within one ground domain.","Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow."],"answer":1,"explanation":"將相同開挖齡期的荷重及收斂放在同地質組比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare loads and convergence at equal excavation age within one ground domain. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b116-v14-20","title":"支護啟動與變形容量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Support activation and deformation capacity: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b116-v14-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「支護安裝時點」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Support activation time” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"跨地質平均參數會把真正局部擠壓訊號稀釋。過晚封閉會讓不可回復變形增加，過硬且行程不足的支護也可能脆裂，兩者都可能表現為裂縫而需不同處理。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Averaging across geology dilutes genuine local squeezing signals. Late closure increases irreversible movement, while excessively stiff support with little travel can fail brittly; both produce cracks but require different diagnoses. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：地盤反力與支護曲線必須連同掌子面距離及封閉順序理解；擠壓性地層還需保留變形容量，不能只追求高剛度與高材料強度。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Squeezing ground also needs deformation capacity; high stiffness and material strength alone do not guarantee a compatible support response.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b116-v14-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"跨地質平均參數會把真正局部擠壓訊號稀釋。過晚封閉會讓不可回復變形增加，過硬且行程不足的支護也可能脆裂，兩者都可能表現為裂縫而需不同處理。","textEn":"Averaging across geology dilutes genuine local squeezing signals. Late closure increases irreversible movement, while excessively stiff support with little travel can fail brittly; both produce cracks but require different diagnoses.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]},{"id":"b116-v14-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「支護啟動與變形容量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Support activation and deformation capacity\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。","跨地質平均參數會把真正局部擠壓訊號稀釋。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance.","Averaging across geology dilutes genuine local squeezing signals."],"answer":2,"explanation":"跨地質平均參數會把真正局部擠壓訊號稀釋。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Averaging across geology dilutes genuine local squeezing signals. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b116-v14-21","title":"掘進利用率與設備停時：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b116-v14-20"],"objective":"說明「有效掘進利用率」如何影響布倫納基線隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Effective boring utilisation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Brenner Base Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"布倫納多機多工作面背景適合比較利用率，教材按岩性和停時原因校正後才比較日進尺。TBM瞬時貫入率只描述刀盤切削的一段時間，拼裝、換刀、出渣與維修決定每天真正進尺。岩石強度與磨蝕性對刀具的影響不同，混合掌子面又產生不對稱作用；比較機器績效須按地質分區和停時原因分類，不能只排序最高進尺。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「有效掘進利用率」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Multiple machines and headings require comparisons normalised by ground and downtime cause before daily advance is ranked. Instantaneous penetration describes only active cutting; erection, cutter changes, muck handling and repairs determine daily advance. Strength and abrasivity affect cutters differently, while mixed faces impose asymmetric loading. Compare performance by ground domain and downtime cause, because the highest short-duration penetration rate can coexist with poor daily production and increased maintenance demand. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Effective boring utilisation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：切削速率=1.95 m/h；有效利用率=0.325 無因次。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: active penetration=1.95 m/h; utilisation=0.325 dimensionless.","failure":"常見誤解：「刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「有效掘進利用率」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Effective boring utilisation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b116-v14-21-k1","title":"掘進利用率與設備停時","titleEn":"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime","text":"布倫納多機多工作面背景適合比較利用率，教材按岩性和停時原因校正後才比較日進尺。TBM瞬時貫入率只描述刀盤切削的一段時間，拼裝、換刀、出渣與維修決定每天真正進尺。","textEn":"Multiple machines and headings require comparisons normalised by ground and downtime cause before daily advance is ranked. Instantaneous penetration describes only active cutting; erection, cutter changes, muck handling and repairs determine daily advance.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]},{"id":"b116-v14-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「掘進利用率與設備停時」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime\" is correct?","options":["布倫納多機多工作面背景適合比較利用率，教材按岩性和停時原因校正後才比較日進尺。","刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。","增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。"],"optionsEn":["Multiple machines and headings require comparisons normalised by ground and downtime cause before daily advance is ranked.","A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance.","Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly."],"answer":0,"explanation":"布倫納多機多工作面背景適合比較利用率，教材按岩性和停時原因校正後才比較日進尺。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Multiple machines and headings require comparisons normalised by ground and downtime cause before daily advance is ranked. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b116-v14-22","title":"掘進利用率與設備停時：定量估算","titleEn":"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b116-v14-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「有效掘進利用率」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Effective boring utilisation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：切削速率=1.95 m/h；有效利用率=0.325 無因次。D=24vu=15.21 m/day。僅把有效利用率增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為16.731 m/day。邊界：平均循環模型，未表示地質轉換及停機分布；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: active penetration=1.95 m/h; utilisation=0.325 dimensionless. D=24vu=15.21 m/day. Increasing only utilisation by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 16.731 m/day. Boundary: Mean-cycle model without ground transitions or downtime distribution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以完整班次重建切削、拼裝、保養和運輸時間帳。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Reconstruct cutting, erection, maintenance and transport over complete shifts.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b116-v14-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：切削速率=1.95 m/h；有效利用率=0.325 無因次。D=24vu=15.21 m/day。僅把有效利用率增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為16.731 m/day。邊界：平均循環模型，未表示地質轉換及停機分布；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: active penetration=1.95 m/h; utilisation=0.325 dimensionless. D=24vu=15.21 m/day. Increasing only utilisation by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 16.731 m/day. Boundary: Mean-cycle model without ground transitions or downtime distribution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]},{"id":"b116-v14-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「掘進利用率與設備停時」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime\", which statement holds?","options":["基線隧道坡度很小，所以不必做牽引與制動分析。","原創教學假設：切削速率=1.95 m/h；有效利用率=0.325 無因次。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["A small base-tunnel gradient eliminates the need for traction and braking analysis.","Original teaching assumptions: active penetration=1.95 m/h; utilisation=0.325 dimensionless.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：切削速率=1.95 m/h；有效利用率=0.325 無因次。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: active penetration=1.95 m/h; utilisation=0.325 dimensionless. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b116-v14-23","title":"掘進利用率與設備停時：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b116-v14-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「有效掘進利用率」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Effective boring utilisation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以完整班次重建切削、拼裝、保養和運輸時間帳。由時間戳分離切削、拼裝與故障，將刀具位置、磨耗量及推力扭矩對齊里程，檢查停時是否集中在特定地層。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Reconstruct cutting, erection, maintenance and transport over complete shifts. Separate cutting, erection and faults by timestamp; align cutter position, wear, thrust and torque with chainage and test clustering by ground type. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「有效掘進利用率」的交付需回答：以完整班次重建切削、拼裝、保養和運輸時間帳。停機紀錄使用可追溯原因碼，把地質變化與設備故障分開統計，參數調整只能在設備和施工團隊核准程序內進行。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Brenner Base Tunnel, the effective boring utilisation handover must address the following evidence: Reconstruct cutting, erection, maintenance and transport over complete shifts. Use traceable downtime codes, separating geological change from equipment faults; parameter changes stay within procedures approved by equipment and construction teams.","failure":"注意干擾：最佳機器日進尺不能直接代表整個工程平均產能。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: The best machine day does not represent project-average production. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b116-v14-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以完整班次重建切削、拼裝、保養和運輸時間帳。由時間戳分離切削、拼裝與故障，將刀具位置、磨耗量及推力扭矩對齊里程，檢查停時是否集中在特定地層。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Reconstruct cutting, erection, maintenance and transport over complete shifts. Separate cutting, erection and faults by timestamp; align cutter position, wear, thrust and torque with chainage and test clustering by ground type. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]},{"id":"b116-v14-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「有效掘進利用率」的交付需回答：以完整班次重建切削、拼裝、保養和運輸時間帳。停機紀錄使用可追溯原因碼，把地質變化與設備故障分開統計，參數調整只能在設備和施工團隊核准程序內進行。","textEn":"For Brenner Base Tunnel, the effective boring utilisation handover must address the following evidence: Reconstruct cutting, erection, maintenance and transport over complete shifts. Use traceable downtime codes, separating geological change from equipment faults; parameter changes stay within procedures approved by equipment and construction teams.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「掘進利用率與設備停時」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。","以完整班次重建切削、拼裝、保養和運輸時間帳。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.","Reconstruct cutting, erection, maintenance and transport over complete shifts."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以完整班次重建切削、拼裝、保養和運輸時間帳。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Reconstruct cutting, erection, maintenance and transport over complete shifts. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b116-v14-24","title":"掘進利用率與設備停時：失效診斷","titleEn":"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b116-v14-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「有效掘進利用率」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Effective boring utilisation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"最佳機器日進尺不能直接代表整個工程平均產能。只提高瞬時進尺可能使出渣或刀具超出有效工況，短暫改善後增加停機，平均進尺和零件壽命反而下降。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"The best machine day does not represent project-average production. Higher instantaneous advance can overload cutters or muck transport and create longer stoppages that reduce average progress and component life. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：岩石強度與磨蝕性對刀具的影響不同，混合掌子面又產生不對稱作用；比較機器績效須按地質分區和停時原因分類，不能只排序最高進尺。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Compare performance by ground domain and downtime cause, because the highest short-duration penetration rate can coexist with poor daily production and increased maintenance demand.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b116-v14-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"最佳機器日進尺不能直接代表整個工程平均產能。只提高瞬時進尺可能使出渣或刀具超出有效工況，短暫改善後增加停機，平均進尺和零件壽命反而下降。","textEn":"The best machine day does not represent project-average production. Higher instantaneous advance can overload cutters or muck transport and create longer stoppages that reduce average progress and component life.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]},{"id":"b116-v14-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「掘進利用率與設備停時」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["最佳機器日進尺不能直接代表整個工程平均產能。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。"],"optionsEn":["The best machine day does not represent project-average production.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly."],"answer":0,"explanation":"最佳機器日進尺不能直接代表整個工程平均產能。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"The best machine day does not represent project-average production. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b116-v14-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」與「控制網與貫通誤差」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Shared access and transport bottlenecks\" and \"Control network and breakthrough error\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b116-v14-25","title":"共享通道與運輸瓶頸：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Shared access and transport bottlenecks: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b116-v14-24"],"objective":"說明「出渣運輸節拍」如何影響布倫納基線隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Muck-transport cycle” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Brenner Base Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"側向施工入口和先進坑共用運輸網，教材研究一個出渣節點故障如何影響多工作面。多工作面只有在供電、通風、出渣與材料供應同步充足時才增加總產量。共用豎井或軌道形成串聯瓶頸，排隊和維修窗口會降低名目容量；緩衝區太大又可能侵占通行與救援空間，因此不能單純把各面產能相加。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「出渣運輸節拍」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Side accesses and exploratory galleries form a shared network; examine how one spoil-node outage propagates to several headings. Multiple headings increase output only when power, air, muck transport and materials support them together. Shared shafts or railways become serial bottlenecks, while queues and maintenance reduce nominal capacity. Large buffers may obstruct personnel and rescue access, so face capacities cannot simply be added without a network-level transport and storage check. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Muck-transport cycle” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=35 t；往返週期=36 min。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=35 t; cycle=36 min.","failure":"常見誤解：「增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「出渣運輸節拍」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Muck-transport cycle”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b116-v14-25-k1","title":"共享通道與運輸瓶頸","titleEn":"Shared access and transport bottlenecks","text":"側向施工入口和先進坑共用運輸網，教材研究一個出渣節點故障如何影響多工作面。多工作面只有在供電、通風、出渣與材料供應同步充足時才增加總產量。","textEn":"Side accesses and exploratory galleries form a shared network; examine how one spoil-node outage propagates to several headings. Multiple headings increase output only when power, air, muck transport and materials support them together.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]},{"id":"b116-v14-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Shared access and transport bottlenecks\" is correct?","options":["增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。","側向施工入口和先進坑共用運輸網，教材研究一個出渣節點故障如何影響多工作面。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.","Side accesses and exploratory galleries form a shared network; examine how one spoil-node outage propagates to several headings.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error."],"answer":1,"explanation":"側向施工入口和先進坑共用運輸網，教材研究一個出渣節點故障如何影響多工作面。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Side accesses and exploratory galleries form a shared network; examine how one spoil-node outage propagates to several headings. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b116-v14-26","title":"共享通道與運輸瓶頸：定量估算","titleEn":"Shared access and transport bottlenecks: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b116-v14-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「出渣運輸節拍」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Muck-transport cycle” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=35 t；往返週期=36 min。C=N payload 60/T=233.333 t/h。僅把往返週期增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為212.121 t/h。邊界：無排隊理想循環，並非共享路段實際產能；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=35 t; cycle=36 min. C=N payload 60/T=233.333 t/h. Increasing only cycle by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 212.121 t/h. Boundary: Ideal cycle without queues, not actual shared-route production. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用排隊時間和緩衝存量找出串聯瓶頸。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Identify serial bottlenecks from queue time and buffer inventory.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b116-v14-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=35 t；往返週期=36 min。C=N payload 60/T=233.333 t/h。僅把往返週期增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為212.121 t/h。邊界：無排隊理想循環，並非共享路段實際產能；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=35 t; cycle=36 min. C=N payload 60/T=233.333 t/h. Increasing only cycle by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 212.121 t/h. Boundary: Ideal cycle without queues, not actual shared-route production. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]},{"id":"b116-v14-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Shared access and transport bottlenecks\", which statement holds?","options":["全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。","岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。","原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=35 t；往返週期=36 min。"],"optionsEn":["Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.","Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow.","Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=35 t; cycle=36 min."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=35 t；往返週期=36 min。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=35 t; cycle=36 min. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b116-v14-27","title":"共享通道與運輸瓶頸：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Shared access and transport bottlenecks: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b116-v14-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「出渣運輸節拍」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Muck-transport cycle” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用排隊時間和緩衝存量找出串聯瓶頸。以裝載質量、往返時間及排隊時間重建物流曲線，再核對緩衝占用、共用通道優先權與維修時段。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Identify serial bottlenecks from queue time and buffer inventory. Reconstruct flow from payload, round-trip and queue times, then check buffer occupancy, shared-route priorities and maintenance periods. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「出渣運輸節拍」的交付需回答：用排隊時間和緩衝存量找出串聯瓶頸。每日排程同時標示人員、材料和維修的占用時段，任何物流改線先檢查通風與應變通道，不能只看運量提升。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Brenner Base Tunnel, the muck-transport cycle handover must address the following evidence: Identify serial bottlenecks from queue time and buffer inventory. Schedules show personnel, materials and maintenance occupancy together; rerouting first checks ventilation and emergency access rather than only throughput gains.","failure":"注意干擾：各面名目產量相加會忽略共同卸料設備的容量。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Summed face ratings omit capacity of shared unloading equipment. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b116-v14-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用排隊時間和緩衝存量找出串聯瓶頸。以裝載質量、往返時間及排隊時間重建物流曲線，再核對緩衝占用、共用通道優先權與維修時段。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Identify serial bottlenecks from queue time and buffer inventory. Reconstruct flow from payload, round-trip and queue times, then check buffer occupancy, shared-route priorities and maintenance periods. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]},{"id":"b116-v14-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「出渣運輸節拍」的交付需回答：用排隊時間和緩衝存量找出串聯瓶頸。每日排程同時標示人員、材料和維修的占用時段，任何物流改線先檢查通風與應變通道，不能只看運量提升。","textEn":"For Brenner Base Tunnel, the muck-transport cycle handover must address the following evidence: Identify serial bottlenecks from queue time and buffer inventory. Schedules show personnel, materials and maintenance occupancy together; rerouting first checks ventilation and emergency access rather than only throughput gains.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Shared access and transport bottlenecks\"?","options":["用排隊時間和緩衝存量找出串聯瓶頸。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。"],"optionsEn":["Identify serial bottlenecks from queue time and buffer inventory.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction."],"answer":0,"explanation":"用排隊時間和緩衝存量找出串聯瓶頸。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Identify serial bottlenecks from queue time and buffer inventory. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b116-v14-28","title":"共享通道與運輸瓶頸：失效診斷","titleEn":"Shared access and transport bottlenecks: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b116-v14-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「出渣運輸節拍」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Muck-transport cycle” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"各面名目產量相加會忽略共同卸料設備的容量。把理想往返時間當全天常數會忽略交會等待與卸料堵塞，導致工作面停工或把材料堆入必要通道。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Summed face ratings omit capacity of shared unloading equipment. Treating an ideal cycle as constant all day misses passing delays and unloading blockages, stopping headings or pushing material into essential access space. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：共用豎井或軌道形成串聯瓶頸，排隊和維修窗口會降低名目容量；緩衝區太大又可能侵占通行與救援空間，因此不能單純把各面產能相加。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Large buffers may obstruct personnel and rescue access, so face capacities cannot simply be added without a network-level transport and storage check.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b116-v14-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"各面名目產量相加會忽略共同卸料設備的容量。把理想往返時間當全天常數會忽略交會等待與卸料堵塞，導致工作面停工或把材料堆入必要通道。","textEn":"Summed face ratings omit capacity of shared unloading equipment. Treating an ideal cycle as constant all day misses passing delays and unloading blockages, stopping headings or pushing material into essential access space.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]},{"id":"b116-v14-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Shared access and transport bottlenecks\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","各面名目產量相加會忽略共同卸料設備的容量。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Summed face ratings omit capacity of shared unloading equipment.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error."],"answer":1,"explanation":"各面名目產量相加會忽略共同卸料設備的容量。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Summed face ratings omit capacity of shared unloading equipment. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b116-v14-29","title":"控制網與貫通誤差：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b116-v14-28"],"objective":"說明「方向角誤差」如何影響布倫納基線隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Orientation error” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Brenner Base Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"跨境兩端控制網需統一坐標尺度與高程，布倫納教材特別檢查地表到深部基準傳遞。長隧道的微小方向誤差會沿距離累積，地下控制網又缺少直接衛星定位，必須把地表基準可靠傳到洞內。閉合差很小不代表無系統誤差；尺度、折光、儀器定向與高程基準可能共同偏移，誤差相關性也使平方和估算失真。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「方向角誤差」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Cross-border networks require common scale and elevation, with explicit checks on transfer from surface to depth. Small orientation errors accumulate over long drives, while underground networks lack direct satellite positioning and depend on transferring surface control. A small closure does not exclude systematic bias: scale, refraction, orientation and vertical datum may shift together. Correlated errors also invalidate a naive root-sum-square combination of supposedly independent observations. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Orientation error” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：控制長度=4800 m；方向偏角=2.7 arcsec。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: control length=4800 m; orientation error=2.7 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0628319 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「方向角誤差」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Orientation error”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b116-v14-29-k1","title":"控制網與貫通誤差","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error","text":"跨境兩端控制網需統一坐標尺度與高程，布倫納教材特別檢查地表到深部基準傳遞。長隧道的微小方向誤差會沿距離累積，地下控制網又缺少直接衛星定位，必須把地表基準可靠傳到洞內。","textEn":"Cross-border networks require common scale and elevation, with explicit checks on transfer from surface to depth. Small orientation errors accumulate over long drives, while underground networks lack direct satellite positioning and depend on transferring surface control.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]},{"id":"b116-v14-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「控制網與貫通誤差」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Control network and breakthrough error\" is correct?","options":["兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。","基線隧道坡度很小，所以不必做牽引與制動分析。","跨境兩端控制網需統一坐標尺度與高程，布倫納教材特別檢查地表到深部基準傳遞。"],"optionsEn":["Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.","A small base-tunnel gradient eliminates the need for traction and braking analysis.","Cross-border networks require common scale and elevation, with explicit checks on transfer from surface to depth."],"answer":2,"explanation":"跨境兩端控制網需統一坐標尺度與高程，布倫納教材特別檢查地表到深部基準傳遞。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Cross-border networks require common scale and elevation, with explicit checks on transfer from surface to depth. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b116-v14-30","title":"控制網與貫通誤差：定量估算","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b116-v14-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「方向角誤差」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Orientation error” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：控制長度=4800 m；方向偏角=2.7 arcsec。e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0628319 m。僅把方向偏角增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.069115 m。邊界：小角度方向偏差，未加入控制網相關性及折光；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: control length=4800 m; orientation error=2.7 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0628319 m. Increasing only orientation error by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.069115 m. Boundary: Small-angle orientation error without network correlation or refraction. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：由獨立網重算尺度及定向，保留溫度改正資料。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Recompute scale and orientation independently and retain thermal corrections.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b116-v14-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：控制長度=4800 m；方向偏角=2.7 arcsec。e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0628319 m。僅把方向偏角增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.069115 m。邊界：小角度方向偏差，未加入控制網相關性及折光；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: control length=4800 m; orientation error=2.7 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0628319 m. Increasing only orientation error by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.069115 m. Boundary: Small-angle orientation error without network correlation or refraction. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]},{"id":"b116-v14-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「控制網與貫通誤差」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Control network and breakthrough error\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：控制長度=4800 m；方向偏角=2.7 arcsec。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。","目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: control length=4800 m; orientation error=2.7 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0628319 m.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.","No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：控制長度=4800 m；方向偏角=2.7 arcsec。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: control length=4800 m; orientation error=2.7 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0628319 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b116-v14-31","title":"控制網與貫通誤差：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b116-v14-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「方向角誤差」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Orientation error” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"由獨立網重算尺度及定向，保留溫度改正資料。由獨立測量組複核地表到洞內的轉換，保留原始角距及溫度資料，用不同控制線比較方向與高程偏差。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Recompute scale and orientation independently and retain thermal corrections. Independently check surface-to-tunnel transformations, retain raw angles, distances and temperatures, and compare orientation and elevation through separate control routes. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「方向角誤差」的交付需回答：由獨立網重算尺度及定向，保留溫度改正資料。貫通前凍結座標、尺度與高程版本，獨立組直接使用原始觀測重算；不得只傳遞整理好的坐標而遺失校正資訊。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Brenner Base Tunnel, the orientation error handover must address the following evidence: Recompute scale and orientation independently and retain thermal corrections. Freeze coordinate, scale and height revisions before breakthrough; independent reviewers recompute raw observations rather than receiving only adjusted coordinates without corrections.","failure":"注意干擾：同一轉換參數用錯可讓兩國網各自閉合卻整體錯接。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A wrong shared transformation permits local closure but a global mismatch. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b116-v14-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"由獨立網重算尺度及定向，保留溫度改正資料。由獨立測量組複核地表到洞內的轉換，保留原始角距及溫度資料，用不同控制線比較方向與高程偏差。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Recompute scale and orientation independently and retain thermal corrections. Independently check surface-to-tunnel transformations, retain raw angles, distances and temperatures, and compare orientation and elevation through separate control routes. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]},{"id":"b116-v14-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「方向角誤差」的交付需回答：由獨立網重算尺度及定向，保留溫度改正資料。貫通前凍結座標、尺度與高程版本，獨立組直接使用原始觀測重算；不得只傳遞整理好的坐標而遺失校正資訊。","textEn":"For Brenner Base Tunnel, the orientation error handover must address the following evidence: Recompute scale and orientation independently and retain thermal corrections. Freeze coordinate, scale and height revisions before breakthrough; independent reviewers recompute raw observations rather than receiving only adjusted coordinates without corrections.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「控制網與貫通誤差」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Control network and breakthrough error\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","由獨立網重算尺度及定向，保留溫度改正資料。","支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Recompute scale and orientation independently and retain thermal corrections.","Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem."],"answer":1,"explanation":"由獨立網重算尺度及定向，保留溫度改正資料。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Recompute scale and orientation independently and retain thermal corrections. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b116-v14-32","title":"控制網與貫通誤差：失效診斷","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b116-v14-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「方向角誤差」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Orientation error” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"同一轉換參數用錯可讓兩國網各自閉合卻整體錯接。共用錯誤基準可能讓兩組測量同時看似一致，直到貫通或軌道銜接才發現系統偏差，修正成本遠高於早期複核。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A wrong shared transformation permits local closure but a global mismatch. A shared wrong datum can make separate surveys appear consistent until breakthrough or track connection exposes bias that is costly to correct. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：閉合差很小不代表無系統誤差；尺度、折光、儀器定向與高程基準可能共同偏移，誤差相關性也使平方和估算失真。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Correlated errors also invalidate a naive root-sum-square combination of supposedly independent observations.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b116-v14-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"同一轉換參數用錯可讓兩國網各自閉合卻整體錯接。共用錯誤基準可能讓兩組測量同時看似一致，直到貫通或軌道銜接才發現系統偏差，修正成本遠高於早期複核。","textEn":"A wrong shared transformation permits local closure but a global mismatch. A shared wrong datum can make separate surveys appear consistent until breakthrough or track connection exposes bias that is costly to correct.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]},{"id":"b116-v14-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「控制網與貫通誤差」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Control network and breakthrough error\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","基線隧道坡度很小，所以不必做牽引與制動分析。","同一轉換參數用錯可讓兩國網各自閉合卻整體錯接。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","A small base-tunnel gradient eliminates the need for traction and braking analysis.","A wrong shared transformation permits local closure but a global mismatch."],"answer":2,"explanation":"同一轉換參數用錯可讓兩國網各自閉合卻整體錯接。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A wrong shared transformation permits local closure but a global mismatch. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b116-v14-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「基線縱坡與牽引需求」與「資產編碼與可追溯交接」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Base-alignment grade and traction demand\" and \"Asset identity and traceable handover\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b116-v14-33","title":"基線縱坡與牽引需求：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Base-alignment grade and traction demand: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b116-v14-32"],"objective":"說明「坡度阻力功率」如何影響布倫納基線隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Grade-resistance power” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Brenner Base Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"低坡度是布倫納運輸目的之一，教材計算坡度功率後另外列出加速、氣動與列車間距需求。基線鐵路用較小縱坡降低重載列車的重力阻力，但仍有滾動、空氣阻力及加速需求。土建線形和供電容量必須使用同一列車與速度情境，短距陡坡也不能被平均坡度掩蓋；制動方向的能量處理則是另一個需要獨立檢核的工況。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「坡度阻力功率」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Low gradient supports the transport purpose; calculate grade power while separately listing acceleration, aerodynamics and spacing demands. A base alignment reduces heavy-train gravity resistance through gentler gradients, but rolling resistance, aerodynamic drag and acceleration remain. Civil geometry and power capacity must use consistent train and speed cases. Short steep sections cannot be hidden in an average gradient, while braking energy in the opposite direction requires its own operating and electrical assessment. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Grade-resistance power” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：列車質量=1.5e+06 kg；縱坡=0.0066 無因次；速度=20 m/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: train mass=1.5e+06 kg; grade=0.0066 dimensionless; speed=20 m/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「基線隧道坡度很小，所以不必做牽引與制動分析。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A small base-tunnel gradient eliminates the need for traction and braking analysis.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「坡度阻力功率」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Grade-resistance power”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b116-v14-33-k1","title":"基線縱坡與牽引需求","titleEn":"Base-alignment grade and traction demand","text":"低坡度是布倫納運輸目的之一，教材計算坡度功率後另外列出加速、氣動與列車間距需求。基線鐵路用較小縱坡降低重載列車的重力阻力，但仍有滾動、空氣阻力及加速需求。","textEn":"Low gradient supports the transport purpose; calculate grade power while separately listing acceleration, aerodynamics and spacing demands. A base alignment reduces heavy-train gravity resistance through gentler gradients, but rolling resistance, aerodynamic drag and acceleration remain.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]},{"id":"b116-v14-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：基線隧道坡度很小，所以不必做牽引與制動分析。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A small base-tunnel gradient eliminates the need for traction and braking analysis. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「基線縱坡與牽引需求」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Base-alignment grade and traction demand\" is correct?","options":["低坡度是布倫納運輸目的之一，教材計算坡度功率後另外列出加速、氣動與列車間距需求。","基線隧道坡度很小，所以不必做牽引與制動分析。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。"],"optionsEn":["Low gradient supports the transport purpose; calculate grade power while separately listing acceleration, aerodynamics and spacing demands.","A small base-tunnel gradient eliminates the need for traction and braking analysis.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted."],"answer":0,"explanation":"低坡度是布倫納運輸目的之一，教材計算坡度功率後另外列出加速、氣動與列車間距需求。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Low gradient supports the transport purpose; calculate grade power while separately listing acceleration, aerodynamics and spacing demands. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b116-v14-34","title":"基線縱坡與牽引需求：定量估算","titleEn":"Base-alignment grade and traction demand: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b116-v14-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「坡度阻力功率」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Grade-resistance power” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：列車質量=1.5e+06 kg；縱坡=0.0066 無因次；速度=20 m/s。P=mgiv/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=1942.38 kW。僅把縱坡增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為2136.62 kW。邊界：僅坡度阻力，不含滾動、氣動、加速及效率；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: train mass=1.5e+06 kg; grade=0.0066 dimensionless; speed=20 m/s. P=mgiv/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=1942.38 kW. Increasing only grade by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 2136.62 kW. Boundary: Grade resistance only, excluding rolling, aerodynamic, acceleration and efficiency losses. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對坡度無因次換算及列車質量，再比同速方案。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check dimensionless grade conversion and mass before equal-speed comparison.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b116-v14-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：列車質量=1.5e+06 kg；縱坡=0.0066 無因次；速度=20 m/s。P=mgiv/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=1942.38 kW。僅把縱坡增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為2136.62 kW。邊界：僅坡度阻力，不含滾動、氣動、加速及效率；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: train mass=1.5e+06 kg; grade=0.0066 dimensionless; speed=20 m/s. P=mgiv/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=1942.38 kW. Increasing only grade by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 2136.62 kW. Boundary: Grade resistance only, excluding rolling, aerodynamic, acceleration and efficiency losses. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]},{"id":"b116-v14-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「基線縱坡與牽引需求」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Base-alignment grade and traction demand\", which statement holds?","options":["岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。","原創教學假設：列車質量=1.5e+06 kg；縱坡=0.0066 無因次；速度=20 m/s。","知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。"],"optionsEn":["Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow.","Original teaching assumptions: train mass=1.5e+06 kg; grade=0.0066 dimensionless; speed=20 m/s.","Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：列車質量=1.5e+06 kg；縱坡=0.0066 無因次；速度=20 m/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: train mass=1.5e+06 kg; grade=0.0066 dimensionless; speed=20 m/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b116-v14-35","title":"基線縱坡與牽引需求：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Base-alignment grade and traction demand: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b116-v14-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「坡度阻力功率」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Grade-resistance power” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對坡度無因次換算及列車質量，再比同速方案。以里程高程表逐段計算坡度，對照列車性能曲線和供電模型，另檢核低速牽引及下坡制動，不只比較平均功率。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check dimensionless grade conversion and mass before equal-speed comparison. Calculate local grades from chainage and elevation, compare with train-performance and power models, and separately check low-speed traction and downhill braking. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「坡度阻力功率」的交付需回答：核對坡度無因次換算及列車質量，再比同速方案。軌頂高程交付前，由土建、軌道、供電和營運共同確認同版線形及列車包絡，變更坡度時同步更新性能與容量計算。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Brenner Base Tunnel, the grade-resistance power handover must address the following evidence: Check dimensionless grade conversion and mass before equal-speed comparison. Civil, track, power and operations teams approve one alignment and train envelope before handover; grade changes update both performance and capacity calculations.","failure":"注意干擾：把千分比當百分比會使坡度功率放大十倍。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Confusing per mille with percent multiplies grade power by ten. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b116-v14-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對坡度無因次換算及列車質量，再比同速方案。以里程高程表逐段計算坡度，對照列車性能曲線和供電模型，另檢核低速牽引及下坡制動，不只比較平均功率。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Check dimensionless grade conversion and mass before equal-speed comparison. Calculate local grades from chainage and elevation, compare with train-performance and power models, and separately check low-speed traction and downhill braking. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]},{"id":"b116-v14-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「坡度阻力功率」的交付需回答：核對坡度無因次換算及列車質量，再比同速方案。軌頂高程交付前，由土建、軌道、供電和營運共同確認同版線形及列車包絡，變更坡度時同步更新性能與容量計算。","textEn":"For Brenner Base Tunnel, the grade-resistance power handover must address the following evidence: Check dimensionless grade conversion and mass before equal-speed comparison. Civil, track, power and operations teams approve one alignment and train envelope before handover; grade changes update both performance and capacity calculations.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「基線縱坡與牽引需求」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Base-alignment grade and traction demand\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。","核對坡度無因次換算及列車質量，再比同速方案。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance.","Check dimensionless grade conversion and mass before equal-speed comparison."],"answer":2,"explanation":"核對坡度無因次換算及列車質量，再比同速方案。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check dimensionless grade conversion and mass before equal-speed comparison. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b116-v14-36","title":"基線縱坡與牽引需求：失效診斷","titleEn":"Base-alignment grade and traction demand: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b116-v14-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「坡度阻力功率」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Grade-resistance power” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把千分比當百分比會使坡度功率放大十倍。平均坡度低卻存在短陡坡時，峰值功率可能超過預估，速度下降又會增加區段占用時間，牽連營運容量。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Confusing per mille with percent multiplies grade power by ten. A short steep grade can exceed power estimates despite a low average, reducing speed and extending block occupation with capacity consequences. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：土建線形和供電容量必須使用同一列車與速度情境，短距陡坡也不能被平均坡度掩蓋；制動方向的能量處理則是另一個需要獨立檢核的工況。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Short steep sections cannot be hidden in an average gradient, while braking energy in the opposite direction requires its own operating and electrical assessment.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「基線隧道坡度很小，所以不必做牽引與制動分析。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A small base-tunnel gradient eliminates the need for traction and braking analysis.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b116-v14-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把千分比當百分比會使坡度功率放大十倍。平均坡度低卻存在短陡坡時，峰值功率可能超過預估，速度下降又會增加區段占用時間，牽連營運容量。","textEn":"Confusing per mille with percent multiplies grade power by ten. A short steep grade can exceed power estimates despite a low average, reducing speed and extending block occupation with capacity consequences.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]},{"id":"b116-v14-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「基線縱坡與牽引需求」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Base-alignment grade and traction demand\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["把千分比當百分比會使坡度功率放大十倍。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。"],"optionsEn":["Confusing per mille with percent multiplies grade power by ten.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted."],"answer":0,"explanation":"把千分比當百分比會使坡度功率放大十倍。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Confusing per mille with percent multiplies grade power by ten. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b116-v14-37","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b116-v14-36"],"objective":"說明「資產資料完整度」如何影響布倫納基線隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Asset-record completeness” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Brenner Base Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"先進坑由調查轉為維護用途時，資料需保留地質與設備兩種索引，避免施工資料在營運期失聯。地下設備的竣工資料必須讓維護人員找到正確位置、材料批次和控制版本。只有上傳圖面而沒有變更歷程，無法分辨元件替換與真正劣化；告警、儀器、線路及工單使用一致識別碼，才可能把量測趨勢連回實際受力或水力系統。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「資產資料完整度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"As the exploratory gallery gains a maintenance role, preserve both geological and equipment indexing through handover. Handover must let maintainers find the correct location, material batch and control revision. Drawings without change history cannot distinguish replacement from deterioration. Consistent identifiers across alarms, instruments, circuits and work orders are essential for linking trends to the physical structural or hydraulic system instead of treating each record as an isolated file. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Asset-record completeness” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：設備總數=115 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: asset count=115 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=86.087 %.","failure":"常見誤解：「全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「資產資料完整度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Asset-record completeness”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b116-v14-37-k1","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover","text":"先進坑由調查轉為維護用途時，資料需保留地質與設備兩種索引，避免施工資料在營運期失聯。地下設備的竣工資料必須讓維護人員找到正確位置、材料批次和控制版本。","textEn":"As the exploratory gallery gains a maintenance role, preserve both geological and equipment indexing through handover. Handover must let maintainers find the correct location, material batch and control revision.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]},{"id":"b116-v14-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「資產編碼與可追溯交接」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Asset identity and traceable handover\" is correct?","options":["全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。","先進坑由調查轉為維護用途時，資料需保留地質與設備兩種索引，避免施工資料在營運期失聯。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.","As the exploratory gallery gains a maintenance role, preserve both geological and equipment indexing through handover.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":1,"explanation":"先進坑由調查轉為維護用途時，資料需保留地質與設備兩種索引，避免施工資料在營運期失聯。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"As the exploratory gallery gains a maintenance role, preserve both geological and equipment indexing through handover. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b116-v14-38","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：定量估算","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b116-v14-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「資產資料完整度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Asset-record completeness” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：設備總數=115 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。coverage=100(N−missing)/N=86.087 %。僅把缺紀錄數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為84.6957 %。邊界：資料完整度，不等於安全或可靠度；擾動為連續敏感度，實際個數為整數；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: asset count=115 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=86.087 %. Increasing only missing records by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 84.6957 %. Boundary: Record completeness, not safety or reliability; perturbation is continuous sensitivity while actual counts are integers. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：從維修位置反查該里程探查、支護和排水紀錄。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Trace a maintenance location back to investigation, support and drainage records.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b116-v14-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：設備總數=115 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。coverage=100(N−missing)/N=86.087 %。僅把缺紀錄數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為84.6957 %。邊界：資料完整度，不等於安全或可靠度；擾動為連續敏感度，實際個數為整數；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: asset count=115 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=86.087 %. Increasing only missing records by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 84.6957 %. Boundary: Record completeness, not safety or reliability; perturbation is continuous sensitivity while actual counts are integers. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]},{"id":"b116-v14-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「資產編碼與可追溯交接」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Asset identity and traceable handover\", which statement holds?","options":["目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。","支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。","原創教學假設：設備總數=115 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。"],"optionsEn":["No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.","Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem.","Original teaching assumptions: asset count=115 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=86.087 %."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：設備總數=115 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: asset count=115 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=86.087 %. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b116-v14-39","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b116-v14-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「資產資料完整度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Asset-record completeness” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"從維修位置反查該里程探查、支護和排水紀錄。抽取一條告警，從控制畫面追到設備、線路、圖面和工單，核對位置、版本及校正日期並記錄無法閉合的欄位。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Trace a maintenance location back to investigation, support and drainage records. Trace a sampled alarm from screen to equipment, circuit, drawing and work order, checking location, revision and calibration dates and recording broken links. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「資產資料完整度」的交付需回答：從維修位置反查該里程探查、支護和排水紀錄。交接以可完成的定位、查找與復原任務驗證，由維護責任人確認現場可用性；完整度只是資料指標，不代表結構安全或設備可靠。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Brenner Base Tunnel, the asset-record completeness handover must address the following evidence: Trace a maintenance location back to investigation, support and drainage records. Validate handover through achievable location, retrieval and recovery tasks witnessed by maintainers; completeness measures records, not structural safety or equipment reliability.","failure":"注意干擾：只有設備清單而缺地質里程連結會妨礙異常水量診斷。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: An asset list without geological chainage linkage impedes abnormal-inflow diagnosis. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b116-v14-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"從維修位置反查該里程探查、支護和排水紀錄。抽取一條告警，從控制畫面追到設備、線路、圖面和工單，核對位置、版本及校正日期並記錄無法閉合的欄位。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Trace a maintenance location back to investigation, support and drainage records. Trace a sampled alarm from screen to equipment, circuit, drawing and work order, checking location, revision and calibration dates and recording broken links. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]},{"id":"b116-v14-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「資產資料完整度」的交付需回答：從維修位置反查該里程探查、支護和排水紀錄。交接以可完成的定位、查找與復原任務驗證，由維護責任人確認現場可用性；完整度只是資料指標，不代表結構安全或設備可靠。","textEn":"For Brenner Base Tunnel, the asset-record completeness handover must address the following evidence: Trace a maintenance location back to investigation, support and drainage records. Validate handover through achievable location, retrieval and recovery tasks witnessed by maintainers; completeness measures records, not structural safety or equipment reliability.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「資產編碼與可追溯交接」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Asset identity and traceable handover\"?","options":["從維修位置反查該里程探查、支護和排水紀錄。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。"],"optionsEn":["Trace a maintenance location back to investigation, support and drainage records.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly."],"answer":0,"explanation":"從維修位置反查該里程探查、支護和排水紀錄。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Trace a maintenance location back to investigation, support and drainage records. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b116-v14-40","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：失效診斷","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b116-v14-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「資產資料完整度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Asset-record completeness” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只有設備清單而缺地質里程連結會妨礙異常水量診斷。設備改名卻未更新控制畫面會引導人員隔離錯誤回路，材料批次缺漏則使同批缺陷無法追蹤到其他位置。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"An asset list without geological chainage linkage impedes abnormal-inflow diagnosis. Renaming an asset without updating the screen can isolate the wrong circuit; missing material batches prevent tracing related defects at other locations. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：只有上傳圖面而沒有變更歷程，無法分辨元件替換與真正劣化；告警、儀器、線路及工單使用一致識別碼，才可能把量測趨勢連回實際受力或水力系統。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Consistent identifiers across alarms, instruments, circuits and work orders are essential for linking trends to the physical structural or hydraulic system instead of treating each record as an isolated file.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b116-v14-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只有設備清單而缺地質里程連結會妨礙異常水量診斷。設備改名卻未更新控制畫面會引導人員隔離錯誤回路，材料批次缺漏則使同批缺陷無法追蹤到其他位置。","textEn":"An asset list without geological chainage linkage impedes abnormal-inflow diagnosis. Renaming an asset without updating the screen can isolate the wrong circuit; missing material batches prevent tracing related defects at other locations.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]},{"id":"b116-v14-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「資產編碼與可追溯交接」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Asset identity and traceable handover\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","只有設備清單而缺地質里程連結會妨礙異常水量診斷。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","An asset list without geological chainage linkage impedes abnormal-inflow diagnosis.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":1,"explanation":"只有設備清單而缺地質里程連結會妨礙異常水量診斷。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"An asset list without geological chainage linkage impedes abnormal-inflow diagnosis. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b116","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b116-history"],"curriculumVersion":14,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000},{"id":"b117","title":"新武界引水隧道","titleEn":"New Wujie water-conveyance tunnel","category":"underground","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"台電典藏說明新武界及栗栖溪引水工程的規劃與施工，列16.5公里引水範圍及其中6.5公里TBM中段，記錄2002年該掘進段貫通。本課把土木、地質與水力目的串接，研究水路能量、探查代表性、支護和施工物流；這些尺度不被混寫成單一孔全長或發電容量。","summaryEn":"Taipower describes planning and construction for New Wujie and Lixi conveyance, including a 16.5 km scope and a 6.5 km TBM middle section that broke through in 2002. This course connects civil, geological and hydraulic purposes through energy, investigation, support and logistics, without confusing those scopes with one bore length or generating capacity.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"ug-landmarks","subcategoryTitle":"世界隧道與地下巨作","subcategoryTitleEn":"World tunnels and underground landmarks","learningTrack":"underground","learningSubdiscipline":"ug-landmarks","learningTags":["underground","ug-landmarks","tunnel"],"architectureFamily":"tunnel","architectureNodes":[["水體平流時間","Water advection time"],["破碎帶連通性","Fault-zone connectivity"],["有效掘進利用率","Effective boring utilisation"],["滿管沿程損失","Full-pipe friction loss"],["方向角誤差","Orientation error"],["邊界水量差","Boundary water-balance residual"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,5],[1,5]],"diagram":{"type":"tunnel","labels":["水體平流時間","破碎帶連通性","有效掘進利用率","滿管沿程損失","方向角誤差"],"labelsEn":["Water advection time","Fault-zone connectivity","Effective boring utilisation","Full-pipe friction loss","Orientation error"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"原創綜合審查：先計算「破碎帶連通與預報更新」，再獨立計算「輸水摩阻與瞬變邊界」。原創教學假設：滲透係數=2e-06 m/s；水力坡降=2.1 無因次；通水面積=360 m²。Q=k i A=0.001512 m³/s。僅把滲透係數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.0016632 m³/s。邊界：均質飽和達西流，不代表裂隙集中流；不是本工程實測或允收值。原創教學假設：達西因子=0.02 無因次；長度=1800 m；直徑=4 m；流速=2 m/s。hf=f(L/D)v²/(2g), g=9.81 m/s²=1.83486 m。僅把流速增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為2.22018 m。邊界：滿管穩態摩阻，不含水錘與局部損失；不是本工程實測或允收值。兩組結果的單位與邊界不同，不能直接相加。請列出一項缺少的現場輸入，說明它會影響哪個結論，以及哪種獨立量測可以縮小不確定度。","textEn":"Original integrated review: first calculate fault connectivity and forecast updating, then independently calculate conveyance friction and transient boundaries. Original teaching assumptions: conductivity=2e-06 m/s; hydraulic gradient=2.1 dimensionless; flow area=360 m². Q=k i A=0.001512 m³/s. Increasing only conductivity by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.0016632 m³/s. Boundary: Homogeneous saturated Darcy flow, not concentrated fracture flow. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.02 dimensionless; length=1800 m; diameter=4 m; velocity=2 m/s. hf=f(L/D)v²/(2g), g=9.81 m/s²=1.83486 m. Increasing only velocity by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 2.22018 m. Boundary: Steady full-pipe friction, excluding water hammer and local loss. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. The outputs have different units and boundaries and cannot simply be added. Identify one missing field input, explain which conclusion it changes and select an independent measurement to reduce uncertainty.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":14,"enrichmentVersion":14,"stages":[{"id":"b117-v14-s1","title":"地層條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Ground conditions, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「地下水路與傳遞時間」與「破碎帶連通與預報更新」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Underground water routes and travel time\" and \"Fault connectivity and forecast updating\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b117-v14-01","title":"地下水路與傳遞時間：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Underground water routes and travel time: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「水體平流時間」如何影響新武界引水隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Water advection time” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “New Wujie water-conveyance tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"新武界是引水工程，路線由取水、出口水位和能量坡度決定，教材用水體平流而非車輛旅行時間。地下排水或引水設施的路線先由集水區、入流點、出口水位及坡度定義，不能以交通旅行時間衡量。定速水體的行程可用距離除速度估算，但洪峰波速、蓄水與回水會改變訊號傳遞；各支路必須在共同水位與時間基準下連接。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「水體平流時間」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"New Wujie is a conveyance work; intake, outlet level and energy gradient define the route, so the example uses water advection rather than vehicle travel. An underground water route is defined by catchments, inflows, outfall level and gradient, not vehicle journey time. Distance divided by velocity estimates constant-speed material travel, while flood-wave celerity, storage and backwater alter signal propagation. Branches must be connected using common level and time references before interpreting arrival or control response. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Water advection time” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：水路長度=2000 m；水體速度=1.5 m/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: reach length=2000 m; water velocity=1.5 m/s. t=L/v/60=22.2222 min.","failure":"常見誤解：「水體流過全程的時間必然等於洪峰抵達的時間。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Material travel time necessarily equals flood-peak arrival time.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「水體平流時間」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Water advection time”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b117-v14-01-k1","title":"地下水路與傳遞時間","titleEn":"Underground water routes and travel time","text":"新武界是引水工程，路線由取水、出口水位和能量坡度決定，教材用水體平流而非車輛旅行時間。地下排水或引水設施的路線先由集水區、入流點、出口水位及坡度定義，不能以交通旅行時間衡量。","textEn":"New Wujie is a conveyance work; intake, outlet level and energy gradient define the route, so the example uses water advection rather than vehicle travel. An underground water route is defined by catchments, inflows, outfall level and gradient, not vehicle journey time.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b117-v14-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：水體流過全程的時間必然等於洪峰抵達的時間。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Material travel time necessarily equals flood-peak arrival time. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「地下水路與傳遞時間」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Underground water routes and travel time\" is correct?","options":["水體流過全程的時間必然等於洪峰抵達的時間。","新武界是引水工程，路線由取水、出口水位和能量坡度決定，教材用水體平流而非車輛旅行時間。","岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。"],"optionsEn":["Material travel time necessarily equals flood-peak arrival time.","New Wujie is a conveyance work; intake, outlet level and energy gradient define the route, so the example uses water advection rather than vehicle travel.","Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow."],"answer":1,"explanation":"新武界是引水工程，路線由取水、出口水位和能量坡度決定，教材用水體平流而非車輛旅行時間。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"New Wujie is a conveyance work; intake, outlet level and energy gradient define the route, so the example uses water advection rather than vehicle travel. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b117-v14-02","title":"地下水路與傳遞時間：定量估算","titleEn":"Underground water routes and travel time: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b117-v14-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「水體平流時間」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Water advection time” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：水路長度=2000 m；水體速度=1.5 m/s。t=L/v/60=22.2222 min。僅把水路長度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為24.4444 min。邊界：定速水體平流，不是洪峰波速或完整洪水演算；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: reach length=2000 m; water velocity=1.5 m/s. t=L/v/60=22.2222 min. Increasing only reach length by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 24.4444 min. Boundary: Constant-speed water advection, not flood-wave celerity or complete routing. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對上下游水位基準和各引水支路的連接範圍。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check level datum and connection scope for upstream, downstream and branch inflows.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b117-v14-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：水路長度=2000 m；水體速度=1.5 m/s。t=L/v/60=22.2222 min。僅把水路長度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為24.4444 min。邊界：定速水體平流，不是洪峰波速或完整洪水演算；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: reach length=2000 m; water velocity=1.5 m/s. t=L/v/60=22.2222 min. Increasing only reach length by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 24.4444 min. Boundary: Constant-speed water advection, not flood-wave celerity or complete routing. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b117-v14-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「地下水路與傳遞時間」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Underground water routes and travel time\", which statement holds?","options":["刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。","只算穩態流量就能排除輸水隧道的水錘與氣囊。","原創教學假設：水路長度=2000 m；水體速度=1.5 m/s。"],"optionsEn":["A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance.","A steady-flow calculation excludes water hammer and trapped air in a conveyance tunnel.","Original teaching assumptions: reach length=2000 m; water velocity=1.5 m/s. t=L/v/60=22.2222 min."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：水路長度=2000 m；水體速度=1.5 m/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: reach length=2000 m; water velocity=1.5 m/s. t=L/v/60=22.2222 min. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b117-v14-03","title":"地下水路與傳遞時間：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Underground water routes and travel time: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b117-v14-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「水體平流時間」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Water advection time” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對上下游水位基準和各引水支路的連接範圍。對齊入口與出口水位流量時間序列，利用允許的示蹤或模型比較平流時間與洪峰時差，保留回水條件。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check level datum and connection scope for upstream, downstream and branch inflows. Align inlet and outlet level-flow histories; use permitted tracer data or modelling to distinguish material travel from peak lag while preserving backwater conditions. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「水體平流時間」的交付需回答：核對上下游水位基準和各引水支路的連接範圍。路線圖同時標示水位基準、支路與控制邊界，所有時間比較註明是物質、波峰或設備延遲，避免混用。","observationEn":"Site practice: For New Wujie water-conveyance tunnel, the water advection time handover must address the following evidence: Check level datum and connection scope for upstream, downstream and branch inflows. Route diagrams show level datum, branches and control boundaries; label each time as material travel, wave propagation or equipment delay.","failure":"注意干擾：把引水長度直接換成交通效益會完全失去功能邊界。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Converting conveyance length into a traffic benefit loses the functional boundary. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b117-v14-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對上下游水位基準和各引水支路的連接範圍。對齊入口與出口水位流量時間序列，利用允許的示蹤或模型比較平流時間與洪峰時差，保留回水條件。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Check level datum and connection scope for upstream, downstream and branch inflows. Align inlet and outlet level-flow histories; use permitted tracer data or modelling to distinguish material travel from peak lag while preserving backwater conditions. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b117-v14-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「水體平流時間」的交付需回答：核對上下游水位基準和各引水支路的連接範圍。路線圖同時標示水位基準、支路與控制邊界，所有時間比較註明是物質、波峰或設備延遲，避免混用。","textEn":"For New Wujie water-conveyance tunnel, the water advection time handover must address the following evidence: Check level datum and connection scope for upstream, downstream and branch inflows. Route diagrams show level datum, branches and control boundaries; label each time as material travel, wave propagation or equipment delay.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「地下水路與傳遞時間」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Underground water routes and travel time\"?","options":["核對上下游水位基準和各引水支路的連接範圍。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Check level datum and connection scope for upstream, downstream and branch inflows.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error."],"answer":0,"explanation":"核對上下游水位基準和各引水支路的連接範圍。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check level datum and connection scope for upstream, downstream and branch inflows. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b117-v14-04","title":"地下水路與傳遞時間：失效診斷","titleEn":"Underground water routes and travel time: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b117-v14-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「水體平流時間」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Water advection time” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把引水長度直接換成交通效益會完全失去功能邊界。把平流時間當洪峰預警時間會忽略波速和支路入流，控制指令可能在假定水體到達之前已失去適用性。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Converting conveyance length into a traffic benefit loses the functional boundary. Using advection time as flood-warning time ignores celerity and side inflows, allowing control assumptions to fail before the assumed arrival. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：定速水體的行程可用距離除速度估算，但洪峰波速、蓄水與回水會改變訊號傳遞；各支路必須在共同水位與時間基準下連接。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Branches must be connected using common level and time references before interpreting arrival or control response.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「水體流過全程的時間必然等於洪峰抵達的時間。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Material travel time necessarily equals flood-peak arrival time.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b117-v14-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把引水長度直接換成交通效益會完全失去功能邊界。把平流時間當洪峰預警時間會忽略波速和支路入流，控制指令可能在假定水體到達之前已失去適用性。","textEn":"Converting conveyance length into a traffic benefit loses the functional boundary. Using advection time as flood-warning time ignores celerity and side inflows, allowing control assumptions to fail before the assumed arrival.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b117-v14-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「地下水路與傳遞時間」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Underground water routes and travel time\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","把引水長度直接換成交通效益會完全失去功能邊界。","岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Converting conveyance length into a traffic benefit loses the functional boundary.","Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把引水長度直接換成交通效益會完全失去功能邊界。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Converting conveyance length into a traffic benefit loses the functional boundary. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b117-v14-05","title":"破碎帶連通與預報更新：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Fault connectivity and forecast updating: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b117-v14-04"],"objective":"說明「破碎帶連通性」如何影響新武界引水隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Fault-zone connectivity” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “New Wujie water-conveyance tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"台電記錄強調探查與機械配合，本課研究長水平孔的岩性代表性及未探區裂隙不確定度。斷層帶可以含很硬的岩塊，但整體變形與湧水常由填充節理和連通裂隙控制。單一岩芯強度不能代表整個掌子面；超前鑽孔、出水變化與揭露地質須回饋同一里程模型，預報則應保留不同情境及其證據權重。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「破碎帶連通性」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Taipower emphasises investigation-machine coordination; examine representativeness of a long horizontal probe and fracture uncertainty outside it. A fault zone may contain strong intact blocks while filled joints and connected fractures govern its bulk deformation and inflow. One core strength does not represent the entire face. Probe records, water response and exposed geology must update a common chainage model, preserving competing interpretations and their evidential weight rather than treating a forecast as certainty. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Fault-zone connectivity” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：滲透係數=2e-06 m/s；水力坡降=2.1 無因次；通水面積=360 m²。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: conductivity=2e-06 m/s; hydraulic gradient=2.1 dimensionless; flow area=360 m².","failure":"常見誤解：「岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「破碎帶連通性」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Fault-zone connectivity”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b117-v14-05-k1","title":"破碎帶連通與預報更新","titleEn":"Fault connectivity and forecast updating","text":"台電記錄強調探查與機械配合，本課研究長水平孔的岩性代表性及未探區裂隙不確定度。斷層帶可以含很硬的岩塊，但整體變形與湧水常由填充節理和連通裂隙控制。","textEn":"Taipower emphasises investigation-machine coordination; examine representativeness of a long horizontal probe and fracture uncertainty outside it. A fault zone may contain strong intact blocks while filled joints and connected fractures govern its bulk deformation and inflow.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b117-v14-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「破碎帶連通與預報更新」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Fault connectivity and forecast updating\" is correct?","options":["岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。","目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。","台電記錄強調探查與機械配合，本課研究長水平孔的岩性代表性及未探區裂隙不確定度。"],"optionsEn":["Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow.","No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.","Taipower emphasises investigation-machine coordination; examine representativeness of a long horizontal probe and fracture uncertainty outside it."],"answer":2,"explanation":"台電記錄強調探查與機械配合，本課研究長水平孔的岩性代表性及未探區裂隙不確定度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Taipower emphasises investigation-machine coordination; examine representativeness of a long horizontal probe and fracture uncertainty outside it. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b117-v14-06","title":"破碎帶連通與預報更新：定量估算","titleEn":"Fault connectivity and forecast updating: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b117-v14-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「破碎帶連通性」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Fault-zone connectivity” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：滲透係數=2e-06 m/s；水力坡降=2.1 無因次；通水面積=360 m²。Q=k i A=0.001512 m³/s。僅把滲透係數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.0016632 m³/s。邊界：均質飽和達西流，不代表裂隙集中流；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: conductivity=2e-06 m/s; hydraulic gradient=2.1 dimensionless; flow area=360 m². Q=k i A=0.001512 m³/s. Increasing only conductivity by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.0016632 m³/s. Boundary: Homogeneous saturated Darcy flow, not concentrated fracture flow. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以後續揭露核對探孔預測，標記偏離路線的取樣區。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check probe predictions against later exposure and mark sampled areas away from the alignment.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b117-v14-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：滲透係數=2e-06 m/s；水力坡降=2.1 無因次；通水面積=360 m²。Q=k i A=0.001512 m³/s。僅把滲透係數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.0016632 m³/s。邊界：均質飽和達西流，不代表裂隙集中流；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: conductivity=2e-06 m/s; hydraulic gradient=2.1 dimensionless; flow area=360 m². Q=k i A=0.001512 m³/s. Increasing only conductivity by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.0016632 m³/s. Boundary: Homogeneous saturated Darcy flow, not concentrated fracture flow. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b117-v14-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「破碎帶連通與預報更新」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Fault connectivity and forecast updating\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：滲透係數=2e-06 m/s；水力坡降=2.1 無因次；通水面積=360 m²。","支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。","混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: conductivity=2e-06 m/s; hydraulic gradient=2.1 dimensionless; flow area=360 m².","Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem.","Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：滲透係數=2e-06 m/s；水力坡降=2.1 無因次；通水面積=360 m²。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: conductivity=2e-06 m/s; hydraulic gradient=2.1 dimensionless; flow area=360 m². Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b117-v14-07","title":"破碎帶連通與預報更新：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Fault connectivity and forecast updating: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b117-v14-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「破碎帶連通性」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Fault-zone connectivity” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以後續揭露核對探孔預測，標記偏離路線的取樣區。將岩心回收、裂隙方位與出水曲線按里程對齊，用未參與建模的孔段作交叉檢驗，檢查是否只擬合已知資料。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check probe predictions against later exposure and mark sampled areas away from the alignment. Align recovery, fracture orientation and inflow by chainage; test the interpretation against a withheld borehole interval to detect fitting only the known observations. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「破碎帶連通性」的交付需回答：以後續揭露核對探孔預測，標記偏離路線的取樣區。每次地質模型更新保留舊版與新增證據，差異由地質及支護設計者共同判讀，施工條件改變需重新確認核准範圍。","observationEn":"Site practice: For New Wujie water-conveyance tunnel, the fault-zone connectivity handover must address the following evidence: Check probe predictions against later exposure and mark sampled areas away from the alignment. Retain previous interpretations and new evidence at every update; geology and support designers jointly interpret differences and reconfirm approved bounds when ground conditions change.","failure":"注意干擾：一支長孔仍可能平行錯過不利構造，長度不等於完整覆蓋。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A long hole can run parallel to an adverse structure; length is not complete coverage. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b117-v14-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以後續揭露核對探孔預測，標記偏離路線的取樣區。將岩心回收、裂隙方位與出水曲線按里程對齊，用未參與建模的孔段作交叉檢驗，檢查是否只擬合已知資料。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Check probe predictions against later exposure and mark sampled areas away from the alignment. Align recovery, fracture orientation and inflow by chainage; test the interpretation against a withheld borehole interval to detect fitting only the known observations. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b117-v14-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「破碎帶連通性」的交付需回答：以後續揭露核對探孔預測，標記偏離路線的取樣區。每次地質模型更新保留舊版與新增證據，差異由地質及支護設計者共同判讀，施工條件改變需重新確認核准範圍。","textEn":"For New Wujie water-conveyance tunnel, the fault-zone connectivity handover must address the following evidence: Check probe predictions against later exposure and mark sampled areas away from the alignment. Retain previous interpretations and new evidence at every update; geology and support designers jointly interpret differences and reconfirm approved bounds when ground conditions change.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「破碎帶連通與預報更新」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Fault connectivity and forecast updating\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","以後續揭露核對探孔預測，標記偏離路線的取樣區。","增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Check probe predictions against later exposure and mark sampled areas away from the alignment.","Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以後續揭露核對探孔預測，標記偏離路線的取樣區。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check probe predictions against later exposure and mark sampled areas away from the alignment. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b117-v14-08","title":"破碎帶連通與預報更新：失效診斷","titleEn":"Fault connectivity and forecast updating: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b117-v14-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「破碎帶連通性」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Fault-zone connectivity” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"一支長孔仍可能平行錯過不利構造，長度不等於完整覆蓋。只用完整岩石強度會漏掉軟弱填充物，可能在看似堅硬的地層中出現收斂加快、支護過載或水量突增。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A long hole can run parallel to an adverse structure; length is not complete coverage. Intact strength alone misses weak infill, allowing accelerating convergence, support overload or sudden inflow in ground that superficially appears strong. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：單一岩芯強度不能代表整個掌子面；超前鑽孔、出水變化與揭露地質須回饋同一里程模型，預報則應保留不同情境及其證據權重。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Probe records, water response and exposed geology must update a common chainage model, preserving competing interpretations and their evidential weight rather than treating a forecast as certainty.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b117-v14-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"一支長孔仍可能平行錯過不利構造，長度不等於完整覆蓋。只用完整岩石強度會漏掉軟弱填充物，可能在看似堅硬的地層中出現收斂加快、支護過載或水量突增。","textEn":"A long hole can run parallel to an adverse structure; length is not complete coverage. Intact strength alone misses weak infill, allowing accelerating convergence, support overload or sudden inflow in ground that superficially appears strong.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b117-v14-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「破碎帶連通與預報更新」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Fault connectivity and forecast updating\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。","一支長孔仍可能平行錯過不利構造，長度不等於完整覆蓋。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.","A long hole can run parallel to an adverse structure; length is not complete coverage."],"answer":2,"explanation":"一支長孔仍可能平行錯過不利構造，長度不等於完整覆蓋。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A long hole can run parallel to an adverse structure; length is not complete coverage. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b117-v14-s2","title":"機制、材料與定量設計","titleEn":"Mechanisms, materials and quantitative design","description":"本階段聚焦「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」與「掘進利用率與設備停時」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\" and \"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b117-v14-09","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b117-v14-08"],"objective":"說明「測壓水頭」如何影響新武界引水隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Piezometric head” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “New Wujie water-conveyance tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"引水隧道施工時外部地下水與營運時內水壓方向不同，教材把內外壓組合按階段列清。水壓取決於連通含水層的測壓水頭，不必等於地表或海面至洞頂的幾何深度。排水降低水壓卻可能增加有效應力與沉陷；停泵或排水堵塞後水頭又會回升，因此防水、排水及環境保水是互相制約的設計選擇。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「測壓水頭」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"External groundwater during excavation and internal conveyance pressure during operation act differently; list pressure combinations by stage. Water pressure follows piezometric head in the connected aquifer, not automatically the geometric depth below ground or sea level. Drainage reduces pressure but can increase effective stress and settlement. Head may recover after a pump outage or blockage, coupling waterproofing, drainage capacity and preservation of surrounding groundwater in the permanent design. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Piezometric head” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=96 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=96 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=941.76 kPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「測壓水頭」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Piezometric head”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b117-v14-09-k1","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure","text":"引水隧道施工時外部地下水與營運時內水壓方向不同，教材把內外壓組合按階段列清。水壓取決於連通含水層的測壓水頭，不必等於地表或海面至洞頂的幾何深度。","textEn":"External groundwater during excavation and internal conveyance pressure during operation act differently; list pressure combinations by stage. Water pressure follows piezometric head in the connected aquifer, not automatically the geometric depth below ground or sea level.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b117-v14-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\" is correct?","options":["引水隧道施工時外部地下水與營運時內水壓方向不同，教材把內外壓組合按階段列清。","目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。","刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。"],"optionsEn":["External groundwater during excavation and internal conveyance pressure during operation act differently; list pressure combinations by stage.","No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.","A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"引水隧道施工時外部地下水與營運時內水壓方向不同，教材把內外壓組合按階段列清。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"External groundwater during excavation and internal conveyance pressure during operation act differently; list pressure combinations by stage. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b117-v14-10","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓：定量估算","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b117-v14-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「測壓水頭」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Piezometric head” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=96 m。p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=941.76 kPa。僅把水頭增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為1035.94 kPa。邊界：靜水表壓，不是土體總壓或原位量測；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=96 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=941.76 kPa. Increasing only head by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 1035.94 kPa. Boundary: Hydrostatic gauge pressure, not total earth pressure or an in-situ measurement. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比較空洞、充水和停水狀態的內外測壓基準。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare internal and external pressure references for empty, filled and shutdown states.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b117-v14-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=96 m。p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=941.76 kPa。僅把水頭增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為1035.94 kPa。邊界：靜水表壓，不是土體總壓或原位量測；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=96 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=941.76 kPa. Increasing only head by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 1035.94 kPa. Boundary: Hydrostatic gauge pressure, not total earth pressure or an in-situ measurement. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b117-v14-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\", which statement holds?","options":["只算穩態流量就能排除輸水隧道的水錘與氣囊。","原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=96 m。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。"],"optionsEn":["A steady-flow calculation excludes water hammer and trapped air in a conveyance tunnel.","Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=96 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=941.76 kPa.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=96 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=96 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=941.76 kPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b117-v14-11","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b117-v14-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「測壓水頭」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Piezometric head” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比較空洞、充水和停水狀態的內外測壓基準。使用分層測壓管及流量計，配合降雨或潮位序列分辨補注與設備影響，將讀值統一換算至同一高程基準。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare internal and external pressure references for empty, filled and shutdown states. Use nested piezometers and flowmeters with rainfall or tide histories to distinguish recharge from equipment effects, converting observations to a common elevation datum. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「測壓水頭」的交付需回答：比較空洞、充水和停水狀態的內外測壓基準。設計檢核應分列正常排水、堵塞與停電水位，將環境受體的容許變化和監測責任一起交付，不把抽水量當唯一指標。","observationEn":"Site practice: For New Wujie water-conveyance tunnel, the piezometric head handover must address the following evidence: Compare internal and external pressure references for empty, filled and shutdown states. Separate normal drainage, blocked-drain and power-outage heads and hand over receptor limits and monitoring responsibility together rather than using pump flow as the sole indicator.","failure":"注意干擾：只驗滿水時淨內壓會漏掉放空後外壓控制情境。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Checking filled-state net internal pressure misses external pressure after draining. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b117-v14-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比較空洞、充水和停水狀態的內外測壓基準。使用分層測壓管及流量計，配合降雨或潮位序列分辨補注與設備影響，將讀值統一換算至同一高程基準。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Compare internal and external pressure references for empty, filled and shutdown states. Use nested piezometers and flowmeters with rainfall or tide histories to distinguish recharge from equipment effects, converting observations to a common elevation datum. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b117-v14-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「測壓水頭」的交付需回答：比較空洞、充水和停水狀態的內外測壓基準。設計檢核應分列正常排水、堵塞與停電水位，將環境受體的容許變化和監測責任一起交付，不把抽水量當唯一指標。","textEn":"For New Wujie water-conveyance tunnel, the piezometric head handover must address the following evidence: Compare internal and external pressure references for empty, filled and shutdown states. Separate normal drainage, blocked-drain and power-outage heads and hand over receptor limits and monitoring responsibility together rather than using pump flow as the sole indicator.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","施工後泉水變少就能單獨證明隧道造成全部減流。","比較空洞、充水和停水狀態的內外測壓基準。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Reduced spring flow after construction alone proves the tunnel caused the entire change.","Compare internal and external pressure references for empty, filled and shutdown states."],"answer":2,"explanation":"比較空洞、充水和停水狀態的內外測壓基準。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare internal and external pressure references for empty, filled and shutdown states. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b117-v14-12","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓：失效診斷","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b117-v14-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「測壓水頭」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Piezometric head” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只驗滿水時淨內壓會漏掉放空後外壓控制情境。將暫時降水後的低水頭當成永久狀態，會漏掉停泵後外壓回升；過度排水也可能引起周邊地層壓密。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Checking filled-state net internal pressure misses external pressure after draining. Treating temporarily lowered head as permanent misses pressure recovery after outage; excessive drainage can also consolidate surrounding ground. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：排水降低水壓卻可能增加有效應力與沉陷；停泵或排水堵塞後水頭又會回升，因此防水、排水及環境保水是互相制約的設計選擇。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Head may recover after a pump outage or blockage, coupling waterproofing, drainage capacity and preservation of surrounding groundwater in the permanent design.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b117-v14-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只驗滿水時淨內壓會漏掉放空後外壓控制情境。將暫時降水後的低水頭當成永久狀態，會漏掉停泵後外壓回升；過度排水也可能引起周邊地層壓密。","textEn":"Checking filled-state net internal pressure misses external pressure after draining. Treating temporarily lowered head as permanent misses pressure recovery after outage; excessive drainage can also consolidate surrounding ground.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b117-v14-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["只驗滿水時淨內壓會漏掉放空後外壓控制情境。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。"],"optionsEn":["Checking filled-state net internal pressure misses external pressure after draining.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"只驗滿水時淨內壓會漏掉放空後外壓控制情境。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Checking filled-state net internal pressure misses external pressure after draining. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b117-v14-13","title":"掘進利用率與設備停時：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b117-v14-12"],"objective":"說明「有效掘進利用率」如何影響新武界引水隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Effective boring utilisation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “New Wujie water-conveyance tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"公開資料的最高日進尺與月平均是不同統計量，本課以新武界背景重建班次利用率而非追逐紀錄。TBM瞬時貫入率只描述刀盤切削的一段時間，拼裝、換刀、出渣與維修決定每天真正進尺。岩石強度與磨蝕性對刀具的影響不同，混合掌子面又產生不對稱作用；比較機器績效須按地質分區和停時原因分類，不能只排序最高進尺。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「有效掘進利用率」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Published peak daily and mean monthly advance are different statistics; reconstruct shift utilisation rather than treating a production record as normal. Instantaneous penetration describes only active cutting; erection, cutter changes, muck handling and repairs determine daily advance. Strength and abrasivity affect cutters differently, while mixed faces impose asymmetric loading. Compare performance by ground domain and downtime cause, because the highest short-duration penetration rate can coexist with poor daily production and increased maintenance demand. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Effective boring utilisation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：切削速率=1.98 m/h；有效利用率=0.295 無因次。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: active penetration=1.98 m/h; utilisation=0.295 dimensionless.","failure":"常見誤解：「刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「有效掘進利用率」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Effective boring utilisation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b117-v14-13-k1","title":"掘進利用率與設備停時","titleEn":"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime","text":"公開資料的最高日進尺與月平均是不同統計量，本課以新武界背景重建班次利用率而非追逐紀錄。TBM瞬時貫入率只描述刀盤切削的一段時間，拼裝、換刀、出渣與維修決定每天真正進尺。","textEn":"Published peak daily and mean monthly advance are different statistics; reconstruct shift utilisation rather than treating a production record as normal. Instantaneous penetration describes only active cutting; erection, cutter changes, muck handling and repairs determine daily advance.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b117-v14-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「掘進利用率與設備停時」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime\" is correct?","options":["刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。","公開資料的最高日進尺與月平均是不同統計量，本課以新武界背景重建班次利用率而非追逐紀錄。","支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。"],"optionsEn":["A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance.","Published peak daily and mean monthly advance are different statistics; reconstruct shift utilisation rather than treating a production record as normal.","Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem."],"answer":1,"explanation":"公開資料的最高日進尺與月平均是不同統計量，本課以新武界背景重建班次利用率而非追逐紀錄。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Published peak daily and mean monthly advance are different statistics; reconstruct shift utilisation rather than treating a production record as normal. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b117-v14-14","title":"掘進利用率與設備停時：定量估算","titleEn":"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b117-v14-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「有效掘進利用率」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Effective boring utilisation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：切削速率=1.98 m/h；有效利用率=0.295 無因次。D=24vu=14.0184 m/day。僅把有效利用率增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為15.4202 m/day。邊界：平均循環模型，未表示地質轉換及停機分布；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: active penetration=1.98 m/h; utilisation=0.295 dimensionless. D=24vu=14.0184 m/day. Increasing only utilisation by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 15.4202 m/day. Boundary: Mean-cycle model without ground transitions or downtime distribution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將最高日、完整月份與停機日納入同一時間帳。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Include peak day, full month and stoppage days in one time balance.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b117-v14-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：切削速率=1.98 m/h；有效利用率=0.295 無因次。D=24vu=14.0184 m/day。僅把有效利用率增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為15.4202 m/day。邊界：平均循環模型，未表示地質轉換及停機分布；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: active penetration=1.98 m/h; utilisation=0.295 dimensionless. D=24vu=14.0184 m/day. Increasing only utilisation by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 15.4202 m/day. Boundary: Mean-cycle model without ground transitions or downtime distribution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b117-v14-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「掘進利用率與設備停時」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime\", which statement holds?","options":["混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。","增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。","原創教學假設：切削速率=1.98 m/h；有效利用率=0.295 無因次。"],"optionsEn":["Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure.","Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.","Original teaching assumptions: active penetration=1.98 m/h; utilisation=0.295 dimensionless."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：切削速率=1.98 m/h；有效利用率=0.295 無因次。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: active penetration=1.98 m/h; utilisation=0.295 dimensionless. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b117-v14-15","title":"掘進利用率與設備停時：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b117-v14-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「有效掘進利用率」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Effective boring utilisation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將最高日、完整月份與停機日納入同一時間帳。由時間戳分離切削、拼裝與故障，將刀具位置、磨耗量及推力扭矩對齊里程，檢查停時是否集中在特定地層。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Include peak day, full month and stoppage days in one time balance. Separate cutting, erection and faults by timestamp; align cutter position, wear, thrust and torque with chainage and test clustering by ground type. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「有效掘進利用率」的交付需回答：將最高日、完整月份與停機日納入同一時間帳。停機紀錄使用可追溯原因碼，把地質變化與設備故障分開統計，參數調整只能在設備和施工團隊核准程序內進行。","observationEn":"Site practice: For New Wujie water-conveyance tunnel, the effective boring utilisation handover must address the following evidence: Include peak day, full month and stoppage days in one time balance. Use traceable downtime codes, separating geological change from equipment faults; parameter changes stay within procedures approved by equipment and construction teams.","failure":"注意干擾：最高日乘整月會系統性高估施工進度。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Multiplying the peak day by a month systematically overstates progress. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b117-v14-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將最高日、完整月份與停機日納入同一時間帳。由時間戳分離切削、拼裝與故障，將刀具位置、磨耗量及推力扭矩對齊里程，檢查停時是否集中在特定地層。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Include peak day, full month and stoppage days in one time balance. Separate cutting, erection and faults by timestamp; align cutter position, wear, thrust and torque with chainage and test clustering by ground type. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b117-v14-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「有效掘進利用率」的交付需回答：將最高日、完整月份與停機日納入同一時間帳。停機紀錄使用可追溯原因碼，把地質變化與設備故障分開統計，參數調整只能在設備和施工團隊核准程序內進行。","textEn":"For New Wujie water-conveyance tunnel, the effective boring utilisation handover must address the following evidence: Include peak day, full month and stoppage days in one time balance. Use traceable downtime codes, separating geological change from equipment faults; parameter changes stay within procedures approved by equipment and construction teams.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「掘進利用率與設備停時」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime\"?","options":["將最高日、完整月份與停機日納入同一時間帳。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","水體流過全程的時間必然等於洪峰抵達的時間。"],"optionsEn":["Include peak day, full month and stoppage days in one time balance.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Material travel time necessarily equals flood-peak arrival time."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將最高日、完整月份與停機日納入同一時間帳。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Include peak day, full month and stoppage days in one time balance. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b117-v14-16","title":"掘進利用率與設備停時：失效診斷","titleEn":"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b117-v14-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「有效掘進利用率」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Effective boring utilisation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"最高日乘整月會系統性高估施工進度。只提高瞬時進尺可能使出渣或刀具超出有效工況，短暫改善後增加停機，平均進尺和零件壽命反而下降。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Multiplying the peak day by a month systematically overstates progress. Higher instantaneous advance can overload cutters or muck transport and create longer stoppages that reduce average progress and component life. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：岩石強度與磨蝕性對刀具的影響不同，混合掌子面又產生不對稱作用；比較機器績效須按地質分區和停時原因分類，不能只排序最高進尺。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Compare performance by ground domain and downtime cause, because the highest short-duration penetration rate can coexist with poor daily production and increased maintenance demand.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b117-v14-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"最高日乘整月會系統性高估施工進度。只提高瞬時進尺可能使出渣或刀具超出有效工況，短暫改善後增加停機，平均進尺和零件壽命反而下降。","textEn":"Multiplying the peak day by a month systematically overstates progress. Higher instantaneous advance can overload cutters or muck transport and create longer stoppages that reduce average progress and component life.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b117-v14-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「掘進利用率與設備停時」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","最高日乘整月會系統性高估施工進度。","支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Multiplying the peak day by a month systematically overstates progress.","Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem."],"answer":1,"explanation":"最高日乘整月會系統性高估施工進度。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Multiplying the peak day by a month systematically overstates progress. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b117-v14-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「支護啟動與變形容量」與「輸水摩阻與瞬變邊界」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Support activation and deformation capacity\" and \"Conveyance friction and transient boundaries\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b117-v14-17","title":"支護啟動與變形容量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Support activation and deformation capacity: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b117-v14-16"],"objective":"說明「支護安裝時點」如何影響新武界引水隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Support activation time” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “New Wujie water-conveyance tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"引水隧道的初期支護先穩定開挖，永久內襯還有水理和耐久功能，教材明確區分兩者驗證。支護荷載由開挖釋放量和支護啟動時間共同決定，越早安裝不一定讓構件受力越小。地盤反力與支護曲線必須連同掌子面距離及封閉順序理解；擠壓性地層還需保留變形容量，不能只追求高剛度與高材料強度。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「支護安裝時點」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Initial support stabilises excavation while permanent lining also serves hydraulics and durability; verify these functions separately. Support load depends on stress release and activation time, so earlier installation does not necessarily reduce member forces. Interpret ground-reaction and support curves together with distance from the face and closure sequence. Squeezing ground also needs deformation capacity; high stiffness and material strength alone do not guarantee a compatible support response. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Support activation time” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：局部剛度=46 kN/mm；位移=9 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: local stiffness=46 kN/mm; movement=9 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「支護安裝時點」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Support activation time”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b117-v14-17-k1","title":"支護啟動與變形容量","titleEn":"Support activation and deformation capacity","text":"引水隧道的初期支護先穩定開挖，永久內襯還有水理和耐久功能，教材明確區分兩者驗證。支護荷載由開挖釋放量和支護啟動時間共同決定，越早安裝不一定讓構件受力越小。","textEn":"Initial support stabilises excavation while permanent lining also serves hydraulics and durability; verify these functions separately. Support load depends on stress release and activation time, so earlier installation does not necessarily reduce member forces.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b117-v14-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「支護啟動與變形容量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Support activation and deformation capacity\" is correct?","options":["支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。","只算穩態流量就能排除輸水隧道的水錘與氣囊。","引水隧道的初期支護先穩定開挖，永久內襯還有水理和耐久功能，教材明確區分兩者驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem.","A steady-flow calculation excludes water hammer and trapped air in a conveyance tunnel.","Initial support stabilises excavation while permanent lining also serves hydraulics and durability; verify these functions separately."],"answer":2,"explanation":"引水隧道的初期支護先穩定開挖，永久內襯還有水理和耐久功能，教材明確區分兩者驗證。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Initial support stabilises excavation while permanent lining also serves hydraulics and durability; verify these functions separately. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b117-v14-18","title":"支護啟動與變形容量：定量估算","titleEn":"Support activation and deformation capacity: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b117-v14-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「支護安裝時點」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Support activation time” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：局部剛度=46 kN/mm；位移=9 mm。F=ku=414 kN。僅把位移增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為455.4 kN。邊界：線性局部彈簧，不含屈服或時間效應；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: local stiffness=46 kN/mm; movement=9 mm. F=ku=414 kN. Increasing only movement by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 455.4 kN. Boundary: Local linear spring without yielding or time effects. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以施工收斂與後續內襯幾何資料分階段核對。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check construction convergence and later lining geometry as separate stages.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b117-v14-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：局部剛度=46 kN/mm；位移=9 mm。F=ku=414 kN。僅把位移增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為455.4 kN。邊界：線性局部彈簧，不含屈服或時間效應；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: local stiffness=46 kN/mm; movement=9 mm. F=ku=414 kN. Increasing only movement by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 455.4 kN. Boundary: Local linear spring without yielding or time effects. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b117-v14-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「支護啟動與變形容量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Support activation and deformation capacity\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：局部剛度=46 kN/mm；位移=9 mm。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。","施工後泉水變少就能單獨證明隧道造成全部減流。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: local stiffness=46 kN/mm; movement=9 mm.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.","Reduced spring flow after construction alone proves the tunnel caused the entire change."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：局部剛度=46 kN/mm；位移=9 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: local stiffness=46 kN/mm; movement=9 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b117-v14-19","title":"支護啟動與變形容量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Support activation and deformation capacity: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b117-v14-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「支護安裝時點」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Support activation time” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以施工收斂與後續內襯幾何資料分階段核對。同步記錄收斂、支護荷重與安裝里程，比較同一地質分區內的速率及荷載，不將不同開挖齡期讀值直接混合。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check construction convergence and later lining geometry as separate stages. Synchronise convergence, support loads and installation chainage; compare rates and loads within one ground domain without mixing readings at different excavation ages. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「支護安裝時點」的交付需回答：以施工收斂與後續內襯幾何資料分階段核對。把安裝時間和量測資料一起交付支護設計者，任何級別變更都需地質及位移證據，不能憑單一瞬間讀值自行改支護。","observationEn":"Site practice: For New Wujie water-conveyance tunnel, the support activation time handover must address the following evidence: Check construction convergence and later lining geometry as separate stages. Submit installation times with measurements to the support designer; class changes need both ground and movement evidence, not an isolated instantaneous reading.","failure":"注意干擾：初期支護穩定不能證明永久水理斷面已達需求。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Stable initial support does not establish the permanent hydraulic section. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b117-v14-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以施工收斂與後續內襯幾何資料分階段核對。同步記錄收斂、支護荷重與安裝里程，比較同一地質分區內的速率及荷載，不將不同開挖齡期讀值直接混合。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Check construction convergence and later lining geometry as separate stages. Synchronise convergence, support loads and installation chainage; compare rates and loads within one ground domain without mixing readings at different excavation ages. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b117-v14-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「支護安裝時點」的交付需回答：以施工收斂與後續內襯幾何資料分階段核對。把安裝時間和量測資料一起交付支護設計者，任何級別變更都需地質及位移證據，不能憑單一瞬間讀值自行改支護。","textEn":"For New Wujie water-conveyance tunnel, the support activation time handover must address the following evidence: Check construction convergence and later lining geometry as separate stages. Submit installation times with measurements to the support designer; class changes need both ground and movement evidence, not an isolated instantaneous reading.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「支護啟動與變形容量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Support activation and deformation capacity\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","以施工收斂與後續內襯幾何資料分階段核對。","岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Check construction convergence and later lining geometry as separate stages.","Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以施工收斂與後續內襯幾何資料分階段核對。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check construction convergence and later lining geometry as separate stages. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b117-v14-20","title":"支護啟動與變形容量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Support activation and deformation capacity: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b117-v14-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「支護安裝時點」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Support activation time” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"初期支護穩定不能證明永久水理斷面已達需求。過晚封閉會讓不可回復變形增加，過硬且行程不足的支護也可能脆裂，兩者都可能表現為裂縫而需不同處理。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Stable initial support does not establish the permanent hydraulic section. Late closure increases irreversible movement, while excessively stiff support with little travel can fail brittly; both produce cracks but require different diagnoses. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：地盤反力與支護曲線必須連同掌子面距離及封閉順序理解；擠壓性地層還需保留變形容量，不能只追求高剛度與高材料強度。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Squeezing ground also needs deformation capacity; high stiffness and material strength alone do not guarantee a compatible support response.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b117-v14-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"初期支護穩定不能證明永久水理斷面已達需求。過晚封閉會讓不可回復變形增加，過硬且行程不足的支護也可能脆裂，兩者都可能表現為裂縫而需不同處理。","textEn":"Stable initial support does not establish the permanent hydraulic section. Late closure increases irreversible movement, while excessively stiff support with little travel can fail brittly; both produce cracks but require different diagnoses.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b117-v14-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「支護啟動與變形容量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Support activation and deformation capacity\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","只算穩態流量就能排除輸水隧道的水錘與氣囊。","初期支護穩定不能證明永久水理斷面已達需求。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","A steady-flow calculation excludes water hammer and trapped air in a conveyance tunnel.","Stable initial support does not establish the permanent hydraulic section."],"answer":2,"explanation":"初期支護穩定不能證明永久水理斷面已達需求。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Stable initial support does not establish the permanent hydraulic section. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b117-v14-21","title":"輸水摩阻與瞬變邊界：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Conveyance friction and transient boundaries: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b117-v14-20"],"objective":"說明「滿管沿程損失」如何影響新武界引水隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Full-pipe friction loss” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “New Wujie water-conveyance tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"新武界水理教材以滿管摩阻建立能量帳，再列閘門瞬變和可能自由水面轉換的額外需求。輸水隧道由上下游能量差驅動，沿程粗糙度、接頭及局部收縮消耗水頭；流速增加使摩阻快速上升。穩態滿管式不能描述水錘、自由水面轉換或氣囊，閘門動作和停機歷程必須另外建立瞬變模型與通氣條件。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「滿管沿程損失」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Build a full-pipe friction balance, then identify separate gate-transient and possible free-surface-transition requirements. A conveyance tunnel is driven by upstream and downstream energy levels; roughness, joints and contractions consume head, with friction rising rapidly with velocity. A steady full-pipe equation does not describe water hammer, free-surface transitions or trapped air. Gate movements and shutdown histories require separate transient modelling and explicit ventilation conditions. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Full-pipe friction loss” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：達西因子=0.02 無因次；長度=1800 m；直徑=4 m；流速=2 m/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.02 dimensionless; length=1800 m; diameter=4 m; velocity=2 m/s. hf=f(L/D)v²/(2g), g=9.81 m/s²=1.83486 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「只算穩態流量就能排除輸水隧道的水錘與氣囊。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A steady-flow calculation excludes water hammer and trapped air in a conveyance tunnel.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「滿管沿程損失」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Full-pipe friction loss”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b117-v14-21-k1","title":"輸水摩阻與瞬變邊界","titleEn":"Conveyance friction and transient boundaries","text":"新武界水理教材以滿管摩阻建立能量帳，再列閘門瞬變和可能自由水面轉換的額外需求。輸水隧道由上下游能量差驅動，沿程粗糙度、接頭及局部收縮消耗水頭；流速增加使摩阻快速上升。","textEn":"Build a full-pipe friction balance, then identify separate gate-transient and possible free-surface-transition requirements. A conveyance tunnel is driven by upstream and downstream energy levels; roughness, joints and contractions consume head, with friction rising rapidly with velocity.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b117-v14-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只算穩態流量就能排除輸水隧道的水錘與氣囊。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A steady-flow calculation excludes water hammer and trapped air in a conveyance tunnel. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「輸水摩阻與瞬變邊界」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Conveyance friction and transient boundaries\" is correct?","options":["新武界水理教材以滿管摩阻建立能量帳，再列閘門瞬變和可能自由水面轉換的額外需求。","只算穩態流量就能排除輸水隧道的水錘與氣囊。","混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。"],"optionsEn":["Build a full-pipe friction balance, then identify separate gate-transient and possible free-surface-transition requirements.","A steady-flow calculation excludes water hammer and trapped air in a conveyance tunnel.","Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure."],"answer":0,"explanation":"新武界水理教材以滿管摩阻建立能量帳，再列閘門瞬變和可能自由水面轉換的額外需求。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Build a full-pipe friction balance, then identify separate gate-transient and possible free-surface-transition requirements. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b117-v14-22","title":"輸水摩阻與瞬變邊界：定量估算","titleEn":"Conveyance friction and transient boundaries: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b117-v14-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「滿管沿程損失」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Full-pipe friction loss” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：達西因子=0.02 無因次；長度=1800 m；直徑=4 m；流速=2 m/s。hf=f(L/D)v²/(2g), g=9.81 m/s²=1.83486 m。僅把流速增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為2.22018 m。邊界：滿管穩態摩阻，不含水錘與局部損失；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.02 dimensionless; length=1800 m; diameter=4 m; velocity=2 m/s. hf=f(L/D)v²/(2g), g=9.81 m/s²=1.83486 m. Increasing only velocity by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 2.22018 m. Boundary: Steady full-pipe friction, excluding water hammer and local loss. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用同時流量和水位反算水頭損失，保留閘門狀態。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Infer head loss from simultaneous flow and levels with gate state recorded.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b117-v14-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：達西因子=0.02 無因次；長度=1800 m；直徑=4 m；流速=2 m/s。hf=f(L/D)v²/(2g), g=9.81 m/s²=1.83486 m。僅把流速增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為2.22018 m。邊界：滿管穩態摩阻，不含水錘與局部損失；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.02 dimensionless; length=1800 m; diameter=4 m; velocity=2 m/s. hf=f(L/D)v²/(2g), g=9.81 m/s²=1.83486 m. Increasing only velocity by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 2.22018 m. Boundary: Steady full-pipe friction, excluding water hammer and local loss. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b117-v14-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「輸水摩阻與瞬變邊界」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Conveyance friction and transient boundaries\", which statement holds?","options":["增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。","原創教學假設：達西因子=0.02 無因次；長度=1800 m；直徑=4 m；流速=2 m/s。","水體流過全程的時間必然等於洪峰抵達的時間。"],"optionsEn":["Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.","Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.02 dimensionless; length=1800 m; diameter=4 m; velocity=2 m/s. hf=f(L/D)v²/(2g), g=9.81 m/s²=1.83486 m.","Material travel time necessarily equals flood-peak arrival time."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：達西因子=0.02 無因次；長度=1800 m；直徑=4 m；流速=2 m/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.02 dimensionless; length=1800 m; diameter=4 m; velocity=2 m/s. hf=f(L/D)v²/(2g), g=9.81 m/s²=1.83486 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b117-v14-23","title":"輸水摩阻與瞬變邊界：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Conveyance friction and transient boundaries: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b117-v14-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「滿管沿程損失」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Full-pipe friction loss” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用同時流量和水位反算水頭損失，保留閘門狀態。以同步上下游水位和流量核對能量坡度，分辨入口損失與沿程損失，保留閘門及氣壓狀態。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Infer head loss from simultaneous flow and levels with gate state recorded. Use synchronised levels and flow to check energy gradient, separate entrance from distributed losses and preserve gate and air-pressure states. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「滿管沿程損失」的交付需回答：用同時流量和水位反算水頭損失，保留閘門狀態。水理交付需包含水位基準、流量、閘門歷程及模型適用狀態；瞬變與通氣由水理設計者另行檢核。","observationEn":"Site practice: For New Wujie water-conveyance tunnel, the full-pipe friction loss handover must address the following evidence: Infer head loss from simultaneous flow and levels with gate state recorded. Hydraulic handover includes level datum, flow, gate histories and model regimes; specialists independently assess transients and air movement.","failure":"注意干擾：把非穩態壓力峰用來反算粗糙度會產生失真參數。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Inferring roughness from transient peaks produces misleading parameters. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b117-v14-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用同時流量和水位反算水頭損失，保留閘門狀態。以同步上下游水位和流量核對能量坡度，分辨入口損失與沿程損失，保留閘門及氣壓狀態。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Infer head loss from simultaneous flow and levels with gate state recorded. Use synchronised levels and flow to check energy gradient, separate entrance from distributed losses and preserve gate and air-pressure states. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b117-v14-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「滿管沿程損失」的交付需回答：用同時流量和水位反算水頭損失，保留閘門狀態。水理交付需包含水位基準、流量、閘門歷程及模型適用狀態；瞬變與通氣由水理設計者另行檢核。","textEn":"For New Wujie water-conveyance tunnel, the full-pipe friction loss handover must address the following evidence: Infer head loss from simultaneous flow and levels with gate state recorded. Hydraulic handover includes level datum, flow, gate histories and model regimes; specialists independently assess transients and air movement.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「輸水摩阻與瞬變邊界」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Conveyance friction and transient boundaries\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。","用同時流量和水位反算水頭損失，保留閘門狀態。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.","Infer head loss from simultaneous flow and levels with gate state recorded."],"answer":2,"explanation":"用同時流量和水位反算水頭損失，保留閘門狀態。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Infer head loss from simultaneous flow and levels with gate state recorded. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b117-v14-24","title":"輸水摩阻與瞬變邊界：失效診斷","titleEn":"Conveyance friction and transient boundaries: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b117-v14-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「滿管沿程損失」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Full-pipe friction loss” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把非穩態壓力峰用來反算粗糙度會產生失真參數。把閘門急動後的壓力峰當穩態摩阻，會錯估粗糙度並漏掉瞬變作用；未排出的氣囊也會改變有效斷面。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Inferring roughness from transient peaks produces misleading parameters. Treating post-gate pressure peaks as steady friction biases roughness and misses transients; trapped air also changes effective area. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：穩態滿管式不能描述水錘、自由水面轉換或氣囊，閘門動作和停機歷程必須另外建立瞬變模型與通氣條件。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Gate movements and shutdown histories require separate transient modelling and explicit ventilation conditions.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只算穩態流量就能排除輸水隧道的水錘與氣囊。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A steady-flow calculation excludes water hammer and trapped air in a conveyance tunnel.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b117-v14-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把非穩態壓力峰用來反算粗糙度會產生失真參數。把閘門急動後的壓力峰當穩態摩阻，會錯估粗糙度並漏掉瞬變作用；未排出的氣囊也會改變有效斷面。","textEn":"Inferring roughness from transient peaks produces misleading parameters. Treating post-gate pressure peaks as steady friction biases roughness and misses transients; trapped air also changes effective area.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b117-v14-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「輸水摩阻與瞬變邊界」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Conveyance friction and transient boundaries\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["把非穩態壓力峰用來反算粗糙度會產生失真參數。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。"],"optionsEn":["Inferring roughness from transient peaks produces misleading parameters.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure."],"answer":0,"explanation":"把非穩態壓力峰用來反算粗糙度會產生失真參數。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Inferring roughness from transient peaks produces misleading parameters. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b117-v14-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「環向受力與接縫柔度」與「控制網與貫通誤差」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Ring force and joint flexibility\" and \"Control network and breakthrough error\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b117-v14-25","title":"環向受力與接縫柔度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Ring force and joint flexibility: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b117-v14-24"],"objective":"說明「襯砌環向壓縮」如何影響新武界引水隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Lining hoop compression” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “New Wujie water-conveyance tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"引水內襯的平整度和接縫同時影響摩阻與結構，教材將環向量級和局部缺陷分開。圓形襯砌對均勻外壓可主要以環向壓縮抵抗，但接頭轉動、偏壓與背填空隙會引起彎矩。薄環膜應力只說明其中一條受力路徑；脫模、運輸、頂推及永久狀態的荷載不同，環片局部接觸與止水條件必須另外檢核。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「襯砌環向壓縮」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Lining smoothness and joints affect hydraulics and structure; separate hoop-force scale from local defects. A circular lining resists uniform external pressure largely through hoop compression, but joint rotation, uneven load and backfill voids generate bending. Thin-ring membrane stress describes only one load path. Demoulding, transport, jacking and permanent states impose different actions, requiring separate checks of local segment contact and sealing rather than one permanent-load calculation. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Lining hoop compression” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：均勻外壓=0.62 MPa；半徑=3.6 m；厚度=0.35 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: uniform external pressure=0.62 MPa; radius=3.6 m; thickness=0.35 m. σθ=pr/t=6.37714 MPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「襯砌環向壓縮」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Lining hoop compression”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b117-v14-25-k1","title":"環向受力與接縫柔度","titleEn":"Ring force and joint flexibility","text":"引水內襯的平整度和接縫同時影響摩阻與結構，教材將環向量級和局部缺陷分開。圓形襯砌對均勻外壓可主要以環向壓縮抵抗，但接頭轉動、偏壓與背填空隙會引起彎矩。","textEn":"Lining smoothness and joints affect hydraulics and structure; separate hoop-force scale from local defects. A circular lining resists uniform external pressure largely through hoop compression, but joint rotation, uneven load and backfill voids generate bending.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b117-v14-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「環向受力與接縫柔度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Ring force and joint flexibility\" is correct?","options":["混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。","引水內襯的平整度和接縫同時影響摩阻與結構，教材將環向量級和局部缺陷分開。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure.","Lining smoothness and joints affect hydraulics and structure; separate hoop-force scale from local defects.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error."],"answer":1,"explanation":"引水內襯的平整度和接縫同時影響摩阻與結構，教材將環向量級和局部缺陷分開。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Lining smoothness and joints affect hydraulics and structure; separate hoop-force scale from local defects. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b117-v14-26","title":"環向受力與接縫柔度：定量估算","titleEn":"Ring force and joint flexibility: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b117-v14-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「襯砌環向壓縮」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Lining hoop compression” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：均勻外壓=0.62 MPa；半徑=3.6 m；厚度=0.35 m。σθ=pr/t=6.37714 MPa。僅把均勻外壓增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為7.01486 MPa。邊界：薄圓環膜應力，不是接縫、偏壓或矩形框架解；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: uniform external pressure=0.62 MPa; radius=3.6 m; thickness=0.35 m. σθ=pr/t=6.37714 MPa. Increasing only uniform external pressure by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 7.01486 MPa. Boundary: Thin circular-ring membrane stress, not a joint, uneven-load or rectangular-frame solution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：把斷面掃描、接縫錯台和水理損失資料連結。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Link section scans, joint offsets and hydraulic-loss data.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b117-v14-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：均勻外壓=0.62 MPa；半徑=3.6 m；厚度=0.35 m。σθ=pr/t=6.37714 MPa。僅把均勻外壓增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為7.01486 MPa。邊界：薄圓環膜應力，不是接縫、偏壓或矩形框架解；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: uniform external pressure=0.62 MPa; radius=3.6 m; thickness=0.35 m. σθ=pr/t=6.37714 MPa. Increasing only uniform external pressure by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 7.01486 MPa. Boundary: Thin circular-ring membrane stress, not a joint, uneven-load or rectangular-frame solution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b117-v14-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「環向受力與接縫柔度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Ring force and joint flexibility\", which statement holds?","options":["施工後泉水變少就能單獨證明隧道造成全部減流。","岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。","原創教學假設：均勻外壓=0.62 MPa；半徑=3.6 m；厚度=0.35 m。"],"optionsEn":["Reduced spring flow after construction alone proves the tunnel caused the entire change.","Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow.","Original teaching assumptions: uniform external pressure=0.62 MPa; radius=3.6 m; thickness=0.35 m. σθ=pr/t=6.37714 MPa."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：均勻外壓=0.62 MPa；半徑=3.6 m；厚度=0.35 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: uniform external pressure=0.62 MPa; radius=3.6 m; thickness=0.35 m. σθ=pr/t=6.37714 MPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b117-v14-27","title":"環向受力與接縫柔度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Ring force and joint flexibility: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b117-v14-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「襯砌環向壓縮」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Lining hoop compression” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"把斷面掃描、接縫錯台和水理損失資料連結。將環形變形、接縫張開與應變和含接頭彈簧的模型比較，分開安裝後、背填後及水頭回升後的基準。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Link section scans, joint offsets and hydraulic-loss data. Compare ring distortion, joint opening and strain with a joint-spring model, separating baselines after installation, grouting and head recovery. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「襯砌環向壓縮」的交付需回答：把斷面掃描、接縫錯台和水理損失資料連結。設計圖應分開標註各施工階段、接頭剛度及背填條件，構件驗收同時核對幾何、材料批次與止水試驗適用包絡。","observationEn":"Site practice: For New Wujie water-conveyance tunnel, the lining hoop compression handover must address the following evidence: Link section scans, joint offsets and hydraulic-loss data. Drawings distinguish stages, joint stiffness and backfill conditions; component acceptance reconciles geometry, material batches and the applicable sealing-test envelope.","failure":"注意干擾：平均直徑合格仍可能有局部縮頸造成額外損失。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Acceptable mean diameter can conceal local constrictions and excess loss. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b117-v14-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"把斷面掃描、接縫錯台和水理損失資料連結。將環形變形、接縫張開與應變和含接頭彈簧的模型比較，分開安裝後、背填後及水頭回升後的基準。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Link section scans, joint offsets and hydraulic-loss data. Compare ring distortion, joint opening and strain with a joint-spring model, separating baselines after installation, grouting and head recovery. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b117-v14-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「襯砌環向壓縮」的交付需回答：把斷面掃描、接縫錯台和水理損失資料連結。設計圖應分開標註各施工階段、接頭剛度及背填條件，構件驗收同時核對幾何、材料批次與止水試驗適用包絡。","textEn":"For New Wujie water-conveyance tunnel, the lining hoop compression handover must address the following evidence: Link section scans, joint offsets and hydraulic-loss data. Drawings distinguish stages, joint stiffness and backfill conditions; component acceptance reconciles geometry, material batches and the applicable sealing-test envelope.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「環向受力與接縫柔度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Ring force and joint flexibility\"?","options":["把斷面掃描、接縫錯台和水理損失資料連結。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。"],"optionsEn":["Link section scans, joint offsets and hydraulic-loss data.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"把斷面掃描、接縫錯台和水理損失資料連結。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Link section scans, joint offsets and hydraulic-loss data. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b117-v14-28","title":"環向受力與接縫柔度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Ring force and joint flexibility: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b117-v14-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「襯砌環向壓縮」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Lining hoop compression” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"平均直徑合格仍可能有局部縮頸造成額外損失。局部脫空增加環片彎曲，裂縫未必代表混凝土平均強度不足；忽略接縫接觸會把補強方向導向錯誤位置。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Acceptable mean diameter can conceal local constrictions and excess loss. Local voids increase bending, so cracks need not indicate inadequate mean concrete strength; neglecting joint contact can misdirect strengthening. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：薄環膜應力只說明其中一條受力路徑；脫模、運輸、頂推及永久狀態的荷載不同，環片局部接觸與止水條件必須另外檢核。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Demoulding, transport, jacking and permanent states impose different actions, requiring separate checks of local segment contact and sealing rather than one permanent-load calculation.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b117-v14-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"平均直徑合格仍可能有局部縮頸造成額外損失。局部脫空增加環片彎曲，裂縫未必代表混凝土平均強度不足；忽略接縫接觸會把補強方向導向錯誤位置。","textEn":"Acceptable mean diameter can conceal local constrictions and excess loss. Local voids increase bending, so cracks need not indicate inadequate mean concrete strength; neglecting joint contact can misdirect strengthening.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b117-v14-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「環向受力與接縫柔度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Ring force and joint flexibility\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","平均直徑合格仍可能有局部縮頸造成額外損失。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Acceptable mean diameter can conceal local constrictions and excess loss.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error."],"answer":1,"explanation":"平均直徑合格仍可能有局部縮頸造成額外損失。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Acceptable mean diameter can conceal local constrictions and excess loss. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b117-v14-29","title":"控制網與貫通誤差：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b117-v14-28"],"objective":"說明「方向角誤差」如何影響新武界引水隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Orientation error” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “New Wujie water-conveyance tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"引水坡度微小時高程誤差可改變排水與淨空判讀，新武界教材強調共同高程基準。長隧道的微小方向誤差會沿距離累積，地下控制網又缺少直接衛星定位，必須把地表基準可靠傳到洞內。閉合差很小不代表無系統誤差；尺度、折光、儀器定向與高程基準可能共同偏移，誤差相關性也使平方和估算失真。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「方向角誤差」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"With small conveyance gradients, height errors alter drainage and clearance interpretation; maintain a common elevation reference. Small orientation errors accumulate over long drives, while underground networks lack direct satellite positioning and depend on transferring surface control. A small closure does not exclude systematic bias: scale, refraction, orientation and vertical datum may shift together. Correlated errors also invalidate a naive root-sum-square combination of supposedly independent observations. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Orientation error” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：控制長度=4920 m；方向偏角=2.7 arcsec。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: control length=4920 m; orientation error=2.7 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0644026 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「方向角誤差」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Orientation error”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b117-v14-29-k1","title":"控制網與貫通誤差","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error","text":"引水坡度微小時高程誤差可改變排水與淨空判讀，新武界教材強調共同高程基準。長隧道的微小方向誤差會沿距離累積，地下控制網又缺少直接衛星定位，必須把地表基準可靠傳到洞內。","textEn":"With small conveyance gradients, height errors alter drainage and clearance interpretation; maintain a common elevation reference. Small orientation errors accumulate over long drives, while underground networks lack direct satellite positioning and depend on transferring surface control.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b117-v14-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「控制網與貫通誤差」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Control network and breakthrough error\" is correct?","options":["兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。","增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。","引水坡度微小時高程誤差可改變排水與淨空判讀，新武界教材強調共同高程基準。"],"optionsEn":["Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.","Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.","With small conveyance gradients, height errors alter drainage and clearance interpretation; maintain a common elevation reference."],"answer":2,"explanation":"引水坡度微小時高程誤差可改變排水與淨空判讀，新武界教材強調共同高程基準。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"With small conveyance gradients, height errors alter drainage and clearance interpretation; maintain a common elevation reference. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b117-v14-30","title":"控制網與貫通誤差：定量估算","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b117-v14-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「方向角誤差」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Orientation error” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：控制長度=4920 m；方向偏角=2.7 arcsec。e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0644026 m。僅把方向偏角增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.0708429 m。邊界：小角度方向偏差，未加入控制網相關性及折光；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: control length=4920 m; orientation error=2.7 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0644026 m. Increasing only orientation error by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.0708429 m. Boundary: Small-angle orientation error without network correlation or refraction. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：由獨立水準路線重算進出口及中段高程。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Recompute inlet, outlet and intermediate elevations through independent levelling.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b117-v14-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：控制長度=4920 m；方向偏角=2.7 arcsec。e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0644026 m。僅把方向偏角增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.0708429 m。邊界：小角度方向偏差，未加入控制網相關性及折光；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: control length=4920 m; orientation error=2.7 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0644026 m. Increasing only orientation error by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.0708429 m. Boundary: Small-angle orientation error without network correlation or refraction. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b117-v14-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「控制網與貫通誤差」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Control network and breakthrough error\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：控制長度=4920 m；方向偏角=2.7 arcsec。","水體流過全程的時間必然等於洪峰抵達的時間。","目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: control length=4920 m; orientation error=2.7 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0644026 m.","Material travel time necessarily equals flood-peak arrival time.","No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：控制長度=4920 m；方向偏角=2.7 arcsec。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: control length=4920 m; orientation error=2.7 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0644026 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b117-v14-31","title":"控制網與貫通誤差：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b117-v14-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「方向角誤差」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Orientation error” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"由獨立水準路線重算進出口及中段高程。由獨立測量組複核地表到洞內的轉換，保留原始角距及溫度資料，用不同控制線比較方向與高程偏差。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Recompute inlet, outlet and intermediate elevations through independent levelling. Independently check surface-to-tunnel transformations, retain raw angles, distances and temperatures, and compare orientation and elevation through separate control routes. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「方向角誤差」的交付需回答：由獨立水準路線重算進出口及中段高程。貫通前凍結座標、尺度與高程版本，獨立組直接使用原始觀測重算；不得只傳遞整理好的坐標而遺失校正資訊。","observationEn":"Site practice: For New Wujie water-conveyance tunnel, the orientation error handover must address the following evidence: Recompute inlet, outlet and intermediate elevations through independent levelling. Freeze coordinate, scale and height revisions before breakthrough; independent reviewers recompute raw observations rather than receiving only adjusted coordinates without corrections.","failure":"注意干擾：角度閉合好不證明縱斷面水準沒有系統偏差。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Good angular closure does not establish an unbiased longitudinal level profile. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b117-v14-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"由獨立水準路線重算進出口及中段高程。由獨立測量組複核地表到洞內的轉換，保留原始角距及溫度資料，用不同控制線比較方向與高程偏差。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Recompute inlet, outlet and intermediate elevations through independent levelling. Independently check surface-to-tunnel transformations, retain raw angles, distances and temperatures, and compare orientation and elevation through separate control routes. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b117-v14-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「方向角誤差」的交付需回答：由獨立水準路線重算進出口及中段高程。貫通前凍結座標、尺度與高程版本，獨立組直接使用原始觀測重算；不得只傳遞整理好的坐標而遺失校正資訊。","textEn":"For New Wujie water-conveyance tunnel, the orientation error handover must address the following evidence: Recompute inlet, outlet and intermediate elevations through independent levelling. Freeze coordinate, scale and height revisions before breakthrough; independent reviewers recompute raw observations rather than receiving only adjusted coordinates without corrections.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「控制網與貫通誤差」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Control network and breakthrough error\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","由獨立水準路線重算進出口及中段高程。","支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Recompute inlet, outlet and intermediate elevations through independent levelling.","Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem."],"answer":1,"explanation":"由獨立水準路線重算進出口及中段高程。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Recompute inlet, outlet and intermediate elevations through independent levelling. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b117-v14-32","title":"控制網與貫通誤差：失效診斷","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b117-v14-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「方向角誤差」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Orientation error” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"角度閉合好不證明縱斷面水準沒有系統偏差。共用錯誤基準可能讓兩組測量同時看似一致，直到貫通或軌道銜接才發現系統偏差，修正成本遠高於早期複核。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Good angular closure does not establish an unbiased longitudinal level profile. A shared wrong datum can make separate surveys appear consistent until breakthrough or track connection exposes bias that is costly to correct. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：閉合差很小不代表無系統誤差；尺度、折光、儀器定向與高程基準可能共同偏移，誤差相關性也使平方和估算失真。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Correlated errors also invalidate a naive root-sum-square combination of supposedly independent observations.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b117-v14-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"角度閉合好不證明縱斷面水準沒有系統偏差。共用錯誤基準可能讓兩組測量同時看似一致，直到貫通或軌道銜接才發現系統偏差，修正成本遠高於早期複核。","textEn":"Good angular closure does not establish an unbiased longitudinal level profile. A shared wrong datum can make separate surveys appear consistent until breakthrough or track connection exposes bias that is costly to correct.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b117-v14-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「控制網與貫通誤差」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Control network and breakthrough error\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。","角度閉合好不證明縱斷面水準沒有系統偏差。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.","Good angular closure does not establish an unbiased longitudinal level profile."],"answer":2,"explanation":"角度閉合好不證明縱斷面水準沒有系統偏差。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Good angular closure does not establish an unbiased longitudinal level profile. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b117-v14-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」與「水量帳與環境受體」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Shared access and transport bottlenecks\" and \"Water balance and environmental receptors\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b117-v14-33","title":"共享通道與運輸瓶頸：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Shared access and transport bottlenecks: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b117-v14-32"],"objective":"說明「出渣運輸節拍」如何影響新武界引水隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Muck-transport cycle” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “New Wujie water-conveyance tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"山區引水工程多面施工仍受材料、出渣及維修通道限制，教材把機械產能與供應節拍分開。多工作面只有在供電、通風、出渣與材料供應同步充足時才增加總產量。共用豎井或軌道形成串聯瓶頸，排隊和維修窗口會降低名目容量；緩衝區太大又可能侵占通行與救援空間，因此不能單純把各面產能相加。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「出渣運輸節拍」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Multiple mountain headings remain limited by material, spoil and maintenance access; distinguish machine capacity from supply cycle. Multiple headings increase output only when power, air, muck transport and materials support them together. Shared shafts or railways become serial bottlenecks, while queues and maintenance reduce nominal capacity. Large buffers may obstruct personnel and rescue access, so face capacities cannot simply be added without a network-level transport and storage check. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Muck-transport cycle” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=36 t；往返週期=38 min。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=36 t; cycle=38 min.","failure":"常見誤解：「增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「出渣運輸節拍」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Muck-transport cycle”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b117-v14-33-k1","title":"共享通道與運輸瓶頸","titleEn":"Shared access and transport bottlenecks","text":"山區引水工程多面施工仍受材料、出渣及維修通道限制，教材把機械產能與供應節拍分開。多工作面只有在供電、通風、出渣與材料供應同步充足時才增加總產量。","textEn":"Multiple mountain headings remain limited by material, spoil and maintenance access; distinguish machine capacity from supply cycle. Multiple headings increase output only when power, air, muck transport and materials support them together.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b117-v14-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Shared access and transport bottlenecks\" is correct?","options":["山區引水工程多面施工仍受材料、出渣及維修通道限制，教材把機械產能與供應節拍分開。","增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。","施工後泉水變少就能單獨證明隧道造成全部減流。"],"optionsEn":["Multiple mountain headings remain limited by material, spoil and maintenance access; distinguish machine capacity from supply cycle.","Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.","Reduced spring flow after construction alone proves the tunnel caused the entire change."],"answer":0,"explanation":"山區引水工程多面施工仍受材料、出渣及維修通道限制，教材把機械產能與供應節拍分開。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Multiple mountain headings remain limited by material, spoil and maintenance access; distinguish machine capacity from supply cycle. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b117-v14-34","title":"共享通道與運輸瓶頸：定量估算","titleEn":"Shared access and transport bottlenecks: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b117-v14-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「出渣運輸節拍」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Muck-transport cycle” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=36 t；往返週期=38 min。C=N payload 60/T=227.368 t/h。僅把往返週期增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為206.699 t/h。邊界：無排隊理想循環，並非共享路段實際產能；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=36 t; cycle=38 min. C=N payload 60/T=227.368 t/h. Increasing only cycle by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 206.699 t/h. Boundary: Ideal cycle without queues, not actual shared-route production. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對環片或內襯材料、刀具和出渣的共用占時。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check shared access time for lining materials, cutters and spoil.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b117-v14-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=36 t；往返週期=38 min。C=N payload 60/T=227.368 t/h。僅把往返週期增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為206.699 t/h。邊界：無排隊理想循環，並非共享路段實際產能；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=36 t; cycle=38 min. C=N payload 60/T=227.368 t/h. Increasing only cycle by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 206.699 t/h. Boundary: Ideal cycle without queues, not actual shared-route production. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b117-v14-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Shared access and transport bottlenecks\", which statement holds?","options":["岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。","原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=36 t；往返週期=38 min。","刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。"],"optionsEn":["Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow.","Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=36 t; cycle=38 min.","A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=36 t；往返週期=38 min。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=36 t; cycle=38 min. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b117-v14-35","title":"共享通道與運輸瓶頸：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Shared access and transport bottlenecks: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b117-v14-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「出渣運輸節拍」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Muck-transport cycle” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對環片或內襯材料、刀具和出渣的共用占時。以裝載質量、往返時間及排隊時間重建物流曲線，再核對緩衝占用、共用通道優先權與維修時段。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check shared access time for lining materials, cutters and spoil. Reconstruct flow from payload, round-trip and queue times, then check buffer occupancy, shared-route priorities and maintenance periods. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「出渣運輸節拍」的交付需回答：核對環片或內襯材料、刀具和出渣的共用占時。每日排程同時標示人員、材料和維修的占用時段，任何物流改線先檢查通風與應變通道，不能只看運量提升。","observationEn":"Site practice: For New Wujie water-conveyance tunnel, the muck-transport cycle handover must address the following evidence: Check shared access time for lining materials, cutters and spoil. Schedules show personnel, materials and maintenance occupancy together; rerouting first checks ventilation and emergency access rather than only throughput gains.","failure":"注意干擾：出渣優先若排擠刀具維修會降低後續有效切削時間。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Spoil priority that displaces cutter maintenance reduces later productive cutting. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b117-v14-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對環片或內襯材料、刀具和出渣的共用占時。以裝載質量、往返時間及排隊時間重建物流曲線，再核對緩衝占用、共用通道優先權與維修時段。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Check shared access time for lining materials, cutters and spoil. Reconstruct flow from payload, round-trip and queue times, then check buffer occupancy, shared-route priorities and maintenance periods. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b117-v14-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「出渣運輸節拍」的交付需回答：核對環片或內襯材料、刀具和出渣的共用占時。每日排程同時標示人員、材料和維修的占用時段，任何物流改線先檢查通風與應變通道，不能只看運量提升。","textEn":"For New Wujie water-conveyance tunnel, the muck-transport cycle handover must address the following evidence: Check shared access time for lining materials, cutters and spoil. Schedules show personnel, materials and maintenance occupancy together; rerouting first checks ventilation and emergency access rather than only throughput gains.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Shared access and transport bottlenecks\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","只算穩態流量就能排除輸水隧道的水錘與氣囊。","核對環片或內襯材料、刀具和出渣的共用占時。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","A steady-flow calculation excludes water hammer and trapped air in a conveyance tunnel.","Check shared access time for lining materials, cutters and spoil."],"answer":2,"explanation":"核對環片或內襯材料、刀具和出渣的共用占時。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check shared access time for lining materials, cutters and spoil. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b117-v14-36","title":"共享通道與運輸瓶頸：失效診斷","titleEn":"Shared access and transport bottlenecks: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b117-v14-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「出渣運輸節拍」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Muck-transport cycle” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"出渣優先若排擠刀具維修會降低後續有效切削時間。把理想往返時間當全天常數會忽略交會等待與卸料堵塞，導致工作面停工或把材料堆入必要通道。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Spoil priority that displaces cutter maintenance reduces later productive cutting. Treating an ideal cycle as constant all day misses passing delays and unloading blockages, stopping headings or pushing material into essential access space. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：共用豎井或軌道形成串聯瓶頸，排隊和維修窗口會降低名目容量；緩衝區太大又可能侵占通行與救援空間，因此不能單純把各面產能相加。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Large buffers may obstruct personnel and rescue access, so face capacities cannot simply be added without a network-level transport and storage check.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b117-v14-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"出渣優先若排擠刀具維修會降低後續有效切削時間。把理想往返時間當全天常數會忽略交會等待與卸料堵塞，導致工作面停工或把材料堆入必要通道。","textEn":"Spoil priority that displaces cutter maintenance reduces later productive cutting. Treating an ideal cycle as constant all day misses passing delays and unloading blockages, stopping headings or pushing material into essential access space.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b117-v14-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Shared access and transport bottlenecks\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["出渣優先若排擠刀具維修會降低後續有效切削時間。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","施工後泉水變少就能單獨證明隧道造成全部減流。"],"optionsEn":["Spoil priority that displaces cutter maintenance reduces later productive cutting.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Reduced spring flow after construction alone proves the tunnel caused the entire change."],"answer":0,"explanation":"出渣優先若排擠刀具維修會降低後續有效切削時間。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Spoil priority that displaces cutter maintenance reduces later productive cutting. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b117-v14-37","title":"水量帳與環境受體：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Water balance and environmental receptors: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b117-v14-36"],"objective":"說明「邊界水量差」如何影響新武界引水隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Boundary water-balance residual” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “New Wujie water-conveyance tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"引水目的與施工排水可能改變不同流域受體，本課以水量帳區分轉移水、地層滲水和天然補注。隧道排水可能改變泉水、溪流或地下水補注，但同時還有降雨、季節與既有抽水等影響。水量平衡需要明確時間和空間邊界，殘差不能直接歸因於某一裂隙；應用施工前基線和對照站區分自然變化與工程效應。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「邊界水量差」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Conveyance and construction drainage affect different receptors; separate transferred water, groundwater inflow and natural recharge. Tunnel drainage may alter springs, streams or groundwater recharge, alongside rainfall, seasonal change and existing abstraction. A water balance needs explicit temporal and spatial boundaries; its residual cannot be assigned directly to one fracture. Baseline observations and control locations help separate natural variability from construction effects rather than equating correlation with causation. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Boundary water-balance residual” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：流入=148 m³/day；流出=79 m³/day；其他損失=20 m³/day。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: inflow=148 m³/day; outflow=79 m³/day; other loss=20 m³/day. ΔS=I−O−loss=49 m³/day.","failure":"常見誤解：「施工後泉水變少就能單獨證明隧道造成全部減流。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Reduced spring flow after construction alone proves the tunnel caused the entire change.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「邊界水量差」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Boundary water-balance residual”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b117-v14-37-k1","title":"水量帳與環境受體","titleEn":"Water balance and environmental receptors","text":"引水目的與施工排水可能改變不同流域受體，本課以水量帳區分轉移水、地層滲水和天然補注。隧道排水可能改變泉水、溪流或地下水補注，但同時還有降雨、季節與既有抽水等影響。","textEn":"Conveyance and construction drainage affect different receptors; separate transferred water, groundwater inflow and natural recharge. Tunnel drainage may alter springs, streams or groundwater recharge, alongside rainfall, seasonal change and existing abstraction.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b117-v14-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：施工後泉水變少就能單獨證明隧道造成全部減流。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Reduced spring flow after construction alone proves the tunnel caused the entire change. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「水量帳與環境受體」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Water balance and environmental receptors\" is correct?","options":["施工後泉水變少就能單獨證明隧道造成全部減流。","引水目的與施工排水可能改變不同流域受體，本課以水量帳區分轉移水、地層滲水和天然補注。","水體流過全程的時間必然等於洪峰抵達的時間。"],"optionsEn":["Reduced spring flow after construction alone proves the tunnel caused the entire change.","Conveyance and construction drainage affect different receptors; separate transferred water, groundwater inflow and natural recharge.","Material travel time necessarily equals flood-peak arrival time."],"answer":1,"explanation":"引水目的與施工排水可能改變不同流域受體，本課以水量帳區分轉移水、地層滲水和天然補注。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Conveyance and construction drainage affect different receptors; separate transferred water, groundwater inflow and natural recharge. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b117-v14-38","title":"水量帳與環境受體：定量估算","titleEn":"Water balance and environmental receptors: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b117-v14-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「邊界水量差」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Boundary water-balance residual” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：流入=148 m³/day；流出=79 m³/day；其他損失=20 m³/day。ΔS=I−O−loss=49 m³/day。僅把流入增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為63.8 m³/day。邊界：指定邊界日水量帳，不是因果或含水層參數證明；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: inflow=148 m³/day; outflow=79 m³/day; other loss=20 m³/day. ΔS=I−O−loss=49 m³/day. Increasing only inflow by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 63.8 m³/day. Boundary: Daily balance in a stated boundary, not causal proof or aquifer-parameter identification. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：明示集水區和時間邊界，以對照點核對季節變化。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: State catchment and time boundaries and use controls to check seasonality.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b117-v14-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：流入=148 m³/day；流出=79 m³/day；其他損失=20 m³/day。ΔS=I−O−loss=49 m³/day。僅把流入增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為63.8 m³/day。邊界：指定邊界日水量帳，不是因果或含水層參數證明；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: inflow=148 m³/day; outflow=79 m³/day; other loss=20 m³/day. ΔS=I−O−loss=49 m³/day. Increasing only inflow by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 63.8 m³/day. Boundary: Daily balance in a stated boundary, not causal proof or aquifer-parameter identification. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b117-v14-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「水量帳與環境受體」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Water balance and environmental receptors\", which statement holds?","options":["目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。","支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。","原創教學假設：流入=148 m³/day；流出=79 m³/day；其他損失=20 m³/day。"],"optionsEn":["No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.","Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem.","Original teaching assumptions: inflow=148 m³/day; outflow=79 m³/day; other loss=20 m³/day. ΔS=I−O−loss=49 m³/day."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：流入=148 m³/day；流出=79 m³/day；其他損失=20 m³/day。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: inflow=148 m³/day; outflow=79 m³/day; other loss=20 m³/day. ΔS=I−O−loss=49 m³/day. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b117-v14-39","title":"水量帳與環境受體：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Water balance and environmental receptors: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b117-v14-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「邊界水量差」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Boundary water-balance residual” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"明示集水區和時間邊界，以對照點核對季節變化。同步比較雨量、泉流、排水與對照井，核對儀器缺測和蓄水變化，對不同季節分別閉合水量帳。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"State catchment and time boundaries and use controls to check seasonality. Compare rainfall, spring flow, drainage and control wells, checking missing data and storage change and closing balances separately by season. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「邊界水量差」的交付需回答：明示集水區和時間邊界，以對照點核對季節變化。預先定義受體、基線及資料缺口，任何因果判斷都需列出替代解釋，補救效果也用同一監測邊界評估。","observationEn":"Site practice: For New Wujie water-conveyance tunnel, the boundary water-balance residual handover must address the following evidence: State catchment and time boundaries and use controls to check seasonality. Define receptors, baselines and data gaps beforehand; causal judgements list alternatives, and mitigation is evaluated within the same monitoring boundary.","failure":"注意干擾：將轉引水量視為地下水損失會錯估環境影響來源。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Treating diverted surface water as groundwater loss misidentifies environmental effects. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b117-v14-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"明示集水區和時間邊界，以對照點核對季節變化。同步比較雨量、泉流、排水與對照井，核對儀器缺測和蓄水變化，對不同季節分別閉合水量帳。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"State catchment and time boundaries and use controls to check seasonality. Compare rainfall, spring flow, drainage and control wells, checking missing data and storage change and closing balances separately by season. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b117-v14-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「邊界水量差」的交付需回答：明示集水區和時間邊界，以對照點核對季節變化。預先定義受體、基線及資料缺口，任何因果判斷都需列出替代解釋，補救效果也用同一監測邊界評估。","textEn":"For New Wujie water-conveyance tunnel, the boundary water-balance residual handover must address the following evidence: State catchment and time boundaries and use controls to check seasonality. Define receptors, baselines and data gaps beforehand; causal judgements list alternatives, and mitigation is evaluated within the same monitoring boundary.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「水量帳與環境受體」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Water balance and environmental receptors\"?","options":["明示集水區和時間邊界，以對照點核對季節變化。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。"],"optionsEn":["State catchment and time boundaries and use controls to check seasonality.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure."],"answer":0,"explanation":"明示集水區和時間邊界，以對照點核對季節變化。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"State catchment and time boundaries and use controls to check seasonality. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b117-v14-40","title":"水量帳與環境受體：失效診斷","titleEn":"Water balance and environmental receptors: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b117-v14-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「邊界水量差」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Boundary water-balance residual” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"將轉引水量視為地下水損失會錯估環境影響來源。未量到的支流或時間錯位會產生假性水量損失，錯把所有減流歸於隧道可能導致無效補救。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Treating diverted surface water as groundwater loss misidentifies environmental effects. Unmeasured tributaries or timing mismatch create false losses; attributing every decrease to the tunnel can prompt ineffective mitigation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：水量平衡需要明確時間和空間邊界，殘差不能直接歸因於某一裂隙；應用施工前基線和對照站區分自然變化與工程效應。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Baseline observations and control locations help separate natural variability from construction effects rather than equating correlation with causation.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「施工後泉水變少就能單獨證明隧道造成全部減流。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Reduced spring flow after construction alone proves the tunnel caused the entire change.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b117-v14-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"將轉引水量視為地下水損失會錯估環境影響來源。未量到的支流或時間錯位會產生假性水量損失，錯把所有減流歸於隧道可能導致無效補救。","textEn":"Treating diverted surface water as groundwater loss misidentifies environmental effects. Unmeasured tributaries or timing mismatch create false losses; attributing every decrease to the tunnel can prompt ineffective mitigation.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b117-v14-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「水量帳與環境受體」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Water balance and environmental receptors\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","將轉引水量視為地下水損失會錯估環境影響來源。","水體流過全程的時間必然等於洪峰抵達的時間。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Treating diverted surface water as groundwater loss misidentifies environmental effects.","Material travel time necessarily equals flood-peak arrival time."],"answer":1,"explanation":"將轉引水量視為地下水損失會錯估環境影響來源。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Treating diverted surface water as groundwater loss misidentifies environmental effects. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b117","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"curriculumVersion":14,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000},{"id":"b118","title":"蘇花改觀音隧道","titleEn":"Suhua Highway Guanyin Tunnel","category":"underground","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"公路機關列觀音隧道約7.9公里、雙孔單向配置，並記錄利用舊北迴隧道增加施工工作面。本課從這項既有設施再利用出發，分析地質弱帶、地下水、控制網、施工交通與通風設備介面；貫通和2020年蘇花改全線通車是不同事件，課程不把兩者混為一談。","summaryEn":"The highway authority describes Guanyin as approximately 7.9 km with twin directional bores and reuse of an old railway tunnel to create working faces. This course follows weak ground, groundwater, survey, construction traffic and ventilation interfaces. Breakthrough and the 2020 opening of the full Suhua improvement corridor remain distinct events.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"ug-landmarks","subcategoryTitle":"世界隧道與地下巨作","subcategoryTitleEn":"World tunnels and underground landmarks","learningTrack":"underground","learningSubdiscipline":"ug-landmarks","learningTags":["underground","ug-landmarks","tunnel"],"architectureFamily":"tunnel","architectureNodes":[["路線里程與端點","Alignment chainage and endpoints"],["破碎帶連通性","Fault-zone connectivity"],["支護安裝時點","Support activation time"],["方向角誤差","Orientation error"],["風道摩擦壓損","Duct friction loss"],["資產資料完整度","Asset-record completeness"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,5],[1,5]],"diagram":{"type":"tunnel","labels":["路線里程與端點","破碎帶連通性","支護安裝時點","方向角誤差","風道摩擦壓損"],"labelsEn":["Alignment chainage and endpoints","Fault-zone connectivity","Support activation time","Orientation error","Duct friction loss"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"原創綜合審查：先計算「破碎帶連通與預報更新」，再獨立計算「控制網與貫通誤差」。原創教學假設：滲透係數=3e-06 m/s；水力坡降=2.1 無因次；通水面積=370 m²。Q=k i A=0.002331 m³/s。僅把滲透係數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.0025641 m³/s。邊界：均質飽和達西流，不代表裂隙集中流；不是本工程實測或允收值。原創教學假設：控制長度=5040 m；方向偏角=2.5 arcsec。e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0610865 m。僅把方向偏角增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.0671952 m。邊界：小角度方向偏差，未加入控制網相關性及折光；不是本工程實測或允收值。兩組結果的單位與邊界不同，不能直接相加。請列出一項缺少的現場輸入，說明它會影響哪個結論，以及哪種獨立量測可以縮小不確定度。","textEn":"Original integrated review: first calculate fault connectivity and forecast updating, then independently calculate control network and breakthrough error. Original teaching assumptions: conductivity=3e-06 m/s; hydraulic gradient=2.1 dimensionless; flow area=370 m². Q=k i A=0.002331 m³/s. Increasing only conductivity by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.0025641 m³/s. Boundary: Homogeneous saturated Darcy flow, not concentrated fracture flow. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Original teaching assumptions: control length=5040 m; orientation error=2.5 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0610865 m. Increasing only orientation error by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.0671952 m. Boundary: Small-angle orientation error without network correlation or refraction. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. The outputs have different units and boundaries and cannot simply be added. Identify one missing field input, explain which conclusion it changes and select an independent measurement to reduce uncertainty.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":14,"enrichmentVersion":14,"stages":[{"id":"b118-v14-s1","title":"地層條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Ground conditions, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「服務邊界與路線代價」與「破碎帶連通與預報更新」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\" and \"Fault connectivity and forecast updating\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b118-v14-01","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「路線里程與端點」如何影響蘇花改觀音隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Alignment chainage and endpoints” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Suhua Highway Guanyin Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"觀音與鄰接谷風及短橋形成連續服務路廊，教材分開單隧道里程與系統連續行車範圍。隧道選線同時改變洞口、覆土與縱坡，短路線不保證低地質風險。比較方案必須使用相同起訖點，並分開主孔、引道及服務坑的工程數量；交通時間只是需求的一個指標，不能代替施工可達性或長期維修評估。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「路線里程與端點」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Guanyin and neighbouring tunnel-bridge links form a continuous corridor; distinguish one tunnel length from the operational route. Alignment changes portals, cover and gradient together, so a shorter tunnel need not have lower geological risk. Compare options between identical endpoints and distinguish running bores, approaches and service galleries. Travel time measures one service benefit but cannot replace assessment of construction access, maintenance closures or exposure to uncertain ground. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Alignment chainage and endpoints” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：長度=18.8 km；速度=60 km/h。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: length=18.8 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=18.8 min.","failure":"常見誤解：「最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「路線里程與端點」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Alignment chainage and endpoints”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b118-v14-01-k1","title":"服務邊界與路線代價","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost","text":"觀音與鄰接谷風及短橋形成連續服務路廊，教材分開單隧道里程與系統連續行車範圍。隧道選線同時改變洞口、覆土與縱坡，短路線不保證低地質風險。","textEn":"Guanyin and neighbouring tunnel-bridge links form a continuous corridor; distinguish one tunnel length from the operational route. Alignment changes portals, cover and gradient together, so a shorter tunnel need not have lower geological risk.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]},{"id":"b118-v14-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「服務邊界與路線代價」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\" is correct?","options":["最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。","觀音與鄰接谷風及短橋形成連續服務路廊，教材分開單隧道里程與系統連續行車範圍。","岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。"],"optionsEn":["The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.","Guanyin and neighbouring tunnel-bridge links form a continuous corridor; distinguish one tunnel length from the operational route.","Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow."],"answer":1,"explanation":"觀音與鄰接谷風及短橋形成連續服務路廊，教材分開單隧道里程與系統連續行車範圍。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Guanyin and neighbouring tunnel-bridge links form a continuous corridor; distinguish one tunnel length from the operational route. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b118-v14-02","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：定量估算","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b118-v14-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「路線里程與端點」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Alignment chainage and endpoints” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：長度=18.8 km；速度=60 km/h。t=60L/v=18.8 min。僅把長度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為20.68 min。邊界：假想交通旅程，未含加減速、排隊及實際時刻表；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: length=18.8 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=18.8 min. Increasing only length by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 20.68 min. Boundary: Hypothetical transport journey excluding acceleration, queues and the real timetable. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以相同起訖點核對觀音、橋及鄰洞的範圍。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Reconcile Guanyin, bridge and adjacent-bore scope between fixed endpoints.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b118-v14-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：長度=18.8 km；速度=60 km/h。t=60L/v=18.8 min。僅把長度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為20.68 min。邊界：假想交通旅程，未含加減速、排隊及實際時刻表；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: length=18.8 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=18.8 min. Increasing only length by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 20.68 min. Boundary: Hypothetical transport journey excluding acceleration, queues and the real timetable. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]},{"id":"b118-v14-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「服務邊界與路線代價」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\", which statement holds?","options":["支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。","原創教學假設：長度=18.8 km；速度=60 km/h。"],"optionsEn":["Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.","Original teaching assumptions: length=18.8 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=18.8 min."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：長度=18.8 km；速度=60 km/h。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: length=18.8 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=18.8 min. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b118-v14-03","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b118-v14-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「路線里程與端點」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Alignment chainage and endpoints” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以相同起訖點核對觀音、橋及鄰洞的範圍。把縱斷面、地形與地質剖面疊合，以端點坐標獨立反算距離，再將主孔與支坑數量分開核對。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Reconcile Guanyin, bridge and adjacent-bore scope between fixed endpoints. Overlay the longitudinal profile, terrain and geology; independently derive distances from endpoint coordinates and reconcile running-bore and gallery quantities separately. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「路線里程與端點」的交付需回答：以相同起訖點核對觀音、橋及鄰洞的範圍。在方案表中凍結起訖點、計量範圍及地質假設，任何改線都要同步更新高程、數量與服務情境，不能只替換總長。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Suhua Highway Guanyin Tunnel, the alignment chainage and endpoints handover must address the following evidence: Reconcile Guanyin, bridge and adjacent-bore scope between fixed endpoints. Freeze endpoints, measurement scope and ground assumptions in the option register; realignment requires coordinated updates to elevations, quantities and service scenarios rather than replacing one length.","failure":"注意干擾：只看單洞長度可能漏掉鄰洞事故對交通及救援的影響。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Single-bore length misses adjacent-tunnel effects on traffic and rescue. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b118-v14-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以相同起訖點核對觀音、橋及鄰洞的範圍。把縱斷面、地形與地質剖面疊合，以端點坐標獨立反算距離，再將主孔與支坑數量分開核對。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Reconcile Guanyin, bridge and adjacent-bore scope between fixed endpoints. Overlay the longitudinal profile, terrain and geology; independently derive distances from endpoint coordinates and reconcile running-bore and gallery quantities separately. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]},{"id":"b118-v14-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「路線里程與端點」的交付需回答：以相同起訖點核對觀音、橋及鄰洞的範圍。在方案表中凍結起訖點、計量範圍及地質假設，任何改線都要同步更新高程、數量與服務情境，不能只替換總長。","textEn":"For Suhua Highway Guanyin Tunnel, the alignment chainage and endpoints handover must address the following evidence: Reconcile Guanyin, bridge and adjacent-bore scope between fixed endpoints. Freeze endpoints, measurement scope and ground assumptions in the option register; realignment requires coordinated updates to elevations, quantities and service scenarios rather than replacing one length.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「服務邊界與路線代價」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\"?","options":["以相同起訖點核對觀音、橋及鄰洞的範圍。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。"],"optionsEn":["Reconcile Guanyin, bridge and adjacent-bore scope between fixed endpoints.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以相同起訖點核對觀音、橋及鄰洞的範圍。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Reconcile Guanyin, bridge and adjacent-bore scope between fixed endpoints. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b118-v14-04","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：失效診斷","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b118-v14-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「路線里程與端點」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Alignment chainage and endpoints” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只看單洞長度可能漏掉鄰洞事故對交通及救援的影響。混用全線與單孔長度會同時扭曲工程數量、行程及逃生距離，造成方案比較失去共同基準。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Single-bore length misses adjacent-tunnel effects on traffic and rescue. Mixing whole-route and single-bore lengths distorts quantities, journey time and escape distance, destroying the common basis of an option comparison. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：比較方案必須使用相同起訖點，並分開主孔、引道及服務坑的工程數量；交通時間只是需求的一個指標，不能代替施工可達性或長期維修評估。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Travel time measures one service benefit but cannot replace assessment of construction access, maintenance closures or exposure to uncertain ground.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b118-v14-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只看單洞長度可能漏掉鄰洞事故對交通及救援的影響。混用全線與單孔長度會同時扭曲工程數量、行程及逃生距離，造成方案比較失去共同基準。","textEn":"Single-bore length misses adjacent-tunnel effects on traffic and rescue. Mixing whole-route and single-bore lengths distorts quantities, journey time and escape distance, destroying the common basis of an option comparison.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]},{"id":"b118-v14-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「服務邊界與路線代價」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","只看單洞長度可能漏掉鄰洞事故對交通及救援的影響。","岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Single-bore length misses adjacent-tunnel effects on traffic and rescue.","Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow."],"answer":1,"explanation":"只看單洞長度可能漏掉鄰洞事故對交通及救援的影響。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Single-bore length misses adjacent-tunnel effects on traffic and rescue. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b118-v14-05","title":"破碎帶連通與預報更新：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Fault connectivity and forecast updating: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b118-v14-04"],"objective":"說明「破碎帶連通性」如何影響蘇花改觀音隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Fault-zone connectivity” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Suhua Highway Guanyin Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"觀音公開論壇討論地質弱帶，本課研究裂隙填充、產狀和掌子面水量如何共同修正預報。斷層帶可以含很硬的岩塊，但整體變形與湧水常由填充節理和連通裂隙控制。單一岩芯強度不能代表整個掌子面；超前鑽孔、出水變化與揭露地質須回饋同一里程模型，預報則應保留不同情境及其證據權重。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「破碎帶連通性」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Official technical forums discuss weak zones; combine infill, orientation and face inflow to update forecasts. A fault zone may contain strong intact blocks while filled joints and connected fractures govern its bulk deformation and inflow. One core strength does not represent the entire face. Probe records, water response and exposed geology must update a common chainage model, preserving competing interpretations and their evidential weight rather than treating a forecast as certainty. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Fault-zone connectivity” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：滲透係數=3e-06 m/s；水力坡降=2.1 無因次；通水面積=370 m²。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: conductivity=3e-06 m/s; hydraulic gradient=2.1 dimensionless; flow area=370 m².","failure":"常見誤解：「岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「破碎帶連通性」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Fault-zone connectivity”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b118-v14-05-k1","title":"破碎帶連通與預報更新","titleEn":"Fault connectivity and forecast updating","text":"觀音公開論壇討論地質弱帶，本課研究裂隙填充、產狀和掌子面水量如何共同修正預報。斷層帶可以含很硬的岩塊，但整體變形與湧水常由填充節理和連通裂隙控制。","textEn":"Official technical forums discuss weak zones; combine infill, orientation and face inflow to update forecasts. A fault zone may contain strong intact blocks while filled joints and connected fractures govern its bulk deformation and inflow.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]},{"id":"b118-v14-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「破碎帶連通與預報更新」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Fault connectivity and forecast updating\" is correct?","options":["岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。","目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。","觀音公開論壇討論地質弱帶，本課研究裂隙填充、產狀和掌子面水量如何共同修正預報。"],"optionsEn":["Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow.","No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.","Official technical forums discuss weak zones; combine infill, orientation and face inflow to update forecasts."],"answer":2,"explanation":"觀音公開論壇討論地質弱帶，本課研究裂隙填充、產狀和掌子面水量如何共同修正預報。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Official technical forums discuss weak zones; combine infill, orientation and face inflow to update forecasts. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b118-v14-06","title":"破碎帶連通與預報更新：定量估算","titleEn":"Fault connectivity and forecast updating: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b118-v14-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「破碎帶連通性」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Fault-zone connectivity” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：滲透係數=3e-06 m/s；水力坡降=2.1 無因次；通水面積=370 m²。Q=k i A=0.002331 m³/s。僅把滲透係數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.0025641 m³/s。邊界：均質飽和達西流，不代表裂隙集中流；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: conductivity=3e-06 m/s; hydraulic gradient=2.1 dimensionless; flow area=370 m². Q=k i A=0.002331 m³/s. Increasing only conductivity by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.0025641 m³/s. Boundary: Homogeneous saturated Darcy flow, not concentrated fracture flow. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：按工作面和里程整理弱帶類型與後續支護反應。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Organise weak-zone types and support response by face and chainage.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b118-v14-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：滲透係數=3e-06 m/s；水力坡降=2.1 無因次；通水面積=370 m²。Q=k i A=0.002331 m³/s。僅把滲透係數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.0025641 m³/s。邊界：均質飽和達西流，不代表裂隙集中流；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: conductivity=3e-06 m/s; hydraulic gradient=2.1 dimensionless; flow area=370 m². Q=k i A=0.002331 m³/s. Increasing only conductivity by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.0025641 m³/s. Boundary: Homogeneous saturated Darcy flow, not concentrated fracture flow. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]},{"id":"b118-v14-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「破碎帶連通與預報更新」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Fault connectivity and forecast updating\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：滲透係數=3e-06 m/s；水力坡降=2.1 無因次；通水面積=370 m²。","增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。","只要空間分成兩層就可以採用相同的樓板荷載。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: conductivity=3e-06 m/s; hydraulic gradient=2.1 dimensionless; flow area=370 m².","Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.","Any space divided into two levels can use the same deck loading."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：滲透係數=3e-06 m/s；水力坡降=2.1 無因次；通水面積=370 m²。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: conductivity=3e-06 m/s; hydraulic gradient=2.1 dimensionless; flow area=370 m². Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b118-v14-07","title":"破碎帶連通與預報更新：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Fault connectivity and forecast updating: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b118-v14-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「破碎帶連通性」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Fault-zone connectivity” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"按工作面和里程整理弱帶類型與後續支護反應。將岩心回收、裂隙方位與出水曲線按里程對齊，用未參與建模的孔段作交叉檢驗，檢查是否只擬合已知資料。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Organise weak-zone types and support response by face and chainage. Align recovery, fracture orientation and inflow by chainage; test the interpretation against a withheld borehole interval to detect fitting only the known observations. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「破碎帶連通性」的交付需回答：按工作面和里程整理弱帶類型與後續支護反應。每次地質模型更新保留舊版與新增證據，差異由地質及支護設計者共同判讀，施工條件改變需重新確認核准範圍。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Suhua Highway Guanyin Tunnel, the fault-zone connectivity handover must address the following evidence: Organise weak-zone types and support response by face and chainage. Retain previous interpretations and new evidence at every update; geology and support designers jointly interpret differences and reconfirm approved bounds when ground conditions change.","failure":"注意干擾：同一弱帶名稱可能含不同水理連通性，不能只套固定參數。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: One weak-zone label can hide differing connectivity and cannot dictate fixed parameters. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b118-v14-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"按工作面和里程整理弱帶類型與後續支護反應。將岩心回收、裂隙方位與出水曲線按里程對齊，用未參與建模的孔段作交叉檢驗，檢查是否只擬合已知資料。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Organise weak-zone types and support response by face and chainage. Align recovery, fracture orientation and inflow by chainage; test the interpretation against a withheld borehole interval to detect fitting only the known observations. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]},{"id":"b118-v14-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「破碎帶連通性」的交付需回答：按工作面和里程整理弱帶類型與後續支護反應。每次地質模型更新保留舊版與新增證據，差異由地質及支護設計者共同判讀，施工條件改變需重新確認核准範圍。","textEn":"For Suhua Highway Guanyin Tunnel, the fault-zone connectivity handover must address the following evidence: Organise weak-zone types and support response by face and chainage. Retain previous interpretations and new evidence at every update; geology and support designers jointly interpret differences and reconfirm approved bounds when ground conditions change.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「破碎帶連通與預報更新」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Fault connectivity and forecast updating\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","按工作面和里程整理弱帶類型與後續支護反應。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Organise weak-zone types and support response by face and chainage.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time."],"answer":1,"explanation":"按工作面和里程整理弱帶類型與後續支護反應。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Organise weak-zone types and support response by face and chainage. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b118-v14-08","title":"破碎帶連通與預報更新：失效診斷","titleEn":"Fault connectivity and forecast updating: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b118-v14-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「破碎帶連通性」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Fault-zone connectivity” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"同一弱帶名稱可能含不同水理連通性，不能只套固定參數。只用完整岩石強度會漏掉軟弱填充物，可能在看似堅硬的地層中出現收斂加快、支護過載或水量突增。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"One weak-zone label can hide differing connectivity and cannot dictate fixed parameters. Intact strength alone misses weak infill, allowing accelerating convergence, support overload or sudden inflow in ground that superficially appears strong. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：單一岩芯強度不能代表整個掌子面；超前鑽孔、出水變化與揭露地質須回饋同一里程模型，預報則應保留不同情境及其證據權重。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Probe records, water response and exposed geology must update a common chainage model, preserving competing interpretations and their evidential weight rather than treating a forecast as certainty.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b118-v14-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"同一弱帶名稱可能含不同水理連通性，不能只套固定參數。只用完整岩石強度會漏掉軟弱填充物，可能在看似堅硬的地層中出現收斂加快、支護過載或水量突增。","textEn":"One weak-zone label can hide differing connectivity and cannot dictate fixed parameters. Intact strength alone misses weak infill, allowing accelerating convergence, support overload or sudden inflow in ground that superficially appears strong.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]},{"id":"b118-v14-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「破碎帶連通與預報更新」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Fault connectivity and forecast updating\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。","同一弱帶名稱可能含不同水理連通性，不能只套固定參數。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.","One weak-zone label can hide differing connectivity and cannot dictate fixed parameters."],"answer":2,"explanation":"同一弱帶名稱可能含不同水理連通性，不能只套固定參數。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"One weak-zone label can hide differing connectivity and cannot dictate fixed parameters. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b118-v14-s2","title":"機制、材料與定量設計","titleEn":"Mechanisms, materials and quantitative design","description":"本階段聚焦「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」與「支護啟動與變形容量」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\" and \"Support activation and deformation capacity\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b118-v14-09","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b118-v14-08"],"objective":"說明「測壓水頭」如何影響蘇花改觀音隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Piezometric head” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Suhua Highway Guanyin Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"舊鐵路坑與新道路孔可能形成水力聯繫，教材檢查增加工作面後出水重新分配的假想情境。水壓取決於連通含水層的測壓水頭，不必等於地表或海面至洞頂的幾何深度。排水降低水壓卻可能增加有效應力與沉陷；停泵或排水堵塞後水頭又會回升，因此防水、排水及環境保水是互相制約的設計選擇。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「測壓水頭」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Old railway galleries and new road bores may interact hydraulically; test hypothetical flow redistribution after new access opens. Water pressure follows piezometric head in the connected aquifer, not automatically the geometric depth below ground or sea level. Drainage reduces pressure but can increase effective stress and settlement. Head may recover after a pump outage or blockage, coupling waterproofing, drainage capacity and preservation of surrounding groundwater in the permanent design. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Piezometric head” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=100 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=100 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=981 kPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「測壓水頭」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Piezometric head”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b118-v14-09-k1","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure","text":"舊鐵路坑與新道路孔可能形成水力聯繫，教材檢查增加工作面後出水重新分配的假想情境。水壓取決於連通含水層的測壓水頭，不必等於地表或海面至洞頂的幾何深度。","textEn":"Old railway galleries and new road bores may interact hydraulically; test hypothetical flow redistribution after new access opens. Water pressure follows piezometric head in the connected aquifer, not automatically the geometric depth below ground or sea level.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]},{"id":"b118-v14-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\" is correct?","options":["舊鐵路坑與新道路孔可能形成水力聯繫，教材檢查增加工作面後出水重新分配的假想情境。","目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。","支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。"],"optionsEn":["Old railway galleries and new road bores may interact hydraulically; test hypothetical flow redistribution after new access opens.","No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.","Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem."],"answer":0,"explanation":"舊鐵路坑與新道路孔可能形成水力聯繫，教材檢查增加工作面後出水重新分配的假想情境。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Old railway galleries and new road bores may interact hydraulically; test hypothetical flow redistribution after new access opens. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b118-v14-10","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓：定量估算","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b118-v14-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「測壓水頭」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Piezometric head” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=100 m。p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=981 kPa。僅把水頭增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為1079.1 kPa。邊界：靜水表壓，不是土體總壓或原位量測；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=100 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=981 kPa. Increasing only head by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 1079.1 kPa. Boundary: Hydrostatic gauge pressure, not total earth pressure or an in-situ measurement. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同步記錄舊坑及新孔水頭與出流變化。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Synchronise old-gallery and new-bore head and flow changes.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b118-v14-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=100 m。p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=981 kPa。僅把水頭增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為1079.1 kPa。邊界：靜水表壓，不是土體總壓或原位量測；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=100 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=981 kPa. Increasing only head by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 1079.1 kPa. Boundary: Hydrostatic gauge pressure, not total earth pressure or an in-situ measurement. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]},{"id":"b118-v14-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\", which statement holds?","options":["兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。","原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=100 m。","風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。"],"optionsEn":["Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.","Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=100 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=981 kPa.","Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=100 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=100 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=981 kPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b118-v14-11","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b118-v14-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「測壓水頭」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Piezometric head” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同步記錄舊坑及新孔水頭與出流變化。使用分層測壓管及流量計，配合降雨或潮位序列分辨補注與設備影響，將讀值統一換算至同一高程基準。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Synchronise old-gallery and new-bore head and flow changes. Use nested piezometers and flowmeters with rainfall or tide histories to distinguish recharge from equipment effects, converting observations to a common elevation datum. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「測壓水頭」的交付需回答：同步記錄舊坑及新孔水頭與出流變化。設計檢核應分列正常排水、堵塞與停電水位，將環境受體的容許變化和監測責任一起交付，不把抽水量當唯一指標。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Suhua Highway Guanyin Tunnel, the piezometric head handover must address the following evidence: Synchronise old-gallery and new-bore head and flow changes. Separate normal drainage, blocked-drain and power-outage heads and hand over receptor limits and monitoring responsibility together rather than using pump flow as the sole indicator.","failure":"注意干擾：新孔水少可能只是舊坑先截水，並非地層原本乾燥。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Low new-bore flow may reflect interception by the old gallery rather than dry ground. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b118-v14-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同步記錄舊坑及新孔水頭與出流變化。使用分層測壓管及流量計，配合降雨或潮位序列分辨補注與設備影響，將讀值統一換算至同一高程基準。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Synchronise old-gallery and new-bore head and flow changes. Use nested piezometers and flowmeters with rainfall or tide histories to distinguish recharge from equipment effects, converting observations to a common elevation datum. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]},{"id":"b118-v14-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「測壓水頭」的交付需回答：同步記錄舊坑及新孔水頭與出流變化。設計檢核應分列正常排水、堵塞與停電水位，將環境受體的容許變化和監測責任一起交付，不把抽水量當唯一指標。","textEn":"For Suhua Highway Guanyin Tunnel, the piezometric head handover must address the following evidence: Synchronise old-gallery and new-bore head and flow changes. Separate normal drainage, blocked-drain and power-outage heads and hand over receptor limits and monitoring responsibility together rather than using pump flow as the sole indicator.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。","同步記錄舊坑及新孔水頭與出流變化。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.","Synchronise old-gallery and new-bore head and flow changes."],"answer":2,"explanation":"同步記錄舊坑及新孔水頭與出流變化。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Synchronise old-gallery and new-bore head and flow changes. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b118-v14-12","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓：失效診斷","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b118-v14-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「測壓水頭」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Piezometric head” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"新孔水少可能只是舊坑先截水，並非地層原本乾燥。將暫時降水後的低水頭當成永久狀態，會漏掉停泵後外壓回升；過度排水也可能引起周邊地層壓密。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Low new-bore flow may reflect interception by the old gallery rather than dry ground. Treating temporarily lowered head as permanent misses pressure recovery after outage; excessive drainage can also consolidate surrounding ground. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：排水降低水壓卻可能增加有效應力與沉陷；停泵或排水堵塞後水頭又會回升，因此防水、排水及環境保水是互相制約的設計選擇。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Head may recover after a pump outage or blockage, coupling waterproofing, drainage capacity and preservation of surrounding groundwater in the permanent design.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b118-v14-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"新孔水少可能只是舊坑先截水，並非地層原本乾燥。將暫時降水後的低水頭當成永久狀態，會漏掉停泵後外壓回升；過度排水也可能引起周邊地層壓密。","textEn":"Low new-bore flow may reflect interception by the old gallery rather than dry ground. Treating temporarily lowered head as permanent misses pressure recovery after outage; excessive drainage can also consolidate surrounding ground.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]},{"id":"b118-v14-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["新孔水少可能只是舊坑先截水，並非地層原本乾燥。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。"],"optionsEn":["Low new-bore flow may reflect interception by the old gallery rather than dry ground.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem."],"answer":0,"explanation":"新孔水少可能只是舊坑先截水，並非地層原本乾燥。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Low new-bore flow may reflect interception by the old gallery rather than dry ground. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b118-v14-13","title":"支護啟動與變形容量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Support activation and deformation capacity: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b118-v14-12"],"objective":"說明「支護安裝時點」如何影響蘇花改觀音隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Support activation time” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Suhua Highway Guanyin Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"多工作面通過弱帶的支護時序不同，教材比較相同地質但不同封閉時間的收斂荷重。支護荷載由開挖釋放量和支護啟動時間共同決定，越早安裝不一定讓構件受力越小。地盤反力與支護曲線必須連同掌子面距離及封閉順序理解；擠壓性地層還需保留變形容量，不能只追求高剛度與高材料強度。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「支護安裝時點」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Different headings cross weak zones with different closure timing; compare loads and convergence within the same geology. Support load depends on stress release and activation time, so earlier installation does not necessarily reduce member forces. Interpret ground-reaction and support curves together with distance from the face and closure sequence. Squeezing ground also needs deformation capacity; high stiffness and material strength alone do not guarantee a compatible support response. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Support activation time” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：局部剛度=47 kN/mm；位移=8 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: local stiffness=47 kN/mm; movement=8 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「支護安裝時點」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Support activation time”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b118-v14-13-k1","title":"支護啟動與變形容量","titleEn":"Support activation and deformation capacity","text":"多工作面通過弱帶的支護時序不同，教材比較相同地質但不同封閉時間的收斂荷重。支護荷載由開挖釋放量和支護啟動時間共同決定，越早安裝不一定讓構件受力越小。","textEn":"Different headings cross weak zones with different closure timing; compare loads and convergence within the same geology. Support load depends on stress release and activation time, so earlier installation does not necessarily reduce member forces.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]},{"id":"b118-v14-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「支護啟動與變形容量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Support activation and deformation capacity\" is correct?","options":["支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。","多工作面通過弱帶的支護時序不同，教材比較相同地質但不同封閉時間的收斂荷重。","增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。"],"optionsEn":["Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem.","Different headings cross weak zones with different closure timing; compare loads and convergence within the same geology.","Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly."],"answer":1,"explanation":"多工作面通過弱帶的支護時序不同，教材比較相同地質但不同封閉時間的收斂荷重。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Different headings cross weak zones with different closure timing; compare loads and convergence within the same geology. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b118-v14-14","title":"支護啟動與變形容量：定量估算","titleEn":"Support activation and deformation capacity: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b118-v14-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「支護安裝時點」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Support activation time” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：局部剛度=47 kN/mm；位移=8 mm。F=ku=376 kN。僅把位移增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為413.6 kN。邊界：線性局部彈簧，不含屈服或時間效應；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: local stiffness=47 kN/mm; movement=8 mm. F=ku=376 kN. Increasing only movement by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 413.6 kN. Boundary: Local linear spring without yielding or time effects. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將封閉時間標在各工作面的同齡期曲線。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Mark closure time on age-aligned histories from each heading.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b118-v14-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：局部剛度=47 kN/mm；位移=8 mm。F=ku=376 kN。僅把位移增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為413.6 kN。邊界：線性局部彈簧，不含屈服或時間效應；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: local stiffness=47 kN/mm; movement=8 mm. F=ku=376 kN. Increasing only movement by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 413.6 kN. Boundary: Local linear spring without yielding or time effects. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]},{"id":"b118-v14-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「支護啟動與變形容量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Support activation and deformation capacity\", which statement holds?","options":["只要空間分成兩層就可以採用相同的樓板荷載。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。","原創教學假設：局部剛度=47 kN/mm；位移=8 mm。"],"optionsEn":["Any space divided into two levels can use the same deck loading.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.","Original teaching assumptions: local stiffness=47 kN/mm; movement=8 mm."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：局部剛度=47 kN/mm；位移=8 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: local stiffness=47 kN/mm; movement=8 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b118-v14-15","title":"支護啟動與變形容量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Support activation and deformation capacity: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b118-v14-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「支護安裝時點」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Support activation time” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將封閉時間標在各工作面的同齡期曲線。同步記錄收斂、支護荷重與安裝里程，比較同一地質分區內的速率及荷載，不將不同開挖齡期讀值直接混合。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Mark closure time on age-aligned histories from each heading. Synchronise convergence, support loads and installation chainage; compare rates and loads within one ground domain without mixing readings at different excavation ages. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「支護安裝時點」的交付需回答：將封閉時間標在各工作面的同齡期曲線。把安裝時間和量測資料一起交付支護設計者，任何級別變更都需地質及位移證據，不能憑單一瞬間讀值自行改支護。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Suhua Highway Guanyin Tunnel, the support activation time handover must address the following evidence: Mark closure time on age-aligned histories from each heading. Submit installation times with measurements to the support designer; class changes need both ground and movement evidence, not an isolated instantaneous reading.","failure":"注意干擾：按施工日期直接比較會混入不同開挖齡期。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Comparing calendar dates directly mixes different excavation ages. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b118-v14-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將封閉時間標在各工作面的同齡期曲線。同步記錄收斂、支護荷重與安裝里程，比較同一地質分區內的速率及荷載，不將不同開挖齡期讀值直接混合。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Mark closure time on age-aligned histories from each heading. Synchronise convergence, support loads and installation chainage; compare rates and loads within one ground domain without mixing readings at different excavation ages. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]},{"id":"b118-v14-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「支護安裝時點」的交付需回答：將封閉時間標在各工作面的同齡期曲線。把安裝時間和量測資料一起交付支護設計者，任何級別變更都需地質及位移證據，不能憑單一瞬間讀值自行改支護。","textEn":"For Suhua Highway Guanyin Tunnel, the support activation time handover must address the following evidence: Mark closure time on age-aligned histories from each heading. Submit installation times with measurements to the support designer; class changes need both ground and movement evidence, not an isolated instantaneous reading.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「支護啟動與變形容量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Support activation and deformation capacity\"?","options":["將封閉時間標在各工作面的同齡期曲線。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Mark closure time on age-aligned histories from each heading.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將封閉時間標在各工作面的同齡期曲線。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Mark closure time on age-aligned histories from each heading. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b118-v14-16","title":"支護啟動與變形容量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Support activation and deformation capacity: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b118-v14-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「支護安裝時點」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Support activation time” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"按施工日期直接比較會混入不同開挖齡期。過晚封閉會讓不可回復變形增加，過硬且行程不足的支護也可能脆裂，兩者都可能表現為裂縫而需不同處理。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Comparing calendar dates directly mixes different excavation ages. Late closure increases irreversible movement, while excessively stiff support with little travel can fail brittly; both produce cracks but require different diagnoses. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：地盤反力與支護曲線必須連同掌子面距離及封閉順序理解；擠壓性地層還需保留變形容量，不能只追求高剛度與高材料強度。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Squeezing ground also needs deformation capacity; high stiffness and material strength alone do not guarantee a compatible support response.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b118-v14-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"按施工日期直接比較會混入不同開挖齡期。過晚封閉會讓不可回復變形增加，過硬且行程不足的支護也可能脆裂，兩者都可能表現為裂縫而需不同處理。","textEn":"Comparing calendar dates directly mixes different excavation ages. Late closure increases irreversible movement, while excessively stiff support with little travel can fail brittly; both produce cracks but require different diagnoses.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]},{"id":"b118-v14-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「支護啟動與變形容量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Support activation and deformation capacity\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","按施工日期直接比較會混入不同開挖齡期。","增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Comparing calendar dates directly mixes different excavation ages.","Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly."],"answer":1,"explanation":"按施工日期直接比較會混入不同開挖齡期。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Comparing calendar dates directly mixes different excavation ages. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b118-v14-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」與「控制網與貫通誤差」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Shared access and transport bottlenecks\" and \"Control network and breakthrough error\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b118-v14-17","title":"共享通道與運輸瓶頸：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Shared access and transport bottlenecks: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b118-v14-16"],"objective":"說明「出渣運輸節拍」如何影響蘇花改觀音隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Muck-transport cycle” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Suhua Highway Guanyin Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"既有鐵路坑增設工作面也帶來共享通道瓶頸，觀音教材用完整循環檢查材料與出渣交會。多工作面只有在供電、通風、出渣與材料供應同步充足時才增加總產量。共用豎井或軌道形成串聯瓶頸，排隊和維修窗口會降低名目容量；緩衝區太大又可能侵占通行與救援空間，因此不能單純把各面產能相加。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「出渣運輸節拍」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Reusing a railway gallery adds headings but also shared-access bottlenecks; examine complete material and spoil cycles. Multiple headings increase output only when power, air, muck transport and materials support them together. Shared shafts or railways become serial bottlenecks, while queues and maintenance reduce nominal capacity. Large buffers may obstruct personnel and rescue access, so face capacities cannot simply be added without a network-level transport and storage check. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Muck-transport cycle” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=37 t；往返週期=34 min。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=37 t; cycle=34 min.","failure":"常見誤解：「增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「出渣運輸節拍」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Muck-transport cycle”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b118-v14-17-k1","title":"共享通道與運輸瓶頸","titleEn":"Shared access and transport bottlenecks","text":"既有鐵路坑增設工作面也帶來共享通道瓶頸，觀音教材用完整循環檢查材料與出渣交會。多工作面只有在供電、通風、出渣與材料供應同步充足時才增加總產量。","textEn":"Reusing a railway gallery adds headings but also shared-access bottlenecks; examine complete material and spoil cycles. Multiple headings increase output only when power, air, muck transport and materials support them together.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]},{"id":"b118-v14-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Shared access and transport bottlenecks\" is correct?","options":["增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。","既有鐵路坑增設工作面也帶來共享通道瓶頸，觀音教材用完整循環檢查材料與出渣交會。"],"optionsEn":["Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.","Reusing a railway gallery adds headings but also shared-access bottlenecks; examine complete material and spoil cycles."],"answer":2,"explanation":"既有鐵路坑增設工作面也帶來共享通道瓶頸，觀音教材用完整循環檢查材料與出渣交會。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Reusing a railway gallery adds headings but also shared-access bottlenecks; examine complete material and spoil cycles. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b118-v14-18","title":"共享通道與運輸瓶頸：定量估算","titleEn":"Shared access and transport bottlenecks: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b118-v14-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「出渣運輸節拍」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Muck-transport cycle” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=37 t；往返週期=34 min。C=N payload 60/T=261.176 t/h。僅把往返週期增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為237.433 t/h。邊界：無排隊理想循環，並非共享路段實際產能；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=37 t; cycle=34 min. C=N payload 60/T=261.176 t/h. Increasing only cycle by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 237.433 t/h. Boundary: Ideal cycle without queues, not actual shared-route production. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：對照各面出渣需求、交會等待及卸料能力。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare heading demand, passing queues and unloading capacity.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b118-v14-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=37 t；往返週期=34 min。C=N payload 60/T=261.176 t/h。僅把往返週期增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為237.433 t/h。邊界：無排隊理想循環，並非共享路段實際產能；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=37 t; cycle=34 min. C=N payload 60/T=261.176 t/h. Increasing only cycle by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 237.433 t/h. Boundary: Ideal cycle without queues, not actual shared-route production. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]},{"id":"b118-v14-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Shared access and transport bottlenecks\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=37 t；往返週期=34 min。","風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=37 t; cycle=34 min.","Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=37 t；往返週期=34 min。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=37 t; cycle=34 min. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b118-v14-19","title":"共享通道與運輸瓶頸：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Shared access and transport bottlenecks: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b118-v14-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「出渣運輸節拍」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Muck-transport cycle” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"對照各面出渣需求、交會等待及卸料能力。以裝載質量、往返時間及排隊時間重建物流曲線，再核對緩衝占用、共用通道優先權與維修時段。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare heading demand, passing queues and unloading capacity. Reconstruct flow from payload, round-trip and queue times, then check buffer occupancy, shared-route priorities and maintenance periods. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「出渣運輸節拍」的交付需回答：對照各面出渣需求、交會等待及卸料能力。每日排程同時標示人員、材料和維修的占用時段，任何物流改線先檢查通風與應變通道，不能只看運量提升。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Suhua Highway Guanyin Tunnel, the muck-transport cycle handover must address the following evidence: Compare heading demand, passing queues and unloading capacity. Schedules show personnel, materials and maintenance occupancy together; rerouting first checks ventilation and emergency access rather than only throughput gains.","failure":"注意干擾：工作面數增加不能直接倍增每日總進尺。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: More headings do not directly multiply daily total advance. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b118-v14-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"對照各面出渣需求、交會等待及卸料能力。以裝載質量、往返時間及排隊時間重建物流曲線，再核對緩衝占用、共用通道優先權與維修時段。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Compare heading demand, passing queues and unloading capacity. Reconstruct flow from payload, round-trip and queue times, then check buffer occupancy, shared-route priorities and maintenance periods. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]},{"id":"b118-v14-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「出渣運輸節拍」的交付需回答：對照各面出渣需求、交會等待及卸料能力。每日排程同時標示人員、材料和維修的占用時段，任何物流改線先檢查通風與應變通道，不能只看運量提升。","textEn":"For Suhua Highway Guanyin Tunnel, the muck-transport cycle handover must address the following evidence: Compare heading demand, passing queues and unloading capacity. Schedules show personnel, materials and maintenance occupancy together; rerouting first checks ventilation and emergency access rather than only throughput gains.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Shared access and transport bottlenecks\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","對照各面出渣需求、交會等待及卸料能力。","岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Compare heading demand, passing queues and unloading capacity.","Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow."],"answer":1,"explanation":"對照各面出渣需求、交會等待及卸料能力。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare heading demand, passing queues and unloading capacity. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b118-v14-20","title":"共享通道與運輸瓶頸：失效診斷","titleEn":"Shared access and transport bottlenecks: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b118-v14-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「出渣運輸節拍」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Muck-transport cycle” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"工作面數增加不能直接倍增每日總進尺。把理想往返時間當全天常數會忽略交會等待與卸料堵塞，導致工作面停工或把材料堆入必要通道。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"More headings do not directly multiply daily total advance. Treating an ideal cycle as constant all day misses passing delays and unloading blockages, stopping headings or pushing material into essential access space. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：共用豎井或軌道形成串聯瓶頸，排隊和維修窗口會降低名目容量；緩衝區太大又可能侵占通行與救援空間，因此不能單純把各面產能相加。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Large buffers may obstruct personnel and rescue access, so face capacities cannot simply be added without a network-level transport and storage check.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b118-v14-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"工作面數增加不能直接倍增每日總進尺。把理想往返時間當全天常數會忽略交會等待與卸料堵塞，導致工作面停工或把材料堆入必要通道。","textEn":"More headings do not directly multiply daily total advance. Treating an ideal cycle as constant all day misses passing delays and unloading blockages, stopping headings or pushing material into essential access space.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]},{"id":"b118-v14-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Shared access and transport bottlenecks\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。","工作面數增加不能直接倍增每日總進尺。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.","More headings do not directly multiply daily total advance."],"answer":2,"explanation":"工作面數增加不能直接倍增每日總進尺。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"More headings do not directly multiply daily total advance. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b118-v14-21","title":"控制網與貫通誤差：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b118-v14-20"],"objective":"說明「方向角誤差」如何影響蘇花改觀音隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Orientation error” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Suhua Highway Guanyin Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"多面貫通需把舊坑坐標傳入新孔，教材分析歷史基準與現代控制網轉換的誤差。長隧道的微小方向誤差會沿距離累積，地下控制網又缺少直接衛星定位，必須把地表基準可靠傳到洞內。閉合差很小不代表無系統誤差；尺度、折光、儀器定向與高程基準可能共同偏移，誤差相關性也使平方和估算失真。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「方向角誤差」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Multiple breakthroughs require transfer from old-gallery coordinates into new bores, including historical-to-modern datum errors. Small orientation errors accumulate over long drives, while underground networks lack direct satellite positioning and depend on transferring surface control. A small closure does not exclude systematic bias: scale, refraction, orientation and vertical datum may shift together. Correlated errors also invalidate a naive root-sum-square combination of supposedly independent observations. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Orientation error” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：控制長度=5040 m；方向偏角=2.5 arcsec。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: control length=5040 m; orientation error=2.5 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0610865 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「方向角誤差」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Orientation error”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b118-v14-21-k1","title":"控制網與貫通誤差","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error","text":"多面貫通需把舊坑坐標傳入新孔，教材分析歷史基準與現代控制網轉換的誤差。長隧道的微小方向誤差會沿距離累積，地下控制網又缺少直接衛星定位，必須把地表基準可靠傳到洞內。","textEn":"Multiple breakthroughs require transfer from old-gallery coordinates into new bores, including historical-to-modern datum errors. Small orientation errors accumulate over long drives, while underground networks lack direct satellite positioning and depend on transferring surface control.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]},{"id":"b118-v14-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「控制網與貫通誤差」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Control network and breakthrough error\" is correct?","options":["多面貫通需把舊坑坐標傳入新孔，教材分析歷史基準與現代控制網轉換的誤差。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。","只要空間分成兩層就可以採用相同的樓板荷載。"],"optionsEn":["Multiple breakthroughs require transfer from old-gallery coordinates into new bores, including historical-to-modern datum errors.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.","Any space divided into two levels can use the same deck loading."],"answer":0,"explanation":"多面貫通需把舊坑坐標傳入新孔，教材分析歷史基準與現代控制網轉換的誤差。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Multiple breakthroughs require transfer from old-gallery coordinates into new bores, including historical-to-modern datum errors. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b118-v14-22","title":"控制網與貫通誤差：定量估算","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b118-v14-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「方向角誤差」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Orientation error” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：控制長度=5040 m；方向偏角=2.5 arcsec。e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0610865 m。僅把方向偏角增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.0671952 m。邊界：小角度方向偏差，未加入控制網相關性及折光；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: control length=5040 m; orientation error=2.5 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0610865 m. Increasing only orientation error by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.0671952 m. Boundary: Small-angle orientation error without network correlation or refraction. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用新地表控制獨立覆核舊坑基準與方向。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Independently recheck old-gallery references and orientation from new surface control.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b118-v14-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：控制長度=5040 m；方向偏角=2.5 arcsec。e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0610865 m。僅把方向偏角增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.0671952 m。邊界：小角度方向偏差，未加入控制網相關性及折光；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: control length=5040 m; orientation error=2.5 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0610865 m. Increasing only orientation error by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.0671952 m. Boundary: Small-angle orientation error without network correlation or refraction. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]},{"id":"b118-v14-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「控制網與貫通誤差」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Control network and breakthrough error\", which statement holds?","options":["只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。","原創教學假設：控制長度=5040 m；方向偏角=2.5 arcsec。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.","Original teaching assumptions: control length=5040 m; orientation error=2.5 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0610865 m.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：控制長度=5040 m；方向偏角=2.5 arcsec。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: control length=5040 m; orientation error=2.5 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0610865 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b118-v14-23","title":"控制網與貫通誤差：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b118-v14-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「方向角誤差」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Orientation error” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用新地表控制獨立覆核舊坑基準與方向。由獨立測量組複核地表到洞內的轉換，保留原始角距及溫度資料，用不同控制線比較方向與高程偏差。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Independently recheck old-gallery references and orientation from new surface control. Independently check surface-to-tunnel transformations, retain raw angles, distances and temperatures, and compare orientation and elevation through separate control routes. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「方向角誤差」的交付需回答：用新地表控制獨立覆核舊坑基準與方向。貫通前凍結座標、尺度與高程版本，獨立組直接使用原始觀測重算；不得只傳遞整理好的坐標而遺失校正資訊。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Suhua Highway Guanyin Tunnel, the orientation error handover must address the following evidence: Independently recheck old-gallery references and orientation from new surface control. Freeze coordinate, scale and height revisions before breakthrough; independent reviewers recompute raw observations rather than receiving only adjusted coordinates without corrections.","failure":"注意干擾：舊坑幾何吻合不證明其坐標可直接用於新道路孔。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Agreement with old-gallery geometry does not validate direct coordinate reuse. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b118-v14-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用新地表控制獨立覆核舊坑基準與方向。由獨立測量組複核地表到洞內的轉換，保留原始角距及溫度資料，用不同控制線比較方向與高程偏差。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Independently recheck old-gallery references and orientation from new surface control. Independently check surface-to-tunnel transformations, retain raw angles, distances and temperatures, and compare orientation and elevation through separate control routes. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]},{"id":"b118-v14-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「方向角誤差」的交付需回答：用新地表控制獨立覆核舊坑基準與方向。貫通前凍結座標、尺度與高程版本，獨立組直接使用原始觀測重算；不得只傳遞整理好的坐標而遺失校正資訊。","textEn":"For Suhua Highway Guanyin Tunnel, the orientation error handover must address the following evidence: Independently recheck old-gallery references and orientation from new surface control. Freeze coordinate, scale and height revisions before breakthrough; independent reviewers recompute raw observations rather than receiving only adjusted coordinates without corrections.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「控制網與貫通誤差」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Control network and breakthrough error\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。","用新地表控制獨立覆核舊坑基準與方向。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.","Independently recheck old-gallery references and orientation from new surface control."],"answer":2,"explanation":"用新地表控制獨立覆核舊坑基準與方向。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Independently recheck old-gallery references and orientation from new surface control. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b118-v14-24","title":"控制網與貫通誤差：失效診斷","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b118-v14-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「方向角誤差」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Orientation error” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"舊坑幾何吻合不證明其坐標可直接用於新道路孔。共用錯誤基準可能讓兩組測量同時看似一致，直到貫通或軌道銜接才發現系統偏差，修正成本遠高於早期複核。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Agreement with old-gallery geometry does not validate direct coordinate reuse. A shared wrong datum can make separate surveys appear consistent until breakthrough or track connection exposes bias that is costly to correct. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：閉合差很小不代表無系統誤差；尺度、折光、儀器定向與高程基準可能共同偏移，誤差相關性也使平方和估算失真。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Correlated errors also invalidate a naive root-sum-square combination of supposedly independent observations.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b118-v14-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"舊坑幾何吻合不證明其坐標可直接用於新道路孔。共用錯誤基準可能讓兩組測量同時看似一致，直到貫通或軌道銜接才發現系統偏差，修正成本遠高於早期複核。","textEn":"Agreement with old-gallery geometry does not validate direct coordinate reuse. A shared wrong datum can make separate surveys appear consistent until breakthrough or track connection exposes bias that is costly to correct.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]},{"id":"b118-v14-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「控制網與貫通誤差」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Control network and breakthrough error\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["舊坑幾何吻合不證明其坐標可直接用於新道路孔。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","只要空間分成兩層就可以採用相同的樓板荷載。"],"optionsEn":["Agreement with old-gallery geometry does not validate direct coordinate reuse.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Any space divided into two levels can use the same deck loading."],"answer":0,"explanation":"舊坑幾何吻合不證明其坐標可直接用於新道路孔。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Agreement with old-gallery geometry does not validate direct coordinate reuse. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b118-v14-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「內部樓板與荷載路徑」與「通風網路與壓力損失」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Internal decks and load paths\" and \"Ventilation network and pressure loss\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b118-v14-25","title":"內部樓板與荷載路徑：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Internal decks and load paths: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b118-v14-24"],"objective":"說明「樓板條帶受彎」如何影響蘇花改觀音隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Deck-strip bending” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Suhua Highway Guanyin Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"觀音通風機房及管道情境中的隔板是設備風道構件，不是雙層道路樓板，荷載功能必須先辨認。雙層公路的樓板、或隧道內設備隔板，都把局部荷載傳給支承，但兩者功能與設計作用並不相同。簡支條帶可估計均載彎矩，集中輪載、剪力、疲勞與火災降強度必須另驗；幾何空間分層不能取代結構邊界的確認。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「樓板條帶受彎」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A ventilation-room or duct partition is an equipment-airway component, not a double-deck roadway slab; establish its function first. A double-deck road slab and an equipment partition both transfer local loads to supports but serve different functions and design actions. A simply supported strip estimates uniform-load bending. Concentrated wheel loads, shear, fatigue and fire-reduced strength require separate checks; dividing space geometrically does not establish the actual structural restraints. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Deck-strip bending” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：單位長載重=37 kN/m；跨距=3.9 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: line load=37 kN/m; span=3.9 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要空間分成兩層就可以採用相同的樓板荷載。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Any space divided into two levels can use the same deck loading.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「樓板條帶受彎」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Deck-strip bending”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b118-v14-25-k1","title":"內部樓板與荷載路徑","titleEn":"Internal decks and load paths","text":"觀音通風機房及管道情境中的隔板是設備風道構件，不是雙層道路樓板，荷載功能必須先辨認。雙層公路的樓板、或隧道內設備隔板，都把局部荷載傳給支承，但兩者功能與設計作用並不相同。","textEn":"A ventilation-room or duct partition is an equipment-airway component, not a double-deck roadway slab; establish its function first. A double-deck road slab and an equipment partition both transfer local loads to supports but serve different functions and design actions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]},{"id":"b118-v14-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要空間分成兩層就可以採用相同的樓板荷載。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Any space divided into two levels can use the same deck loading. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「內部樓板與荷載路徑」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Internal decks and load paths\" is correct?","options":["只要空間分成兩層就可以採用相同的樓板荷載。","觀音通風機房及管道情境中的隔板是設備風道構件，不是雙層道路樓板，荷載功能必須先辨認。","風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。"],"optionsEn":["Any space divided into two levels can use the same deck loading.","A ventilation-room or duct partition is an equipment-airway component, not a double-deck roadway slab; establish its function first.","Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel."],"answer":1,"explanation":"觀音通風機房及管道情境中的隔板是設備風道構件，不是雙層道路樓板，荷載功能必須先辨認。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A ventilation-room or duct partition is an equipment-airway component, not a double-deck roadway slab; establish its function first. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b118-v14-26","title":"內部樓板與荷載路徑：定量估算","titleEn":"Internal decks and load paths: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b118-v14-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「樓板條帶受彎」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Deck-strip bending” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：單位長載重=37 kN/m；跨距=3.9 m。M=qL²/8=70.3462 kN·m。僅把跨距增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為85.119 kN·m。邊界：均載簡支單向條帶，連續框架及板效應另驗；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: line load=37 kN/m; span=3.9 m. M=qL²/8=70.3462 kN·m. Increasing only span by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 85.119 kN·m. Boundary: Uniformly loaded simply supported strip; frame continuity and plate action need separate checks. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對隔板支承、風壓及維修荷載，不套車輪荷載。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check partition supports, air pressure and maintenance loading without substituting wheel loads.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b118-v14-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：單位長載重=37 kN/m；跨距=3.9 m。M=qL²/8=70.3462 kN·m。僅把跨距增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為85.119 kN·m。邊界：均載簡支單向條帶，連續框架及板效應另驗；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: line load=37 kN/m; span=3.9 m. M=qL²/8=70.3462 kN·m. Increasing only span by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 85.119 kN·m. Boundary: Uniformly loaded simply supported strip; frame continuity and plate action need separate checks. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]},{"id":"b118-v14-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「內部樓板與荷載路徑」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Internal decks and load paths\", which statement holds?","options":["全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。","岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。","原創教學假設：單位長載重=37 kN/m；跨距=3.9 m。"],"optionsEn":["Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.","Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow.","Original teaching assumptions: line load=37 kN/m; span=3.9 m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：單位長載重=37 kN/m；跨距=3.9 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: line load=37 kN/m; span=3.9 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b118-v14-27","title":"內部樓板與荷載路徑：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Internal decks and load paths: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b118-v14-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「樓板條帶受彎」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Deck-strip bending” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對隔板支承、風壓及維修荷載，不套車輪荷載。核對支承位置、施工接縫及荷載分布，將實測撓度與分階段模型比較，分辨整體變形與支承滑移。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check partition supports, air pressure and maintenance loading without substituting wheel loads. Check support positions, construction joints and load distribution; compare measured deflection with staged models to distinguish member bending from support slip. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「樓板條帶受彎」的交付需回答：核對隔板支承、風壓及維修荷載，不套車輪荷載。交付時明示樓板用途、支承及各施工階段，讓建築淨空、設備配置及結構假設在同一版本中核對。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Suhua Highway Guanyin Tunnel, the deck-strip bending handover must address the following evidence: Check partition supports, air pressure and maintenance loading without substituting wheel loads. State deck function, supports and construction stages at handover so clearance, equipment layout and structural assumptions can be reconciled in one revision.","failure":"注意干擾：將風道隔板當行車樓板會錯置荷載與檢核目的。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Treating an airway partition as a roadway deck misassigns loads and checks. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b118-v14-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對隔板支承、風壓及維修荷載，不套車輪荷載。核對支承位置、施工接縫及荷載分布，將實測撓度與分階段模型比較，分辨整體變形與支承滑移。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Check partition supports, air pressure and maintenance loading without substituting wheel loads. Check support positions, construction joints and load distribution; compare measured deflection with staged models to distinguish member bending from support slip. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]},{"id":"b118-v14-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「樓板條帶受彎」的交付需回答：核對隔板支承、風壓及維修荷載，不套車輪荷載。交付時明示樓板用途、支承及各施工階段，讓建築淨空、設備配置及結構假設在同一版本中核對。","textEn":"For Suhua Highway Guanyin Tunnel, the deck-strip bending handover must address the following evidence: Check partition supports, air pressure and maintenance loading without substituting wheel loads. State deck function, supports and construction stages at handover so clearance, equipment layout and structural assumptions can be reconciled in one revision.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「內部樓板與荷載路徑」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Internal decks and load paths\"?","options":["核對隔板支承、風壓及維修荷載，不套車輪荷載。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。"],"optionsEn":["Check partition supports, air pressure and maintenance loading without substituting wheel loads.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem."],"answer":0,"explanation":"核對隔板支承、風壓及維修荷載，不套車輪荷載。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check partition supports, air pressure and maintenance loading without substituting wheel loads. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b118-v14-28","title":"內部樓板與荷載路徑：失效診斷","titleEn":"Internal decks and load paths: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b118-v14-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「樓板條帶受彎」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Deck-strip bending” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"將風道隔板當行車樓板會錯置荷載與檢核目的。把隔板誤當行車樓板會使用錯誤荷載，反之漏掉交通集中荷載則低估局部彎剪與疲勞。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Treating an airway partition as a roadway deck misassigns loads and checks. Mistaking a partition for a roadway deck applies the wrong actions, while omitting concentrated traffic load underestimates local bending, shear and fatigue. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：簡支條帶可估計均載彎矩，集中輪載、剪力、疲勞與火災降強度必須另驗；幾何空間分層不能取代結構邊界的確認。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Concentrated wheel loads, shear, fatigue and fire-reduced strength require separate checks; dividing space geometrically does not establish the actual structural restraints.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要空間分成兩層就可以採用相同的樓板荷載。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Any space divided into two levels can use the same deck loading.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b118-v14-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"將風道隔板當行車樓板會錯置荷載與檢核目的。把隔板誤當行車樓板會使用錯誤荷載，反之漏掉交通集中荷載則低估局部彎剪與疲勞。","textEn":"Treating an airway partition as a roadway deck misassigns loads and checks. Mistaking a partition for a roadway deck applies the wrong actions, while omitting concentrated traffic load underestimates local bending, shear and fatigue.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]},{"id":"b118-v14-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「內部樓板與荷載路徑」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Internal decks and load paths\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","將風道隔板當行車樓板會錯置荷載與檢核目的。","風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Treating an airway partition as a roadway deck misassigns loads and checks.","Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel."],"answer":1,"explanation":"將風道隔板當行車樓板會錯置荷載與檢核目的。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Treating an airway partition as a roadway deck misassigns loads and checks. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b118-v14-29","title":"通風網路與壓力損失：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Ventilation network and pressure loss: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b118-v14-28"],"objective":"說明「風道摩擦壓損」如何影響蘇花改觀音隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Duct friction loss” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Suhua Highway Guanyin Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"觀音與相鄰設施的通風控制需保留門位和車流邊界，教材分析設備維修時支路阻力重分配。風機提供壓差，實際風量由風道摩阻、局部損失、外風與其他風機共同決定。支路開關會重新分配整個網路，不能把額定風量直接加總；正常污染稀釋與火災控煙也有不同目標，需要分別建立受控邊界和故障情境。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「風道摩擦壓損」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Ventilation control must retain door and traffic boundaries across linked facilities; examine resistance redistribution during maintenance. Fans supply pressure, but actual flow follows friction, local losses, external wind and interactions with other fans. Switching a branch redistributes the network rather than simply adding rated flows. Routine dilution and fire smoke control have different objectives, so each needs explicit boundaries, operating states and failure cases rather than one universal flow target. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Duct friction loss” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：達西因子=0.025 無因次；風道長度=1180 m；水力直徑=4 m；空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；平均風速=3.7 m/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.025 dimensionless; duct length=1180 m; hydraulic diameter=4 m; air density=1.2 kg/m³; mean velocity=3.7 m/s. Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=60.5783 Pa.","failure":"常見誤解：「風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「風道摩擦壓損」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Duct friction loss”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b118-v14-29-k1","title":"通風網路與壓力損失","titleEn":"Ventilation network and pressure loss","text":"觀音與相鄰設施的通風控制需保留門位和車流邊界，教材分析設備維修時支路阻力重分配。風機提供壓差，實際風量由風道摩阻、局部損失、外風與其他風機共同決定。","textEn":"Ventilation control must retain door and traffic boundaries across linked facilities; examine resistance redistribution during maintenance. Fans supply pressure, but actual flow follows friction, local losses, external wind and interactions with other fans.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]},{"id":"b118-v14-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「通風網路與壓力損失」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Ventilation network and pressure loss\" is correct?","options":["風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。","觀音與相鄰設施的通風控制需保留門位和車流邊界，教材分析設備維修時支路阻力重分配。"],"optionsEn":["Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.","Ventilation control must retain door and traffic boundaries across linked facilities; examine resistance redistribution during maintenance."],"answer":2,"explanation":"觀音與相鄰設施的通風控制需保留門位和車流邊界，教材分析設備維修時支路阻力重分配。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Ventilation control must retain door and traffic boundaries across linked facilities; examine resistance redistribution during maintenance. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b118-v14-30","title":"通風網路與壓力損失：定量估算","titleEn":"Ventilation network and pressure loss: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b118-v14-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「風道摩擦壓損」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Duct friction loss” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：達西因子=0.025 無因次；風道長度=1180 m；水力直徑=4 m；空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；平均風速=3.7 m/s。Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=60.5783 Pa。僅把平均風速增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為73.2997 Pa。邊界：定密度直管摩阻，局部損失及外風另計；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.025 dimensionless; duct length=1180 m; hydraulic diameter=4 m; air density=1.2 kg/m³; mean velocity=3.7 m/s. Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=60.5783 Pa. Increasing only mean velocity by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 73.2997 Pa. Boundary: Constant-density straight-duct friction; local loss and external wind are separate. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同步比較風門狀態、機房壓差與孔內風速。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare damper state, plant-room pressure and in-bore velocity simultaneously.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b118-v14-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：達西因子=0.025 無因次；風道長度=1180 m；水力直徑=4 m；空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；平均風速=3.7 m/s。Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=60.5783 Pa。僅把平均風速增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為73.2997 Pa。邊界：定密度直管摩阻，局部損失及外風另計；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.025 dimensionless; duct length=1180 m; hydraulic diameter=4 m; air density=1.2 kg/m³; mean velocity=3.7 m/s. Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=60.5783 Pa. Increasing only mean velocity by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 73.2997 Pa. Boundary: Constant-density straight-duct friction; local loss and external wind are separate. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]},{"id":"b118-v14-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「通風網路與壓力損失」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Ventilation network and pressure loss\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：達西因子=0.025 無因次；風道長度=1180 m；水力直徑=4 m；空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；平均風速=3.7 m/s。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。","目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.025 dimensionless.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.","No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：達西因子=0.025 無因次；風道長度=1180 m；水力直徑=4 m；空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；平均風速=3.7 m/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.025 dimensionless; duct length=1180 m; hydraulic diameter=4 m; air density=1.2 kg/m³; mean velocity=3.7 m/s. Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=60.5783 Pa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b118-v14-31","title":"通風網路與壓力損失：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Ventilation network and pressure loss: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b118-v14-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「風道摩擦壓損」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Duct friction loss” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同步比較風門狀態、機房壓差與孔內風速。沿線同步量測靜壓與風速，記錄風門及其他風機狀態，再把實測工作點和風機曲線、網路壓損比較。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare damper state, plant-room pressure and in-bore velocity simultaneously. Measure pressure and velocity synchronously, record dampers and other fans, and compare the measured duty point with fan curves and network resistance. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「風道摩擦壓損」的交付需回答：同步比較風門狀態、機房壓差與孔內風速。驗收採明確風門和車流邊界，維修改線後重新核對網路工作點，火災模式由防災責任工程師簽認而非沿用正常模式。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Suhua Highway Guanyin Tunnel, the duct friction loss handover must address the following evidence: Compare damper state, plant-room pressure and in-bore velocity simultaneously. Commission with specified damper and traffic boundaries, recheck duty points after rerouting, and have the fire-safety engineer approve emergency modes independently.","failure":"注意干擾：機房風量正常可能伴隨風道漏風而使道路區效果不足。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Normal plant flow can coexist with duct leakage and inadequate roadway flow. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b118-v14-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同步比較風門狀態、機房壓差與孔內風速。沿線同步量測靜壓與風速，記錄風門及其他風機狀態，再把實測工作點和風機曲線、網路壓損比較。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Compare damper state, plant-room pressure and in-bore velocity simultaneously. Measure pressure and velocity synchronously, record dampers and other fans, and compare the measured duty point with fan curves and network resistance. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]},{"id":"b118-v14-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「風道摩擦壓損」的交付需回答：同步比較風門狀態、機房壓差與孔內風速。驗收採明確風門和車流邊界，維修改線後重新核對網路工作點，火災模式由防災責任工程師簽認而非沿用正常模式。","textEn":"For Suhua Highway Guanyin Tunnel, the duct friction loss handover must address the following evidence: Compare damper state, plant-room pressure and in-bore velocity simultaneously. Commission with specified damper and traffic boundaries, recheck duty points after rerouting, and have the fire-safety engineer approve emergency modes independently.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「通風網路與壓力損失」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Ventilation network and pressure loss\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","同步比較風門狀態、機房壓差與孔內風速。","增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Compare damper state, plant-room pressure and in-bore velocity simultaneously.","Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly."],"answer":1,"explanation":"同步比較風門狀態、機房壓差與孔內風速。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare damper state, plant-room pressure and in-bore velocity simultaneously. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b118-v14-32","title":"通風網路與壓力損失：失效診斷","titleEn":"Ventilation network and pressure loss: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b118-v14-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「風道摩擦壓損」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Duct friction loss” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"機房風量正常可能伴隨風道漏風而使道路區效果不足。只看風機轉速會漏掉風門誤位或短路漏風，可能在總耗電增加時，真正需要的區段反而風量不足。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Normal plant flow can coexist with duct leakage and inadequate roadway flow. Fan speed alone misses a misplaced damper or leakage shortcut; total power may rise while the critical section receives less air. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：支路開關會重新分配整個網路，不能把額定風量直接加總；正常污染稀釋與火災控煙也有不同目標，需要分別建立受控邊界和故障情境。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Routine dilution and fire smoke control have different objectives, so each needs explicit boundaries, operating states and failure cases rather than one universal flow target.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b118-v14-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"機房風量正常可能伴隨風道漏風而使道路區效果不足。只看風機轉速會漏掉風門誤位或短路漏風，可能在總耗電增加時，真正需要的區段反而風量不足。","textEn":"Normal plant flow can coexist with duct leakage and inadequate roadway flow. Fan speed alone misses a misplaced damper or leakage shortcut; total power may rise while the critical section receives less air.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]},{"id":"b118-v14-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「通風網路與壓力損失」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Ventilation network and pressure loss\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。","機房風量正常可能伴隨風道漏風而使道路區效果不足。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.","Normal plant flow can coexist with duct leakage and inadequate roadway flow."],"answer":2,"explanation":"機房風量正常可能伴隨風道漏風而使道路區效果不足。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Normal plant flow can coexist with duct leakage and inadequate roadway flow. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b118-v14-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「疏散時間與分區可用性」與「資產編碼與可追溯交接」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Evacuation time and zone availability\" and \"Asset identity and traceable handover\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b118-v14-33","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b118-v14-32"],"objective":"說明「所需疏散時間」如何影響蘇花改觀音隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Required evacuation time” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Suhua Highway Guanyin Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"連續長隧道路廊的救援需確認鄰孔及出口狀態，教材把最短橫通道距離和完整轉移路徑分開。疏散時間包含辨識、反應、移動及排隊，不只由出口距離決定。人員速度會受煙熱、能見度及行動能力影響，安全判斷還要比較可用安全時間；橫通道存在但門或鄰孔不可用時，圖上的最短路線不一定能作實際選擇。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「所需疏散時間」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A linked long-tunnel corridor needs receiving-bore and exit checks; separate nearest passage distance from the complete transfer route. Evacuation includes detection, response, travel and queues, not merely distance to an exit. Smoke, visibility and mobility alter walking speed, while safety requires comparison with available safe time. A passage shown on a plan may be unusable because its door or receiving bore is unavailable, invalidating the nominal shortest route. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Required evacuation time” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：前置時間=114 s；行走距離=360 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=114 s; travel distance=360 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「所需疏散時間」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Required evacuation time”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b118-v14-33-k1","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability","text":"連續長隧道路廊的救援需確認鄰孔及出口狀態，教材把最短橫通道距離和完整轉移路徑分開。疏散時間包含辨識、反應、移動及排隊，不只由出口距離決定。","textEn":"A linked long-tunnel corridor needs receiving-bore and exit checks; separate nearest passage distance from the complete transfer route. Evacuation includes detection, response, travel and queues, not merely distance to an exit.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]},{"id":"b118-v14-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「疏散時間與分區可用性」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Evacuation time and zone availability\" is correct?","options":["連續長隧道路廊的救援需確認鄰孔及出口狀態，教材把最短橫通道距離和完整轉移路徑分開。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。"],"optionsEn":["A linked long-tunnel corridor needs receiving-bore and exit checks; separate nearest passage distance from the complete transfer route.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted."],"answer":0,"explanation":"連續長隧道路廊的救援需確認鄰孔及出口狀態，教材把最短橫通道距離和完整轉移路徑分開。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A linked long-tunnel corridor needs receiving-bore and exit checks; separate nearest passage distance from the complete transfer route. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b118-v14-34","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性：定量估算","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b118-v14-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「所需疏散時間」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Required evacuation time” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：前置時間=114 s；行走距離=360 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。RSET=tpre+d/v=564 s。僅把行走距離增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為609 s。邊界：單群體固定速度，不含排隊煙熱及能力差異，不能單獨判安全；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=114 s; travel distance=360 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s. RSET=tpre+d/v=564 s. Increasing only travel distance by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 609 s. Boundary: One group at fixed speed without queues, smoke or mobility differences; not a safety conclusion. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：走查橫通道後續路徑及實際門位，保留施工封閉。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Walk the route beyond each passage and record actual doors and closures.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b118-v14-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：前置時間=114 s；行走距離=360 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。RSET=tpre+d/v=564 s。僅把行走距離增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為609 s。邊界：單群體固定速度，不含排隊煙熱及能力差異，不能單獨判安全；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=114 s; travel distance=360 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s. RSET=tpre+d/v=564 s. Increasing only travel distance by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 609 s. Boundary: One group at fixed speed without queues, smoke or mobility differences; not a safety conclusion. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]},{"id":"b118-v14-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「疏散時間與分區可用性」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Evacuation time and zone availability\", which statement holds?","options":["岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。","原創教學假設：前置時間=114 s；行走距離=360 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。","支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。"],"optionsEn":["Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow.","Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=114 s; travel distance=360 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s.","Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：前置時間=114 s；行走距離=360 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=114 s; travel distance=360 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b118-v14-35","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b118-v14-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「所需疏散時間」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Required evacuation time” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"走查橫通道後續路徑及實際門位，保留施工封閉。以人流模擬或受控演練分辨前置時間、行走與門口排隊，核對每個出口接收區的可用狀態及通訊紀錄。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Walk the route beyond each passage and record actual doors and closures. Separate pre-movement, travel and doorway queues through simulation or controlled drills, checking receiving-zone availability and communication records for each exit. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「所需疏散時間」的交付需回答：走查橫通道後續路徑及實際門位，保留施工封閉。疏散模型保留人口、速度分布及出口狀態，演練改動由營運與防災責任者批准，教材算例不得當作現場指揮程序。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Suhua Highway Guanyin Tunnel, the required evacuation time handover must address the following evidence: Walk the route beyond each passage and record actual doors and closures. Retain population, speed distribution and exit states; operations and fire-safety owners approve drill changes, and classroom calculations are not incident-command procedures.","failure":"注意干擾：到達橫通道並不等於已抵達可持續停留的安全位置。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Reaching a cross passage does not establish arrival at a sustainable safe location. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b118-v14-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"走查橫通道後續路徑及實際門位，保留施工封閉。以人流模擬或受控演練分辨前置時間、行走與門口排隊，核對每個出口接收區的可用狀態及通訊紀錄。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Walk the route beyond each passage and record actual doors and closures. Separate pre-movement, travel and doorway queues through simulation or controlled drills, checking receiving-zone availability and communication records for each exit. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]},{"id":"b118-v14-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「所需疏散時間」的交付需回答：走查橫通道後續路徑及實際門位，保留施工封閉。疏散模型保留人口、速度分布及出口狀態，演練改動由營運與防災責任者批准，教材算例不得當作現場指揮程序。","textEn":"For Suhua Highway Guanyin Tunnel, the required evacuation time handover must address the following evidence: Walk the route beyond each passage and record actual doors and closures. Retain population, speed distribution and exit states; operations and fire-safety owners approve drill changes, and classroom calculations are not incident-command procedures.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「疏散時間與分區可用性」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Evacuation time and zone availability\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。","走查橫通道後續路徑及實際門位，保留施工封閉。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.","Walk the route beyond each passage and record actual doors and closures."],"answer":2,"explanation":"走查橫通道後續路徑及實際門位，保留施工封閉。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Walk the route beyond each passage and record actual doors and closures. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b118-v14-36","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性：失效診斷","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b118-v14-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「所需疏散時間」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Required evacuation time” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"到達橫通道並不等於已抵達可持續停留的安全位置。以最快成人速度套全部旅客會低估需求，若忽略接收孔受煙或車流影響，疏散可能移到另一個危險邊界。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Reaching a cross passage does not establish arrival at a sustainable safe location. Applying the fastest adult speed to everyone understates demand; overlooking smoke or traffic in the receiving bore can transfer evacuees into another hazard. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：人員速度會受煙熱、能見度及行動能力影響，安全判斷還要比較可用安全時間；橫通道存在但門或鄰孔不可用時，圖上的最短路線不一定能作實際選擇。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A passage shown on a plan may be unusable because its door or receiving bore is unavailable, invalidating the nominal shortest route.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b118-v14-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"到達橫通道並不等於已抵達可持續停留的安全位置。以最快成人速度套全部旅客會低估需求，若忽略接收孔受煙或車流影響，疏散可能移到另一個危險邊界。","textEn":"Reaching a cross passage does not establish arrival at a sustainable safe location. Applying the fastest adult speed to everyone understates demand; overlooking smoke or traffic in the receiving bore can transfer evacuees into another hazard.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]},{"id":"b118-v14-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「疏散時間與分區可用性」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Evacuation time and zone availability\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["到達橫通道並不等於已抵達可持續停留的安全位置。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。"],"optionsEn":["Reaching a cross passage does not establish arrival at a sustainable safe location.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted."],"answer":0,"explanation":"到達橫通道並不等於已抵達可持續停留的安全位置。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Reaching a cross passage does not establish arrival at a sustainable safe location. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b118-v14-37","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b118-v14-36"],"objective":"說明「資產資料完整度」如何影響蘇花改觀音隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Asset-record completeness” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Suhua Highway Guanyin Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"舊坑再利用與新機電資料須保留不同來源和狀態，教材檢查舊圖與竣工圖的里程對照。地下設備的竣工資料必須讓維護人員找到正確位置、材料批次和控制版本。只有上傳圖面而沒有變更歷程，無法分辨元件替換與真正劣化；告警、儀器、線路及工單使用一致識別碼，才可能把量測趨勢連回實際受力或水力系統。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「資產資料完整度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Reuse and new systems require distinct provenance and status; check chainage mapping between old and as-built drawings. Handover must let maintainers find the correct location, material batch and control revision. Drawings without change history cannot distinguish replacement from deterioration. Consistent identifiers across alarms, instruments, circuits and work orders are essential for linking trends to the physical structural or hydraulic system instead of treating each record as an isolated file. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Asset-record completeness” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：設備總數=117 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: asset count=117 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=86.3248 %.","failure":"常見誤解：「全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「資產資料完整度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Asset-record completeness”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b118-v14-37-k1","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover","text":"舊坑再利用與新機電資料須保留不同來源和狀態，教材檢查舊圖與竣工圖的里程對照。地下設備的竣工資料必須讓維護人員找到正確位置、材料批次和控制版本。","textEn":"Reuse and new systems require distinct provenance and status; check chainage mapping between old and as-built drawings. Handover must let maintainers find the correct location, material batch and control revision.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]},{"id":"b118-v14-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「資產編碼與可追溯交接」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Asset identity and traceable handover\" is correct?","options":["全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。","舊坑再利用與新機電資料須保留不同來源和狀態，教材檢查舊圖與竣工圖的里程對照。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.","Reuse and new systems require distinct provenance and status; check chainage mapping between old and as-built drawings.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":1,"explanation":"舊坑再利用與新機電資料須保留不同來源和狀態，教材檢查舊圖與竣工圖的里程對照。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Reuse and new systems require distinct provenance and status; check chainage mapping between old and as-built drawings. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b118-v14-38","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：定量估算","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b118-v14-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「資產資料完整度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Asset-record completeness” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：設備總數=117 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。coverage=100(N−missing)/N=86.3248 %。僅把缺紀錄數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為84.9573 %。邊界：資料完整度，不等於安全或可靠度；擾動為連續敏感度，實際個數為整數；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: asset count=117 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=86.3248 %. Increasing only missing records by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 84.9573 %. Boundary: Record completeness, not safety or reliability; perturbation is continuous sensitivity while actual counts are integers. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：抽查現場設備可否回溯到新孔里程與舊坑介面。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Trace field assets to new-bore chainage and old-gallery interfaces.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b118-v14-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：設備總數=117 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。coverage=100(N−missing)/N=86.3248 %。僅把缺紀錄數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為84.9573 %。邊界：資料完整度，不等於安全或可靠度；擾動為連續敏感度，實際個數為整數；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: asset count=117 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=86.3248 %. Increasing only missing records by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 84.9573 %. Boundary: Record completeness, not safety or reliability; perturbation is continuous sensitivity while actual counts are integers. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]},{"id":"b118-v14-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「資產編碼與可追溯交接」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Asset identity and traceable handover\", which statement holds?","options":["目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。","增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。","原創教學假設：設備總數=117 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。"],"optionsEn":["No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.","Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.","Original teaching assumptions: asset count=117 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=86.3248 %."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：設備總數=117 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: asset count=117 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=86.3248 %. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b118-v14-39","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b118-v14-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「資產資料完整度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Asset-record completeness” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"抽查現場設備可否回溯到新孔里程與舊坑介面。抽取一條告警，從控制畫面追到設備、線路、圖面和工單，核對位置、版本及校正日期並記錄無法閉合的欄位。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Trace field assets to new-bore chainage and old-gallery interfaces. Trace a sampled alarm from screen to equipment, circuit, drawing and work order, checking location, revision and calibration dates and recording broken links. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「資產資料完整度」的交付需回答：抽查現場設備可否回溯到新孔里程與舊坑介面。交接以可完成的定位、查找與復原任務驗證，由維護責任人確認現場可用性；完整度只是資料指標，不代表結構安全或設備可靠。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Suhua Highway Guanyin Tunnel, the asset-record completeness handover must address the following evidence: Trace field assets to new-bore chainage and old-gallery interfaces. Validate handover through achievable location, retrieval and recovery tasks witnessed by maintainers; completeness measures records, not structural safety or equipment reliability.","failure":"注意干擾：舊新里程混用會把漏水和設備工單派到不同實體位置。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Mixed old and new chainages assign leak and equipment work orders to different physical locations. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b118-v14-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"抽查現場設備可否回溯到新孔里程與舊坑介面。抽取一條告警，從控制畫面追到設備、線路、圖面和工單，核對位置、版本及校正日期並記錄無法閉合的欄位。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Trace field assets to new-bore chainage and old-gallery interfaces. Trace a sampled alarm from screen to equipment, circuit, drawing and work order, checking location, revision and calibration dates and recording broken links. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]},{"id":"b118-v14-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「資產資料完整度」的交付需回答：抽查現場設備可否回溯到新孔里程與舊坑介面。交接以可完成的定位、查找與復原任務驗證，由維護責任人確認現場可用性；完整度只是資料指標，不代表結構安全或設備可靠。","textEn":"For Suhua Highway Guanyin Tunnel, the asset-record completeness handover must address the following evidence: Trace field assets to new-bore chainage and old-gallery interfaces. Validate handover through achievable location, retrieval and recovery tasks witnessed by maintainers; completeness measures records, not structural safety or equipment reliability.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「資產編碼與可追溯交接」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Asset identity and traceable handover\"?","options":["抽查現場設備可否回溯到新孔里程與舊坑介面。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","只要空間分成兩層就可以採用相同的樓板荷載。"],"optionsEn":["Trace field assets to new-bore chainage and old-gallery interfaces.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Any space divided into two levels can use the same deck loading."],"answer":0,"explanation":"抽查現場設備可否回溯到新孔里程與舊坑介面。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Trace field assets to new-bore chainage and old-gallery interfaces. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b118-v14-40","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：失效診斷","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b118-v14-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「資產資料完整度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Asset-record completeness” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"舊新里程混用會把漏水和設備工單派到不同實體位置。設備改名卻未更新控制畫面會引導人員隔離錯誤回路，材料批次缺漏則使同批缺陷無法追蹤到其他位置。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Mixed old and new chainages assign leak and equipment work orders to different physical locations. Renaming an asset without updating the screen can isolate the wrong circuit; missing material batches prevent tracing related defects at other locations. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：只有上傳圖面而沒有變更歷程，無法分辨元件替換與真正劣化；告警、儀器、線路及工單使用一致識別碼，才可能把量測趨勢連回實際受力或水力系統。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Consistent identifiers across alarms, instruments, circuits and work orders are essential for linking trends to the physical structural or hydraulic system instead of treating each record as an isolated file.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b118-v14-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"舊新里程混用會把漏水和設備工單派到不同實體位置。設備改名卻未更新控制畫面會引導人員隔離錯誤回路，材料批次缺漏則使同批缺陷無法追蹤到其他位置。","textEn":"Mixed old and new chainages assign leak and equipment work orders to different physical locations. Renaming an asset without updating the screen can isolate the wrong circuit; missing material batches prevent tracing related defects at other locations.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]},{"id":"b118-v14-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「資產編碼與可追溯交接」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Asset identity and traceable handover\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","舊新里程混用會把漏水和設備工單派到不同實體位置。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Mixed old and new chainages assign leak and equipment work orders to different physical locations.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":1,"explanation":"舊新里程混用會把漏水和設備工單派到不同實體位置。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Mixed old and new chainages assign leak and equipment work orders to different physical locations. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b118","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b118-history"],"curriculumVersion":14,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000},{"id":"b119","title":"港珠澳大橋海底隧道","titleEn":"Hong Kong–Zhuhai–Macao immersed tunnel","category":"underground","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"香港政府工程頁把港珠澳主橋分為約23公里海上高架及約7公里隧道段，並說明外海沉管浮運落底的環境挑戰。本課集中隧道和人工島介面，循序分析箱體框架、浮力、基床、止水、測量及耐久；主橋、整體跨海計畫和沉管段的尺度各自保留原計量邊界。","summaryEn":"The Hong Kong government separates the main crossing into about 23 km of viaduct and 7 km of tunnel and describes open-sea immersion challenges. This course focuses on tunnel-island interfaces through box-frame action, buoyancy, bedding, seals, surveying and durability. Main-crossing, whole-programme and immersed-section dimensions retain their distinct measurement boundaries.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"ug-landmarks","subcategoryTitle":"世界隧道與地下巨作","subcategoryTitleEn":"World tunnels and underground landmarks","learningTrack":"underground","learningSubdiscipline":"ug-landmarks","learningTags":["underground","ug-landmarks","tunnel"],"architectureFamily":"tunnel","architectureNodes":[["路線里程與端點","Alignment chainage and endpoints"],["頂板跨中彎矩","Roof-span bending"],["差異沉陷梯度","Differential settlement gradient"],["方向角誤差","Orientation error"],["擴散特徵長度","Diffusion characteristic length"],["資產資料完整度","Asset-record completeness"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,5],[1,5]],"diagram":{"type":"tunnel","labels":["路線里程與端點","頂板跨中彎矩","差異沉陷梯度","方向角誤差","擴散特徵長度"],"labelsEn":["Alignment chainage and endpoints","Roof-span bending","Differential settlement gradient","Orientation error","Diffusion characteristic length"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"原創綜合審查：先計算「矩形沉管的框架受力」，再獨立計算「控制網與貫通誤差」。原創教學假設：單位長載重=38 kN/m；跨距=3.15 m。M=qL²/8=47.1319 kN·m。僅把跨距增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為57.0296 kN·m。邊界：均載簡支單向條帶，連續框架及板效應另驗；不是本工程實測或允收值。原創教學假設：控制長度=5160 m；方向偏角=2.5 arcsec。e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.062541 m。僅把方向偏角增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.0687951 m。邊界：小角度方向偏差，未加入控制網相關性及折光；不是本工程實測或允收值。兩組結果的單位與邊界不同，不能直接相加。請列出一項缺少的現場輸入，說明它會影響哪個結論，以及哪種獨立量測可以縮小不確定度。","textEn":"Original integrated review: first calculate rectangular immersed-box frame action, then independently calculate control network and breakthrough error. Original teaching assumptions: line load=38 kN/m; span=3.15 m. M=qL²/8=47.1319 kN·m. Increasing only span by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 57.0296 kN·m. Boundary: Uniformly loaded simply supported strip; frame continuity and plate action need separate checks. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Original teaching assumptions: control length=5160 m; orientation error=2.5 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.062541 m. Increasing only orientation error by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.0687951 m. Boundary: Small-angle orientation error without network correlation or refraction. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. The outputs have different units and boundaries and cannot simply be added. Identify one missing field input, explain which conclusion it changes and select an independent measurement to reduce uncertainty.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":14,"enrichmentVersion":14,"stages":[{"id":"b119-v14-s1","title":"地層條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Ground conditions, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「服務邊界與路線代價」與「矩形沉管的框架受力」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\" and \"Rectangular immersed-box frame action\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b119-v14-01","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「路線里程與端點」如何影響港珠澳大橋海底隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Alignment chainage and endpoints” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Hong Kong–Zhuhai–Macao immersed tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"港珠澳的橋、隧道與口岸不是同一工程範圍，教材先確定隧道段端點再比較道路服務。隧道選線同時改變洞口、覆土與縱坡，短路線不保證低地質風險。比較方案必須使用相同起訖點，並分開主孔、引道及服務坑的工程數量；交通時間只是需求的一個指標，不能代替施工可達性或長期維修評估。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「路線里程與端點」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Bridge, tunnel and border facilities have different scope; define tunnel endpoints before comparing road service. Alignment changes portals, cover and gradient together, so a shorter tunnel need not have lower geological risk. Compare options between identical endpoints and distinguish running bores, approaches and service galleries. Travel time measures one service benefit but cannot replace assessment of construction access, maintenance closures or exposure to uncertain ground. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Alignment chainage and endpoints” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：長度=19.2 km；速度=60 km/h。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: length=19.2 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=19.2 min.","failure":"常見誤解：「最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「路線里程與端點」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Alignment chainage and endpoints”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b119-v14-01-k1","title":"服務邊界與路線代價","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost","text":"港珠澳的橋、隧道與口岸不是同一工程範圍，教材先確定隧道段端點再比較道路服務。隧道選線同時改變洞口、覆土與縱坡，短路線不保證低地質風險。","textEn":"Bridge, tunnel and border facilities have different scope; define tunnel endpoints before comparing road service. Alignment changes portals, cover and gradient together, so a shorter tunnel need not have lower geological risk.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]},{"id":"b119-v14-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「服務邊界與路線代價」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\" is correct?","options":["最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。","港珠澳的橋、隧道與口岸不是同一工程範圍，教材先確定隧道段端點再比較道路服務。","矩形沉管可以直接使用圓環均勻外壓公式設計。"],"optionsEn":["The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.","Bridge, tunnel and border facilities have different scope; define tunnel endpoints before comparing road service.","A rectangular immersed tube can be designed directly with a circular-ring pressure formula."],"answer":1,"explanation":"港珠澳的橋、隧道與口岸不是同一工程範圍，教材先確定隧道段端點再比較道路服務。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Bridge, tunnel and border facilities have different scope; define tunnel endpoints before comparing road service. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b119-v14-02","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：定量估算","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b119-v14-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「路線里程與端點」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Alignment chainage and endpoints” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：長度=19.2 km；速度=60 km/h。t=60L/v=19.2 min。僅把長度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為21.12 min。邊界：假想交通旅程，未含加減速、排隊及實際時刻表；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: length=19.2 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=19.2 min. Increasing only length by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 21.12 min. Boundary: Hypothetical transport journey excluding acceleration, queues and the real timetable. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在數量表分開主橋、隧道與接線里程。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Separate main crossing, tunnel and approach lengths in the quantity register.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b119-v14-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：長度=19.2 km；速度=60 km/h。t=60L/v=19.2 min。僅把長度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為21.12 min。邊界：假想交通旅程，未含加減速、排隊及實際時刻表；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: length=19.2 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=19.2 min. Increasing only length by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 21.12 min. Boundary: Hypothetical transport journey excluding acceleration, queues and the real timetable. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]},{"id":"b119-v14-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「服務邊界與路線代價」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\", which statement holds?","options":["各管節平均高程接近就能排除接頭差異變形。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。","原創教學假設：長度=19.2 km；速度=60 km/h。"],"optionsEn":["Similar mean element elevations exclude differential movement at joints.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.","Original teaching assumptions: length=19.2 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=19.2 min."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：長度=19.2 km；速度=60 km/h。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: length=19.2 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=19.2 min. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b119-v14-03","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b119-v14-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「路線里程與端點」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Alignment chainage and endpoints” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在數量表分開主橋、隧道與接線里程。把縱斷面、地形與地質剖面疊合，以端點坐標獨立反算距離，再將主孔與支坑數量分開核對。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Separate main crossing, tunnel and approach lengths in the quantity register. Overlay the longitudinal profile, terrain and geology; independently derive distances from endpoint coordinates and reconcile running-bore and gallery quantities separately. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「路線里程與端點」的交付需回答：在數量表分開主橋、隧道與接線里程。在方案表中凍結起訖點、計量範圍及地質假設，任何改線都要同步更新高程、數量與服務情境，不能只替換總長。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Hong Kong–Zhuhai–Macao immersed tunnel, the alignment chainage and endpoints handover must address the following evidence: Separate main crossing, tunnel and approach lengths in the quantity register. Freeze endpoints, measurement scope and ground assumptions in the option register; realignment requires coordinated updates to elevations, quantities and service scenarios rather than replacing one length.","failure":"注意干擾：把整體跨海長度當沉管長度會放大水下施工數量。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using total crossing length as immersed length inflates underwater quantities. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b119-v14-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在數量表分開主橋、隧道與接線里程。把縱斷面、地形與地質剖面疊合，以端點坐標獨立反算距離，再將主孔與支坑數量分開核對。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Separate main crossing, tunnel and approach lengths in the quantity register. Overlay the longitudinal profile, terrain and geology; independently derive distances from endpoint coordinates and reconcile running-bore and gallery quantities separately. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]},{"id":"b119-v14-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「路線里程與端點」的交付需回答：在數量表分開主橋、隧道與接線里程。在方案表中凍結起訖點、計量範圍及地質假設，任何改線都要同步更新高程、數量與服務情境，不能只替換總長。","textEn":"For Hong Kong–Zhuhai–Macao immersed tunnel, the alignment chainage and endpoints handover must address the following evidence: Separate main crossing, tunnel and approach lengths in the quantity register. Freeze endpoints, measurement scope and ground assumptions in the option register; realignment requires coordinated updates to elevations, quantities and service scenarios rather than replacing one length.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「服務邊界與路線代價」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\"?","options":["在數量表分開主橋、隧道與接線里程。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","擴散長度就是鋼筋開始腐蝕的位置和精確時間。"],"optionsEn":["Separate main crossing, tunnel and approach lengths in the quantity register.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Diffusion length gives the exact location and time of corrosion initiation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"在數量表分開主橋、隧道與接線里程。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Separate main crossing, tunnel and approach lengths in the quantity register. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b119-v14-04","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：失效診斷","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b119-v14-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「路線里程與端點」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Alignment chainage and endpoints” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把整體跨海長度當沉管長度會放大水下施工數量。混用全線與單孔長度會同時扭曲工程數量、行程及逃生距離，造成方案比較失去共同基準。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using total crossing length as immersed length inflates underwater quantities. Mixing whole-route and single-bore lengths distorts quantities, journey time and escape distance, destroying the common basis of an option comparison. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：比較方案必須使用相同起訖點，並分開主孔、引道及服務坑的工程數量；交通時間只是需求的一個指標，不能代替施工可達性或長期維修評估。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Travel time measures one service benefit but cannot replace assessment of construction access, maintenance closures or exposure to uncertain ground.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b119-v14-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把整體跨海長度當沉管長度會放大水下施工數量。混用全線與單孔長度會同時扭曲工程數量、行程及逃生距離，造成方案比較失去共同基準。","textEn":"Using total crossing length as immersed length inflates underwater quantities. Mixing whole-route and single-bore lengths distorts quantities, journey time and escape distance, destroying the common basis of an option comparison.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]},{"id":"b119-v14-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「服務邊界與路線代價」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","把整體跨海長度當沉管長度會放大水下施工數量。","矩形沉管可以直接使用圓環均勻外壓公式設計。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Using total crossing length as immersed length inflates underwater quantities.","A rectangular immersed tube can be designed directly with a circular-ring pressure formula."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把整體跨海長度當沉管長度會放大水下施工數量。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using total crossing length as immersed length inflates underwater quantities. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b119-v14-05","title":"矩形沉管的框架受力：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Rectangular immersed-box frame action: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b119-v14-04"],"objective":"說明「頂板跨中彎矩」如何影響港珠澳大橋海底隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Roof-span bending” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Hong Kong–Zhuhai–Macao immersed tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"港珠澳沉管是矩形多室箱體，教材研究中牆對頂板跨距的控制，禁止以圓環膜應力取代框架。矩形沉管的頂板、側牆與中牆透過框架連續性傳遞水土壓力，不能套圓形薄環的膜應力。單向簡支條帶只能估計局部彎矩量級；施工浮運、落底、回填和使用期的邊界不同，支承沉陷、接頭剪力及裂縫寬度仍須分階段檢核。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「頂板跨中彎矩」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The immersed structure is a multicell rectangular box; examine how partitions control roof spans without substituting circular-ring membrane stress. A rectangular immersed tube transfers water and earth pressure through roof, walls and internal partitions acting as a frame. A circular thin-ring membrane formula is inappropriate. A simply supported strip estimates one bending scale only; flotation, placement, backfill and service change the restraints, requiring staged checks of settlement, joint shear and cracking. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Roof-span bending” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：單位長載重=38 kN/m；跨距=3.15 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: line load=38 kN/m; span=3.15 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「矩形沉管可以直接使用圓環均勻外壓公式設計。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A rectangular immersed tube can be designed directly with a circular-ring pressure formula.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「頂板跨中彎矩」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Roof-span bending”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b119-v14-05-k1","title":"矩形沉管的框架受力","titleEn":"Rectangular immersed-box frame action","text":"港珠澳沉管是矩形多室箱體，教材研究中牆對頂板跨距的控制，禁止以圓環膜應力取代框架。矩形沉管的頂板、側牆與中牆透過框架連續性傳遞水土壓力，不能套圓形薄環的膜應力。","textEn":"The immersed structure is a multicell rectangular box; examine how partitions control roof spans without substituting circular-ring membrane stress. A rectangular immersed tube transfers water and earth pressure through roof, walls and internal partitions acting as a frame.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]},{"id":"b119-v14-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：矩形沉管可以直接使用圓環均勻外壓公式設計。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A rectangular immersed tube can be designed directly with a circular-ring pressure formula. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「矩形沉管的框架受力」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Rectangular immersed-box frame action\" is correct?","options":["矩形沉管可以直接使用圓環均勻外壓公式設計。","剩餘浮力為正就代表浮運姿態在所有波況穩定。","港珠澳沉管是矩形多室箱體，教材研究中牆對頂板跨距的控制，禁止以圓環膜應力取代框架。"],"optionsEn":["A rectangular immersed tube can be designed directly with a circular-ring pressure formula.","Positive residual buoyancy establishes stability in every sea state.","The immersed structure is a multicell rectangular box; examine how partitions control roof spans without substituting circular-ring membrane stress."],"answer":2,"explanation":"港珠澳沉管是矩形多室箱體，教材研究中牆對頂板跨距的控制，禁止以圓環膜應力取代框架。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The immersed structure is a multicell rectangular box; examine how partitions control roof spans without substituting circular-ring membrane stress. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b119-v14-06","title":"矩形沉管的框架受力：定量估算","titleEn":"Rectangular immersed-box frame action: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b119-v14-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「頂板跨中彎矩」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Roof-span bending” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：單位長載重=38 kN/m；跨距=3.15 m。M=qL²/8=47.1319 kN·m。僅把跨距增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為57.0296 kN·m。邊界：均載簡支單向條帶，連續框架及板效應另驗；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: line load=38 kN/m; span=3.15 m. M=qL²/8=47.1319 kN·m. Increasing only span by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 57.0296 kN·m. Boundary: Uniformly loaded simply supported strip; frame continuity and plate action need separate checks. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對每個室的支承與荷載分配，再作局部條帶比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check support and load distribution for each cell before local strip comparison.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b119-v14-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：單位長載重=38 kN/m；跨距=3.15 m。M=qL²/8=47.1319 kN·m。僅把跨距增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為57.0296 kN·m。邊界：均載簡支單向條帶，連續框架及板效應另驗；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: line load=38 kN/m; span=3.15 m. M=qL²/8=47.1319 kN·m. Increasing only span by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 57.0296 kN·m. Boundary: Uniformly loaded simply supported strip; frame continuity and plate action need separate checks. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]},{"id":"b119-v14-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「矩形沉管的框架受力」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Rectangular immersed-box frame action\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：單位長載重=38 kN/m；跨距=3.15 m。","接縫平均寬度合格就不必量測局部錯台及扭轉。","混凝土抗壓強度合格就代表厚壁構件不會產生熱裂縫。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: line load=38 kN/m; span=3.15 m.","An acceptable average joint width makes local offset and twist measurements unnecessary.","Adequate compressive strength proves that thick concrete cannot develop thermal cracks."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：單位長載重=38 kN/m；跨距=3.15 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: line load=38 kN/m; span=3.15 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b119-v14-07","title":"矩形沉管的框架受力：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Rectangular immersed-box frame action: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b119-v14-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「頂板跨中彎矩」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Roof-span bending” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對每個室的支承與荷載分配，再作局部條帶比較。比對頂板及中牆應變，使用含支承剛度的框架模型核對彎矩分配，將落底前後量測分開。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check support and load distribution for each cell before local strip comparison. Compare roof and partition strain with a frame model including support stiffness, keeping measurements before and after bedding separate. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「頂板跨中彎矩」的交付需回答：核對每個室的支承與荷載分配，再作局部條帶比較。把單條帶、整體框架及接頭模型分開提交，標註適用施工階段和受力方向，保留裂縫及水密試驗的獨立判定。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Hong Kong–Zhuhai–Macao immersed tunnel, the roof-span bending handover must address the following evidence: Check support and load distribution for each cell before local strip comparison. Submit strip, whole-frame and joint models separately, identifying stage and load direction while retaining independent cracking and watertightness assessments.","failure":"注意干擾：忽略內牆連續性可能錯估支點負彎矩與裂縫位置。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Ignoring wall continuity misstates support hogging and crack location. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b119-v14-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對每個室的支承與荷載分配，再作局部條帶比較。比對頂板及中牆應變，使用含支承剛度的框架模型核對彎矩分配，將落底前後量測分開。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Check support and load distribution for each cell before local strip comparison. Compare roof and partition strain with a frame model including support stiffness, keeping measurements before and after bedding separate. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]},{"id":"b119-v14-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「頂板跨中彎矩」的交付需回答：核對每個室的支承與荷載分配，再作局部條帶比較。把單條帶、整體框架及接頭模型分開提交，標註適用施工階段和受力方向，保留裂縫及水密試驗的獨立判定。","textEn":"For Hong Kong–Zhuhai–Macao immersed tunnel, the roof-span bending handover must address the following evidence: Check support and load distribution for each cell before local strip comparison. Submit strip, whole-frame and joint models separately, identifying stage and load direction while retaining independent cracking and watertightness assessments.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「矩形沉管的框架受力」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Rectangular immersed-box frame action\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","核對每個室的支承與荷載分配，再作局部條帶比較。","風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Check support and load distribution for each cell before local strip comparison.","Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel."],"answer":1,"explanation":"核對每個室的支承與荷載分配，再作局部條帶比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check support and load distribution for each cell before local strip comparison. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b119-v14-08","title":"矩形沉管的框架受力：失效診斷","titleEn":"Rectangular immersed-box frame action: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b119-v14-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「頂板跨中彎矩」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Roof-span bending” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"忽略內牆連續性可能錯估支點負彎矩與裂縫位置。忽略中牆支承或不均勻底床會錯估正負彎矩，局部裂縫可能是邊界變化而非材料強度不足。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Ignoring wall continuity misstates support hogging and crack location. Omitting partition support or uneven bedding misallocates positive and negative moments; local cracking may reflect changed restraints rather than weak material. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：單向簡支條帶只能估計局部彎矩量級；施工浮運、落底、回填和使用期的邊界不同，支承沉陷、接頭剪力及裂縫寬度仍須分階段檢核。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A simply supported strip estimates one bending scale only; flotation, placement, backfill and service change the restraints, requiring staged checks of settlement, joint shear and cracking.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「矩形沉管可以直接使用圓環均勻外壓公式設計。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A rectangular immersed tube can be designed directly with a circular-ring pressure formula.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b119-v14-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"忽略內牆連續性可能錯估支點負彎矩與裂縫位置。忽略中牆支承或不均勻底床會錯估正負彎矩，局部裂縫可能是邊界變化而非材料強度不足。","textEn":"Ignoring wall continuity misstates support hogging and crack location. Omitting partition support or uneven bedding misallocates positive and negative moments; local cracking may reflect changed restraints rather than weak material.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]},{"id":"b119-v14-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「矩形沉管的框架受力」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Rectangular immersed-box frame action\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","剩餘浮力為正就代表浮運姿態在所有波況穩定。","忽略內牆連續性可能錯估支點負彎矩與裂縫位置。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Positive residual buoyancy establishes stability in every sea state.","Ignoring wall continuity misstates support hogging and crack location."],"answer":2,"explanation":"忽略內牆連續性可能錯估支點負彎矩與裂縫位置。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Ignoring wall continuity misstates support hogging and crack location. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b119-v14-s2","title":"機制、材料與定量設計","titleEn":"Mechanisms, materials and quantitative design","description":"本階段聚焦「浮運重量帳與姿態穩定」與「基床變形與接頭轉角」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Tow-out mass balance and stability\" and \"Bedding movement and joint rotation\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b119-v14-09","title":"浮運重量帳與姿態穩定：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Tow-out mass balance and stability: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b119-v14-08"],"objective":"說明「剩餘浮力」如何影響港珠澳大橋海底隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Residual buoyancy” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Hong Kong–Zhuhai–Macao immersed tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"外海管節浮運需將重量、波浪和流場分開，教材的剩餘浮力只能說明靜態垂直力。浮力由排開水體重量決定，總質量還包含設備、臨時封端及艙內液體。重量帳只能判定淨垂直力，不能證明浮運穩定；壓載液自由表面、重心位置、拖纜與波浪都會改變傾斜反應，落底接觸亦需另建模型。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「剩餘浮力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Open-sea towing needs separate mass, wave and current assessments; residual buoyancy describes only static vertical force. Buoyancy equals displaced water weight, while total mass includes equipment, temporary bulkheads and liquid contents. A mass balance determines net vertical force but does not establish towing stability. Ballast free surfaces, centre of gravity, tow lines and waves affect heel response, and initial contact with the bed needs another model. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Residual buoyancy” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：水密度=1025 kg/m³；排水體積=13600 m³；總質量=1.35218e+07 kg。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: water density=1025 kg/m³; displacement=13600 m³; mass=1.35218e+07 kg.","failure":"常見誤解：「剩餘浮力為正就代表浮運姿態在所有波況穩定。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Positive residual buoyancy establishes stability in every sea state.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「剩餘浮力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Residual buoyancy”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b119-v14-09-k1","title":"浮運重量帳與姿態穩定","titleEn":"Tow-out mass balance and stability","text":"外海管節浮運需將重量、波浪和流場分開，教材的剩餘浮力只能說明靜態垂直力。浮力由排開水體重量決定，總質量還包含設備、臨時封端及艙內液體。","textEn":"Open-sea towing needs separate mass, wave and current assessments; residual buoyancy describes only static vertical force. Buoyancy equals displaced water weight, while total mass includes equipment, temporary bulkheads and liquid contents.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]},{"id":"b119-v14-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：剩餘浮力為正就代表浮運姿態在所有波況穩定。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Positive residual buoyancy establishes stability in every sea state. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「浮運重量帳與姿態穩定」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Tow-out mass balance and stability\" is correct?","options":["外海管節浮運需將重量、波浪和流場分開，教材的剩餘浮力只能說明靜態垂直力。","剩餘浮力為正就代表浮運姿態在所有波況穩定。","各管節平均高程接近就能排除接頭差異變形。"],"optionsEn":["Open-sea towing needs separate mass, wave and current assessments; residual buoyancy describes only static vertical force.","Positive residual buoyancy establishes stability in every sea state.","Similar mean element elevations exclude differential movement at joints."],"answer":0,"explanation":"外海管節浮運需將重量、波浪和流場分開，教材的剩餘浮力只能說明靜態垂直力。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Open-sea towing needs separate mass, wave and current assessments; residual buoyancy describes only static vertical force. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b119-v14-10","title":"浮運重量帳與姿態穩定：定量估算","titleEn":"Tow-out mass balance and stability: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b119-v14-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「剩餘浮力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Residual buoyancy” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：水密度=1025 kg/m³；排水體積=13600 m³；總質量=1.35218e+07 kg。R=(ρV−m)g/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=4102.54 kN。僅把排水體積增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為17777.7 kN。邊界：靜水剩餘浮力，不驗證傾斜穩性及自由液面；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: water density=1025 kg/m³; displacement=13600 m³; mass=1.35218e+07 kg. R=(ρV−m)g/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=4102.54 kN. Increasing only displacement by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 17777.7 kN. Boundary: Still-water buoyancy reserve, not heel stability or free-surface verification. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以吃水、液艙水位及重量清冊互查，另列海況。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Cross-check draught, tank levels and the mass register while recording sea state separately.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b119-v14-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：水密度=1025 kg/m³；排水體積=13600 m³；總質量=1.35218e+07 kg。R=(ρV−m)g/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=4102.54 kN。僅把排水體積增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為17777.7 kN。邊界：靜水剩餘浮力，不驗證傾斜穩性及自由液面；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: water density=1025 kg/m³; displacement=13600 m³; mass=1.35218e+07 kg. R=(ρV−m)g/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=4102.54 kN. Increasing only displacement by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 17777.7 kN. Boundary: Still-water buoyancy reserve, not heel stability or free-surface verification. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]},{"id":"b119-v14-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「浮運重量帳與姿態穩定」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Tow-out mass balance and stability\", which statement holds?","options":["兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。","原創教學假設：水密度=1025 kg/m³；排水體積=13600 m³；總質量=1.35218e+07 kg。","擴散長度就是鋼筋開始腐蝕的位置和精確時間。"],"optionsEn":["Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.","Original teaching assumptions: water density=1025 kg/m³; displacement=13600 m³; mass=1.35218e+07 kg.","Diffusion length gives the exact location and time of corrosion initiation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：水密度=1025 kg/m³；排水體積=13600 m³；總質量=1.35218e+07 kg。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: water density=1025 kg/m³; displacement=13600 m³; mass=1.35218e+07 kg. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b119-v14-11","title":"浮運重量帳與姿態穩定：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Tow-out mass balance and stability: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b119-v14-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「剩餘浮力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Residual buoyancy” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以吃水、液艙水位及重量清冊互查，另列海況。以實際重量清冊和吃水測量互核，量測液艙水位及橫傾，檢查密度與體積是否採同一狀態。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Cross-check draught, tank levels and the mass register while recording sea state separately. Reconcile an itemised mass register with draught measurements, tank levels and heel, checking that density and displaced volume describe the same state. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「剩餘浮力」的交付需回答：以吃水、液艙水位及重量清冊互查，另列海況。質量清冊每次變更都重新確認重心和吃水，操作窗口依核准海事方案及量測決定，不由本課靜力式制定。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Hong Kong–Zhuhai–Macao immersed tunnel, the residual buoyancy handover must address the following evidence: Cross-check draught, tank levels and the mass register while recording sea state separately. Update centre of gravity and draught after every mass-register change; approved marine procedures and observations determine operating windows, not this static classroom equation.","failure":"注意干擾：相同剩餘浮力的兩個壓載配置可能有不同傾斜穩性。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Two ballast arrangements with equal residual buoyancy can have different heel stability. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b119-v14-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以吃水、液艙水位及重量清冊互查，另列海況。以實際重量清冊和吃水測量互核，量測液艙水位及橫傾，檢查密度與體積是否採同一狀態。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Cross-check draught, tank levels and the mass register while recording sea state separately. Reconcile an itemised mass register with draught measurements, tank levels and heel, checking that density and displaced volume describe the same state. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]},{"id":"b119-v14-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「剩餘浮力」的交付需回答：以吃水、液艙水位及重量清冊互查，另列海況。質量清冊每次變更都重新確認重心和吃水，操作窗口依核准海事方案及量測決定，不由本課靜力式制定。","textEn":"For Hong Kong–Zhuhai–Macao immersed tunnel, the residual buoyancy handover must address the following evidence: Cross-check draught, tank levels and the mass register while recording sea state separately. Update centre of gravity and draught after every mass-register change; approved marine procedures and observations determine operating windows, not this static classroom equation.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「浮運重量帳與姿態穩定」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Tow-out mass balance and stability\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。","以吃水、液艙水位及重量清冊互查，另列海況。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.","Cross-check draught, tank levels and the mass register while recording sea state separately."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以吃水、液艙水位及重量清冊互查，另列海況。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Cross-check draught, tank levels and the mass register while recording sea state separately. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b119-v14-12","title":"浮運重量帳與姿態穩定：失效診斷","titleEn":"Tow-out mass balance and stability: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b119-v14-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「剩餘浮力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Residual buoyancy” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"相同剩餘浮力的兩個壓載配置可能有不同傾斜穩性。漏列臨時設備或自由液面會使浮力帳看似足夠卻缺乏回正能力，偏載也可能先造成局部接觸。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Two ballast arrangements with equal residual buoyancy can have different heel stability. Missing temporary equipment or free-surface effects can leave an apparently adequate buoyancy balance with insufficient restoring capacity and premature local contact. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：重量帳只能判定淨垂直力，不能證明浮運穩定；壓載液自由表面、重心位置、拖纜與波浪都會改變傾斜反應，落底接觸亦需另建模型。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Ballast free surfaces, centre of gravity, tow lines and waves affect heel response, and initial contact with the bed needs another model.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「剩餘浮力為正就代表浮運姿態在所有波況穩定。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Positive residual buoyancy establishes stability in every sea state.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b119-v14-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"相同剩餘浮力的兩個壓載配置可能有不同傾斜穩性。漏列臨時設備或自由液面會使浮力帳看似足夠卻缺乏回正能力，偏載也可能先造成局部接觸。","textEn":"Two ballast arrangements with equal residual buoyancy can have different heel stability. Missing temporary equipment or free-surface effects can leave an apparently adequate buoyancy balance with insufficient restoring capacity and premature local contact.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]},{"id":"b119-v14-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「浮運重量帳與姿態穩定」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Tow-out mass balance and stability\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["相同剩餘浮力的兩個壓載配置可能有不同傾斜穩性。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","各管節平均高程接近就能排除接頭差異變形。"],"optionsEn":["Two ballast arrangements with equal residual buoyancy can have different heel stability.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Similar mean element elevations exclude differential movement at joints."],"answer":0,"explanation":"相同剩餘浮力的兩個壓載配置可能有不同傾斜穩性。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Two ballast arrangements with equal residual buoyancy can have different heel stability. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b119-v14-13","title":"基床變形與接頭轉角：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Bedding movement and joint rotation: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b119-v14-12"],"objective":"說明「差異沉陷梯度」如何影響港珠澳大橋海底隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Differential settlement gradient” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Hong Kong–Zhuhai–Macao immersed tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"人工島附近與中央沉管的地層支承不同，教材追蹤差異固結對接頭轉角的影響。沉管基床將箱體荷載傳給海床，局部沖刷、回填不均與軟弱層固結會改變接觸分布。總沉陷小不代表接頭轉角小；相鄰管節的差異位移和支承長度才控制局部變形，施工量測須保留時間與潮位基準。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「差異沉陷梯度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Island approaches and central tubes have different support conditions; trace differential consolidation into joint rotation. The bed transfers tube load into the seabed, and scour, uneven backfill or consolidation alter contact. Small total settlement does not imply small joint rotation; differential movement and support length control local distortion. Construction observations must preserve time and tidal datum because immediate placement and delayed consolidation describe different mechanisms. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Differential settlement gradient” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：差異沉陷=6 mm；基線長度=130 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: differential settlement=6 mm; baseline=130 m. β=Δs/L=0.0461538 mm/m.","failure":"常見誤解：「各管節平均高程接近就能排除接頭差異變形。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Similar mean element elevations exclude differential movement at joints.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「差異沉陷梯度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Differential settlement gradient”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b119-v14-13-k1","title":"基床變形與接頭轉角","titleEn":"Bedding movement and joint rotation","text":"人工島附近與中央沉管的地層支承不同，教材追蹤差異固結對接頭轉角的影響。沉管基床將箱體荷載傳給海床，局部沖刷、回填不均與軟弱層固結會改變接觸分布。","textEn":"Island approaches and central tubes have different support conditions; trace differential consolidation into joint rotation. The bed transfers tube load into the seabed, and scour, uneven backfill or consolidation alter contact.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]},{"id":"b119-v14-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：各管節平均高程接近就能排除接頭差異變形。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Similar mean element elevations exclude differential movement at joints. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「基床變形與接頭轉角」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Bedding movement and joint rotation\" is correct?","options":["各管節平均高程接近就能排除接頭差異變形。","人工島附近與中央沉管的地層支承不同，教材追蹤差異固結對接頭轉角的影響。","接縫平均寬度合格就不必量測局部錯台及扭轉。"],"optionsEn":["Similar mean element elevations exclude differential movement at joints.","Island approaches and central tubes have different support conditions; trace differential consolidation into joint rotation.","An acceptable average joint width makes local offset and twist measurements unnecessary."],"answer":1,"explanation":"人工島附近與中央沉管的地層支承不同，教材追蹤差異固結對接頭轉角的影響。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Island approaches and central tubes have different support conditions; trace differential consolidation into joint rotation. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b119-v14-14","title":"基床變形與接頭轉角：定量估算","titleEn":"Bedding movement and joint rotation: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b119-v14-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「差異沉陷梯度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Differential settlement gradient” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：差異沉陷=6 mm；基線長度=130 m。β=Δs/L=0.0461538 mm/m。僅把差異沉陷增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.0507692 mm/m。邊界：小變形角變化指標，不是完整固結解；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: differential settlement=6 mm; baseline=130 m. β=Δs/L=0.0461538 mm/m. Increasing only differential settlement by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.0507692 mm/m. Boundary: Small-deformation angular-distortion indicator, not a consolidation solution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：按管節編號對照沉陷、孔壓及回填時間。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare settlement, pore pressure and backfill timing by element identifier.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b119-v14-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：差異沉陷=6 mm；基線長度=130 m。β=Δs/L=0.0461538 mm/m。僅把差異沉陷增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.0507692 mm/m。邊界：小變形角變化指標，不是完整固結解；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: differential settlement=6 mm; baseline=130 m. β=Δs/L=0.0461538 mm/m. Increasing only differential settlement by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.0507692 mm/m. Boundary: Small-deformation angular-distortion indicator, not a consolidation solution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]},{"id":"b119-v14-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「基床變形與接頭轉角」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Bedding movement and joint rotation\", which statement holds?","options":["混凝土抗壓強度合格就代表厚壁構件不會產生熱裂縫。","風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。","原創教學假設：差異沉陷=6 mm；基線長度=130 m。"],"optionsEn":["Adequate compressive strength proves that thick concrete cannot develop thermal cracks.","Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.","Original teaching assumptions: differential settlement=6 mm; baseline=130 m. β=Δs/L=0.0461538 mm/m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：差異沉陷=6 mm；基線長度=130 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: differential settlement=6 mm; baseline=130 m. β=Δs/L=0.0461538 mm/m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b119-v14-15","title":"基床變形與接頭轉角：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Bedding movement and joint rotation: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b119-v14-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「差異沉陷梯度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Differential settlement gradient” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"按管節編號對照沉陷、孔壓及回填時間。用管節水準網、海床剖面及孔壓變化交叉核對，將整體下沉與相鄰節轉角分開評估。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare settlement, pore pressure and backfill timing by element identifier. Cross-check tube levelling, seabed profiles and pore-pressure change, separating overall settlement from rotation between neighbouring elements. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「差異沉陷梯度」的交付需回答：按管節編號對照沉陷、孔壓及回填時間。將基床施工紀錄與長期水準資料連結至管節編號，差異變形先查基準和孔壓，再由設計者判斷接觸及接頭。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Hong Kong–Zhuhai–Macao immersed tunnel, the differential settlement gradient handover must address the following evidence: Compare settlement, pore pressure and backfill timing by element identifier. Link bedding records and long-term levelling to element identifiers; check datum and pore pressure before designers interpret contact and joint behaviour.","failure":"注意干擾：只核總沉陷可能漏掉島隧轉換處的局部折角。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Total settlement alone misses local angular distortion at island transitions. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b119-v14-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"按管節編號對照沉陷、孔壓及回填時間。用管節水準網、海床剖面及孔壓變化交叉核對，將整體下沉與相鄰節轉角分開評估。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Compare settlement, pore pressure and backfill timing by element identifier. Cross-check tube levelling, seabed profiles and pore-pressure change, separating overall settlement from rotation between neighbouring elements. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]},{"id":"b119-v14-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「差異沉陷梯度」的交付需回答：按管節編號對照沉陷、孔壓及回填時間。將基床施工紀錄與長期水準資料連結至管節編號，差異變形先查基準和孔壓，再由設計者判斷接觸及接頭。","textEn":"For Hong Kong–Zhuhai–Macao immersed tunnel, the differential settlement gradient handover must address the following evidence: Compare settlement, pore pressure and backfill timing by element identifier. Link bedding records and long-term levelling to element identifiers; check datum and pore pressure before designers interpret contact and joint behaviour.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「基床變形與接頭轉角」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Bedding movement and joint rotation\"?","options":["按管節編號對照沉陷、孔壓及回填時間。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Compare settlement, pore pressure and backfill timing by element identifier.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":0,"explanation":"按管節編號對照沉陷、孔壓及回填時間。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare settlement, pore pressure and backfill timing by element identifier. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b119-v14-16","title":"基床變形與接頭轉角：失效診斷","titleEn":"Bedding movement and joint rotation: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b119-v14-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「差異沉陷梯度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Differential settlement gradient” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只核總沉陷可能漏掉島隧轉換處的局部折角。只追蹤平均高程可能漏掉單側失去支承，接頭剪力與止水錯台會先於明顯整體下沉增加。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Total settlement alone misses local angular distortion at island transitions. Mean elevation can conceal loss of support on one side, allowing joint shear and gasket offset to grow before obvious overall settlement. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：總沉陷小不代表接頭轉角小；相鄰管節的差異位移和支承長度才控制局部變形，施工量測須保留時間與潮位基準。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Construction observations must preserve time and tidal datum because immediate placement and delayed consolidation describe different mechanisms.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「各管節平均高程接近就能排除接頭差異變形。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Similar mean element elevations exclude differential movement at joints.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b119-v14-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只核總沉陷可能漏掉島隧轉換處的局部折角。只追蹤平均高程可能漏掉單側失去支承，接頭剪力與止水錯台會先於明顯整體下沉增加。","textEn":"Total settlement alone misses local angular distortion at island transitions. Mean elevation can conceal loss of support on one side, allowing joint shear and gasket offset to grow before obvious overall settlement.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]},{"id":"b119-v14-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「基床變形與接頭轉角」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Bedding movement and joint rotation\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","只核總沉陷可能漏掉島隧轉換處的局部折角。","接縫平均寬度合格就不必量測局部錯台及扭轉。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Total settlement alone misses local angular distortion at island transitions.","An acceptable average joint width makes local offset and twist measurements unnecessary."],"answer":1,"explanation":"只核總沉陷可能漏掉島隧轉換處的局部折角。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Total settlement alone misses local angular distortion at island transitions. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b119-v14-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「接頭壓縮與水密包絡」與「控制網與貫通誤差」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Joint compression and sealing envelope\" and \"Control network and breakthrough error\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b119-v14-17","title":"接頭壓縮與水密包絡：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Joint compression and sealing envelope: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b119-v14-16"],"objective":"說明「止水壓縮餘量」如何影響港珠澳大橋海底隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Gasket compression reserve” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Hong Kong–Zhuhai–Macao immersed tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"長管列的接頭壓縮與閉合段幾何相互限制，教材分開局部水密包絡與全線累積誤差。止水條依受控壓縮維持連續接觸，接縫轉角、錯台、污染與材料鬆弛都會降低最不利點的接觸能力。平均壓縮量不能掩蓋局部脫離；全尺寸試驗的結果只對測試過的幾何、水壓及荷載歷程有效，幾何餘量本身並不是接觸壓力。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「止水壓縮餘量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Joint compression and closure geometry interact across the long element chain; separate local seal envelopes from accumulated alignment error. A gasket seals through controlled continuous compression; rotation, offset, contamination and relaxation reduce contact at the weakest point. Average compression cannot compensate for local separation. Full-size test results apply only to their tested geometry, head and load history, while a calculated geometric reserve is neither contact pressure nor evidence of watertightness. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Gasket compression reserve” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：初始壓縮=20 mm；張開量=3.8 mm；幾何公差=2 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: initial compression=20 mm; opening=3.8 mm; tolerance=2 mm. c_res=c0−opening−tolerance=14.2 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「接縫平均寬度合格就不必量測局部錯台及扭轉。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"An acceptable average joint width makes local offset and twist measurements unnecessary.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「止水壓縮餘量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Gasket compression reserve”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b119-v14-17-k1","title":"接頭壓縮與水密包絡","titleEn":"Joint compression and sealing envelope","text":"長管列的接頭壓縮與閉合段幾何相互限制，教材分開局部水密包絡與全線累積誤差。止水條依受控壓縮維持連續接觸，接縫轉角、錯台、污染與材料鬆弛都會降低最不利點的接觸能力。","textEn":"Joint compression and closure geometry interact across the long element chain; separate local seal envelopes from accumulated alignment error. A gasket seals through controlled continuous compression; rotation, offset, contamination and relaxation reduce contact at the weakest point.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]},{"id":"b119-v14-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：接縫平均寬度合格就不必量測局部錯台及扭轉。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: An acceptable average joint width makes local offset and twist measurements unnecessary. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「接頭壓縮與水密包絡」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Joint compression and sealing envelope\" is correct?","options":["接縫平均寬度合格就不必量測局部錯台及扭轉。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。","長管列的接頭壓縮與閉合段幾何相互限制，教材分開局部水密包絡與全線累積誤差。"],"optionsEn":["An acceptable average joint width makes local offset and twist measurements unnecessary.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.","Joint compression and closure geometry interact across the long element chain; separate local seal envelopes from accumulated alignment error."],"answer":2,"explanation":"長管列的接頭壓縮與閉合段幾何相互限制，教材分開局部水密包絡與全線累積誤差。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Joint compression and closure geometry interact across the long element chain; separate local seal envelopes from accumulated alignment error. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b119-v14-18","title":"接頭壓縮與水密包絡：定量估算","titleEn":"Joint compression and sealing envelope: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b119-v14-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「止水壓縮餘量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Gasket compression reserve” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：初始壓縮=20 mm；張開量=3.8 mm；幾何公差=2 mm。c_res=c0−opening−tolerance=14.2 mm。僅把張開量增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為13.82 mm。邊界：單向幾何餘量，不是接觸壓或水密合格證明；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: initial compression=20 mm; opening=3.8 mm; tolerance=2 mm. c_res=c0−opening−tolerance=14.2 mm. Increasing only opening by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 13.82 mm. Boundary: One-direction geometric reserve, not contact pressure or proof of watertightness. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：各接頭記錄張開、錯台與水壓，閉合段再核總幾何。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Record opening, offset and pressure at each joint and separately check closure geometry.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b119-v14-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：初始壓縮=20 mm；張開量=3.8 mm；幾何公差=2 mm。c_res=c0−opening−tolerance=14.2 mm。僅把張開量增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為13.82 mm。邊界：單向幾何餘量，不是接觸壓或水密合格證明；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: initial compression=20 mm; opening=3.8 mm; tolerance=2 mm. c_res=c0−opening−tolerance=14.2 mm. Increasing only opening by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 13.82 mm. Boundary: One-direction geometric reserve, not contact pressure or proof of watertightness. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]},{"id":"b119-v14-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「接頭壓縮與水密包絡」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Joint compression and sealing envelope\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：初始壓縮=20 mm；張開量=3.8 mm；幾何公差=2 mm。","擴散長度就是鋼筋開始腐蝕的位置和精確時間。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: initial compression=20 mm; opening=3.8 mm; tolerance=2 mm. c_res=c0−opening−tolerance=14.2 mm.","Diffusion length gives the exact location and time of corrosion initiation.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：初始壓縮=20 mm；張開量=3.8 mm；幾何公差=2 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: initial compression=20 mm; opening=3.8 mm; tolerance=2 mm. c_res=c0−opening−tolerance=14.2 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b119-v14-19","title":"接頭壓縮與水密包絡：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Joint compression and sealing envelope: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b119-v14-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「止水壓縮餘量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Gasket compression reserve” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"各接頭記錄張開、錯台與水壓，閉合段再核總幾何。全尺寸接頭試驗分別改變張開、錯台與外水壓，記錄漏水起點與卸載後殘餘位移，對照材料批次及溫度。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Record opening, offset and pressure at each joint and separately check closure geometry. Vary opening, offset and pressure in full-size joint tests, recording leakage onset and residual movement against material batch and temperature. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「止水壓縮餘量」的交付需回答：各接頭記錄張開、錯台與水壓，閉合段再核總幾何。保存接縫幾何與試驗壓力的配對紀錄，由設計者核定允收包絡；驗收時不能把課堂的幾何餘量當產品認證數字。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Hong Kong–Zhuhai–Macao immersed tunnel, the gasket compression reserve handover must address the following evidence: Record opening, offset and pressure at each joint and separately check closure geometry. Retain paired joint geometry and test pressure, with the designer approving the acceptance envelope; classroom geometric reserves are not product certification values.","failure":"注意干擾：全線貫通不證明每個接頭都在水密試驗包絡內。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Geometric closure does not prove every joint lies within the tested seal envelope. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b119-v14-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"各接頭記錄張開、錯台與水壓，閉合段再核總幾何。全尺寸接頭試驗分別改變張開、錯台與外水壓，記錄漏水起點與卸載後殘餘位移，對照材料批次及溫度。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Record opening, offset and pressure at each joint and separately check closure geometry. Vary opening, offset and pressure in full-size joint tests, recording leakage onset and residual movement against material batch and temperature. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]},{"id":"b119-v14-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「止水壓縮餘量」的交付需回答：各接頭記錄張開、錯台與水壓，閉合段再核總幾何。保存接縫幾何與試驗壓力的配對紀錄，由設計者核定允收包絡；驗收時不能把課堂的幾何餘量當產品認證數字。","textEn":"For Hong Kong–Zhuhai–Macao immersed tunnel, the gasket compression reserve handover must address the following evidence: Record opening, offset and pressure at each joint and separately check closure geometry. Retain paired joint geometry and test pressure, with the designer approving the acceptance envelope; classroom geometric reserves are not product certification values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「接頭壓縮與水密包絡」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Joint compression and sealing envelope\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","各接頭記錄張開、錯台與水壓，閉合段再核總幾何。","矩形沉管可以直接使用圓環均勻外壓公式設計。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Record opening, offset and pressure at each joint and separately check closure geometry.","A rectangular immersed tube can be designed directly with a circular-ring pressure formula."],"answer":1,"explanation":"各接頭記錄張開、錯台與水壓，閉合段再核總幾何。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Record opening, offset and pressure at each joint and separately check closure geometry. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b119-v14-20","title":"接頭壓縮與水密包絡：失效診斷","titleEn":"Joint compression and sealing envelope: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b119-v14-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「止水壓縮餘量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Gasket compression reserve” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"全線貫通不證明每個接頭都在水密試驗包絡內。扭曲或沾污的止水條可形成旁通通道，即使平均縫寬合格仍可能漏水；盲目灌漿也可能只轉移出水位置。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Geometric closure does not prove every joint lies within the tested seal envelope. A twisted or contaminated gasket creates bypass leakage despite acceptable mean width; indiscriminate grouting may merely move the outlet. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：平均壓縮量不能掩蓋局部脫離；全尺寸試驗的結果只對測試過的幾何、水壓及荷載歷程有效，幾何餘量本身並不是接觸壓力。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Full-size test results apply only to their tested geometry, head and load history, while a calculated geometric reserve is neither contact pressure nor evidence of watertightness.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「接縫平均寬度合格就不必量測局部錯台及扭轉。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"An acceptable average joint width makes local offset and twist measurements unnecessary.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b119-v14-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"全線貫通不證明每個接頭都在水密試驗包絡內。扭曲或沾污的止水條可形成旁通通道，即使平均縫寬合格仍可能漏水；盲目灌漿也可能只轉移出水位置。","textEn":"Geometric closure does not prove every joint lies within the tested seal envelope. A twisted or contaminated gasket creates bypass leakage despite acceptable mean width; indiscriminate grouting may merely move the outlet.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]},{"id":"b119-v14-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「接頭壓縮與水密包絡」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Joint compression and sealing envelope\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。","全線貫通不證明每個接頭都在水密試驗包絡內。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.","Geometric closure does not prove every joint lies within the tested seal envelope."],"answer":2,"explanation":"全線貫通不證明每個接頭都在水密試驗包絡內。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Geometric closure does not prove every joint lies within the tested seal envelope. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b119-v14-21","title":"控制網與貫通誤差：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b119-v14-20"],"objective":"說明「方向角誤差」如何影響港珠澳大橋海底隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Orientation error” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Hong Kong–Zhuhai–Macao immersed tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"海上沉放量測須處理潮位、姿態和控制網版本，教材研究偏差如何沿管列累積。長隧道的微小方向誤差會沿距離累積，地下控制網又缺少直接衛星定位，必須把地表基準可靠傳到洞內。閉合差很小不代表無系統誤差；尺度、折光、儀器定向與高程基準可能共同偏移，誤差相關性也使平方和估算失真。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「方向角誤差」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Immersion surveying must handle tide, attitude and control revisions; examine accumulated bias along the element chain. Small orientation errors accumulate over long drives, while underground networks lack direct satellite positioning and depend on transferring surface control. A small closure does not exclude systematic bias: scale, refraction, orientation and vertical datum may shift together. Correlated errors also invalidate a naive root-sum-square combination of supposedly independent observations. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Orientation error” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：控制長度=5160 m；方向偏角=2.5 arcsec。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: control length=5160 m; orientation error=2.5 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.062541 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「方向角誤差」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Orientation error”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b119-v14-21-k1","title":"控制網與貫通誤差","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error","text":"海上沉放量測須處理潮位、姿態和控制網版本，教材研究偏差如何沿管列累積。長隧道的微小方向誤差會沿距離累積，地下控制網又缺少直接衛星定位，必須把地表基準可靠傳到洞內。","textEn":"Immersion surveying must handle tide, attitude and control revisions; examine accumulated bias along the element chain. Small orientation errors accumulate over long drives, while underground networks lack direct satellite positioning and depend on transferring surface control.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]},{"id":"b119-v14-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「控制網與貫通誤差」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Control network and breakthrough error\" is correct?","options":["海上沉放量測須處理潮位、姿態和控制網版本，教材研究偏差如何沿管列累積。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。","混凝土抗壓強度合格就代表厚壁構件不會產生熱裂縫。"],"optionsEn":["Immersion surveying must handle tide, attitude and control revisions; examine accumulated bias along the element chain.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.","Adequate compressive strength proves that thick concrete cannot develop thermal cracks."],"answer":0,"explanation":"海上沉放量測須處理潮位、姿態和控制網版本，教材研究偏差如何沿管列累積。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Immersion surveying must handle tide, attitude and control revisions; examine accumulated bias along the element chain. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b119-v14-22","title":"控制網與貫通誤差：定量估算","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b119-v14-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「方向角誤差」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Orientation error” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：控制長度=5160 m；方向偏角=2.5 arcsec。e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.062541 m。僅把方向偏角增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.0687951 m。邊界：小角度方向偏差，未加入控制網相關性及折光；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: control length=5160 m; orientation error=2.5 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.062541 m. Increasing only orientation error by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.0687951 m. Boundary: Small-angle orientation error without network correlation or refraction. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以獨立岸基觀測覆核定位及落底後高程。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Independently check positioning and post-placement elevation from shore control.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b119-v14-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：控制長度=5160 m；方向偏角=2.5 arcsec。e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.062541 m。僅把方向偏角增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.0687951 m。邊界：小角度方向偏差，未加入控制網相關性及折光；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: control length=5160 m; orientation error=2.5 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.062541 m. Increasing only orientation error by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.0687951 m. Boundary: Small-angle orientation error without network correlation or refraction. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]},{"id":"b119-v14-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「控制網與貫通誤差」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Control network and breakthrough error\", which statement holds?","options":["風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。","原創教學假設：控制長度=5160 m；方向偏角=2.5 arcsec。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.","Original teaching assumptions: control length=5160 m; orientation error=2.5 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.062541 m.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：控制長度=5160 m；方向偏角=2.5 arcsec。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: control length=5160 m; orientation error=2.5 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.062541 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b119-v14-23","title":"控制網與貫通誤差：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b119-v14-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「方向角誤差」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Orientation error” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以獨立岸基觀測覆核定位及落底後高程。由獨立測量組複核地表到洞內的轉換，保留原始角距及溫度資料，用不同控制線比較方向與高程偏差。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Independently check positioning and post-placement elevation from shore control. Independently check surface-to-tunnel transformations, retain raw angles, distances and temperatures, and compare orientation and elevation through separate control routes. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「方向角誤差」的交付需回答：以獨立岸基觀測覆核定位及落底後高程。貫通前凍結座標、尺度與高程版本，獨立組直接使用原始觀測重算；不得只傳遞整理好的坐標而遺失校正資訊。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Hong Kong–Zhuhai–Macao immersed tunnel, the orientation error handover must address the following evidence: Independently check positioning and post-placement elevation from shore control. Freeze coordinate, scale and height revisions before breakthrough; independent reviewers recompute raw observations rather than receiving only adjusted coordinates without corrections.","failure":"注意干擾：多次觀測若共用錯誤潮位基準，不會自行消除高程偏差。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Repeated observations sharing a wrong tidal datum do not remove elevation bias. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b119-v14-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以獨立岸基觀測覆核定位及落底後高程。由獨立測量組複核地表到洞內的轉換，保留原始角距及溫度資料，用不同控制線比較方向與高程偏差。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Independently check positioning and post-placement elevation from shore control. Independently check surface-to-tunnel transformations, retain raw angles, distances and temperatures, and compare orientation and elevation through separate control routes. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]},{"id":"b119-v14-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「方向角誤差」的交付需回答：以獨立岸基觀測覆核定位及落底後高程。貫通前凍結座標、尺度與高程版本，獨立組直接使用原始觀測重算；不得只傳遞整理好的坐標而遺失校正資訊。","textEn":"For Hong Kong–Zhuhai–Macao immersed tunnel, the orientation error handover must address the following evidence: Independently check positioning and post-placement elevation from shore control. Freeze coordinate, scale and height revisions before breakthrough; independent reviewers recompute raw observations rather than receiving only adjusted coordinates without corrections.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「控制網與貫通誤差」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Control network and breakthrough error\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","剩餘浮力為正就代表浮運姿態在所有波況穩定。","以獨立岸基觀測覆核定位及落底後高程。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Positive residual buoyancy establishes stability in every sea state.","Independently check positioning and post-placement elevation from shore control."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以獨立岸基觀測覆核定位及落底後高程。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Independently check positioning and post-placement elevation from shore control. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b119-v14-24","title":"控制網與貫通誤差：失效診斷","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b119-v14-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「方向角誤差」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Orientation error” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"多次觀測若共用錯誤潮位基準，不會自行消除高程偏差。共用錯誤基準可能讓兩組測量同時看似一致，直到貫通或軌道銜接才發現系統偏差，修正成本遠高於早期複核。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Repeated observations sharing a wrong tidal datum do not remove elevation bias. A shared wrong datum can make separate surveys appear consistent until breakthrough or track connection exposes bias that is costly to correct. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：閉合差很小不代表無系統誤差；尺度、折光、儀器定向與高程基準可能共同偏移，誤差相關性也使平方和估算失真。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Correlated errors also invalidate a naive root-sum-square combination of supposedly independent observations.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b119-v14-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"多次觀測若共用錯誤潮位基準，不會自行消除高程偏差。共用錯誤基準可能讓兩組測量同時看似一致，直到貫通或軌道銜接才發現系統偏差，修正成本遠高於早期複核。","textEn":"Repeated observations sharing a wrong tidal datum do not remove elevation bias. A shared wrong datum can make separate surveys appear consistent until breakthrough or track connection exposes bias that is costly to correct.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]},{"id":"b119-v14-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「控制網與貫通誤差」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Control network and breakthrough error\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["多次觀測若共用錯誤潮位基準，不會自行消除高程偏差。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","混凝土抗壓強度合格就代表厚壁構件不會產生熱裂縫。"],"optionsEn":["Repeated observations sharing a wrong tidal datum do not remove elevation bias.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Adequate compressive strength proves that thick concrete cannot develop thermal cracks."],"answer":0,"explanation":"多次觀測若共用錯誤潮位基準，不會自行消除高程偏差。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Repeated observations sharing a wrong tidal datum do not remove elevation bias. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b119-v14-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「溫度拘束與構件裂縫」與「氯鹽遷移與耐久判讀」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Thermal restraint and component cracking\" and \"Chloride transport and durability interpretation\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b119-v14-25","title":"溫度拘束與構件裂縫：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Thermal restraint and component cracking: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b119-v14-24"],"objective":"說明「拘束溫度應變」如何影響港珠澳大橋海底隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Restrained thermal strain” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Hong Kong–Zhuhai–Macao immersed tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"大型預製箱體受早期水化熱與後續降溫，教材把熱應力量級和裂縫水密要求分開。厚壁構件在水化升溫後冷卻，若相鄰構件或基座限制收縮，熱應變會轉為拉應力。抗壓強度達標不等於抗裂合格，因為彈性模數成熟、徐變、溫度梯度與澆置順序都影響實際拘束；完全拘束彈性估算只能當量級上限比較。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「拘束溫度應變」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Large precast boxes experience hydration heat and later cooling; distinguish thermal-stress scale from crack-watertightness requirements. A thick element cools after hydration, and restraint from adjacent pours or its base converts contraction into tension. Compressive-strength compliance does not establish crack resistance because modulus development, creep, gradients and pour sequence influence restraint. A fully restrained elastic estimate is therefore a scale bound, not a prediction of actual cracking or residual stress. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Restrained thermal strain” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：線膨脹係數=1e-05 K⁻¹；溫差=28 K；彈性模數=25 GPa。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: expansion coefficient=1e-05 K⁻¹; temperature difference=28 K; elastic modulus=25 GPa. σ=EαΔT, GPa→MPa ×1000=7 MPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「混凝土抗壓強度合格就代表厚壁構件不會產生熱裂縫。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Adequate compressive strength proves that thick concrete cannot develop thermal cracks.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「拘束溫度應變」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Restrained thermal strain”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b119-v14-25-k1","title":"溫度拘束與構件裂縫","titleEn":"Thermal restraint and component cracking","text":"大型預製箱體受早期水化熱與後續降溫，教材把熱應力量級和裂縫水密要求分開。厚壁構件在水化升溫後冷卻，若相鄰構件或基座限制收縮，熱應變會轉為拉應力。","textEn":"Large precast boxes experience hydration heat and later cooling; distinguish thermal-stress scale from crack-watertightness requirements. A thick element cools after hydration, and restraint from adjacent pours or its base converts contraction into tension.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]},{"id":"b119-v14-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：混凝土抗壓強度合格就代表厚壁構件不會產生熱裂縫。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Adequate compressive strength proves that thick concrete cannot develop thermal cracks. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「溫度拘束與構件裂縫」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Thermal restraint and component cracking\" is correct?","options":["混凝土抗壓強度合格就代表厚壁構件不會產生熱裂縫。","大型預製箱體受早期水化熱與後續降溫，教材把熱應力量級和裂縫水密要求分開。","擴散長度就是鋼筋開始腐蝕的位置和精確時間。"],"optionsEn":["Adequate compressive strength proves that thick concrete cannot develop thermal cracks.","Large precast boxes experience hydration heat and later cooling; distinguish thermal-stress scale from crack-watertightness requirements.","Diffusion length gives the exact location and time of corrosion initiation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"大型預製箱體受早期水化熱與後續降溫，教材把熱應力量級和裂縫水密要求分開。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Large precast boxes experience hydration heat and later cooling; distinguish thermal-stress scale from crack-watertightness requirements. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b119-v14-26","title":"溫度拘束與構件裂縫：定量估算","titleEn":"Thermal restraint and component cracking: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b119-v14-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「拘束溫度應變」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Restrained thermal strain” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：線膨脹係數=1e-05 K⁻¹；溫差=28 K；彈性模數=25 GPa。σ=EαΔT, GPa→MPa ×1000=7 MPa。僅把溫差增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為7.7 MPa。邊界：完全拘束線彈性量級，未含徐變開裂和拘束鬆弛；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: expansion coefficient=1e-05 K⁻¹; temperature difference=28 K; elastic modulus=25 GPa. σ=EαΔT, GPa→MPa ×1000=7 MPa. Increasing only temperature difference by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 7.7 MPa. Boundary: Fully restrained linear-elastic scale without creep, cracking or restraint relaxation. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比較厚壁內外溫差及拘束位置的裂縫分布。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare through-wall gradients with cracking near restraints.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b119-v14-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：線膨脹係數=1e-05 K⁻¹；溫差=28 K；彈性模數=25 GPa。σ=EαΔT, GPa→MPa ×1000=7 MPa。僅把溫差增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為7.7 MPa。邊界：完全拘束線彈性量級，未含徐變開裂和拘束鬆弛；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: expansion coefficient=1e-05 K⁻¹; temperature difference=28 K; elastic modulus=25 GPa. σ=EαΔT, GPa→MPa ×1000=7 MPa. Increasing only temperature difference by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 7.7 MPa. Boundary: Fully restrained linear-elastic scale without creep, cracking or restraint relaxation. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]},{"id":"b119-v14-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「溫度拘束與構件裂縫」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Thermal restraint and component cracking\", which statement holds?","options":["全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。","矩形沉管可以直接使用圓環均勻外壓公式設計。","原創教學假設：線膨脹係數=1e-05 K⁻¹；溫差=28 K；彈性模數=25 GPa。"],"optionsEn":["Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.","A rectangular immersed tube can be designed directly with a circular-ring pressure formula.","Original teaching assumptions: expansion coefficient=1e-05 K⁻¹; temperature difference=28 K; elastic modulus=25 GPa. σ=EαΔT, GPa→MPa ×1000=7 MPa."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：線膨脹係數=1e-05 K⁻¹；溫差=28 K；彈性模數=25 GPa。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: expansion coefficient=1e-05 K⁻¹; temperature difference=28 K; elastic modulus=25 GPa. σ=EαΔT, GPa→MPa ×1000=7 MPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b119-v14-27","title":"溫度拘束與構件裂縫：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Thermal restraint and component cracking: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b119-v14-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「拘束溫度應變」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Restrained thermal strain” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比較厚壁內外溫差及拘束位置的裂縫分布。記錄核心表面溫度及同條件試體成熟度，將裂縫位置與溫差、拆模及鄰段澆置時間配對，檢查熱歷程是否被遺漏。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare through-wall gradients with cracking near restraints. Record core/surface temperature and matched-cured maturity, pairing cracks with temperature differences, formwork removal and adjacent pours to identify missing thermal history. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「拘束溫度應變」的交付需回答：比較厚壁內外溫差及拘束位置的裂縫分布。澆置前核准溫度監測及養護方案，變更材料、拆模或澆置順序時重新檢查熱分析，將裂縫與接縫止水的責任一併交付。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Hong Kong–Zhuhai–Macao immersed tunnel, the restrained thermal strain handover must address the following evidence: Compare through-wall gradients with cracking near restraints. Approve monitoring and curing before pours, revisit thermal analysis after material or sequence changes, and hand over crack and waterstop responsibilities together.","failure":"注意干擾：單一平均溫度無法代表厚壁熱梯度引起的局部應力。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: One average temperature does not represent local stress from thick-wall gradients. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b119-v14-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比較厚壁內外溫差及拘束位置的裂縫分布。記錄核心表面溫度及同條件試體成熟度，將裂縫位置與溫差、拆模及鄰段澆置時間配對，檢查熱歷程是否被遺漏。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Compare through-wall gradients with cracking near restraints. Record core/surface temperature and matched-cured maturity, pairing cracks with temperature differences, formwork removal and adjacent pours to identify missing thermal history. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]},{"id":"b119-v14-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「拘束溫度應變」的交付需回答：比較厚壁內外溫差及拘束位置的裂縫分布。澆置前核准溫度監測及養護方案，變更材料、拆模或澆置順序時重新檢查熱分析，將裂縫與接縫止水的責任一併交付。","textEn":"For Hong Kong–Zhuhai–Macao immersed tunnel, the restrained thermal strain handover must address the following evidence: Compare through-wall gradients with cracking near restraints. Approve monitoring and curing before pours, revisit thermal analysis after material or sequence changes, and hand over crack and waterstop responsibilities together.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「溫度拘束與構件裂縫」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Thermal restraint and component cracking\"?","options":["比較厚壁內外溫差及拘束位置的裂縫分布。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","各管節平均高程接近就能排除接頭差異變形。"],"optionsEn":["Compare through-wall gradients with cracking near restraints.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Similar mean element elevations exclude differential movement at joints."],"answer":0,"explanation":"比較厚壁內外溫差及拘束位置的裂縫分布。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare through-wall gradients with cracking near restraints. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b119-v14-28","title":"溫度拘束與構件裂縫：失效診斷","titleEn":"Thermal restraint and component cracking: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b119-v14-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「拘束溫度應變」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Restrained thermal strain” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"單一平均溫度無法代表厚壁熱梯度引起的局部應力。標準養護試體合格而現場過早冷卻，仍可能形成貫穿裂縫並影響止水；僅增加後續抗壓試驗無法重建失去的養護。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"One average temperature does not represent local stress from thick-wall gradients. Passing standard-cured specimens does not prevent through-cracking after rapid cooling, and more later strength tests cannot reconstruct inadequate curing. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：抗壓強度達標不等於抗裂合格，因為彈性模數成熟、徐變、溫度梯度與澆置順序都影響實際拘束；完全拘束彈性估算只能當量級上限比較。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A fully restrained elastic estimate is therefore a scale bound, not a prediction of actual cracking or residual stress.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「混凝土抗壓強度合格就代表厚壁構件不會產生熱裂縫。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Adequate compressive strength proves that thick concrete cannot develop thermal cracks.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b119-v14-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"單一平均溫度無法代表厚壁熱梯度引起的局部應力。標準養護試體合格而現場過早冷卻，仍可能形成貫穿裂縫並影響止水；僅增加後續抗壓試驗無法重建失去的養護。","textEn":"One average temperature does not represent local stress from thick-wall gradients. Passing standard-cured specimens does not prevent through-cracking after rapid cooling, and more later strength tests cannot reconstruct inadequate curing.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]},{"id":"b119-v14-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「溫度拘束與構件裂縫」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Thermal restraint and component cracking\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","單一平均溫度無法代表厚壁熱梯度引起的局部應力。","擴散長度就是鋼筋開始腐蝕的位置和精確時間。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","One average temperature does not represent local stress from thick-wall gradients.","Diffusion length gives the exact location and time of corrosion initiation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"單一平均溫度無法代表厚壁熱梯度引起的局部應力。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"One average temperature does not represent local stress from thick-wall gradients. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b119-v14-29","title":"氯鹽遷移與耐久判讀：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Chloride transport and durability interpretation: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b119-v14-28"],"objective":"說明「擴散特徵長度」如何影響港珠澳大橋海底隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Diffusion characteristic length” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Hong Kong–Zhuhai–Macao immersed tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"外海鹽水環境下箱體表面與接頭傳輸不同，教材將擴散特徵長度和鋼筋腐蝕啟動分開。海水或除冰鹽可提供氯離子，材料孔隙與裂縫控制其傳輸；鋼筋腐蝕還需要局部電化學條件。平方根擴散長度僅顯示時間尺度，並不是腐蝕門檻深度；表面濃度變化、乾濕循環、結合效應及施工裂縫須另行辨識。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「擴散特徵長度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Box surfaces and joints transport chloride differently; distinguish characteristic diffusion length from reinforcement corrosion initiation. Seawater or deicing salt supplies chloride, while pores and cracks govern transport; reinforcement corrosion also depends on local electrochemical conditions. A square-root diffusion length indicates a time scale, not a corrosion-threshold depth. Surface concentration, wetting cycles, binding and construction cracks must be distinguished rather than hidden in one fitted diffusivity. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Diffusion characteristic length” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：擴散係數=3e-12 m²/s；暴露時間=17 year。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: diffusivity=3e-12 m²/s; exposure=17 year. ℓ=√(Dt); 1 year=365.25×86400 s; m→mm ×1000=40.1178 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「擴散長度就是鋼筋開始腐蝕的位置和精確時間。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Diffusion length gives the exact location and time of corrosion initiation.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「擴散特徵長度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Diffusion characteristic length”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b119-v14-29-k1","title":"氯鹽遷移與耐久判讀","titleEn":"Chloride transport and durability interpretation","text":"外海鹽水環境下箱體表面與接頭傳輸不同，教材將擴散特徵長度和鋼筋腐蝕啟動分開。海水或除冰鹽可提供氯離子，材料孔隙與裂縫控制其傳輸；鋼筋腐蝕還需要局部電化學條件。","textEn":"Box surfaces and joints transport chloride differently; distinguish characteristic diffusion length from reinforcement corrosion initiation. Seawater or deicing salt supplies chloride, while pores and cracks govern transport; reinforcement corrosion also depends on local electrochemical conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]},{"id":"b119-v14-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：擴散長度就是鋼筋開始腐蝕的位置和精確時間。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Diffusion length gives the exact location and time of corrosion initiation. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「氯鹽遷移與耐久判讀」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Chloride transport and durability interpretation\" is correct?","options":["擴散長度就是鋼筋開始腐蝕的位置和精確時間。","風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。","外海鹽水環境下箱體表面與接頭傳輸不同，教材將擴散特徵長度和鋼筋腐蝕啟動分開。"],"optionsEn":["Diffusion length gives the exact location and time of corrosion initiation.","Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.","Box surfaces and joints transport chloride differently; distinguish characteristic diffusion length from reinforcement corrosion initiation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"外海鹽水環境下箱體表面與接頭傳輸不同，教材將擴散特徵長度和鋼筋腐蝕啟動分開。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Box surfaces and joints transport chloride differently; distinguish characteristic diffusion length from reinforcement corrosion initiation. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b119-v14-30","title":"氯鹽遷移與耐久判讀：定量估算","titleEn":"Chloride transport and durability interpretation: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b119-v14-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「擴散特徵長度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Diffusion characteristic length” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：擴散係數=3e-12 m²/s；暴露時間=17 year。ℓ=√(Dt); 1 year=365.25×86400 s; m→mm ×1000=40.1178 mm。僅把暴露時間增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為42.0759 mm。邊界：特徵長度，不是腐蝕起始壽命或氯鹽門檻深度；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: diffusivity=3e-12 m²/s; exposure=17 year. ℓ=√(Dt); 1 year=365.25×86400 s; m→mm ×1000=40.1178 mm. Increasing only exposure by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 42.0759 mm. Boundary: Characteristic length, not corrosion-initiation life or chloride-threshold depth. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：按裂縫與未裂區分層取樣，不把接縫水當材料係數。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Sample cracked and uncracked zones separately rather than fitting joint water into a material coefficient.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b119-v14-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：擴散係數=3e-12 m²/s；暴露時間=17 year。ℓ=√(Dt); 1 year=365.25×86400 s; m→mm ×1000=40.1178 mm。僅把暴露時間增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為42.0759 mm。邊界：特徵長度，不是腐蝕起始壽命或氯鹽門檻深度；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: diffusivity=3e-12 m²/s; exposure=17 year. ℓ=√(Dt); 1 year=365.25×86400 s; m→mm ×1000=40.1178 mm. Increasing only exposure by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 42.0759 mm. Boundary: Characteristic length, not corrosion-initiation life or chloride-threshold depth. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]},{"id":"b119-v14-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「氯鹽遷移與耐久判讀」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Chloride transport and durability interpretation\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：擴散係數=3e-12 m²/s；暴露時間=17 year。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。","剩餘浮力為正就代表浮運姿態在所有波況穩定。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: diffusivity=3e-12 m²/s; exposure=17 year. ℓ=√(Dt); 1 year=365.25×86400 s; m→mm ×1000=40.1178 mm.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.","Positive residual buoyancy establishes stability in every sea state."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：擴散係數=3e-12 m²/s；暴露時間=17 year。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: diffusivity=3e-12 m²/s; exposure=17 year. ℓ=√(Dt); 1 year=365.25×86400 s; m→mm ×1000=40.1178 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b119-v14-31","title":"氯鹽遷移與耐久判讀：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Chloride transport and durability interpretation: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b119-v14-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「擴散特徵長度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Diffusion characteristic length” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"按裂縫與未裂區分層取樣，不把接縫水當材料係數。以分層取樣的氯鹽剖面配合裂縫圖與電位量測，檢查擴散模型是否只適用未開裂材料。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Sample cracked and uncracked zones separately rather than fitting joint water into a material coefficient. Combine depth-resolved chloride samples with crack maps and potential measurements, checking whether the diffusion model applies only to uncracked material. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「擴散特徵長度」的交付需回答：按裂縫與未裂區分層取樣，不把接縫水當材料係數。保留取樣深度、含水狀態及材料批次，用多種證據解釋劣化；維修優先序依構件功能與實際病害制定。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Hong Kong–Zhuhai–Macao immersed tunnel, the diffusion characteristic length handover must address the following evidence: Sample cracked and uncracked zones separately rather than fitting joint water into a material coefficient. Retain sample depth, moisture and material batches and interpret deterioration using multiple evidence types; prioritise repairs by function and observed defects.","failure":"注意干擾：高滲透接頭可能控制局部病害，平均擴散值會掩蓋它。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A permeable joint can govern local deterioration concealed by mean diffusivity. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b119-v14-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"按裂縫與未裂區分層取樣，不把接縫水當材料係數。以分層取樣的氯鹽剖面配合裂縫圖與電位量測，檢查擴散模型是否只適用未開裂材料。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Sample cracked and uncracked zones separately rather than fitting joint water into a material coefficient. Combine depth-resolved chloride samples with crack maps and potential measurements, checking whether the diffusion model applies only to uncracked material. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]},{"id":"b119-v14-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「擴散特徵長度」的交付需回答：按裂縫與未裂區分層取樣，不把接縫水當材料係數。保留取樣深度、含水狀態及材料批次，用多種證據解釋劣化；維修優先序依構件功能與實際病害制定。","textEn":"For Hong Kong–Zhuhai–Macao immersed tunnel, the diffusion characteristic length handover must address the following evidence: Sample cracked and uncracked zones separately rather than fitting joint water into a material coefficient. Retain sample depth, moisture and material batches and interpret deterioration using multiple evidence types; prioritise repairs by function and observed defects.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「氯鹽遷移與耐久判讀」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Chloride transport and durability interpretation\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","按裂縫與未裂區分層取樣，不把接縫水當材料係數。","接縫平均寬度合格就不必量測局部錯台及扭轉。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Sample cracked and uncracked zones separately rather than fitting joint water into a material coefficient.","An acceptable average joint width makes local offset and twist measurements unnecessary."],"answer":1,"explanation":"按裂縫與未裂區分層取樣，不把接縫水當材料係數。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Sample cracked and uncracked zones separately rather than fitting joint water into a material coefficient. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b119-v14-32","title":"氯鹽遷移與耐久判讀：失效診斷","titleEn":"Chloride transport and durability interpretation: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b119-v14-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「擴散特徵長度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Diffusion characteristic length” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"高滲透接頭可能控制局部病害，平均擴散值會掩蓋它。把一次電位讀值當腐蝕速率會誤判剩餘壽命，裂縫快速傳輸也可能被平均材料係數掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A permeable joint can govern local deterioration concealed by mean diffusivity. Treating one potential reading as corrosion rate misjudges remaining life, while averaged material coefficients conceal rapid crack transport. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：平方根擴散長度僅顯示時間尺度，並不是腐蝕門檻深度；表面濃度變化、乾濕循環、結合效應及施工裂縫須另行辨識。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Surface concentration, wetting cycles, binding and construction cracks must be distinguished rather than hidden in one fitted diffusivity.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「擴散長度就是鋼筋開始腐蝕的位置和精確時間。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Diffusion length gives the exact location and time of corrosion initiation.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b119-v14-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"高滲透接頭可能控制局部病害，平均擴散值會掩蓋它。把一次電位讀值當腐蝕速率會誤判剩餘壽命，裂縫快速傳輸也可能被平均材料係數掩蓋。","textEn":"A permeable joint can govern local deterioration concealed by mean diffusivity. Treating one potential reading as corrosion rate misjudges remaining life, while averaged material coefficients conceal rapid crack transport.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]},{"id":"b119-v14-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「氯鹽遷移與耐久判讀」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Chloride transport and durability interpretation\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。","高滲透接頭可能控制局部病害，平均擴散值會掩蓋它。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.","A permeable joint can govern local deterioration concealed by mean diffusivity."],"answer":2,"explanation":"高滲透接頭可能控制局部病害，平均擴散值會掩蓋它。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A permeable joint can govern local deterioration concealed by mean diffusivity. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b119-v14-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「通風網路與壓力損失」與「資產編碼與可追溯交接」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Ventilation network and pressure loss\" and \"Asset identity and traceable handover\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b119-v14-33","title":"通風網路與壓力損失：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Ventilation network and pressure loss: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b119-v14-32"],"objective":"說明「風道摩擦壓損」如何影響港珠澳大橋海底隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Duct friction loss” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Hong Kong–Zhuhai–Macao immersed tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"隧道與人工島通風設施互為邊界，教材研究島上外風與孔內車流對工況點的聯合作用。風機提供壓差，實際風量由風道摩阻、局部損失、外風與其他風機共同決定。支路開關會重新分配整個網路，不能把額定風量直接加總；正常污染稀釋與火災控煙也有不同目標，需要分別建立受控邊界和故障情境。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「風道摩擦壓損」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Island ventilation facilities and the tunnel share boundaries; examine external wind and traffic effects on operating points. Fans supply pressure, but actual flow follows friction, local losses, external wind and interactions with other fans. Switching a branch redistributes the network rather than simply adding rated flows. Routine dilution and fire smoke control have different objectives, so each needs explicit boundaries, operating states and failure cases rather than one universal flow target. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Duct friction loss” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：達西因子=0.025 無因次；風道長度=1220 m；水力直徑=4 m；空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；平均風速=3.8 m/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.025 dimensionless; duct length=1220 m; hydraulic diameter=4 m; air density=1.2 kg/m³; mean velocity=3.8 m/s. Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=66.063 Pa.","failure":"常見誤解：「風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「風道摩擦壓損」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Duct friction loss”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b119-v14-33-k1","title":"通風網路與壓力損失","titleEn":"Ventilation network and pressure loss","text":"隧道與人工島通風設施互為邊界，教材研究島上外風與孔內車流對工況點的聯合作用。風機提供壓差，實際風量由風道摩阻、局部損失、外風與其他風機共同決定。","textEn":"Island ventilation facilities and the tunnel share boundaries; examine external wind and traffic effects on operating points. Fans supply pressure, but actual flow follows friction, local losses, external wind and interactions with other fans.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]},{"id":"b119-v14-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「通風網路與壓力損失」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Ventilation network and pressure loss\" is correct?","options":["隧道與人工島通風設施互為邊界，教材研究島上外風與孔內車流對工況點的聯合作用。","風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。"],"optionsEn":["Island ventilation facilities and the tunnel share boundaries; examine external wind and traffic effects on operating points.","Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted."],"answer":0,"explanation":"隧道與人工島通風設施互為邊界，教材研究島上外風與孔內車流對工況點的聯合作用。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Island ventilation facilities and the tunnel share boundaries; examine external wind and traffic effects on operating points. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b119-v14-34","title":"通風網路與壓力損失：定量估算","titleEn":"Ventilation network and pressure loss: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b119-v14-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「風道摩擦壓損」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Duct friction loss” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：達西因子=0.025 無因次；風道長度=1220 m；水力直徑=4 m；空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；平均風速=3.8 m/s。Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=66.063 Pa。僅把平均風速增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為79.9362 Pa。邊界：定密度直管摩阻，局部損失及外風另計；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.025 dimensionless; duct length=1220 m; hydraulic diameter=4 m; air density=1.2 kg/m³; mean velocity=3.8 m/s. Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=66.063 Pa. Increasing only mean velocity by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 79.9362 Pa. Boundary: Constant-density straight-duct friction; local loss and external wind are separate. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同步量測外風、風機狀態、風道壓差及道路風速。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Synchronise wind, fan state, duct pressure and roadway velocity.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b119-v14-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：達西因子=0.025 無因次；風道長度=1220 m；水力直徑=4 m；空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；平均風速=3.8 m/s。Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=66.063 Pa。僅把平均風速增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為79.9362 Pa。邊界：定密度直管摩阻，局部損失及外風另計；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.025 dimensionless; duct length=1220 m; hydraulic diameter=4 m; air density=1.2 kg/m³; mean velocity=3.8 m/s. Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=66.063 Pa. Increasing only mean velocity by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 79.9362 Pa. Boundary: Constant-density straight-duct friction; local loss and external wind are separate. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]},{"id":"b119-v14-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「通風網路與壓力損失」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Ventilation network and pressure loss\", which statement holds?","options":["矩形沉管可以直接使用圓環均勻外壓公式設計。","原創教學假設：達西因子=0.025 無因次；風道長度=1220 m；水力直徑=4 m；空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；平均風速=3.8 m/s。","各管節平均高程接近就能排除接頭差異變形。"],"optionsEn":["A rectangular immersed tube can be designed directly with a circular-ring pressure formula.","Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.025 dimensionless.","Similar mean element elevations exclude differential movement at joints."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：達西因子=0.025 無因次；風道長度=1220 m；水力直徑=4 m；空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；平均風速=3.8 m/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.025 dimensionless; duct length=1220 m; hydraulic diameter=4 m; air density=1.2 kg/m³; mean velocity=3.8 m/s. Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=66.063 Pa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b119-v14-35","title":"通風網路與壓力損失：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Ventilation network and pressure loss: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b119-v14-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「風道摩擦壓損」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Duct friction loss” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同步量測外風、風機狀態、風道壓差及道路風速。沿線同步量測靜壓與風速，記錄風門及其他風機狀態，再把實測工作點和風機曲線、網路壓損比較。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Synchronise wind, fan state, duct pressure and roadway velocity. Measure pressure and velocity synchronously, record dampers and other fans, and compare the measured duty point with fan curves and network resistance. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「風道摩擦壓損」的交付需回答：同步量測外風、風機狀態、風道壓差及道路風速。驗收採明確風門和車流邊界，維修改線後重新核對網路工作點，火災模式由防災責任工程師簽認而非沿用正常模式。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Hong Kong–Zhuhai–Macao immersed tunnel, the duct friction loss handover must address the following evidence: Synchronise wind, fan state, duct pressure and roadway velocity. Commission with specified damper and traffic boundaries, recheck duty points after rerouting, and have the fire-safety engineer approve emergency modes independently.","failure":"注意干擾：額定風量不含島上風壓變化，不能直接代表實際換氣。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Rated flow excludes varying island wind pressure and is not actual ventilation. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b119-v14-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同步量測外風、風機狀態、風道壓差及道路風速。沿線同步量測靜壓與風速，記錄風門及其他風機狀態，再把實測工作點和風機曲線、網路壓損比較。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Synchronise wind, fan state, duct pressure and roadway velocity. Measure pressure and velocity synchronously, record dampers and other fans, and compare the measured duty point with fan curves and network resistance. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]},{"id":"b119-v14-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「風道摩擦壓損」的交付需回答：同步量測外風、風機狀態、風道壓差及道路風速。驗收採明確風門和車流邊界，維修改線後重新核對網路工作點，火災模式由防災責任工程師簽認而非沿用正常模式。","textEn":"For Hong Kong–Zhuhai–Macao immersed tunnel, the duct friction loss handover must address the following evidence: Synchronise wind, fan state, duct pressure and roadway velocity. Commission with specified damper and traffic boundaries, recheck duty points after rerouting, and have the fire-safety engineer approve emergency modes independently.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「通風網路與壓力損失」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Ventilation network and pressure loss\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。","同步量測外風、風機狀態、風道壓差及道路風速。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.","Synchronise wind, fan state, duct pressure and roadway velocity."],"answer":2,"explanation":"同步量測外風、風機狀態、風道壓差及道路風速。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Synchronise wind, fan state, duct pressure and roadway velocity. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b119-v14-36","title":"通風網路與壓力損失：失效診斷","titleEn":"Ventilation network and pressure loss: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b119-v14-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「風道摩擦壓損」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Duct friction loss” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"額定風量不含島上風壓變化，不能直接代表實際換氣。只看風機轉速會漏掉風門誤位或短路漏風，可能在總耗電增加時，真正需要的區段反而風量不足。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Rated flow excludes varying island wind pressure and is not actual ventilation. Fan speed alone misses a misplaced damper or leakage shortcut; total power may rise while the critical section receives less air. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：支路開關會重新分配整個網路，不能把額定風量直接加總；正常污染稀釋與火災控煙也有不同目標，需要分別建立受控邊界和故障情境。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Routine dilution and fire smoke control have different objectives, so each needs explicit boundaries, operating states and failure cases rather than one universal flow target.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b119-v14-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"額定風量不含島上風壓變化，不能直接代表實際換氣。只看風機轉速會漏掉風門誤位或短路漏風，可能在總耗電增加時，真正需要的區段反而風量不足。","textEn":"Rated flow excludes varying island wind pressure and is not actual ventilation. Fan speed alone misses a misplaced damper or leakage shortcut; total power may rise while the critical section receives less air.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]},{"id":"b119-v14-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「通風網路與壓力損失」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Ventilation network and pressure loss\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["額定風量不含島上風壓變化，不能直接代表實際換氣。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。"],"optionsEn":["Rated flow excludes varying island wind pressure and is not actual ventilation.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted."],"answer":0,"explanation":"額定風量不含島上風壓變化，不能直接代表實際換氣。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Rated flow excludes varying island wind pressure and is not actual ventilation. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b119-v14-37","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b119-v14-36"],"objective":"說明「資產資料完整度」如何影響港珠澳大橋海底隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Asset-record completeness” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Hong Kong–Zhuhai–Macao immersed tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"管節量產與多區施工的資料須對應最終安裝位置，教材檢查材料批次、接頭和檢修點的關聯。地下設備的竣工資料必須讓維護人員找到正確位置、材料批次和控制版本。只有上傳圖面而沒有變更歷程，無法分辨元件替換與真正劣化；告警、儀器、線路及工單使用一致識別碼，才可能把量測趨勢連回實際受力或水力系統。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「資產資料完整度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Production and multiple work zones need records tied to final installation, linking batches, joints and inspection points. Handover must let maintainers find the correct location, material batch and control revision. Drawings without change history cannot distinguish replacement from deterioration. Consistent identifiers across alarms, instruments, circuits and work orders are essential for linking trends to the physical structural or hydraulic system instead of treating each record as an isolated file. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Asset-record completeness” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：設備總數=118 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: asset count=118 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=86.4407 %.","failure":"常見誤解：「全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「資產資料完整度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Asset-record completeness”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b119-v14-37-k1","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover","text":"管節量產與多區施工的資料須對應最終安裝位置，教材檢查材料批次、接頭和檢修點的關聯。地下設備的竣工資料必須讓維護人員找到正確位置、材料批次和控制版本。","textEn":"Production and multiple work zones need records tied to final installation, linking batches, joints and inspection points. Handover must let maintainers find the correct location, material batch and control revision.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]},{"id":"b119-v14-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「資產編碼與可追溯交接」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Asset identity and traceable handover\" is correct?","options":["全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。","管節量產與多區施工的資料須對應最終安裝位置，教材檢查材料批次、接頭和檢修點的關聯。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.","Production and multiple work zones need records tied to final installation, linking batches, joints and inspection points.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":1,"explanation":"管節量產與多區施工的資料須對應最終安裝位置，教材檢查材料批次、接頭和檢修點的關聯。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Production and multiple work zones need records tied to final installation, linking batches, joints and inspection points. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b119-v14-38","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：定量估算","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b119-v14-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「資產資料完整度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Asset-record completeness” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：設備總數=118 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。coverage=100(N−missing)/N=86.4407 %。僅把缺紀錄數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為85.0847 %。邊界：資料完整度，不等於安全或可靠度；擾動為連續敏感度，實際個數為整數；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: asset count=118 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=86.4407 %. Increasing only missing records by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 85.0847 %. Boundary: Record completeness, not safety or reliability; perturbation is continuous sensitivity while actual counts are integers. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：由一個漏點反查管節編號、試驗和接頭施工紀錄。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Trace one leak to element identity, tests and joint-construction records.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b119-v14-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：設備總數=118 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。coverage=100(N−missing)/N=86.4407 %。僅把缺紀錄數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為85.0847 %。邊界：資料完整度，不等於安全或可靠度；擾動為連續敏感度，實際個數為整數；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: asset count=118 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=86.4407 %. Increasing only missing records by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 85.0847 %. Boundary: Record completeness, not safety or reliability; perturbation is continuous sensitivity while actual counts are integers. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]},{"id":"b119-v14-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「資產編碼與可追溯交接」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Asset identity and traceable handover\", which statement holds?","options":["剩餘浮力為正就代表浮運姿態在所有波況穩定。","接縫平均寬度合格就不必量測局部錯台及扭轉。","原創教學假設：設備總數=118 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。"],"optionsEn":["Positive residual buoyancy establishes stability in every sea state.","An acceptable average joint width makes local offset and twist measurements unnecessary.","Original teaching assumptions: asset count=118 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=86.4407 %."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：設備總數=118 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: asset count=118 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=86.4407 %. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b119-v14-39","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b119-v14-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「資產資料完整度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Asset-record completeness” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"由一個漏點反查管節編號、試驗和接頭施工紀錄。抽取一條告警，從控制畫面追到設備、線路、圖面和工單，核對位置、版本及校正日期並記錄無法閉合的欄位。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Trace one leak to element identity, tests and joint-construction records. Trace a sampled alarm from screen to equipment, circuit, drawing and work order, checking location, revision and calibration dates and recording broken links. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「資產資料完整度」的交付需回答：由一個漏點反查管節編號、試驗和接頭施工紀錄。交接以可完成的定位、查找與復原任務驗證，由維護責任人確認現場可用性；完整度只是資料指標，不代表結構安全或設備可靠。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Hong Kong–Zhuhai–Macao immersed tunnel, the asset-record completeness handover must address the following evidence: Trace one leak to element identity, tests and joint-construction records. Validate handover through achievable location, retrieval and recovery tasks witnessed by maintainers; completeness measures records, not structural safety or equipment reliability.","failure":"注意干擾：編號沿用工廠順序而未改安裝序會錯配維修證據。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Keeping factory order instead of installed order mislinks repair evidence. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b119-v14-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"由一個漏點反查管節編號、試驗和接頭施工紀錄。抽取一條告警，從控制畫面追到設備、線路、圖面和工單，核對位置、版本及校正日期並記錄無法閉合的欄位。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Trace one leak to element identity, tests and joint-construction records. Trace a sampled alarm from screen to equipment, circuit, drawing and work order, checking location, revision and calibration dates and recording broken links. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]},{"id":"b119-v14-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「資產資料完整度」的交付需回答：由一個漏點反查管節編號、試驗和接頭施工紀錄。交接以可完成的定位、查找與復原任務驗證，由維護責任人確認現場可用性；完整度只是資料指標，不代表結構安全或設備可靠。","textEn":"For Hong Kong–Zhuhai–Macao immersed tunnel, the asset-record completeness handover must address the following evidence: Trace one leak to element identity, tests and joint-construction records. Validate handover through achievable location, retrieval and recovery tasks witnessed by maintainers; completeness measures records, not structural safety or equipment reliability.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「資產編碼與可追溯交接」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Asset identity and traceable handover\"?","options":["由一個漏點反查管節編號、試驗和接頭施工紀錄。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","混凝土抗壓強度合格就代表厚壁構件不會產生熱裂縫。"],"optionsEn":["Trace one leak to element identity, tests and joint-construction records.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Adequate compressive strength proves that thick concrete cannot develop thermal cracks."],"answer":0,"explanation":"由一個漏點反查管節編號、試驗和接頭施工紀錄。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Trace one leak to element identity, tests and joint-construction records. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b119-v14-40","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：失效診斷","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b119-v14-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「資產資料完整度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Asset-record completeness” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"編號沿用工廠順序而未改安裝序會錯配維修證據。設備改名卻未更新控制畫面會引導人員隔離錯誤回路，材料批次缺漏則使同批缺陷無法追蹤到其他位置。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Keeping factory order instead of installed order mislinks repair evidence. Renaming an asset without updating the screen can isolate the wrong circuit; missing material batches prevent tracing related defects at other locations. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：只有上傳圖面而沒有變更歷程，無法分辨元件替換與真正劣化；告警、儀器、線路及工單使用一致識別碼，才可能把量測趨勢連回實際受力或水力系統。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Consistent identifiers across alarms, instruments, circuits and work orders are essential for linking trends to the physical structural or hydraulic system instead of treating each record as an isolated file.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b119-v14-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"編號沿用工廠順序而未改安裝序會錯配維修證據。設備改名卻未更新控制畫面會引導人員隔離錯誤回路，材料批次缺漏則使同批缺陷無法追蹤到其他位置。","textEn":"Keeping factory order instead of installed order mislinks repair evidence. Renaming an asset without updating the screen can isolate the wrong circuit; missing material batches prevent tracing related defects at other locations.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]},{"id":"b119-v14-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「資產編碼與可追溯交接」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Asset identity and traceable handover\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","編號沿用工廠順序而未改安裝序會錯配維修證據。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Keeping factory order instead of installed order mislinks repair evidence.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":1,"explanation":"編號沿用工廠順序而未改安裝序會錯配維修證據。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Keeping factory order instead of installed order mislinks repair evidence. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b119","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc","v14s-landmark-b119-history"],"curriculumVersion":14,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000},{"id":"b120","title":"獅子洋隧道","titleEn":"Shiziyang Tunnel","category":"underground","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"國家鐵路局公開技術資料列獅子洋隧道10.8公里、雙孔單線，並記錄2011年12月通車及軟土、土岩複合與岩層的變化。本課從地層切換到結構和軌道平順性，串接長距離盾構、接合測量、列車氣動及救援；公開設計數字與本課假想模型分開呈現。","summaryEn":"The National Railway Administration records Shiziyang as 10.8 km with twin single-track bores, opening in December 2011 through soft soil, mixed and rock strata. This course links ground transitions to structural and track geometry, long shield drives, connection surveys, train aerodynamics and rescue, keeping published design context separate from teaching calculations.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"ug-landmarks","subcategoryTitle":"世界隧道與地下巨作","subcategoryTitleEn":"World tunnels and underground landmarks","learningTrack":"underground","learningSubdiscipline":"ug-landmarks","learningTags":["underground","ug-landmarks","tunnel"],"architectureFamily":"tunnel","architectureNodes":[["路線里程與端點","Alignment chainage and endpoints"],["破碎帶連通性","Fault-zone connectivity"],["有效掘進利用率","Effective boring utilisation"],["襯砌環向壓縮","Lining hoop compression"],["入口壓力擾動","Portal pressure disturbance"],["資產資料完整度","Asset-record completeness"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,5],[1,5]],"diagram":{"type":"tunnel","labels":["路線里程與端點","破碎帶連通性","有效掘進利用率","襯砌環向壓縮","入口壓力擾動"],"labelsEn":["Alignment chainage and endpoints","Fault-zone connectivity","Effective boring utilisation","Lining hoop compression","Portal pressure disturbance"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"原創綜合審查：先計算「破碎帶連通與預報更新」，再獨立計算「環向受力與接縫柔度」。原創教學假設：滲透係數=5e-06 m/s；水力坡降=2.1 無因次；通水面積=390 m²。Q=k i A=0.004095 m³/s。僅把滲透係數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.0045045 m³/s。邊界：均質飽和達西流，不代表裂隙集中流；不是本工程實測或允收值。原創教學假設：均勻外壓=0.68 MPa；半徑=3.5 m；厚度=0.35 m。σθ=pr/t=6.8 MPa。僅把均勻外壓增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為7.48 MPa。邊界：薄圓環膜應力，不是接縫、偏壓或矩形框架解；不是本工程實測或允收值。兩組結果的單位與邊界不同，不能直接相加。請列出一項缺少的現場輸入，說明它會影響哪個結論，以及哪種獨立量測可以縮小不確定度。","textEn":"Original integrated review: first calculate fault connectivity and forecast updating, then independently calculate ring force and joint flexibility. Original teaching assumptions: conductivity=5e-06 m/s; hydraulic gradient=2.1 dimensionless; flow area=390 m². Q=k i A=0.004095 m³/s. Increasing only conductivity by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.0045045 m³/s. Boundary: Homogeneous saturated Darcy flow, not concentrated fracture flow. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Original teaching assumptions: uniform external pressure=0.68 MPa; radius=3.5 m; thickness=0.35 m. σθ=pr/t=6.8 MPa. Increasing only uniform external pressure by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 7.48 MPa. Boundary: Thin circular-ring membrane stress, not a joint, uneven-load or rectangular-frame solution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. The outputs have different units and boundaries and cannot simply be added. Identify one missing field input, explain which conclusion it changes and select an independent measurement to reduce uncertainty.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":14,"enrichmentVersion":14,"stages":[{"id":"b120-v14-s1","title":"地層條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Ground conditions, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「服務邊界與路線代價」與「破碎帶連通與預報更新」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\" and \"Fault connectivity and forecast updating\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b120-v14-01","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「路線里程與端點」如何影響獅子洋隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Alignment chainage and endpoints” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Shiziyang Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"獅子洋總隧道與盾構段的範圍不同，教材先確認雙孔單線的計量方式，不把兩孔相加當列車行程。隧道選線同時改變洞口、覆土與縱坡，短路線不保證低地質風險。比較方案必須使用相同起訖點，並分開主孔、引道及服務坑的工程數量；交通時間只是需求的一個指標，不能代替施工可達性或長期維修評估。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「路線里程與端點」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Total tunnel and shielded sections have different extents; define twin single-track measurement without adding both bores into train travel distance. Alignment changes portals, cover and gradient together, so a shorter tunnel need not have lower geological risk. Compare options between identical endpoints and distinguish running bores, approaches and service galleries. Travel time measures one service benefit but cannot replace assessment of construction access, maintenance closures or exposure to uncertain ground. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Alignment chainage and endpoints” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：長度=19.6 km；速度=60 km/h。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: length=19.6 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=19.6 min.","failure":"常見誤解：「最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「路線里程與端點」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Alignment chainage and endpoints”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b120-v14-01-k1","title":"服務邊界與路線代價","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost","text":"獅子洋總隧道與盾構段的範圍不同，教材先確認雙孔單線的計量方式，不把兩孔相加當列車行程。隧道選線同時改變洞口、覆土與縱坡，短路線不保證低地質風險。","textEn":"Total tunnel and shielded sections have different extents; define twin single-track measurement without adding both bores into train travel distance. Alignment changes portals, cover and gradient together, so a shorter tunnel need not have lower geological risk.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b120-v14-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「服務邊界與路線代價」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\" is correct?","options":["最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。","獅子洋總隧道與盾構段的範圍不同，教材先確認雙孔單線的計量方式，不把兩孔相加當列車行程。","岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。"],"optionsEn":["The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.","Total tunnel and shielded sections have different extents; define twin single-track measurement without adding both bores into train travel distance.","Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow."],"answer":1,"explanation":"獅子洋總隧道與盾構段的範圍不同，教材先確認雙孔單線的計量方式，不把兩孔相加當列車行程。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Total tunnel and shielded sections have different extents; define twin single-track measurement without adding both bores into train travel distance. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b120-v14-02","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：定量估算","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b120-v14-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「路線里程與端點」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Alignment chainage and endpoints” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：長度=19.6 km；速度=60 km/h。t=60L/v=19.6 min。僅把長度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為21.56 min。邊界：假想交通旅程，未含加減速、排隊及實際時刻表；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: length=19.6 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=19.6 min. Increasing only length by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 21.56 min. Boundary: Hypothetical transport journey excluding acceleration, queues and the real timetable. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對中心線長、總開挖長與接線範圍。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Reconcile centreline travel length, total excavation length and approaches.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b120-v14-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：長度=19.6 km；速度=60 km/h。t=60L/v=19.6 min。僅把長度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為21.56 min。邊界：假想交通旅程，未含加減速、排隊及實際時刻表；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: length=19.6 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=19.6 min. Increasing only length by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 21.56 min. Boundary: Hypothetical transport journey excluding acceleration, queues and the real timetable. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b120-v14-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「服務邊界與路線代價」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\", which statement holds?","options":["刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。","混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。","原創教學假設：長度=19.6 km；速度=60 km/h。"],"optionsEn":["A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance.","Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure.","Original teaching assumptions: length=19.6 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=19.6 min."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：長度=19.6 km；速度=60 km/h。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: length=19.6 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=19.6 min. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b120-v14-03","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b120-v14-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「路線里程與端點」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Alignment chainage and endpoints” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對中心線長、總開挖長與接線範圍。把縱斷面、地形與地質剖面疊合，以端點坐標獨立反算距離，再將主孔與支坑數量分開核對。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Reconcile centreline travel length, total excavation length and approaches. Overlay the longitudinal profile, terrain and geology; independently derive distances from endpoint coordinates and reconcile running-bore and gallery quantities separately. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「路線里程與端點」的交付需回答：核對中心線長、總開挖長與接線範圍。在方案表中凍結起訖點、計量範圍及地質假設，任何改線都要同步更新高程、數量與服務情境，不能只替換總長。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Shiziyang Tunnel, the alignment chainage and endpoints handover must address the following evidence: Reconcile centreline travel length, total excavation length and approaches. Freeze endpoints, measurement scope and ground assumptions in the option register; realignment requires coordinated updates to elevations, quantities and service scenarios rather than replacing one length.","failure":"注意干擾：把雙孔工程量當單趟長度會使時間和容量估算加倍。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using twin-bore quantities as one journey length doubles time and capacity inputs. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b120-v14-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對中心線長、總開挖長與接線範圍。把縱斷面、地形與地質剖面疊合，以端點坐標獨立反算距離，再將主孔與支坑數量分開核對。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Reconcile centreline travel length, total excavation length and approaches. Overlay the longitudinal profile, terrain and geology; independently derive distances from endpoint coordinates and reconcile running-bore and gallery quantities separately. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b120-v14-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「路線里程與端點」的交付需回答：核對中心線長、總開挖長與接線範圍。在方案表中凍結起訖點、計量範圍及地質假設，任何改線都要同步更新高程、數量與服務情境，不能只替換總長。","textEn":"For Shiziyang Tunnel, the alignment chainage and endpoints handover must address the following evidence: Reconcile centreline travel length, total excavation length and approaches. Freeze endpoints, measurement scope and ground assumptions in the option register; realignment requires coordinated updates to elevations, quantities and service scenarios rather than replacing one length.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「服務邊界與路線代價」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\"?","options":["核對中心線長、總開挖長與接線範圍。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","動壓公式算出的數值就是長鐵路隧道完整壓力波。"],"optionsEn":["Reconcile centreline travel length, total excavation length and approaches.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","A dynamic-pressure calculation is the complete pressure-wave prediction for a long rail tunnel."],"answer":0,"explanation":"核對中心線長、總開挖長與接線範圍。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Reconcile centreline travel length, total excavation length and approaches. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b120-v14-04","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：失效診斷","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b120-v14-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「路線里程與端點」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Alignment chainage and endpoints” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把雙孔工程量當單趟長度會使時間和容量估算加倍。混用全線與單孔長度會同時扭曲工程數量、行程及逃生距離，造成方案比較失去共同基準。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using twin-bore quantities as one journey length doubles time and capacity inputs. Mixing whole-route and single-bore lengths distorts quantities, journey time and escape distance, destroying the common basis of an option comparison. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：比較方案必須使用相同起訖點，並分開主孔、引道及服務坑的工程數量；交通時間只是需求的一個指標，不能代替施工可達性或長期維修評估。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Travel time measures one service benefit but cannot replace assessment of construction access, maintenance closures or exposure to uncertain ground.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b120-v14-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把雙孔工程量當單趟長度會使時間和容量估算加倍。混用全線與單孔長度會同時扭曲工程數量、行程及逃生距離，造成方案比較失去共同基準。","textEn":"Using twin-bore quantities as one journey length doubles time and capacity inputs. Mixing whole-route and single-bore lengths distorts quantities, journey time and escape distance, destroying the common basis of an option comparison.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b120-v14-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「服務邊界與路線代價」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","把雙孔工程量當單趟長度會使時間和容量估算加倍。","岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Using twin-bore quantities as one journey length doubles time and capacity inputs.","Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把雙孔工程量當單趟長度會使時間和容量估算加倍。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using twin-bore quantities as one journey length doubles time and capacity inputs. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b120-v14-05","title":"破碎帶連通與預報更新：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Fault connectivity and forecast updating: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b120-v14-04"],"objective":"說明「破碎帶連通性」如何影響獅子洋隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Fault-zone connectivity” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Shiziyang Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"公開資料記載軟土至土岩複合及岩層變化，本課研究混合面比例和裂隙如何共同改變掘進反應。斷層帶可以含很硬的岩塊，但整體變形與湧水常由填充節理和連通裂隙控制。單一岩芯強度不能代表整個掌子面；超前鑽孔、出水變化與揭露地質須回饋同一里程模型，預報則應保留不同情境及其證據權重。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「破碎帶連通性」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Published ground transitions motivate analysis of mixed-face proportions and fractures that change boring response together. A fault zone may contain strong intact blocks while filled joints and connected fractures govern its bulk deformation and inflow. One core strength does not represent the entire face. Probe records, water response and exposed geology must update a common chainage model, preserving competing interpretations and their evidential weight rather than treating a forecast as certainty. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Fault-zone connectivity” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：滲透係數=5e-06 m/s；水力坡降=2.1 無因次；通水面積=390 m²。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: conductivity=5e-06 m/s; hydraulic gradient=2.1 dimensionless; flow area=390 m².","failure":"常見誤解：「岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「破碎帶連通性」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Fault-zone connectivity”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b120-v14-05-k1","title":"破碎帶連通與預報更新","titleEn":"Fault connectivity and forecast updating","text":"公開資料記載軟土至土岩複合及岩層變化，本課研究混合面比例和裂隙如何共同改變掘進反應。斷層帶可以含很硬的岩塊，但整體變形與湧水常由填充節理和連通裂隙控制。","textEn":"Published ground transitions motivate analysis of mixed-face proportions and fractures that change boring response together. A fault zone may contain strong intact blocks while filled joints and connected fractures govern its bulk deformation and inflow.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b120-v14-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「破碎帶連通與預報更新」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Fault connectivity and forecast updating\" is correct?","options":["岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。","目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。","公開資料記載軟土至土岩複合及岩層變化，本課研究混合面比例和裂隙如何共同改變掘進反應。"],"optionsEn":["Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow.","No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.","Published ground transitions motivate analysis of mixed-face proportions and fractures that change boring response together."],"answer":2,"explanation":"公開資料記載軟土至土岩複合及岩層變化，本課研究混合面比例和裂隙如何共同改變掘進反應。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Published ground transitions motivate analysis of mixed-face proportions and fractures that change boring response together. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b120-v14-06","title":"破碎帶連通與預報更新：定量估算","titleEn":"Fault connectivity and forecast updating: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b120-v14-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「破碎帶連通性」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Fault-zone connectivity” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：滲透係數=5e-06 m/s；水力坡降=2.1 無因次；通水面積=390 m²。Q=k i A=0.004095 m³/s。僅把滲透係數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.0045045 m³/s。邊界：均質飽和達西流，不代表裂隙集中流；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: conductivity=5e-06 m/s; hydraulic gradient=2.1 dimensionless; flow area=390 m². Q=k i A=0.004095 m³/s. Increasing only conductivity by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.0045045 m³/s. Boundary: Homogeneous saturated Darcy flow, not concentrated fracture flow. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：對齊扭矩波動、地質揭露與出渣粒徑。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Align torque fluctuation, exposures and spoil grading.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b120-v14-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：滲透係數=5e-06 m/s；水力坡降=2.1 無因次；通水面積=390 m²。Q=k i A=0.004095 m³/s。僅把滲透係數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.0045045 m³/s。邊界：均質飽和達西流，不代表裂隙集中流；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: conductivity=5e-06 m/s; hydraulic gradient=2.1 dimensionless; flow area=390 m². Q=k i A=0.004095 m³/s. Increasing only conductivity by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.0045045 m³/s. Boundary: Homogeneous saturated Darcy flow, not concentrated fracture flow. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b120-v14-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「破碎帶連通與預報更新」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Fault connectivity and forecast updating\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：滲透係數=5e-06 m/s；水力坡降=2.1 無因次；通水面積=390 m²。","灌入體積等於理論空隙就能證明襯砌背後全部填滿。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: conductivity=5e-06 m/s; hydraulic gradient=2.1 dimensionless; flow area=390 m².","Injected volume equal to the theoretical annulus proves complete filling behind the lining.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：滲透係數=5e-06 m/s；水力坡降=2.1 無因次；通水面積=390 m²。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: conductivity=5e-06 m/s; hydraulic gradient=2.1 dimensionless; flow area=390 m². Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b120-v14-07","title":"破碎帶連通與預報更新：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Fault connectivity and forecast updating: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b120-v14-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「破碎帶連通性」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Fault-zone connectivity” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"對齊扭矩波動、地質揭露與出渣粒徑。將岩心回收、裂隙方位與出水曲線按里程對齊，用未參與建模的孔段作交叉檢驗，檢查是否只擬合已知資料。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Align torque fluctuation, exposures and spoil grading. Align recovery, fracture orientation and inflow by chainage; test the interpretation against a withheld borehole interval to detect fitting only the known observations. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「破碎帶連通性」的交付需回答：對齊扭矩波動、地質揭露與出渣粒徑。每次地質模型更新保留舊版與新增證據，差異由地質及支護設計者共同判讀，施工條件改變需重新確認核准範圍。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Shiziyang Tunnel, the fault-zone connectivity handover must address the following evidence: Align torque fluctuation, exposures and spoil grading. Retain previous interpretations and new evidence at every update; geology and support designers jointly interpret differences and reconfirm approved bounds when ground conditions change.","failure":"注意干擾：把所有扭矩峰當岩石變硬會漏掉面內不均和設備因素。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Treating all torque peaks as harder rock misses face heterogeneity and equipment causes. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b120-v14-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"對齊扭矩波動、地質揭露與出渣粒徑。將岩心回收、裂隙方位與出水曲線按里程對齊，用未參與建模的孔段作交叉檢驗，檢查是否只擬合已知資料。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Align torque fluctuation, exposures and spoil grading. Align recovery, fracture orientation and inflow by chainage; test the interpretation against a withheld borehole interval to detect fitting only the known observations. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b120-v14-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「破碎帶連通性」的交付需回答：對齊扭矩波動、地質揭露與出渣粒徑。每次地質模型更新保留舊版與新增證據，差異由地質及支護設計者共同判讀，施工條件改變需重新確認核准範圍。","textEn":"For Shiziyang Tunnel, the fault-zone connectivity handover must address the following evidence: Align torque fluctuation, exposures and spoil grading. Retain previous interpretations and new evidence at every update; geology and support designers jointly interpret differences and reconfirm approved bounds when ground conditions change.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「破碎帶連通與預報更新」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Fault connectivity and forecast updating\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","對齊扭矩波動、地質揭露與出渣粒徑。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Align torque fluctuation, exposures and spoil grading.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time."],"answer":1,"explanation":"對齊扭矩波動、地質揭露與出渣粒徑。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Align torque fluctuation, exposures and spoil grading. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b120-v14-08","title":"破碎帶連通與預報更新：失效診斷","titleEn":"Fault connectivity and forecast updating: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b120-v14-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「破碎帶連通性」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Fault-zone connectivity” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把所有扭矩峰當岩石變硬會漏掉面內不均和設備因素。只用完整岩石強度會漏掉軟弱填充物，可能在看似堅硬的地層中出現收斂加快、支護過載或水量突增。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Treating all torque peaks as harder rock misses face heterogeneity and equipment causes. Intact strength alone misses weak infill, allowing accelerating convergence, support overload or sudden inflow in ground that superficially appears strong. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：單一岩芯強度不能代表整個掌子面；超前鑽孔、出水變化與揭露地質須回饋同一里程模型，預報則應保留不同情境及其證據權重。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Probe records, water response and exposed geology must update a common chainage model, preserving competing interpretations and their evidential weight rather than treating a forecast as certainty.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b120-v14-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把所有扭矩峰當岩石變硬會漏掉面內不均和設備因素。只用完整岩石強度會漏掉軟弱填充物，可能在看似堅硬的地層中出現收斂加快、支護過載或水量突增。","textEn":"Treating all torque peaks as harder rock misses face heterogeneity and equipment causes. Intact strength alone misses weak infill, allowing accelerating convergence, support overload or sudden inflow in ground that superficially appears strong.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b120-v14-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「破碎帶連通與預報更新」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Fault connectivity and forecast updating\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。","把所有扭矩峰當岩石變硬會漏掉面內不均和設備因素。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.","Treating all torque peaks as harder rock misses face heterogeneity and equipment causes."],"answer":2,"explanation":"把所有扭矩峰當岩石變硬會漏掉面內不均和設備因素。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Treating all torque peaks as harder rock misses face heterogeneity and equipment causes. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b120-v14-s2","title":"機制、材料與定量設計","titleEn":"Mechanisms, materials and quantitative design","description":"本階段聚焦「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」與「掘進利用率與設備停時」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\" and \"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b120-v14-09","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b120-v14-08"],"objective":"說明「測壓水頭」如何影響獅子洋隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Piezometric head” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Shiziyang Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"獅子洋水下地層的水壓教材採分層測壓，不以同一海面水頭代表所有軟硬交界。水壓取決於連通含水層的測壓水頭，不必等於地表或海面至洞頂的幾何深度。排水降低水壓卻可能增加有效應力與沉陷；停泵或排水堵塞後水頭又會回升，因此防水、排水及環境保水是互相制約的設計選擇。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「測壓水頭」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Use layered pressure observations rather than assigning one sea-level head to every soft-hard interface. Water pressure follows piezometric head in the connected aquifer, not automatically the geometric depth below ground or sea level. Drainage reduces pressure but can increase effective stress and settlement. Head may recover after a pump outage or blockage, coupling waterproofing, drainage capacity and preservation of surrounding groundwater in the permanent design. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Piezometric head” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=108 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=108 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=1059.48 kPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「測壓水頭」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Piezometric head”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b120-v14-09-k1","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure","text":"獅子洋水下地層的水壓教材採分層測壓，不以同一海面水頭代表所有軟硬交界。水壓取決於連通含水層的測壓水頭，不必等於地表或海面至洞頂的幾何深度。","textEn":"Use layered pressure observations rather than assigning one sea-level head to every soft-hard interface. Water pressure follows piezometric head in the connected aquifer, not automatically the geometric depth below ground or sea level.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b120-v14-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\" is correct?","options":["獅子洋水下地層的水壓教材採分層測壓，不以同一海面水頭代表所有軟硬交界。","目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。","刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。"],"optionsEn":["Use layered pressure observations rather than assigning one sea-level head to every soft-hard interface.","No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.","A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"獅子洋水下地層的水壓教材採分層測壓，不以同一海面水頭代表所有軟硬交界。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Use layered pressure observations rather than assigning one sea-level head to every soft-hard interface. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b120-v14-10","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓：定量估算","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b120-v14-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「測壓水頭」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Piezometric head” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=108 m。p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=1059.48 kPa。僅把水頭增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為1165.43 kPa。邊界：靜水表壓，不是土體總壓或原位量測；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=108 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=1059.48 kPa. Increasing only head by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 1165.43 kPa. Boundary: Hydrostatic gauge pressure, not total earth pressure or an in-situ measurement. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比較不同層位孔壓與潮位，保留反應延遲。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare layer-specific pore pressures and tide with response lag preserved.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b120-v14-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=108 m。p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=1059.48 kPa。僅把水頭增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為1165.43 kPa。邊界：靜水表壓，不是土體總壓或原位量測；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=108 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=1059.48 kPa. Increasing only head by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 1165.43 kPa. Boundary: Hydrostatic gauge pressure, not total earth pressure or an in-situ measurement. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b120-v14-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\", which statement holds?","options":["混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。","原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=108 m。","動壓公式算出的數值就是長鐵路隧道完整壓力波。"],"optionsEn":["Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure.","Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=108 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=1059.48 kPa.","A dynamic-pressure calculation is the complete pressure-wave prediction for a long rail tunnel."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=108 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=108 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=1059.48 kPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b120-v14-11","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b120-v14-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「測壓水頭」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Piezometric head” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比較不同層位孔壓與潮位，保留反應延遲。使用分層測壓管及流量計，配合降雨或潮位序列分辨補注與設備影響，將讀值統一換算至同一高程基準。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare layer-specific pore pressures and tide with response lag preserved. Use nested piezometers and flowmeters with rainfall or tide histories to distinguish recharge from equipment effects, converting observations to a common elevation datum. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「測壓水頭」的交付需回答：比較不同層位孔壓與潮位，保留反應延遲。設計檢核應分列正常排水、堵塞與停電水位，將環境受體的容許變化和監測責任一起交付，不把抽水量當唯一指標。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Shiziyang Tunnel, the piezometric head handover must address the following evidence: Compare layer-specific pore pressures and tide with response lag preserved. Separate normal drainage, blocked-drain and power-outage heads and hand over receptor limits and monitoring responsibility together rather than using pump flow as the sole indicator.","failure":"注意干擾：低透水層的延遲水壓可能被短時讀值漏掉。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Short observations can miss delayed pressure in low-permeability layers. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b120-v14-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比較不同層位孔壓與潮位，保留反應延遲。使用分層測壓管及流量計，配合降雨或潮位序列分辨補注與設備影響，將讀值統一換算至同一高程基準。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Compare layer-specific pore pressures and tide with response lag preserved. Use nested piezometers and flowmeters with rainfall or tide histories to distinguish recharge from equipment effects, converting observations to a common elevation datum. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b120-v14-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「測壓水頭」的交付需回答：比較不同層位孔壓與潮位，保留反應延遲。設計檢核應分列正常排水、堵塞與停電水位，將環境受體的容許變化和監測責任一起交付，不把抽水量當唯一指標。","textEn":"For Shiziyang Tunnel, the piezometric head handover must address the following evidence: Compare layer-specific pore pressures and tide with response lag preserved. Separate normal drainage, blocked-drain and power-outage heads and hand over receptor limits and monitoring responsibility together rather than using pump flow as the sole indicator.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。","比較不同層位孔壓與潮位，保留反應延遲。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.","Compare layer-specific pore pressures and tide with response lag preserved."],"answer":2,"explanation":"比較不同層位孔壓與潮位，保留反應延遲。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare layer-specific pore pressures and tide with response lag preserved. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b120-v14-12","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓：失效診斷","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b120-v14-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「測壓水頭」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Piezometric head” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"低透水層的延遲水壓可能被短時讀值漏掉。將暫時降水後的低水頭當成永久狀態，會漏掉停泵後外壓回升；過度排水也可能引起周邊地層壓密。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Short observations can miss delayed pressure in low-permeability layers. Treating temporarily lowered head as permanent misses pressure recovery after outage; excessive drainage can also consolidate surrounding ground. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：排水降低水壓卻可能增加有效應力與沉陷；停泵或排水堵塞後水頭又會回升，因此防水、排水及環境保水是互相制約的設計選擇。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Head may recover after a pump outage or blockage, coupling waterproofing, drainage capacity and preservation of surrounding groundwater in the permanent design.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b120-v14-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"低透水層的延遲水壓可能被短時讀值漏掉。將暫時降水後的低水頭當成永久狀態，會漏掉停泵後外壓回升；過度排水也可能引起周邊地層壓密。","textEn":"Short observations can miss delayed pressure in low-permeability layers. Treating temporarily lowered head as permanent misses pressure recovery after outage; excessive drainage can also consolidate surrounding ground.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b120-v14-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["低透水層的延遲水壓可能被短時讀值漏掉。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。"],"optionsEn":["Short observations can miss delayed pressure in low-permeability layers.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"低透水層的延遲水壓可能被短時讀值漏掉。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Short observations can miss delayed pressure in low-permeability layers. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b120-v14-13","title":"掘進利用率與設備停時：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b120-v14-12"],"objective":"說明「有效掘進利用率」如何影響獅子洋隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Effective boring utilisation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Shiziyang Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"長距離盾構的磨耗與停機需要按軟土、混合面及岩段分類，教材不以單一平均進尺判斷所有區段。TBM瞬時貫入率只描述刀盤切削的一段時間，拼裝、換刀、出渣與維修決定每天真正進尺。岩石強度與磨蝕性對刀具的影響不同，混合掌子面又產生不對稱作用；比較機器績效須按地質分區和停時原因分類，不能只排序最高進尺。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「有效掘進利用率」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Classify wear and downtime by soft soil, mixed face and rock rather than judging all reaches by one average advance. Instantaneous penetration describes only active cutting; erection, cutter changes, muck handling and repairs determine daily advance. Strength and abrasivity affect cutters differently, while mixed faces impose asymmetric loading. Compare performance by ground domain and downtime cause, because the highest short-duration penetration rate can coexist with poor daily production and increased maintenance demand. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Effective boring utilisation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：切削速率=2.07 m/h；有效利用率=0.295 無因次。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: active penetration=2.07 m/h; utilisation=0.295 dimensionless.","failure":"常見誤解：「刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「有效掘進利用率」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Effective boring utilisation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b120-v14-13-k1","title":"掘進利用率與設備停時","titleEn":"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime","text":"長距離盾構的磨耗與停機需要按軟土、混合面及岩段分類，教材不以單一平均進尺判斷所有區段。TBM瞬時貫入率只描述刀盤切削的一段時間，拼裝、換刀、出渣與維修決定每天真正進尺。","textEn":"Classify wear and downtime by soft soil, mixed face and rock rather than judging all reaches by one average advance. Instantaneous penetration describes only active cutting; erection, cutter changes, muck handling and repairs determine daily advance.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b120-v14-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「掘進利用率與設備停時」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime\" is correct?","options":["刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。","長距離盾構的磨耗與停機需要按軟土、混合面及岩段分類，教材不以單一平均進尺判斷所有區段。","灌入體積等於理論空隙就能證明襯砌背後全部填滿。"],"optionsEn":["A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance.","Classify wear and downtime by soft soil, mixed face and rock rather than judging all reaches by one average advance.","Injected volume equal to the theoretical annulus proves complete filling behind the lining."],"answer":1,"explanation":"長距離盾構的磨耗與停機需要按軟土、混合面及岩段分類，教材不以單一平均進尺判斷所有區段。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Classify wear and downtime by soft soil, mixed face and rock rather than judging all reaches by one average advance. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b120-v14-14","title":"掘進利用率與設備停時：定量估算","titleEn":"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b120-v14-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「有效掘進利用率」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Effective boring utilisation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：切削速率=2.07 m/h；有效利用率=0.295 無因次。D=24vu=14.6556 m/day。僅把有效利用率增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為16.1212 m/day。邊界：平均循環模型，未表示地質轉換及停機分布；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: active penetration=2.07 m/h; utilisation=0.295 dimensionless. D=24vu=14.6556 m/day. Increasing only utilisation by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 16.1212 m/day. Boundary: Mean-cycle model without ground transitions or downtime distribution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：逐刀具位置比較磨耗與地層暴露時間。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare wear by cutter position and time exposed to each ground type.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b120-v14-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：切削速率=2.07 m/h；有效利用率=0.295 無因次。D=24vu=14.6556 m/day。僅把有效利用率增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為16.1212 m/day。邊界：平均循環模型，未表示地質轉換及停機分布；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: active penetration=2.07 m/h; utilisation=0.295 dimensionless. D=24vu=14.6556 m/day. Increasing only utilisation by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 16.1212 m/day. Boundary: Mean-cycle model without ground transitions or downtime distribution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b120-v14-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「掘進利用率與設備停時」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime\", which statement holds?","options":["兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。","原創教學假設：切削速率=2.07 m/h；有效利用率=0.295 無因次。"],"optionsEn":["Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.","Original teaching assumptions: active penetration=2.07 m/h; utilisation=0.295 dimensionless."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：切削速率=2.07 m/h；有效利用率=0.295 無因次。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: active penetration=2.07 m/h; utilisation=0.295 dimensionless. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b120-v14-15","title":"掘進利用率與設備停時：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b120-v14-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「有效掘進利用率」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Effective boring utilisation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"逐刀具位置比較磨耗與地層暴露時間。由時間戳分離切削、拼裝與故障，將刀具位置、磨耗量及推力扭矩對齊里程，檢查停時是否集中在特定地層。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare wear by cutter position and time exposed to each ground type. Separate cutting, erection and faults by timestamp; align cutter position, wear, thrust and torque with chainage and test clustering by ground type. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「有效掘進利用率」的交付需回答：逐刀具位置比較磨耗與地層暴露時間。停機紀錄使用可追溯原因碼，把地質變化與設備故障分開統計，參數調整只能在設備和施工團隊核准程序內進行。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Shiziyang Tunnel, the effective boring utilisation handover must address the following evidence: Compare wear by cutter position and time exposed to each ground type. Use traceable downtime codes, separating geological change from equipment faults; parameter changes stay within procedures approved by equipment and construction teams.","failure":"注意干擾：平均磨耗可能掩蓋局部刀具先失效造成的非對稱作用。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Mean wear conceals early local cutter failure and asymmetric loading. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b120-v14-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"逐刀具位置比較磨耗與地層暴露時間。由時間戳分離切削、拼裝與故障，將刀具位置、磨耗量及推力扭矩對齊里程，檢查停時是否集中在特定地層。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Compare wear by cutter position and time exposed to each ground type. Separate cutting, erection and faults by timestamp; align cutter position, wear, thrust and torque with chainage and test clustering by ground type. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b120-v14-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「有效掘進利用率」的交付需回答：逐刀具位置比較磨耗與地層暴露時間。停機紀錄使用可追溯原因碼，把地質變化與設備故障分開統計，參數調整只能在設備和施工團隊核准程序內進行。","textEn":"For Shiziyang Tunnel, the effective boring utilisation handover must address the following evidence: Compare wear by cutter position and time exposed to each ground type. Use traceable downtime codes, separating geological change from equipment faults; parameter changes stay within procedures approved by equipment and construction teams.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「掘進利用率與設備停時」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime\"?","options":["逐刀具位置比較磨耗與地層暴露時間。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Compare wear by cutter position and time exposed to each ground type.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":0,"explanation":"逐刀具位置比較磨耗與地層暴露時間。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare wear by cutter position and time exposed to each ground type. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b120-v14-16","title":"掘進利用率與設備停時：失效診斷","titleEn":"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b120-v14-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「有效掘進利用率」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Effective boring utilisation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"平均磨耗可能掩蓋局部刀具先失效造成的非對稱作用。只提高瞬時進尺可能使出渣或刀具超出有效工況，短暫改善後增加停機，平均進尺和零件壽命反而下降。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Mean wear conceals early local cutter failure and asymmetric loading. Higher instantaneous advance can overload cutters or muck transport and create longer stoppages that reduce average progress and component life. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：岩石強度與磨蝕性對刀具的影響不同，混合掌子面又產生不對稱作用；比較機器績效須按地質分區和停時原因分類，不能只排序最高進尺。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Compare performance by ground domain and downtime cause, because the highest short-duration penetration rate can coexist with poor daily production and increased maintenance demand.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b120-v14-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"平均磨耗可能掩蓋局部刀具先失效造成的非對稱作用。只提高瞬時進尺可能使出渣或刀具超出有效工況，短暫改善後增加停機，平均進尺和零件壽命反而下降。","textEn":"Mean wear conceals early local cutter failure and asymmetric loading. Higher instantaneous advance can overload cutters or muck transport and create longer stoppages that reduce average progress and component life.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b120-v14-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「掘進利用率與設備停時」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","平均磨耗可能掩蓋局部刀具先失效造成的非對稱作用。","灌入體積等於理論空隙就能證明襯砌背後全部填滿。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Mean wear conceals early local cutter failure and asymmetric loading.","Injected volume equal to the theoretical annulus proves complete filling behind the lining."],"answer":1,"explanation":"平均磨耗可能掩蓋局部刀具先失效造成的非對稱作用。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Mean wear conceals early local cutter failure and asymmetric loading. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b120-v14-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「背填連續性與體積帳」與「環向受力與接縫柔度」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Backfill continuity and volume balance\" and \"Ring force and joint flexibility\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b120-v14-17","title":"背填連續性與體積帳：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Backfill continuity and volume balance: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b120-v14-16"],"objective":"說明「襯砌背後幾何空隙」如何影響獅子洋隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Geometric lining annulus” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Shiziyang Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"高速軌道對沉陷敏感，獅子洋教材把背填幾何空隙與實際地層損失分開，不以注量當沉陷控制證明。盾尾空隙須由背填恢復襯砌與地層的接觸，但幾何空隙不是必然注入量。超挖、地層吸收、回流和材料體積變化都會改變收支；注入量達到目標仍不代表每個位置填滿，需要把壓力、時間與後續變形一起判讀。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「襯砌背後幾何空隙」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Track geometry is sensitive to settlement; separate annular void from actual ground loss and do not use grout volume alone as proof of control. Backfill restores contact across the shield-tail gap, but geometric void is not the required injected volume. Overbreak, absorption, return and material volume change alter the balance. Meeting a volume target does not prove complete spatial filling; pressure, timing and later deformation must be interpreted together rather than using a single total. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Geometric lining annulus” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：開挖外徑=8.76 m；襯砌外徑=8.46 m；環長=1.5 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: excavated diameter=8.76 m; lining diameter=8.46 m; ring length=1.5 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「灌入體積等於理論空隙就能證明襯砌背後全部填滿。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Injected volume equal to the theoretical annulus proves complete filling behind the lining.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「襯砌背後幾何空隙」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Geometric lining annulus”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b120-v14-17-k1","title":"背填連續性與體積帳","titleEn":"Backfill continuity and volume balance","text":"高速軌道對沉陷敏感，獅子洋教材把背填幾何空隙與實際地層損失分開，不以注量當沉陷控制證明。盾尾空隙須由背填恢復襯砌與地層的接觸，但幾何空隙不是必然注入量。","textEn":"Track geometry is sensitive to settlement; separate annular void from actual ground loss and do not use grout volume alone as proof of control. Backfill restores contact across the shield-tail gap, but geometric void is not the required injected volume.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b120-v14-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：灌入體積等於理論空隙就能證明襯砌背後全部填滿。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Injected volume equal to the theoretical annulus proves complete filling behind the lining. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「背填連續性與體積帳」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Backfill continuity and volume balance\" is correct?","options":["灌入體積等於理論空隙就能證明襯砌背後全部填滿。","混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。","高速軌道對沉陷敏感，獅子洋教材把背填幾何空隙與實際地層損失分開，不以注量當沉陷控制證明。"],"optionsEn":["Injected volume equal to the theoretical annulus proves complete filling behind the lining.","Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure.","Track geometry is sensitive to settlement; separate annular void from actual ground loss and do not use grout volume alone as proof of control."],"answer":2,"explanation":"高速軌道對沉陷敏感，獅子洋教材把背填幾何空隙與實際地層損失分開，不以注量當沉陷控制證明。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Track geometry is sensitive to settlement; separate annular void from actual ground loss and do not use grout volume alone as proof of control. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b120-v14-18","title":"背填連續性與體積帳：定量估算","titleEn":"Backfill continuity and volume balance: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b120-v14-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「襯砌背後幾何空隙」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Geometric lining annulus” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：開挖外徑=8.76 m；襯砌外徑=8.46 m；環長=1.5 m。V=π(De²−Dl²)L/4=6.08605 m³。僅把環長增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為6.69466 m³。邊界：同心幾何空隙，不等於實際灌漿需求或完成證明；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: excavated diameter=8.76 m; lining diameter=8.46 m; ring length=1.5 m. V=π(De²−Dl²)L/4=6.08605 m³. Increasing only ring length by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 6.69466 m³. Boundary: Concentric geometric void, not actual grout demand or proof of completion. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：結合注壓、注量、環片浮動和地表或孔內位移。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Combine pressure, volume, segment flotation and ground or tunnel movement.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b120-v14-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：開挖外徑=8.76 m；襯砌外徑=8.46 m；環長=1.5 m。V=π(De²−Dl²)L/4=6.08605 m³。僅把環長增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為6.69466 m³。邊界：同心幾何空隙，不等於實際灌漿需求或完成證明；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: excavated diameter=8.76 m; lining diameter=8.46 m; ring length=1.5 m. V=π(De²−Dl²)L/4=6.08605 m³. Increasing only ring length by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 6.69466 m³. Boundary: Concentric geometric void, not actual grout demand or proof of completion. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b120-v14-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「背填連續性與體積帳」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Backfill continuity and volume balance\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：開挖外徑=8.76 m；襯砌外徑=8.46 m；環長=1.5 m。","動壓公式算出的數值就是長鐵路隧道完整壓力波。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: excavated diameter=8.76 m; lining diameter=8.46 m; ring length=1.5 m.","A dynamic-pressure calculation is the complete pressure-wave prediction for a long rail tunnel.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：開挖外徑=8.76 m；襯砌外徑=8.46 m；環長=1.5 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: excavated diameter=8.76 m; lining diameter=8.46 m; ring length=1.5 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b120-v14-19","title":"背填連續性與體積帳：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Backfill continuity and volume balance: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b120-v14-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「襯砌背後幾何空隙」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Geometric lining annulus” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"結合注壓、注量、環片浮動和地表或孔內位移。用環片及開挖尺寸計算幾何空隙，核對注入回流質量與時間戳，再以適當無損檢測及變形資料查局部缺填。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Combine pressure, volume, segment flotation and ground or tunnel movement. Calculate the annulus from lining and excavation dimensions, reconcile injected/returned mass and timing, then use suitable nondestructive and deformation evidence for local gaps. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「襯砌背後幾何空隙」的交付需回答：結合注壓、注量、環片浮動和地表或孔內位移。將每環幾何、材料批次及注入回流紀錄綁定，缺填診斷由土建及地工共同確認，後續處置不只追求增加總注量。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Shiziyang Tunnel, the geometric lining annulus handover must address the following evidence: Combine pressure, volume, segment flotation and ground or tunnel movement. Link each ring to geometry, material batch and injection/return records; structural and ground teams diagnose gaps together rather than merely increasing volume.","failure":"注意干擾：高注量可能伴隨流失，並不能保證軌道支承均勻。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: High take may reflect loss and does not ensure uniform track support. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b120-v14-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"結合注壓、注量、環片浮動和地表或孔內位移。用環片及開挖尺寸計算幾何空隙，核對注入回流質量與時間戳，再以適當無損檢測及變形資料查局部缺填。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Combine pressure, volume, segment flotation and ground or tunnel movement. Calculate the annulus from lining and excavation dimensions, reconcile injected/returned mass and timing, then use suitable nondestructive and deformation evidence for local gaps. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b120-v14-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「襯砌背後幾何空隙」的交付需回答：結合注壓、注量、環片浮動和地表或孔內位移。將每環幾何、材料批次及注入回流紀錄綁定，缺填診斷由土建及地工共同確認，後續處置不只追求增加總注量。","textEn":"For Shiziyang Tunnel, the geometric lining annulus handover must address the following evidence: Combine pressure, volume, segment flotation and ground or tunnel movement. Link each ring to geometry, material batch and injection/return records; structural and ground teams diagnose gaps together rather than merely increasing volume.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「背填連續性與體積帳」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Backfill continuity and volume balance\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","結合注壓、注量、環片浮動和地表或孔內位移。","岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Combine pressure, volume, segment flotation and ground or tunnel movement.","Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow."],"answer":1,"explanation":"結合注壓、注量、環片浮動和地表或孔內位移。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Combine pressure, volume, segment flotation and ground or tunnel movement. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b120-v14-20","title":"背填連續性與體積帳：失效診斷","titleEn":"Backfill continuity and volume balance: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b120-v14-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「襯砌背後幾何空隙」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Geometric lining annulus” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"高注量可能伴隨流失，並不能保證軌道支承均勻。局部通道讓材料回流時，總注量可能正常但背後仍有空洞，環片變形與接頭滲漏可能延後出現。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"High take may reflect loss and does not ensure uniform track support. Preferential return paths can give normal total injection while leaving voids, with delayed segment distortion and leakage. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：超挖、地層吸收、回流和材料體積變化都會改變收支；注入量達到目標仍不代表每個位置填滿，需要把壓力、時間與後續變形一起判讀。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Meeting a volume target does not prove complete spatial filling; pressure, timing and later deformation must be interpreted together rather than using a single total.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「灌入體積等於理論空隙就能證明襯砌背後全部填滿。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Injected volume equal to the theoretical annulus proves complete filling behind the lining.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b120-v14-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"高注量可能伴隨流失，並不能保證軌道支承均勻。局部通道讓材料回流時，總注量可能正常但背後仍有空洞，環片變形與接頭滲漏可能延後出現。","textEn":"High take may reflect loss and does not ensure uniform track support. Preferential return paths can give normal total injection while leaving voids, with delayed segment distortion and leakage.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b120-v14-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「背填連續性與體積帳」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Backfill continuity and volume balance\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。","高注量可能伴隨流失，並不能保證軌道支承均勻。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure.","High take may reflect loss and does not ensure uniform track support."],"answer":2,"explanation":"高注量可能伴隨流失，並不能保證軌道支承均勻。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"High take may reflect loss and does not ensure uniform track support. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b120-v14-21","title":"環向受力與接縫柔度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Ring force and joint flexibility: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b120-v14-20"],"objective":"說明「襯砌環向壓縮」如何影響獅子洋隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Lining hoop compression” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Shiziyang Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"公開技術背景包含不同地層對應結構，本課用薄環示例後指出內襯與縱向構件需另建空間模型。圓形襯砌對均勻外壓可主要以環向壓縮抵抗，但接頭轉動、偏壓與背填空隙會引起彎矩。薄環膜應力只說明其中一條受力路徑；脫模、運輸、頂推及永久狀態的荷載不同，環片局部接觸與止水條件必須另外檢核。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「襯砌環向壓縮」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Different ground-dependent structures require a spatial model for internal lining and longitudinal members beyond a thin-ring example. A circular lining resists uniform external pressure largely through hoop compression, but joint rotation, uneven load and backfill voids generate bending. Thin-ring membrane stress describes only one load path. Demoulding, transport, jacking and permanent states impose different actions, requiring separate checks of local segment contact and sealing rather than one permanent-load calculation. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Lining hoop compression” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：均勻外壓=0.68 MPa；半徑=3.5 m；厚度=0.35 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: uniform external pressure=0.68 MPa; radius=3.5 m; thickness=0.35 m. σθ=pr/t=6.8 MPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「襯砌環向壓縮」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Lining hoop compression”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b120-v14-21-k1","title":"環向受力與接縫柔度","titleEn":"Ring force and joint flexibility","text":"公開技術背景包含不同地層對應結構，本課用薄環示例後指出內襯與縱向構件需另建空間模型。圓形襯砌對均勻外壓可主要以環向壓縮抵抗，但接頭轉動、偏壓與背填空隙會引起彎矩。","textEn":"Different ground-dependent structures require a spatial model for internal lining and longitudinal members beyond a thin-ring example. A circular lining resists uniform external pressure largely through hoop compression, but joint rotation, uneven load and backfill voids generate bending.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b120-v14-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「環向受力與接縫柔度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Ring force and joint flexibility\" is correct?","options":["公開技術背景包含不同地層對應結構，本課用薄環示例後指出內襯與縱向構件需另建空間模型。","混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Different ground-dependent structures require a spatial model for internal lining and longitudinal members beyond a thin-ring example.","Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error."],"answer":0,"explanation":"公開技術背景包含不同地層對應結構，本課用薄環示例後指出內襯與縱向構件需另建空間模型。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Different ground-dependent structures require a spatial model for internal lining and longitudinal members beyond a thin-ring example. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b120-v14-22","title":"環向受力與接縫柔度：定量估算","titleEn":"Ring force and joint flexibility: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b120-v14-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「襯砌環向壓縮」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Lining hoop compression” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：均勻外壓=0.68 MPa；半徑=3.5 m；厚度=0.35 m。σθ=pr/t=6.8 MPa。僅把均勻外壓增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為7.48 MPa。邊界：薄圓環膜應力，不是接縫、偏壓或矩形框架解；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: uniform external pressure=0.68 MPa; radius=3.5 m; thickness=0.35 m. σθ=pr/t=6.8 MPa. Increasing only uniform external pressure by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 7.48 MPa. Boundary: Thin circular-ring membrane stress, not a joint, uneven-load or rectangular-frame solution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比較環向應變、縱向沉陷和軌道基座反應。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare hoop strain, longitudinal settlement and track-support response.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b120-v14-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：均勻外壓=0.68 MPa；半徑=3.5 m；厚度=0.35 m。σθ=pr/t=6.8 MPa。僅把均勻外壓增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為7.48 MPa。邊界：薄圓環膜應力，不是接縫、偏壓或矩形框架解；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: uniform external pressure=0.68 MPa; radius=3.5 m; thickness=0.35 m. σθ=pr/t=6.8 MPa. Increasing only uniform external pressure by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 7.48 MPa. Boundary: Thin circular-ring membrane stress, not a joint, uneven-load or rectangular-frame solution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b120-v14-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「環向受力與接縫柔度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Ring force and joint flexibility\", which statement holds?","options":["只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。","原創教學假設：均勻外壓=0.68 MPa；半徑=3.5 m；厚度=0.35 m。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.","Original teaching assumptions: uniform external pressure=0.68 MPa; radius=3.5 m; thickness=0.35 m. σθ=pr/t=6.8 MPa.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：均勻外壓=0.68 MPa；半徑=3.5 m；厚度=0.35 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: uniform external pressure=0.68 MPa; radius=3.5 m; thickness=0.35 m. σθ=pr/t=6.8 MPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b120-v14-23","title":"環向受力與接縫柔度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Ring force and joint flexibility: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b120-v14-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「襯砌環向壓縮」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Lining hoop compression” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比較環向應變、縱向沉陷和軌道基座反應。將環形變形、接縫張開與應變和含接頭彈簧的模型比較，分開安裝後、背填後及水頭回升後的基準。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare hoop strain, longitudinal settlement and track-support response. Compare ring distortion, joint opening and strain with a joint-spring model, separating baselines after installation, grouting and head recovery. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「襯砌環向壓縮」的交付需回答：比較環向應變、縱向沉陷和軌道基座反應。設計圖應分開標註各施工階段、接頭剛度及背填條件，構件驗收同時核對幾何、材料批次與止水試驗適用包絡。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Shiziyang Tunnel, the lining hoop compression handover must address the following evidence: Compare hoop strain, longitudinal settlement and track-support response. Drawings distinguish stages, joint stiffness and backfill conditions; component acceptance reconciles geometry, material batches and the applicable sealing-test envelope.","failure":"注意干擾：只驗環向壓縮會漏掉軟硬交界縱向彎曲。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Hoop compression alone misses longitudinal bending across a stiffness transition. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b120-v14-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比較環向應變、縱向沉陷和軌道基座反應。將環形變形、接縫張開與應變和含接頭彈簧的模型比較，分開安裝後、背填後及水頭回升後的基準。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Compare hoop strain, longitudinal settlement and track-support response. Compare ring distortion, joint opening and strain with a joint-spring model, separating baselines after installation, grouting and head recovery. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b120-v14-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「襯砌環向壓縮」的交付需回答：比較環向應變、縱向沉陷和軌道基座反應。設計圖應分開標註各施工階段、接頭剛度及背填條件，構件驗收同時核對幾何、材料批次與止水試驗適用包絡。","textEn":"For Shiziyang Tunnel, the lining hoop compression handover must address the following evidence: Compare hoop strain, longitudinal settlement and track-support response. Drawings distinguish stages, joint stiffness and backfill conditions; component acceptance reconciles geometry, material batches and the applicable sealing-test envelope.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「環向受力與接縫柔度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Ring force and joint flexibility\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。","比較環向應變、縱向沉陷和軌道基座反應。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.","Compare hoop strain, longitudinal settlement and track-support response."],"answer":2,"explanation":"比較環向應變、縱向沉陷和軌道基座反應。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare hoop strain, longitudinal settlement and track-support response. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b120-v14-24","title":"環向受力與接縫柔度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Ring force and joint flexibility: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b120-v14-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「襯砌環向壓縮」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Lining hoop compression” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只驗環向壓縮會漏掉軟硬交界縱向彎曲。局部脫空增加環片彎曲，裂縫未必代表混凝土平均強度不足；忽略接縫接觸會把補強方向導向錯誤位置。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Hoop compression alone misses longitudinal bending across a stiffness transition. Local voids increase bending, so cracks need not indicate inadequate mean concrete strength; neglecting joint contact can misdirect strengthening. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：薄環膜應力只說明其中一條受力路徑；脫模、運輸、頂推及永久狀態的荷載不同，環片局部接觸與止水條件必須另外檢核。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Demoulding, transport, jacking and permanent states impose different actions, requiring separate checks of local segment contact and sealing rather than one permanent-load calculation.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b120-v14-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只驗環向壓縮會漏掉軟硬交界縱向彎曲。局部脫空增加環片彎曲，裂縫未必代表混凝土平均強度不足；忽略接縫接觸會把補強方向導向錯誤位置。","textEn":"Hoop compression alone misses longitudinal bending across a stiffness transition. Local voids increase bending, so cracks need not indicate inadequate mean concrete strength; neglecting joint contact can misdirect strengthening.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b120-v14-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「環向受力與接縫柔度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Ring force and joint flexibility\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["只驗環向壓縮會漏掉軟硬交界縱向彎曲。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Hoop compression alone misses longitudinal bending across a stiffness transition.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error."],"answer":0,"explanation":"只驗環向壓縮會漏掉軟硬交界縱向彎曲。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Hoop compression alone misses longitudinal bending across a stiffness transition. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b120-v14-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「控制網與貫通誤差」與「列車壓力波與動壓量級」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Control network and breakthrough error\" and \"Train pressure waves and dynamic-pressure scale\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b120-v14-25","title":"控制網與貫通誤差：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b120-v14-24"],"objective":"說明「方向角誤差」如何影響獅子洋隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Orientation error” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Shiziyang Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"水下長驅接合需把控制網誤差與盾構姿態分開，獅子洋教材分析相向掘進的方向累積。長隧道的微小方向誤差會沿距離累積，地下控制網又缺少直接衛星定位，必須把地表基準可靠傳到洞內。閉合差很小不代表無系統誤差；尺度、折光、儀器定向與高程基準可能共同偏移，誤差相關性也使平方和估算失真。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「方向角誤差」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Underwater connection requires separation of network error from machine attitude, including direction accumulation in opposing drives. Small orientation errors accumulate over long drives, while underground networks lack direct satellite positioning and depend on transferring surface control. A small closure does not exclude systematic bias: scale, refraction, orientation and vertical datum may shift together. Correlated errors also invalidate a naive root-sum-square combination of supposedly independent observations. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Orientation error” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：控制長度=5280 m；方向偏角=2.6 arcsec。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: control length=5280 m; orientation error=2.6 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0665552 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「方向角誤差」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Orientation error”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b120-v14-25-k1","title":"控制網與貫通誤差","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error","text":"水下長驅接合需把控制網誤差與盾構姿態分開，獅子洋教材分析相向掘進的方向累積。長隧道的微小方向誤差會沿距離累積，地下控制網又缺少直接衛星定位，必須把地表基準可靠傳到洞內。","textEn":"Underwater connection requires separation of network error from machine attitude, including direction accumulation in opposing drives. Small orientation errors accumulate over long drives, while underground networks lack direct satellite positioning and depend on transferring surface control.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b120-v14-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「控制網與貫通誤差」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Control network and breakthrough error\" is correct?","options":["兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。","水下長驅接合需把控制網誤差與盾構姿態分開，獅子洋教材分析相向掘進的方向累積。","動壓公式算出的數值就是長鐵路隧道完整壓力波。"],"optionsEn":["Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.","Underwater connection requires separation of network error from machine attitude, including direction accumulation in opposing drives.","A dynamic-pressure calculation is the complete pressure-wave prediction for a long rail tunnel."],"answer":1,"explanation":"水下長驅接合需把控制網誤差與盾構姿態分開，獅子洋教材分析相向掘進的方向累積。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Underwater connection requires separation of network error from machine attitude, including direction accumulation in opposing drives. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b120-v14-26","title":"控制網與貫通誤差：定量估算","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b120-v14-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「方向角誤差」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Orientation error” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：控制長度=5280 m；方向偏角=2.6 arcsec。e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0665552 m。僅把方向偏角增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.0732107 m。邊界：小角度方向偏差，未加入控制網相關性及折光；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: control length=5280 m; orientation error=2.6 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0665552 m. Increasing only orientation error by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.0732107 m. Boundary: Small-angle orientation error without network correlation or refraction. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：獨立核對兩端原始角距及接合前探測。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Independently check raw observations from both ends and preconnection surveys.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b120-v14-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：控制長度=5280 m；方向偏角=2.6 arcsec。e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0665552 m。僅把方向偏角增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.0732107 m。邊界：小角度方向偏差，未加入控制網相關性及折光；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: control length=5280 m; orientation error=2.6 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0665552 m. Increasing only orientation error by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.0732107 m. Boundary: Small-angle orientation error without network correlation or refraction. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b120-v14-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「控制網與貫通誤差」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Control network and breakthrough error\", which statement holds?","options":["全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。","岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。","原創教學假設：控制長度=5280 m；方向偏角=2.6 arcsec。"],"optionsEn":["Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.","Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow.","Original teaching assumptions: control length=5280 m; orientation error=2.6 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0665552 m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：控制長度=5280 m；方向偏角=2.6 arcsec。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: control length=5280 m; orientation error=2.6 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0665552 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b120-v14-27","title":"控制網與貫通誤差：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b120-v14-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「方向角誤差」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Orientation error” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"獨立核對兩端原始角距及接合前探測。由獨立測量組複核地表到洞內的轉換，保留原始角距及溫度資料，用不同控制線比較方向與高程偏差。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Independently check raw observations from both ends and preconnection surveys. Independently check surface-to-tunnel transformations, retain raw angles, distances and temperatures, and compare orientation and elevation through separate control routes. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「方向角誤差」的交付需回答：獨立核對兩端原始角距及接合前探測。貫通前凍結座標、尺度與高程版本，獨立組直接使用原始觀測重算；不得只傳遞整理好的坐標而遺失校正資訊。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Shiziyang Tunnel, the orientation error handover must address the following evidence: Independently check raw observations from both ends and preconnection surveys. Freeze coordinate, scale and height revisions before breakthrough; independent reviewers recompute raw observations rather than receiving only adjusted coordinates without corrections.","failure":"注意干擾：盾構姿態看似正常可能只是跟隨偏移的導向基準。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Normal machine attitude may merely follow a biased guidance reference. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b120-v14-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"獨立核對兩端原始角距及接合前探測。由獨立測量組複核地表到洞內的轉換，保留原始角距及溫度資料，用不同控制線比較方向與高程偏差。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Independently check raw observations from both ends and preconnection surveys. Independently check surface-to-tunnel transformations, retain raw angles, distances and temperatures, and compare orientation and elevation through separate control routes. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b120-v14-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「方向角誤差」的交付需回答：獨立核對兩端原始角距及接合前探測。貫通前凍結座標、尺度與高程版本，獨立組直接使用原始觀測重算；不得只傳遞整理好的坐標而遺失校正資訊。","textEn":"For Shiziyang Tunnel, the orientation error handover must address the following evidence: Independently check raw observations from both ends and preconnection surveys. Freeze coordinate, scale and height revisions before breakthrough; independent reviewers recompute raw observations rather than receiving only adjusted coordinates without corrections.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「控制網與貫通誤差」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Control network and breakthrough error\"?","options":["獨立核對兩端原始角距及接合前探測。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。"],"optionsEn":["Independently check raw observations from both ends and preconnection surveys.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"獨立核對兩端原始角距及接合前探測。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Independently check raw observations from both ends and preconnection surveys. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b120-v14-28","title":"控制網與貫通誤差：失效診斷","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b120-v14-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「方向角誤差」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Orientation error” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"盾構姿態看似正常可能只是跟隨偏移的導向基準。共用錯誤基準可能讓兩組測量同時看似一致，直到貫通或軌道銜接才發現系統偏差，修正成本遠高於早期複核。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Normal machine attitude may merely follow a biased guidance reference. A shared wrong datum can make separate surveys appear consistent until breakthrough or track connection exposes bias that is costly to correct. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：閉合差很小不代表無系統誤差；尺度、折光、儀器定向與高程基準可能共同偏移，誤差相關性也使平方和估算失真。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Correlated errors also invalidate a naive root-sum-square combination of supposedly independent observations.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b120-v14-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"盾構姿態看似正常可能只是跟隨偏移的導向基準。共用錯誤基準可能讓兩組測量同時看似一致，直到貫通或軌道銜接才發現系統偏差，修正成本遠高於早期複核。","textEn":"Normal machine attitude may merely follow a biased guidance reference. A shared wrong datum can make separate surveys appear consistent until breakthrough or track connection exposes bias that is costly to correct.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b120-v14-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「控制網與貫通誤差」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Control network and breakthrough error\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","盾構姿態看似正常可能只是跟隨偏移的導向基準。","動壓公式算出的數值就是長鐵路隧道完整壓力波。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Normal machine attitude may merely follow a biased guidance reference.","A dynamic-pressure calculation is the complete pressure-wave prediction for a long rail tunnel."],"answer":1,"explanation":"盾構姿態看似正常可能只是跟隨偏移的導向基準。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Normal machine attitude may merely follow a biased guidance reference. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b120-v14-29","title":"列車壓力波與動壓量級：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Train pressure waves and dynamic-pressure scale: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b120-v14-28"],"objective":"說明「入口壓力擾動」如何影響獅子洋隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Portal pressure disturbance” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Shiziyang Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"高速列車的動壓與洞口波形不同，教材以速度平方尺度說明為何還需阻塞比和緩衝結構分析。列車進洞壓縮前方空氣，波動在洞口、橫通道和斷面變化處傳播與反射。速度和阻塞比影響壓力量級，但不可壓動壓只是比較尺度，不能替代可壓縮瞬變計算；兩車交會、門位與列車外形都可能改變乘客及設備的壓力歷程。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「入口壓力擾動」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Dynamic pressure differs from portal wave shape; velocity-squared scaling explains why blockage and entrance structures still need analysis. A train entering a tunnel compresses the air ahead, producing waves reflected at portals, passages and section changes. Speed and blockage influence magnitude, but incompressible dynamic pressure is only a comparison scale, not a compressible transient solution. Train encounters, door states and vehicle shape change the pressure histories experienced by passengers and equipment. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Portal pressure disturbance” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；列車速度=59 m/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: air density=1.2 kg/m³; train speed=59 m/s. q=ρv²/2=2088.6 Pa.","failure":"常見誤解：「動壓公式算出的數值就是長鐵路隧道完整壓力波。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A dynamic-pressure calculation is the complete pressure-wave prediction for a long rail tunnel.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「入口壓力擾動」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Portal pressure disturbance”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b120-v14-29-k1","title":"列車壓力波與動壓量級","titleEn":"Train pressure waves and dynamic-pressure scale","text":"高速列車的動壓與洞口波形不同，教材以速度平方尺度說明為何還需阻塞比和緩衝結構分析。列車進洞壓縮前方空氣，波動在洞口、橫通道和斷面變化處傳播與反射。","textEn":"Dynamic pressure differs from portal wave shape; velocity-squared scaling explains why blockage and entrance structures still need analysis. A train entering a tunnel compresses the air ahead, producing waves reflected at portals, passages and section changes.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b120-v14-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：動壓公式算出的數值就是長鐵路隧道完整壓力波。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A dynamic-pressure calculation is the complete pressure-wave prediction for a long rail tunnel. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「列車壓力波與動壓量級」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Train pressure waves and dynamic-pressure scale\" is correct?","options":["動壓公式算出的數值就是長鐵路隧道完整壓力波。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。","高速列車的動壓與洞口波形不同，教材以速度平方尺度說明為何還需阻塞比和緩衝結構分析。"],"optionsEn":["A dynamic-pressure calculation is the complete pressure-wave prediction for a long rail tunnel.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.","Dynamic pressure differs from portal wave shape; velocity-squared scaling explains why blockage and entrance structures still need analysis."],"answer":2,"explanation":"高速列車的動壓與洞口波形不同，教材以速度平方尺度說明為何還需阻塞比和緩衝結構分析。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Dynamic pressure differs from portal wave shape; velocity-squared scaling explains why blockage and entrance structures still need analysis. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b120-v14-30","title":"列車壓力波與動壓量級：定量估算","titleEn":"Train pressure waves and dynamic-pressure scale: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b120-v14-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「入口壓力擾動」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Portal pressure disturbance” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；列車速度=59 m/s。q=ρv²/2=2088.6 Pa。僅把列車速度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為2527.21 Pa。邊界：不可壓動壓尺度，不是可壓縮列車壓力波解；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: air density=1.2 kg/m³; train speed=59 m/s. q=ρv²/2=2088.6 Pa. Increasing only train speed by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 2527.21 Pa. Boundary: Incompressible dynamic-pressure scale, not a compressible train pressure-wave solution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同步量測速度和多位置壓力，辨識反射到達。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Synchronise speed and pressure at several locations to identify reflected arrivals.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b120-v14-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；列車速度=59 m/s。q=ρv²/2=2088.6 Pa。僅把列車速度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為2527.21 Pa。邊界：不可壓動壓尺度，不是可壓縮列車壓力波解；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: air density=1.2 kg/m³; train speed=59 m/s. q=ρv²/2=2088.6 Pa. Increasing only train speed by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 2527.21 Pa. Boundary: Incompressible dynamic-pressure scale, not a compressible train pressure-wave solution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b120-v14-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「列車壓力波與動壓量級」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Train pressure waves and dynamic-pressure scale\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；列車速度=59 m/s。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。","目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: air density=1.2 kg/m³; train speed=59 m/s. q=ρv²/2=2088.6 Pa.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.","No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；列車速度=59 m/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: air density=1.2 kg/m³; train speed=59 m/s. q=ρv²/2=2088.6 Pa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b120-v14-31","title":"列車壓力波與動壓量級：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Train pressure waves and dynamic-pressure scale: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b120-v14-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「入口壓力擾動」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Portal pressure disturbance” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同步量測速度和多位置壓力，辨識反射到達。以相同列車編組、速度和門位量測多點壓力歷程，檢查峰值、上升時間及反射抵達時刻，而不只比較一個最大值。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Synchronise speed and pressure at several locations to identify reflected arrivals. Measure pressure histories at several points with matching train formation, speed and door states, comparing rise time and reflection arrival as well as peaks. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「入口壓力擾動」的交付需回答：同步量測速度和多位置壓力，辨識反射到達。試車報告記錄編組、速度、溫度及門位版本，土建斷面變更與設備耐壓驗證共用同一氣動模型，不能各自選有利情境。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Shiziyang Tunnel, the portal pressure disturbance handover must address the following evidence: Synchronise speed and pressure at several locations to identify reflected arrivals. Trial reports retain formation, speed, temperature and door revisions; civil changes and equipment-pressure checks share one aerodynamic model rather than selectively favourable cases.","failure":"注意干擾：直接用動壓預測舒適性會忽略列車與隧道幾何。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using dynamic pressure alone for comfort ignores train and tunnel geometry. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b120-v14-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同步量測速度和多位置壓力，辨識反射到達。以相同列車編組、速度和門位量測多點壓力歷程，檢查峰值、上升時間及反射抵達時刻，而不只比較一個最大值。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Synchronise speed and pressure at several locations to identify reflected arrivals. Measure pressure histories at several points with matching train formation, speed and door states, comparing rise time and reflection arrival as well as peaks. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b120-v14-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「入口壓力擾動」的交付需回答：同步量測速度和多位置壓力，辨識反射到達。試車報告記錄編組、速度、溫度及門位版本，土建斷面變更與設備耐壓驗證共用同一氣動模型，不能各自選有利情境。","textEn":"For Shiziyang Tunnel, the portal pressure disturbance handover must address the following evidence: Synchronise speed and pressure at several locations to identify reflected arrivals. Trial reports retain formation, speed, temperature and door revisions; civil changes and equipment-pressure checks share one aerodynamic model rather than selectively favourable cases.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「列車壓力波與動壓量級」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Train pressure waves and dynamic-pressure scale\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","同步量測速度和多位置壓力，辨識反射到達。","灌入體積等於理論空隙就能證明襯砌背後全部填滿。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Synchronise speed and pressure at several locations to identify reflected arrivals.","Injected volume equal to the theoretical annulus proves complete filling behind the lining."],"answer":1,"explanation":"同步量測速度和多位置壓力，辨識反射到達。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Synchronise speed and pressure at several locations to identify reflected arrivals. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b120-v14-32","title":"列車壓力波與動壓量級：失效診斷","titleEn":"Train pressure waves and dynamic-pressure scale: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b120-v14-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「入口壓力擾動」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Portal pressure disturbance” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"直接用動壓預測舒適性會忽略列車與隧道幾何。以單一動壓數字當允收值會漏掉壓力梯度與反射疊加，可能使門扇、密封或乘客舒適度需求被低估。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using dynamic pressure alone for comfort ignores train and tunnel geometry. Using one dynamic-pressure value for acceptance misses gradients and superposed reflections, understating demands on doors, seals or passenger comfort. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：速度和阻塞比影響壓力量級，但不可壓動壓只是比較尺度，不能替代可壓縮瞬變計算；兩車交會、門位與列車外形都可能改變乘客及設備的壓力歷程。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Train encounters, door states and vehicle shape change the pressure histories experienced by passengers and equipment.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「動壓公式算出的數值就是長鐵路隧道完整壓力波。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A dynamic-pressure calculation is the complete pressure-wave prediction for a long rail tunnel.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b120-v14-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"直接用動壓預測舒適性會忽略列車與隧道幾何。以單一動壓數字當允收值會漏掉壓力梯度與反射疊加，可能使門扇、密封或乘客舒適度需求被低估。","textEn":"Using dynamic pressure alone for comfort ignores train and tunnel geometry. Using one dynamic-pressure value for acceptance misses gradients and superposed reflections, understating demands on doors, seals or passenger comfort.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b120-v14-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「列車壓力波與動壓量級」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Train pressure waves and dynamic-pressure scale\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。","直接用動壓預測舒適性會忽略列車與隧道幾何。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.","Using dynamic pressure alone for comfort ignores train and tunnel geometry."],"answer":2,"explanation":"直接用動壓預測舒適性會忽略列車與隧道幾何。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using dynamic pressure alone for comfort ignores train and tunnel geometry. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b120-v14-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「疏散時間與分區可用性」與「資產編碼與可追溯交接」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Evacuation time and zone availability\" and \"Asset identity and traceable handover\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b120-v14-33","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b120-v14-32"],"objective":"說明「所需疏散時間」如何影響獅子洋隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Required evacuation time” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Shiziyang Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"水下雙孔鐵路的救援需確定列車停車位置和鄰孔狀態，教材將下車流率和步行分開。疏散時間包含辨識、反應、移動及排隊，不只由出口距離決定。人員速度會受煙熱、能見度及行動能力影響，安全判斷還要比較可用安全時間；橫通道存在但門或鄰孔不可用時，圖上的最短路線不一定能作實際選擇。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「所需疏散時間」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Subsea twin-bore rescue depends on stopping position and receiving-bore state; separate detraining flow from walking. Evacuation includes detection, response, travel and queues, not merely distance to an exit. Smoke, visibility and mobility alter walking speed, while safety requires comparison with available safe time. A passage shown on a plan may be unusable because its door or receiving bore is unavailable, invalidating the nominal shortest route. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Required evacuation time” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：前置時間=118 s；行走距離=360 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=118 s; travel distance=360 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「所需疏散時間」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Required evacuation time”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b120-v14-33-k1","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability","text":"水下雙孔鐵路的救援需確定列車停車位置和鄰孔狀態，教材將下車流率和步行分開。疏散時間包含辨識、反應、移動及排隊，不只由出口距離決定。","textEn":"Subsea twin-bore rescue depends on stopping position and receiving-bore state; separate detraining flow from walking. Evacuation includes detection, response, travel and queues, not merely distance to an exit.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b120-v14-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「疏散時間與分區可用性」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Evacuation time and zone availability\" is correct?","options":["水下雙孔鐵路的救援需確定列車停車位置和鄰孔狀態，教材將下車流率和步行分開。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。"],"optionsEn":["Subsea twin-bore rescue depends on stopping position and receiving-bore state; separate detraining flow from walking.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted."],"answer":0,"explanation":"水下雙孔鐵路的救援需確定列車停車位置和鄰孔狀態，教材將下車流率和步行分開。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Subsea twin-bore rescue depends on stopping position and receiving-bore state; separate detraining flow from walking. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b120-v14-34","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性：定量估算","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b120-v14-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「所需疏散時間」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Required evacuation time” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：前置時間=118 s；行走距離=360 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。RSET=tpre+d/v=568 s。僅把行走距離增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為613 s。邊界：單群體固定速度，不含排隊煙熱及能力差異，不能單獨判安全；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=118 s; travel distance=360 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s. RSET=tpre+d/v=568 s. Increasing only travel distance by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 613 s. Boundary: One group at fixed speed without queues, smoke or mobility differences; not a safety conclusion. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以不同停車點演練門位及可用路徑。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Exercise door positions and usable routes for different stopping points.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b120-v14-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：前置時間=118 s；行走距離=360 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。RSET=tpre+d/v=568 s。僅把行走距離增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為613 s。邊界：單群體固定速度，不含排隊煙熱及能力差異，不能單獨判安全；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=118 s; travel distance=360 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s. RSET=tpre+d/v=568 s. Increasing only travel distance by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 613 s. Boundary: One group at fixed speed without queues, smoke or mobility differences; not a safety conclusion. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b120-v14-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b120","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「疏散時間與分區可用性」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Evacuation time and zone availab